y manejo de errores","fr":"Guide complet pour écrire des scripts Bash de production en utilisant des techniques de programmation défensive et de gestion d''erreurs","de":"Umfassende Anleitung zum Schreiben von Bash-Produktionsskripten mit defensiver Programmierung und Fehlerbehandlung","pt":"Padrões defensivos Bash para scripts de produção robustos e seguros","ru":"Защитные шаблоны Bash для надежных и безопасных производственных скриптов","ar":"نماذج ديفنسيف باش من أجل scripts إنتاج قوي وآمن","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["错误处理和安全最佳实践","防御性编程技术","边缘情况处理","可靠性和安全性","自动化脚本编写","CI/CD 流水线脚本构建"],"ja":["エラー処理とセキュリティのベストプラクティス","ディフェンシブ プログラミング テクニック","エッジ ケースの処理","信頼性とセキュリティ","自動化スクリプトの作成","CI/CD パイプライン スクリプトの構築"],"ko":["오류 처리 및 보안 모범 사례","방어적 프로그래밍 기술","엣지 케이스 처리","안정성 및 보안","자동화 스크립트 작성","CI/CD 파이프라인 스크립트 구축"],"es":["Técnicas de programación defensiva","Manejo de errores y excepciones"," Mejores prácticas de seguridad","Preención de errores comunes","Creación de scripts de automatización de producción","Desarrollo de utilidades de administración de sistema"],"fr":["Techniques de programmation défensive","Gestion des erreurs et des exceptions","Meilleures pratiques de sécurité","Prévention des erreurs courantes","Création de scripts d''automatisation de production","Développement d''utilitaires d''administration de système"],"de":["Defensive ProgrammierTechniken","Fehler- und Ausnahmehandling","Sicherheitsbest Practices","Vermeidung häufiger Fehler","Erstellung von Produktionsautomatisierungsskripten","Entwicklung von Systemadministrationstools"],"pt":["Técnicas de programação defensiva","Tratamento de erros e exceções","Melhores práticas de segurança","Prevenção de pits comuns","Desenvolvimento de scripts robustos"],"ru":["Защитные техники программирования","Обработка ошибок и исключений","Лучшие практики безопасности","Предотвращение распространенных ошибок","Разработка надежных скриптов"],"ar":["تقنيات البرمجة الدفاعية","معالجة الأخطاء والاستثناءات","أفضل الممارسات الأمنية","منع الأخطاء الشائعة","تطوير scripts قوية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Bash 脚本","防御性编程","错误处理","安全最佳实践","自动化脚本","CI/CD 流水线","边缘情况处理","可靠性和安全性"],"ja":["Bash スクリプト","ディフェンシブ プログラミング","エラー処理","セキュリティのベストプラクティス","自動化スクリプト","CI/CD パイプライン","エッジ ケースの処理","信頼性とセキュリティ"],"ko":["Bash 스크립트","방어적 프로그래밍","오류 처리","보안 모범 사례","자동화 스크립트","CI/CD 파이프라인","엣지 케이스 처리","안정성 및 보안"],"es":["patrones defensivos de Bash","programación defensiva","manejo de errores","seguridad en Bash","automatización de producción","administración de sistema","desarrollo de scripts","Bash para desarrolladores"],"fr":["modèles de défense Bash","programmation défensive","gestion des erreurs","sécurité Bash","automatisation de production","administration de système","développement de scripts","Bash pour développeurs"],"de":["Bash-Defensivmuster","defensive Programmierung","Fehlerbehandlung","Sicherheit in Bash","Produktionsautomatisierung","Systemadministration","Skriptentwicklung","Bash für Entwickler"],"pt":["bash defensivo","programação segura","scripts de produção","automação de produção","desenvolvimento de scripts","segurança de scripts"],"ru":["защитный bash","безопасное программирование","производственные скрипты","автоматизация производства","разработка скриптов","безопасность скриптов"],"ar":["با什 ديفنسيف","برمجة آمنة","scripts إنتاج","أتمتة الإنتاج","تطوير scripts","أمان scripts"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.523Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bash-defensive-patterns","description":"Master defensive Bash programming techniques for production-grade scripts. Use when writing robust shell scripts, CI/CD pipelines, or system utilities requiring fault tolerance and safety.","bodyPreview":"# Bash Defensive Patterns\n\nComprehensive guidance for writing production-ready Bash scripts using defensive programming techniques, error handling, and safety best practices to prevent common pitfalls and ensure reliability.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing production automation scripts\n- Building CI/CD pipeline scripts\n- Creating system administration utilities\n- Developing error-resilient deployment automation\n- Writing scripts that must handle edge cases safely\n- Building maintainable sh","body":"# Bash Defensive Patterns\n\nComprehensive guidance for writing production-ready Bash scripts using defensive programming techniques, error handling, and safety best practices to prevent common pitfalls and ensure reliability.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing production automation scripts\n- Building CI/CD pipeline scripts\n- Creating system administration utilities\n- Developing error-resilient deployment automation\n- Writing scripts that must handle edge cases safely\n- Building maintainable shell script libraries\n- Implementing comprehensive logging and monitoring\n- Creating scripts that must work across different platforms\n\n## Core Defensive Principles\n\n### 1. Strict Mode\n\nEnable bash strict mode at the start of every script to catch errors early.\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail  # Exit on error, unset variables, pipe failures\n```\n\n**Key flags:**\n\n- `set -E`: Inherit ERR trap in functions\n- `set -e`: Exit on any error (command returns non-zero)\n- `set -u`: Exit on undefined variable reference\n- `set -o pipefail`: Pipe fails if any command fails (not just last)\n\n### 2. Error Trapping and Cleanup\n\nImplement proper cleanup on script exit or error.\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\ntrap ''echo \"Error on line $LINENO\"'' ERR\ntrap ''echo \"Cleaning up...\"; rm -rf \"$TMPDIR\"'' EXIT\n\nTMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)\n# Script code here\n```\n\n### 3. Variable Safety\n\nAlways quote variables to prevent word splitting and globbing issues.\n\n```bash\n# Wrong - unsafe\ncp $source $dest\n\n# Correct - safe\ncp \"$source\" \"$dest\"\n\n# Required variables - fail with message if unset\n: \"${REQUIRED_VAR:?REQUIRED_VAR is not set}\"\n```\n\n### 4. Array Handling\n\nUse arrays safely for complex data handling.\n\n```bash\n# Safe array iteration\ndeclare -a items=(\"item 1\" \"item 2\" \"item 3\")\n\nfor item in \"${items[@]}\"; do\n    echo \"Processing: $item\"\ndone\n\n# Reading output into array safely\nmapfile -t lines < <(some_command)\nreadarray -t numbers < <(seq 1 10)\n```\n\n### 5. Conditional Safety\n\nUse `[[ ]]` for Bash-specific features, `[ ]` for POSIX.\n\n```bash\n# Bash - safer\nif [[ -f \"$file\" && -r \"$file\" ]]; then\n    content=$(<\"$file\")\nfi\n\n# POSIX - portable\nif [ -f \"$file\" ] && [ -r \"$file\" ]; then\n    content=$(cat \"$file\")\nfi\n\n# Test for existence before operations\nif [[ -z \"${VAR:-}\" ]]; then\n    echo \"VAR is not set or is empty\"\nfi\n```\n\n## Fundamental Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Safe Script Directory Detection\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Correctly determine script directory\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\nSCRIPT_NAME=\"$(basename -- \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\"\n\necho \"Script location: $SCRIPT_DIR/$SCRIPT_NAME\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Comprehensive Function Templat\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Prefix for functions: handle_*, process_*, check_*, validate_*\n# Include documentation and error handling\n\nvalidate_file() {\n    local -r file=\"$1\"\n    local -r message=\"${2:-File not found: $file}\"\n\n    if [[ ! -f \"$file\" ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: $message\" >&2\n        return 1\n    fi\n    return 0\n}\n\nprocess_files() {\n    local -r input_dir=\"$1\"\n    local -r output_dir=\"$2\"\n\n    # Validate inputs\n    [[ -d \"$input_dir\" ]] || { echo \"ERROR: input_dir not a directory\" >&2; return 1; }\n\n    # Create output directory if needed\n    mkdir -p \"$output_dir\" || { echo \"ERROR: Cannot create output_dir\" >&2; return 1; }\n\n    # Process files safely\n    while IFS= read -r -d '''' file; do\n        echo \"Processing: $file\"\n        # Do work\n    done < <(find \"$input_dir\" -maxdepth 1 -type f -print0)\n\n    return 0\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Safe Temporary File Handling\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\ntrap ''rm -rf -- \"$TMPDIR\"'' EXIT\n\n# Create temporary directory\nTMPDIR=$(mktemp -d) || { echo \"ERROR: Failed to create temp directory\" >&2; exit 1; }\n\n# Create temporary files in directory\nTMPFILE1=\"$TMPDIR/temp1.txt\"\nTMPFILE2=\"$TMPDIR/temp2.txt\"\n\n# Use temporary files\ntouch \"$TMPFILE1\" \"$TMPFILE2\"\n\necho \"Temp files created in: $TMPDIR\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Robust Argument Parsing\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Default values\nVERBOSE=false\nDRY_RUN=false\nOUTPUT_FILE=\"\"\nTHREADS=4\n\nusage() {\n    cat <<EOF\nUsage: $0 [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n    -v, --verbose       Enable verbose output\n    -d, --dry-run       Run without making changes\n    -o, --output FILE   Output file path\n    -j, --jobs NUM      Number of parallel jobs\n    -h, --help          Show this help message\nEOF\n    exit \"${1:-0}\"\n}\n\n# Parse arguments\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n    case \"$1\" in\n        -v|--verbose)\n            VERBOSE=true\n            shift\n            ;;\n        -d|--dry-run)\n            DRY_RUN=true\n            shift\n            ;;\n        -o|--output)\n            OUTPUT_FILE=\"$2\"\n            shift 2\n            ;;\n        -j|--jobs)\n            THREADS=\"$2\"\n            shift 2\n            ;;\n        -h|--help)\n            usage 0\n            ;;\n        --)\n            shift\n            break\n            ;;\n        *)\n            echo \"ERROR: Unknown option: $1\" >&2\n            usage 1\n            ;;\n    esac\ndone\n\n# Validate required arguments\n[[ -n \"$OUTPUT_FILE\" ]] || { echo \"ERROR: -o/--output is required\" >&2; usage 1; }\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Structured Logging\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Logging functions\nlog_info() {\n    echo \"[$(date +''%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'')] INFO: $*\" >&2\n}\n\nlog_warn() {\n    echo \"[$(date +''%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'')] WARN: $*\" >&2\n}\n\nlog_error() {\n    echo \"[$(date +''%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'')] ERROR: $*\" >&2\n}\n\nlog_debug() {\n    if [[ \"${DEBUG:-0}\" == \"1\" ]]; then\n        echo \"[$(date +''%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'')] DEBUG: $*\" >&2\n    fi\n}\n\n# Usage\nlog_info \"Starting script\"\nlog_debug \"Debug information\"\nlog_warn \"Warning message\"\nlog_error \"Error occurred\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Process Orchestration with Signals\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Track background processes\nPIDS=()\n\ncleanup() {\n    log_info \"Shutting down...\"\n\n    # Terminate all background processes\n    for pid in \"${PIDS[@]}\"; do\n        if kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null; then\n            kill -TERM \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\n        fi\n    done\n\n    # Wait for graceful shutdown\n    for pid in \"${PIDS[@]}\"; do\n        wait \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    done\n}\n\ntrap cleanup SIGTERM SIGINT\n\n# Start background tasks\nbackground_task &\nPIDS+=($!)\n\nanother_task &\nPIDS+=($!)\n\n# Wait for all background processes\nwait\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: Safe File Operations\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Use -i flag to move safely without overwriting\nsafe_move() {\n    local -r source=\"$1\"\n    local -r dest=\"$2\"\n\n    if [[ ! -e \"$source\" ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: Source does not exist: $source\" >&2\n        return 1\n    fi\n\n    if [[ -e \"$dest\" ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: Destination already exists: $dest\" >&2\n        return 1\n    fi\n\n    mv \"$source\" \"$dest\"\n}\n\n# Safe directory cleanup\nsafe_rmdir() {\n    local -r dir=\"$1\"\n\n    if [[ ! -d \"$dir\" ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: Not a directory: $dir\" >&2\n        return 1\n    fi\n\n    # Use -I flag to prompt before rm (BSD/GNU compatible)\n    rm -rI -- \"$dir\"\n}\n\n# Atomic file writes\natomic_write() {\n    local -r target=\"$1\"\n    local -r tmpfile\n    tmpfile=$(mktemp) || return 1\n\n    # Write to temp file first\n    cat > \"$tmpfile\"\n\n    # Atomic rename\n    mv \"$tmpfile\" \"$target\"\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 8: Idempotent Script Design\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Check if resource already exists\nensure_directory() {\n    local -r dir=\"$1\"\n\n    if [[ -d \"$dir\" ]]; then\n        log_info \"Directory already exists: $dir\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    mkdir -p \"$dir\" || {\n        log_error \"Failed to create directory: $dir\"\n        return 1\n    }\n\n    log_info \"Created directory: $dir\"\n}\n\n# Ensure configuration state\nensure_config() {\n    local -r config_file=\"$1\"\n    local -r default_value=\"$2\"\n\n    if [[ ! -f \"$config_file\" ]]; then\n        echo \"$default_value\" > \"$config_file\"\n        log_info \"Created config: $config_file\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Rerunning script multiple times should be safe\nensure_directory \"/var/cache/myapp\"\nensure_config \"/etc/myapp/config\" \"DEBUG=false\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 9: Safe Command Substitution\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\n# Use $() instead of backticks\nname=$(<\"$file\")  # Modern, safe variable assignment from file\noutput=$(command -v python3)  # Get command location safely\n\n# Handle command substitution with error checking\nresult=$(command -v node) || {\n    log_error \"node command not found\"\n    return 1\n}\n\n# For multiple lines\nmapfile -t lines < <(grep \"pattern\" \"$file\")\n\n# NUL-safe iteration\nwhile IFS= read -r -d '''' file; do\n    echo \"Processing: $file\"\ndone < <(find /path -type f -print0)\n```\n\n### Pattern 10: Dry-Run Support\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\nDRY_RUN=\"${DRY_RUN:-false}\"\n\nrun_cmd() {\n    if [[ \"$DRY_RUN\" == \"true\" ]]; then\n        echo \"[DRY RUN] Would execute: $*\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    \"$@\"\n}\n\n# Usage\nrun_cmd cp \"$source\" \"$dest\"\nrun_cmd rm \"$file\"\nrun_cmd chown \"$owner\" \"$target\"\n```\n\n## Advanced Defensive Techniques\n\n### Named Parameters Pattern\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\nprocess_data() {\n    local input_file=\"\"\n    local output_dir=\"\"\n    local format=\"json\"\n\n    # Parse named parameters\n    while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n        case \"$1\" in\n            --input=*)\n                input_file=\"${1#*=}\"\n                ;;\n            --output=*)\n                output_dir=\"${1#*=}\"\n                ;;\n            --format=*)\n                format=\"${1#*=}\"\n                ;;\n            *)\n                echo \"ERROR: Unknown parameter: $1\" >&2\n                return 1\n                ;;\n        esac\n        shift\n    done\n\n    # Validate required parameters\n    [[ -n \"$input_file\" ]] || { echo \"ERROR: --input is required\" >&2; return 1; }\n    [[ -n \"$output_dir\" ]] || { echo \"ERROR: --output is required\" >&2; return 1; }\n}\n```\n\n### Dependency Checking\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\ncheck_dependencies() {\n    local -a missing_deps=()\n    local -a required=(\"jq\" \"curl\" \"git\")\n\n    for cmd in \"${required[@]}\"; do\n        if ! command -v \"$cmd\" &>/dev/null; then\n            missing_deps+=(\"$cmd\")\n        fi\n    done\n\n    if [[ ${#missing_deps[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: Missing required commands: ${missing_deps[*]}\" >&2\n        return 1\n    fi\n}\n\ncheck_dependencies\n```\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Always use strict mode** - `set -Eeuo pipefail`\n2. **Quote all variables** - `\"$variable\"` prevents word splitting\n3. **Use [[]] conditionals** - More robust than [ ]\n4. **Implement error trapping** - Catch and handle errors gracefully\n5. **Validate all inputs** - Check file existence, permissions, formats\n6. **Use functions for reusability** - Prefix with meaningful names\n7. **Implement structured logging** - Include timestamps and levels\n8. **Support dry-run mode** - Allow users to preview changes\n9. **Handle temporary files safely** - Use mktemp, cleanup with trap\n10. **Design for idempotency** - Scripts should be safe to rerun\n11. **Document requirements** - List dependencies and minimum versions\n12. **Test error paths** - Ensure error handling works correctly\n13. **Use `command -v`** - Safer than `which` for checking executables\n14. **Prefer printf over echo** - More predictable across systems\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Bash Strict Mode**: http://redsymbol.net/articles/unofficial-bash-strict-mode/\n- **Google Shell Style Guide**: https://google.github.io/styleguide/shellguide.html\n- **Defensive BASH Programming**: https://www.lifepipe.net/\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:51:23.279Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for System Administration Agents requiring robust Bash scripting with defensive programming techniques.","zh":"适合需要强大的Bash脚本和防御性编程技术的系统管理代理。","ja":"ロバストなBashスクリプトと防御的プログラミング技術を必要とするシステム管理エージェントに最適です。","ko":"강력한 Bash 스크립트 및 방어적 프로그래밍 기술이 필요한 시스템 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Administración de Sistemas que requieren programación de Bash robusta con técnicas de programación defensiva.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''administration système nécessitant un scripting Bash robuste avec des techniques de programmation défensives.","de":"Ideal für Systemadministration-Agenten, die robustes Bash-Scripting mit defensiven Programmiertechniken erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Administração de Sistema que exigem programação de script Bash robusta com técnicas de programação defensiva.","ru":"Идеально для агентов системного администрирования, требующих прочного скриптинга Bash с техниками защитного программирования.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة النظام الذي يتطلب برمجة نصية قوية Bash مع تقنيات البرمجة الدفاعية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write production-ready Bash scripts using error handling, safety best practices, and defensive programming techniques, ensuring reliability and preventing common pitfalls in automation scripts, CI/CD pipelines, and system administration utilities.","zh":"赋予代理编写生产就绪的Bash脚本的能力，使用错误处理、安全最佳实践和防御性编程技术，确保可靠性并防止自动化脚本、CI/CD管道和系统管理实用程序中的常见陷阱。","ja":"エージェントに、エラー処理、安全なベストプラクティス、防御的プログラミング技術を使用して、生産性の高いBashスクリプトを記述する能力を付与し、自動化スクリプト、CI/CDパイプライン、システム管理ユーティリティの一般的な落とし穴を防ぎ、信頼性を確保します。","ko":"에러 처리, 안전한 모범 사례 및 방어적 프로그래밍 기술을 사용하여 생산 준비가 된 Bash 스크립트를 작성할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하여 자동화 스크립트, CI/CD 파이프라인 및 시스템 관리 유틸리티의 일반적인 함정을 방지하고 신뢰성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir scripts de Bash listos para producción utilizando el control de errores, las mejores prácticas de seguridad y las técnicas de programación defensiva, garantizando la confiabilidad y evitando trampas comunes en scripts de automatización, pipelines de CI/CD y utilidades de administración de sistemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des scripts Bash prêts pour la production en utilisant la gestion des erreurs, les meilleures pratiques de sécurité et les techniques de programmation défensive, garantissant la fiabilité et évitant les pièges courants dans les scripts d''automatisation, les pipelines CI/CD et les utilitaires d''administration système.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, produktionsbereite Bash-Skripte zu schreiben, die Fehlerbehandlung, Sicherheitsbest-Practices und defensive ProgrammierTechniken verwenden, um Zuverlässigkeit zu gewährleisten und häufige Fallstricke in Automatisierungsskripten, CI/CD-Pipelines und Systemadministration-Utilities zu vermeiden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever scripts Bash de produção prontos usando tratamento de erros, práticas recomendadas de segurança e técnicas de programação defensiva, garantindo confiabilidade e prevenindo armadilhas comuns em scripts de automação, pipelines de CI/CD e utilitários de administração de sistema.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать готовые к производству скрипты Bash, используя обработку ошибок, лучшие практики безопасности и техники защитного программирования, обеспечивая надежность и предотвращая распространенные ловушки в скриптах автоматизации, конвейерах CI/CD и утилитах системного администрирования.","ar":"تمكين العملاء من كتابة نصوص Bash جاهزة للإنتاج باستخدام معالجة الأخطاء وأفضل الممارسات الأمنية وتقنيات البرمجة الدفاعية، مما يضمن الموثوقية وت防يص الفخاخ الشائعة في نصوص الأتمتة وأنابيب CI/CD وأدوات إدارة النظام."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating system administration tasks with error-resilient scripts","Building reliable CI/CD pipeline scripts with defensive programming","Developing maintainable and safe deployment automation scripts"],"zh":["使用容错脚本自动执行系统管理任务","使用防御性编程构建可靠的CI/CD管道脚本","开发可维护和安全的部署自动化脚本"],"ja":["エラー耐性のあるスクリプトを使用してシステム管理タスクを自動化する","防御的プログラミングを使用して信頼性の高いCI/CDパイプラインスクリプトを構築する","保守性と安全性の高い展開自動化スクリプトを開発する"],"ko":["에러 내성 있는 스크립트를 사용하여 시스템 관리 작업을 자동화하는 것","방어적 프로그래밍을 사용하여 안정적인 CI/CD 파이프라인 스크립트를 구축하는 것","유지 보수와 안전한 배포 자동화 스크립트를 개발하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar tareas de administración de sistemas con scripts resistentes a errores","Crear scripts de pipelines de CI/CD confiables con programación defensiva","Desarrollar scripts de automatización de implementación mantenibles y seguros"],"fr":["Automatiser les tâches d''administration système avec des scripts résistants aux erreurs","Construire des scripts de pipeline CI/CD fiables avec une programmation défensive","Développer des scripts d''automatisation de déploiement maintenables et sûrs"],"de":["Automatisierung von Systemadministrationaufgaben mit fehlertoleranten Skripten","Erstellung zuverlässiger CI/CD-Pipeline-Skripte mit defensiver Programmierung","Entwicklung von wartbaren und sicheren Skripten für die Automatisierung der Bereitstellung"],"pt":["Automatizar tarefas de administração de sistema com scripts resistentes a erros","Construir scripts de pipeline de CI/CD confiáveis com programação defensiva","Desenvolver scripts de automação de implantação mantenedores e seguros"],"ru":["Автоматизация задач системного администрирования с помощью скриптов, устойчивых к ошибкам","Создание надежных скриптов конвейера CI/CD с защитным программированием","Разработка поддерживаемых и безопасных скриптов автоматизации развертывания"],"ar":["أتمتة مهام إدارة النظام مع نصوص مقاومة للأخطاء","بناء نصوص أنابيب CI/CD موثوقة مع برمجة دفاعية","تطوير نصوص أتمتة الإنشاء القابلة للصيانة والأمن"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Bash environment","Linux/Unix-based systems only","Scripting knowledge required for effective implementation"],"zh":["需要Bash环境","仅限Linux/Unix 기반系统","需要脚本知识以有效实施"],"ja":["Bash環境が必要","Linux/Unixベースのシステムのみ","効果的な実装にはスクリプトの知識が必要"],"ko":["Bash 환경이 필요합니다.","리눅스/유닉스 기반 시스템만 해당","유효한 구현을 위해서는 스크립트 지식이 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere entorno de Bash","Sistemas basados en Linux/Unix solo","Conocimiento de scripting necesario para una implementación efectiva"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Bash","Systèmes basés sur Linux/Unix uniquement","Connaissances en scripting nécessaires pour une mise en œuvre efficace"],"de":["Benötigt Bash-Umgebung","Nur Linux/Unix-basierte Systeme","Skriptkenntnisse erforderlich für eine effektive Implementierung"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Bash","Sistemas baseados em Linux/Unix apenas","Conhecimento de script necessário para implementação eficaz"],"ru":["Требуется среда Bash","Только системы на основе Linux/Unix","Необходимо знание скриптов для эффективной реализации"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Bash","نظم مبنية على Linux/Unix فقط","معلومات برمجية ضرورية للتنفيذ الفعال"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
