ypeScript para Agentes de IA","ru":"ts-agent-sdk: Генератор SDK для TypeScript-агентов ИИ","ar":"ts-agent-sdk: مولد SDKs ناشئة للوكلاء الذكيين","en":"ts-agent-sdk"},"description":{"zh":"ts-agent-sdk是一种技能，生成TypeScript SDK，允许AI代理与Web应用程序交互。它简化了JSON-RPC curl命令，提供了清晰的函数调用","ja":"ts-agent-sdkは、AIエージェントがWebアプリケーションと交互作用できるTypeScript SDKを生成するスキルです。JSON-RPC curlコマンドを簡素化し、クリーンな関数呼び出しを提供します","ko":"ts-agent-sdk는 AI 에이전트가 웹 애플리케이션과 상호 작용할 수 있는 TypeScript SDK를 생성하는 스킬입니다. JSON-RPC curl 명령을 단순화하고 깨끗한 함수 호출을 제공합니다","es":"El SDK de TypeScript para agentes de IA permite interactuar con aplicaciones web de manera sencilla y eficiente","fr":"Le SDK TypeScript pour les agents d''IA permet d''interagir avec des applications web de manière simple et efficace","de":"Das TypeScript-SDK für KI-Agents ermöglicht eine einfache und effiziente Interaktion mit Webanwendungen","pt":"O ts-agent-sdk gera SDKs TypeScript tipados para permitir que agentes de IA interajam com aplicações web via servidores MCP. Ele substitui comandos JSON-RPC ...","ru":"Ts-agent-sdk генерирует типизированные SDK для TypeScript, позволяя агентам ИИ взаимодействовать с веб-приложениями через серверы MCP. Он заменяет громоздкие...","ar":"يولد ts-agent-sdk SDKs ناشئة مكتوبة بلغة TypeScript لمكتبات الوكلاء الذكيين للتفاعل مع تطبيقات الويب عبر خوادم MCP. 그는 يحل محل أوامر JSON-RPC المعقدة بإجراءا...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["生成TypeScript SDK","简化JSON-RPC curl命令","提供清晰的函数调用","支持AI代理与Web应用程序的交互","包含核心SDK模板文件"],"ja":["TypeScript SDKの生成","JSON-RPC curlコマンドの簡素化","クリーンな関数呼び出しの提供","AIエージェントとWebアプリケーションの間の相互作用のサポート","コアSDKテンプレートファイルの包含"],"ko":["TypeScript SDK 생성","JSON-RPC curl 명령 단순화","깨끗한 함수 호출 제공","AI 에이전트와 웹 애플리케이션 간의 상호 작용 지원","코어 SDK 템플릿 파일 포함"],"es":["Generación de SDKs de TypeScript tipados","Interacción con aplicaciones web a través de servidores MCP","Reemplazo de comandos JSON-RPC verbosos","Llamadas a funciones limpias y eficientes","Compatibilidad con Claude Code y otros agentes de IA","Plantillas de SDK personalizables"],"fr":["Génération de SDK TypeScript typés","Interaction avec des applications web via des serveurs MCP","Remplacement de commandes JSON-RPC verbeuses","Appels de fonctions propres et efficaces","Compatibilité avec Claude Code et d''autres agents d''IA","Modèles de SDK personnalisables"],"de":["Erzeugung typisierter TypeScript-SDKs","Interaktion mit Webanwendungen über MCP-Server","Ersetzen von verbose JSON-RPC-Befehlen","Sauber und effiziente Funktionsaufrufe","Kompatibilität mit Claude Code und anderen KI-Agents","Anpassbare SDK-Vorlagen"],"pt":["Geração de SDKs TypeScript personalizados","Interação com aplicações web via servidores MCP","Substituição de comandos JSON-RPC verbosos por chamadas de funções limpas","Modelos de SDK pré-concebidos para simplificar o desenvolvimento","Suporte a agentes de IA, como Claude Code"],"ru":["Генерация индивидуальных SDK для TypeScript","Взаимодействие с веб-приложениями через серверы MCP","Замена громоздких команд JSON-RPC чистыми вызовами функций","Предварительно разработанные шаблоны SDK для упрощения разработки","Поддержка агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code"],"ar":["مولد SDKs ناشئة مخصصة","التفاعل مع تطبيقات الويب عبر خوادم MCP","استبدال أوامر JSON-RPC المعقدة بإجراءات دالة نظيفة","قوالب SDK مسبقة التصميم لتسهيل التطوير","دعم الوكلاء الذكيين، مثل Claude Code"]},"keywords":{"zh":["ts-agent-sdk","TypeScript SDK","AI代理","Web应用程序","JSON-RPC","curl命令","函数调用"],"ja":["ts-agent-sdk","TypeScript SDK","AIエージェント","Webアプリケーション","JSON-RPC","curlコマンド","関数呼び出し"],"ko":["ts-agent-sdk","TypeScript SDK","AI 에이전트","웹 애플리케이션","JSON-RPC","curl 명령","함수 호출"],"es":["SDK de TypeScript para agentes de IA","Interacción con aplicaciones web","Servidores MCP"," Claude Code","Desarrollo de software","TypeScript","Agentes de IA","Automatización de procesos","Integración de sistemas"],"fr":["SDK TypeScript pour les agents d''IA","Interaction avec des applications web","Serveurs MCP","Claude Code","Développement de logiciels","TypeScript","Agents d''IA","Automatisation de processus","Intégration de systèmes"],"de":["TypeScript-SDK für KI-Agents","Interaktion mit Webanwendungen","MCP-Server","Claude Code","Softwareentwicklung","TypeScript","KI-Agents","Prozessautomatisierung","Systemintegration"],"pt":["ts-agent-sdk","SDK TypeScript","agentes de IA","aplicações web","servidores MCP","desenvolvimento de software"," Claude Code"],"ru":["ts-agent-sdk","SDK для TypeScript","агенты ИИ","веб-приложения","серверы MCP","разработка программного обеспечения","Claude Code"],"ar":["ts-agent-sdk","SDK ناشئة","الوكلاء الذكيين","تطبيقات الويب","خوادم MCP","تطوير البرمجيات","Claude Code"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ts-agent-sdk","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# ts-agent-sdk\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill generates typed TypeScript SDKs that allow AI agents (primarily Claude Code) to interact with web applications via MCP servers. It replaces verbose JSON-RPC curl commands with clean function calls.\n\n## Template Location\n\nThe core SDK template files are bundled with this skill at:\n`templates/`\n\nCopy these files to the target project''s `scripts/sdk/` directory as a starting point:\n\n```bash\ncp -r ~/.claude/skills/ts-agent-sdk/templates/* ./scripts/sdk/\n```\n\n#","body":"# ts-agent-sdk\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill generates typed TypeScript SDKs that allow AI agents (primarily Claude Code) to interact with web applications via MCP servers. It replaces verbose JSON-RPC curl commands with clean function calls.\n\n## Template Location\n\nThe core SDK template files are bundled with this skill at:\n`templates/`\n\nCopy these files to the target project''s `scripts/sdk/` directory as a starting point:\n\n```bash\ncp -r ~/.claude/skills/ts-agent-sdk/templates/* ./scripts/sdk/\n```\n\n## SDK Generation Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Detect MCP Servers\n\nScan the project for MCP server modules:\n```\nsrc/server/modules/mcp*/server.ts\n```\n\nEach server.ts file contains tool definitions using the pattern:\n```typescript\nserver.tool(\n  ''tool_name'',\n  ''Tool description'',\n  zodInputSchema,\n  async (params) => { ... }\n)\n```\n\n### Step 2: Extract Tool Definitions\n\nFor each tool, extract:\n1. **name**: The tool identifier (e.g., ''create_document'')\n2. **description**: Tool description for JSDoc\n3. **inputSchema**: Zod schema defining input parameters\n4. **endpoint**: The MCP endpoint path (e.g., ''/api/mcp-docs/message'')\n\n### Step 3: Generate TypeScript Interfaces\n\nConvert Zod schemas to TypeScript interfaces:\n\n```typescript\n// From: z.object({ name: z.string(), email: z.string().email() })\n// To:\nexport interface CreateEnquiryInput {\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n}\n```\n\n### Step 4: Generate Module Client\n\nCreate a client class with methods for each tool:\n\n```typescript\n// scripts/sdk/docs/client.ts\nimport { MCPClient, defaultClient } from ''../client'';\nimport type { CreateDocumentInput, CreateDocumentOutput } from ''./types'';\n\nconst ENDPOINT = ''/api/mcp-docs/message'';\n\nexport class DocsClient {\n  private mcp: MCPClient;\n\n  constructor(client?: MCPClient) {\n    this.mcp = client || defaultClient;\n  }\n\n  async createDocument(input: CreateDocumentInput): Promise<CreateDocumentOutput> {\n    return this.mcp.callTool(ENDPOINT, ''create_document'', input);\n  }\n\n  async listDocuments(input: ListDocumentsInput): Promise<ListDocumentsOutput> {\n    return this.mcp.callTool(ENDPOINT, ''list_documents'', input);\n  }\n\n  // ... one method per tool\n}\n\nexport const docs = new DocsClient();\n```\n\n### Step 5: Generate Example Scripts\n\nCreate runnable examples in `scripts/sdk/examples/`:\n\n```typescript\n#!/usr/bin/env npx tsx\n// scripts/sdk/examples/create-doc.ts\nimport { docs } from ''../'';\n\nasync function main() {\n  const result = await docs.createDocument({\n    spaceId: ''wiki'',\n    title: ''Getting Started'',\n    content: ''# Welcome\\n\\nThis is the intro.'',\n  });\n\n  console.log(`Created document: ${result.document.id}`);\n}\n\nmain().catch(console.error);\n```\n\n### Step 6: Update Index Exports\n\nAdd module exports to `scripts/sdk/index.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nexport { docs } from ''./docs'';\nexport { enquiries } from ''./enquiries'';\n```\n\n## Output Structure\n\n```\nproject/\n└── scripts/sdk/\n    ├── index.ts           # Main exports\n    ├── config.ts          # Environment config\n    ├── errors.ts          # Error classes\n    ├── client.ts          # MCP client\n    │\n    ├── docs/              # Generated module\n    │   ├── types.ts       # TypeScript interfaces\n    │   ├── client.ts      # Typed methods\n    │   └── index.ts       # Module exports\n    │\n    ├── enquiries/         # Another module\n    │   ├── types.ts\n    │   ├── client.ts\n    │   └── index.ts\n    │\n    └── examples/          # Runnable scripts\n        ├── create-doc.ts\n        ├── list-spaces.ts\n        └── create-enquiry.ts\n```\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nThe SDK uses these environment variables:\n\n| Variable | Description | Default |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| `SDK_MODE` | Execution mode: ''local'', ''remote'', ''auto'' | ''auto'' |\n| `SDK_BASE_URL` | Target Worker URL | http://localhost:8787 |\n| `SDK_API_TOKEN` | Bearer token for auth | (none) |\n\n## Execution\n\nRun generated scripts with:\n```bash\nSDK_API_TOKEN=\"your-token\" SDK_BASE_URL=\"https://app.workers.dev\" npx tsx scripts/sdk/examples/create-doc.ts\n```\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n- **Module names**: Lowercase, from MCP server name (e.g., ''mcp-docs'' → ''docs'')\n- **Method names**: camelCase from tool name (e.g., ''create_document'' → ''createDocument'')\n- **Type names**: PascalCase (e.g., ''CreateDocumentInput'', ''CreateDocumentOutput'')\n\n## Error Handling\n\nThe SDK provides typed errors:\n\n- `AuthError` - 401, invalid token\n- `ValidationError` - Invalid input\n- `NotFoundError` - Resource not found\n- `RateLimitError` - 429, too many requests\n- `MCPError` - MCP protocol errors\n- `NetworkError` - Connection failures\n\n## Regeneration\n\nWhen MCP tools change, regenerate the SDK:\n1. Re-scan `src/server/modules/mcp*/server.ts`\n2. Update types.ts with new/changed schemas\n3. Update client.ts with new/changed methods\n4. Preserve any custom code in examples/\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:52:48.762Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Claude Code agents seeking streamlined interactions with web applications via MCP servers","zh":"适用于寻求通过MCP服务器与Web应用程序进行流线化交互的Claude Code代理","ja":"MCPサーバーを介したWebアプリケーションとのストリームライン化された相互作用を求めるClaude Codeエージェントに最適","ko":"MCP 서버를 통해 웹 애플리케이션과 상호 작용을 간소화하려는 Claude Code 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de Claude Code que buscan interacciones optimizadas con aplicaciones web a través de servidores MCP","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Claude Code cherchant à optimiser les interactions avec les applications web via les serveurs MCP","de":"Ideal für Claude-Code-Agents, die optimierte Interaktionen mit Webanwendungen über MCP-Server suchen","pt":"Ideal para agentes Claude Code que buscam interações simplificadas com aplicações web via servidores MCP","ru":"Идеально для агентов Claude Code, которым необходимы оптимизированные взаимодействия с веб-приложениями через серверы MCP","ar":"مثالي لعميل كلود كود الذي يبحث عن تفاعلات مبسطة مع تطبيقات الويب من خلال خوادم MCP"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to replace verbose JSON-RPC curl commands with clean function calls, leveraging typed TypeScript SDKs for seamless integration, and utilizing MCP servers for efficient communication","zh":"赋予代理以清晰的函数调用替换冗长的JSON-RPC curl命令的能力，利用类型化的TypeScript SDK进行无缝集成，并利用MCP服务器进行高效的通信","ja":"JSON-RPC curlコマンドをクリーンな関数呼び出しに置き換えるエージェントを可能にし、TypeScript SDKを使用してシームレスに統合し、MCPサーバーを使用して効率的な通信を実現する","ko":"에이전트가冗长한 JSON-RPC curl 명령어를 깨끗한 함수 호출로 대체할 수 있도록 하며, 유형화된 TypeScript SDK를 사용하여无缝한 통합을 제공하고, MCP 서버를 사용하여 효율적인 통신을 thực現","es":"Permite a los agentes reemplazar los verbosos comandos JSON-RPC curl con llamadas a funciones limpias, aprovechando los SDK de TypeScript tipados para una integración sin problemas y utilizando servidores MCP para una comunicación eficiente","fr":"Permet aux agents de remplacer les commandes JSON-RPC curl verbeuses par des appels de fonctions propres, en exploitant les SDK TypeScript typés pour une intégration transparente et en utilisant les serveurs MCP pour une communication efficace","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, die umfangreichen JSON-RPC-Curl-Befehle durch saubere Funktionsaufrufe zu ersetzen, indem sie auf typisierte TypeScript-SDKs für eine nahtlose Integration zurückgreifen und MCP-Server für eine effiziente Kommunikation nutzen","pt":"Habilita agentes a substituir comandos JSON-RPC curl verbosos por chamadas de função limpas, aproveitando SDKs TypeScript tipados para integração transparente e utilizando servidores MCP para comunicação eficiente","ru":"Позволяет агентам заменять многословные команды JSON-RPC curl чистыми вызовами функций, используя типизированные SDK TypeScript для бесшовной интеграции и серверы MCP для эффективного обмена информацией","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية استبدال أوامر JSON-RPC curl冗长 بالدعوات الوظيفية النظيفة، وتفعيل SDKs TypeScript المُقسمة لنظام الإدماج الخفي، وتشغيل خوادم MCP للاتصال الفعال"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating typed TypeScript SDKs for web application integration","Replacing JSON-RPC curl commands with functional calls","Interacting with MCP servers for AI agent communication"],"zh":["为Web应用程序集成生成类型化的TypeScript SDK","用函数调用替换JSON-RPC curl命令","与MCP服务器交互以实现AI代理通信"],"ja":["Webアプリケーション統合のための型付けTypeScript SDKの生成","JSON-RPC curlコマンドを関数呼び出しに置き換える","MCPサーバーとの相互作用によるAIエージェント通信"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션 통합을 위한 유형화된 TypeScript SDK 생성","JSON-RPC curl 명령어를 함수 호출로 대체","MCP 서버와의 상호 작용을 통한 AI 에이전트 통신"],"es":["Generación de SDK de TypeScript tipados para la integración de aplicaciones web","Reemplazo de comandos JSON-RPC curl con llamadas funcionales","Interacción con servidores MCP para la comunicación de agentes de inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["Génération de SDK TypeScript typés pour l''intégration d''applications web","Remplacement des commandes JSON-RPC curl par des appels fonctionnels","Interaction avec les serveurs MCP pour la communication des agents d''intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Generierung von typisierten TypeScript-SDKs für die Integration von Webanwendungen","Ersetzen von JSON-RPC-Curl-Befehlen durch Funktionsaufrufe","Interaktion mit MCP-Servern für die Kommunikation von KI-Agents"],"pt":["Geração de SDKs TypeScript tipados para integração de aplicações web","Substituição de comandos JSON-RPC curl por chamadas funcionais","Interação com servidores MCP para comunicação de agente de IA"],"ru":["Генерация типизированных SDK TypeScript для интеграции веб-приложений","Замена команд JSON-RPC curl функциональными вызовами","Взаимодействие с серверами MCP для коммуникации агентов ИИ"],"ar":["توليد SDKs TypeScript المُقسمة لإدماج تطبيقات الويب","استبدال أوامر JSON-RPC curl بالدعوات الوظيفية","التفاعل مع خوادم MCP للاتصال بعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Primarily designed for Claude Code agents","Requires MCP server setup","TypeScript expertise recommended for customization"],"zh":["主要设计用于Claude Code代理","需要MCP服务器设置","建议具有TypeScript专业知识以进行自定义"],"ja":["主にClaude Codeエージェントのために設計","MCPサーバーの設定が必要","カスタマイズのためのTypeScriptの専門知識が推奨"],"ko":["주로 Claude Code 에이전트를 위해 설계","MCP 서버 설정 필요","사용자 지정을 위해 TypeScript 전문 지식이 권장"],"es":["Diseñado principalmente para agentes de Claude Code","Requiere configuración de servidor MCP","Se recomienda experiencia en TypeScript para la personalización"],"fr":["Conçu principalement pour les agents Claude Code","Nécessite une configuration de serveur MCP","Une expérience de TypeScript est recommandée pour la personnalisation"],"de":["Hauptsächlich für Claude-Code-Agents konzipiert","Benötigt MCP-Server-Konfiguration","TypeScript-Erfahrung wird für die Anpassung empfohlen"],"pt":["Primariamente projetado para agentes Claude Code","Requer configuração do servidor MCP","Conhecimento de TypeScript recomendado para personalização"],"ru":["В основном предназначен для агентов Claude Code","Требует настройки сервера MCP","Рекомендуется опыт работы с TypeScript для настройки"],"ar":["مصمم في المقام الأول لعميل كلود كود","يتطلب إعداد خادم MCP","م kiếnةخبرة في TypeScript لمتطلبات التخصيص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/skill-judge', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'skill-judge', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z', '2026-02-18T13:53:26.472Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/skill-judge","name":"skill-judge","description":{"zh":"Skill Judge是一种评估AI技能的机制，能够减少开发时间和成本，提高AI模型的效率。它可以帮助开发者快速评估和改进AI技能","ja":"Skill JudgeはAIスキルを評価するメカニズムであり、開発時間とコストを削減し、AIモデルの効率を向上させることができます。開発者がAIスキルを迅速に評価して改善するのに役立ちます","ko":"Skill Judge는 AI 스킬을 평가하는 메커니즘으로 개발 시간과 비용을 줄이고 AI 모델의 효율성을 향상시킬 수 있습니다. 개발자가 AI 스킬을迅速하게 평가하고 개선하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Skill Judge es un mecanismo de externalización de conocimientos que evalúa habilidades de agentes AI contra especificaciones oficiales.","fr":"Skill Judge est un mécanisme d''externalisation des connaissances qui évalue les compétences des agents IA par rapport aux spécifications officielles.","de":"Skill Judge ist ein Mechanismus zur Externalisierung von Wissen, der die Fähigkeiten von KI-Agenten anhand offizieller Spezifikationen bewertet.","pt":"O Julgador de Habilidades é uma ferramenta para avaliar habilidades de agentes contra especificações oficiais, permitindo a externalização do conhecimento","ru":"Судья Навыков - это инструмент для оценки навыков агентов по официальным спецификациям, позволяющий внешнеизировать знания","ar":"قاضي المهارات هو أداة لتقييم مهارات الوكيل مقابل المواصفات الرسمية، مما يسمح بتحويل المعرفة إلى شكل خارجي","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Skill Judge: 评估AI技能","ja":"Skill Judge: AIスキルの評価","ko":"Skill Judge: AI 스킬 평가","es":"Skill Judge: Evaluación de habilidades de agentes AI","fr":"Skill Judge : Évaluation des compétences des agents IA","de":"Skill Judge: Bewertung von KI-Agentenfähigkeiten","pt":"Julgador de Habilidades: Avalie Habilidades de Agentes","ru":"Судья Навыков: Оцените Навыки Агентов","ar":"قاضي المهارات: تقييم مهارات الوكيل","en":"skill-judge"},"description":{"zh":"Skill Judge是一种评估AI技能的机制，能够减少开发时间和成本，提高AI模型的效率。它可以帮助开发者快速评估和改进AI技能","ja":"Skill JudgeはAIスキルを評価するメカニズムであり、開発時間とコストを削減し、AIモデルの効率を向上させることができます。開発者がAIスキルを迅速に評価して改善するのに役立ちます","ko":"Skill Judge는 AI 스킬을 평가하는 메커니즘으로 개발 시간과 비용을 줄이고 AI 모델의 효율성을 향상시킬 수 있습니다. 개발자가 AI 스킬을迅速하게 평가하고 개선하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Skill Judge es un mecanismo de externalización de conocimientos que evalúa habilidades de agentes AI contra especificaciones oficiales.","fr":"Skill Judge est un mécanisme d''externalisation des connaissances qui évalue les compétences des agents IA par rapport aux spécifications officielles.","de":"Skill Judge ist ein Mechanismus zur Externalisierung von Wissen, der die Fähigkeiten von KI-Agenten anhand offizieller Spezifikationen bewertet.","pt":"O Julgador de Habilidades é uma ferramenta para avaliar habilidades de agentes contra especificações oficiais, permitindo a externalização do conhecimento","ru":"Судья Навыков - это инструмент для оценки навыков агентов по официальным спецификациям, позволяющий внешнеизировать знания","ar":"قاضي المهارات هو أداة لتقييم مهارات الوكيل مقابل المواصفات الرسمية، مما يسمح بتحويل المعرفة إلى شكل خارجي","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["评估AI技能","减少开发时间和成本","提高AI模型的效率","支持17+官方示例","快速评估和改进AI技能"],"ja":["AIスキルの評価","開発時間とコストの削減","AIモデルの効率の向上","17+の公式例のサポート","AIスキルの迅速な評価と改善"],"ko":["AI 스킬 평가","개발 시간과 비용의 감소","AI 모델의 효율성 향상","17+ 공식 예제 지원","AI 스킬의迅速한 평가와 개선"],"es":["Evaluación de habilidades de agentes AI","Comparación con especificaciones oficiales","Reducción de costos en el desarrollo de IA","Mejora de la eficiencia en la enseñanza de nuevas capacidades","Integración con 17+ ejemplos oficiales"],"fr":["Évaluation des compétences des agents IA","Comparaison avec les spécifications officielles","Réduction des coûts dans le développement de l''IA","Amélioration de l''efficacité dans l''enseignement de nouvelles capacités","Intégration avec 17+ exemples officiels"],"de":["Bewertung von KI-Agentenfähigkeiten","Vergleich mit offiziellen Spezifikationen","Kostenreduzierung bei der Entwicklung von KI","Verbesserung der Effizienz bei der Vermittlung neuer Fähigkeiten","Integration mit 17+ offiziellen Beispielen"],"pt":["Avaliação de habilidades de agentes","Compatibilidade com especificações oficiais","Externalização do conhecimento","Redução do custo e tempo de treinamento","Integração com exemplos oficiais"],"ru":["Оценка навыков агентов","Совместимость с официальными спецификациями","Внешнеизирование знаний","Сокращение стоимости и времени обучения","Интеграция с официальными примерами"],"ar":["تقييم مهارات الوكيل","التوافق مع المواصفات الرسمية","تحويل المعرفة إلى شكل خارجي","تقليل التكلفة والوقت التدريبي","التكامل مع الأمثلة الرسمية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI技能评估","知识外部化","AI模型效率","开发时间减少","开发成本减少","AI技能改进"],"ja":["AIスキルの評価","知識の外部化","AIモデルの効率","開発時間の削減","開発コストの削減","AIスキルの改善"],"ko":["AI 스킬 평가","지식 외부화","AI 모델 효율성","개발 시간 감소","개발 비용 감소","AI 스킬 개선"],"es":["evaluación de habilidades de agentes AI","desarrollo de IA","externalización de conocimientos","mejora de la eficiencia","reducción de costos","agentes AI","IA","inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["évaluation des compétences des agents IA","développement de l''IA","externalisation des connaissances","amélioration de l''efficacité","réduction des coûts","agents IA","IA","intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Bewertung von KI-Agentenfähigkeiten","Entwicklung von KI","Externalisierung von Wissen","Verbesserung der Effizienz","Kostenreduzierung","KI-Agenten","KI","künstliche Intelligenz"],"pt":["julgador de habilidades","avaliação de habilidades","especificações oficiais","externalização do conhecimento","treinamento de agentes","desenvolvimento de habilidades"],"ru":["судья навыков","оценка навыков","официальные спецификации","внешнеизирование знаний","обучение агентов","развитие навыков"],"ar":["قاضي المهارات","تقييم مهارات","المواصفات الرسمية","تحويل المعرفة","تدريب الوكيل","تطوير المهارات"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-judge","description":"Evaluate Agent Skill design quality against official specifications and best practices. Use when reviewing, auditing, or improving SKILL.md files and skill packages. Provides multi-dimensional scoring and actionable improvement suggestions.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Judge\n\nEvaluate Agent Skills against official specifications and patterns derived from 17+ official examples.\n\n---\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n### What is a Skill?\n\nA Skill is NOT a tutorial. A Skill is a **knowledge externalization mechanism**.\n\nTraditional AI knowledge is locked in model parameters. To teach new capabilities:\n```\nTraditional: Collect data → GPU cluster → Train → Deploy new version\nCost: $10,000 - $1,000,000+\nTimeline: Weeks to months\n```\n\nSkills change this:\n```\nSkill: Edit S","body":"# Skill Judge\n\nEvaluate Agent Skills against official specifications and patterns derived from 17+ official examples.\n\n---\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n### What is a Skill?\n\nA Skill is NOT a tutorial. A Skill is a **knowledge externalization mechanism**.\n\nTraditional AI knowledge is locked in model parameters. To teach new capabilities:\n```\nTraditional: Collect data → GPU cluster → Train → Deploy new version\nCost: $10,000 - $1,000,000+\nTimeline: Weeks to months\n```\n\nSkills change this:\n```\nSkill: Edit SKILL.md → Save → Takes effect on next invocation\nCost: $0\nTimeline: Instant\n```\n\nThis is the paradigm shift from \"training AI\" to \"educating AI\" — like a hot-swappable LoRA adapter that requires no training. You edit a Markdown file in natural language, and the model''s behavior changes.\n\n### The Core Formula\n\n> **Good Skill = Expert-only Knowledge − What Claude Already Knows**\n\nA Skill''s value is measured by its **knowledge delta** — the gap between what it provides and what the model already knows.\n\n- **Expert-only knowledge**: Decision trees, trade-offs, edge cases, anti-patterns, domain-specific thinking frameworks — things that take years of experience to accumulate\n- **What Claude already knows**: Basic concepts, standard library usage, common programming patterns, general best practices\n\nWhen a Skill explains \"what is PDF\" or \"how to write a for-loop\", it''s compressing knowledge Claude already has. This is **token waste** — context window is a public resource shared with system prompts, conversation history, other Skills, and user requests.\n\n### Tool vs Skill\n\n| Concept | Essence | Function | Example |\n|---------|---------|----------|---------|\n| **Tool** | What model CAN do | Execute actions | bash, read_file, write_file, WebSearch |\n| **Skill** | What model KNOWS how to do | Guide decisions | PDF processing, MCP building, frontend design |\n\nTools define capability boundaries — without bash tool, model can''t execute commands.\nSkills inject knowledge — without frontend-design Skill, model produces generic UI.\n\n**The equation**:\n```\nGeneral Agent + Excellent Skill = Domain Expert Agent\n```\n\nSame Claude model, different Skills loaded, becomes different experts.\n\n### Three Types of Knowledge in Skills\n\nWhen evaluating, categorize each section:\n\n| Type | Definition | Treatment |\n|------|------------|-----------|\n| **Expert** | Claude genuinely doesn''t know this | Must keep — this is the Skill''s value |\n| **Activation** | Claude knows but may not think of | Keep if brief — serves as reminder |\n| **Redundant** | Claude definitely knows this | Should delete — wastes tokens |\n\nThe art of Skill design is maximizing Expert content, using Activation sparingly, and eliminating Redundant ruthlessly.\n\n---\n\n## Evaluation Dimensions (120 points total)\n\n### D1: Knowledge Delta (20 points) — THE CORE DIMENSION\n\nThe most important dimension. Does the Skill add genuine expert knowledge?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-5 | Explains basics Claude knows (what is X, how to write code, standard library tutorials) |\n| 6-10 | Mixed: some expert knowledge diluted by obvious content |\n| 11-15 | Mostly expert knowledge with minimal redundancy |\n| 16-20 | Pure knowledge delta — every paragraph earns its tokens |\n\n**Red flags** (instant score ≤5):\n- \"What is [basic concept]\" sections\n- Step-by-step tutorials for standard operations\n- Explaining how to use common libraries\n- Generic best practices (\"write clean code\", \"handle errors\")\n- Definitions of industry-standard terms\n\n**Green flags** (indicators of high knowledge delta):\n- Decision trees for non-obvious choices (\"when X fails, try Y because Z\")\n- Trade-offs only an expert would know (\"A is faster but B handles edge case C\")\n- Edge cases from real-world experience\n- \"NEVER do X because [non-obvious reason]\"\n- Domain-specific thinking frameworks\n\n**Evaluation questions**:\n1. For each section, ask: \"Does Claude already know this?\"\n2. If explaining something, ask: \"Is this explaining TO Claude or FOR Claude?\"\n3. Count paragraphs that are Expert vs Activation vs Redundant\n\n---\n\n### D2: Mindset + Appropriate Procedures (15 points)\n\nDoes the Skill transfer expert **thinking patterns** along with **necessary domain-specific procedures**?\n\nThe difference between experts and novices isn''t \"knowing how to operate\" — it''s \"how to think about the problem.\" But thinking patterns alone aren''t enough when Claude lacks domain-specific procedural knowledge.\n\n**Key distinction**:\n| Type | Example | Value |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| **Thinking patterns** | \"Before designing, ask: What makes this memorable?\" | High — shapes decision-making |\n| **Domain-specific procedures** | \"OOXML workflow: unpack → edit XML → validate → pack\" | High — Claude may not know this |\n| **Generic procedures** | \"Step 1: Open file, Step 2: Edit, Step 3: Save\" | Low — Claude already knows |\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-3 | Only generic procedures Claude already knows |\n| 4-7 | Has domain procedures but lacks thinking frameworks |\n| 8-11 | Good balance: thinking patterns + domain-specific workflows |\n| 12-15 | Expert-level: shapes thinking AND provides procedures Claude wouldn''t know |\n\n**What counts as valuable procedures**:\n- Workflows Claude hasn''t been trained on (new tools, proprietary systems)\n- Correct ordering that''s non-obvious (e.g., \"validate BEFORE packing, not after\")\n- Critical steps that are easy to miss (e.g., \"MUST recalculate formulas after editing\")\n- Domain-specific sequences (e.g., MCP server''s 4-phase development process)\n\n**What counts as redundant procedures**:\n- Generic file operations (open, read, write, save)\n- Standard programming patterns (loops, conditionals, error handling)\n- Common library usage that''s well-documented\n\n**Expert thinking patterns look like**:\n```markdown\nBefore [action], ask yourself:\n- **Purpose**: What problem does this solve? Who uses it?\n- **Constraints**: What are the hidden requirements?\n- **Differentiation**: What makes this solution memorable?\n```\n\n**Valuable domain procedures look like**:\n```markdown\n### Redlining Workflow (Claude wouldn''t know this sequence)\n1. Convert to markdown: `pandoc --track-changes=all`\n2. Map text to XML: grep for text in document.xml\n3. Implement changes in batches of 3-10\n4. Pack and verify: check ALL changes were applied\n```\n\n**Redundant generic procedures look like**:\n```markdown\nStep 1: Open the file\nStep 2: Find the section\nStep 3: Make the change\nStep 4: Save and test\n```\n\n**The test**:\n1. Does it tell Claude WHAT to think about? (thinking patterns)\n2. Does it tell Claude HOW to do things it wouldn''t know? (domain procedures)\n\nA good Skill provides both when needed.\n\n---\n\n### D3: Anti-Pattern Quality (15 points)\n\nDoes the Skill have effective NEVER lists?\n\n**Why this matters**: Half of expert knowledge is knowing what NOT to do. A senior designer sees purple gradient on white background and instinctively cringes — \"too AI-generated.\" This intuition for \"what absolutely not to do\" comes from stepping on countless landmines.\n\nClaude hasn''t stepped on these landmines. It doesn''t know Inter font is overused, doesn''t know purple gradients are the signature of AI-generated content. Good Skills must explicitly state these \"absolute don''ts.\"\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-3 | No anti-patterns mentioned |\n| 4-7 | Generic warnings (\"avoid errors\", \"be careful\", \"consider edge cases\") |\n| 8-11 | Specific NEVER list with some reasoning |\n| 12-15 | Expert-grade anti-patterns with WHY — things only experience teaches |\n\n**Expert anti-patterns** (specific + reason):\n```markdown\nNEVER use generic AI-generated aesthetics like:\n- Overused font families (Inter, Roboto, Arial)\n- Cliched color schemes (particularly purple gradients on white backgrounds)\n- Predictable layouts and component patterns\n- Default border-radius on everything\n```\n\n**Weak anti-patterns** (vague, no reasoning):\n```markdown\nAvoid making mistakes.\nBe careful with edge cases.\nDon''t write bad code.\n```\n\n**The test**: Would an expert read the anti-pattern list and say \"yes, I learned this the hard way\"? Or would they say \"this is obvious to everyone\"?\n\n---\n\n### D4: Specification Compliance — Especially Description (15 points)\n\nDoes the Skill follow official format requirements? **Special focus on description quality.**\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-5 | Missing frontmatter or invalid format |\n| 6-10 | Has frontmatter but description is vague or incomplete |\n| 11-13 | Valid frontmatter, description has WHAT but weak on WHEN |\n| 14-15 | Perfect: comprehensive description with WHAT, WHEN, and trigger keywords |\n\n**Frontmatter requirements**:\n- `name`: lowercase, alphanumeric + hyphens only, ≤64 characters\n- `description`: **THE MOST CRITICAL FIELD** — determines if skill gets used at all\n\n---\n\n**Why description is THE MOST IMPORTANT field**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  SKILL ACTIVATION FLOW                                              │\n│                                                                     │\n│  User Request → Agent sees ALL skill descriptions → Decides which  │\n│                 (only descriptions, not bodies!)     to activate    │\n│                                                                     │\n│  If description doesn''t match → Skill NEVER gets loaded            │\n│  If description is vague → Skill might not trigger when it should  │\n│  If description lacks keywords → Skill is invisible to the Agent   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**The brutal truth**: A Skill with perfect content but poor description is **useless** — it will never be activated. The description is the **only chance** to tell the Agent \"use me in these situations.\"\n\n---\n\n**Description must answer THREE questions**:\n\n1. **WHAT**: What does this Skill do? (functionality)\n2. **WHEN**: In what situations should it be used? (trigger scenarios)\n3. **KEYWORDS**: What terms should trigger this Skill? (searchable terms)\n\n**Excellent description** (all three elements):\n```yaml\ndescription: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support\nfor tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction.\nWhen Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for:\n(1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content,\n(3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n```\n\nAnalysis:\n- WHAT: creation, editing, analysis, tracked changes, comments\n- WHEN: \"When Claude needs to work with... for: (1)... (2)... (3)...\"\n- KEYWORDS: .docx files, tracked changes, professional documents\n\n**Poor description** (missing elements):\n```yaml\ndescription: \"处理文档相关功能\"\n```\n\nProblems:\n- WHAT: vague (\"文档相关功能\" — what specifically?)\n- WHEN: missing (when should Agent use this?)\n- KEYWORDS: missing (no \".docx\", no specific scenarios)\n\n**Another poor example**:\n```yaml\ndescription: \"A helpful skill for various tasks\"\n```\n\nThis is useless — Agent has no idea when to activate it.\n\n---\n\n**Description quality checklist**:\n- [ ] Lists specific capabilities (not just \"helps with X\")\n- [ ] Includes explicit trigger scenarios (\"Use when...\", \"When user asks for...\")\n- [ ] Contains searchable keywords (file extensions, domain terms, action verbs)\n- [ ] Specific enough that Agent knows EXACTLY when to use it\n- [ ] Includes scenarios where this skill MUST be used (not just \"can be used\")\n\n---\n\n### D5: Progressive Disclosure (15 points)\n\nDoes the Skill implement proper content layering?\n\nSkill loading has three layers:\n```\nLayer 1: Metadata (always in memory)\n         Only name + description\n         ~100 tokens per skill\n\nLayer 2: SKILL.md Body (loaded after triggering)\n         Detailed guidelines, code examples, decision trees\n         Ideal: < 500 lines\n\nLayer 3: Resources (loaded on demand)\n         scripts/, references/, assets/\n         No limit\n```\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-5 | Everything dumped in SKILL.md (>500 lines, no structure) |\n| 6-10 | Has references but unclear when to load them |\n| 11-13 | Good layering with MANDATORY triggers present |\n| 14-15 | Perfect: decision trees + explicit triggers + \"Do NOT Load\" guidance |\n\n**For Skills WITH references directory**, check Loading Trigger Quality:\n\n| Trigger Quality | Characteristics |\n|-----------------|-----------------|\n| Poor | References listed at end, no loading guidance |\n| Mediocre | Some triggers but not embedded in workflow |\n| Good | MANDATORY triggers in workflow steps |\n| Excellent | Scenario detection + conditional triggers + \"Do NOT Load\" |\n\n**The loading problem**:\n```\nLoading too little ◄─────────────────────────────────► Loading too much\n- References sit unused                    - Wastes context space\n- Agent doesn''t know when to load          - Irrelevant info dilutes key content\n- Knowledge is there but never accessed    - Unnecessary token overhead\n```\n\n**Good loading trigger** (embedded in workflow):\n```markdown\n### Creating New Document\n\n**MANDATORY - READ ENTIRE FILE**: Before proceeding, you MUST read\n[`docx-js.md`](docx-js.md) (~500 lines) completely from start to finish.\n**NEVER set any range limits when reading this file.**\n\n**Do NOT load** `ooxml.md` or `redlining.md` for this task.\n```\n\n**Bad loading trigger** (just listed):\n```markdown\n## References\n- docx-js.md - for creating documents\n- ooxml.md - for editing\n- redlining.md - for tracking changes\n```\n\n**For simple Skills** (no references, <100 lines): Score based on conciseness and self-containment.\n\n---\n\n### D6: Freedom Calibration (15 points)\n\nIs the level of specificity appropriate for the task''s fragility?\n\nDifferent tasks need different levels of constraint. This is about matching freedom to fragility.\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-5 | Severely mismatched (rigid scripts for creative tasks, vague for fragile ops) |\n| 6-10 | Partially appropriate, some mismatches |\n| 11-13 | Good calibration for most scenarios |\n| 14-15 | Perfect freedom calibration throughout |\n\n**The freedom spectrum**:\n\n| Task Type | Should Have | Why | Example Skill |\n|-----------|-------------|-----|---------------|\n| Creative/Design | High freedom | Multiple valid approaches, differentiation is value | frontend-design |\n| Code review | Medium freedom | Principles exist but judgment required | code-review |\n| File format operations | Low freedom | One wrong byte corrupts file, consistency critical | docx, xlsx, pdf |\n\n**High freedom** (text-based instructions):\n```markdown\nCommit to a BOLD aesthetic direction. Pick an extreme: brutally minimal,\nmaximalist chaos, retro-futuristic, organic natural...\n```\n\n**Medium freedom** (pseudocode or parameterized):\n```markdown\nReview priority:\n1. Security vulnerabilities (must fix)\n2. Logic errors (must fix)\n3. Performance issues (should fix)\n4. Maintainability (optional)\n```\n\n**Low freedom** (specific scripts, exact steps):\n```markdown\n**MANDATORY**: Use exact script in `scripts/create-doc.py`\nParameters: --title \"X\" --author \"Y\"\nDo NOT modify the script.\n```\n\n**The test**: Ask \"if Agent makes a mistake, what''s the consequence?\"\n- High consequence → Low freedom\n- Low consequence → High freedom\n\n---\n\n### D7: Pattern Recognition (10 points)\n\nDoes the Skill follow an established official pattern?\n\nThrough analyzing 17 official Skills, we identified 5 main design patterns:\n\n| Pattern | ~Lines | Key Characteristics | Example | When to Use |\n|---------|--------|---------------------|---------|-------------|\n| **Mindset** | ~50 | Thinking > technique, strong NEVER list, high freedom | frontend-design | Creative tasks requiring taste |\n| **Navigation** | ~30 | Minimal SKILL.md, routes to sub-files | internal-comms | Multiple distinct scenarios |\n| **Philosophy** | ~150 | Two-step: Philosophy → Express, emphasizes craft | canvas-design | Art/creation requiring originality |\n| **Process** | ~200 | Phased workflow, checkpoints, medium freedom | mcp-builder | Complex multi-step projects |\n| **Tool** | ~300 | Decision trees, code examples, low freedom | docx, pdf, xlsx | Precise operations on specific formats |\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-3 | No recognizable pattern, chaotic structure |\n| 4-6 | Partially follows a pattern with significant deviations |\n| 7-8 | Clear pattern with minor deviations |\n| 9-10 | Masterful application of appropriate pattern |\n\n**Pattern selection guide**:\n\n| Your Task Characteristics | Recommended Pattern |\n|---------------------------|---------------------|\n| Needs taste and creativity | Mindset (~50 lines) |\n| Needs originality and craft quality | Philosophy (~150 lines) |\n| Has multiple distinct sub-scenarios | Navigation (~30 lines) |\n| Complex multi-step project | Process (~200 lines) |\n| Precise operations on specific format | Tool (~300 lines) |\n\n---\n\n### D8: Practical Usability (15 points)\n\nCan an Agent actually use this Skill effectively?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 0-5 | Confusing, incomplete, contradictory, or untested guidance |\n| 6-10 | Usable but with noticeable gaps |\n| 11-13 | Clear guidance for common cases |\n| 14-15 | Comprehensive coverage including edge cases and error handling |\n\n**Check for**:\n- **Decision trees**: For multi-path scenarios, is there clear guidance on which path to take?\n- **Code examples**: Do they actually work? Or are they pseudocode that breaks?\n- **Error handling**: What if the main approach fails? Are fallbacks provided?\n- **Edge cases**: Are unusual but realistic scenarios covered?\n- **Actionability**: Can Agent immediately act, or needs to figure things out?\n\n**Good usability** (decision tree + fallback):\n```markdown\n| Task | Primary Tool | Fallback | When to Use Fallback |\n|------|-------------|----------|----------------------|\n| Read text | pdftotext | PyMuPDF | Need layout info |\n| Extract tables | camelot-py | tabula-py | camelot fails |\n\n**Common issues**:\n- Scanned PDF: pdftotext returns blank → Use OCR first\n- Encrypted PDF: Permission error → Use PyMuPDF with password\n```\n\n**Poor usability** (vague):\n```markdown\nUse appropriate tools for PDF processing.\nHandle errors properly.\nConsider edge cases.\n```\n\n---\n\n## NEVER Do When Evaluating\n\n- **NEVER** give high scores just because it \"looks professional\" or is well-formatted\n- **NEVER** ignore token waste — every redundant paragraph should result in deduction\n- **NEVER** let length impress you — a 43-line Skill can outperform a 500-line Skill\n- **NEVER** skip mentally testing the decision trees — do they actually lead to correct choices?\n- **NEVER** forgive explaining basics with \"but it provides helpful context\"\n- **NEVER** overlook missing anti-patterns — if there''s no NEVER list, that''s a significant gap\n- **NEVER** assume all procedures are valuable — distinguish domain-specific from generic\n- **NEVER** undervalue the description field — poor description = skill never gets used\n- **NEVER** put \"when to use\" info only in the body — Agent only sees description before loading\n\n---\n\n## Evaluation Protocol\n\n### Step 1: First Pass — Knowledge Delta Scan\n\nRead SKILL.md completely and for each section ask:\n> \"Does Claude already know this?\"\n\nMark each section as:\n- **[E] Expert**: Claude genuinely doesn''t know this — value-add\n- **[A] Activation**: Claude knows but brief reminder is useful — acceptable\n- **[R] Redundant**: Claude definitely knows this — should be deleted\n\nCalculate rough ratio: E:A:R\n- Good Skill: >70% Expert, <20% Activation, <10% Redundant\n- Mediocre Skill: 40-70% Expert, high Activation\n- Bad Skill: <40% Expert, high Redundant\n\n### Step 2: Structure Analysis\n\n```\n[ ] Check frontmatter validity\n[ ] Count total lines in SKILL.md\n[ ] List all reference files and their sizes\n[ ] Identify which pattern the Skill follows\n[ ] Check for loading triggers (if references exist)\n```\n\n### Step 3: Score Each Dimension\n\nFor each of the 8 dimensions:\n1. Find specific evidence (quote relevant lines)\n2. Assign score with one-line justification\n3. Note specific improvements if score < max\n\n### Step 4: Calculate Total & Grade\n\n```\nTotal = D1 + D2 + D3 + D4 + D5 + D6 + D7 + D8\nMax = 120 points\n```\n\n**Grade Scale** (percentage-based):\n| Grade | Percentage | Meaning |\n|-------|------------|---------|\n| A | 90%+ (108+) | Excellent — production-ready expert Skill |\n| B | 80-89% (96-107) | Good — minor improvements needed |\n| C | 70-79% (84-95) | Adequate — clear improvement path |\n| D | 60-69% (72-83) | Below Average — significant issues |\n| F | <60% (<72) | Poor — needs fundamental redesign |\n\n### Step 5: Generate Report\n\n```markdown\n# Skill Evaluation Report: [Skill Name]\n\n## Summary\n- **Total Score**: X/120 (X%)\n- **Grade**: [A/B/C/D/F]\n- **Pattern**: [Mindset/Navigation/Philosophy/Process/Tool]\n- **Knowledge Ratio**: E:A:R = X:Y:Z\n- **Verdict**: [One sentence assessment]\n\n## Dimension Scores\n\n| Dimension | Score | Max | Notes |\n|-----------|-------|-----|-------|\n| D1: Knowledge Delta | X | 20 | |\n| D2: Mindset vs Mechanics | X | 15 | |\n| D3: Anti-Pattern Quality | X | 15 | |\n| D4: Specification Compliance | X | 15 | |\n| D5: Progressive Disclosure | X | 15 | |\n| D6: Freedom Calibration | X | 15 | |\n| D7: Pattern Recognition | X | 10 | |\n| D8: Practical Usability | X | 15 | |\n\n## Critical Issues\n[List must-fix problems that significantly impact the Skill''s effectiveness]\n\n## Top 3 Improvements\n1. [Highest impact improvement with specific guidance]\n2. [Second priority improvement]\n3. [Third priority improvement]\n\n## Detailed Analysis\n[For each dimension scoring below 80%, provide:\n- What''s missing or problematic\n- Specific examples from the Skill\n- Concrete suggestions for improvement]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Failure Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: The Tutorial\n```\nSymptom: Explains what PDF is, how Python works, basic library usage\nRoot cause: Author assumes Skill should \"teach\" the model\nFix: Claude already knows this. Delete all basic explanations.\n     Focus on expert decisions, trade-offs, and anti-patterns.\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: The Dump\n```\nSymptom: SKILL.md is 800+ lines with everything included\nRoot cause: No progressive disclosure design\nFix: Core routing and decision trees in SKILL.md (<300 lines ideal)\n     Detailed content in references/, loaded on-demand\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: The Orphan References\n```\nSymptom: References directory exists but files are never loaded\nRoot cause: No explicit loading triggers\nFix: Add \"MANDATORY - READ ENTIRE FILE\" at workflow decision points\n     Add \"Do NOT Load\" to prevent over-loading\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: The Checkbox Procedure\n```\nSymptom: Step 1, Step 2, Step 3... mechanical procedures\nRoot cause: Author thinks in procedures, not thinking frameworks\nFix: Transform into \"Before doing X, ask yourself...\"\n     Focus on decision principles, not operation sequences\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: The Vague Warning\n```\nSymptom: \"Be careful\", \"avoid errors\", \"consider edge cases\"\nRoot cause: Author knows things can go wrong but hasn''t articulated specifics\nFix: Specific NEVER list with concrete examples and non-obvious reasons\n     \"NEVER use X because [specific problem that takes experience to learn]\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: The Invisible Skill\n```\nSymptom: Great content but skill rarely gets activated\nRoot cause: Description is vague, missing keywords, or lacks trigger scenarios\nFix: Description must answer WHAT, WHEN, and include KEYWORDS\n     \"Use when...\" + specific scenarios + searchable terms\n\nExample fix:\nBAD:  \"Helps with document tasks\"\nGOOD: \"Create, edit, and analyze .docx files. Use when working with\n       Word documents, tracked changes, or professional document formatting.\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: The Wrong Location\n```\nSymptom: \"When to use this Skill\" section in body, not in description\nRoot cause: Misunderstanding of three-layer loading\nFix: Move all triggering information to description field\n     Body is only loaded AFTER triggering decision is made\n```\n\n### Pattern 8: The Over-Engineered\n```\nSymptom: README.md, CHANGELOG.md, INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md\nRoot cause: Treating Skill like a software project\nFix: Delete all auxiliary files. Only include what Agent needs for the task.\n     No documentation about the Skill itself.\n```\n\n### Pattern 9: The Freedom Mismatch\n```\nSymptom: Rigid scripts for creative tasks, vague guidance for fragile operations\nRoot cause: Not considering task fragility\nFix: High freedom for creative (principles, not steps)\n     Low freedom for fragile (exact scripts, no parameters)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference Checklist\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  SKILL EVALUATION QUICK CHECK                                           │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                         │\n│  KNOWLEDGE DELTA (most important):                                      │\n│    [ ] No \"What is X\" explanations for basic concepts                   │\n│    [ ] No step-by-step tutorials for standard operations                │\n│    [ ] Has decision trees for non-obvious choices                       │\n│    [ ] Has trade-offs only experts would know                           │\n│    [ ] Has edge cases from real-world experience                        │\n│                                                                         │\n│  MINDSET + PROCEDURES:                                                  │\n│    [ ] Transfers thinking patterns (how to think about problems)        │\n│    [ ] Has \"Before doing X, ask yourself...\" frameworks                 │\n│    [ ] Includes domain-specific procedures Claude wouldn''t know         │\n│    [ ] Distinguishes valuable procedures from generic ones              │\n│                                                                         │\n│  ANTI-PATTERNS:                                                         │\n│    [ ] Has explicit NEVER list                                          │\n│    [ ] Anti-patterns are specific, not vague                            │\n│    [ ] Includes WHY (non-obvious reasons)                               │\n│                                                                         │\n│  SPECIFICATION (description is critical!):                              │\n│    [ ] Valid YAML frontmatter                                           │\n│    [ ] name: lowercase, ≤64 chars                                       │\n│    [ ] description answers: WHAT does it do?                            │\n│    [ ] description answers: WHEN should it be used?                     │\n│    [ ] description contains trigger KEYWORDS                            │\n│    [ ] description is specific enough for Agent to know when to use     │\n│                                                                         │\n│  STRUCTURE:                                                             │\n│    [ ] SKILL.md < 500 lines (ideal < 300)                               │\n│    [ ] Heavy content in references/                                     │\n│    [ ] Loading triggers embedded in workflow                            │\n│    [ ] Has \"Do NOT Load\" for preventing over-loading                    │\n│                                                                         │\n│  FREEDOM:                                                               │\n│    [ ] Creative tasks → High freedom (principles)                       │\n│    [ ] Fragile operations → Low freedom (exact scripts)                 │\n│                                                                         │\n│  USABILITY:                                                             │\n│    [ ] Decision trees for multi-path scenarios                          │\n│    [ ] Working code examples                                            │\n│    [ ] Error handling and fallbacks                                     │\n│    [ ] Edge cases covered                                               │\n│                                                                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## The Meta-Question\n\nWhen evaluating any Skill, always return to this fundamental question:\n\n> **\"Would an expert in this domain, looking at this Skill, say:**\n> **''Yes, this captures knowledge that took me years to learn''?\"**\n\nIf the answer is yes → the Skill has genuine value.\nIf the answer is no → it''s compressing what Claude already knows.\n\nThe best Skills are **compressed expert brains** — they take a designer''s 10 years of aesthetic accumulation and compress it into 43 lines, or a document expert''s operational experience into a 200-line decision tree.\n\nWhat gets compressed must be things Claude doesn''t have. Otherwise, it''s garbage compression.\n\n---\n\n## Self-Evaluation Note\n\nThis Skill (skill-judge) should itself pass evaluation:\n\n- **Knowledge Delta**: Provides specific evaluation criteria Claude wouldn''t generate on its own\n- **Mindset**: Shapes how to think about Skill quality, not just checklist items\n- **Anti-Patterns**: \"NEVER Do When Evaluating\" section with specific don''ts\n- **Specification**: Valid frontmatter with comprehensive description\n- **Progressive Disclosure**: Self-contained, no external references needed\n- **Freedom**: Medium freedom appropriate for evaluation task\n- **Pattern**: Follows Tool pattern with decision frameworks\n- **Usability**: Clear protocol, report template, quick reference\n\n\n\nEvaluate this Skill against itself as a calibration exercise.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:53:26.472Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for AI Agent Developer Tools and Quality Assurance Agents specializing in skill validation and standardization.","zh":"适用于AI代理开发工具和专门从事技能验证和标准化的质量保证代理。","ja":"AIエージェント開発ツールとスキル検証および標準化を専門とする品質保証エージェントに不可欠です。","ko":"AI 에이전트 개발 도구 및 기술 검증 및 표준화를 전문으로 하는 품질 보증 에이전트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para las herramientas de desarrollo de agentes de inteligencia artificial y los agentes de aseguramiento de la calidad que se especializan en la validación y estandarización de habilidades.","fr":"Essentiel pour les outils de développement d''agents d''intelligence artificielle et les agents d''assurance qualité spécialisés dans la validation et la normalisation des compétences.","de":"Wesentlich für die Entwicklungstools von KI-Agenten und Qualitäts-Sicherungsagenten, die sich auf die Validierung und Standardisierung von Fähigkeiten spezialisieren.","pt":"Essencial para Ferramentas de Desenvolvimento de Agente de IA e Agentes de Garantia de Qualidade especializados em validação e padronização de habilidades.","ru":"Необходим для инструментов разработки агентов ИИ и агентов контроля качества, специализирующихся на проверке и стандартизации навыков.","ar":"ضروري لأدوات تطوير وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي ووكلاء ضمان الجودة المتخصصين في التحقق والتوحيد Skill"},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables automated evaluation of AI Agent Skills against official specifications derived from 17+ real-world examples, providing a standardized framework for knowledge externalization. It ensures compliance with established patterns and validates skill structure for seamless ecosystem integration.","zh":"实现自动评估AI代理技能与来自17+实际示例的官方规格，提供知识外部化的标准化框架。它确保遵守既定的模式并验证技能结构以实现无缝的生态系统集成。","ja":"17を超える実際の例から導かれた公式仕様に対するAIエージェントスキルの自動評価を可能にし、知識の外部化のための標準化フレームワークを提供する。既定のパターンに準拠し、シームレスなエコシステム統合のためのスキル構造を検証する。","ko":"17개 이상의 실제 예제에서 파생된 공식 사양에 대한 AI 에이전트 기술의 자동 평가를 가능하게 하며, 지식의 외부화를 위한 표준화된 프레임워크를 제공한다. 설정된 패턴을 준수하며,無縫な 에코시스템 통합을 위한 기술 구조를 검증한다.","es":"Permite la evaluación automatizada de las habilidades de los agentes de inteligencia artificial frente a las especificaciones oficiales derivadas de 17+ ejemplos del mundo real, proporcionando un marco estandarizado para la externalización del conocimiento. Asegura el cumplimiento de los patrones establecidos y valida la estructura de habilidades para una integración sin problemas en el ecosistema.","fr":"Permet l''évaluation automatisée des compétences des agents d''intelligence artificielle par rapport aux spécifications officielles dérivées de 17+ exemples du monde réel, fournissant un cadre normalisé pour l''externalisation des connaissances. Elle assure la conformité aux modèles établis et valide la structure des compétences pour une intégration sans problème dans l''écosystème.","de":"Ermöglicht die automatisierte Bewertung der Fähigkeiten von KI-Agenten gegenüber den offiziellen Spezifikationen, die aus 17+ Beispielen der realen Welt abgeleitet werden, und bietet ein standardisiertes Rahmenwerk für die Externalisierung von Wissen. Sie stellt sicher, dass die etablierten Muster eingehalten werden und validiert die Fähigkeitsstruktur für eine nahtlose Integration in das Ökosystem.","pt":"Permite a avaliação automatizada das Habilidades do Agente de IA contra especificações oficiais derivadas de 17+ exemplos do mundo real, fornecendo um framework padronizado para externalização do conhecimento. Ele garante a conformidade com padrões estabelecidos e valida a estrutura da habilidade para integração de ecossistema sem interrupções.","ru":"Позволяет автоматически оценивать навыки агента ИИ по официальным спецификациям, полученным из 17+ реальных примеров, обеспечивая стандартизированную основу для внешней реализации знаний. Он гарантирует соответствие установленным шаблонам и проверяет структуру навыка для бесперебойной интеграции в экосистему.","ar":"يمكن التقييم الآلي لمهارات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي مقابل المواصفات الرسمية المستمدة من 17+ مثال من العالم الحقيقي، وتوفير إطار موحد لتحقيق المعرفة. ويتأكد من الامتثال للنماذج المقبولة ويحقق هيكل المهارة من أجل دمج النظام البيئي دون انقطاع."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating new skills against official specifications","Automating skill quality assurance checks","Generating standardized skill documentation","Comparing skill implementations against reference patterns"],"zh":["验证新技能是否符合官方规格","自动化技能质量保证检查","生成标准化技能文档","比较技能实现与参考模式"],"ja":["公式仕様に準拠した新しいスキルの検証","スキル品質保証チェックの自動化","標準化されたスキル文書の生成","スキル実装とリファレンスパターンの比較"],"ko":["공식 사양에 부합하는 새로운 기술의 검증","기술 품질 보증 점검의 자동화","표준화된 기술 문서의 생성","기술 구현과 참조 패턴의 비교"],"es":["Validar nuevas habilidades contra las especificaciones oficiales","Automatizar las comprobaciones de aseguramiento de la calidad de las habilidades","Generar documentación de habilidades estandarizadas","Comparar implementaciones de habilidades con patrones de referencia"],"fr":["Valider les nouvelles compétences par rapport aux spécifications officielles","Automatiser les vérifications d''assurance qualité des compétences","Générer une documentation de compétences normalisées","Comparer les implementations de compétences avec des modèles de référence"],"de":["Neue Fähigkeiten gegen die offiziellen Spezifikationen validieren","Automatisieren der Qualitäts-Sicherungsprüfungen für Fähigkeiten","Erzeugen standardisierter Fähigkeitsdokumentation","Vergleichen von Fähigkeitsimplementierungen mit Referenzmustern"],"pt":["Validar novas habilidades contra especificações oficiais","Automatizar verificações de garantia de qualidade de habilidades","Gerar documentação de habilidades padronizada","Comparar implementações de habilidades com padrões de referência"],"ru":["Проверка новых навыков против официальных спецификаций","Автоматизация проверок качества навыков","Генерация стандартизированной документации навыков","Сравнение реализаций навыков с образцовыми шаблонами"],"ar":["التحقق من مهارات جديدة مقابل المواصفات الرسمية","تأتمتة فحص جودة المهارات","توليد توثيق موحد للمهارات","مقارنة تنفيذ المهارات بنماذج المرجعية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to skill source code for analysis","Limited to patterns derived from the 17 reference examples","May need updates as official specifications evolve"],"zh":["需要访问技能源代码以进行分析","仅限于从17个参考示例中派生的模式","可能需要在官方规格演化时更新"],"ja":["分析のためにスキルソースコードへのアクセスが必要","17のリファレンス例から導かれたパターンに限定される","公式仕様が進化するにつれて更新する必要があるかもしれない"],"ko":["분석을 위해 기술 소스 코드에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","17개의 참조 예제에서 파생된 패턴으로 제한됩니다.","공식 사양이 발전함에 따라 업데이트가 필요할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso al código fuente de la habilidad para el análisis","Limitado a patrones derivados de los 17 ejemplos de referencia","Puede necesitar actualizaciones a medida que evolucionan las especificaciones oficiales"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au code source de la compétence pour l''analyse","Limité aux modèles dérivés des 17 exemples de référence","Peut nécessiter des mises à jour à mesure que les spécifications officielles évoluent"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf den Quellcode der Fähigkeit für die Analyse","Begrenzt auf Muster, die aus den 17 Referenzbeispielen abgeleitet werden","Kann Aktualisierungen benötigen, wenn die offiziellen Spezifikationen weiterentwickelt werden"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao código-fonte da habilidade para análise","Limitado a padrões derivados dos 17 exemplos de referência","Pode necessitar de atualizações à medida que as especificações oficiais evoluem"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к исходному коду навыка для анализа","Ограничен шаблонами, полученными из 17 образцовых примеров","Может потребовать обновлений по мере эволюции официальных спецификаций"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى код المصدر للمهارة للتحليل","محدود بالنماذج المستمدة من 17 مثال مرجعي","يمكن أن يتطلب تحديثات مع تطور المواصفات الرسمية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
