Kompatibilität mit IDEs und CLIs","Anpassbare Konfigurationen","Verbesserung der Entscheidungsfindung"],"pt":["Modos de operação adaptáveis","Otimização de desempenho para tarefas específicas","Abordagem de problemas personalizada","Comunicação e priorização ajustáveis","Integração com IDEs e CLIs"],"ru":["Адаптивные режимы работы","Оптимизация производительности для конкретных задач","Персонализированный подход к задаче","Настраиваемая коммуникация и приоритизация","Интеграция с IDE и CLI"],"ar":["أوضاع تشغيل متكيفة","تحسين الأداء لعمليات محددة","نهج مشكلة شخصي","تواصل وتوجيه قابلين للتعديل","التكامل مع بيئات التطوير المتكاملة وواجهات سطر الأوامر"]},"keywords":{"zh":["行为模式","AI操作模式","适应性AI","开发效率","IDE","CLI","Antigravity IDE"],"ja":["行動モード","AI操作モード","適応性AI","開発効率","IDE","CLI","Antigravity IDE"],"ko":["행동 모드","AI 운영 모드","적응형 AI","개발 효율성","IDE","CLI","Antigravity IDE"],"es":["modos de comportamiento","IA adaptativa","optimización del rendimiento","configuraciones de la IA","desarrollo de software","integración con IDEs","CLI compatible"],"fr":["modes de comportement","IA adaptative","optimisation des performances","configurations de l''IA","développement de logiciels","intégration avec les IDE","CLI compatible"],"de":["Verhaltensmodi","adaptive KI","Leistungsoptimierung","KI-Konfigurationen","Softwareentwicklung","Integration mit IDEs","CLI-kompatibel"],"pt":["modos comportamentais","otimização de desempenho de IA","desenvolvimento de IA","inteligência artificial","aprendizado de máquina","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["поведенческие режимы","оптимизация производительности ИИ","разработка ИИ","искусственный интеллект","машинное обучение","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["الوضعيات السلوكية","تحسين أداء الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","الذكاء الاصطناعي","التعلم الآلي","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"behavioral-modes","description":"AI operational modes (brainstorm, implement, debug, review, teach, ship, orchestrate). Use to adapt behavior based on task type.","bodyPreview":"# Behavioral Modes - Adaptive AI Operating Modes\n\n## Purpose\nThis skill defines distinct behavioral modes that optimize AI performance for specific tasks. Modes change how the AI approaches problems, communicates, and prioritizes.\n\n---\n\n## Available Modes\n\n### 1. 🧠 BRAINSTORM Mode\n\n**When to use:** Early project planning, feature ideation, architecture decisions\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Ask clarifying questions before assumptions\n- Offer multiple alternatives (at least 3)\n- Think divergently - explore","body":"# Behavioral Modes - Adaptive AI Operating Modes\n\n## Purpose\nThis skill defines distinct behavioral modes that optimize AI performance for specific tasks. Modes change how the AI approaches problems, communicates, and prioritizes.\n\n---\n\n## Available Modes\n\n### 1. 🧠 BRAINSTORM Mode\n\n**When to use:** Early project planning, feature ideation, architecture decisions\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Ask clarifying questions before assumptions\n- Offer multiple alternatives (at least 3)\n- Think divergently - explore unconventional solutions\n- No code yet - focus on ideas and options\n- Use visual diagrams (mermaid) to explain concepts\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n\"Let''s explore this together. Here are some approaches:\n\nOption A: [description]\n  ✅ Pros: ...\n  ❌ Cons: ...\n\nOption B: [description]\n  ✅ Pros: ...\n  ❌ Cons: ...\n\nWhat resonates with you? Or should we explore a different direction?\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. ⚡ IMPLEMENT Mode\n\n**When to use:** Writing code, building features, executing plans\n\n**Behavior:**\n- **CRITICAL: Use `clean-code` skill standards** - concise, direct, no verbose explanations\n- Fast execution - minimize questions\n- Use established patterns and best practices\n- Write complete, production-ready code\n- Include error handling and edge cases\n- **NO tutorial-style explanations** - just code\n- **NO unnecessary comments** - let code self-document\n- **NO over-engineering** - solve the problem directly\n- **NO RUSHING** - Quality > Speed. Read ALL references before coding.\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n[Code block]\n\n[Brief summary, max 1-2 sentences]\n```\n\n**NOT:**\n```\n\"Building [feature]...\n\n✓ Created [file1]\n✓ Created [file2]\n✓ Updated [file3]\n\n[long explanation]\n\nRun `npm run dev` to test.\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. 🔍 DEBUG Mode\n\n**When to use:** Fixing bugs, troubleshooting errors, investigating issues\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Ask for error messages and reproduction steps\n- Think systematically - check logs, trace data flow\n- Form hypothesis → test → verify\n- Explain the root cause, not just the fix\n- Prevent future occurrences\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n\"Investigating...\n\n🔍 Symptom: [what''s happening]\n🎯 Root cause: [why it''s happening]\n✅ Fix: [the solution]\n🛡️ Prevention: [how to avoid in future]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. 📋 REVIEW Mode\n\n**When to use:** Code review, architecture review, security audit\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Be thorough but constructive\n- Categorize by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\n- Explain the \"why\" behind suggestions\n- Offer improved code examples\n- Acknowledge what''s done well\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n## Code Review: [file/feature]\n\n### 🔴 Critical\n- [issue with explanation]\n\n### 🟠 Improvements\n- [suggestion with example]\n\n### 🟢 Good\n- [positive observation]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. 📚 TEACH Mode\n\n**When to use:** Explaining concepts, documentation, onboarding\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Explain from fundamentals\n- Use analogies and examples\n- Progress from simple to complex\n- Include practical exercises\n- Check understanding\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n## Understanding [Concept]\n\n### What is it?\n[Simple explanation with analogy]\n\n### How it works\n[Technical explanation with diagram]\n\n### Example\n[Code example with comments]\n\n### Try it yourself\n[Exercise or task]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. 🚀 SHIP Mode\n\n**When to use:** Production deployment, final polish, release preparation\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Focus on stability over features\n- Check for missing error handling\n- Verify environment configs\n- Run all tests\n- Create deployment checklist\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n## Pre-Ship Checklist\n\n### ✅ Code Quality\n- [ ] No TypeScript errors\n- [ ] ESLint passing\n- [ ] All tests passing\n\n### ✅ Security\n- [ ] No exposed secrets\n- [ ] Input validation complete\n\n### ✅ Performance\n- [ ] Bundle size acceptable\n- [ ] No console.logs\n\n### 🚀 Ready to deploy\n```\n\n---\n\n## Mode Detection\n\nThe AI should automatically detect the appropriate mode based on:\n\n| Trigger | Mode |\n|---------|------|\n| \"what if\", \"ideas\", \"options\" | BRAINSTORM |\n| \"build\", \"create\", \"add\" | IMPLEMENT |\n| \"not working\", \"error\", \"bug\" | DEBUG |\n| \"review\", \"check\", \"audit\" | REVIEW |\n| \"explain\", \"how does\", \"learn\" | TEACH |\n| \"deploy\", \"release\", \"production\" | SHIP |\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Agent Collaboration Patterns (2025)\n\nModern architectures optimized for agent-to-agent collaboration:\n\n### 1. 🔭 EXPLORE Mode\n**Role:** Discovery and Analysis (Explorer Agent)\n**Behavior:** Socratic questioning, deep-dive code reading, dependency mapping.\n**Output:** `discovery-report.json`, architectural visualization.\n\n### 2. 🗺️ PLAN-EXECUTE-CRITIC (PEC)\nCyclic mode transitions for high-complexity tasks:\n1. **Planner:** Decomposes the task into atomic steps (`task.md`).\n2. **Executor:** Performs the actual coding (`IMPLEMENT`).\n3. **Critic:** Reviews the code, performs security and performance checks (`REVIEW`).\n\n### 3. 🧠 MENTAL MODEL SYNC\nBehavior for creating and loading \"Mental Model\" summaries to preserve context between sessions.\n\n---\n\n## Combining Modes\n\n---\n\n## Manual Mode Switching\n\nUsers can explicitly request a mode:\n\n```\n/brainstorm new feature ideas\n/implement the user profile page\n/debug why login fails\n/review this pull request\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:53:18.183Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Adaptive AI Agents needing dynamic task optimization through distinct behavioral modes.","zh":"非常适合需要通过不同行为模式进行动态任务优化的自适应AI代理。","ja":"異なる行動モードを通じて動的なタスク最適化を必要とする適応型AIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"독특한 행동 모드를 통해 동적 작업 최적화가 필요한 적응형 AI 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA adaptativos que necesitan una optimización de tareas dinámica a través de modos de comportamiento distintos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA adaptatifs ayant besoin d''une optimisation de tâches dynamique via des modes de comportement distincts.","de":"Perfekt für adaptive KI-Agents, die eine dynamische Aufgabenoptimierung durch unterschiedliche Verhaltensmodi benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Adaptativos que necessitam de otimização de tarefas dinâmicas por meio de modos comportamentais distintos.","ru":"Идеально для адаптивных агентов ИИ, которым необходима динамическая оптимизация задач посредством различных режимов поведения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتكيف الذي يحتاج إلى تحسين任务 ديناميكي من خلال أوضاع سلوكية متميزة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to switch between modes like BRAINSTORM for exploratory tasks, optimizing performance by asking clarifying questions, offering multiple alternatives, and thinking divergently, utilizing protocols like GitHub Copilot and Cursor for seamless integration.","zh":"使代理能够在诸如BRAINSTORM之类的模式之间切换，用于探索性任务，通过提出澄清性问题、提供多种替代方案以及发散性思考来优化性能，并利用GitHub Copilot和Cursor等协议实现无缝集成。","ja":"探索的タスクのためにBRAINSTORMのようなモード間の切り替えを可能にし、明確化の質問を投げかけ、複数の代替案を提供し、発散的に思考することでパフォーマンスを最適化し、GitHub CopilotやCursorなどのプロトコルを利用してシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"탐색적 작업을 위한 BRAINSTORM 모드와 같은 모드 간 전환을 통해 에이전트의 성능을 최적화하며, 명확한 질문을 하고 여러 대안을 제공하며 확산적으로 사고하고, GitHub Copilot 및 Cursor와 같은 프로토콜을 활용하여 원활한 통합을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes cambiar entre modos como BRAINSTORM para tareas de exploración, optimizando el rendimiento al hacer preguntas aclaratorias, ofrecer múltiples alternativas y pensar de manera divergente, utilizando protocolos como GitHub Copilot y Cursor para una integración sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de basculer entre des modes comme BRAINSTORM pour les tâches d''exploration, en optimisant les performances en posant des questions de clarification, en offrant plusieurs alternatives et en pensant de manière divergente, en utilisant des protocoles tels que GitHub Copilot et Cursor pour une intégration sans problème.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, zwischen Modi wie BRAINSTORM für Explorationsaufgaben zu wechseln, die Leistung zu optimieren, indem sie klärende Fragen stellen, mehrere Alternativen anbieten und divergent denken, wobei Protokolle wie GitHub Copilot und Cursor für eine nahtlose Integration verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a alternar entre modos como BRAINSTORM para tarefas exploratórias, otimizando o desempenho ao fazer perguntas esclarecedoras, oferecer alternativas múltiplas e pensar de forma divergente, utilizando protocolos como GitHub Copilot e Cursor para integração transparente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью переключаться между режимами, такими как BRAINSTORM для исследовательских задач, оптимизируя производительность за счет постановки уточняющих вопросов, предлагая несколько альтернатив и мыслить дивергентно, используя протоколы, такие как GitHub Copilot и Cursor для бесшовной интеграции.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من التبديل بين أوضاع مثل BRAINSTORM للمهام الاستكشافية، و تحسين الأداء من خلال طرح أسئلة توضيحية، و تقديم بديلات متعددة، و التفكير بشكل منقسم، و باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل GitHub Copilot و Cursor للدمج السلس."},"useCases":{"en":["Switching to BRAINSTORM Mode for early project planning and feature ideation","Utilizing distinct modes for architecture decisions and prioritization","Adapting AI behavior for specific tasks through mode selection"],"zh":["切换到BRAINSTORM模式用于早期项目规划和功能构思","利用不同模式进行架构决策和优先级排序","通过模式选择使AI行为适应特定任务"],"ja":["初期プロジェクト計画と機能アイデア創出のためのBRAINSTORMモードへの切り替え","アーキテクチャ決定と優先順位付けのための異なるモードの利用","モード選択による特定のタスクへのAI動作の適応"],"ko":["초기 프로젝트 계획 및 기능 아이디어 구상을 위한 BRAINSTORM 모드로 전환","아키텍처 결정 및 우선순위 지정을 위한 독특한 모드 활용","모드 선택을 통해 특정 작업에 맞게 AI 동작 적응"],"es":["Cambiar al modo BRAINSTORM para la planificación temprana de proyectos y la ideación de características","Utilizar modos distintos para decisiones de arquitectura y priorización","Adaptar el comportamiento de la IA para tareas específicas a través de la selección de modos"],"fr":["Basculer en mode BRAINSTORM pour la planification précoce de projets et l''idéation de fonctionnalités","Utiliser des modes distincts pour les décisions d''architecture et la priorisation","Adapter le comportement de l''IA pour des tâches spécifiques via la sélection de modes"],"de":["Wechseln in den BRAINSTORM-Modus für die frühzeitige Projektplanung und die Ideenfindung für Funktionen","Verwenden von unterschiedlichen Modi für Architekturentscheidungen und Priorisierung","Anpassen des KI-Verhaltens für bestimmte Aufgaben durch Modusaufwahl"],"pt":["Alternar para o modo BRAINSTORM para planejamento de projetos iniciais e ideação de recursos","Utilizar modos distintos para decisões de arquitetura e priorização","Adaptar o comportamento do IA para tarefas específicas por meio da seleção de modos"],"ru":["Переключение в режим BRAINSTORM для первоначального планирования проектов и генерации идей","Использование различных режимов для архитектурных решений и определения приоритетов","Адаптация поведения ИИ для конкретных задач посредством выбора режимов"],"ar":["التحول إلى وضع BRAINSTORM للتنظيم المبكر للمشاريع و تجميع الأفكار","استخدام أوضاع متميزة لاتخاذ قرارات بنية و تحديد الأولويات","تعديل سلوك الذكاء الاصطناعي للأدوار المحددة من خلال اختيار الأوضاع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires compatibility with IDEs like GitHub Copilot and CLIs like Kiro","Limited to configurations convertible from Antigravity IDE"],"zh":["需要与GitHub Copilot等IDE和Kiro等CLI兼容","仅限于可从Antigravity IDE转换的配置"],"ja":["GitHub CopilotのようなIDEやKiroのようなCLIとの互換性が必要","Antigravity IDEから変換可能な構成に限定される"],"ko":["GitHub Copilot과 같은 IDE 및 Kiro와 같은 CLI와의 호환성 필요","Antigravity IDE에서 변환 가능한 구성으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con IDE como GitHub Copilot y CLI como Kiro","Limitado a configuraciones convertibles desde Antigravity IDE"],"fr":["Nécessite une compatibilité avec des IDE comme GitHub Copilot et des CLI comme Kiro","Limité aux configurations convertibles à partir de Antigravity IDE"],"de":["Benötigt Kompatibilität mit IDE wie GitHub Copilot und CLI wie Kiro","Begrenzt auf Konfigurationen, die von Antigravity IDE konvertiert werden können"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com IDEs como GitHub Copilot e CLIs como Kiro","Limitado a configurações convertíveis a partir do Antigravity IDE"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с IDE, такими как GitHub Copilot, и CLI, такими как Kiro","Ограничен конфигурациями, конвертируемыми из Antigravity IDE"],"ar":["يتطلب التوافق مع بيئات التطوير المتكاملة مثل GitHub Copilot و واجهات سطر الأوامر مثل Kiro","محدود بالتكوينات القابلة للتحويل من بيئة Antigravity IDE"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/zustand-state-management', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'zustand-state-management', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z', '2026-02-18T13:53:12.545Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/zustand-state-management","name":"zustand-state-management","description":{"zh":"Zustand 是一个用于 React 的状态管理库，提供了简单易用的 API 来创建和管理全局状态","ja":"Zustand は React 用の状態管理ライブラリであり、グローバル状態を作成して管理するためのシンプルで使いやすい API を提供する","ko":"Zustand는 React용 상태 관리 라이브러리로서, 전역 상태를 생성하고 관리하기 위한 단순하고 사용하기 쉬운 API를 제공한다","es":"Zustand es una biblioteca de gestión de estado para React y TypeScript que simplifica la administración de datos en aplicaciones complejas","fr":"Zustand est une bibliothèque de gestion d''état pour React et TypeScript qui simplifie la gestion des données dans les applications complexes","de":"Zustand ist eine Bibliothek für die Statusverwaltung in React- und TypeScript-Anwendungen, die die Verwaltung von Daten in komplexen Anwendungen vereinfacht","pt":"O Zustand é uma biblioteca de gerenciamento de estado para React e TypeScript que fornece uma forma simples de gerenciar o estado da aplicação.","ru":"Zustand — библиотека управления состоянием для React и TypeScript, которая предоставляет простой способ управления состоянием приложения.","ar":"Zustand هي مكتبة لإدارة الحالة ل React و TypeScript توفر طريقة بسيطة لإدارة حالة التطبيق.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Zustand 状态管理库","ja":"Zustand ステート管理ライブラリ","ko":"Zustand 상태 관리 라이브러리","es":"Gestión de Estado con Zustand","fr":"Gestion d''État avec Zustand","de":"Statusverwaltung mit Zustand","pt":"Gerenciamento de Estado Zustand","ru":"Управление состоянием Zustand","ar":"إدارة الحالة Zustand","en":"zustand-state-management"},"description":{"zh":"Zustand 是一个用于 React 的状态管理库，提供了简单易用的 API 来创建和管理全局状态","ja":"Zustand は React 用の状態管理ライブラリであり、グローバル状態を作成して管理するためのシンプルで使いやすい API を提供する","ko":"Zustand는 React용 상태 관리 라이브러리로서, 전역 상태를 생성하고 관리하기 위한 단순하고 사용하기 쉬운 API를 제공한다","es":"Zustand es una biblioteca de gestión de estado para React y TypeScript que simplifica la administración de datos en aplicaciones complejas","fr":"Zustand est une bibliothèque de gestion d''état pour React et TypeScript qui simplifie la gestion des données dans les applications complexes","de":"Zustand ist eine Bibliothek für die Statusverwaltung in React- und TypeScript-Anwendungen, die die Verwaltung von Daten in komplexen Anwendungen vereinfacht","pt":"O Zustand é uma biblioteca de gerenciamento de estado para React e TypeScript que fornece uma forma simples de gerenciar o estado da aplicação.","ru":"Zustand — библиотека управления состоянием для React и TypeScript, которая предоставляет простой способ управления состоянием приложения.","ar":"Zustand هي مكتبة لإدارة الحالة ل React و TypeScript توفر طريقة بسيطة لإدارة حالة التطبيق.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["简单易用的 API","支持 React 18-19","支持 TypeScript 5+","轻松创建和管理全局状态","小尺寸和高性能"],"ja":["シンプルで使いやすい API","React 18-19 をサポート","TypeScript 5+ をサポート","グローバル状態を簡単に作成して管理","小さなサイズと高パフォーマンス"],"ko":["단순하고 사용하기 쉬운 API","React 18-19 지원","TypeScript 5+ 지원","전역 상태를 쉽게 생성하고 관리","작은 크기와 높은 성능"],"es":["Gestión de estado simplificada","Compatibilidad con React 18-19","Soporte para TypeScript 5+","Implementación fácil con create<T>()()","Acceso a la tienda con useBearStore"],"fr":["Gestion d''état simplifiée","Compatibilité avec React 18-19","Prise en charge de TypeScript 5+","Mise en œuvre facile avec create<T>()()","Accès au magasin avec useBearStore"],"de":["Vereinfachte Statusverwaltung","Kompatibilität mit React 18-19","Unterstützung für TypeScript 5+","Einfache Implementierung mit create<T>()()","Zugriff auf den Shop mit useBearStore"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de estado simples","Integração com React 18-19","Suporte a TypeScript 5+","Instalação fácil com npm","Uso de stores personalizadas"],"ru":["Простое управление состоянием","Интеграция с React 18-19","Поддержка TypeScript 5+","Легкая установка с помощью npm","Использование пользовательских магазинов"],"ar":["إدارة الحالة البسيطة","التكامل مع React 18-19","دعم TypeScript 5+","التثبيت السهل مع npm","استخدام المتاجر المخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Zustand","状态管理","React","JavaScript","TypeScript","全局状态","状态库"],"ja":["Zustand","状態管理","React","JavaScript","TypeScript","グローバル状態","状態ライブラリ"],"ko":["Zustand","상태 관리","React","JavaScript","TypeScript","전역 상태","상태 라이브러리"],"es":["zustand","gestión de estado","react","typescript","biblioteca de gestión de estado","estado en react","typescript 5+","react 18-19"],"fr":["zustand","gestion d''état","react","typescript","bibliothèque de gestion d''état","état en react","typescript 5+","react 18-19"],"de":["zustand","statusverwaltung","react","typescript","bibliothek für statusverwaltung","status in react","typescript 5+","react 18-19"],"pt":["zustand","gerenciamento de estado","react","typescript","npm","desenvolvimento web","bibliotecas javascript"],"ru":["zustand","управление состоянием","react","typescript","npm","веб-разработка","библиотеки javascript"],"ar":["zustand","إدارة الحالة","react","typescript","npm","تطوير الويب","مكتبات جافاسكريبت"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"zustand-state-management","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Zustand State Management\n\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-21\n**Latest Version**: zustand@5.0.10 (released 2026-01-12)\n**Dependencies**: React 18-19, TypeScript 5+\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\nnpm install zustand\n```\n\n**TypeScript Store** (CRITICAL: use `create<T>()()` double parentheses):\n```typescript\nimport { create } from ''zustand''\n\ninterface BearStore {\n  bears: number\n  increase: (by: number) => void\n}\n\nconst useBearStore = create<BearStore>()((set) => ({\n  bears: 0,\n  increase: (by) => set((s","body":"# Zustand State Management\n\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-21\n**Latest Version**: zustand@5.0.10 (released 2026-01-12)\n**Dependencies**: React 18-19, TypeScript 5+\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\nnpm install zustand\n```\n\n**TypeScript Store** (CRITICAL: use `create<T>()()` double parentheses):\n```typescript\nimport { create } from ''zustand''\n\ninterface BearStore {\n  bears: number\n  increase: (by: number) => void\n}\n\nconst useBearStore = create<BearStore>()((set) => ({\n  bears: 0,\n  increase: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears + by })),\n}))\n```\n\n**Use in Components**:\n```tsx\nconst bears = useBearStore((state) => state.bears)  // Only re-renders when bears changes\nconst increase = useBearStore((state) => state.increase)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Core Patterns\n\n**Basic Store** (JavaScript):\n```javascript\nconst useStore = create((set) => ({\n  count: 0,\n  increment: () => set((state) => ({ count: state.count + 1 })),\n}))\n```\n\n**TypeScript Store** (Recommended):\n```typescript\ninterface CounterStore { count: number; increment: () => void }\nconst useStore = create<CounterStore>()((set) => ({\n  count: 0,\n  increment: () => set((state) => ({ count: state.count + 1 })),\n}))\n```\n\n**Persistent Store** (survives page reloads):\n```typescript\nimport { persist, createJSONStorage } from ''zustand/middleware''\n\nconst useStore = create<UserPreferences>()(\n  persist(\n    (set) => ({ theme: ''system'', setTheme: (theme) => set({ theme }) }),\n    { name: ''user-preferences'', storage: createJSONStorage(() => localStorage) },\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n### Always Do\n\n✅ Use `create<T>()()` (double parentheses) in TypeScript for middleware compatibility\n✅ Define separate interfaces for state and actions\n✅ Use selector functions to extract specific state slices\n✅ Use `set` with updater functions for derived state: `set((state) => ({ count: state.count + 1 }))`\n✅ Use unique names for persist middleware storage keys\n✅ Handle Next.js hydration with `hasHydrated` flag pattern\n✅ Use `useShallow` hook for selecting multiple values\n✅ Keep actions pure (no side effects except state updates)\n\n### Never Do\n\n❌ Use `create<T>(...)` (single parentheses) in TypeScript - breaks middleware types\n❌ Mutate state directly: `set((state) => { state.count++; return state })` - use immutable updates\n❌ Create new objects in selectors: `useStore((state) => ({ a: state.a }))` - causes infinite renders\n❌ Use same storage name for multiple stores - causes data collisions\n❌ Access localStorage during SSR without hydration check\n❌ Use Zustand for server state - use TanStack Query instead\n❌ Export store instance directly - always export the hook\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues Prevention\n\nThis skill prevents **6** documented issues:\n\n### Issue #1: Next.js Hydration Mismatch\n\n**Error**: `\"Text content does not match server-rendered HTML\"` or `\"Hydration failed\"`\n\n**Source**:\n- [DEV Community: Persist middleware in Next.js](https://dev.to/abdulsamad/how-to-use-zustands-persist-middleware-in-nextjs-4lb5)\n- GitHub Discussions #2839\n\n**Why It Happens**:\nPersist middleware reads from localStorage on client but not on server, causing state mismatch.\n\n**Prevention**:\n```typescript\nimport { create } from ''zustand''\nimport { persist } from ''zustand/middleware''\n\ninterface StoreWithHydration {\n  count: number\n  _hasHydrated: boolean\n  setHasHydrated: (hydrated: boolean) => void\n  increase: () => void\n}\n\nconst useStore = create<StoreWithHydration>()(\n  persist(\n    (set) => ({\n      count: 0,\n      _hasHydrated: false,\n      setHasHydrated: (hydrated) => set({ _hasHydrated: hydrated }),\n      increase: () => set((state) => ({ count: state.count + 1 })),\n    }),\n    {\n      name: ''my-store'',\n      onRehydrateStorage: () => (state) => {\n        state?.setHasHydrated(true)\n      },\n    },\n  ),\n)\n\n// In component\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const hasHydrated = useStore((state) => state._hasHydrated)\n\n  if (!hasHydrated) {\n    return <div>Loading...</div>\n  }\n\n  // Now safe to render with persisted state\n  return <ActualContent />\n}\n```\n\n### Issue #2: TypeScript Double Parentheses Missing\n\n**Error**: Type inference fails, `StateCreator` types break with middleware\n\n**Source**: [Official Zustand TypeScript Guide](https://zustand.docs.pmnd.rs/guides/typescript)\n\n**Why It Happens**:\nThe currying syntax `create<T>()()` is required for middleware to work with TypeScript inference.\n\n**Prevention**:\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - Single parentheses\nconst useStore = create<MyStore>((set) => ({\n  // ...\n}))\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Double parentheses\nconst useStore = create<MyStore>()((set) => ({\n  // ...\n}))\n```\n\n**Rule**: Always use `create<T>()()` in TypeScript, even without middleware (future-proof).\n\n### Issue #3: Persist Middleware Import Error\n\n**Error**: `\"Attempted import error: ''createJSONStorage'' is not exported from ''zustand/middleware''\"`\n\n**Source**: GitHub Discussion #2839\n\n**Why It Happens**:\nWrong import path or version mismatch between zustand and build tools.\n\n**Prevention**:\n```typescript\n// ✅ CORRECT imports for v5\nimport { create } from ''zustand''\nimport { persist, createJSONStorage } from ''zustand/middleware''\n\n// Verify versions\n// zustand@5.0.9 includes createJSONStorage\n// zustand@4.x uses different API\n\n// Check your package.json\n// \"zustand\": \"^5.0.9\"\n```\n\n### Issue #4: Infinite Render Loop\n\n**Error**: Component re-renders infinitely, browser freezes\n```\nUncaught Error: Maximum update depth exceeded. This can happen when a component repeatedly calls setState inside componentWillUpdate or componentDidUpdate.\n```\n\n**Source**:\n- GitHub Discussions #2642\n- [Issue #2863](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand/issues/2863)\n\n**Why It Happens**:\nCreating new object references in selectors causes Zustand to think state changed.\n\n**v5 Breaking Change**: Zustand v5 made this error MORE explicit compared to v4. In v4, this behavior was \"non-ideal\" but could go unnoticed. In v5, you''ll immediately see the \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" error.\n\n**Prevention**:\n```typescript\nimport { useShallow } from ''zustand/shallow''\n\n// ❌ WRONG - Creates new object every time\nconst { bears, fishes } = useStore((state) => ({\n  bears: state.bears,\n  fishes: state.fishes,\n}))\n\n// ✅ CORRECT Option 1 - Select primitives separately\nconst bears = useStore((state) => state.bears)\nconst fishes = useStore((state) => state.fishes)\n\n// ✅ CORRECT Option 2 - Use useShallow hook for multiple values\nconst { bears, fishes } = useStore(\n  useShallow((state) => ({ bears: state.bears, fishes: state.fishes }))\n)\n```\n\n### Issue #5: Slices Pattern TypeScript Complexity\n\n**Error**: `StateCreator` types fail to infer, complex middleware types break\n\n**Source**: [Official Slices Pattern Guide](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand/blob/main/docs/guides/slices-pattern.md)\n\n**Why It Happens**:\nCombining multiple slices requires explicit type annotations for middleware compatibility.\n\n**Prevention**:\n```typescript\nimport { create, StateCreator } from ''zustand''\n\n// Define slice types\ninterface BearSlice {\n  bears: number\n  addBear: () => void\n}\n\ninterface FishSlice {\n  fishes: number\n  addFish: () => void\n}\n\n// Create slices with proper types\nconst createBearSlice: StateCreator<\n  BearSlice & FishSlice,  // Combined store type\n  [],                      // Middleware mutators (empty if none)\n  [],                      // Chained middleware (empty if none)\n  BearSlice               // This slice''s type\n> = (set) => ({\n  bears: 0,\n  addBear: () => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears + 1 })),\n})\n\nconst createFishSlice: StateCreator<\n  BearSlice & FishSlice,\n  [],\n  [],\n  FishSlice\n> = (set) => ({\n  fishes: 0,\n  addFish: () => set((state) => ({ fishes: state.fishes + 1 })),\n})\n\n// Combine slices\nconst useStore = create<BearSlice & FishSlice>()((...a) => ({\n  ...createBearSlice(...a),\n  ...createFishSlice(...a),\n}))\n```\n\n### Issue #6: Persist Middleware Race Condition (Fixed v5.0.10+)\n\n**Error**: Inconsistent state during concurrent rehydration attempts\n\n**Source**:\n- [GitHub PR #3336](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand/pull/3336)\n- [Release v5.0.10](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand/releases/tag/v5.0.10)\n\n**Why It Happens**:\nIn Zustand v5.0.9 and earlier, concurrent calls to rehydrate during persist middleware initialization could cause a race condition where multiple hydration attempts would interfere with each other, leading to inconsistent state.\n\n**Prevention**:\nUpgrade to Zustand v5.0.10 or later. No code changes needed - the fix is internal to the persist middleware.\n\n```bash\nnpm install zustand@latest  # Ensure v5.0.10+\n```\n\n**Note**: This was fixed in v5.0.10 (January 2026). If you''re using v5.0.9 or earlier and experiencing state inconsistencies with persist middleware, upgrade immediately.\n\n---\n\n## Middleware\n\n**Persist** (localStorage):\n```typescript\nimport { persist, createJSONStorage } from ''zustand/middleware''\n\nconst useStore = create<MyStore>()(\n  persist(\n    (set) => ({ data: [], addItem: (item) => set((state) => ({ data: [...state.data, item] })) }),\n    {\n      name: ''my-storage'',\n      partialize: (state) => ({ data: state.data }),  // Only persist ''data''\n    },\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n**Devtools** (Redux DevTools):\n```typescript\nimport { devtools } from ''zustand/middleware''\n\nconst useStore = create<CounterStore>()(\n  devtools(\n    (set) => ({ count: 0, increment: () => set((s) => ({ count: s.count + 1 }), undefined, ''increment'') }),\n    { name: ''CounterStore'' },\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n**v4→v5 Migration Note**: In Zustand v4, devtools was imported from `''zustand/middleware/devtools''`. In v5, use `''zustand/middleware''` (as shown above). If you see \"Module not found: Can''t resolve ''zustand/middleware/devtools''\", update your import path.\n\n**Combining Middlewares** (order matters):\n```typescript\nconst useStore = create<MyStore>()(devtools(persist((set) => ({ /* ... */ }), { name: ''storage'' }), { name: ''MyStore'' }))\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n**Computed/Derived Values** (in selector, not stored):\n```typescript\nconst count = useStore((state) => state.items.length)  // Computed on read\n```\n\n**Async Actions**:\n```typescript\nconst useAsyncStore = create<AsyncStore>()((set) => ({\n  data: null,\n  isLoading: false,\n  fetchData: async () => {\n    set({ isLoading: true })\n    const response = await fetch(''/api/data'')\n    set({ data: await response.text(), isLoading: false })\n  },\n}))\n```\n\n**Resetting Store**:\n```typescript\nconst initialState = { count: 0, name: '''' }\nconst useStore = create<ResettableStore>()((set) => ({\n  ...initialState,\n  reset: () => set(initialState),\n}))\n```\n\n**Selector with Params**:\n```typescript\nconst todo = useStore((state) => state.todos.find((t) => t.id === id))\n```\n\n---\n\n## Bundled Resources\n\n**Templates**: `basic-store.ts`, `typescript-store.ts`, `persist-store.ts`, `slices-pattern.ts`, `devtools-store.ts`, `nextjs-store.ts`, `computed-store.ts`, `async-actions-store.ts`\n\n**References**: `middleware-guide.md` (persist/devtools/immer/custom), `typescript-patterns.md` (type inference issues), `nextjs-hydration.md` (SSR/hydration), `migration-guide.md` (from Redux/Context/v4)\n\n**Scripts**: `check-versions.sh` (version compatibility)\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Topics\n\n**Vanilla Store** (Without React):\n```typescript\nimport { createStore } from ''zustand/vanilla''\n\nconst store = createStore<CounterStore>()((set) => ({ count: 0, increment: () => set((s) => ({ count: s.count + 1 })) }))\nconst unsubscribe = store.subscribe((state) => console.log(state.count))\nstore.getState().increment()\n```\n\n**Custom Middleware**:\n```typescript\nconst logger: Logger = (f, name) => (set, get, store) => {\n  const loggedSet: typeof set = (...a) => { set(...a); console.log(`[${name}]:`, get()) }\n  return f(loggedSet, get, store)\n}\n```\n\n**Immer Middleware** (Mutable Updates):\n```typescript\nimport { immer } from ''zustand/middleware/immer''\n\nconst useStore = create<TodoStore>()(immer((set) => ({\n  todos: [],\n  addTodo: (text) => set((state) => { state.todos.push({ id: Date.now().toString(), text }) }),\n})))\n```\n\n**v5.0.3→v5.0.4 Migration Note**: If upgrading from v5.0.3 to v5.0.4+ and immer middleware stops working, verify you''re using the import path shown above (`zustand/middleware/immer`). Some users reported issues after the v5.0.4 update that were resolved by confirming the correct import.\n\n**Experimental SSR Safe Middleware** (v5.0.9+):\n\n**Status**: Experimental (API may change)\n\nZustand v5.0.9 introduced experimental `unstable_ssrSafe` middleware for Next.js usage. This provides an alternative approach to the `_hasHydrated` pattern (see Issue #1).\n\n```typescript\nimport { unstable_ssrSafe } from ''zustand/middleware''\n\nconst useStore = create<Store>()(\n  unstable_ssrSafe(\n    persist(\n      (set) => ({ /* state */ }),\n      { name: ''my-store'' }\n    )\n  )\n)\n```\n\n**Recommendation**: Continue using the `_hasHydrated` pattern documented in Issue #1 until this API stabilizes. Monitor [Discussion #2740](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand/discussions/2740) for updates on when this becomes stable.\n\n---\n\n## Official Documentation\n\n- **Zustand**: https://zustand.docs.pmnd.rs/\n- **GitHub**: https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand\n- **TypeScript Guide**: https://zustand.docs.pmnd.rs/guides/typescript\n- **Context7 Library ID**: `/pmndrs/zustand`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:53:12.545Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing efficient state management in React applications.","zh":"非常适合需要在React应用中高效管理状态的前端代理。","ja":"Reactアプリケーションで状態管理を効率的に行う必要があるフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。","ko":"리액트 애플리케이션에서 상태 관리를 효율적으로 처리해야 하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes frontend que necesitan un manejo de estado eficiente en aplicaciones de React.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents frontend ayant besoin d''une gestion d''état efficace dans les applications React.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die ein effizientes Zustandsmanagement in React-Anwendungen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de gerenciamento de estado eficiente em aplicações React.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым необходим эффективный управление состоянием в приложениях React.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأمامية الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة حالة فعالة في تطبيقات React."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage global state with ease using zustand''s simple and scalable API, supporting React 18-19 and TypeScript 5+, enabling seamless integration with existing React projects.","zh":"赋予代理使用zustand的简单且可扩展的API轻松管理全局状态，支持React 18-19和TypeScript 5+，实现与现有React项目的无缝集成。","ja":"zustandのシンプルでスケーラブルなAPIを使用してグローバル状態を簡単に管理できるようにエージェントをエンパワーメントし、React 18-19とTypeScript 5+をサポートして、既存のReactプロジェクトとのシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"zustand의 단순하고 확장 가능한 API를 사용하여 글로벌 상태를 쉽게 관리할 수 있도록 에이전트를 에ンパ워하며, 리액트 18-19와 타입스크립트 5+를 지원하여 기존 리액트 프로젝트와의 무장해적 통합을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar el estado global con facilidad utilizando la API simple y escalable de zustand, compatible con React 18-19 y TypeScript 5+, lo que permite una integración perfecta con proyectos de React existentes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer l''état global avec facilité en utilisant l''API simple et évolutivité de zustand, prenant en charge React 18-19 et TypeScript 5+, permettant ainsi une intégration sans problème avec les projets React existants.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, den globalen Zustand mühelos mit zustands einfacher und skalierbarer API zu verwalten, die React 18-19 und TypeScript 5+ unterstützt, was eine nahtlose Integration mit bestehenden React-Projekten ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar o estado global com facilidade usando a API simples e escalável do zustand, suportando React 18-19 e TypeScript 5+, permitindo integração perfeita com projetos React existentes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять глобальным состоянием с легкостью, используя простой и масштабируемый API zustand, поддерживающий React 18-19 и TypeScript 5+, обеспечивая бесшовную интеграцию с существующими проектами React.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة الحالة العالمية بسهولة باستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات البسيطة والموسعة من zustand، ودعم React 18-19 وTypeScript 5+، وتمكين التكامل السلس مع مشاريع React الحالية."},"useCases":{"en":["Managing global state in complex React applications","Implementing efficient state updates with zustand''s set function","Creating type-safe stores with TypeScript support"],"zh":["在复杂的React应用中管理全局状态","使用zustand的set函数实现高效的状态更新","使用TypeScript支持创建类型安全的存储"],"ja":["複雑なReactアプリケーションでグローバル状態を管理する","zustandのset関数を使用して効率的な状態更新を実装する","TypeScriptサポートを使用してタイプセーフなストアを作成する"],"ko":["복잡한 리액트 애플리케이션에서 글로벌 상태를 관리하는 것","zustand의 set 함수를 사용하여 효율적인 상태 업데이트를 구현하는 것","타입스크립트 지원을 사용하여 타입 안전한 스토어를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Gestión del estado global en aplicaciones React complejas","Implementación de actualizaciones de estado eficientes con la función set de zustand","Creación de almacenes seguros con soporte de TypeScript"],"fr":["Gestion de l''état global dans des applications React complexes","Mise en œuvre de mises à jour d''état efficaces avec la fonction set de zustand","Création de magasins sécurisés avec prise en charge de TypeScript"],"de":["Verwaltung des globalen Zustands in komplexen React-Anwendungen","Implementierung effizienter Zustandsaktualisierungen mit der Set-Funktion von zustand","Erstellung von Typ-sicheren Stores mit TypeScript-Unterstützung"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de estado global em aplicações React complexas","Implementação de atualizações de estado eficientes com a função set do zustand","Criação de lojas seguras com suporte ao TypeScript"],"ru":["Управление глобальным состоянием в сложных приложениях React","Реализация эффективных обновлений состояния с помощью функции set zustand","Создание безопасных магазинов с поддержкой TypeScript"],"ar":["إدارة الحالة العالمية في تطبيقات React المعقدة","تنفيذ تحديثات الحالة الفعالة باستخدام دالة zustand set","إنشاء متاجر آمنة مع دعم TypeScript"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React 18-19","TypeScript 5+ required","Limited to frontend state management"],"zh":["需要React 18-19","需要TypeScript 5+","仅限前端状态管理"],"ja":["React 18-19が必要","TypeScript 5+が必要","フロントエンド状態管理のみ"],"ko":["리액트 18-19가 필요합니다","타입스크립트 5+가 필요합니다","프론트엔드 상태 관리만 해당"],"es":["Requiere React 18-19","Se requiere TypeScript 5+","Limitado a la gestión de estado frontend"],"fr":["Nécessite React 18-19","TypeScript 5+ requis","Limité à la gestion d''état frontend"],"de":["Benötigt React 18-19","TypeScript 5+ erforderlich","Begrenzt auf Frontend-Zustandsverwaltung"],"pt":["Requer React 18-19","TypeScript 5+ é necessário","Limitado ao gerenciamento de estado frontend"],"ru":["Требуется React 18-19","Требуется TypeScript 5+","Ограничен управлением состоянием frontend"],"ar":["يتطلب React 18-19","مطلوب TypeScript 5+","محدود لإدارة حالة الواجهة الأمامية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
