,"en":"unix-review"},"description":{"zh":"Unix 代码审查技能按照 Eric S. Raymond 的《The Art of Unix Programming》原则审查代码，关注代码的模块性和可读性","ja":"Unix コードレビュースキルは、Eric S. Raymond の『The Art of Unix Programming』の原則に従ってコードをレビューし、コードのモジュール性と可読性に焦点を当てています","ko":"유닉스 코드 리뷰 스킬은 Eric S. Raymond 의 『The Art of Unix Programming』의 원칙에 따라 코드를 리뷰하며, 코드의 모듈성과 가독성에 집중합니다","es":"La revisión de código Unix se basa en los principios de Eric S. Raymond. Aprende a aplicarlos para mejorar tu código","fr":"L''examen de code Unix repose sur les principes d''Eric S. Raymond. Apprenez à les appliquer pour améliorer votre code","de":"Die Unix-Code-Überprüfung basiert auf den Prinzipien von Eric S. Raymond. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie anwenden, um Ihren Code zu verbessern","pt":"A revisão de código Unix é uma ferramenta que aplica os princípios do Unix para melhorar a qualidade do código. Ela analisa o código e fornece feedback","ru":"Проверка кода Unix - это инструмент, который применяет принципы Unix для улучшения качества кода. Он анализирует код и предоставляет обратную связь","ar":"استعراض شفرة يونكس هو أداة تطبق مبادئ يونكس لتحسين جودة الشفرة. وهي تحليل الشفرة وتقدم ملاحظات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["按照 Unix 哲理原则审查代码","关注代码的模块性和可读性","支持 Glob 和 Grep 来发现源文件","支持读取单个文件或目录","根据代码语言和模式进行审查"],"ja":["Unix 哲学の原則に従ってコードをレビューする","コードのモジュール性と可読性に焦点を当てる","Glob と Grep を使用してソースファイルを発見する","単一のファイルまたはディレクトリを読み取ることができる","コード言語とパターンに基づいてレビューする"],"ko":["유닉스 철학의 원칙에 따라 코드를 리뷰한다","코드의 모듈성과 가독성에 집중한다","Glob 및 Grep을 사용하여 소스 파일을 발견한다","단일 파일 또는 디렉토리를 읽을 수 있다","코드 언어 및 패턴에 따라 리뷰한다"],"es":["Revisión de código modular","Aplicación de los 17 principios de Unix","Uso de Glob y Grep para descubrir archivos fuente","Análisis de patrones y lenguaje de programación","Mejora de la eficiencia y calidad del código"],"fr":["Examen de code modulaire","Application des 17 principes d''Unix","Utilisation de Glob et Grep pour découvrir les fichiers source","Analyse de motifs et de langage de programmation","Amélioration de l''efficacité et de la qualité du code"],"de":["Modulare Code-Überprüfung","Anwendung der 17 Unix-Prinzipien","Verwendung von Glob und Grep zur Entdeckung von Quellcode-Dateien","Analyse von Mustern und Programmiersprache","Verbesserung der Effizienz und Qualität des Codes"],"pt":["Análise de código baseada nos 17 princípios do Unix","Detecção de problemas de modularidade e legibilidade","Análise de padrões de código e sugestões de melhoria","Suporte a múltiplos arquivos e diretórios","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Анализ кода на основе 17 принципов Unix","Обнаружение проблем модульности и читаемости","Анализ шаблонов кода и предложения улучшения","Поддержка нескольких файлов и каталогов","Интеграция с инструментами разработки"],"ar":["تحليل الشفرة بناءً على مبادئ يونكس الـ 17","اكتشاف مشاكل التركيب والقراءة","تحليل أنماط الشفرة واقتراحات التحسين","دعم الملفات والمجلدات المتعددة","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Unix 代码审查","代码质量","可维护性","模块性","可读性","Glob","Grep"],"ja":["Unix コードレビュー","コード品質","保守性","モジュール性","可読性","Glob","Grep"],"ko":["유닉스 코드 리뷰","코드 품질","유지 보수성","모듈성","가독성","Glob","Grep"],"es":["revisión de código unix","principios de unix","código modular","eficiencia del código","mejora de código","eric s raymond","the art of unix programming"],"fr":["examen de code unix","principes d''unix","code modulaire","efficacité du code","amélioration de code","eric s raymond","l''art de la programmation unix"],"de":["unix-code-überprüfung","unix-prinzipien","modularer code","code-effizienz","code-verbesserung","eric s raymond","die kunst der unix-programmierung"],"pt":["revisão de código unix","princípios do unix","análise de código","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade de código","modularidade","legibilidade"],"ru":["проверка кода unix","принципы unix","анализ кода","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","модульность","читаемость"],"ar":["استعراض شفرة يونكس","مبادئ يونكس","تحليل الشفرة","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الشفرة","التركيب","القراءة"]}},"owner":"gdgeek","repo":"murder-mystery-generator","repoPath":"gdgeek/murder-mystery-generator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"unix-review","description":"Review code against Eric S. Raymonds Unix philosophy from The Art of Unix Programming","bodyPreview":"# Unix Philosophy Code Review\n\nYou are a code reviewer applying the principles from Eric S. Raymond''s *The Art of Unix Programming*. Review the code at the path provided by the user argument.\n\nIf the argument is a directory, use Glob and Grep to discover source files, then Read the most important ones. If it''s a single file, Read it directly. Focus your review on the language and patterns actually used in the code.\n\n## The 17 Unix Rules to Evaluate\n\n### 1. Rule of Modularity\nWrite simple parts c","body":"# Unix Philosophy Code Review\n\nYou are a code reviewer applying the principles from Eric S. Raymond''s *The Art of Unix Programming*. Review the code at the path provided by the user argument.\n\nIf the argument is a directory, use Glob and Grep to discover source files, then Read the most important ones. If it''s a single file, Read it directly. Focus your review on the language and patterns actually used in the code.\n\n## The 17 Unix Rules to Evaluate\n\n### 1. Rule of Modularity\nWrite simple parts connected by clean interfaces. Look for:\n- Are modules/functions focused on one thing?\n- Are interfaces between components narrow and well-defined?\n- Could a module be understood in isolation?\n\n### 2. Rule of Clarity\nClarity is better than cleverness. Look for:\n- Is the code straightforward to read?\n- Are clever tricks used where simple code would work?\n- Are names descriptive and intention-revealing?\n\n### 3. Rule of Composition\nDesign programs to be connected with other programs. Look for:\n- Can components be combined with others?\n- Are inputs/outputs in standard, parseable formats?\n- Do components avoid unnecessary assumptions about their callers?\n\n### 4. Rule of Separation\nSeparate policy from mechanism; separate interfaces from engines. Look for:\n- Is configuration/policy mixed into core logic?\n- Are UI/API layers entangled with business logic?\n- Could the mechanism be reused with different policy?\n\n### 5. Rule of Simplicity\nDesign for simplicity; add complexity only where you must. Look for:\n- Features that aren''t used or justified\n- Abstractions that don''t earn their complexity\n- Code that could be simpler without losing functionality\n\n### 6. Rule of Parsimony\nWrite a big program only when nothing else will do. Look for:\n- Could this be broken into smaller, independent tools/modules?\n- Are there monolithic components that do too much?\n- Could a library replace custom code?\n\n### 7. Rule of Transparency\nDesign for visibility to make inspection and debugging easy. Look for:\n- Can you tell what the program is doing by looking at its output/logs?\n- Is internal state inspectable?\n- Are data flows easy to trace?\n\n### 8. Rule of Robustness\nRobustness is the child of transparency and simplicity. Look for:\n- Does the code handle edge cases through simplicity rather than special-case logic?\n- Is error handling straightforward?\n- Are failure modes obvious from the code structure?\n\n### 9. Rule of Representation\nFold knowledge into data so program logic can be stupid and robust. Look for:\n- Complex conditional logic that could be replaced by data structures (tables, maps, configs)\n- Hardcoded behavior that could be data-driven\n- State machines encoded as spaghetti if/else instead of transition tables\n\n### 10. Rule of Least Surprise\nIn interface design, always do the least surprising thing. Look for:\n- Functions/methods that do more than their name implies\n- Surprising side effects\n- Inconsistent conventions within the codebase\n- APIs that violate common expectations for the language/framework\n\n### 11. Rule of Silence\nWhen a program has nothing surprising to say, it should say nothing. Look for:\n- Excessive logging or debug output in normal operation\n- Noisy success messages\n- Output that makes it hard to spot important information\n\n### 12. Rule of Repair\nWhen you must fail, fail noisily and as soon as possible. Look for:\n- Silent error swallowing (bare except, empty catch blocks)\n- Errors that propagate far from their source before being noticed\n- Fallback behavior that masks real problems\n- Missing validation at system boundaries\n\n### 13. Rule of Economy\nProgrammer time is expensive; conserve it in preference to machine time. Look for:\n- Premature optimization that hurts readability\n- Manual processes that could be automated\n- Boilerplate that a tool or abstraction could eliminate\n\n### 14. Rule of Generation\nAvoid hand-hacking; write programs to write programs when you can. Look for:\n- Repetitive code that could be generated\n- Boilerplate that a metaprogramming approach could handle\n- Data transformations done manually that could be templated\n\n### 15. Rule of Optimization\nPrototype before polishing. Get it working before you optimize it. Look for:\n- Premature optimization (complex caching, bit manipulation, etc.) without evidence of need\n- Micro-optimizations that sacrifice clarity\n- Missing the actual bottleneck while optimizing the wrong thing\n\n### 16. Rule of Diversity\nDistrust all claims of \"one true way.\" Look for:\n- Unnecessary lock-in to specific implementations\n- Code that can''t adapt to alternative approaches\n- Over-reliance on a single library/framework when the coupling isn''t justified\n\n### 17. Rule of Extensibility\nDesign for the future, because it will be here sooner than you think. Look for:\n- Hardcoded values that should be configurable\n- Closed designs that can''t accommodate new requirements\n- Missing extension points where growth is likely\n\n## Unix-Specific Anti-Patterns\n\nAlso check for these common anti-patterns:\n- **Binary data formats** where text would work — text is universal, inspectable, and composable\n- **Monolithic designs** where pipeable components would work — small tools chained together beat one big program\n- **Configuration baked into code** — separate config from logic so behavior can change without recompilation\n- **Noisy logging** — quiet on success, noisy on failure (Rule of Silence + Rule of Repair)\n- **Silent failures** — swallowing errors instead of failing fast and loud\n\n## Output Format\n\nStructure your review as follows:\n\n### Summary\n1-2 sentences on how well the code follows Unix philosophy.\n\n### Rule Violations\nGroup findings by rule. For each violation:\n- Which rule is violated\n- The specific location (file:line or function/class name)\n- What the violation is\n- A concrete suggestion for improvement\n\nOnly flag genuine violations — do not manufacture issues. If a rule doesn''t meaningfully apply to this code, skip it.\n\n### Unix Anti-Patterns\nList any anti-patterns detected with specific locations and brief explanations.\n\n### Refactoring Suggestions\nConcrete, actionable steps to better align with Unix philosophy. Prioritize by impact.\n\n### What Follows Unix Philosophy Well\nCall out things the code does right — good modularity, clean composition, transparent operation, smart use of data structures, etc. Be specific.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:55:53.079Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents applying Unix philosophy principles to evaluate modularity and simplicity in codebases.","zh":"非常适合应用 Unix 哲学原则来评估代码库模块化与简洁性的代码审查智能体。","ja":"Unix哲学の原則を適用してコードベースのモジュール性と単純さを評価するコードレビューエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Unix 철학 원칙을 적용하여 코드베이스의 모듈성과 단순성을 평가하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 완벽하게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Revisión de Código que aplican principios de la filosofía Unix para evaluar la modularidad y la simplicidad en los repositorios de código.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Revue de Code appliquant les principes de la philosophie Unix pour évaluer la modularité et la simplicité dans les bases de code.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die die Unix-Philosophie-Prinzipien anwenden, um Modularität und Einfachheit in Codebasen zu bewerten.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que aplicam princípios da filosofia Unix para avaliar a modularidade e a simplicidade em repositórios de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, применяющих принципы философии Unix для оценки модульности и простоты в кодовых базах.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الشفرة الذي يطبق مبادئ فلسفة يونكس لتقييم الإمكانية والتوجيه في قواعد البيانات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply Eric S. Raymond''s 17 Unix Rules, utilizing Glob and Grep for source file discovery, and focusing on language and patterns used in the code, including modularity and simplicity principles.","zh":"使智能体能够应用 Eric S. Raymond 提出的 17 条 Unix 规则，利用 Glob 和 Grep 进行源代码文件发现，并重点关注代码中使用的语言和模式，包括模块化与简洁性原则。","ja":"エージェントがEric S. Raymondの17のUnixルールを適用し、GlobとGrepを利用したソースファイルの発見を行い、モジュール性と単純性の原則を含むコードで使用される言語とパターンに焦点を当てることを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 Eric S. Raymond의 17가지 Unix 규칙을 적용하고, Glob 및 Grep을 활용한 소스 파일 발견을 수행하며, 모듈성 및 단순성 원칙을 포함한 코드에서 사용되는 언어와 패턴에 집중할 수 있도록 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar las 17 Reglas Unix de Eric S. Raymond, utilizando Glob y Grep para el descubrimiento de archivos fuente, y centrándose en el lenguaje y los patrones utilizados en el código, incluyendo principios de modularidad y simplicidad.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer les 17 Règles Unix d''Eric S. Raymond, en utilisant Glob et Grep pour la découverte de fichiers source, et en se concentrant sur le langage et les modèles utilisés dans le code, y compris les principes de modularité et de simplicité.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die 17 Unix-Regeln von Eric S. Raymond anzuwenden, indem Glob und Grep für die Quellcode-Datei-Erkennung verwendet werden, und sich auf die in Code verwendete Sprache und Muster konzentrieren, einschließlich Modularitäts- und Einfachheitsprinzipien.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicarem as 17 Regras Unix de Eric S. Raymond, utilizando Glob e Grep para descoberta de arquivos de origem e se concentrando na linguagem e nos padrões utilizados no código, incluindo princípios de modularidade e simplicidade.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять 17 правил Unix Эрика С. Рэймонда, используя Glob и Grep для обнаружения исходных файлов и сосредотачиваясь на языке и паттернах, используемых в коде, включая принципы модульности и простоты.","ar":"يمكن للعميل تطبيق قواعد يونكس السبعة عشر لإيريك س رايموند، واستخدام.glob و grep لاكتشاف الملفات المصدريه والتركيز علي اللغه والانماط المستخدمة في الشفرة، بما في ذلك مبادئ الوحدات والبساطه"},"useCases":{"en":["Evaluating code modularity in Unix-based systems","Applying the Rule of Modularity to simplify codebases","Discovering source files using Glob and Grep for efficient code review"],"zh":["评估基于 Unix 的系统中的代码模块化","应用模块化规则以简化代码库","使用 Glob 和 Grep 发现源代码文件以实现高效代码审查"],"ja":["Unixベースシステムにおけるコードのモジュール性の評価","モジュール性のルールを適用してコードベースを簡素化","効率的なコードレビューのためのGlobとGrepを使用したソースファイルの発見"],"ko":["Unix 기반 시스템에서 코드 모듈성 평가","모듈성 규칙 적용으로 코드베이스 단순화","효율적인 코드 리뷰를 위한 Glob 및 Grep을 사용한 소스 파일 발견"],"es":["Evaluación de la modularidad del código en sistemas basados en Unix","Aplicación de la Regla de Modularidad para simplificar los repositorios de código","Descubrimiento de archivos fuente utilizando Glob y Grep para una revisión de código eficiente"],"fr":["Évaluation de la modularité du code dans les systèmes basés sur Unix","Application de la Règle de Modularité pour simplifier les bases de code","Découverte de fichiers source en utilisant Glob et Grep pour une revue de code efficace"],"de":["Bewertung der Modularität des Codes in Unix-basierten Systemen","Anwendung der Modularitätsregel zur Vereinfachung von Codebasen","Entdeckung von Quellcode-Dateien unter Verwendung von Glob und Grep für eine effiziente Code-Überprüfung"],"pt":["Avaliar a modularidade do código em sistemas baseados em Unix","Aplicar a Regra da Modularidade para simplificar repositórios de código","Descobrir arquivos de origem usando Glob e Grep para revisão de código eficiente"],"ru":["Оценка модульности кода в системах на основе Unix","Применение правила модульности для упрощения кодовых баз","Обнаружение исходных файлов с помощью Glob и Grep для эффективного обзора кода"],"ar":["تقييم الوحدات في شفرة النظام المبني على يونكس","تطبيق قانون الوحدات لتسهيل قواعد البيانات","اكتشاف الملفات المصدريه باستخدام.glob و grep لمراجعة شفرة فعالة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to file system or directory path","Limited to evaluating code in a Unix environment","Focus on Unix-specific principles and tools like Glob and Grep"],"zh":["需要访问文件系统或目录路径","仅限于在 Unix 环境中评估代码","专注于 Glob 和 Grep 等 Unix 特有原则和工具"],"ja":["ファイルシステムまたはディレクトリパスへのアクセスが必要","Unix環境でのコード評価に限定される","GlobやGrepなどのUnix固有の原則とツールに焦点を当てている"],"ko":["파일 시스템 또는 디렉토리 경로에 대한 액세스 필요","Unix 환경에서의 코드 평가로 제한됨","Glob 및 Grep과 같은 Unix 특정 원칙 및 도구에 집중"],"es":["Requiere acceso al sistema de archivos o ruta del directorio","Limitado a la evaluación de código en un entorno Unix","Enfocarse en principios y herramientas específicos de Unix como Glob y Grep"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au système de fichiers ou au chemin du répertoire","Limité à l''évaluation du code dans un environnement Unix","Se concentrer sur les principes et les outils spécifiques à Unix tels que Glob et Grep"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf Dateisystem oder Verzeichnispfad","Begrenzt auf die Bewertung von Code in einer Unix-Umgebung","Fokus auf Unix-spezifische Prinzipien und Tools wie Glob und Grep"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao sistema de arquivos ou caminho do diretório","Limitado à avaliação de código em um ambiente Unix","Foco em princípios e ferramentas específicos do Unix, como Glob e Grep"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к файловой системе или пути к директории","Ограничен оценкой кода в среде Unix","Фокус на принципах и инструментах, специфичных для Unix, таких как Glob и Grep"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام الملفات أو مسار الدليل","محدود لتقييم الشفرة في بيئة يونكس","التركيز علي مبادئ وأدوات محددة لليونكس، مثل.glob و grep"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit/vulnerability-scanner', 'community', 'HaoNgo232', 'agent-bridge-kit', 'HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit', 'vulnerability-scanner', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z', '2026-02-18T13:56:27.558Z', NULL, '{"id":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit/vulnerability-scanner","name":"vulnerability-scanner","description":{"zh":"漏洞扫描工具是一种自动化安全验证工具，帮助开发者检测并修复安全漏洞","ja":"脆弱性スキャナーは自動化セキュリティ検証ツールであり、開発者がセキュリティの脆弱性を検出して修復するのに役立ちます","ko":"취약점 스キャ너는 자동화된 보안 검증 도구로 개발자가 보안 취약점을 감지하고 수정하는 데 도움을 줍니다","es":"El escáner de vulnerabilidades es una herramienta para identificar y corregir debilidades en tu código","fr":"L''analyseur de vulnérabilités est un outil pour identifier et corriger les faiblesses dans votre code","de":"Der Sicherheitslückenscanner ist ein Tool zum Erkennen und Beheben von Schwachstellen in Ihrem Code","pt":"O Vulnerability Scanner é uma ferramenta de segurança que ajuda a identificar vulnerabilidades em projetos de código aberto.","ru":"Сканирование уязвимостей - это инструмент безопасности, который помогает выявить уязвимости в проектах с открытым исходным кодом.","ar":"ماسح التهديدات هو أداة أمان تساعد في اكتشاف الثغرات في مشاريع الكود المفتوح.","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"漏洞扫描工具 - 自动化安全验证","ja":"脆弱性スキャナー - 自動化セキュリティ検証","ko":"취약점 스キャ너 - 자동화된 보안 검증","es":"Escáner de vulnerabilidades: protege tu código","fr":"Analyseur de vulnérabilités: sécurisez votre code","de":"Sicherheitslückenscanner: schützen Sie Ihren Code","pt":"Vulnerability Scanner: Ferramenta de Segurança","ru":"Сканирование уязвимостей: инструмент безопасности","ar":"ماسح التهديدات: أداة أمان","en":"vulnerability-scanner"},"description":{"zh":"漏洞扫描工具是一种自动化安全验