vos importantes","Foco na linguagem e padrões utilizados no código"],"ru":["Анализ кода на основе принципов SOLID","Код-ревью в директориях и отдельных файлах","Использование Glob и Grep для обнаружения исходных файлов","Чтение важных файлов","Фокус на языке и паттернах, использованных в коде"],"ar":["تحليل الكود المستند إلى مبادئ SOLID","استعراض الكود في المجلدات والملفات الفردية","استخدام Glob و Grep لاكتشاف ملفات المصدر","قراءة الملفات المهمة","التركيز على اللغة والنماذج المستخدمة في الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["敏捷代码审查","SOLID原则","语言模式","代码质量","敏捷软件开发","代码审查实践"],"ja":["アジャイルコードレビュー","SOLID原則","言語パターン","コード品質","アジャイルソフトウェア開発","コードレビュー実践"],"ko":["敏捷 코드 리뷰","SOLID 원칙","언어 패턴","코드 품질","敏捷 소프트웨어 개발","코드 리뷰 실践"],"es":["revisión de código ágil","principios SOLID","desarrollo de software ágil","calidad del código","patrones de diseño","análisis de código","mejora del código","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["révision de code agile","principes SOLID","développement de logiciels agiles","qualité du code","modèles de conception","analyse de code","amélioration du code","outils de développement"],"de":["agile Code-Review","SOLID-Prinzipien","agile Softwareentwicklung","Code-Qualität","Entwurfsmuster","Code-Analyse","Code-Verbesserung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["revisão ágil de código","princípios SOLID","análise de código","revisão de código","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade de software"],"ru":["агилевая код-ревью","принципы SOLID","анализ кода","код-ревью","разработка программного обеспечения","качество программного обеспечения"],"ar":["استعراض الكود المُتحرك","مبادئ SOLID","تحليل الكود","استعراض الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"gdgeek","repo":"murder-mystery-generator","repoPath":"gdgeek/murder-mystery-generator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agile-review","description":"Review code against Robert C. Martins Agile/SOLID principles from Agile Software Development: Principles, Patterns, and Practices","bodyPreview":"# Agile Code Review\n\nYou are a code reviewer applying the principles from Robert C. Martin''s *Agile Software Development: Principles, Patterns, and Practices*. Review the code at the path provided by the user argument.\n\nIf the argument is a directory, use Glob and Grep to discover source files, then Read the most important ones. If it''s a single file, Read it directly. Focus your review on the language and patterns actually used in the code.\n\n## Principles to Evaluate\n\n### SOLID Principles (Clas","body":"# Agile Code Review\n\nYou are a code reviewer applying the principles from Robert C. Martin''s *Agile Software Development: Principles, Patterns, and Practices*. Review the code at the path provided by the user argument.\n\nIf the argument is a directory, use Glob and Grep to discover source files, then Read the most important ones. If it''s a single file, Read it directly. Focus your review on the language and patterns actually used in the code.\n\n## Principles to Evaluate\n\n### SOLID Principles (Class/Module Design)\n\n- **SRP (Single Responsibility Principle)**: Does each class/module/function have one and only one reason to change? Look for classes doing too many things, functions with multiple unrelated responsibilities, or modules mixing concerns (e.g., I/O mixed with business logic).\n\n- **OCP (Open-Closed Principle)**: Is the code open for extension but closed for modification? Could new behavior be added without changing existing code? Look for long if/elif chains or switch statements that would need modification for new cases.\n\n- **LSP (Liskov Substitution Principle)**: Can subtypes replace their base types without breaking behavior? Look for subclasses that override methods in ways that violate the base class contract, or isinstance checks that indicate broken substitutability.\n\n- **ISP (Interface Segregation Principle)**: Are interfaces focused and client-specific rather than general-purpose? Look for \"fat\" interfaces/base classes that force implementers to depend on methods they don''t use.\n\n- **DIP (Dependency Inversion Principle)**: Do high-level modules depend on abstractions rather than concrete implementations? Look for direct instantiation of dependencies, hardcoded class references, or missing dependency injection.\n\n### Package/Component Principles\n\n- **REP (Release-Reuse Equivalency)**: Is the unit of reuse the unit of release? Are reusable components properly packaged?\n\n- **CCP (Common Closure Principle)**: Do classes that change together live together? Look for changes that would require touching many unrelated modules.\n\n- **CRP (Common Reuse Principle)**: Do classes that are used together live together? Look for packages where clients only use a small fraction of what''s inside.\n\n- **ADP (Acyclic Dependencies Principle)**: Are there circular dependencies between modules/packages? Trace import chains for cycles.\n\n- **SDP (Stable Dependencies Principle)**: Do dependencies point toward stability? Volatile modules should not be depended upon by many others.\n\n- **SAP (Stable Abstractions Principle)**: Are stable packages abstract? Are unstable packages concrete? Highly-depended-upon modules should define abstractions.\n\n### Code Smells to Flag\n\n- **Rigidity**: Would a simple change cascade through many modules?\n- **Fragility**: Do changes in one area break unrelated areas?\n- **Immobility**: Is code hard to reuse because it''s entangled with its context?\n- **Viscosity**: Is it easier to do the wrong thing than the right thing? (e.g., copy-paste is easier than proper abstraction)\n- **Needless Complexity**: Are there speculative generalizations or over-engineered abstractions not justified by current requirements?\n- **Needless Repetition**: Is there duplicated code or logic that should be consolidated?\n- **Opacity**: Is the code hard to understand? Are names unclear? Is intent hidden?\n\n### Design Patterns to Suggest (Only When They Clearly Fit)\n\nWhen a specific problem would benefit from a pattern, suggest it:\n- **Command**: For undoable operations or request queuing\n- **Strategy**: For interchangeable algorithms behind a common interface\n- **Template Method**: For algorithms with varying steps\n- **Facade**: For simplifying complex subsystem interfaces\n- **Mediator**: For reducing coupling between many interacting objects\n- **Null Object**: For eliminating null checks with a do-nothing implementation\n\n## Output Format\n\nStructure your review as follows:\n\n### Summary\n1-2 sentences on the overall code quality from an Agile/SOLID perspective.\n\n### Principle Violations\nFor each violation found, state:\n- Which principle is violated\n- The specific location (file:line or function/class name)\n- What the violation is\n- Why it matters\n\nOnly flag genuine violations — do not manufacture issues. If the code is simple enough that a principle doesn''t meaningfully apply, skip it.\n\n### Code Smells\nList any code smells detected with specific locations and brief explanations.\n\n### Refactoring Suggestions\nConcrete, actionable refactoring steps. Where a design pattern would help, name it and sketch how it would apply. Prioritize suggestions by impact.\n\n### What''s Done Well\nCall out things the code does right — good separation of concerns, clean abstractions, clear naming, etc. Be specific.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:56:37.799Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents applying agile principles and SOLID patterns to software development projects.","zh":"非常适合应用敏捷原则和SOLID模式的代码审查代理，用于软件开发项目。","ja":"アジャイル原則とSOLIDパターンを適用したコードレビューエージェントに最適です。","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합하며, 애자일 원칙과 SOLID 패턴을 소프트웨어 개발 프로젝트에 적용합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que aplican principios ágiles y patrones SOLID a proyectos de desarrollo de software.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de revue de code appliquant les principes agiles et les modèles SOLID aux projets de développement de logiciels.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die agile Prinzipien und SOLID-Muster auf Software-Entwicklungsprojekte anwenden.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que aplicam princípios ágeis e padrões SOLID em projetos de desenvolvimento de software.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов код-ревью, применяющих гибкие принципы и шаблоны SOLID в проектах разработки программного обеспечения.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المراجعة للكود الذين يطبقون مبادئ敏捷ة ونماذج SOLID في مشاريع تطوير البرمجيات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to evaluate code quality using Glob and Grep for file discovery, applying principles from Robert C. Martin''s Agile Software Development, and focusing on languages and patterns used in the code, such as SOLID principles.","zh":"赋予代理评估代码质量的能力，使用Glob和Grep进行文件发现，应用罗伯特·C·马丁的《敏捷软件开发》中的原则，并关注代码中使用的语言和模式，例如SOLID原则。","ja":"エージェントにコード品質を評価する能力を与え、GlobとGrepを使用してファイルを発見し、ロバート・C・マーティンの『アジャイルソフトウェア開発』からの原則を適用し、コードで使用される言語やパターン、例えばSOLID原則に焦点を当てます。","ko":"에이전트가 코드 품질을 평가할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 Glob과 Grep를 사용하여 파일을 발견하고, 로버트 C. 마틴의 《애자일 소프트웨어 개발》에서 유래한 원칙을 적용하며, 코드에서 사용되는 언어 및 패턴, 예를 들어 SOLID 원칙에 초점을 맞춥니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a evaluar la calidad del código utilizando Glob y Grep para la detección de archivos, aplicando principios de Desarrollo de Software Ágil de Robert C. Martin y centrándose en los lenguajes y patrones utilizados en el código, como los principios SOLID.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''évaluer la qualité du code en utilisant Glob et Grep pour la découverte de fichiers, en appliquant les principes du Développement de Logiciels Agiles de Robert C. Martin et en se concentrant sur les langages et les modèles utilisés dans le code, tels que les principes SOLID.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Codequalität unter Verwendung von Glob und Grep für die Datei-Erkennung zu bewerten, Prinzipien aus Robert C. Martins Agiler Software-Entwicklung anzuwenden und sich auf die in dem Code verwendeten Sprachen und Muster zu konzentrieren, wie z.B. die SOLID-Prinzipien.","pt":"Permite que os agentes avaliem a qualidade do código usando Glob e Grep para descoberta de arquivos, aplicando princípios do livro Desenvolvimento de Software Ágil de Robert C. Martin, e se concentrando em linguagens e padrões usados no código, como os princípios SOLID.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью оценивать качество кода с помощью Glob и Grep для обнаружения файлов, применяя принципы книги «Гибкая разработка программного обеспечения» Роберта С. Мартина, и фокусируясь на языках и шаблонах, используемых в коде, таких как принципы SOLID.","ar":"يُمكِّن الوكلاء من تقييم جودة الكود باستخدام Glob و Grep لاكتشاف الملفات، وتطبيق مبادئ كتاب روبرت سي مارتن عن تطوير البرمجيات المتنقلة، والتركيز على اللغات وانماط المستخدمة في الكود، مثل مبادئ SOLID."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing codebases for adherence to agile principles","Evaluating directory structures using Glob and Grep","Applying SOLID principles to improve code maintainability"],"zh":["审查代码库以确保遵守敏捷原则","使用Glob和Grep评估目录结构","应用SOLID原则以提高代码的可维护性"],"ja":["アジャイル原則への準拠を確認するためのコードベースのレビュー","GlobとGrepを使用したディレクトリ構造の評価","コードの保守性を高めるためのSOLID原則の適用"],"ko":["애자일 원칙을 준수하는 코드베이스의審查","Glob과 Grep를 사용한 디렉토리 구조의 평가","코드의 유지보수성을 높이기 위한 SOLID 원칙의 적용"],"es":["Revisar las bases de código para el cumplimiento de los principios ágiles","Evaluar estructuras de directorios utilizando Glob y Grep","Aplicar principios SOLID para mejorar la mantenibilidad del código"],"fr":["Réviser les bases de code pour l''adhésion aux principes agiles","Évaluer les structures de répertoires en utilisant Glob et Grep","Appliquer les principes SOLID pour améliorer la maintenabilité du code"],"de":["Codebasen auf die Einhaltung agiler Prinzipien überprüfen","Verzeichnisstrukturen mit Glob und Grep auswerten","SOLID-Prinzipien anwenden, um die Wartbarkeit des Codes zu verbessern"],"pt":["Revisar bases de código para aderência a princípios ágeis","Avaliar estruturas de diretórios usando Glob e Grep","Aplicar princípios SOLID para melhorar a manutenibilidade do código"],"ru":["Просмотр кодовой базы для соблюдения гибких принципов","Оценка структуры директорий с помощью Glob и Grep","Применение принципов SOLID для улучшения поддерживаемости кода"],"ar":["مراجعة قواعد الكود لتطبيق مبادئ التطوير المتنقل","تقييم هياكل الدلائل باستخدام Glob و Grep","تطبيق مبادئ SOLID لتحسين صيانة الكود"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to file system or code repository","Limited to evaluating code in directories or single files provided as arguments"],"zh":["需要访问文件系统或代码仓库","仅限于评估作为参数提供的目录或单个文件中的代码"],"ja":["ファイルシステムまたはコードリポジトリへのアクセスが必要","ディレクトリまたは引数として提供された単一のファイル内のコードの評価のみが可能"],"ko":["파일 시스템 또는 코드 저장소에 대한 액세스가 필요","디렉토리 또는 인수로 제공된 단일 파일 내의 코드의 평가만 가능"],"es":["Requiere acceso al sistema de archivos o al repositorio de código","Limitado a la evaluación del código en directorios o archivos individuales proporcionados como argumentos"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au système de fichiers ou au référentiel de code","Limité à l''évaluation du code dans les répertoires ou les fichiers individuels fournis comme arguments"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Dateisystem oder das Code-Repository","Begrenzt auf die Auswertung von Code in Verzeichnissen oder einzelnen Dateien, die als Argumente bereitgestellt werden"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao sistema de arquivos ou repositório de código","Limitado à avaliação de código em diretórios ou arquivos únicos fornecidos como argumentos"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файловой системе или хранилищу кода","Ограничен оценкой кода в директориях или отдельных файлах, переданных в качестве аргументов"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام الملفات أو مستودع الكود","محدود بتقييم الكود في الدلائل أو الملفات الفردية المقدمة كوسائط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
