토키오 런타임을 사용한 동시성 프로그래밍을 위한 생산 패턴을 제공합니다. 태스크, 채널, 스트림, 에러 핸들링 등을 포함합니다","es":"El patrón de programación asíncrona en Rust permite crear aplicaciones concurrentes y de alto rendimiento con Tokio","fr":"Le modèle d''exécution asynchrone en Rust permet de créer des applications concurrentes et hautes performances avec Tokio","de":"Das asynchrone Muster in Rust ermöglicht die Erstellung von konkurrierenden und leistungsstarken Anwendungen mit Tokio","pt":"Padrões de programação assíncrona em Rust para construir aplicações concorrentes e escaláveis com Tokio","ru":"Шаблоны асинхронного программирования на Rust для создания конкуретных и масштабируемых приложений с Tokio","ar":"نماط البرمجة غير المتزامنة في روست لبناء تطبيقات متوازيّة ومتسامحّة مع الأخطاء مع توكايو","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["任务管理","通道和流的使用","错误处理和调试","性能优化","Tokio运行时集成"],"ja":["タスク管理","チャネルとストリームの使用","エラーハンドリングとデバッグ","パフォーマンス最適化","Tokioランタイムの統合"],"ko":["태스크 관리","채널과 스트림의 사용","에러 핸들링과 디버깅","성능 최적화","토키오 런타임의 통합"],"es":["Ejecución asíncrona con Tokio","Creación de tareas y canales","Manipulación de flujos de datos","Control de errores y excepciones","Depuración y optimización del rendimiento"],"fr":["Exécution asynchrone avec Tokio","Création de tâches et de canaux","Manipulation de flux de données","Contrôle des erreurs et des exceptions","Débogage et optimisation des performances"],"de":["Asynchrone Ausführung mit Tokio","Erstellung von Tasks und Kanälen","Manipulation von Datenströmen","Fehler- und Ausnahmehandling","Fehlersuche und Leistungsoptimierung"],"pt":["Execução assíncrona com Tokio","Trabalho com tarefas e canais","Manipulação de streams e erros","Otimização de desempenho assíncrono","Depuração de código assíncrono"],"ru":["Асинхронное выполнение с Tokio","Работа с задачами и каналами","Обработка потоков и ошибок","Оптимизация асинхронного выполнения","Отладка асинхронного кода"],"ar":["تنفيذ غير متزامن مع توكايو","العمل مع المهام والقنوات","تعامل مع تدفقات والأخطاء","تحسين أداء غير متزامن","تصحيح أخطاء الشفرة غير المتزامنة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust异步编程","Tokio运行时","并发编程","异步模式","任务管理","错误处理","性能优化"],"ja":["Rustアシンクロナスプログラミング","Tokioランタイム","並行プログラミング","アシンクロナスパターン","タスク管理","エラーハンドリング","パフォーマンス最適化"],"ko":["러스트 비동기 프로그래밍","토키오 런타임","동시성 프로그래밍","비동기 패턴","태스크 관리","에러 핸들링","성능 최적화"],"es":["programación asíncrona en Rust","patrones de programación asíncrona","Tokio","tareas asíncronas","canales asíncronos","manipulación de flujos de datos","control de errores","depuración y optimización"],"fr":["programmation asynchrone en Rust","modèles d''exécution asynchrone","Tokio","tâches asynchrones","canaux asynchrones","manipulation de flux de données","contrôle des erreurs","débogage et optimisation"],"de":["asynchrone Programmierung in Rust","asynchrone Muster","Tokio","asynchrone Tasks","asynchrone Kanäle","Manipulation von Datenströmen","Fehler- und Ausnahmehandling","Fehlersuche und Leistungsoptimierung"],"pt":["Rust assíncrono","Tokio","Programação concorrente","Tarefas e canais","Streams e erros","Otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["Rust асинхронный","Tokio","Конкуретное программирование","Задачи и каналы","Потоки и ошибки","Оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["روست غير متزامن","توكايو","برمجة متوازيّة","المهام والقنوات","التدفقات والأخطاء","تحسين الأداء"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.524Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust-async-patterns","description":"Master Rust async programming with Tokio, async traits, error handling, and concurrent patterns. Use when building async Rust applications, implementing concurrent systems, or debugging async code.","bodyPreview":"# Rust Async Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for async Rust programming with Tokio runtime, including tasks, channels, streams, and error handling.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building async Rust applications\n- Implementing concurrent network services\n- Using Tokio for async I/O\n- Handling async errors properly\n- Debugging async code issues\n- Optimizing async performance\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Async Execution Model\n\n```\nFuture (lazy) → poll() → Ready(value) | Pending\n                ↑","body":"# Rust Async Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for async Rust programming with Tokio runtime, including tasks, channels, streams, and error handling.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building async Rust applications\n- Implementing concurrent network services\n- Using Tokio for async I/O\n- Handling async errors properly\n- Debugging async code issues\n- Optimizing async performance\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Async Execution Model\n\n```\nFuture (lazy) → poll() → Ready(value) | Pending\n                ↑           ↓\n              Waker ← Runtime schedules\n```\n\n### 2. Key Abstractions\n\n| Concept    | Purpose                                  |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `Future`   | Lazy computation that may complete later |\n| `async fn` | Function returning impl Future           |\n| `await`    | Suspend until future completes           |\n| `Task`     | Spawned future running concurrently      |\n| `Runtime`  | Executor that polls futures              |\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```toml\n# Cargo.toml\n[dependencies]\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\nfutures = \"0.3\"\nasync-trait = \"0.1\"\nanyhow = \"1.0\"\ntracing = \"0.1\"\ntracing-subscriber = \"0.3\"\n```\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::time::{sleep, Duration};\nuse anyhow::Result;\n\n#[tokio::main]\nasync fn main() -> Result<()> {\n    // Initialize tracing\n    tracing_subscriber::fmt::init();\n\n    // Async operations\n    let result = fetch_data(\"https://api.example.com\").await?;\n    println!(\"Got: {}\", result);\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nasync fn fetch_data(url: &str) -> Result<String> {\n    // Simulated async operation\n    sleep(Duration::from_millis(100)).await;\n    Ok(format!(\"Data from {}\", url))\n}\n```\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Concurrent Task Execution\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::task::JoinSet;\nuse anyhow::Result;\n\n// Spawn multiple concurrent tasks\nasync fn fetch_all_concurrent(urls: Vec<String>) -> Result<Vec<String>> {\n    let mut set = JoinSet::new();\n\n    for url in urls {\n        set.spawn(async move {\n            fetch_data(&url).await\n        });\n    }\n\n    let mut results = Vec::new();\n    while let Some(res) = set.join_next().await {\n        match res {\n            Ok(Ok(data)) => results.push(data),\n            Ok(Err(e)) => tracing::error!(\"Task failed: {}\", e),\n            Err(e) => tracing::error!(\"Join error: {}\", e),\n        }\n    }\n\n    Ok(results)\n}\n\n// With concurrency limit\nuse futures::stream::{self, StreamExt};\n\nasync fn fetch_with_limit(urls: Vec<String>, limit: usize) -> Vec<Result<String>> {\n    stream::iter(urls)\n        .map(|url| async move { fetch_data(&url).await })\n        .buffer_unordered(limit) // Max concurrent tasks\n        .collect()\n        .await\n}\n\n// Select first to complete\nuse tokio::select;\n\nasync fn race_requests(url1: &str, url2: &str) -> Result<String> {\n    select! {\n        result = fetch_data(url1) => result,\n        result = fetch_data(url2) => result,\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Channels for Communication\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::sync::{mpsc, broadcast, oneshot, watch};\n\n// Multi-producer, single-consumer\nasync fn mpsc_example() {\n    let (tx, mut rx) = mpsc::channel::<String>(100);\n\n    // Spawn producer\n    let tx2 = tx.clone();\n    tokio::spawn(async move {\n        tx2.send(\"Hello\".to_string()).await.unwrap();\n    });\n\n    // Consume\n    while let Some(msg) = rx.recv().await {\n        println!(\"Got: {}\", msg);\n    }\n}\n\n// Broadcast: multi-producer, multi-consumer\nasync fn broadcast_example() {\n    let (tx, _) = broadcast::channel::<String>(100);\n\n    let mut rx1 = tx.subscribe();\n    let mut rx2 = tx.subscribe();\n\n    tx.send(\"Event\".to_string()).unwrap();\n\n    // Both receivers get the message\n    let _ = rx1.recv().await;\n    let _ = rx2.recv().await;\n}\n\n// Oneshot: single value, single use\nasync fn oneshot_example() -> String {\n    let (tx, rx) = oneshot::channel::<String>();\n\n    tokio::spawn(async move {\n        tx.send(\"Result\".to_string()).unwrap();\n    });\n\n    rx.await.unwrap()\n}\n\n// Watch: single producer, multi-consumer, latest value\nasync fn watch_example() {\n    let (tx, mut rx) = watch::channel(\"initial\".to_string());\n\n    tokio::spawn(async move {\n        loop {\n            // Wait for changes\n            rx.changed().await.unwrap();\n            println!(\"New value: {}\", *rx.borrow());\n        }\n    });\n\n    tx.send(\"updated\".to_string()).unwrap();\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Async Error Handling\n\n```rust\nuse anyhow::{Context, Result, bail};\nuse thiserror::Error;\n\n#[derive(Error, Debug)]\npub enum ServiceError {\n    #[error(\"Network error: {0}\")]\n    Network(#[from] reqwest::Error),\n\n    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\n    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\n\n    #[error(\"Not found: {0}\")]\n    NotFound(String),\n\n    #[error(\"Timeout after {0:?}\")]\n    Timeout(std::time::Duration),\n}\n\n// Using anyhow for application errors\nasync fn process_request(id: &str) -> Result<Response> {\n    let data = fetch_data(id)\n        .await\n        .context(\"Failed to fetch data\")?;\n\n    let parsed = parse_response(&data)\n        .context(\"Failed to parse response\")?;\n\n    Ok(parsed)\n}\n\n// Using custom errors for library code\nasync fn get_user(id: &str) -> Result<User, ServiceError> {\n    let result = db.query(id).await?;\n\n    match result {\n        Some(user) => Ok(user),\n        None => Err(ServiceError::NotFound(id.to_string())),\n    }\n}\n\n// Timeout wrapper\nuse tokio::time::timeout;\n\nasync fn with_timeout<T, F>(duration: Duration, future: F) -> Result<T, ServiceError>\nwhere\n    F: std::future::Future<Output = Result<T, ServiceError>>,\n{\n    timeout(duration, future)\n        .await\n        .map_err(|_| ServiceError::Timeout(duration))?\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Graceful Shutdown\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::signal;\nuse tokio::sync::broadcast;\nuse tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken;\n\nasync fn run_server() -> Result<()> {\n    // Method 1: CancellationToken\n    let token = CancellationToken::new();\n    let token_clone = token.clone();\n\n    // Spawn task that respects cancellation\n    tokio::spawn(async move {\n        loop {\n            tokio::select! {\n                _ = token_clone.cancelled() => {\n                    tracing::info!(\"Task shutting down\");\n                    break;\n                }\n                _ = do_work() => {}\n            }\n        }\n    });\n\n    // Wait for shutdown signal\n    signal::ctrl_c().await?;\n    tracing::info!(\"Shutdown signal received\");\n\n    // Cancel all tasks\n    token.cancel();\n\n    // Give tasks time to cleanup\n    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(5)).await;\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n// Method 2: Broadcast channel for shutdown\nasync fn run_with_broadcast() -> Result<()> {\n    let (shutdown_tx, _) = broadcast::channel::<()>(1);\n\n    let mut rx = shutdown_tx.subscribe();\n    tokio::spawn(async move {\n        tokio::select! {\n            _ = rx.recv() => {\n                tracing::info!(\"Received shutdown\");\n            }\n            _ = async { loop { do_work().await } } => {}\n        }\n    });\n\n    signal::ctrl_c().await?;\n    let _ = shutdown_tx.send(());\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Async Traits\n\n```rust\nuse async_trait::async_trait;\n\n#[async_trait]\npub trait Repository {\n    async fn get(&self, id: &str) -> Result<Entity>;\n    async fn save(&self, entity: &Entity) -> Result<()>;\n    async fn delete(&self, id: &str) -> Result<()>;\n}\n\npub struct PostgresRepository {\n    pool: sqlx::PgPool,\n}\n\n#[async_trait]\nimpl Repository for PostgresRepository {\n    async fn get(&self, id: &str) -> Result<Entity> {\n        sqlx::query_as!(Entity, \"SELECT * FROM entities WHERE id = $1\", id)\n            .fetch_one(&self.pool)\n            .await\n            .map_err(Into::into)\n    }\n\n    async fn save(&self, entity: &Entity) -> Result<()> {\n        sqlx::query!(\n            \"INSERT INTO entities (id, data) VALUES ($1, $2)\n             ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET data = $2\",\n            entity.id,\n            entity.data\n        )\n        .execute(&self.pool)\n        .await?;\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    async fn delete(&self, id: &str) -> Result<()> {\n        sqlx::query!(\"DELETE FROM entities WHERE id = $1\", id)\n            .execute(&self.pool)\n            .await?;\n        Ok(())\n    }\n}\n\n// Trait object usage\nasync fn process(repo: &dyn Repository, id: &str) -> Result<()> {\n    let entity = repo.get(id).await?;\n    // Process...\n    repo.save(&entity).await\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Streams and Async Iteration\n\n```rust\nuse futures::stream::{self, Stream, StreamExt};\nuse async_stream::stream;\n\n// Create stream from async iterator\nfn numbers_stream() -> impl Stream<Item = i32> {\n    stream! {\n        for i in 0..10 {\n            tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(100)).await;\n            yield i;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Process stream\nasync fn process_stream() {\n    let stream = numbers_stream();\n\n    // Map and filter\n    let processed: Vec<_> = stream\n        .filter(|n| futures::future::ready(*n % 2 == 0))\n        .map(|n| n * 2)\n        .collect()\n        .await;\n\n    println!(\"{:?}\", processed);\n}\n\n// Chunked processing\nasync fn process_in_chunks() {\n    let stream = numbers_stream();\n\n    let mut chunks = stream.chunks(3);\n\n    while let Some(chunk) = chunks.next().await {\n        println!(\"Processing chunk: {:?}\", chunk);\n    }\n}\n\n// Merge multiple streams\nasync fn merge_streams() {\n    let stream1 = numbers_stream();\n    let stream2 = numbers_stream();\n\n    let merged = stream::select(stream1, stream2);\n\n    merged\n        .for_each(|n| async move {\n            println!(\"Got: {}\", n);\n        })\n        .await;\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: Resource Management\n\n```rust\nuse std::sync::Arc;\nuse tokio::sync::{Mutex, RwLock, Semaphore};\n\n// Shared state with RwLock (prefer for read-heavy)\nstruct Cache {\n    data: RwLock<HashMap<String, String>>,\n}\n\nimpl Cache {\n    async fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<String> {\n        self.data.read().await.get(key).cloned()\n    }\n\n    async fn set(&self, key: String, value: String) {\n        self.data.write().await.insert(key, value);\n    }\n}\n\n// Connection pool with semaphore\nstruct Pool {\n    semaphore: Semaphore,\n    connections: Mutex<Vec<Connection>>,\n}\n\nimpl Pool {\n    fn new(size: usize) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            semaphore: Semaphore::new(size),\n            connections: Mutex::new((0..size).map(|_| Connection::new()).collect()),\n        }\n    }\n\n    async fn acquire(&self) -> PooledConnection<''_> {\n        let permit = self.semaphore.acquire().await.unwrap();\n        let conn = self.connections.lock().await.pop().unwrap();\n        PooledConnection { pool: self, conn: Some(conn), _permit: permit }\n    }\n}\n\nstruct PooledConnection<''a> {\n    pool: &''a Pool,\n    conn: Option<Connection>,\n    _permit: tokio::sync::SemaphorePermit<''a>,\n}\n\nimpl Drop for PooledConnection<''_> {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        if let Some(conn) = self.conn.take() {\n            let pool = self.pool;\n            tokio::spawn(async move {\n                pool.connections.lock().await.push(conn);\n            });\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Debugging Tips\n\n```rust\n// Enable tokio-console for runtime debugging\n// Cargo.toml: tokio = { features = [\"tracing\"] }\n// Run: RUSTFLAGS=\"--cfg tokio_unstable\" cargo run\n// Then: tokio-console\n\n// Instrument async functions\nuse tracing::instrument;\n\n#[instrument(skip(pool))]\nasync fn fetch_user(pool: &PgPool, id: &str) -> Result<User> {\n    tracing::debug!(\"Fetching user\");\n    // ...\n}\n\n// Track task spawning\nlet span = tracing::info_span!(\"worker\", id = %worker_id);\ntokio::spawn(async move {\n    // Enters span when polled\n}.instrument(span));\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Use `tokio::select!`** - For racing futures\n- **Prefer channels** - Over shared state when possible\n- **Use `JoinSet`** - For managing multiple tasks\n- **Instrument with tracing** - For debugging async code\n- **Handle cancellation** - Check `CancellationToken`\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t block** - Never use `std::thread::sleep` in async\n- **Don''t hold locks across awaits** - Causes deadlocks\n- **Don''t spawn unboundedly** - Use semaphores for limits\n- **Don''t ignore errors** - Propagate with `?` or log\n- **Don''t forget Send bounds** - For spawned futures\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Tokio Tutorial](https://tokio.rs/tokio/tutorial)\n- [Async Book](https://rust-lang.github.io/async-book/)\n- [Tokio Console](https://github.com/tokio-rs/console)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T13:57:45.359Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents building high-performance concurrent systems with Rust''s async/await paradigm.","zh":"适用于使用Rust的异步/等待范式构建高性能并发系统的AI代理。","ja":"Rustの非同期/待機パラダイムを使用して高性能の並行システムを構築するAIエージェントに適しています。","ko":"Rust의 비동기/대기 패러다임을 사용하여 고성능 병렬 시스템을 구축하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que construyen sistemas concurrentes de alto rendimiento con el paradigma async/await de Rust.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA qui construisent des systèmes concurrents à haute performance avec le paradigme async/await de Rust.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die Hochleistungs-Systeme mit Rusts async/await-Paradigma erstellen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA que constroem sistemas concorrentes de alto desempenho com o paradigma async/await do Rust.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, создающих высокопроизводительные конкьюрентные системы с помощью парадигмы async/await в Rust.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يبني أنظمة متزامنة عالية الأداء باستخدام نمط async/await في Rust."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to implement production-ready async Rust applications using Tokio runtime patterns, including task spawning, channel-based communication, stream processing, and proper async error handling. Provides essential tools for building concurrent network services and debugging async execution flows.","zh":"使代理能够使用Tokio运行时模式实现生产就绪的异步Rust应用程序，包括任务生成、基于通道的通信、流处理和适当的异步错误处理。为构建并发网络服务和调试异步执行流提供了必需的工具。","ja":"エージェントがTokioランタイムパターンを使用して、タスクの生成、チャネルベースの通信、ストリーム処理、および適切な非同期エラーハンドリングを含む、生产就绪の非同期Rustアプリケーションを実装できるようにします。並行ネットワークサービスを構築し、非同期実行フローをデバッグするための基本的なツールを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 Tokio 런타임 패턴을 사용하여 생산 준비가 된 비동기 Rust 애플리케이션을 구현할 수 있도록 합니다. 작업 생성, 채널 기반 통신, 스트림 처리 및 적절한 비동기 오류 처리를 포함합니다. 병렬 네트워크 서비스를 구축하고 비동기 실행 흐름을 디버깅하는 데 필요한 도구를 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar aplicaciones de Rust asíncronas listas para producción utilizando patrones de ejecución de Tokio, incluyendo la creación de tareas, la comunicación basada en canales, el procesamiento de flujos y el control de errores asíncronos adecuado. Proporciona herramientas esenciales para construir servicios de red concurrentes y depurar flujos de ejecución asíncronos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des applications Rust async prêtes pour la production en utilisant des modèles d''exécution Tokio, notamment la création de tâches, la communication basée sur les canaux, le traitement de flux et la gestion correcte des erreurs async. Fournit des outils essentiels pour construire des services de réseau concurrents et déboguer les flux d''exécution async.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, produktionsreife asynchrone Rust-Anwendungen mithilfe von Tokio-Laufzeitmustern zu implementieren, einschließlich der Erstellung von Aufgaben, der kanalbasierten Kommunikation, der Streamverarbeitung und der ordnungsgemäßen asynchronen Fehlerbehandlung. Bietet wesentliche Werkzeuge für den Bau von gleichzeitigen Netzwerkdiensten und das Debuggen von asynchronen Ausführungsflüssen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes implementem aplicações Rust assíncronas prontas para produção usando padrões de tempo de execução do Tokio, incluindo a criação de tarefas, comunicação baseada em canais, processamento de fluxos e tratamento adequado de erros assíncronos. Fornece ferramentas essenciais para construir serviços de rede concorrentes e depurar fluxos de execução assíncronos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать приложения async Rust, готовые к производству, используя шаблоны среды выполнения Tokio, включая создание задач, обмен данными на основе каналов, обработку потоков и правильную обработку асинхронных ошибок. Предоставляет необходимые инструменты для создания сетевых служб с конкьюрентным доступом и отладки потоков асинхронного выполнения.","ar":"يمكن للعميل تنفيذ تطبيقات Rust غير متزامنة جاهزة للإنتاج باستخدام أنماط زمن تشغيل Tokio، بما في ذلك إنشاء المهام والاتصالات القائمة على القنوات ومعالجة التدفقات والت xửير الصحيح للأخطاء غير المتزامنة. يوفر الأدوات الأساسية لبناء خدمات الشبكة المتزامنة وتصحيح خطأ تدفقات التنفيذ غير المتزامن."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing concurrent network services with async I/O","Debugging async code execution issues","Optimizing async task performance in Rust applications","Building channel-based communication between async tasks","Handling complex error propagation in async contexts"],"zh":["使用异步I/O实现并发网络服务","调试异步代码执行问题","在Rust应用程序中优化异步任务性能","在异步任务之间构建基于通道的通信","处理异步上下文中的复杂错误传播"],"ja":["非同期I/Oを使用した並行ネットワークサービスの実装","非同期コードの実行に関する問題のデバッグ","Rustアプリケーションの非同期タスクのパフォーマンスの最適化","非同期タスク間のチャネルベースの通信の構築","非同期コンテキストでの複雑なエラープロパゲーションの処理"],"ko":["비동기 I/O를 사용한 병렬 네트워크 서비스 구현","비동기 코드 실행 문제 디버깅","Rust 애플리케이션의 비동기 작업 성능 최적화","비동기 작업 간 채널 기반 통신 구축","비동기 컨텍스트에서 복잡한 오류 전파 처리"],"es":["Implementar servicios de red concurrentes con E/S asíncrona","Depurar problemas de ejecución de código asíncrono","Optimizar el rendimiento de tareas asíncronas en aplicaciones de Rust","Construir comunicación basada en canales entre tareas asíncronas","Controlar la propagación compleja de errores en contextos asíncronos"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des services de réseau concurrents avec E/S async","Déboguer les problèmes d''exécution de code async","Optimiser les performances des tâches async dans les applications Rust","Construire une communication basée sur les canaux entre les tâches async","Gérer la propagation complexe d''erreurs dans les contextes async"],"de":["Implementierung von gleichzeitigen Netzwerkdiensten mit asynchroner E/A","Debuggen von Problemen bei der Ausführung von asynchronem Code","Optimieren des Leistungsverhaltens asynchroner Aufgaben in Rust-Anwendungen","Aufbau einer kanalbasierten Kommunikation zwischen asynchronen Aufgaben","Handhabung der komplexen Fehlerweiterleitung in asynchronen Kontexten"],"pt":["Implementação de serviços de rede concorrentes com E/S assíncrona","Depuração de problemas de execução de código assíncrono","Otimização do desempenho de tarefas assíncronas em aplicações Rust","Construção de comunicação baseada em canais entre tarefas assíncronas","Tratamento de propagação de erros complexos em contextos assíncronos"],"ru":["Реализация конкьюрентных сетевых служб с асинхронным вводом/выводом","Отладка проблем выполнения асинхронного кода","Оптимизация производительности асинхронных задач в приложениях Rust","Создание обмена данными на основе каналов между асинхронными задачами","Обработка сложной пропагации ошибок в асинхронных контекстах"],"ar":["تنفيذ خدمات الشبكة المتزامنة مع الإدخال/الإخراج غير المتزامن","تصحيح أخطاء تنفيذ الشفرة غير المتزامنة","تحسين أداء المهام غير المتزامنة في تطبيقات Rust","بناء اتصالات قائمة على القنوات بين المهام غير المتزامنة","معالجة انتشار الأخطاء المعقدة في السياقات غير المتزامنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Tokio runtime environment","Assumes Rust async/await knowledge","Focused on production patterns rather than basic async concepts"],"zh":["需要Tokio运行时环境","假设Rust异步/等待知识","专注于生产模式而不是基本异步概念"],"ja":["Tokioランタイム環境が必要","Rustの非同期/待機に関する知識が前提","基本的な非同期概念よりも生産パターンに焦点を当てている"],"ko":["Tokio 런타임 환경이 필요","Rust의 비동기/대기 지식이 전제","기본 비동기 개념보다 생산 패턴에 중점"],"es":["Requiere entorno de ejecución de Tokio","Supone conocimiento de Rust async/await","Centrado en patrones de producción en lugar de conceptos básicos async"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement d''exécution Tokio","Suppose des connaissances en Rust async/await","Axé sur les modèles de production plutôt que sur les concepts async de base"],"de":["Erfordert Tokio-Laufzeitumgebung","Geht von Rust-async/await-Kenntnissen aus","Konzentriert sich auf Produktionsmuster anstelle von grundlegenden asynchronen Konzepten"],"pt":["Requer ambiente de tempo de execução do Tokio","Pressupõe conhecimento de async/await do Rust","Focado em padrões de produção em vez de conceitos básicos assíncronos"],"ru":["Требует среды выполнения Tokio","Предполагает знание async/await в Rust","Сосредоточен на производственных шаблонах, а не на базовых асинхронных понятиях"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة زمن تشغيل Tokio","يفترض معرفة async/await في Rust","يركز على الأنماط الإنتاجية بدلاً من المفاهيم الأساسية غير المتزامنة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
