ws, Worker, CPU","es":"Cloudflare Workflows es una herramienta de automatización en la nube que permite a los desarrolladores crear flujos de trabajo personalizados.","fr":"Cloudflare Workflows est un outil d''automatisation dans le cloud qui permet aux développeurs de créer des flux de travail personnalisés.","de":"Cloudflare Workflows ist ein Automatisierungstool in der Cloud, das es Entwicklern ermöglicht, benutzerdefinierte Workflows zu erstellen.","pt":"Cloudflare Workflows é uma ferramenta de automação de tarefas na nuvem que permite aos desenvolvedores criar fluxos de trabalho personalizados.","ru":"Cloudflare Workflows — это инструмент для автоматизации задач в облаке, который позволяет разработчикам создавать индивидуальные рабочие процессы.","ar":"Cloudflare Workflows هي أداة أتمتة المهام على السحابة تسمح للمطورين بإنشاء تدفقات عمل مخصصة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["100/sec","10,000","Worker","CPU","waitForEvent API","Vitest"],"ja":["100/","10,000","Worker","CPU","waitForEvent API","Vitest"],"ko":["100/","10,000","Worker","CPU","waitForEvent API","Vitest"],"es":["Automatización de tareas en la nube","Creación de flujos de trabajo personalizados","Integración con Cloudflare Worker","Compatibilidad con Vitest para pruebas","Métricas de tiempo de CPU y concurrencia"],"fr":["Automatisation de tâches dans le cloud","Création de flux de travail personnalisés","Intégration avec Cloudflare Worker","Compatibilité avec Vitest pour les tests","Métriques de temps de CPU et de concurrence"],"de":["Automatisierung von Aufgaben in der Cloud","Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Workflows","Integration mit Cloudflare Worker","Unterstützung für Vitest-Tests","CPU-Zeit- und Konkurrenzmessungen"],"pt":["Criação de fluxos de trabalho personalizados","Integração com o Cloudflare Worker","Suporte a até 10.000 instâncias concorrentes","Taxa de criação de instâncias 10x mais rápida","Suporte ao Vitest para testes","Métricas de tempo de CPU"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных рабочих процессов","Интеграция с Cloudflare Worker","Поддержка до 10 000 одновременных экземпляров","Скорость создания экземпляров в 10 раз быстрее","Поддержка Vitest для тестирования","Метрики времени CPU"],"ar":["إنشاء تدفقات عمل مخصصة","التكامل مع Cloudflare Worker","دعم حتى 10،000 مثيل متزامن","معدل إنشاء المثيلات 10 أضعاف أسرع","دعم Vitest للاختبارات","مقياسات وقت المعالج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cloudflare Workflows","Worker","CPU","Cloudflare","Workflows","Serverless","Cloud Computing","DevOps"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workflows","Worker","CPU","Cloudflare","Workflows","Serverless","Cloud Computing","DevOps"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workflows","Worker","CPU","Cloudflare","Workflows","Serverless","Cloud Computing","DevOps"],"es":["Cloudflare Workflows","automatización en la nube","flujos de trabajo personalizados","desarrollo de software en la nube","Cloudflare Worker","Vitest","métricas de rendimiento"],"fr":["Cloudflare Workflows","automatisation dans le cloud","flux de travail personnalisés","développement de logiciels dans le cloud","Cloudflare Worker","Vitest","métriques de performance"],"de":["Cloudflare Workflows","Automatisierung in der Cloud","benutzerdefinierte Workflows","Softwareentwicklung in der Cloud","Cloudflare Worker","Vitest","Leistungsmessungen"],"pt":["Cloudflare Workflows","automação de tarefas na nuvem","desenvolvedores","fluxos de trabalho personalizados","Cloudflare Worker","Vitest","métricas de tempo de CPU"],"ru":["Cloudflare Workflows","автоматизация задач в облаке","разработчики","индивидуальные рабочие процессы","Cloudflare Worker","Vitest","метрики времени CPU"],"ar":["Cloudflare Workflows","أتمتة المهام على السحابة","مطورين","تدفقات عمل مخصصة","Cloudflare Worker","Vitest","مقياسات وقت المعالج"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cloudflare-workflows","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Cloudflare Workflows\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅ (GA since April 2025)\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-09\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.58.0, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **April 2025**: Workflows GA release - waitForEvent API, Vitest testing, CPU time metrics, 4,500 concurrent instances\n- **October 2025**: Instance creation rate 10x faster (100/sec), concurrency increased to 10,000\n- **2025 Lim","body":"# Cloudflare Workflows\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅ (GA since April 2025)\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-09\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.58.0, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **April 2025**: Workflows GA release - waitForEvent API, Vitest testing, CPU time metrics, 4,500 concurrent instances\n- **October 2025**: Instance creation rate 10x faster (100/sec), concurrency increased to 10,000\n- **2025 Limits**: Max steps 1,024, state persistence 1MB/step (100MB-1GB per instance), event payloads 1MB, CPU time 5 min max\n- **Testing**: cloudflare:test module with introspectWorkflowInstance, disableSleeps, mockStepResult, mockEvent modifiers\n- **Platform**: Waiting instances don''t count toward concurrency, retention 3-30 days, subrequests 50-1,000\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Scaffold project\nnpm create cloudflare@latest my-workflow -- --template cloudflare/workflows-starter --git --deploy false\ncd my-workflow\n\n# 2. Configure wrangler.jsonc\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-workflow\",\n  \"main\": \"src/index.ts\",\n  \"compatibility_date\": \"2025-11-25\",\n  \"workflows\": [{\n    \"name\": \"my-workflow\",\n    \"binding\": \"MY_WORKFLOW\",\n    \"class_name\": \"MyWorkflow\"\n  }]\n}\n\n# 3. Create workflow (src/index.ts)\nimport { WorkflowEntrypoint, WorkflowStep, WorkflowEvent } from ''cloudflare:workers'';\n\nexport class MyWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint<Env, Params> {\n  async run(event: WorkflowEvent<Params>, step: WorkflowStep) {\n    const result = await step.do(''process'', async () => { /* work */ });\n    await step.sleep(''wait'', ''1 hour'');\n    await step.do(''continue'', async () => { /* more work */ });\n  }\n}\n\n# 4. Deploy and test\nnpm run deploy\nnpx wrangler workflows instances list my-workflow\n```\n\n**CRITICAL**: Extends `WorkflowEntrypoint`, implements `run()` with `step` methods, bindings in wrangler.jsonc\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues Prevention\n\nThis skill prevents **12** documented errors with Cloudflare Workflows.\n\n### Issue #1: waitForEvent Skips Events After Timeout in Local Dev\n\n**Error**: Events sent after a `waitForEvent()` timeout are ignored in subsequent `waitForEvent()` calls\n**Environment**: Local development (`wrangler dev`) only - works correctly in production\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #11740](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/11740)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Bug in miniflare that was fixed in production (May 2025) but not ported to local emulator. After a timeout, the event queue becomes corrupted for that instance.\n\n**Prevention**:\n- **Test waitForEvent timeout scenarios in production/staging**, not local dev\n- Avoid chaining multiple `waitForEvent()` calls where timeouts are expected\n\n**Example of Bug**:\n```typescript\nexport class MyWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint<Env, Params> {\n  async run(event: WorkflowEvent<Params>, step: WorkflowStep) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n      try {\n        const evt = await step.waitForEvent(`wait-${i}`, {\n          type: ''user-action'',\n          timeout: ''5 seconds''\n        });\n        console.log(`Iteration ${i}: Received event`);\n      } catch {\n        console.log(`Iteration ${i}: Timeout`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n// In wrangler dev:\n// - Iteration 1: ✅ receives event\n// - Iteration 2: ⏱️ times out (expected)\n// - Iteration 3: ❌ does not receive event (BUG - event is sent but ignored)\n```\n\n**Status**: Known bug, fix pending for miniflare.\n\n---\n\n### Issue #2: getPlatformProxy() Fails With Workflow Bindings\n\n**Error**: `MiniflareCoreError [ERR_RUNTIME_FAILURE]: The Workers runtime failed to start`\n**Message**: Worker''s binding refers to service with named entrypoint, but service has no such entrypoint\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #9402](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/9402)\n\n**Why It Happens**: `getPlatformProxy()` from `wrangler` package doesn''t support Workflow bindings (similar to how it handles Durable Objects). This blocks Next.js integration and local CLI scripts.\n\n**Prevention**:\n- **Option 1**: Comment out workflow bindings when using `getPlatformProxy()`\n- **Option 2**: Create separate `wrangler.cli.jsonc` without workflows for CLI scripts\n- **Option 3**: Access workflow bindings directly via deployed worker, not proxy\n\n```typescript\n// Workaround: Separate config for CLI scripts\n// wrangler.cli.jsonc (no workflows)\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-worker\",\n  \"main\": \"src/index.ts\",\n  \"compatibility_date\": \"2025-01-20\"\n  // workflows commented out\n}\n\n// Use in script:\nimport { getPlatformProxy } from ''wrangler'';\nconst { env } = await getPlatformProxy({ configPath: ''./wrangler.cli.jsonc'' });\n```\n\n**Status**: Known limitation, fix planned (filter workflows similar to DOs).\n\n---\n\n### Issue #3: Workflow Instance Lost After Immediate Redirect (Local Dev)\n\n**Error**: Instance ID returned but `instance.not_found` when queried\n**Environment**: Local development (`wrangler dev`) only - works correctly in production\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #10806](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10806)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Returning a redirect immediately after `workflow.create()` causes request to \"soft abort\" before workflow initialization completes (single-threaded execution in dev).\n\n**Prevention**: Use `ctx.waitUntil()` to ensure workflow initialization completes before redirect:\n\n```typescript\nexport default {\n  async fetch(req: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext): Promise<Response> {\n    const workflow = await env.MY_WORKFLOW.create({ params: { userId: ''123'' } });\n\n    // ✅ Ensure workflow initialization completes\n    ctx.waitUntil(workflow.status());\n\n    return Response.redirect(''/dashboard'', 302);\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Status**: Fixed in recent wrangler versions (post-Sept 2025), but workaround still recommended for compatibility.\n\n---\n\n### Issue #4: Vitest Tests Unreliable in CI Environments\n\n**Error**: `[vitest-worker]: Timeout calling \"resolveId\"`\n**Environment**: CI/CD pipelines (GitLab, GitHub Actions) - works locally\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #10600](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10600)\n\n**Why It Happens**: `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` has resource constraint issues in CI containers, affecting workflow tests more than other worker types.\n\n**Prevention**:\n1. Increase `testTimeout` in vitest config:\n   ```typescript\n   export default defineWorkersConfig({\n     test: {\n       testTimeout: 60_000 // Default: 5000ms\n     }\n   });\n   ```\n2. Check CI resource limits (CPU/memory)\n3. Use `isolatedStorage: false` if not testing storage isolation\n4. Consider testing against deployed instances instead of vitest for critical workflows\n\n**Status**: Known issue, investigating (Internal: WOR-945).\n\n---\n\n### Issue #5: Instance restart() and terminate() Not Implemented in Local Dev\n\n**Error**: `Error: Not implemented yet` when calling `instance.restart()` or `instance.terminate()`\n**Environment**: Local development (`wrangler dev`) only - works in production\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #11312](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/11312)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Instance management APIs not yet implemented in miniflare. Additionally, instance status shows `running` even when workflow is sleeping.\n\n**Prevention**: Test instance lifecycle management (pause/resume/terminate) in production or staging environment until local dev support is added.\n\n```typescript\nconst instance = await env.MY_WORKFLOW.get(instanceId);\n\n// ❌ Fails in wrangler dev\nawait instance.restart();    // Error: Not implemented yet\nawait instance.terminate();  // Error: Not implemented yet\n\n// ✅ Works in production\n```\n\n**Status**: Known limitation, no timeline for local dev support.\n\n---\n\n### Issue #6: I/O Must Be Inside step.do() Callbacks\n\n**Error**: `\"Cannot perform I/O on behalf of a different request\"`\n**Source**: Cloudflare runtime behavior\n\n**Why It Happens**: Trying to use I/O objects created in one request context from another request handler.\n\n**Prevention**: Always perform I/O within `step.do()` callbacks:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bad - I/O outside step\nconst response = await fetch(''https://api.example.com/data'');\nconst data = await response.json();\n\nawait step.do(''use data'', async () => {\n  return data;  // This will fail!\n});\n\n// ✅ Good - I/O inside step\nconst data = await step.do(''fetch data'', async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(''https://api.example.com/data'');\n  return await response.json();\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Issue #7: NonRetryableError Behaves Differently in Dev vs Production\n\n**Error**: NonRetryableError with empty message causes retries in dev mode but works correctly in production\n**Environment**: Development-specific bug\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #10113](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10113)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Empty error messages are handled differently between miniflare and production runtime.\n\n**Prevention**: Always provide a message to NonRetryableError:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Retries in dev, exits in prod\nthrow new NonRetryableError('''');\n\n// ✅ Exits in both environments\nthrow new NonRetryableError(''Validation failed'');\n```\n\n**Status**: Known issue, workaround documented.\n\n---\n\n### Issue #8: In-Memory State Lost on Hibernation\n\n**Error**: Variables declared outside `step.do()` reset to initial values after sleep/hibernation\n**Source**: [Cloudflare Workflows Rules](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Workflows hibernate when the engine detects no pending work. All in-memory state is lost during hibernation.\n\n**Prevention**: Only use state returned from `step.do()` - everything else is ephemeral:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD - In-memory variable lost on hibernation\nlet counter = 0;\nexport class MyWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint<Env, Params> {\n  async run(event: WorkflowEvent<Params>, step: WorkflowStep) {\n    counter = await step.do(''increment'', async () => counter + 1);\n    await step.sleep(''wait'', ''1 hour''); // ← Hibernates here, in-memory state lost\n    console.log(counter); // ❌ Will be 0, not 1!\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD - State from step.do() return values persists\nexport class MyWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint<Env, Params> {\n  async run(event: WorkflowEvent<Params>, step: WorkflowStep) {\n    const counter = await step.do(''increment'', async () => 1);\n    await step.sleep(''wait'', ''1 hour'');\n    console.log(counter); // ✅ Still 1\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Issue #9: Non-Deterministic Step Names Break Caching\n\n**Error**: Steps re-run unnecessarily, performance degradation\n**Source**: [Cloudflare Workflows Rules](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Step names act as cache keys. Using `Date.now()`, `Math.random()`, or other non-deterministic values causes new cache keys every run.\n\n**Prevention**: Use static, deterministic step names:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD - Non-deterministic step name\nawait step.do(`fetch-data-${Date.now()}`, async () => {\n  return await fetchExpensiveData();\n});\n// Every execution creates new cache key → step always re-runs\n\n// ✅ GOOD - Deterministic step name\nawait step.do(''fetch-data'', async () => {\n  return await fetchExpensiveData();\n});\n// Same cache key → result reused on restart/retry\n```\n\n---\n\n### Issue #10: Promise.race/any Outside step.do() Causes Inconsistency\n\n**Error**: Different promises resolve on restart, inconsistent behavior\n**Source**: [Cloudflare Workflows Rules](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Non-deterministic operations outside steps run again on restart, potentially with different results.\n\n**Prevention**: Keep all non-deterministic logic inside `step.do()`:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD - Race outside step\nconst fastest = await Promise.race([fetchA(), fetchB()]);\nawait step.do(''use result'', async () => fastest);\n// On restart: race runs again, different promise might win\n\n// ✅ GOOD - Race inside step\nconst fastest = await step.do(''fetch fastest'', async () => {\n  return await Promise.race([fetchA(), fetchB()]);\n});\n// On restart: cached result used, consistent behavior\n```\n\n---\n\n### Issue #11: Side Effects Repeat on Restart\n\n**Error**: Duplicate logs, metrics, or operations after workflow restart\n**Source**: [Cloudflare Workflows Rules](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Code outside `step.do()` executes multiple times if the workflow restarts mid-execution.\n\n**Prevention**: Put logging, metrics, and other side effects inside `step.do()`:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD - Side effect outside step\nconsole.log(''Workflow started''); // ← Logs multiple times on restart\nawait step.do(''work'', async () => { /* work */ });\n\n// ✅ GOOD - Side effects inside step\nawait step.do(''log start'', async () => {\n  console.log(''Workflow started''); // ← Logs once (cached)\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Issue #12: Non-Idempotent Operations Can Repeat\n\n**Error**: Double charges, duplicate database writes after step timeout\n**Source**: [Cloudflare Workflows Rules](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/)\n\n**Why It Happens**: Steps retry individually. If an API call succeeds but the step times out before returning, the retry will call the API again.\n\n**Prevention**: Guard non-idempotent operations with existence checks:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD - Charge customer without check\nawait step.do(''charge'', async () => {\n  return await stripe.charges.create({ amount: 1000, customer: customerId });\n});\n// If step times out after charge succeeds, retry charges AGAIN!\n\n// ✅ GOOD - Check for existing charge first\nawait step.do(''charge'', async () => {\n  const existing = await stripe.charges.list({ customer: customerId, limit: 1 });\n  if (existing.data.length > 0) return existing.data[0]; // Idempotent\n  return await stripe.charges.create({ amount: 1000, customer: customerId });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n\n## Step Methods\n\n### step.do() - Execute Work\n\n```typescript\nstep.do<T>(name: string, config?: WorkflowStepConfig, callback: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `name` - Step name (for observability)\n- `config` (optional) - Retry configuration (retries, timeout, backoff)\n- `callback` - Async function that does the work\n\n**Returns:** Value from callback (must be serializable)\n\n**Example:**\n```typescript\nconst result = await step.do(''call API'', { retries: { limit: 10, delay: ''10s'', backoff: ''exponential'' }, timeout: ''5 min'' }, async () => {\n  return await fetch(''https://api.example.com/data'').then(r => r.json());\n});\n```\n\n**CRITICAL - Serialization:**\n- ✅ Allowed: string, number, boolean, Array, Object, null\n- ❌ Forbidden: Function, Symbol, circular references, undefined\n- Throws error if return value isn''t JSON serializable\n\n---\n\n### step.sleep() - Relative Sleep\n\n```typescript\nstep.sleep(name: string, duration: WorkflowDuration): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `name` - Step name\n- `duration` - Number (ms) or string: `\"second\"`, `\"minute\"`, `\"hour\"`, `\"day\"`, `\"week\"`, `\"month\"`, `\"year\"` (plural forms accepted)\n\n**Examples:**\n```typescript\nawait step.sleep(''wait 5 minutes'', ''5 minutes'');\nawait step.sleep(''wait 1 hour'', ''1 hour'');\nawait step.sleep(''wait 2 days'', ''2 days'');\nawait step.sleep(''wait 30 seconds'', 30000);  // milliseconds\n```\n\n**Note:** Resuming workflows take priority over new instances. Sleeps don''t count toward step limits.\n\n---\n\n### step.sleepUntil() - Sleep to Specific Date\n\n```typescript\nstep.sleepUntil(name: string, timestamp: Date | number): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `name` - Step name\n- `timestamp` - Date object or UNIX timestamp (milliseconds)\n\n**Examples:**\n```typescript\nawait step.sleepUntil(''wait for launch'', new Date(''2025-12-25T00:00:00Z''));\nawait step.sleepUntil(''wait until time'', Date.parse(''24 Oct 2024 13:00:00 UTC''));\n```\n\n---\n\n### step.waitForEvent() - Wait for External Event (GA April 2025)\n\n```typescript\nstep.waitForEvent<T>(name: string, options: { type: string; timeout?: string | number }): Promise<T>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `name` - Step name\n- `options.type` - Event type to match\n- `options.timeout` (optional) - Max wait time (default: 24 hours, max: 30 days)\n\n**Returns:** Event payload sent via `instance.sendEvent()`\n\n**Example:**\n```typescript\nexport class PaymentWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint<Env, Params> {\n  async run(event: WorkflowEvent<Params>, step: WorkflowStep) {\n    await step.do(''create payment'', async () => { /* Stripe API */ });\n\n    const webhookData = await step.waitForEvent<StripeWebhook>(\n      ''wait for payment confirmation'',\n      { type: ''stripe-webhook'', timeout: ''1 hour'' }\n    );\n\n    if (webhookData.status === ''succeeded'') {\n      await step.do(''fulfill order'', async () => { /* fulfill */ });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Worker sends event to workflow\nexport default {\n  async fetch(req: Request, env: Env): Promise<Response> {\n    if (req.url.includes(''/webhook/stripe'')) {\n      const instance = await env.PAYMENT_WORKFLOW.get(instanceId);\n      await instance.sendEvent({ type: ''stripe-webhook'', payload: await req.json() });\n      return new Response(''OK'');\n    }\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Timeout handling:**\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const event = await step.waitForEvent(''wait for user'', { type: ''user-submitted'', timeout: ''10 minutes'' });\n} catch (error) {\n  await step.do(''send reminder'', async () => { /* reminder */ });\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## WorkflowStepConfig\n\n```typescript\ninterface WorkflowStepConfig {\n  retries?: {\n    limit: number;          // Max attempts (Infinity allowed)\n    delay: string | number; // Delay between retries\n    backoff?: ''constant'' | ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n  };\n  timeout?: string | number; // Max time per attempt\n}\n```\n\n**Default:** `{ retries: { limit: 5, delay: 10000, backoff: ''exponential'' }, timeout: ''10 minutes'' }`\n\n**Backoff Examples:**\n```typescript\n// Constant: 30s, 30s, 30s\n{ retries: { limit: 3, delay: ''30 seconds'', backoff: ''constant'' } }\n\n// Linear: 1m, 2m, 3m, 4m, 5m\n{ retries: { limit: 5, delay: ''1 minute'', backoff: ''linear'' } }\n\n// Exponential (recommended): 10s, 20s, 40s, 80s, 160s\n{ retries: { limit: 10, delay: ''10 seconds'', backoff: ''exponential'' }, timeout: ''5 minutes'' }\n\n// Unlimited retries\n{ retries: { limit: Infinity, delay: ''1 minute'', backoff: ''exponential'' } }\n\n// No retries\n{ retries: { limit: 0 } }\n```\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### NonRetryableError\n\nForce workflow to fail immediately without retrying:\n\n```typescript\nimport { WorkflowEntrypoint, WorkflowStep, WorkflowEvent } from ''cloudflare:workers'';\nimport { NonRetryableError } from ''cloudflare:workflows'';\n\nexport class MyWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint<Env, Params> {\n  async run(event: WorkflowEvent<Params>, step: WorkflowStep) {\n    await step.do(''validate input'', async () => {\n      if (!event.payload.userId) {\n        throw new NonRetryableError(''userId is required'');\n      }\n\n      // Validate user exists\n      const user = await this.env.DB.prepare(\n        ''SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?''\n      ).bind(event.payload.userId).first();\n\n      if (!user) {\n        // Terminal error - retrying won''t help\n        throw new NonRetryableError(''User not found'');\n      }\n\n      return user;\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**When to use NonRetryableError:**\n- ✅ Authentication/authorization failures\n- ✅ Invalid input that won''t change\n- ✅ Resource doesn''t exist (404)\n- ✅ Validation errors\n- ❌ Network failures (should retry)\n- ❌ Rate limits (should retry with backoff)\n- ❌ Temporary service outages (should retry)\n\n---\n\n### Catch Errors to Continue Workflow\n\nPrevent workflow failure by catching optional step errors:\n\n```typescript\nexport class MyWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint<Env, Params> {\n  async run(event: WorkflowEvent<Params>, step: WorkflowStep) {\n    await step.do(''process payment'', async () => { /* critical */ });\n\n    try {\n      await step.do(''send email'', async () => { /* optional */ });\n    } catch (error) {\n      await step.do(''log failure'', async () => {\n        await this.env.DB.prepare(''INSERT INTO failed_emails VALUES (?, ?)'').bind(event.payload.userId, error.message).run();\n      });\n    }\n\n    await step.do(''update status'', async () => { /* continues */ });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Graceful Degradation:**\n```typescript\nlet result;\ntry {\n  result = await step.do(''call primary API'', async () => await callPrimaryAPI());\n} catch {\n  result = await step.do(''call backup API'', async () => await callBackupAPI());\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Triggering Workflows\n\n**Configure binding (wrangler.jsonc):**\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"workflows\": [{\n    \"name\": \"my-workflow\",\n    \"binding\": \"MY_WORKFLOW\",\n    \"class_name\": \"MyWorkflow\",\n    \"script_name\": \"workflow-worker\"  // If workflow in different Worker\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n**Trigger from Worker:**\n```typescript\nconst instance = await env.MY_WORKFLOW.create({ params: { userId: ''123'' } });\nreturn Response.json({ id: instance.id, status: await instance.status() });\n```\n\n**Instance Management:**\n```typescript\nconst instance = await env.MY_WORKFLOW.get(instanceId);\nconst status = await instance.status();  // { status: ''running''|''complete''|''errored''|''queued'', error, output }\nawait instance.sendEvent({ type: ''user-action'', payload: { action: ''approved'' } });\nawait instance.pause();\nawait instance.resume();\nawait instance.terminate();\n```\n\n---\n\n\n## State Persistence\n\nWorkflows automatically persist state returned from `step.do()`:\n\n**✅ Serializable:**\n- Primitives: `string`, `number`, `boolean`, `null`\n- Arrays, Objects, Nested structures\n\n**❌ Non-Serializable:**\n- Functions, Symbols, circular references, undefined, class instances\n\n**Example:**\n```typescript\n// ✅ Good\nconst result = await step.do(''fetch data'', async () => ({\n  users: [{ id: 1, name: ''Alice'' }],\n  timestamp: Date.now(),\n  metadata: null\n}));\n\n// ❌ Bad - function not serializable\nconst bad = await step.do(''bad'', async () => ({ data: [1, 2, 3], transform: (x) => x * 2 }));  // Throws error!\n```\n\n**Access State Across Steps:**\n```typescript\nconst userData = await step.do(''fetch user'', async () => ({ id: 123, email: ''user@example.com'' }));\nconst orderData = await step.do(''create order'', async () => ({ userId: userData.id, orderId: ''ORD-456'' }));\nawait step.do(''send email'', async () => sendEmail({ to: userData.email, subject: `Order ${orderData.orderId}` }));\n```\n\n---\n\n## Observability\n\n### Built-in Metrics (Enhanced in 2025)\n\nWorkflows automatically track:\n- **Instance status**: queued, running, complete, errored, paused, waiting\n- **Step execution**: start/end times, duration, success/failure\n- **Retry history**: attempts, errors, delays\n- **Sleep state**: when workflow will wake up\n- **Output**: return values from steps and run()\n- **CPU time** (GA April 2025): Active processing time per instance for billing insights\n\n### View Metrics in Dashboard\n\nAccess via Cloudflare dashboard:\n1. Workers & Pages\n2. Select your workflow\n3. View instances and metrics\n\n**Metrics include:**\n- Total instances created\n- Success/error rates\n- Average execution time\n- Step-level performance\n- **CPU time consumption** (2025 feature)\n\n### Programmatic Access\n\n```typescript\nconst instance = await env.MY_WORKFLOW.get(instanceId);\nconst status = await instance.status();\n\nconsole.log(status);\n// {\n//   status: ''complete'' | ''running'' | ''errored'' | ''queued'' | ''waiting'' | ''unknown'',\n//   error: string | null,\n//   output: { userId: ''123'', status: ''processed'' }\n// }\n```\n\n**CPU Time Configuration (2025):**\n```jsonc\n// wrangler.jsonc\n{ \"limits\": { \"cpu_ms\": 300000 } }  // 5 minutes max (default: 30 seconds)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Limits (Updated 2025)\n\n| Feature | Workers Free | Workers Paid |\n|---------|--------------|--------------|\n| **Max steps per workflow** | 1,024 | 1,024 |\n| **Max state per step** | 1 MiB | 1 MiB |\n| **Max state per instance** | 100 MB | 1 GB |\n| **Max event payload size** | 1 MiB | 1 MiB |\n| **Max sleep/sleepUntil duration** | 365 days | 365 days |\n| **Max waitForEvent timeout** | 365 days | 365 days |\n| **CPU time per step** | 10 ms | 30 sec (default), 5 min (max) |\n| **Duration (wall clock) per step** | Unlimited | Unlimited |\n| **Max workflow executions** | 100,000/day | Unlimited |\n| **Concurrent instances** | 25 | 10,000 (Oct 2025, up from 4,500) |\n| **Instance creation rate** | 100/second | 100/second (Oct 2025, 10x faster) |\n| **Max queued instances** | 100,000 | 1,000,000 |\n| **Max subrequests per instance** | 50/request | 1,000/request |\n| **Retention (completed state)** | 3 days | 30 days |\n| **Max Workflow name length** | 64 chars | 64 chars |\n| **Max instance ID length** | 100 chars | 100 chars |\n\n**CRITICAL Notes:**\n- `step.sleep()` and `step.sleepUntil()` do NOT count toward 1,024 step limit\n- **Waiting instances** (sleeping, retrying, or waiting for events) do NOT count toward concurrency limits\n- Instance creation rate increased 10x (October 2025): 100 per 10 seconds → 100 per second\n- Max concurrency increased (October 2025): 4,500 → 10,000 concurrent instances\n- State persistence limits increased (2025): 128 KB → 1 MiB per step, 100 MB - 1 GB per instance\n- Event payload size increased (2025): 128 KB → 1 MiB\n- CPU time configurable via `wrangler.jsonc`: `{ \"limits\": { \"cpu_ms\": 300000 } }` (5 min max)\n\n---\n\n## Pricing\n\n**Requires Workers Paid plan** ($5/month)\n\n**Workflow Executions:**\n- First 10,000,000 step executions/month: **FREE**\n- After that: **$0.30 per million step executions**\n\n**What counts as a step execution:**\n- Each `step.do()` call\n- Each retry of a step\n- `step.sleep()`, `step.sleepUntil()`, `step.waitForEvent()` do NOT count\n\n**Cost examples:**\n- Workflow with 5 steps, no retries: **5 step executions**\n- Workflow with 3 steps, 1 step retries 2 times: **5 step executions** (3 + 2)\n- 10M simple workflows/month (5 steps each): ((50M - 10M) / 1M) × $0.30 = **$12/month**\n\n\n\n## Vitest Testing (GA April 2025)\n\nWorkflows support full testing integration via `cloudflare:test` module.\n\n### Setup\n\n```bash\nnpm install -D vitest@latest @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers@latest\n```\n\n**vitest.config.ts:**\n```typescript\nimport { defineWorkersConfig } from ''@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers/config'';\nexport default defineWorkersConfig({ test: { poolOptions: { workers: { miniflare: { bindings: { MY_WORKFLOW: { scriptName: ''workflow'' } } } } } } });\n```\n\n### Introspection API\n\n```typescript\nimport { env, introspectWorkflowInstance } from ''cloudflare:test'';\n\nit(''should complete workflow'', async () => {\n  const instance = await introspectWorkflowInstance(env.MY_WORKFLOW, ''test-123'');\n\n  try {\n    await instance.modify(async (m) => {\n      await m.disableSleeps();  // Skip all sleeps\n      await m.mockStepResult({ name: ''fetch data'' }, { users: [{ id: 1 }] });  // Mock step result\n      await m.mockEvent({ type: ''approval'', payload: { approved: true } });  // Send mock event\n      await m.mockStepError({ name: ''call API'' }, new Error(''Network timeout''), 1);  // Force error once\n    });\n\n    await env.MY_WORKFLOW.create({ id: ''test-123'' });\n    await expect(instance.waitForStatus(''complete'')).resolves.not.toThrow();\n  } finally {\n    await instance.dispose();  // Cleanup\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Test Modifiers\n\n- `disableSleeps(steps?)` - Skip sleeps instantly\n- `mockStepResult(step, result)` - Mock step.do() result\n- `mockStepError(step, error, times?)` - Force step.do() to throw\n- `mockEvent(event)` - Send mock event to step.waitForEvent()\n- `forceStepTimeout(step, times?)` - Force step.do() timeout\n- `forceEventTimeout(step)` - Force step.waitForEvent() timeout\n\n**Official Docs**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- **Cloudflare Workflows Docs**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/\n- **Get Started Guide**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/get-started/guide/\n- **Workers API**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/workers-api/\n- **Vitest Testing**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/\n- **Sleeping and Retrying**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/sleeping-and-retrying/\n- **Events and Parameters**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/events-and-parameters/\n- **Limits**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/reference/limits/\n- **Pricing**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/platform/pricing/\n- **Changelog**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/reference/changelog/\n- **MCP Tool**: Use `mcp__cloudflare-docs__search_cloudflare_documentation` for latest docs\n\n---\n\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-21\n**Version**: 2.0.0\n**Changes**: Added 12 documented Known Issues (TIER 1-2 research findings): waitForEvent timeout bug, getPlatformProxy failure, redirect instance loss, Vitest CI issues, local dev limitations, state persistence rules, caching gotchas, and idempotency patterns\n**Maintainer**: Jeremy Dawes | jeremy@jezweb.net\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:00:53.397Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloudflare-native automation agents requiring high-concurrency workflow orchestration.","zh":"适用于需要高并发工作流编排的 Cloudflare 原生自动化代理。","ja":"Cloudflare ネイティブの自動化エージェントで、高並列性のワークフロー オーケストレーションを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고 并发성 워크플ロー 오케스트레이션이 필요한 Cloudflare 네이티브 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de automatización nativos de Cloudflare que requieren una orquestación de flujo de trabajo de alta concurrencia.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''automatisation natifs de Cloudflare nécessitant une orchestration de flux de travail à haute concurrence.","de":"Ideal für Cloudflare-native Automatisierungsagenten, die eine Workflow-Orchestrierung mit hoher Konkurrenz erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de automação nativos da Cloudflare que exigem orquestração de fluxo de trabalho de alta concorrência.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации Cloudflare, требующих оркестровки рабочих процессов с высокой степенью параллелизма.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الأتمتة الأصلي من Cloudflare الذي يتطلب تنسيق تدفق عمل مع высокى التزامن."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to orchestrate complex, long-running workflows directly on Cloudflare''s edge network with up to 10,000 concurrent instances and 100 instances/second creation rate. Provides native integration with waitForEvent API for event-driven automation and Vitest testing capabilities.","zh":"使代理能够直接在 Cloudflare 的边缘网络上编排复杂、长时间运行的工作流，最高可达 10,000 个并发实例和每秒 100 个实例创建速率。提供与 waitForEvent API 的原生集成和 Vitest 测试功能。","ja":"エージェントが Cloudflare のエッジ ネットワーク上で直接、複雑で長時間実行されるワークフローをオーケストレーションできるようにします。最大 10,000 個の並列インスタンスと、1 秒あたり 100 個のインスタンス作成レートを提供します。waitForEvent API とのネイティブ統合と Vitest テスト機能も提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 Cloudflare의 에지 네트워크에서 직접 복잡하고 장시간 실행되는 워크플로우를 오케스트레이션할 수 있도록 합니다. 최대 10,000개의 并发 인스턴스와 1초당 100개의 인스턴스 생성 속도를 제공합니다. waitForEvent API와의 네이티브 통합 및 Vitest 테스트 기능도 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes orquestar flujos de trabajo complejos y de larga duración directamente en la red de borde de Cloudflare con hasta 10,000 instancias concurrentes y una tasa de creación de 100 instancias/segundo. Proporciona una integración nativa con la API waitForEvent para la automatización basada en eventos y las capacidades de prueba de Vitest.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''orchestrer des flux de travail complexes et à longue durée directement sur le réseau de bord de Cloudflare avec jusqu''à 10 000 instances concurrentes et un taux de création de 100 instances/seconde. Fournit une intégration native avec l''API waitForEvent pour l''automatisation basée sur les événements et les capacités de test de Vitest.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, komplexe und lang laufende Workflows direkt im Cloudflare-Edge-Netzwerk mit bis zu 10.000 gleichzeitigen Instanzen und einer Erstellungsgeschwindigkeit von 100 Instanzen/Sekunde zu orchestrieren. Bietet eine native Integration mit der waitForEvent-API für ereignisgesteuerte Automatisierung und Vitest-Testfunktionen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes orquestram fluxos de trabalho complexos e de longa duração diretamente na rede de borda da Cloudflare com até 10.000 instâncias concorrentes e uma taxa de criação de 100 instâncias/segundo. Fornece integração nativa com a API waitForEvent para automação baseada em eventos e capacidades de teste do Vitest.","ru":"Позволяет агентам оркестровать сложные, длительные рабочие процессы напрямую в сетях Cloudflare с до 10 000 одновременных экземпляров и скоростью создания 100 экземпляров в секунду. Обеспечивает родную интеграцию с API waitForEvent для событийной автоматизации и возможностей тестирования Vitest.","ar":"يمكن للعميل تنسيق تدفقات عمل معقدة وطويلة الأجل مباشرة على شبكة الحافة من Cloudflare مع ما يصل إلى 10،000 مثيل متزامن ومعدل إنشاء 100 مثيل في الثانية. يوفر تكاملًا أصليًا مع واجهة برمجة تطبيقات waitForEvent للتحكم الآلي المعتمد على الحدث وقدرات الاختبار من Vitest."},"useCases":{"en":["Orchestrating multi-step API integrations across Cloudflare services","Automating event-driven workflows with waitForEvent triggers","Testing workflow logic with Vitest integration","Scaling concurrent workflow execution to 10,000 instances"],"zh":["跨 Cloudflare 服务编排多步骤 API 集成","使用 waitForEvent 触发器自动化事件驱动工作流","使用 Vitest 集成测试工作流逻辑","将并发工作流执行扩展到 10,000 个实例"],"ja":["Cloudflare サービスの間でマルチステップ API 統合をオーケストレーションする","waitForEvent トリガーを使用してイベント ドリブンのワークフローを自動化する","Vitest 統合を使用してワークフロー ロジックをテストする","並列ワークフロー実行を 10,000 インスタンスにスケールする"],"ko":["Cloudflare 서비스 간 멀티ステップ API 통합 오케스트레이션","waitForEvent 트리거를 사용한 이벤트驱iven 워크플로우 자동화","Vitest 통합을 통한 워크플로우 로직 테스트","并发 워크플로우 실행을 10,000개의 인스턴스로 확장"],"es":["Orquestar integraciones de API de varios pasos en los servicios de Cloudflare","Automatizar flujos de trabajo basados en eventos con desencadenadores waitForEvent","Probar la lógica de flujo de trabajo con la integración de Vitest","Escalado de la ejecución de flujos de trabajo concurrentes a 10,000 instancias"],"fr":["Orchestrer des intégrations d''API à plusieurs étapes sur les services Cloudflare","Automatiser des flux de travail basés sur les événements avec des déclencheurs waitForEvent","Tester la logique de flux de travail avec l''intégration de Vitest","Mettre à l''échelle l''exécution de flux de travail concurrents à 10 000 instances"],"de":["Orchestrieren von API-Integrationen mit mehreren Schritten über Cloudflare-Dienste","Automatisieren von ereignisgesteuerten Workflows mit waitForEvent-Trigger","Testen der Workflow-Logik mit Vitest-Integration","Skalieren der gleichzeitigen Workflow-Ausführung auf 10.000 Instanzen"],"pt":["Orquestração de integrações de API de vários passos em serviços da Cloudflare","Automação de fluxos de trabalho baseados em eventos com gatilhos waitForEvent","Testar lógica de fluxo de trabalho com integração do Vitest","Dimensionamento da execução de fluxo de trabalho concorrente para 10.000 instâncias"],"ru":["Оркестровка многоступенчатых интеграций API в сервисах Cloudflare","Автоматизация рабочих процессов, основанных на событиях, с помощью триггеров waitForEvent","Тестирование логики рабочего процесса с помощью интеграции Vitest","Масштабирование параллельного выполнения рабочих процессов до 10 000 экземпляров"],"ar":["تنسيق تكاملات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات متعددة المراحل عبر خدمات Cloudflare","التحكم الآلي في سير العمل المعتمد على الأحداث مع.trigger waitForEvent","اختبار منطق سير العمل مع إدماج Vitest","توسيع تنفيذ سير العمل المتزامن إلى 10،000 مثيل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires cloudflare-worker-base dependency for setup","Limited to Cloudflare''s ecosystem and edge network","Maximum concurrency of 10,000 instances"],"zh":["需要 cloudflare-worker-base 依赖项进行设置","仅限 Cloudflare 的生态系统和边缘网络","最大并发性为 10,000 个实例"],"ja":["セットアップには cloudflare-worker-base 依存関係が必要","Cloudflare のエコシステムとエッジ ネットワークに限定される","最大並列性は 10,000 インスタンス"],"ko":["설정에는 cloudflare-worker-base 종속성이 필요","Cloudflare의 에코시스템과 에지 네트워크로 제한","최대 并发성은 10,000개의 인스턴스"],"es":["Requiere la dependencia cloudflare-worker-base para la configuración","Limitado al ecosistema y la red de borde de Cloudflare","Concurrencia máxima de 10,000 instancias"],"fr":["Nécessite la dépendance cloudflare-worker-base pour la configuration","Limité à l''écosystème et au réseau de bord de Cloudflare","Concurrence maximale de 10 000 instances"],"de":["Benötigt die Abhängigkeit cloudflare-worker-base für die Einrichtung","Begrenzt auf das Cloudflare-Ökosystem und das Edge-Netzwerk","Maximale Konkurrenz von 10.000 Instanzen"],"pt":["Exige dependência de cloudflare-worker-base para configuração","Limitado ao ecossistema e rede de borda da Cloudflare","Concurrencia máxima de 10.000 instâncias"],"ru":["Требует зависимости cloudflare-worker-base для настройки","Ограничен экосистемой и сетью Cloudflare","Максимальная параллелизм 10 000 экземпляров"],"ar":["يتطلب-dependency cloudflare-worker-base لإعداد","محدود بنظام البيئة وشبكة الحافة من Cloudflare","الحد الأقصى للتزامن هو 10،000 مثيل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit/performance-profiling', 'community', 'HaoNgo232', 'agent-bridge-kit', 'HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit', 'performance-profiling', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z', '2026-02-18T14:01:04.320Z', NULL, '{"id":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit/performance-profiling","name":"performance-profiling","description":{"zh":"性能分析工具帮助开发者优化Web应用，提高加载速度和用户体验","ja":"パフォーマンスプロファイリングツールは、開発者がWebアプリを最適化し、ロード時間とユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させるのに役立ちます","ko":"성능 프로파일링 도구는 개발자가 웹 애플리케이션을 최적화하여 로드 시간과 사용자 경험을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"El perfíl de rendimiento es una herramienta para medir y optimizar el rendimiento de aplicaciones. Incluye scripts de ejecución para análisis automatizado.","fr":"Le profiling de performance est un outil pour mesurer et optimiser les performances des applications. Il inclut des scripts d''exécution pour l''analyse automatisée.","de":"Das Leistungsprofiling ist ein Tool zur Messung und Optimierung der Leistung von Anwendungen. Es enthält Runtime-Scripts für die automatisierte Analyse.","pt":"O performance-profiling é uma ferramenta para otimizar o desempenho dos aplicativos, medindo e analisando o tempo de carregamento e interação.","ru":"Профилирование производительности - это инструмент для оптимизации производительности приложений, измеряющий и анализирующий время загрузки и взаимодействия.","ar":"تعريف الأداء هو أداة لتحسين أداء التطبيقات، يقيس ويفحص وقت التحميل والتفاعل.","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"性能分析工具","ja":"パフォーマンスプロファイリングツール","ko":"성능 프로파일링 도구","es":"Perfíl de rendimiento: optimiza tu código","fr":"Profiling de performance: améliorez votre code","de":"Leistungsprofiling: optimieren Sie Ihren Code","pt":"Otimização de Desempenho - Perfiling de Aplicativos","ru":"Профилирование Производительности - Оптимизация Приложений","ar":"تحسين الأداء - تعريف البرامج التطبيقية","en":"performance-profiling"},"description":{"zh":"性能分析工具帮助开发者优化Web应用，提高加载速度和用户体验","ja":"パフォーマンスプロファイリングツールは、開発者がWebアプリを最適化し、ロード時間とユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させるのに役立ちます","ko":"성능 프로파일링 도구는 개발자가 웹 애플리케이션을 최적화하여 로드 시간과 사용자 경험을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"El perfíl de rendimiento es una herramienta para medir y optimizar el rendimiento de aplicaciones. Incluye scripts de ejecución para análisis automatizado.","fr":"Le profiling de performance est un outil pour mesurer et optimiser les performances des applications. Il inclut des scripts d''exécution pour l''analyse automa...","de":"Das Leistungsprofiling ist ein Tool zur Messung und Optimierung der Leistung von Anwendungen. Es enthält Runtime-Scripts für die automatisierte Analyse.","pt":"O performance-profiling é uma ferramenta para otimizar o desempenho dos aplicativos, medindo e analisando o tempo de carregamento e interação.","ru":"Профилирование производительности - это инструмент для оптимизации производительности приложений, измеряющий и анализирующий время загрузки и взаимодействия.","ar":"تعريف الأداء هو أداة لتحسين أداء التطبيقات، يقيس ويفحص وقت التحميل والتفاعل.","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro..."},"definition":{"en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"features":{"zh":["自动化性能分析","Lighthouse性能审计","Core Web Vitals支持","自定义脚本执行","多IDE和CLI支持"],"ja":["自動化されたパフォーマンスプロファイリング","Lighthouseパフォーマンス監査","Core Web Vitalsのサポート","カスタムスクリプトの実行","複数のIDEとCLIのサポート"],"ko":["자동화된 성능 프로파일링","Lighthouse 성능 감사","Core Web Vitals 지원","사용자 정의 스크립트 실행","다중 IDE 및 CLI 지원"],"es":["Medición y análisis de rendimiento","Optimización de aplicaciones","Script de ejecución para análisis automatizado","Soporte para Core Web Vitals","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Mesure et analyse des performances","Optimisation des applications","Script d''exécution pour l''analyse automatisée","Prise en charge des Core Web Vitals","Intégration avec les outils de développement"],"de":["Leistungsmessung und -analyse","Optimierung von Anwendungen","Runtime-Script für die automatisierte Analyse","Unterstützung für Core Web Vitals","Integration mit Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Medição do tempo de carregamento","Análise da interação do usuário","Otimização do desempenho","Execução de scripts de perfil","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Relatórios detalhados de desempenho"],"ru":["Измерение времени загрузки","Анализ взаимодействия пользователя","Оптимизация производительности","Выполнение скриптов профилирования","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Детальные отчеты о производительности"],"ar":["قياس وقت التحميل","تحليل تفاعل المستخدم","تحسين الأداء","تشغيل نصوص تعريف البرامج","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","تقارير مفصلة عن الأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["性能分析","Web性能优化","Lighthouse","Core Web Vitals","自动化测试","开发者工具"],"ja":["パフォーマンスプロファイリング","Webパフォーマンス最適化","Lighthouse","Core Web Vitals","自動テスト","開発者ツール"],"ko":["성능 프로파일링","웹 성능 최적화","Lighthouse","Core Web Vitals","자동화 테스트","개발자 도구"],"es":["perfíl de rendimiento","optimización de aplicaciones","análisis de rendimiento","Core Web Vitals","desarrollo de aplicaciones","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["profiling de performance","optimisation des applications","analyse des performances","Core Web Vitals","développement d''applications","outils de développement"],"de":["Leistungsprofiling","Optimierung von Anwendungen","Leistungsanalyse","Core Web Vitals","Anwendungsentwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["performance-profiling","otimização de desempenho","medição de desempenho","análise de desempenho","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","relatórios de desempenho","tempo de carregamento","interação do usuário"],"ru":["профилирование производительности","оптимизация производительности","измерение производительности","анализ производительности","разработка приложений","инструменты разработки","отчеты о производительности","время загрузки","взаимодействие пользователя"],"ar":["تحسين الأداء","قياس الأداء","تحليل الأداء","تطوير التطبيقات","أدوات التطوير","تقارير الأداء","وقت التحميل","تفاعل المستخدم","تعريف البرامج"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"performance-profiling","description":"Performance profiling principles. Measurement, analysis, and optimization techniques.","bodyPreview":"# Performance Profiling\n\n> Measure, analyze, optimize - in that order.\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for automated profiling:**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/lighthouse_audit.py` | Lighthouse performance audit | `python scripts/lighthouse_audit.py https://example.com` |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Web Vitals\n\n### Targets\n\n| Metric | Good | Poor | Measures |\n|--------|------|------|----------|\n| **LCP** | < 2.5s | > 4.0s | Loading |\n| **INP** | < 200ms | > 5","body":"# Performance Profiling\n\n> Measure, analyze, optimize - in that order.\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for automated profiling:**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/lighthouse_audit.py` | Lighthouse performance audit | `python scripts/lighthouse_audit.py https://example.com` |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Web Vitals\n\n### Targets\n\n| Metric | Good | Poor | Measures |\n|--------|------|------|----------|\n| **LCP** | < 2.5s | > 4.0s | Loading |\n| **INP** | < 200ms | > 500ms | Interactivity |\n| **CLS** | < 0.1 | > 0.25 | Stability |\n\n### When to Measure\n\n| Stage | Tool |\n|-------|------|\n| Development | Local Lighthouse |\n| CI/CD | Lighthouse CI |\n| Production | RUM (Real User Monitoring) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Profiling Workflow\n\n### The 4-Step Process\n\n```\n1. BASELINE → Measure current state\n2. IDENTIFY → Find the bottleneck\n3. FIX → Make targeted change\n4. VALIDATE → Confirm improvement\n```\n\n### Profiling Tool Selection\n\n| Problem | Tool |\n|---------|------|\n| Page load | Lighthouse |\n| Bundle size | Bundle analyzer |\n| Runtime | DevTools Performance |\n| Memory | DevTools Memory |\n| Network | DevTools Network |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Bundle Analysis\n\n### What to Look For\n\n| Issue | Indicator |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Large dependencies | Top of bundle |\n| Duplicate code | Multiple chunks |\n| Unused code | Low coverage |\n| Missing splits | Single large chunk |\n\n### Optimization Actions\n\n| Finding | Action |\n|---------|--------|\n| Big library | Import specific modules |\n| Duplicate deps | Dedupe, update versions |\n| Route in main | Code split |\n| Unused exports | Tree shake |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Runtime Profiling\n\n### Performance Tab Analysis\n\n| Pattern | Meaning |\n|---------|---------|\n| Long tasks (>50ms) | UI blocking |\n| Many small tasks | Possible batching opportunity |\n| Layout/paint | Rendering bottleneck |\n| Script | JavaScript execution |\n\n### Memory Tab Analysis\n\n| Pattern | Meaning |\n|---------|---------|\n| Growing heap | Possible leak |\n| Large retained | Check references |\n| Detached DOM | Not cleaned up |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Common Bottlenecks\n\n### By Symptom\n\n| Symptom | Likely Cause |\n|---------|--------------|\n| Slow initial load | Large JS, render blocking |\n| Slow interactions | Heavy event handlers |\n| Jank during scroll | Layout thrashing |\n| Growing memory | Leaks, retained refs |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Quick Win Priorities\n\n| Priority | Action | Impact |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| 1 | Enable compression | High |\n| 2 | Lazy load images | High |\n| 3 | Code split routes | High |\n| 4 | Cache static assets | Medium |\n| 5 | Optimize images | Medium |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ Don''t | ✅ Do |\n|----------|-------|\n| Guess at problems | Profile first |\n| Micro-optimize | Fix biggest issue |\n| Optimize early | Optimize when needed |\n| Ignore real users | Use RUM data |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** The fastest code is code that doesn''t run. Remove before optimizing.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:01:04.320Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Performance Optimization Agents needing advanced runtime analysis and visualization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级运行时分析和可视化功能的性能优化代理。","ja":"パフォーマンス最適化エージェントが高度なランタイム分析および視覚化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 런타임 분석 및 시각화 기능이 필요한 성능 최적화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de optimización de rendimiento que necesitan análisis y capacidades de visualización de tiempo de ejecución avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''optimisation de performances nécessitant une analyse et des capacités de visualisation de runtime avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Leistungsoptimierungsagenten, die erweiterte Laufzeitanalyse- und Visualisierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Otimização de Desempenho que necessitam de análise e capacidades de visualização de tempo de execução avançadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов оптимизации производительности, требующих продвинутого анализа и возможностей визуализации во время выполнения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل محسن الأداء الذي يحتاج إلى تحليل وقت تشغيل متقدم وقدرات مرئية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute automated Lighthouse audits and analyze Core Web Vitals metrics like LCP and INP, providing actionable insights for optimization using Python scripts.","zh":"赋予代理执行自动化的Lighthouse审计并分析核心网络生命指标（如LCP和INP），为使用Python脚本的优化提供可行的见解。","ja":"エージェントが自動化されたLighthouse監査を実行し、LCPやINPなどのCore Web Vitalsメトリクスを分析して、Pythonスクリプトを使用した最適化のためのアクション可能な洞察を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 자동화된 라이트하우스 감사를 실행하고 LCP 및 INP와 같은 코어 웹 비탈 메트릭스를 분석하여 파이썬 스크립트를 사용한 최적화에 대한 실행 가능한 통찰력을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar auditorías automatizadas de Lighthouse y analizar métricas de Core Web Vitals como LCP e INP, proporcionando conocimientos operativos para la optimización utilizando scripts de Python.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des audits Lighthouse automatisés et d''analyser les métriques Core Web Vitals comme LCP et INP, fournissant des connaissances opérationnelles pour l''optimisation en utilisant des scripts Python.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, automatisierte Lighthouse-Audits auszuführen und Core Web Vitals-Metriken wie LCP und INP zu analysieren, um mit Python-Skripten handhabbare Erkenntnisse für die Optimierung bereitzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar auditorias automatizadas do Lighthouse e analisar métricas de Core Web Vitals, como LCP e INP, fornecendo insights ação para otimização usando scripts Python.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять автоматические аудиты Lighthouse и анализировать метрики Core Web Vitals, такие как LCP и INP, предоставляя действенные идеи для оптимизации с помощью скриптов Python.","ar":"يمكن للعميل تنفيذ عمليات تدقيق لighthouse أوتوماتيكية وتحليل مقاييس لبناء ويب أساسي مثل LCP و INP، مما يوفر رؤى قابلة للتنفيذ لتحسين الأداء باستخدام نصوص بايثون."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating performance audits with Lighthouse","Analyzing Core Web Vitals for web application optimization","Debugging performance issues with runtime scripting"],"zh":["使用Lighthouse自动化性能审计","分析核心网络生命指标以优化Web应用程序","使用运行时脚本调试性能问题"],"ja":["Lighthouseを使用したパフォーマンス監査の自動化","Webアプリケーションの最適化のためのCore Web Vitalsの分析","ランタイムスクリプティングを使用したパフォーマンス問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["라이트하우스를 사용한 성능 감사의 자동화","웹 애플리케이션 최적화를 위한 코어 웹 비탈의 분석","런타임 스크립팅을 사용한 성능 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de auditorías de rendimiento con Lighthouse","Análisis de Core Web Vitals para la optimización de aplicaciones web","Depuración de problemas de rendimiento con scripting de tiempo de ejecución"],"fr":["Automatisation des audits de performances avec Lighthouse","Analyse des Core Web Vitals pour l''optimisation des applications Web","Débogage des problèmes de performances avec un scripting de runtime"],"de":["Automatisierung von Leistungsaudits mit Lighthouse","Analyse von Core Web Vitals für die Optimierung von Webanwendungen","Fehlerbehebung bei Leistungsproblemen mit Laufzeit-Skripting"],"pt":["Automatizar auditorias de desempenho com Lighthouse","Analisar Core Web Vitals para otimização de aplicativos web","Depurar problemas de desempenho com script de tempo de execução"],"ru":["Автоматизация аудитов производительности с помощью Lighthouse","Анализ Core Web Vitals для оптимизации веб-приложений","Отладка проблем с производительностью с помощью скриптов во время выполнения"],"ar":["أتمتة فحص الأداء مع لايت هاوس","تحليل لبناء ويب أساسي لتحسين التطبيقات الويب","تصحيح أخطاء الأداء مع برمجة وقت التشغيل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment","Limited to Lighthouse audit functionality"],"zh":["需要Python环境","仅限Lighthouse审计功能"],"ja":["Python環境が必要","Lighthouse監査機能のみに限定される"],"ko":["파이썬 환경이 필요함","라이트하우스 감사 기능만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Python","Limitado a la funcionalidad de auditoría de Lighthouse"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python","Limité à la fonctionnalité d''audit Lighthouse"],"de":["Benötigt Python-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf Lighthouse-Audit-Funktion"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python","Limitado à funcionalidade de auditoria do Lighthouse"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python","Ограниченная функциональность аудита Lighthouse"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة بايثون","محدود بالوظيفة التدقيق لايت هاوس"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/react-state-management', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'react-state-management', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z', '2026-02-18T14:01:03.491Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/react-state-management","name":"react-state-management","description":{"zh":"React, Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai, React Query, SWR","ja":"React, Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai, React Query, SWR","ko":"React, Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai, React Query, SWR","es":"Guía completa sobre gestión de estado en React, desde el estado local de componentes hasta tiendas globales y sincronización de estado de servidor","fr":"Guide complet sur la gestion d''état dans React, des états locaux de composants aux magasins globaux et à la synchronisation d''état de serveur","de":"Umfassender Leitfaden zur Zustandsverwaltung in React, von lokalem Komponentenzustand bis hin zu globalen Stores und Serverzustandssynchronisation","pt":"Guia abrangente sobre gerenciamento de estado no React, cobrindo padrões modernos e soluções para gerenciar estado em aplicações React.","ru":"Комплексное руководство по управлению состоянием в React, охватывающее современные паттерны и решения для управления состоянием в приложениях React.","ar":"دليل شامل حول إدارة الحالة في ري액ت، يغطي الأنماط الحديثة والحلول لإدارة الحالة في تطبيقات ري액ت.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"React ","ja":"React","ko":"React ","es":"Gestión de Estado en React","fr":"Gestion d''État React","de":"React Zustandsverwaltung","pt":"Gerenciamento de Estado React","ru":"Управление состоянием React","ar":"إدارة حالة ري액ت","en":"react-state-management"},"description":{"zh":"React, Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai, React Query, SWR","ja":"React, Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai, React Query, SWR","ko":"React, Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai, React Query, SWR","es":"Guía completa sobre gestión de estado en React, desde el estado local de componentes hasta tiendas globales y sincronización de estado de servidor","fr":"Guide complet sur la gestion d''état dans React, des états locaux de composants aux magasins globaux et à la synchronisation d''état de serveur","de":"Umfassender Leitfaden zur Zustandsverwaltung in React, von lokalem Komponentenzustand bis hin zu globalen Stores und Serverzustandssynchronisation","pt":"Guia abrangente sobre gerenciamento de estado no React, cobrindo padrões modernos e soluções para gerenciar estado em aplicações React.","ru":"Комплексное руководство по управлению состоянием в React, охватывающее современные паттерны и решения для управления состоянием в приложениях React.","ar":"دليل شامل حول إدارة الحالة في ري액ت، يغطي الأنماط الحديثة والحلول لإدارة الحالة في تطبيقات ري액ت.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","React "],"ja":["Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","React "],"ko":["Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","React "],"es":["Patrones de gestión de estado modernos","Uso de Redux Toolkit, Zustand y Jotai","Sincronización de estado de servidor con React Query o SWR","Actualizaciones optimistas","Depuración de problemas relacionados con el estado"],"fr":["Modèles de gestion d''état modernes","Utilisation de Redux Toolkit, Zustand et Jotai","Synchronisation d''état de serveur avec React Query ou SWR","Mises à jour optimistes","Débogage des problèmes liés à l''état"],"de":["Moderne Zustandsverwaltungsmuster","Verwendung von Redux Toolkit, Zustand und Jotai","Serverzustandssynchronisation mit React Query oder SWR","Optimistische Updates","Fehlerbehebung bei Zustandsproblemen"],"pt":["Padrões de gerenciamento de estado local","Lojas globais de estado com Redux Toolkit, Zustand ou Jotai","Sincronização de estado do servidor com React Query ou SWR","Atualizações otimistas","Depuração de problemas relacionados ao estado"],"ru":["Паттерны локального управления состоянием","Глобальные хранилища состояния с Redux Toolkit, Zustand или Jotai","Синхронизация состояния сервера с React Query или SWR","Оптимистические обновления","Отладка проблем, связанных с состоянием"],"ar":["أنماط إدارة الحالة المحلية","مخازن عالمية للحالة مع Redux Toolkit، Zustand أو Jotai","مزامنة حالة الخادم مع React Query أو SWR","تحديثات متفائلة","تصحيح أخطاء متعلقة بالحالة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["React","Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","React ","React "],"ja":["React","Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","React ","React "],"ko":["React","Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","React ","React "],"es":["gestión de estado en React","patrones de gestión de estado","Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","sincronización de estado de servidor"],"fr":["gestion d''état dans React","modèles de gestion d''état","Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","synchronisation d''état de serveur"],"de":["Zustandsverwaltung in React","Zustandsverwaltungsmuster","Redux Toolkit","Zustand","Jotai","React Query","SWR","Serverzustandssynchronisation"],"pt":["gerenciamento de estado react","padrões de estado react","redux toolkit","zustand","jotai","react query","swr"],"ru":["управление состоянием react","паттерны состояния react","redux toolkit","zustand","jotai","react query","swr"],"ar":["إدارة حالة ري액ت","أنماط حالة ري액ت","redux toolkit","zustand","jotai","react query","swr"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"react-state-management","description":"Master modern React state management with Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai, and React Query. Use when setting up global state, managing server state, or choosing between state management solutions.","bodyPreview":"# React State Management\n\nComprehensive guide to modern React state management patterns, from local component state to global stores and server state synchronization.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up global state management in a React app\n- Choosing between Redux Toolkit, Zustand, or Jotai\n- Managing server state with React Query or SWR\n- Implementing optimistic updates\n- Debugging state-related issues\n- Migrating from legacy Redux to modern patterns\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. State Categ","body":"# React State Management\n\nComprehensive guide to modern React state management patterns, from local component state to global stores and server state synchronization.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up global state management in a React app\n- Choosing between Redux Toolkit, Zustand, or Jotai\n- Managing server state with React Query or SWR\n- Implementing optimistic updates\n- Debugging state-related issues\n- Migrating from legacy Redux to modern patterns\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. State Categories\n\n| Type             | Description                  | Solutions                     |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| **Local State**  | Component-specific, UI state | useState, useReducer          |\n| **Global State** | Shared across components     | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Jotai |\n| **Server State** | Remote data, caching         | React Query, SWR, RTK Query   |\n| **URL State**    | Route parameters, search     | React Router, nuqs            |\n| **Form State**   | Input values, validation     | React Hook Form, Formik       |\n\n### 2. Selection Criteria\n\n```\nSmall app, simple state → Zustand or Jotai\nLarge app, complex state → Redux Toolkit\nHeavy server interaction → React Query + light client state\nAtomic/granular updates → Jotai\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Zustand (Simplest)\n\n```typescript\n// store/useStore.ts\nimport { create } from ''zustand''\nimport { devtools, persist } from ''zustand/middleware''\n\ninterface AppState {\n  user: User | null\n  theme: ''light'' | ''dark''\n  setUser: (user: User | null) => void\n  toggleTheme: () => void\n}\n\nexport const useStore = create<AppState>()(\n  devtools(\n    persist(\n      (set) => ({\n        user: null,\n        theme: ''light'',\n        setUser: (user) => set({ user }),\n        toggleTheme: () => set((state) => ({\n          theme: state.theme === ''light'' ? ''dark'' : ''light''\n        })),\n      }),\n      { name: ''app-storage'' }\n    )\n  )\n)\n\n// Usage in component\nfunction Header() {\n  const { user, theme, toggleTheme } = useStore()\n  return (\n    <header className={theme}>\n      {user?.name}\n      <button onClick={toggleTheme}>Toggle Theme</button>\n    </header>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Redux Toolkit with TypeScript\n\n```typescript\n// store/index.ts\nimport { configureStore } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\nimport { TypedUseSelectorHook, useDispatch, useSelector } from \"react-redux\";\nimport userReducer from \"./slices/userSlice\";\nimport cartReducer from \"./slices/cartSlice\";\n\nexport const store = configureStore({\n  reducer: {\n    user: userReducer,\n    cart: cartReducer,\n  },\n  middleware: (getDefaultMiddleware) =>\n    getDefaultMiddleware({\n      serializableCheck: {\n        ignoredActions: [\"persist/PERSIST\"],\n      },\n    }),\n});\n\nexport type RootState = ReturnType<typeof store.getState>;\nexport type AppDispatch = typeof store.dispatch;\n\n// Typed hooks\nexport const useAppDispatch: () => AppDispatch = useDispatch;\nexport const useAppSelector: TypedUseSelectorHook<RootState> = useSelector;\n```\n\n```typescript\n// store/slices/userSlice.ts\nimport { createSlice, createAsyncThunk, PayloadAction } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\n\ninterface User {\n  id: string;\n  email: string;\n  name: string;\n}\n\ninterface UserState {\n  current: User | null;\n  status: \"idle\" | \"loading\" | \"succeeded\" | \"failed\";\n  error: string | null;\n}\n\nconst initialState: UserState = {\n  current: null,\n  status: \"idle\",\n  error: null,\n};\n\nexport const fetchUser = createAsyncThunk(\n  \"user/fetchUser\",\n  async (userId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`);\n      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(\"Failed to fetch user\");\n      return await response.json();\n    } catch (error) {\n      return rejectWithValue((error as Error).message);\n    }\n  },\n);\n\nconst userSlice = createSlice({\n  name: \"user\",\n  initialState,\n  reducers: {\n    setUser: (state, action: PayloadAction<User>) => {\n      state.current = action.payload;\n      state.status = \"succeeded\";\n    },\n    clearUser: (state) => {\n      state.current = null;\n      state.status = \"idle\";\n    },\n  },\n  extraReducers: (builder) => {\n    builder\n      .addCase(fetchUser.pending, (state) => {\n        state.status = \"loading\";\n        state.error = null;\n      })\n      .addCase(fetchUser.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n        state.status = \"succeeded\";\n        state.current = action.payload;\n      })\n      .addCase(fetchUser.rejected, (state, action) => {\n        state.status = \"failed\";\n        state.error = action.payload as string;\n      });\n  },\n});\n\nexport const { setUser, clearUser } = userSlice.actions;\nexport default userSlice.reducer;\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Zustand with Slices (Scalable)\n\n```typescript\n// store/slices/createUserSlice.ts\nimport { StateCreator } from \"zustand\";\n\nexport interface UserSlice {\n  user: User | null;\n  isAuthenticated: boolean;\n  login: (credentials: Credentials) => Promise<void>;\n  logout: () => void;\n}\n\nexport const createUserSlice: StateCreator<\n  UserSlice & CartSlice, // Combined store type\n  [],\n  [],\n  UserSlice\n> = (set, get) => ({\n  user: null,\n  isAuthenticated: false,\n  login: async (credentials) => {\n    const user = await authApi.login(credentials);\n    set({ user, isAuthenticated: true });\n  },\n  logout: () => {\n    set({ user: null, isAuthenticated: false });\n    // Can access other slices\n    // get().clearCart()\n  },\n});\n\n// store/index.ts\nimport { create } from \"zustand\";\nimport { createUserSlice, UserSlice } from \"./slices/createUserSlice\";\nimport { createCartSlice, CartSlice } from \"./slices/createCartSlice\";\n\ntype StoreState = UserSlice & CartSlice;\n\nexport const useStore = create<StoreState>()((...args) => ({\n  ...createUserSlice(...args),\n  ...createCartSlice(...args),\n}));\n\n// Selective subscriptions (prevents unnecessary re-renders)\nexport const useUser = () => useStore((state) => state.user);\nexport const useCart = () => useStore((state) => state.cart);\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Jotai for Atomic State\n\n```typescript\n// atoms/userAtoms.ts\nimport { atom } from ''jotai''\nimport { atomWithStorage } from ''jotai/utils''\n\n// Basic atom\nexport const userAtom = atom<User | null>(null)\n\n// Derived atom (computed)\nexport const isAuthenticatedAtom = atom((get) => get(userAtom) !== null)\n\n// Atom with localStorage persistence\nexport const themeAtom = atomWithStorage<''light'' | ''dark''>(''theme'', ''light'')\n\n// Async atom\nexport const userProfileAtom = atom(async (get) => {\n  const user = get(userAtom)\n  if (!user) return null\n  const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${user.id}/profile`)\n  return response.json()\n})\n\n// Write-only atom (action)\nexport const logoutAtom = atom(null, (get, set) => {\n  set(userAtom, null)\n  set(cartAtom, [])\n  localStorage.removeItem(''token'')\n})\n\n// Usage\nfunction Profile() {\n  const [user] = useAtom(userAtom)\n  const [, logout] = useAtom(logoutAtom)\n  const [profile] = useAtom(userProfileAtom) // Suspense-enabled\n\n  return (\n    <Suspense fallback={<Skeleton />}>\n      <ProfileContent profile={profile} onLogout={logout} />\n    </Suspense>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: React Query for Server State\n\n```typescript\n// hooks/useUsers.ts\nimport { useQuery, useMutation, useQueryClient } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\n// Query keys factory\nexport const userKeys = {\n  all: [\"users\"] as const,\n  lists: () => [...userKeys.all, \"list\"] as const,\n  list: (filters: UserFilters) => [...userKeys.lists(), filters] as const,\n  details: () => [...userKeys.all, \"detail\"] as const,\n  detail: (id: string) => [...userKeys.details(), id] as const,\n};\n\n// Fetch hook\nexport function useUsers(filters: UserFilters) {\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: userKeys.list(filters),\n    queryFn: () => fetchUsers(filters),\n    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes\n    gcTime: 30 * 60 * 1000, // 30 minutes (formerly cacheTime)\n  });\n}\n\n// Single user hook\nexport function useUser(id: string) {\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: userKeys.detail(id),\n    queryFn: () => fetchUser(id),\n    enabled: !!id, // Don''t fetch if no id\n  });\n}\n\n// Mutation with optimistic update\nexport function useUpdateUser() {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient();\n\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: updateUser,\n    onMutate: async (newUser) => {\n      // Cancel outgoing refetches\n      await queryClient.cancelQueries({\n        queryKey: userKeys.detail(newUser.id),\n      });\n\n      // Snapshot previous value\n      const previousUser = queryClient.getQueryData(\n        userKeys.detail(newUser.id),\n      );\n\n      // Optimistically update\n      queryClient.setQueryData(userKeys.detail(newUser.id), newUser);\n\n      return { previousUser };\n    },\n    onError: (err, newUser, context) => {\n      // Rollback on error\n      queryClient.setQueryData(\n        userKeys.detail(newUser.id),\n        context?.previousUser,\n      );\n    },\n    onSettled: (data, error, variables) => {\n      // Refetch after mutation\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n        queryKey: userKeys.detail(variables.id),\n      });\n    },\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Combining Client + Server State\n\n```typescript\n// Zustand for client state\nconst useUIStore = create<UIState>((set) => ({\n  sidebarOpen: true,\n  modal: null,\n  toggleSidebar: () => set((s) => ({ sidebarOpen: !s.sidebarOpen })),\n  openModal: (modal) => set({ modal }),\n  closeModal: () => set({ modal: null }),\n}))\n\n// React Query for server state\nfunction Dashboard() {\n  const { sidebarOpen, toggleSidebar } = useUIStore()\n  const { data: users, isLoading } = useUsers({ active: true })\n  const { data: stats } = useStats()\n\n  if (isLoading) return <DashboardSkeleton />\n\n  return (\n    <div className={sidebarOpen ? ''with-sidebar'' : ''''}>\n      <Sidebar open={sidebarOpen} onToggle={toggleSidebar} />\n      <main>\n        <StatsCards stats={stats} />\n        <UserTable users={users} />\n      </main>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Colocate state** - Keep state as close to where it''s used as possible\n- **Use selectors** - Prevent unnecessary re-renders with selective subscriptions\n- **Normalize data** - Flatten nested structures for easier updates\n- **Type everything** - Full TypeScript coverage prevents runtime errors\n- **Separate concerns** - Server state (React Query) vs client state (Zustand)\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t over-globalize** - Not everything needs to be in global state\n- **Don''t duplicate server state** - Let React Query manage it\n- **Don''t mutate directly** - Always use immutable updates\n- **Don''t store derived data** - Compute it instead\n- **Don''t mix paradigms** - Pick one primary solution per category\n\n## Migration Guides\n\n### From Legacy Redux to RTK\n\n```typescript\n// Before (legacy Redux)\nconst ADD_TODO = \"ADD_TODO\";\nconst addTodo = (text) => ({ type: ADD_TODO, payload: text });\nfunction todosReducer(state = [], action) {\n  switch (action.type) {\n    case ADD_TODO:\n      return [...state, { text: action.payload, completed: false }];\n    default:\n      return state;\n  }\n}\n\n// After (Redux Toolkit)\nconst todosSlice = createSlice({\n  name: \"todos\",\n  initialState: [],\n  reducers: {\n    addTodo: (state, action: PayloadAction<string>) => {\n      // Immer allows \"mutations\"\n      state.push({ text: action.payload, completed: false });\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Redux Toolkit Documentation](https://redux-toolkit.js.org/)\n- [Zustand GitHub](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand)\n- [Jotai Documentation](https://jotai.org/)\n- [TanStack Query](https://tanstack.com/query)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:01:03.491Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents specializing in React applications needing efficient state management solutions.","zh":"适合专门从事 React 应用程序并需要高效状态管理解决方案的前端代理。","ja":"React アプリケーションで効率的な状態管理ソリューションを必要とするフロントエンド エージェントに最適です。","ko":"리액트 애플리케이션에서 효율적인 상태 관리 솔루션을 필요로 하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes frontend que se especializan en aplicaciones de React que necesitan soluciones de gestión de estado eficientes.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents frontend spécialisés dans les applications React nécessitant des solutions de gestion d''état efficaces.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agenten, die sich auf React-Anwendungen spezialisieren, die effiziente Statusverwaltungslösungen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Frontend especializados em aplicações React que necessitam de soluções de gerenciamento de estado eficientes.","ru":"Идеально для фронтенд-агентов, специализирующихся на приложениях React, требующих эффективных решений для управления состоянием.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية المتخصص في تطبيقات React التي تحتاج إلى حلول إدارة الحالة الفعالة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage complex React state using Redux Toolkit, Zustand, or Jotai, and synchronize server state with React Query or SWR, while implementing optimistic updates and debugging state-related issues.","zh":"赋予代理管理复杂的 React 状态，使用 Redux Toolkit、Zustand 或 Jotai，并使用 React Query 或 SWR 同步服务器状态，同时实现乐观更新和调试状态相关问题。","ja":"エージェントが複雑な React 状態を管理できるようにし、Redux Toolkit、Zustand、または Jotai を使用し、React Query または SWR を使用してサーバー状態を同期し、楽観的な更新と状態関連の問題のデバッグを実装します。","ko":"에이전트가 복잡한 리액트 상태를 관리할 수 있도록 해주며, Redux Toolkit, Zustand 또는 Jotai를 사용하고, React Query 또는 SWR를 사용하여 서버 상태를 동기화하며, 낙관적인 업데이트와 상태 관련 문제를 디버깅하는 기능을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar el estado complejo de React utilizando Redux Toolkit, Zustand o Jotai, y sincronizar el estado del servidor con React Query o SWR, al mismo tiempo que implementa actualizaciones optimistas y depura problemas relacionados con el estado.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer l''état complexe de React en utilisant Redux Toolkit, Zustand ou Jotai, et de synchroniser l''état du serveur avec React Query ou SWR, tout en mettant en œuvre des mises à jour optimistes et en déboguant les problèmes liés à l''état.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, den komplexen React-Zustand mit Redux Toolkit, Zustand oder Jotai zu verwalten und den Serverzustand mit React Query oder SWR zu synchronisieren, während gleichzeitig optimistische Updates implementiert und Zustandsbezogene Probleme behoben werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar o estado complexo do React usando Redux Toolkit, Zustand ou Jotai, e sincronizar o estado do servidor com React Query ou SWR, além de implementar atualizações otimistas e depurar problemas relacionados ao estado.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять сложным состоянием React с помощью Redux Toolkit, Zustand или Jotai, а также синхронизировать состояние сервера с React Query или SWR, реализуя оптимистические обновления и отладку проблем, связанных с состоянием.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إدارة حالة React المعقدة باستخدام أداة Redux أو Zustand أو Jotai، وتزامن حالة الخادم مع استعلام React أو SWR، بالإضافة إلى تنفيذ تحديثات مُتَفَائِلة وتصحيح مشاكل متعلقة بالحالة."},"useCases":{"en":["Setting up global state management in React apps","Debugging state-related issues in React applications","Migrating legacy Redux to modern state management patterns"],"zh":["在 React 应用程序中设置全局状态管理","在 React 应用程序中调试状态相关问题","将传统的 Redux 迁移到现代状态管理模式"],"ja":["React アプリケーションでグローバル状態管理を設定する","React アプリケーションで状態関連の問題をデバッグする","レガシーの Redux をモダンな状態管理パターンに移行する"],"ko":["리액트 애플리케이션에서 글로벌 상태 관리를 설정하는 것","리액트 애플리케이션에서 상태 관련 문제를 디버깅하는 것","레거시 리덕스를 현대적인 상태 관리 패턴으로 마이그레이션하는 것"],"es":["Configuración de la gestión de estado global en aplicaciones de React","Depuración de problemas relacionados con el estado en aplicaciones de React","Migración de patrones de gestión de estado de legacy a patrones de gestión de estado modernos"],"fr":["Configuration de la gestion d''état global dans les applications React","Débogage des problèmes liés à l''état dans les applications React","Migration de modèles de gestion d''état legacy vers des modèles de gestion d''état modernes"],"de":["Einrichtung der globalen Statusverwaltung in React-Anwendungen","Behandlung von statusbezogenen Problemen in React-Anwendungen","Migration von Legacy-Statusverwaltungsmustern zu modernen Statusverwaltungsmustern"],"pt":["Configurar o gerenciamento de estado global em aplicativos React","Depurar problemas relacionados ao estado em aplicativos React","Migrar o Redux legado para padrões de gerenciamento de estado modernos"],"ru":["Настройка глобального управления состоянием в приложениях React","Отладка проблем, связанных с состоянием, в приложениях React","Миграция устаревшего Redux на современные шаблоны управления состоянием"],"ar":["تكوين إدارة الحالة العالمية في تطبيقات React","تصحيح الأخطاء المتعلقة بالحالة في تطبيقات React","هجرة Redux القديم إلى أنماط إدارة الحالة الحديثة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React application setup","Limited to React state management solutions"],"zh":["需要 React 应用程序设置","仅限 React 状态管理解决方案"],"ja":["React アプリケーションの設定が必要","React 状態管理ソリューションのみに限定される"],"ko":["리액트 애플리케이션 설정이 필요","리액트 상태 관리 솔루션에만限定"],"es":["Requiere configuración de la aplicación de React","Limitado a soluciones de gestión de estado de React"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration d''application React","Limité aux solutions de gestion d''état React"],"de":["Erfordert React-Anwendungskonfiguration","Begrenzt auf React-Statusverwaltungslösungen"],"pt":["Requer configuração de aplicativo React","Limitado a soluções de gerenciamento de estado do React"],"ru":["Требует настройки приложения React","Ограничен решениями для управления состоянием React"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد تطبيق React","محدود بحلول إدارة الحالة في React"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
