rabajo de Proyecto automatiza todo el ciclo de vida del proyecto, desde la validación de ideas hasta la ejecución y lanzamiento.","fr":"Le Skill de Flux de Travail de Projet automatise tout le cycle de vie du projet, de la validation des idées à l''exécution et au lancement.","de":"Das Projekt-Workflown-Skill automatisiert den gesamten Projekt-Lebenszyklus, von der Ideenvalidierung bis zur Ausführung und Veröffentlichung.","pt":"O skill de fluxo de projeto automatiza o ciclo de vida do projeto, desde a validação da ideia até a liberação.","ru":"Навык рабочего процесса проекта автоматизирует цикл жизни проекта, от проверки идеи до выпуска.","ar":"مهارة تدفق المشروع تتمتع بآليّة دورة حياة المشروع، بدءًا من التحقق من الفكرة وحتى الإصدار.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["9个集成的斜杠命令","自动化项目生命周期","节省35-55分钟的时间","支持idea验证","支持项目规划","支持项目执行"],"ja":["9つの統合されたスラッシュコマンド","プロジェクトライフサイクルの自動化","35〜55分の時間の節約","アイデアの検証のサポート","プロジェクト計画のサポート","プロジェクト実行のサポート"],"ko":["9개의 통합 슬래시 명령","프로젝트 生命周期의 자동화","35〜55분의 시간 절약","아이디어 검증 지원","프로젝트 계획 지원","프로젝트 실행 지원"],"es":["9 comandos integrados para automatizar el ciclo de vida del proyecto","Validación de ideas y planificación","Ejecución y gestión de sesiones","Preservación del contexto y lanzamiento","Ahorro de 35-55 minutos por proyecto"],"fr":["9 commandes intégrées pour automatiser le cycle de vie du projet","Validation des idées et planification","Exécution et gestion de sessions","Préservation du contexte et lancement","Économie de 35-55 minutes par projet"],"de":["9 integrierte Befehle für die Automatisierung des Projekt-Lebenszyklus","Ideenvalidierung und Planung","Ausführung und Sitzungsverwaltung","Kontexterhaltung und Veröffentlichung","Einsparung von 35-55 Minuten pro Projekt"],"pt":["9 comandos integrados para automação do ciclo de vida do projeto","Validação de ideias","Planejamento","Execução","Gerenciamento de sessões","Preservação de contexto","Lançamento"],"ru":["9 интегрированных команд для автоматизации цикла жизни проекта","Проверка идей","Планирование","Выполнение","Управление сессиями","Сохранение контекста","Выпуск"],"ar":["9 أوامر متكاملة لآليّة دورة حياة المشروع","التحقق من الأفكار","التخطيط","التنفيذ","إدارة الجلسات","الحفاظ على السياق","الإصدار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["项目工作流","自动化","项目生命周期","斜杠命令","idea验证","项目规划","项目执行"],"ja":["プロジェクトワークフロー","自動化","プロジェクトライフサイクル","スラッシュコマンド","アイデアの検証","プロジェクト計画","プロジェクト実行"],"ko":["프로젝트 워크플로","자동화","프로젝트 生命周期","슬래시 명령","아이디어 검증","프로젝트 계획","프로젝트 실행"],"es":["automatización de flujo de trabajo","proyecto","ciclo de vida","validación de ideas","planificación","ejecución","gestión de sesiones","preservación del contexto","lanzamiento","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["automatisation du flux de travail","projet","cycle de vie","validation des idées","planification","exécution","gestion de sessions","préservation du contexte","lancement","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Automatisierung des Workflows","Projekt","Lebenszyklus","Ideenvalidierung","Planung","Ausführung","Sitzungsverwaltung","Kontexterhaltung","Veröffentlichung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["fluxo de projeto","automação de projeto","gerenciamento de projeto","validação de ideias","planejamento de projeto","execução de projeto","lançamento de projeto","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["рабочий процесс проекта","автоматизация проекта","управление проектом","проверка идей","планирование проекта","выполнение проекта","выпуск проекта","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["تدفق المشروع","آليّة المشروع","إدارة المشروع","التحقق من الأفكار","تخطيط المشروع","تنفيذ المشروع","إصدار المشروع","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"project-workflow","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Project Workflow Skill\n\n9 integrated slash commands for complete project lifecycle automation: idea validation → planning → execution → session management → context preservation → release.\n\n**Time savings**: 35-55 minutes per project lifecycle\n\n## Installation\n\n**Marketplace**: `/plugin install project-workflow@claude-skills`\n\n**Manual**: Copy `commands/*.md` to `~/.claude/commands/`\n\n## The 7 Commands\n\n### 1. `/explore-idea` - Pre-Planning Exploration\n\n**Use when**: Rough idea that needs tech","body":"# Project Workflow Skill\n\n9 integrated slash commands for complete project lifecycle automation: idea validation → planning → execution → session management → context preservation → release.\n\n**Time savings**: 35-55 minutes per project lifecycle\n\n## Installation\n\n**Marketplace**: `/plugin install project-workflow@claude-skills`\n\n**Manual**: Copy `commands/*.md` to `~/.claude/commands/`\n\n## The 7 Commands\n\n### 1. `/explore-idea` - Pre-Planning Exploration\n\n**Use when**: Rough idea that needs tech stack validation, scope management, or research before planning.\n\n**Creates**: PROJECT_BRIEF.md with validated decisions → hands off to /plan-project\n\n**Time savings**: 10-15 min\n\n---\n\n### 2. `/plan-project` - Generate Project Planning Docs\n\n**Use when**: Starting new project with clear requirements, or after /explore-idea.\n\n**Creates**: IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md, SESSION.md, DATABASE_SCHEMA.md (if needed), API_ENDPOINTS.md (if needed), ARCHITECTURE.md\n\n**Invokes**: project-planning skill\n\n**Time savings**: 5-7 min\n\n---\n\n### 3. `/plan-feature` - Add Features to Existing Projects\n\n**Use when**: Adding feature to existing project with SESSION.md + IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md.\n\n**Does**: Generates new phases via project-planning skill, integrates into IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md with renumbering, updates SESSION.md.\n\n**Time savings**: 7-10 min\n\n---\n\n### 4. `/wrap-session` - End-of-Session Checkpoint\n\n**Use when**: Context full (>150k tokens), end of work session, or before task switch.\n\n**Does**: Task agent analyzes session → updates SESSION.md (progress, Next Action, blockers) → git checkpoint commit → formatted handoff summary.\n\n**Time savings**: 2-3 min\n\n---\n\n### 5. `/continue-session` - Start-of-Session Context Loading\n\n**Use when**: Starting new session or after /wrap-session checkpoint.\n\n**Does**: Explore agent loads SESSION.md + planning docs → shows git history + session summary (phase, progress, Next Action, blockers) → optionally opens file → asks permission to continue.\n\n**Time savings**: 1-2 min\n\n---\n\n### 6. `/workflow` - Interactive Workflow Guide\n\n**Use when**: First time user, unsure which command to use, or need quick reference.\n\n**Does**: Shows all 7 commands → context-aware guidance with decision trees → offers to execute appropriate command.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `/release` - Pre-Release Safety Checks\n\n**Use when**: Ready to push to public GitHub or create release.\n\n**8 Phases**:\n1. **Critical Safety** (BLOCKERS): Secrets scan (gitleaks), personal artifacts check, git remote verification\n2. **Documentation** (REQUIRED): LICENSE, README (>100 words), CONTRIBUTING.md (>500 LOC), CODE_OF_CONDUCT (>1000 LOC)\n3. **Configuration**: .gitignore, package.json, git branch warning\n4. **Quality** (NON-BLOCKING): Build test, npm audit, large files (>1MB)\n5. **Report**: Blockers/warnings/recommendations + safe to release verdict\n6-8. **Auto-Fix & Publish**: Fix issues, release prep commit, optional git tag + GitHub release\n\n**Time savings**: 10-15 min\n\n---\n\n### 8. `/brief` - Context Preservation Document\n\n**Use when**: Before clearing context, to preserve key decisions and requirements for future sessions.\n\n**Creates**: `docs/brief-[slug].md` with extracted information from current conversation.\n\n**Does**: Analyzes conversation → extracts what''s being built, decisions made, technical details → creates organized markdown file → optionally creates GitHub issue for tracking.\n\n**Time savings**: 3-5 min\n\n---\n\n### 9. `/reflect` - Capture Operational Knowledge\n\n**Use when**: Before context compaction, after completing significant work, or when valuable learnings accumulated.\n\n**Does**: Reviews conversation → identifies workflows discovered, patterns learned, tool sequences, corrections made → routes each learning to appropriate destination (rules, CLAUDE.md, skills, docs) → optionally suggests automation (scripts, commands, custom agents).\n\n**Key Feature**: Considers whether processes should become custom agents when they require reasoning/decisions, benefit from parallel execution, or involve research/exploration.\n\n**Time savings**: 5-10 min\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Examples\n\n**Full**: /explore-idea → /plan-project → work → /wrap-session → /continue-session → /plan-feature (if needed) → repeat → /reflect → /release\n\n**Quick** (clear requirements): /plan-project → work → /wrap-session → /continue-session → /release\n\n**Context Preservation**: /brief (before clearing context), /reflect (capture learnings)\n\n**Helpers**: /workflow (guidance), /plan-feature (add feature), /release (publish)\n\n---\n\n## Integration\n\n**project-planning**: Invoked by /plan-project and /plan-feature (generates IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md, DATABASE_SCHEMA.md, API_ENDPOINTS.md)\n\n**project-session-management**: SESSION.md protocol for /wrap-session and /continue-session\n\n**Claude Code agents**: /wrap-session (Task agent), /continue-session + /explore-idea (Explore agent)\n\n---\n\n## Command Relationships\n\n```\nEXPLORATION PHASE\n/explore-idea (optional)\n    ↓\n    Creates PROJECT_BRIEF.md\n    ↓\nPLANNING PHASE\n/plan-project (reads PROJECT_BRIEF.md if exists)\n    ↓\n    Creates IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md + SESSION.md\n    ↓\nEXECUTION PHASE\nWork on phases\n    ↓\n/wrap-session (when context full)\n    ↓\n    Updates SESSION.md, git checkpoint\n    ↓\n/continue-session (new session)\n    ↓\n    Loads SESSION.md, continues work\n    ↓\n/plan-feature (when need new features)\n    ↓\n    Adds phases to IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md\n    ↓\nContinue wrap → resume cycle\n    ↓\nCONTEXT PRESERVATION\n/brief (before clearing context)\n    ↓\n    Creates docs/brief-[slug].md\n    ↓\n/reflect (capture learnings)\n    ↓\n    Routes knowledge to rules, docs, CLAUDE.md\n    ↓\nRELEASE PHASE\n/release (when ready to publish)\n    ↓\n    Safety checks → GitHub release\n\nHELPER\n/workflow (anytime)\n    ↓\n    Interactive guidance\n```\n\n---\n\n## Time Savings Breakdown\n\n| Command | Time Saved | Tasks Automated |\n|---------|------------|-----------------|\n| `/explore-idea` | 10-15 min | Research, validation, scope management, tech stack evaluation |\n| `/plan-project` | 5-7 min | Planning doc generation, git setup, phase structuring |\n| `/plan-feature` | 7-10 min | Feature planning, phase integration, doc updates |\n| `/wrap-session` | 2-3 min | SESSION.md updates, git checkpoint, handoff summary |\n| `/continue-session` | 1-2 min | Context loading, git history review, next action display |\n| `/workflow` | Instant | Navigation, decision trees, command selection |\n| `/release` | 10-15 min | Secret scanning, doc validation, build testing, release creation |\n| `/brief` | 3-5 min | Context extraction, decisions capture, markdown generation |\n| `/reflect` | 5-10 min | Learning extraction, knowledge routing, automation suggestions |\n\n**Total per project lifecycle:** 45-70 minutes\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n**All**: Claude Code CLI, git repo (recommended)\n\n**/plan-feature**: Existing SESSION.md + IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md\n\n**/wrap-session, /continue-session**: SESSION.md (created by /plan-project)\n\n**/release**: Git repo with commits, package.json (Node.js), remote URL (for publishing)\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**/plan-project \"No project description\"**: Use /explore-idea first or discuss project with Claude\n\n**/plan-feature \"Prerequisites not met\"**: Run /plan-project first (creates SESSION.md + IMPLEMENTATION_PHASES.md)\n\n**/wrap-session \"No git repository\"**: Run `git init`\n\n**/continue-session \"SESSION.md not found\"**: Run /plan-project\n\n**/release \"Secrets detected\"**: Add to .gitignore, remove from git history\n\n---\n\n## Version History\n\n**1.1.0** (2026-01-11)\n- Added `/brief` command for context preservation\n- Added `/reflect` command for capturing operational knowledge\n- `/reflect` now suggests custom agents for processes requiring reasoning\n- Total commands: 9\n\n**1.0.0** (2025-11-12)\n- Initial release\n- 7 integrated slash commands\n- Plugin marketplace distribution\n- Command bundling via plugin.json\n\n---\n\n**Issues**: https://github.com/jezweb/claude-skills/issues | **Author**: Jeremy Dawes (jeremy@jezweb.net) | **License**: MIT\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:01:21.172Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing end-to-end lifecycle automation from ideation to release.","zh":"非常适合需要从概念到发布的端到端生命周期自动化的项目管理代理。","ja":"プロジェクト管理エージェントが概念からリリースまでのエンドツーエンドのライフサイクル自動化を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"개념에서 출시까지의 종단 간 라이프 사이클 자동화를 필요한 프로젝트 관리 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing end-to-end lifecycle automation from ideation to release.","fr":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing end-to-end lifecycle automation from ideation to release.","de":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing end-to-end lifecycle automation from ideation to release.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Projetos que necessitam de automação de ciclo de vida de ponta a ponta, desde a ideia até a liberação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления проектами, которым требуется автоматизация жизненного цикла от идеи до выпуска.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء لإدارة المشاريع الذين يحتاجون إلى أتمتة دورة حياة متكاملة من الفكرة إلى الإصدار."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to automate the complete project workflow with 9 integrated slash commands, providing session management and context preservation capabilities throughout the entire development lifecycle.","zh":"使代理能够使用 9 个集成的斜杠命令来自动化整个项目工作流，并在整个开发生命周期中提供会话管理和上下文保留功能。","ja":"エージェントが 9 つの統合スラッシュコマンドを使用してプロジェクトのワークフローを自動化し、開発ライフサイクル全体でセッション管理とコンテキスト保留機能を提供できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 9개의 통합 슬래시 명령을 사용하여 프로젝트 워크플로를 자동화하고, 전체 개발 라이프 사이클에서 세션 관리와 컨텍스트 보존 기능을 제공할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Enables agents to automate the complete project workflow with 9 integrated slash commands, providing session management and context preservation capabilities throughout the entire development lifecycle.","fr":"Enables agents to automate the complete project workflow with 9 integrated slash commands, providing session management and context preservation capabilities throughout the entire development lifecycle.","de":"Enables agents to automate the complete project workflow with 9 integrated slash commands, providing session management and context preservation capabilities throughout the entire development lifecycle.","pt":"Permite que os agentes automatem o fluxo de trabalho do projeto completo com 9 comandos de barra integrados, fornecendo capacidades de gerenciamento de sessão e preservação de contexto em todo o ciclo de vida de desenvolvimento.","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать полный рабочий процесс проекта с 9 интегрированными командами-слэш, обеспечивая возможности управления сеансами и сохранения контекста на протяжении всего цикла разработки.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء بأتمتة تدفق عمل المشروع الكامل مع 9 أوامر شريطية متكاملة ، وتوفير إمكانيات إدارة الجلسة والحفاظ على السياق في جميع أنحاء دورة حياة التطوير."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating technical feasibility of rough ideas","Automating project planning and execution workflows","Managing development sessions with context preservation","Streamlining release preparation processes"],"zh":["验证技术上粗略想法的可行性","自动化项目规划和执行工作流","使用上下文保留管理开发会话","简化发布准备流程"],"ja":["細かいアイデアの技術的妥当性を検証する","プロジェクト計画と実行ワークフローを自動化する","コンテキスト保留を使用して開発セッションを管理する","リリース準備プロセスを簡素化する"],"ko":["거친 아이디어의 기술적 타당성을 검증하는 것","프로젝트 계획 및 실행 워크플로 자동화","컨텍스트 보존을 사용하여 개발 세션 관리","릴리즈 준비 프로세스 간소화"],"es":["Validating technical feasibility of rough ideas","Automating project planning and execution workflows","Managing development sessions with context preservation","Streamlining release preparation processes"],"fr":["Validating technical feasibility of rough ideas","Automating project planning and execution workflows","Managing development sessions with context preservation","Streamlining release preparation processes"],"de":["Validating technical feasibility of rough ideas","Automating project planning and execution workflows","Managing development sessions with context preservation","Streamlining release preparation processes"],"pt":["Validar a viabilidade técnica de ideias vagas","Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de planejamento e execução de projetos","Gerenciar sessões de desenvolvimento com preservação de contexto","Otimitzar processos de preparação para lançamento"],"ru":["Проверка технической осуществимости приблизительных идей","Автоматизация рабочих процессов планирования и выполнения проектов","Управление сеансами разработки с сохранением контекста","Оптимизация процессов подготовки к выпуску"],"ar":["التحقق من الجدوى الفنية للأفكار الغامضة","أتمتة تدفقات العمل التخطيطية والتنفيذية للمشاريع","إدارة جلسات التطوير مع الحفاظ على السياق","تحسين عمليات التحضير للإصدار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires manual installation via Claude Skills marketplace","Depends on slash command compatibility with host agent","Needs ~/.claude/commands/ directory access for manual setup"],"zh":["需要通过 Claude Skills 市场进行手动安装","依赖于主机代理的斜杠命令兼容性","需要 ~/.claude/commands/ 目录访问权限以进行手动设置"],"ja":["Claude Skills マーケットプレイスを介した手動インストールが必要","ホストエージェントのスラッシュコマンド互換性に依存する","手動セットアップのために ~/.claude/commands/ ディレクトリへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["클라우드 스킬스 마켓플레이스를 통한 수동 설치가 필요합니다.","호스트 에이전트의 슬래시 명령어 호환성에 의존합니다.","수동 설정을 위한 ~/.claude/commands/ 디렉토리 접근 권한이 필요합니다."],"es":["Requires manual installation via Claude Skills marketplace","Depends on slash command compatibility with host agent","Needs ~/.claude/commands/ directory access for manual setup"],"fr":["Requires manual installation via Claude Skills marketplace","Depends on slash command compatibility with host agent","Needs ~/.claude/commands/ directory access for manual setup"],"de":["Requires manual installation via Claude Skills marketplace","Depends on slash command compatibility with host agent","Needs ~/.claude/commands/ directory access for manual setup"],"pt":["Exige instalação manual via mercado de habilidades Claude","Depende da compatibilidade do comando de barra com o agente hospedeiro","Necessita de acesso ao diretório ~/.claude/commands/ para configuração manual"],"ru":["Требует ручной установки через рынок навыков Claude","Зависит от совместимости команды-слэш с хост-агентом","Требует доступа к каталогу ~/.claude/commands/ для ручной настройки"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيتًا يدويًا عبر سوق مهارات كلود","يعتمد على توافق أمر الشريط مع وكلاء الاستضافة","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى الدليل ~/.claude/commands/ لإعداد يدوي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/tailwind-css-patterns', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'tailwind-css-patterns', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z', '2026-02-18T14:01:28.038Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/tailwind-css-patterns","name":"tailwind-css-patterns","description":{"zh":"Tailwind CSS ","ja":"Tailwind CSS","ko":"Tailwind CSS ","es":"Guía experta para desarrolladores sobre patrones de Tailwind CSS para crear interfaces de usuario modernas y responsivas","fr":"Guide expert pour les développeurs sur les modèles Tailwind CSS pour créer des interfaces utilisateur modernes et responsives","de":"Expertenführer für Entwickler zu Tailwind CSS-Mustern für die Erstellung moderner und responsiver Benutzeroberflächen","pt":"Guia de padrões de Tailwind CSS para desenvolvedores. Aprenda a criar interfaces de usuário modernas e responsivas com a estrutura de utilidade em primeiro lugar.","ru":"Руководство по шаблонам Tailwind CSS для разработчиков. Узнайте, как создавать современные и адаптивные пользовательские интерфейсы с помощью утилитарной структуры","ar":"دليل نمذجة تايلويند سي إس للمطورين. تعلم كيفية إنشاء واجهات مستخدم حديثة ومتجاوبة مع الإطار الأول للوظائف","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Tailwind CSS ","ja":"Tailwind CSS","ko":"Tailwind CSS ","es":"Patrones de Tailwind CSS para Desarrolladores","fr":"Modèles Tailwind CSS pour les Développeurs","de":"Tailwind CSS-Muster für Entwickler","pt":"Padrões de Tailwind CSS para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Шаблоны Tailwind CSS для разработчиков","ar":"نماذج تايلويند سي إس لل مطورين","en":"tailwind-css-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"Tailwind CSS ","ja":"Tailwind CSS","ko":"Tailwind CSS ","es":"Guía experta para desarrolladores sobre patrones de Tailwind CSS para crear interfaces de usuario modernas y responsivas","fr":"Guide expert pour les développeurs sur les modèles Tailwind CSS pour créer des interfaces utilisateur modernes et responsives","de":"Expertenführer für Entwickler zu Tailwind CSS-Mustern für die Erstellung moderner und responsiver Benutzeroberflächen","pt":"Guia de padrões de Tailwind CSS para desenvolvedores. Aprenda a criar interfaces de usuário modernas e responsivas com a estrutura de utilidade em primeiro l...","ru":"Руководство по шаблонам Tailwind CSS для разработчиков. Узнайте, как создавать современные и адаптивные пользовательские интерфейсы с помощью утилитарной стр...","ar":"دليل نمذجة تايلويند سي إس للمطورين. تعلم كيفية إنشاء واجهات مستخدم حديثة ومتجاوبة مع الإطار الأول للوظائف","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["CSS","React/HTML","responsive","flexbox","grid","CSS"],"ja":["CSS","React/HTML","responsive","flexbox","grid","CSS"],"ko":["CSS","React/HTML","responsive","flexbox","grid","CSS"],"es":["Configuración de CSS primero","Utilidades personalizadas","Mejoras en la experiencia del desarrollador","Diseño de layouts responsivos","Implementación de flexbox y grid","Gestión de espaciado, colores y tipografía"],"fr":["Configuration CSS première","Utilitaires personnalisés","Améliorations de l''expérience du développeur","Conception de layouts responsifs","Mise en œuvre de flexbox et de grid","Gestion de l''espacement, des couleurs et de la typographie"],"de":["CSS-erstes Konfiguration","Benutzerdefinierte Utilities","Verbesserungen in der Entwicklererfahrung","Entwurf von responsiven Layouts","Implementierung von Flexbox und Grid","Verwaltung von Abständen, Farben und Typografie"],"pt":["Criação de layouts responsivos com pontos de interrupção","Implementação de layouts flexbox e grid","Gerenciamento de espaçamento, cores e tipografia","Criação de sistemas de design personalizados","Otimização para experiência do desenvolvedor"],"ru":["Создание адаптивных макетов с точками разрыва","Реализация макетов flexbox и grid","Управление расстоянием, цветами и типографией","Создание индивидуальных систем дизайна","Оптимизация для опыта разработчика"],"ar":["إنشاء تخطيطات متجاوبة مع نقاط انقطاع","تنفيذ تخطيطات flexbox و grid","إدارة المسافات والألوان والطباعة","إنشاء أنظمة تصميم مخصصة","تحسين خوارزمية لتجربة المطور"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Tailwind CSS","CSS","React","HTML","responsive","flexbox","grid","CSS"],"ja":["Tailwind CSS","CSS","React","HTML","responsive","flexbox","grid","CSS"],"ko":["Tailwind CSS","CSS","React","HTML","responsive","flexbox","grid","CSS"],"es":["Tailwind CSS","desarrollo web","interfaces de usuario","diseño responsivo","utilidades de CSS","flexbox","grid","tipografía","colores","espaciado"],"fr":["Tailwind CSS","développement web","interfaces utilisateur","conception responsives","utilitaires de CSS","flexbox","grid","typographie","couleurs","espacement"],"de":["Tailwind CSS","Webentwicklung","Benutzeroberflächen","responsives Design","CSS-Utilities","Flexbox","Grid","Typografie","Farben","Abstände"],"pt":["Tailwind CSS","Desenvolvimento de interfaces de usuário","Layouts responsivos","Flexbox","Grid","Sistemas de design personalizados","Otimização para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Tailwind CSS","Разработка пользовательских интерфейсов","Адаптивные макеты","Flexbox","Grid","Индивидуальные системы дизайна","Оптимизация для разработчиков"],"ar":["تايلويند سي إس","تطوير واجهات المستخدم","تخطيطات متجاوبة","flexbox","grid","أنظمة تصميم مخصصة","تحسين خوارزمية للمطورين"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tailwind-css-patterns","description":"Comprehensive Tailwind CSS utility-first styling patterns including responsive design, layout utilities, flexbox, grid, spacing, typography, colors, and modern CSS best practices. Use when styling React/Vue/Svelte components, building responsive layouts, implementing design systems, or optimizing CSS workflow.","bodyPreview":"# Tailwind CSS Development Patterns\n\nExpert guide for building modern, responsive user interfaces with Tailwind CSS utility-first framework. Covers v4.1+ features including CSS-first configuration, custom utilities, and enhanced developer experience.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Styling React/HTML components with utility classes\n- Building responsive layouts with breakpoints\n- Implementing flexbox and grid layouts\n- Managing spacing, colors, and typography\n- Creating custom design systems\n- Optimizing for","body":"# Tailwind CSS Development Patterns\n\nExpert guide for building modern, responsive user interfaces with Tailwind CSS utility-first framework. Covers v4.1+ features including CSS-first configuration, custom utilities, and enhanced developer experience.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Styling React/HTML components with utility classes\n- Building responsive layouts with breakpoints\n- Implementing flexbox and grid layouts\n- Managing spacing, colors, and typography\n- Creating custom design systems\n- Optimizing for mobile-first design\n- Building dark mode interfaces\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Utility-First Approach\n\nApply styles directly in markup using utility classes:\n\n```html\n<button class=\"bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded\">\n  Click me\n</button>\n```\n\n### Responsive Design\n\nMobile-first breakpoints with prefixes:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"w-full md:w-1/2 lg:w-1/3\">\n  <!-- Full width on mobile, half on tablet, third on desktop -->\n</div>\n```\n\nBreakpoint prefixes:\n- `sm:` - 640px and above\n- `md:` - 768px and above\n- `lg:` - 1024px and above\n- `xl:` - 1280px and above\n- `2xl:` - 1536px and above\n\n## Layout Utilities\n\n### Flexbox Layouts\n\nBasic flex container:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n  <div>Left</div>\n  <div>Center</div>\n  <div>Right</div>\n</div>\n```\n\nResponsive flex direction:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4\">\n  <div class=\"flex-1\">Item 1</div>\n  <div class=\"flex-1\">Item 2</div>\n  <div class=\"flex-1\">Item 3</div>\n</div>\n```\n\nCommon flex patterns:\n\n```html\n<!-- Center content -->\n<div class=\"flex items-center justify-center min-h-screen\">\n  <div>Centered Content</div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Space between items -->\n<div class=\"flex justify-between items-center\">\n  <span>Left</span>\n  <span>Right</span>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Vertical stack with gap -->\n<div class=\"flex flex-col gap-4\">\n  <div>Item 1</div>\n  <div>Item 2</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Grid Layouts\n\nBasic grid:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n  <div>Column 1</div>\n  <div>Column 2</div>\n  <div>Column 3</div>\n</div>\n```\n\nResponsive grid:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6\">\n  <!-- 1 column mobile, 2 tablet, 4 desktop -->\n  <div>Item 1</div>\n  <div>Item 2</div>\n  <div>Item 3</div>\n  <div>Item 4</div>\n</div>\n```\n\nAuto-fit columns:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr))] gap-4\">\n  <!-- Automatically fit columns based on container width -->\n</div>\n```\n\n### Container & Max Width\n\nCentered container with max width:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"container mx-auto px-4 max-w-7xl\">\n  <!-- Centered content with padding -->\n</div>\n```\n\nResponsive max width:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\">\n  <!-- Max 448px width, centered -->\n</div>\n```\n\n## Spacing\n\n### Padding & Margin\n\nUniform spacing:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"p-4\">Padding all sides</div>\n<div class=\"m-4\">Margin all sides</div>\n```\n\nIndividual sides:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"pt-4 pr-8 pb-4 pl-8\">\n  <!-- Top 1rem, Right 2rem, Bottom 1rem, Left 2rem -->\n</div>\n```\n\nAxis-based spacing:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"px-4 py-8\">\n  <!-- Horizontal padding 1rem, Vertical padding 2rem -->\n</div>\n```\n\nResponsive spacing:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"p-4 md:p-8 lg:p-12\">\n  <!-- Increases padding at larger breakpoints -->\n</div>\n```\n\nSpace between children:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"space-y-4\">\n  <div>Item 1</div>\n  <div>Item 2</div>\n  <div>Item 3</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Typography\n\n### Font Size & Weight\n\n```html\n<h1 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\">Large Heading</h1>\n<h2 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold\">Subheading</h2>\n<p class=\"text-base font-normal\">Body text</p>\n<small class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Small text</small>\n```\n\nResponsive typography:\n\n```html\n<h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-bold\">\n  Responsive Heading\n</h1>\n```\n\n### Line Height & Letter Spacing\n\n```html\n<p class=\"leading-relaxed tracking-wide\">\n  Text with relaxed line height and wide letter spacing\n</p>\n```\n\n### Text Alignment\n\n```html\n<p class=\"text-left md:text-center\">\n  Left aligned on mobile, centered on tablet+\n</p>\n```\n\n## Colors\n\n### Background Colors\n\n```html\n<div class=\"bg-blue-500\">Blue background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-gray-100\">Light gray background</div>\n<div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-purple-600\">\n  Gradient background\n</div>\n```\n\n### Text Colors\n\n```html\n<p class=\"text-gray-900\">Dark text</p>\n<p class=\"text-blue-600\">Blue text</p>\n<p class=\"text-red-500\">Error text</p>\n```\n\n### Opacity\n\n```html\n<div class=\"bg-blue-500 bg-opacity-50\">\n  Semi-transparent blue\n</div>\n```\n\n## Interactive States\n\n### Hover States\n\n```html\n<button class=\"bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-700 transition\">\n  Hover me\n</button>\n\n<a class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 hover:underline\">\n  Hover link\n</a>\n```\n\n### Focus States\n\n```html\n<input class=\"border border-gray-300 focus:border-blue-500 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-200 outline-none\">\n```\n\n### Active & Disabled States\n\n```html\n<button class=\"bg-blue-500 active:bg-blue-800 disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed\">\n  Button\n</button>\n```\n\n### Group Hover\n\n```html\n<div class=\"group\">\n  <img class=\"group-hover:opacity-75\" src=\"image.jpg\" />\n  <p class=\"group-hover:text-blue-600\">Hover the parent</p>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Component Patterns\n\n### Card Component\n\n```html\n<div class=\"bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg overflow-hidden\">\n  <img class=\"w-full h-48 object-cover\" src=\"image.jpg\" alt=\"Card image\" />\n  <div class=\"p-6\">\n    <h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold mb-2\">Card Title</h3>\n    <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Card description text goes here.</p>\n    <button class=\"bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded\">\n      Action\n    </button>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Responsive User Card\n\n```html\n<div class=\"max-w-sm mx-auto bg-white rounded-xl shadow-lg overflow-hidden sm:flex sm:max-w-2xl\">\n  <img class=\"h-48 w-full object-cover sm:h-auto sm:w-48\" \n       src=\"profile.jpg\" \n       alt=\"Profile\" />\n  <div class=\"p-8\">\n    <div class=\"uppercase tracking-wide text-sm text-indigo-500 font-semibold\">\n      Product Engineer\n    </div>\n    <h2 class=\"mt-1 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">\n      John Doe\n    </h2>\n    <p class=\"mt-2 text-gray-500\">\n      Building amazing products with modern technology.\n    </p>\n    <button class=\"mt-4 px-4 py-2 bg-indigo-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-indigo-700 transition\">\n      Contact\n    </button>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Navigation Bar\n\n```html\n<nav class=\"bg-white shadow-lg\">\n  <div class=\"container mx-auto px-4\">\n    <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center h-16\">\n      <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-800\">Logo</a>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"hidden md:flex space-x-8\">\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-gray-700 hover:text-blue-600 transition\">Home</a>\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-gray-700 hover:text-blue-600 transition\">About</a>\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-gray-700 hover:text-blue-600 transition\">Services</a>\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-gray-700 hover:text-blue-600 transition\">Contact</a>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"md:hidden\">\n        <svg class=\"w-6 h-6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\n          <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16\"></path>\n        </svg>\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</nav>\n```\n\n### Form Elements\n\n```html\n<form class=\"space-y-6 max-w-md mx-auto\">\n  <div>\n    <label class=\"block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\">\n      Email\n    </label>\n    <input \n      type=\"email\" \n      class=\"w-full px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-transparent\"\n      placeholder=\"you@example.com\"\n    />\n  </div>\n  \n  <div>\n    <label class=\"block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\">\n      Password\n    </label>\n    <input \n      type=\"password\" \n      class=\"w-full px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-transparent\"\n    />\n  </div>\n  \n  <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n    <input type=\"checkbox\" class=\"mr-2\" />\n    <label class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Remember me</label>\n  </div>\n  \n  <button \n    type=\"submit\"\n    class=\"w-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold py-2 px-4 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition\"\n  >\n    Sign In\n  </button>\n</form>\n```\n\n### Modal/Dialog\n\n```html\n<div class=\"fixed inset-0 bg-black bg-opacity-50 flex items-center justify-center p-4\">\n  <div class=\"bg-white rounded-lg shadow-xl max-w-md w-full p-6\">\n    <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mb-4\">\n      <h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold\">Modal Title</h3>\n      <button class=\"text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-700\">\n        <svg class=\"w-6 h-6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\n          <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12\"></path>\n        </svg>\n      </button>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-6\">\n      Modal content goes here.\n    </p>\n    <div class=\"flex justify-end space-x-4\">\n      <button class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-800\">\n        Cancel\n      </button>\n      <button class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded hover:bg-blue-700\">\n        Confirm\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Responsive Design Patterns\n\n### Mobile-First Responsive Layout\n\n```html\n<div class=\"container mx-auto px-4\">\n  <!-- Hero Section -->\n  <div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-8 py-12\">\n    <div class=\"flex-1\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4\">\n        Welcome to Our Site\n      </h1>\n      <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-600 mb-6\">\n        Build amazing things with Tailwind CSS\n      </p>\n      <button class=\"bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700\">\n        Get Started\n      </button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"flex-1\">\n      <img src=\"hero.jpg\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg shadow-lg\" />\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Responsive Grid Gallery\n\n```html\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 p-4\">\n  <div class=\"aspect-square bg-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n    <img src=\"image1.jpg\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover hover:scale-105 transition\" />\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"aspect-square bg-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n    <img src=\"image2.jpg\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover hover:scale-105 transition\" />\n  </div>\n  <!-- More items... -->\n</div>\n```\n\n## Dark Mode\n\n### Basic Dark Mode Support\n\n```html\n<div class=\"bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 text-gray-900 dark:text-white\">\n  <h1 class=\"text-gray-900 dark:text-white\">Title</h1>\n  <p class=\"text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400\">Description</p>\n</div>\n```\n\nEnable dark mode in tailwind.config.js:\n\n```javascript\nmodule.exports = {\n  darkMode: ''class'', // or ''media''\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n## Animations & Transitions\n\n### Basic Transitions\n\n```html\n<button class=\"bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-700 transition duration-300\">\n  Smooth transition\n</button>\n```\n\n### Transform Effects\n\n```html\n<div class=\"transform hover:scale-110 transition duration-300\">\n  Scale on hover\n</div>\n\n<img class=\"transform hover:rotate-6 transition duration-300\" />\n```\n\n### Built-in Animations\n\n```html\n<div class=\"animate-spin\">Spinning</div>\n<div class=\"animate-pulse\">Pulsing</div>\n<div class=\"animate-bounce\">Bouncing</div>\n```\n\n## Performance Optimization\n\n### Bundle Size Optimization\n\nConfigure content sources for optimal purging:\n\n```javascript\n// tailwind.config.js\nexport default {\n  content: [\n    \"./index.html\",\n    \"./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx,vue,svelte}\",\n    \"./node_modules/@mycompany/ui-lib/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}\",\n  ],\n  // Enable JIT for faster builds\n  jit: true,\n}\n```\n\n### CSS Optimization Techniques\n\n```html\n<!-- Use content-visibility for offscreen content -->\n<div class=\"content-visibility-auto\">\n  <div>Heavy content that''s initially offscreen</div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Optimize images with aspect-ratio -->\n<img class=\"aspect-video w-full object-cover\" src=\"video.jpg\" alt=\"Video thumbnail\" />\n\n<!-- Use contain for paint optimization -->\n<div class=\"contain-layout\">\n  Complex layout that doesn''t affect outside elements\n</div>\n```\n\n### Development Performance\n\n```css\n/* Enable CSS-first configuration in v4.1 */\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n@theme {\n  /* Define once, use everywhere */\n  --color-brand: #3b82f6;\n  --font-mono: \"Fira Code\", monospace;\n}\n\n/* Critical CSS for above-the-fold content */\n@layer critical {\n  .hero-title {\n    @apply text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Accessibility Guidelines\n\n### Focus Management\n\n```html\n<!-- Custom focus styles that meet WCAG AA -->\n<button class=\"focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-2\">\n  Accessible Button\n</button>\n\n<!-- Skip links for keyboard navigation -->\n<a href=\"#main-content\" class=\"sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4\">\n  Skip to main content\n</a>\n```\n\n### Screen Reader Support\n\n```html\n<!-- Semantic buttons with ARIA labels -->\n<button aria-label=\"Close dialog\" class=\"p-2\">\n  <svg class=\"w-5 h-5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n    <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12\" />\n  </svg>\n</button>\n\n<!-- Descriptive links -->\n<a href=\"/docs\" aria-describedby=\"docs-description\">\n  Documentation\n</a>\n<p id=\"docs-description\" class=\"sr-only\">\n  Learn how to use our API and integration guides\n</p>\n```\n\n### Color Contrast\n\n```html\n<!-- Ensure sufficient contrast ratios -->\n<div class=\"bg-gray-900 text-white\">\n  High contrast text (WCAG AAA)\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"bg-blue-500 text-blue-100\">\n  Good contrast on colored backgrounds\n</div>\n\n<!-- Use contrast utilities for testing -->\n<div class=\"bg-red-500 text-white contrast-more:bg-red-600 contrast-more:text-red-100\">\n  Adjusts for high contrast mode\n</div>\n```\n\n### Motion Preferences\n\n```html\n<!-- Respect prefers-reduced-motion -->\n<div class=\"transform transition-transform motion-reduce:transition-none\">\n  Doesn''t animate when user prefers reduced motion\n</div>\n\n<!-- Conditional animations -->\n<div class=\"animate-pulse motion-safe:hover:animate-spin\">\n  Only animates when motion is preferred\n</div>\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Mobile-First**: Start with mobile styles, add responsive prefixes for larger screens\n2. **Consistent Spacing**: Use Tailwind''s spacing scale (4, 8, 12, 16, etc.)\n3. **Color Palette**: Stick to Tailwind''s color system for consistency\n4. **Component Extraction**: Extract repeated patterns into components\n5. **Utility Composition**: Prefer utility classes over @apply for better maintainability\n6. **Semantic HTML**: Use proper HTML elements with Tailwind classes\n7. **Performance**: Configure content paths correctly for optimal CSS purging\n8. **Accessibility**: Include focus styles, ARIA labels, and respect user preferences\n9. **CSS-First Config**: Use @theme directive for v4.1+ instead of JavaScript config\n10. **Custom Utilities**: Create reusable utilities with @utility for complex patterns\n\n## Configuration\n\n### CSS-First Configuration (v4.1+)\n\nUse the `@theme` directive for CSS-based configuration:\n\n```css\n/* src/styles.css */\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n@theme {\n  /* Custom colors */\n  --color-brand-50: #f0f9ff;\n  --color-brand-500: #3b82f6;\n  --color-brand-900: #1e3a8a;\n\n  /* Custom fonts */\n  --font-display: \"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif;\n  --font-mono: \"Fira Code\", monospace;\n\n  /* Custom spacing */\n  --spacing-128: 32rem;\n\n  /* Custom animations */\n  --animate-fade-in: fadeIn 0.5s ease-in-out;\n\n  /* Custom breakpoints */\n  --breakpoint-3xl: 1920px;\n}\n\n/* Define custom animations */\n@keyframes fadeIn {\n  from { opacity: 0; }\n  to { opacity: 1; }\n}\n\n/* Custom utilities */\n@utility content-auto {\n  content-visibility: auto;\n}\n```\n\n### JavaScript Configuration (Legacy)\n\n```javascript\n/** @type {import(''tailwindcss'').Config} */\nexport default {\n  content: [\n    \"./index.html\",\n    \"./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx,vue,svelte}\",\n  ],\n  theme: {\n    extend: {\n      colors: {\n        primary: {\n          50: ''#f0f9ff'',\n          500: ''#3b82f6'',\n          900: ''#1e3a8a'',\n        },\n      },\n      fontFamily: {\n        sans: [''Inter'', ''system-ui'', ''sans-serif''],\n      },\n      spacing: {\n        ''128'': ''32rem'',\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  plugins: [],\n}\n```\n\n### Vite Integration (v4.1+)\n\n```javascript\n// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from ''vite''\nimport tailwindcss from ''@tailwindcss/vite''\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tailwindcss(),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n## Advanced v4.1 Features\n\n### Native CSS Custom Properties\n\n```html\n<div class=\"bg-[var(--color-brand-500)] text-[var(--color-white)]\">\n  Using CSS custom properties directly\n</div>\n```\n\n### Enhanced Arbitrary Values\n\n```html\n<!-- Complex grid with custom tracks -->\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr))] gap-4\">\n  Responsive grid without custom CSS\n</div>\n\n<!-- Custom animation timing -->\n<div class=\"animate-bounce ease-[cubic-bezier(0.68,-0.55,0.265,1.55)]\">\n  Bounce with custom easing\n</div>\n```\n\n### Container Queries\n\n```html\n<!-- Component that responds to its container size -->\n<div class=\"@container\">\n  <div class=\"@lg:text-xl @2xl:text-2xl\">\n    Text size based on container, not viewport\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Common Patterns with React/JSX\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from ''react'';\n\nfunction Button({ \n  variant = ''primary'', \n  size = ''md'', \n  children \n}: {\n  variant?: ''primary'' | ''secondary'';\n  size?: ''sm'' | ''md'' | ''lg'';\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}) {\n  const baseClasses = ''font-semibold rounded transition'';\n  \n  const variantClasses = {\n    primary: ''bg-blue-600 text-white hover:bg-blue-700'',\n    secondary: ''bg-gray-200 text-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-300'',\n  };\n  \n  const sizeClasses = {\n    sm: ''px-3 py-1 text-sm'',\n    md: ''px-4 py-2 text-base'',\n    lg: ''px-6 py-3 text-lg'',\n  };\n  \n  return (\n    <button \n      className={`${baseClasses} ${variantClasses[variant]} ${sizeClasses[size]}`}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## References\n\n- Tailwind CSS Docs: https://tailwindcss.com/docs\n- Tailwind UI: https://tailwindui.com\n- Tailwind Play: https://play.tailwindcss.com\n- Headless UI: https://headlessui.com\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:01:28.038Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing responsive and customizable user interface styling with Tailwind CSS utility-first framework.","zh":"非常适合需要响应式和可定制的用户界面样式的前端代理，使用 Tailwind CSS 实用优先框架。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントがレスポンシブでカスタマイズ可能なユーザーインターフェイスのスタイリングを必要とする場合に最適です。Tailwind CSS ユーティリティファーストフレームワークを使用しています。","ko":"반응형 및 사용자 지정 가능한 사용자 인터페이스 스타일이 필요한 프런트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다. Tailwind CSS 유틸리티 우선 프레임워크를 사용합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan un estilo de interfaz de usuario receptivo y personalizable con el marco de utilidad primero de Tailwind CSS.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin d''un style d''interface utilisateur réactif et personnalisable avec le framework utility-first de Tailwind CSS.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die ein responsives und anpassbares Benutzeroberflächen-Styling mit dem Utility-First-Framework von Tailwind CSS benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de estilização de interface do usuário responsiva e personalizável com o framework utility-first do Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым необходима отзывчивая и настраиваемая стилизация пользовательского интерфейса с помощью фреймворка Tailwind CSS utility-first.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية التي تحتاج إلى تنسيق واجهة المستخدم المستجيبة والقابلة للتعديل مع إطار العمل Tailwind CSS utility-first."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build modern, responsive user interfaces with utility classes, leveraging CSS-first configuration, custom utilities, and enhanced developer experience, including features like breakpoints, flexbox, and grid layouts.","zh":"赋予代理构建现代化、响应式用户界面的能力，利用实用类、CSS优先配置、自定义实用工具和增强的开发体验，包括断点、弹性盒和网格布局等功能。","ja":"エージェントがユーティリティクラス、CSS優先の構成、カスタムユーティリティ、開発者のエクスペリエンスの向上など、ブレークポイント、フレックスボックス、グリッドレイアウトなどの機能を利用して、モダンでレスポンシブなユーザーインターフェイスを構築できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 유틸리티 클래스, CSS 우선 구성, 사용자 지정 유틸리티 및 개발자 경험 향상 등과 같은 기능을 사용하여 현대적인 반응형 사용자 인터페이스를 구축할 수 있도록 합니다. 여기에는 브레이크 포인트, 플렉스 박스 및 그리드 레이아웃과 같은 기능이 포함됩니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear interfaces de usuario modernas y receptivas con clases de utilidad, aprovechando la configuración CSS-first, utilidades personalizadas y una experiencia de desarrollador mejorada, incluyendo características como puntos de interrupción, flexbox y diseños de cuadrícula.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces utilisateur modernes et réactives avec des classes d''utilité, en exploitant la configuration CSS-first, les utilités personnalisées et une expérience de développeur améliorée, notamment des fonctionnalités telles que les points d''arrêt, flexbox et les dispositions de grille.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, moderne, responsive Benutzeroberflächen mit Utility-Klassen zu erstellen, indem es die CSS-first-Konfiguration, benutzerdefinierte Utilities und eine verbesserte Entwicklererfahrung nutzt, einschließlich Funktionen wie Breakpoints, Flexbox und Rasterlayouts.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir interfaces do usuário modernas e responsivas com classes de utilidade, aproveitando a configuração CSS-first, utilidades personalizadas e experiência de desenvolvedor melhorada, incluindo recursos como pontos de quebra, flexbox e layouts de grade.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать современные и отзывчивые пользовательские интерфейсы с помощью утилитных классов, используя конфигурацию CSS-first, настраиваемые утилиты и улучшенный опыт разработчика, включая функции, такие как точки разрыва, flexbox и сеточные макеты.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية بناء واجهات مستخدم حديثة ومتجاوبة مع فئات المنفعة، واستغلال تكوين CSS-first والمنافع المخصصة وتجربة مطور محسنة، بما في ذلك الميزات مثل نقاط الكسر وflexbox وتصميمات الشبكة."},"useCases":{"en":["Styling React and HTML components with utility classes","Building responsive layouts with breakpoints and grid systems","Implementing custom design systems with tailored typography and color schemes"],"zh":["使用实用类样式化 React 和 HTML 组件","使用断点和网格系统构建响应式布局","实现自定义设计系统，具有定制的排版和颜色方案"],"ja":["ユーティリティクラスを使用して React と HTML コンポーネントをスタイリングする","ブレークポイントとグリッドシステムを使用してレスポンシブレイアウトを構築する","カスタムデザインシステムを実装し、カスタマイズされたタイポグラフィと色のスキームを使用する"],"ko":["유틸리티 클래스를 사용하여 React 및 HTML 컴포넌트를 스타일링합니다","브레이크 포인트 및 그리드 시스템을 사용하여 반응형 레이아웃을 구축합니다","사용자 지정 디자인 시스템을 구현하고 맞춤형 타이포그래피 및 색상 체계를 사용합니다"],"es":["Estilizar componentes React y HTML con clases de utilidad","Crear diseños receptivos con puntos de interrupción y sistemas de cuadrícula","Implementar sistemas de diseño personalizados con tipografía y esquemas de color personalizados"],"fr":["Styliser les composants React et HTML avec des classes d''utilité","Créer des dispositions réactives avec des points d''arrêt et des systèmes de grille","Mettre en œuvre des systèmes de conception personnalisés avec une typographie et des schémas de couleur personnalisés"],"de":["Stilisieren von React- und HTML-Komponenten mit Utility-Klassen","Erstellen von responsiven Layouts mit Breakpoints und Rastersystemen","Implementieren von benutzerdefinierten Designsystemen mit maßgeschneiderter Typografie und Farbschemata"],"pt":["Estilização de componentes React e HTML com classes de utilidade","Criação de layouts responsivos com pontos de quebra e sistemas de grade","Implementação de sistemas de design personalizados com tipografia e esquemas de cores personalizados"],"ru":["Стилизация компонентов React и HTML с помощью утилитных классов","Создание отзывчивых макетов с точками разрыва и сеточными системами","Реализация настраиваемых систем дизайна с индивидуальной типографией и цветовыми схемами"],"ar":["تنسيق مكونات React وHTML مع فئات المنفعة","إنشاء تخطيطات متجاوبة مع نقاط الكسر وأنظمة الشبكة","تنفيذ أنظمة تصميم مخصصة مع طباعة وخطوط وألوان مخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Tailwind CSS v4.1+","Limited to CSS-based styling and layout management"],"zh":["需要 Tailwind CSS v4.1+","仅限于基于 CSS 的样式和布局管理"],"ja":["Tailwind CSS v4.1+ が必要","CSSベースのスタイリングとレイアウト管理に限定される"],"ko":["Tailwind CSS v4.1+ 필요","CSS 기반 스타일링 및 레이아웃 관리에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere Tailwind CSS v4.1+","Limitado a la administración de estilo y diseño basada en CSS"],"fr":["Nécessite Tailwind CSS v4.1+","Limité à la gestion de style et de disposition basée sur CSS"],"de":["Erfordert Tailwind CSS v4.1+","Begrenzt auf CSS-basiertes Styling und Layout-Management"],"pt":["Exige Tailwind CSS v4.1+","Limitado à estilização e gestão de layout baseada em CSS"],"ru":["Требует Tailwind CSS v4.1+","Ограничен стилизацией и управлением макетом на основе CSS"],"ar":["يتطلب Tailwind CSS v4.1+","محدود بالتنسيق والإدارة القائمة على CSS"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/security-requirement-extraction', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'security-requirement-extraction', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z', '2026-02-18T14:02:21.692Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/security-requirement-extraction","name":"security-requirement-extraction","description":{"zh":"安全要求提取技能可以将威胁分析转换为可行的安全要求，用于开发安全软件和系统","ja":"セキュリティ要件抽出スキルは、脅威分析を実行可能なセキュリティ要件に変換し、セキュアなソフトウェアとシステムの開発に使用できます","ko":"보안 요구사항 추출 스킬은 위협 분석을 실행 가능한 보안 요구사항으로 변환하여 보안 소프트웨어와 시스템 개발에 사용할 수 있습니다","pt":"Extração de requisitos de segurança transforma análises de ameaças em requisitos de segurança açãoaveis.","ru":"Извлечение требований безопасности преобразует анализ угроз в действенные требования безопасности.","ar":"استخراج متطلبات الأمان يتحول تحليل التهديدات إلى متطلبات أمان قابلة للتنفيذ.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"安全要求提取 - 转换威胁分析为可行的安全要求","ja":"セキュリティ要件抽出 - 脅威分析を実行可能なセキュリティ要件に変換","ko":"보안 요구사항 추출 - 위협 분석을 실행 가능한 보안 요구사항으로 변환","pt":"Extração de Requisitos de Segurança","ru":"Извлечение Требований Безопасности","ar":"استخراج متطلبات الأمان","en":"security-requirement-extraction"},"description":{"zh":"安全要求提取技能可以将威胁分析转换为可行的安全要求，用于开发安全软件和系统","ja":"セキュリティ要件抽出スキルは、脅威分析を実行可能なセキュリティ要件に変換し、セキュアなソフトウェアとシステムの開発に使用できます","ko":"보안 요구사항 추출 스킬은 위협 분석을 실행 가능한 보안 요구사항으로 변환하여 보안 소프트웨어와 시스템 개발에 사용할 수 있습니다","pt":"Extração de requisitos de segurança transforma análises de ameaças em requisitos de segurança açãoaveis.","ru":"Извлечение требований безопасности преобразует анализ угроз в действенные требования безопасности.","ar":"استخراج متطلبات الأمان يتحول تحليل التهديدات إلى متطلبات أمان قابلة للتنفيذ.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["威胁模型转换为安全要求","安全用户故事编写","安全测试用例创建","安全验收标准建立","合规性要求映射","安全架构文档创建"],"ja":["脅威モデルをセキュリティ要件に変換","セキュリティユーザー ストーリーの作成","セキュリティテスト ケースの作成","セキュリティ受け入れ基準の確立","コンプライアンス要件のマッピング","セキュリティアーキテクチャ ドキュメントの作成"],"ko":["위협 모델을 보안 요구사항으로 변환","보안 사용자 스토리 작성","보안 테스트 케이스 생성","보안 승인 기준 설정","규정 준수 요구사항 매핑","보안 아키텍처 문서 생성"],"pt":["Conversão de modelos de ameaças em requisitos","Criação de histórias de usuário de segurança","Desenvolvimento de casos de teste de segurança","Criação de critérios de aceitação de segurança","Mapeamento de requisitos de conformidade","Documentação de arquitetura de segurança"],"ru":["Преобразование моделей угроз в требования","Создание историй пользователя безопасности","Разработка случаев тестирования безопасности","Создание критериев приемки безопасности","Сопоставление требований соответствия","Документация архитектуры безопасности"],"ar":["تحويل نماذج التهديدات إلى متطلبات","إنشاء قصص المستخدمين للأمان","تحويل حالات اختبار الأمان","إنشاء معايير قبول الأمان","تحويل متطلبات المطابقة","توثيق هندسة الأمان"]},"keywords":{"zh":["安全要求提取","威胁分析","安全软件开发","安全系统开发","合规性要求","安全架构","安全测试","安全验收"],"ja":["セキュリティ要件抽出","脅威分析","セキュアなソフトウェア開発","セキュアなシステム開発","コンプライアンス要件","セキュリティアーキテクチャ","セキュリティテスト","セキュリティ受け入れ"],"ko":["보안 요구사항 추출","위협 분석","보안 소프트웨어 개발","보안 시스템 개발","규정 준수 요구사항","보안 아키텍처","보안 테스트","보안 승인"],"pt":["segurança cibernética","análise de ameaças","requisitos de segurança","testes de segurança","conformidade","arquitetura de segurança","desenvolvimento de software seguro"],"ru":["кибербезопасность","анализ угроз","требования безопасности","тестирование безопасности","соответствие","архитектура безопасности","разработка безопасного программного обеспечения"],"ar":["أمن المعلومات","تحليل التهديدات","متطلبات الأمان","اختبارات الأمان","المطابقة","هندسة الأمان","تطوير برمجيات آمنة"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"security-requirement-extraction","description":"Derive security requirements from threat models and business context. Use when translating threats into actionable requirements, creating security user stories, or building security test cases.","bodyPreview":"# Security Requirement Extraction\n\nTransform threat analysis into actionable security requirements.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Converting threat models to requirements\n- Writing security user stories\n- Creating security test cases\n- Building security acceptance criteria\n- Compliance requirement mapping\n- Security architecture documentation\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Requirement Categories\n\n```\nBusiness Requirements → Security Requirements → Technical Controls\n         ↓                       ↓","body":"# Security Requirement Extraction\n\nTransform threat analysis into actionable security requirements.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Converting threat models to requirements\n- Writing security user stories\n- Creating security test cases\n- Building security acceptance criteria\n- Compliance requirement mapping\n- Security architecture documentation\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Requirement Categories\n\n```\nBusiness Requirements → Security Requirements → Technical Controls\n         ↓                       ↓                      ↓\n  \"Protect customer    \"Encrypt PII at rest\"   \"AES-256 encryption\n   data\"                                        with KMS key rotation\"\n```\n\n### 2. Security Requirement Types\n\n| Type               | Focus                   | Example                               |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| **Functional**     | What system must do     | \"System must authenticate users\"      |\n| **Non-functional** | How system must perform | \"Authentication must complete in <2s\" |\n| **Constraint**     | Limitations imposed     | \"Must use approved crypto libraries\"  |\n\n### 3. Requirement Attributes\n\n| Attribute        | Description                 |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------- |\n| **Traceability** | Links to threats/compliance |\n| **Testability**  | Can be verified             |\n| **Priority**     | Business importance         |\n| **Risk Level**   | Impact if not met           |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Security Requirement Model\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional, Set\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nclass RequirementType(Enum):\n    FUNCTIONAL = \"functional\"\n    NON_FUNCTIONAL = \"non_functional\"\n    CONSTRAINT = \"constraint\"\n\n\nclass Priority(Enum):\n    CRITICAL = 1\n    HIGH = 2\n    MEDIUM = 3\n    LOW = 4\n\n\nclass SecurityDomain(Enum):\n    AUTHENTICATION = \"authentication\"\n    AUTHORIZATION = \"authorization\"\n    DATA_PROTECTION = \"data_protection\"\n    AUDIT_LOGGING = \"audit_logging\"\n    INPUT_VALIDATION = \"input_validation\"\n    ERROR_HANDLING = \"error_handling\"\n    SESSION_MANAGEMENT = \"session_management\"\n    CRYPTOGRAPHY = \"cryptography\"\n    NETWORK_SECURITY = \"network_security\"\n    AVAILABILITY = \"availability\"\n\n\nclass ComplianceFramework(Enum):\n    PCI_DSS = \"pci_dss\"\n    HIPAA = \"hipaa\"\n    GDPR = \"gdpr\"\n    SOC2 = \"soc2\"\n    NIST_CSF = \"nist_csf\"\n    ISO_27001 = \"iso_27001\"\n    OWASP = \"owasp\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass SecurityRequirement:\n    id: str\n    title: str\n    description: str\n    req_type: RequirementType\n    domain: SecurityDomain\n    priority: Priority\n    rationale: str = \"\"\n    acceptance_criteria: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    test_cases: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    threat_refs: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    compliance_refs: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    dependencies: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    status: str = \"draft\"\n    owner: str = \"\"\n    created_date: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.now)\n\n    def to_user_story(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Convert to user story format.\"\"\"\n        return f\"\"\"\n**{self.id}: {self.title}**\n\nAs a security-conscious system,\nI need to {self.description.lower()},\nSo that {self.rationale.lower()}.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n{chr(10).join(f''- [ ] {ac}'' for ac in self.acceptance_criteria)}\n\n**Priority:** {self.priority.name}\n**Domain:** {self.domain.value}\n**Threat References:** {'', ''.join(self.threat_refs)}\n\"\"\"\n\n    def to_test_spec(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Convert to test specification.\"\"\"\n        return f\"\"\"\n## Test Specification: {self.id}\n\n### Requirement\n{self.description}\n\n### Test Cases\n{chr(10).join(f''{i+1}. {tc}'' for i, tc in enumerate(self.test_cases))}\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Verification\n{chr(10).join(f''- {ac}'' for ac in self.acceptance_criteria)}\n\"\"\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass RequirementSet:\n    name: str\n    version: str\n    requirements: List[SecurityRequirement] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n    def add(self, req: SecurityRequirement) -> None:\n        self.requirements.append(req)\n\n    def get_by_domain(self, domain: SecurityDomain) -> List[SecurityRequirement]:\n        return [r for r in self.requirements if r.domain == domain]\n\n    def get_by_priority(self, priority: Priority) -> List[SecurityRequirement]:\n        return [r for r in self.requirements if r.priority == priority]\n\n    def get_by_threat(self, threat_id: str) -> List[SecurityRequirement]:\n        return [r for r in self.requirements if threat_id in r.threat_refs]\n\n    def get_critical_requirements(self) -> List[SecurityRequirement]:\n        return [r for r in self.requirements if r.priority == Priority.CRITICAL]\n\n    def export_markdown(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Export all requirements as markdown.\"\"\"\n        lines = [f\"# Security Requirements: {self.name}\\n\"]\n        lines.append(f\"Version: {self.version}\\n\")\n\n        for domain in SecurityDomain:\n            domain_reqs = self.get_by_domain(domain)\n            if domain_reqs:\n                lines.append(f\"\\n## {domain.value.replace(''_'', '' '').title()}\\n\")\n                for req in domain_reqs:\n                    lines.append(req.to_user_story())\n\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n    def traceability_matrix(self) -> Dict[str, List[str]]:\n        \"\"\"Generate threat-to-requirement traceability.\"\"\"\n        matrix = {}\n        for req in self.requirements:\n            for threat_id in req.threat_refs:\n                if threat_id not in matrix:\n                    matrix[threat_id] = []\n                matrix[threat_id].append(req.id)\n        return matrix\n```\n\n### Template 2: Threat-to-Requirement Extractor\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Tuple\n\n@dataclass\nclass ThreatInput:\n    id: str\n    category: str  # STRIDE category\n    title: str\n    description: str\n    target: str\n    impact: str\n    likelihood: str\n\n\nclass RequirementExtractor:\n    \"\"\"Extract security requirements from threats.\"\"\"\n\n    # Mapping of STRIDE categories to security domains and requirement patterns\n    STRIDE_MAPPINGS = {\n        \"SPOOFING\": {\n            \"domains\": [SecurityDomain.AUTHENTICATION, SecurityDomain.SESSION_MANAGEMENT],\n            \"patterns\": [\n                (\"Implement strong authentication for {target}\",\n                 \"Ensure {target} authenticates all users before granting access\"),\n                (\"Validate identity tokens for {target}\",\n                 \"All authentication tokens must be cryptographically verified\"),\n                (\"Implement session management for {target}\",\n                 \"Sessions must be securely managed with proper expiration\"),\n            ]\n        },\n        \"TAMPERING\": {\n            \"domains\": [SecurityDomain.INPUT_VALIDATION, SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION],\n            \"patterns\": [\n                (\"Validate all input to {target}\",\n                 \"All input must be validated against expected formats\"),\n                (\"Implement integrity checks for {target}\",\n                 \"Data integrity must be verified using cryptographic signatures\"),\n                (\"Protect {target} from modification\",\n                 \"Implement controls to prevent unauthorized data modification\"),\n            ]\n        },\n        \"REPUDIATION\": {\n            \"domains\": [SecurityDomain.AUDIT_LOGGING],\n            \"patterns\": [\n                (\"Log all security events for {target}\",\n                 \"Security-relevant events must be logged for audit purposes\"),\n                (\"Implement non-repudiation for {target}\",\n                 \"Critical actions must have cryptographic proof of origin\"),\n                (\"Protect audit logs for {target}\",\n                 \"Audit logs must be tamper-evident and protected\"),\n            ]\n        },\n        \"INFORMATION_DISCLOSURE\": {\n            \"domains\": [SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION, SecurityDomain.CRYPTOGRAPHY],\n            \"patterns\": [\n                (\"Encrypt sensitive data in {target}\",\n                 \"Sensitive data must be encrypted at rest and in transit\"),\n                (\"Implement access controls for {target}\",\n                 \"Data access must be restricted based on need-to-know\"),\n                (\"Prevent information leakage from {target}\",\n                 \"Error messages and logs must not expose sensitive information\"),\n            ]\n        },\n        \"DENIAL_OF_SERVICE\": {\n            \"domains\": [SecurityDomain.AVAILABILITY, SecurityDomain.INPUT_VALIDATION],\n            \"patterns\": [\n                (\"Implement rate limiting for {target}\",\n                 \"Requests must be rate-limited to prevent resource exhaustion\"),\n                (\"Ensure availability of {target}\",\n                 \"System must remain available under high load conditions\"),\n                (\"Implement resource quotas for {target}\",\n                 \"Resource consumption must be bounded and monitored\"),\n            ]\n        },\n        \"ELEVATION_OF_PRIVILEGE\": {\n            \"domains\": [SecurityDomain.AUTHORIZATION],\n            \"patterns\": [\n                (\"Enforce authorization for {target}\",\n                 \"All actions must be authorized based on user permissions\"),\n                (\"Implement least privilege for {target}\",\n                 \"Users must only have minimum necessary permissions\"),\n                (\"Validate permissions for {target}\",\n                 \"Permission checks must be performed server-side\"),\n            ]\n        },\n    }\n\n    def extract_requirements(\n        self,\n        threats: List[ThreatInput],\n        project_name: str\n    ) -> RequirementSet:\n        \"\"\"Extract security requirements from threats.\"\"\"\n        req_set = RequirementSet(\n            name=f\"{project_name} Security Requirements\",\n            version=\"1.0\"\n        )\n\n        req_counter = 1\n        for threat in threats:\n            reqs = self._threat_to_requirements(threat, req_counter)\n            for req in reqs:\n                req_set.add(req)\n            req_counter += len(reqs)\n\n        return req_set\n\n    def _threat_to_requirements(\n        self,\n        threat: ThreatInput,\n        start_id: int\n    ) -> List[SecurityRequirement]:\n        \"\"\"Convert a single threat to requirements.\"\"\"\n        requirements = []\n        mapping = self.STRIDE_MAPPINGS.get(threat.category, {})\n        domains = mapping.get(\"domains\", [])\n        patterns = mapping.get(\"patterns\", [])\n\n        priority = self._calculate_priority(threat.impact, threat.likelihood)\n\n        for i, (title_pattern, desc_pattern) in enumerate(patterns):\n            req = SecurityRequirement(\n                id=f\"SR-{start_id + i:03d}\",\n                title=title_pattern.format(target=threat.target),\n                description=desc_pattern.format(target=threat.target),\n                req_type=RequirementType.FUNCTIONAL,\n                domain=domains[i % len(domains)] if domains else SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION,\n                priority=priority,\n                rationale=f\"Mitigates threat: {threat.title}\",\n                threat_refs=[threat.id],\n                acceptance_criteria=self._generate_acceptance_criteria(\n                    threat.category, threat.target\n                ),\n                test_cases=self._generate_test_cases(\n                    threat.category, threat.target\n                )\n            )\n            requirements.append(req)\n\n        return requirements\n\n    def _calculate_priority(self, impact: str, likelihood: str) -> Priority:\n        \"\"\"Calculate requirement priority from threat attributes.\"\"\"\n        score_map = {\"LOW\": 1, \"MEDIUM\": 2, \"HIGH\": 3, \"CRITICAL\": 4}\n        impact_score = score_map.get(impact.upper(), 2)\n        likelihood_score = score_map.get(likelihood.upper(), 2)\n\n        combined = impact_score * likelihood_score\n\n        if combined >= 12:\n            return Priority.CRITICAL\n        elif combined >= 6:\n            return Priority.HIGH\n        elif combined >= 3:\n            return Priority.MEDIUM\n        return Priority.LOW\n\n    def _generate_acceptance_criteria(\n        self,\n        category: str,\n        target: str\n    ) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Generate acceptance criteria for requirement.\"\"\"\n        criteria_templates = {\n            \"SPOOFING\": [\n                f\"Users must authenticate before accessing {target}\",\n                \"Authentication failures are logged and monitored\",\n                \"Multi-factor authentication is available for sensitive operations\",\n            ],\n            \"TAMPERING\": [\n                f\"All input to {target} is validated\",\n                \"Data integrity is verified before processing\",\n                \"Modification attempts trigger alerts\",\n            ],\n            \"REPUDIATION\": [\n                f\"All actions on {target} are logged with user identity\",\n                \"Logs cannot be modified by regular users\",\n                \"Log retention meets compliance requirements\",\n            ],\n            \"INFORMATION_DISCLOSURE\": [\n                f\"Sensitive data in {target} is encrypted\",\n                \"Access to sensitive data is logged\",\n                \"Error messages do not reveal sensitive information\",\n            ],\n            \"DENIAL_OF_SERVICE\": [\n                f\"Rate limiting is enforced on {target}\",\n                \"System degrades gracefully under load\",\n                \"Resource exhaustion triggers alerts\",\n            ],\n            \"ELEVATION_OF_PRIVILEGE\": [\n                f\"Authorization is checked for all {target} operations\",\n                \"Users cannot access resources beyond their permissions\",\n                \"Privilege changes are logged and monitored\",\n            ],\n        }\n        return criteria_templates.get(category, [])\n\n    def _generate_test_cases(\n        self,\n        category: str,\n        target: str\n    ) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Generate test cases for requirement.\"\"\"\n        test_templates = {\n            \"SPOOFING\": [\n                f\"Test: Unauthenticated access to {target} is denied\",\n                \"Test: Invalid credentials are rejected\",\n                \"Test: Session tokens cannot be forged\",\n            ],\n            \"TAMPERING\": [\n                f\"Test: Invalid input to {target} is rejected\",\n                \"Test: Tampered data is detected and rejected\",\n                \"Test: SQL injection attempts are blocked\",\n            ],\n            \"REPUDIATION\": [\n                \"Test: Security events are logged\",\n                \"Test: Logs include sufficient detail for forensics\",\n                \"Test: Log integrity is protected\",\n            ],\n            \"INFORMATION_DISCLOSURE\": [\n                f\"Test: {target} data is encrypted in transit\",\n                f\"Test: {target} data is encrypted at rest\",\n                \"Test: Error messages are sanitized\",\n            ],\n            \"DENIAL_OF_SERVICE\": [\n                f\"Test: Rate limiting on {target} works correctly\",\n                \"Test: System handles burst traffic gracefully\",\n                \"Test: Resource limits are enforced\",\n            ],\n            \"ELEVATION_OF_PRIVILEGE\": [\n                f\"Test: Unauthorized access to {target} is denied\",\n                \"Test: Privilege escalation attempts are blocked\",\n                \"Test: IDOR vulnerabilities are not present\",\n            ],\n        }\n        return test_templates.get(category, [])\n```\n\n### Template 3: Compliance Mapping\n\n```python\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Set\n\nclass ComplianceMapper:\n    \"\"\"Map security requirements to compliance frameworks.\"\"\"\n\n    FRAMEWORK_CONTROLS = {\n        ComplianceFramework.PCI_DSS: {\n            SecurityDomain.AUTHENTICATION: [\"8.1\", \"8.2\", \"8.3\"],\n            SecurityDomain.AUTHORIZATION: [\"7.1\", \"7.2\"],\n            SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION: [\"3.4\", \"3.5\", \"4.1\"],\n            SecurityDomain.AUDIT_LOGGING: [\"10.1\", \"10.2\", \"10.3\"],\n            SecurityDomain.NETWORK_SECURITY: [\"1.1\", \"1.2\", \"1.3\"],\n            SecurityDomain.CRYPTOGRAPHY: [\"3.5\", \"3.6\", \"4.1\"],\n        },\n        ComplianceFramework.HIPAA: {\n            SecurityDomain.AUTHENTICATION: [\"164.312(d)\"],\n            SecurityDomain.AUTHORIZATION: [\"164.312(a)(1)\"],\n            SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION: [\"164.312(a)(2)(iv)\", \"164.312(e)(2)(ii)\"],\n            SecurityDomain.AUDIT_LOGGING: [\"164.312(b)\"],\n        },\n        ComplianceFramework.GDPR: {\n            SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION: [\"Art. 32\", \"Art. 25\"],\n            SecurityDomain.AUDIT_LOGGING: [\"Art. 30\"],\n            SecurityDomain.AUTHORIZATION: [\"Art. 25\"],\n        },\n        ComplianceFramework.OWASP: {\n            SecurityDomain.AUTHENTICATION: [\"V2.1\", \"V2.2\", \"V2.3\"],\n            SecurityDomain.SESSION_MANAGEMENT: [\"V3.1\", \"V3.2\", \"V3.3\"],\n            SecurityDomain.INPUT_VALIDATION: [\"V5.1\", \"V5.2\", \"V5.3\"],\n            SecurityDomain.CRYPTOGRAPHY: [\"V6.1\", \"V6.2\"],\n            SecurityDomain.ERROR_HANDLING: [\"V7.1\", \"V7.2\"],\n            SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION: [\"V8.1\", \"V8.2\", \"V8.3\"],\n            SecurityDomain.AUDIT_LOGGING: [\"V7.1\", \"V7.2\"],\n        },\n    }\n\n    def map_requirement_to_compliance(\n        self,\n        requirement: SecurityRequirement,\n        frameworks: List[ComplianceFramework]\n    ) -> Dict[str, List[str]]:\n        \"\"\"Map a requirement to compliance controls.\"\"\"\n        mapping = {}\n        for framework in frameworks:\n            controls = self.FRAMEWORK_CONTROLS.get(framework, {})\n            domain_controls = controls.get(requirement.domain, [])\n            if domain_controls:\n                mapping[framework.value] = domain_controls\n        return mapping\n\n    def get_requirements_for_control(\n        self,\n        requirement_set: RequirementSet,\n        framework: ComplianceFramework,\n        control_id: str\n    ) -> List[SecurityRequirement]:\n        \"\"\"Find requirements that satisfy a compliance control.\"\"\"\n        matching = []\n        framework_controls = self.FRAMEWORK_CONTROLS.get(framework, {})\n\n        for domain, controls in framework_controls.items():\n            if control_id in controls:\n                matching.extend(requirement_set.get_by_domain(domain))\n\n        return matching\n\n    def generate_compliance_matrix(\n        self,\n        requirement_set: RequirementSet,\n        frameworks: List[ComplianceFramework]\n    ) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, List[str]]]:\n        \"\"\"Generate compliance traceability matrix.\"\"\"\n        matrix = {}\n\n        for framework in frameworks:\n            matrix[framework.value] = {}\n            framework_controls = self.FRAMEWORK_CONTROLS.get(framework, {})\n\n            for domain, controls in framework_controls.items():\n                for control in controls:\n                    reqs = self.get_requirements_for_control(\n                        requirement_set, framework, control\n                    )\n                    if reqs:\n                        matrix[framework.value][control] = [r.id for r in reqs]\n\n        return matrix\n\n    def gap_analysis(\n        self,\n        requirement_set: RequirementSet,\n        framework: ComplianceFramework\n    ) -> Dict[str, List[str]]:\n        \"\"\"Identify compliance gaps.\"\"\"\n        gaps = {\"missing_controls\": [], \"weak_coverage\": []}\n        framework_controls = self.FRAMEWORK_CONTROLS.get(framework, {})\n\n        for domain, controls in framework_controls.items():\n            domain_reqs = requirement_set.get_by_domain(domain)\n            for control in controls:\n                matching = self.get_requirements_for_control(\n                    requirement_set, framework, control\n                )\n                if not matching:\n                    gaps[\"missing_controls\"].append(f\"{framework.value}:{control}\")\n                elif len(matching) < 2:\n                    gaps[\"weak_coverage\"].append(f\"{framework.value}:{control}\")\n\n        return gaps\n```\n\n### Template 4: Security User Story Generator\n\n```python\nclass SecurityUserStoryGenerator:\n    \"\"\"Generate security-focused user stories.\"\"\"\n\n    STORY_TEMPLATES = {\n        SecurityDomain.AUTHENTICATION: {\n            \"as_a\": \"security-conscious user\",\n            \"so_that\": \"my identity is protected from impersonation\",\n        },\n        SecurityDomain.AUTHORIZATION: {\n            \"as_a\": \"system administrator\",\n            \"so_that\": \"users can only access resources appropriate to their role\",\n        },\n        SecurityDomain.DATA_PROTECTION: {\n            \"as_a\": \"data owner\",\n            \"so_that\": \"my sensitive information remains confidential\",\n        },\n        SecurityDomain.AUDIT_LOGGING: {\n            \"as_a\": \"security analyst\",\n            \"so_that\": \"I can investigate security incidents\",\n        },\n        SecurityDomain.INPUT_VALIDATION: {\n            \"as_a\": \"application developer\",\n            \"so_that\": \"the system is protected from malicious input\",\n        },\n    }\n\n    def generate_story(self, requirement: SecurityRequirement) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Generate a user story from requirement.\"\"\"\n        template = self.STORY_TEMPLATES.get(\n            requirement.domain,\n            {\"as_a\": \"user\", \"so_that\": \"the system is secure\"}\n        )\n\n        story = f\"\"\"\n## {requirement.id}: {requirement.title}\n\n**User Story:**\nAs a {template[''as_a'']},\nI want the system to {requirement.description.lower()},\nSo that {template[''so_that'']}.\n\n**Priority:** {requirement.priority.name}\n**Type:** {requirement.req_type.value}\n**Domain:** {requirement.domain.value}\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n{self._format_acceptance_criteria(requirement.acceptance_criteria)}\n\n**Definition of Done:**\n- [ ] Implementation complete\n- [ ] Security tests pass\n- [ ] Code review complete\n- [ ] Security review approved\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n\n**Security Test Cases:**\n{self._format_test_cases(requirement.test_cases)}\n\n**Traceability:**\n- Threats: {'', ''.join(requirement.threat_refs) or ''N/A''}\n- Compliance: {'', ''.join(requirement.compliance_refs) or ''N/A''}\n\"\"\"\n        return story\n\n    def _format_acceptance_criteria(self, criteria: List[str]) -> str:\n        return \"\\n\".join(f\"- [ ] {c}\" for c in criteria) if criteria else \"- [ ] TBD\"\n\n    def _format_test_cases(self, tests: List[str]) -> str:\n        return \"\\n\".join(f\"- {t}\" for t in tests) if tests else \"- TBD\"\n\n    def generate_epic(\n        self,\n        requirement_set: RequirementSet,\n        domain: SecurityDomain\n    ) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Generate an epic for a security domain.\"\"\"\n        reqs = requirement_set.get_by_domain(domain)\n\n        epic = f\"\"\"\n# Security Epic: {domain.value.replace(''_'', '' '').title()}\n\n## Overview\nThis epic covers all security requirements related to {domain.value.replace(''_'', '' '')}.\n\n## Business Value\n- Protect against {domain.value.replace(''_'', '' '')} related threats\n- Meet compliance requirements\n- Reduce security risk\n\n## Stories in this Epic\n{chr(10).join(f''- [{r.id}] {r.title}'' for r in reqs)}\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- All stories complete\n- Security tests passing\n- Security review approved\n- Compliance requirements met\n\n## Risk if Not Implemented\n- Vulnerability to {domain.value.replace(''_'', '' '')} attacks\n- Compliance violations\n- Potential data breach\n\n## Dependencies\n{chr(10).join(f''- {d}'' for r in reqs for d in r.dependencies) or ''- None identified''}\n\"\"\"\n        return epic\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Trace to threats** - Every requirement should map to threats\n- **Be specific** - Vague requirements can''t be tested\n- **Include acceptance criteria** - Define \"done\"\n- **Consider compliance** - Map to frameworks early\n- **Review regularly** - Requirements evolve with threats\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t be generic** - \"Be secure\" is not a requirement\n- **Don''t skip rationale** - Explain why it matters\n- **Don''t ignore priorities** - Not all requirements are equal\n- **Don''t forget testability** - If you can''t test it, you can''t verify it\n- **Don''t work in isolation** - Involve stakeholders\n\n## Resources\n\n- [OWASP ASVS](https://owasp.org/www-project-application-security-verification-standard/)\n- [NIST SP 800-53](https://csrc.nist.gov/publications/detail/sp/800-53/rev-5/final)\n- [Security User Stories](https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/agile-application-security/9781491938836/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:02:21.692Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Compliance Agents needing to extract and transform threat analysis into actionable security requirements","zh":"非常适合需要提取威胁分析并将其转化为可操作安全要求的合规代理","ja":"脅威分析を抽出し、実践可能なセキュリティ要件に変換する必要があるコンプライアンスエージェントに最適です","ko":"위협 분석을 추출하여 실행 가능한 보안 요구사항으로 변환해야 하는 컴플라이언스 에이전트에 이상적입니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de cumplimiento que necesitan extraer y transformar el análisis de amenazas en requisitos de seguridad accionables","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de conformité ayant besoin d''extraire et de transformer l''analyse de menace en exigences de sécurité actionnables","de":"Ideal für Compliance-Agenten, die Bedrohungsanalysen in handhabbare Sicherheitsanforderungen umwandeln müssen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Conformidade que precisam extrair e transformar análise de ameaças em requisitos de segurança atuáveis","ru":"Идеально для агентов по соблюдению требований, которым необходимо извлекать и преобразовывать анализ угроз в действенные требования безопасности","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الامتثال التي تحتاج إلى استخراج وتحويل تحليل التهديدات إلى متطلبات أمنية قابلة للتنفيذ"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate security user stories, create security test cases, and map compliance requirements using threat models and security architecture documentation, leveraging technical controls and requirement categories","zh":"使代理能够利用技术控制和需求类别，生成安全用户故事、创建安全测试用例，并使用威胁模型和安全架构文档映射合规要求","ja":"技術的制御と要件カテゴリを活用し、脅威モデルとセキュリティアーキテクチャ文書を使用して、セキュリティユーザーストーリーの生成、セキュリティテストケースの作成、コンプライアンス要件のマッピングをエージェントに可能にします","ko":"기술적 통제와 요구사항 범주를 활용하여 위협 모델 및 보안 아키텍처 문서를 사용하여 보안 사용자 스토리 생성, 보안 테스트 케이스 작성, 컴플라이언스 요구사항 매핑을 통해 에이전트의 역량을 강화합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar historias de usuario de seguridad, crear casos de prueba de seguridad y asignar requisitos de cumplimiento utilizando modelos de amenazas y documentación de arquitectura de seguridad, aprovechando controles técnicos y categorías de requisitos","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des histoires d''utilisateur de sécurité, de créer des cas de test de sécurité et de mapper les exigences de conformité en utilisant des modèles de menace et une documentation d''architecture de sécurité, en exploitant les contrôles techniques et les catégories d''exigences","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Sicherheitsbenutzerstories zu generieren, Sicherheitstestfälle zu erstellen und Compliance-Anforderungen mithilfe von Bedrohungsmodellen und Sicherheitsarchitekturdokumentation zuzuordnen, indem technische Kontrollen und Anforderungskategorien genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar histórias de usuário de segurança, criar casos de teste de segurança e mapear requisitos de conformidade usando modelos de ameaças e documentação de arquitetura de segurança, aproveitando controles técnicos e categorias de requisitos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать истории пользователей безопасности, создавать тестовые случаи безопасности и сопоставлять требования соблюдения требований с использованием моделей угроз и документации по безопасности архитектуры, используя технические средства контроля и категории требований","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من generar histórias de usuário de segurança، إنشاء قضايا اختبار الأمن وتصوير متطلبات الامتثال باستخدام نماذج التهديدات وتوثيق هندسة الأمن، وذلك بالاستفادة من وسائل التحكم الفنية وفئات المتطلبات"},"useCases":{"en":["Converting threat models to security requirements","Building security acceptance criteria","Creating security architecture documentation"],"zh":["将威胁模型转换为安全要求","构建安全验收标准","创建安全架构文档"],"ja":["脅威モデルからセキュリティ要件への変換","セキュリティ受け入れ基準の構築","セキュリティアーキテクチャ文書の作成"],"ko":["위협 모델을 보안 요구사항으로 변환","보안 승인 기준 구축","보안 아키텍처 문서 작성"],"es":["Conversión de modelos de amenazas en requisitos de seguridad","Creación de criterios de aceptación de seguridad","Generación de documentación de arquitectura de seguridad"],"fr":["Conversion de modèles de menace en exigences de sécurité","Création de critères d''acceptation de sécurité","Génération de documentation d''architecture de sécurité"],"de":["Umwandlung von Bedrohungsmodellen in Sicherheitsanforderungen","Erstellung von Sicherheitsabnahmekriterien","Erzeugung von Sicherheitsarchitekturdokumentation"],"pt":["Converter modelos de ameaças em requisitos de segurança","Construir critérios de aceitação de segurança","Criar documentação de arquitetura de segurança"],"ru":["Преобразование моделей угроз в требования безопасности","Построение критериев приемки безопасности","Создание документации по безопасности архитектуры"],"ar":["تحويل نماذج التهديدات إلى متطلبات أمنية","بناء معايير قبول الأمن","إنشاء توثيق هندسة الأمن"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires threat analysis data","Limited to security requirement extraction and mapping"],"zh":["需要威胁分析数据","仅限于安全需求的提取和映射"],"ja":["脅威分析データが必要","セキュリティ要件の抽出とマッピングに限定される"],"ko":["위협 분석 데이터 필요","보안 요구사항 추출 및 매핑으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere datos de análisis de amenazas","Limitado a la extracción y asignación de requisitos de seguridad"],"fr":["Nécessite des données d''analyse de menace","Limité à l''extraction et au mappage des exigences de sécurité"],"de":["Benötigt Bedrohungsanalyse-Daten","Begrenzt auf die Extraktion und Zuordnung von Sicherheitsanforderungen"],"pt":["Exige dados de análise de ameaças","Limitado à extração e mapeamento de requisitos de segurança"],"ru":["Требует данных анализа угроз","Ограничен извлечением и сопоставлением требований безопасности"],"ar":["يتطلب بيانات تحليل التهديدات","محدود بالاستخراج وتصوير متطلبات الأمن"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
