teller mit React und TypeScript","pt":"Construtor de Artefatos Web - Crie Artefatos Poderosos","ru":"Создатель Веб-Артефактов - Создайте Мощные Артефакты","ar":"بناء قطع فنية ويب - قم بإنشاء قطع فنية قوية","en":"web-artifacts-builder"},"description":{"zh":"Web Artifacts Builder 是一个用于构建前端应用的工具，支持 React 18、TypeScript 和 Vite。使用此工具可以轻松构建强大的前端应用","ja":"Web アーティファクト ビルダーはフロントエンド アプリケーションを構築するためのツールです。React 18、TypeScript、Vite をサポートします","ko":"웹 아티팩트 빌더는 프런트엔드 애플리케이션을 구축하는 데 사용되는 도구입니다. React 18, TypeScript, Vite를 지원합니다","es":"El constructor de artefactos web es una herramienta para crear artefactos web con React, TypeScript y Vite. Sigue nuestros pasos para inicializar, desarrolla...","fr":"Le constructeur d''artefacts web est un outil pour créer des artefacts web avec React, TypeScript et Vite. Suivez nos étapes pour initialiser, développer et e...","de":"Der Web-Artifact-Ersteller ist ein Werkzeug zum Erstellen von Web-Artifacts mit React, TypeScript und Vite. Befolgen Sie unsere Schritte, um Ihr Artifact zu ...","pt":"O construtor de artefatos web é uma ferramenta para criar artefatos web poderosos. Ele utiliza React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Parcel e Tailwind CSS","ru":"Создатель веб-артефактов - это инструмент для создания мощных веб-артефактов. Он использует React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Parcel и Tailwind CSS","ar":"بناء قطع الفنية هي أداة لإنشاء قطع فنية ويب قوية. تستخدم React 18 و TypeScript و Vite و Parcel و Tailwind CSS","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持 React 18","支持 TypeScript","支持 Vite","支持 Parcel 打包","支持 Tailwind CSS","支持 shadcn/ui"],"ja":["React 18 をサポート","TypeScript をサポート","Vite をサポート","Parcel でバンドル","Tailwind CSS をサポート","shadcn/ui をサポート"],"ko":["React 18 지원","TypeScript 지원","Vite 지원","Parcel로 번들링","Tailwind CSS 지원","shadcn/ui 지원"],"es":["Inicialización de repositorio frontend con scripts","Desarrollo de artefactos con React y TypeScript","Empaquetado de código en un solo archivo HTML","Visualización de artefactos para el usuario","Pruebas opcionales para el artefacto"],"fr":["Initialisation du référentiel frontend avec des scripts","Développement d''artefacts avec React et TypeScript","Empaquetage de code dans un seul fichier HTML","Affichage d''artefacts pour l''utilisateur","Tests optionnels pour l''artefact"],"de":["Initialisierung des Frontend-Repositorys mit Skripten","Entwicklung von Artifacts mit React und TypeScript","Bündelung von Code in eine einzige HTML-Datei","Anzeige von Artifacts für den Benutzer","Optionale Tests für das Artifact"],"pt":["Inicialização do repositório frontend com script","Desenvolvimento de artefatos com React 18 e TypeScript","Empacotamento de código com Parcel e Vite","Estilização com Tailwind CSS","Testes opcionais para artefatos"],"ru":["Инициализация репозитория frontend с помощью скрипта","Разработка артефактов с помощью React 18 и TypeScript","Упаковка кода с помощью Parcel и Vite","Стилизация с помощью Tailwind CSS","Необязательные тесты для артефактов"],"ar":["تهيئة مستودع واجهة المستخدم الأمامية مع سكريبت","تطوير قطع الفنية باستخدام React 18 و TypeScript","حزم الشفرة مع Parcel و Vite","تنسيق باستخدام Tailwind CSS","اختبارات اختيارية لقطع الفنية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Web Artifacts Builder","前端构建工具","React 18","TypeScript","Vite","Parcel","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui"],"ja":["Web アーティファクト ビルダー","フロントエンド構築ツール","React 18","TypeScript","Vite","Parcel","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui"],"ko":["웹 아티팩트 빌더","프런트엔드 구축 도구","React 18","TypeScript","Vite","Parcel","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui"],"es":["constructor de artefactos web","react","typescript","vite","parcel","tailwind css","desarrollo web","artefactos web","frontend"],"fr":["constructeur d''artefacts web","react","typescript","vite","parcel","tailwind css","développement web","artefacts web","frontend"],"de":["web-artifact-ersteller","react","typescript","vite","parcel","tailwind css","webentwicklung","web-artifacts","frontend"],"pt":["construtor de artefatos web","arteefatos web","React 18","TypeScript","Vite","Parcel","Tailwind CSS","desenvolvimento web","frontend"],"ru":["создатель веб-артефактов","веб-артефакты","React 18","TypeScript","Vite","Parcel","Tailwind CSS","разработка веб-приложений","фронтенд"],"ar":["بناء قطع الفنية","قطع فنية ويب","React 18","TypeScript","Vite","Parcel","Tailwind CSS","تطوير ويب","واجهة المستخدم الأمامية"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"web-artifacts-builder","description":"Suite of tools for creating elaborate, multi-component claude.ai HTML artifacts using modern frontend web technologies (React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui). Use for complex artifacts requiring state management, routing, or shadcn/ui components - not for simple single-file HTML/JSX artifacts.","bodyPreview":"# Web Artifacts Builder\n\nTo build powerful frontend claude.ai artifacts, follow these steps:\n1. Initialize the frontend repo using `scripts/init-artifact.sh`\n2. Develop your artifact by editing the generated code\n3. Bundle all code into a single HTML file using `scripts/bundle-artifact.sh`\n4. Display artifact to user\n5. (Optional) Test the artifact\n\n**Stack**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Parcel (bundling) + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui\n\n## Design & Style Guidelines\n\nVERY IMPORTANT: To avoid what","body":"# Web Artifacts Builder\n\nTo build powerful frontend claude.ai artifacts, follow these steps:\n1. Initialize the frontend repo using `scripts/init-artifact.sh`\n2. Develop your artifact by editing the generated code\n3. Bundle all code into a single HTML file using `scripts/bundle-artifact.sh`\n4. Display artifact to user\n5. (Optional) Test the artifact\n\n**Stack**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Parcel (bundling) + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui\n\n## Design & Style Guidelines\n\nVERY IMPORTANT: To avoid what is often referred to as \"AI slop\", avoid using excessive centered layouts, purple gradients, uniform rounded corners, and Inter font.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Step 1: Initialize Project\n\nRun the initialization script to create a new React project:\n```bash\nbash scripts/init-artifact.sh <project-name>\ncd <project-name>\n```\n\nThis creates a fully configured project with:\n- ✅ React + TypeScript (via Vite)\n- ✅ Tailwind CSS 3.4.1 with shadcn/ui theming system\n- ✅ Path aliases (`@/`) configured\n- ✅ 40+ shadcn/ui components pre-installed\n- ✅ All Radix UI dependencies included\n- ✅ Parcel configured for bundling (via .parcelrc)\n- ✅ Node 18+ compatibility (auto-detects and pins Vite version)\n\n### Step 2: Develop Your Artifact\n\nTo build the artifact, edit the generated files. See **Common Development Tasks** below for guidance.\n\n### Step 3: Bundle to Single HTML File\n\nTo bundle the React app into a single HTML artifact:\n```bash\nbash scripts/bundle-artifact.sh\n```\n\nThis creates `bundle.html` - a self-contained artifact with all JavaScript, CSS, and dependencies inlined. This file can be directly shared in Claude conversations as an artifact.\n\n**Requirements**: Your project must have an `index.html` in the root directory.\n\n**What the script does**:\n- Installs bundling dependencies (parcel, @parcel/config-default, parcel-resolver-tspaths, html-inline)\n- Creates `.parcelrc` config with path alias support\n- Builds with Parcel (no source maps)\n- Inlines all assets into single HTML using html-inline\n\n### Step 4: Share Artifact with User\n\nFinally, share the bundled HTML file in conversation with the user so they can view it as an artifact.\n\n### Step 5: Testing/Visualizing the Artifact (Optional)\n\nNote: This is a completely optional step. Only perform if necessary or requested.\n\nTo test/visualize the artifact, use available tools (including other Skills or built-in tools like Playwright or Puppeteer). In general, avoid testing the artifact upfront as it adds latency between the request and when the finished artifact can be seen. Test later, after presenting the artifact, if requested or if issues arise.\n\n## Reference\n\n- **shadcn/ui components**: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:03:15.677Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing advanced React-based artifact development capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 React 基础的前端代理开发能力的前端代理。","ja":"React を基盤とした高度なアーティファクト開発機能が必要なフロントエンド エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 React 기반 아티팩트 개발 기능이 필요한 프런트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes frontend que necesitan capacidades de desarrollo de artefactos avanzados basados en React.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents frontend ayant besoin de capacités de développement d''artefacts avancés basés sur React.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die erweiterte React-basierte Artefakt-Entwicklungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de capacidades avançadas de desenvolvimento de artefatos baseados em React.","ru":"Идеально подходит для фронтенд-агентов, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности разработки артефактов на основе React.","ar":"مثالي للوكيلات الأمامية التي تحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لتطوير المكونات القائمة على React."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build powerful frontend claude.ai artifacts using React 18, TypeScript, Vite, and Tailwind CSS, while streamlining the development process with automated bundling via Parcel and shadcn/ui integration.","zh":"赋予代理构建强大的前端 claude.ai アーティファクト的能力，使用 React 18、TypeScript、Vite 和 Tailwind CSS，同时通过 Parcel 自动化打包和 shadcn/ui 集成简化开发流程。","ja":"React 18、TypeScript、Vite、Tailwind CSS を使用して、強力なフロントエンドの claude.ai アーティファクトを構築し、Parcel と shadcn/ui の統合によって開発プロセスを自動化することでエージェントをEmpowerします。","ko":"React 18, TypeScript, Vite 및 Tailwind CSS를 사용하여 강력한 프런트엔드 claude.ai 아티팩트를 구축할 수 있도록 에이전트를 강화하고, Parcel 및 shadcn/ui 통합을 통해 개발 프로세스를 자동화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear potentes artefactos frontend de claude.ai utilizando React 18, TypeScript, Vite y Tailwind CSS, mientras que se simplifica el proceso de desarrollo con la automatización de la creación de paquetes a través de Parcel y la integración de shadcn/ui.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des artefacts frontend puissants pour claude.ai en utilisant React 18, TypeScript, Vite et Tailwind CSS, tout en simplifiant le processus de développement avec la mise en bundle automatique via Parcel et l''intégration de shadcn/ui.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, leistungsstarke Frontend-Artefakte von claude.ai zu erstellen, indem React 18, TypeScript, Vite und Tailwind CSS verwendet werden, während der Entwicklungsprozess durch automatisierte Bündelung über Parcel und shadcn/ui-Integration vereinfacht wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar artefatos poderosos de frontend claude.ai usando React 18, TypeScript, Vite e Tailwind CSS, além de otimizar o processo de desenvolvimento com empacotamento automático via Parcel e integração com shadcn/ui.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать мощные артефакты фронтенда claude.ai с использованием React 18, TypeScript, Vite и Tailwind CSS, а также оптимизировать процесс разработки с помощью автоматического пакетирования через Parcel и интеграции с shadcn/ui.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء مكونات قوية لبرامج claude.ai الأمامية باستخدام React 18 و TypeScript و Vite و Tailwind CSS، بالإضافة إلى تحسين عملية التطوير من خلال حزمة تلقائية عبر Parcel ودمج shadcn/ui."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing custom frontend artifacts for claude.ai","Automating the bundling of React code into single HTML files","Generating visually appealing UI components using Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui"],"zh":["为 claude.ai 开发自定义前端アーティファクト","自动将 React 代码打包成单个 HTML 文件","使用 Tailwind CSS 和 shadcn/ui 生成视觉上吸引人的 UI 组件"],"ja":["claude.ai 用のカスタム フロントエンド アーティファクトを開発する","React コードを単一の HTML ファイルに自動でバンドルする","Tailwind CSS と shadcn/ui を使用して視覚的に魅力的な UI コンポーネントを生成する"],"ko":["claude.ai를 위한 커스텀 프런트엔드 아티팩트 개발","React 코드를 단일 HTML 파일로 자동으로 번들링","Tailwind CSS 및 shadcn/ui를 사용하여 시각적으로 매력적인 UI 컴포넌트 생성"],"es":["Desarrollar artefactos frontend personalizados para claude.ai","Automatizar la creación de paquetes de código React en archivos HTML únicos","Generar componentes de interfaz de usuario visualmente atractivos utilizando Tailwind CSS y shadcn/ui"],"fr":["Développer des artefacts frontend personnalisés pour claude.ai","Automatiser la mise en bundle du code React en fichiers HTML uniques","Générer des composants d''interface utilisateur visuellement attrayants en utilisant Tailwind CSS et shadcn/ui"],"de":["Erstellen von benutzerdefinierten Frontend-Artefakten für claude.ai","Automatisieren der Bündelung von React-Code in einzelne HTML-Dateien","Erzeugen visuell ansprechender Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten unter Verwendung von Tailwind CSS und shadcn/ui"],"pt":["Desenvolver artefatos personalizados de frontend para claude.ai","Automatizar a criação de código React em arquivos HTML únicos","Gerar componentes de UI visualmente atraentes usando Tailwind CSS e shadcn/ui"],"ru":["Разработка пользовательских артефактов фронтенда для claude.ai","Автоматизация сборки кода React в единственный файл HTML","Генерация визуально привлекательных компонентов UI с использованием Tailwind CSS и shadcn/ui"],"ar":["إنشاء مكونات أمامية مخصصة لبرامج claude.ai","تأتميم حزمة رمز React في ملفات HTML منفردة","توليد مكونات واجهة مستخدم بصريًا جذابة باستخدام Tailwind CSS و shadcn/ui"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of React 18, TypeScript, and Vite","Dependent on Parcel for bundling and shadcn/ui for UI components","Limited to frontend artifact development for claude.ai"],"zh":["需要 React 18、TypeScript 和 Vite 的知识","依赖 Parcel 进行打包和 shadcn/ui 进行 UI 组件","仅限 claude.ai 前端アーティファクト开发"],"ja":["React 18、TypeScript、Vite の知識が必要","Parcel によるバンドルと shadcn/ui による UI コンポーネントに依存","claude.ai フロントエンド アーティファクト開発に限定"],"ko":["React 18, TypeScript, Vite에 대한 지식이 필요","Parcel을 통한 번들링 및 shadcn/ui를 통한 UI 컴포넌트에 의존","claude.ai 프런트엔드 아티팩트 개발에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de React 18, TypeScript y Vite","Dependiente de Parcel para la creación de paquetes y de shadcn/ui para los componentes de la interfaz de usuario","Limitado al desarrollo de artefactos frontend para claude.ai"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en React 18, TypeScript et Vite","Dépend de Parcel pour la mise en bundle et de shadcn/ui pour les composants d''interface utilisateur","Limité au développement d''artefacts frontend pour claude.ai"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von React 18, TypeScript und Vite","Ist von Parcel für die Bündelung und von shadcn/ui für die Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten abhängig","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von Frontend-Artefakten für claude.ai"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de React 18, TypeScript e Vite","Dependente de Parcel para empacotamento e shadcn/ui para componentes de UI","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de artefatos de frontend para claude.ai"],"ru":["Требует знания React 18, TypeScript и Vite","Зависит от Parcel для пакетирования и shadcn/ui для компонентов UI","Ограничен разработкой артефактов фронтенда для claude.ai"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة React 18 و TypeScript و Vite","يعتمد على Parcel لحزمة وتشكيل shadcn/ui لمكونات واجهة المستخدم","محدود بتطوير المكونات الأمامية لبرامج claude.ai"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/test-driven-development', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'test-driven-development', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z', '2026-02-18T14:03:04.187Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/test-driven-development","name":"test-driven-development","description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）是一种通过先写测试用例来驱动开发的方法，确保代码的可靠性和可维护性","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）は、テストケースを先に書くことで開発を促進する手法で、コードの信頼性と保守性を確保します","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)은 테스트 케이스를 먼저 작성하여 개발을 주도하는 방법으로 코드의 신뢰성과 유지보수성을 확보합니다","es":"El desarrollo dirigido por pruebas es una práctica de desarrollo de software que implica escribir las pruebas antes de escribir el código. Esto garantiza que el código sea correcto y cumpla con los requisitos","fr":"Le développement piloté par les tests est une pratique de développement de logiciels qui consiste à écrire les tests avant de rédiger le code. Cela garantit que le code soit correct et répond aux exigences","de":"Die testgetriebene Entwicklung ist eine Praxis der Softwareentwicklung, bei der die Tests vor dem Schreiben des Codes erstellt werden. Dies stellt sicher, dass der Code korrekt ist und die Anforderungen erfüllt","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por testes (TDD) é uma metodologia de desenvolvimento de software que envolve a escrita de testes antes da implementação do código.","ru":"Разработка через тестирование (TDD) - это методология разработки программного обеспечения, включающая написание тестов до реализации кода.","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) هو منهجية لتنمية البرمجيات التي تتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل تنفيذ الكود.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）最佳实践","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）入門","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD) 가이드","es":"Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","fr":"Développement Piloté par les Tests","de":"Testgetriebene Entwicklung","pt":"Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD) - Melhores Prát...","ru":"Разработка через тестирование (TDD) - Лучшие практики","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) - أفضل الممارسات","en":"test-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）是一种通过先写测试用例来驱动开发的方法，确保代码的可靠性和可维护性","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）は、テストケースを先に書くことで開発を促進する手法で、コードの信頼性と保守性を確保します","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)은 테스트 케이스를 먼저 작성하여 개발을 주도하는 방법으로 코드의 신뢰성과 유지보수성을 확보합니다","es":"El desarrollo dirigido por pruebas es una práctica de desarrollo de software que implica escribir las pruebas antes de escribir el código. Esto garantiza que...","fr":"Le développement piloté par les tests est une pratique de développement de logiciels qui consiste à écrire les tests avant de rédiger le code. Cela garantit ...","de":"Die testgetriebene Entwicklung ist eine Praxis der Softwareentwicklung, bei der die Tests vor dem Schreiben des Codes erstellt werden. Dies stellt sicher, da...","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por testes (TDD) é uma metodologia de desenvolvimento de software que envolve a escrita de testes antes da implementação do código.","ru":"Разработка через тестирование (TDD) - это методология разработки программного обеспечения, включающая написание тестов до реализации кода.","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) هو منهجية لتنمية البرمجيات التي تتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل تنفيذ الكود.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提高代码质量","减少bug数量","提高开发效率","确保代码可靠性","简化代码维护"],"ja":["コード品質の向上","バグの削減","開発効率の向上","コードの信頼性の確保","コードの保守の簡素化"],"ko":["코드 품질 향상","버그 수减少","개발 효율성 향상","코드 신뢰성 확보","코드 유지보수 간소화"],"es":["Escribe las pruebas antes de escribir el código","Garantiza que el código sea correcto y cumpla con los requisitos","Mejora la calidad del código","Reduce los errores y bugs","Facilita el proceso de depuración"],"fr":["Écrivez les tests avant de rédiger le code","Assurez-vous que le code soit correct et réponde aux exigences","Améliorez la qualité du code","Réduisez les erreurs et les bogues","Facilitez le processus de débogage"],"de":["Schreiben Sie die Tests vor dem Schreiben des Codes","Stellen Sie sicher, dass der Code korrekt ist und die Anforderungen erfüllt","Verbessern Sie die Qualität des Codes","Reduzieren Sie die Fehler und Bugs","Vereinfachen Sie den Prozess der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Escrita de testes antes da implementação do código","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Redução de bugs e erros","Desenvolvimento mais rápido e eficiente","Maior confiabilidade do código"],"ru":["Написание тестов до реализации кода","Улучшение качества кода","Снижение количества багов и ошибок","Быстрое и эффективное развитие","Большая надежность кода"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات قبل تنفيذ الكود","تحسين جودة الكود","تقليل الأخطاء والعيوب","تنمية أسرع وأكثر كفاءة","زيادة ثقة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","TDD","软件开发","代码质量","开发效率","测试用例","代码可靠性"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","TDD","ソフトウェア開発","コード品質","開発効率","テストケース","コードの信頼性"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","TDD","소프트웨어 개발","코드 품질","개발 효율성","테스트 케이스","코드 신뢰성"],"es":["desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","pruebas unitarias","pruebas de integración","calidad del código","depuración","desarrollo de software","pruebas automatizadas","TDD"],"fr":["développement piloté par les tests","tests unitaires","tests d''intégration","qualité du code","débogage","développement de logiciels","tests automatisés","TDD"],"de":["testgetriebene Entwicklung","Einheitstests","Integrationstests","Code-Qualität","Fehlersuche","Softwareentwicklung","automatisierte Tests","TDD"],"pt":["desenvolvimento dirigido por testes","tdd","testes de unidade","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade do código","melhoria da qualidade","redução de bugs"],"ru":["разработка через тестирование","tdd","юнит-тесты","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","улучшение качества","снижение багов"],"ar":["التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","tdd","اختبارات الوحدة","تنمية البرمجيات","جودة الكود","تحسين الجودة","تقليل الأخطاء"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.525Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"test-driven-development","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","bodyPreview":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD","body":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That''s rationalization.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_red -> red [label=\"wrong\\nfailure\"];\n    green -> verify_green;\n    verify_green -> refactor [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_green -> green [label=\"no\"];\n    refactor -> verify_green [label=\"stay\\ngreen\"];\n    verify_green -> next;\n    next -> red;\n}\n```\n\n### RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\ntest(''retries failed operations 3 times'', async () => {\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const operation = () => {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts < 3) throw new Error(''fail'');\n    return ''success'';\n  };\n\n  const result = await retryOperation(operation);\n\n  expect(result).toBe(''success'');\n  expect(attempts).toBe(3);\n});\n```\nClear name, tests real behavior, one thing\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\ntest(''retry works'', async () => {\n  const mock = jest.fn()\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(''success'');\n  await retryOperation(mock);\n  expect(mock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);\n});\n```\nVague name, tests mock not code\n</Bad>\n\n**Requirements:**\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n### Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n**Test errors?** Fix error, re-run until it fails correctly.\n\n### GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      if (i === 2) throw e;\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(''unreachable'');\n}\n```\nJust enough to pass\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options?: {\n    maxRetries?: number;\n    backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n    onRetry?: (attempt: number) => void;\n  }\n): Promise<T> {\n  // YAGNI\n}\n```\nOver-engineered\n</Bad>\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n### Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n**Other tests fail?** Fix now.\n\n### REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n### Repeat\n\nNext failing test for next feature.\n\n## Good Tests\n\n| Quality | Good | Bad |\n|---------|------|-----|\n| **Minimal** | One thing. \"and\" in name? Split it. | `test(''validates email and domain and whitespace'')` |\n| **Clear** | Name describes behavior | `test(''test1'')` |\n| **Shows intent** | Demonstrates desired API | Obscures what code should do |\n\n## Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n- You never saw it catch the bug\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n- \"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive\n\nAutomated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust. Working code without real tests is technical debt.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower.\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required. You verify remembered edge cases, not discovered ones.\n\nTests-first force edge case discovery before implementing. Tests-after verify you remembered everything (you didn''t).\n\n30 minutes of tests after ≠ TDD. You get coverage, lose proof tests work.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference, write tests first\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n| \"TDD will slow me down\" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |\n| \"Manual test faster\" | Manual doesn''t prove edge cases. You''ll re-test every change. |\n| \"Existing code has no tests\" | You''re improving it. Add tests for existing code. |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- Rationalizing \"just this once\"\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n- \"TDD is dogmatic, I''m being pragmatic\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n## Example: Bug Fix\n\n**Bug:** Empty email accepted\n\n**RED**\n```typescript\ntest(''rejects empty email'', async () => {\n  const result = await submitForm({ email: '''' });\n  expect(result.error).toBe(''Email required'');\n});\n```\n\n**Verify RED**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nFAIL: expected ''Email required'', got undefined\n```\n\n**GREEN**\n```typescript\nfunction submitForm(data: FormData) {\n  if (!data.email?.trim()) {\n    return { error: ''Email required'' };\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Verify GREEN**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nPASS\n```\n\n**REFACTOR**\nExtract validation for multiple fields if needed.\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nBefore marking work complete:\n\n- [ ] Every new function/method has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n## When Stuck\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Don''t know how to test | Write wished-for API. Write assertion first. Ask your human partner. |\n| Test too complicated | Design too complicated. Simplify interface. |\n| Must mock everything | Code too coupled. Use dependency injection. |\n| Test setup huge | Extract helpers. Still complex? Simplify design. |\n\n## Debugging Integration\n\nBug found? Write failing test reproducing it. Follow TDD cycle. Test proves fix and prevents regression.\n\nNever fix bugs without a test.\n\n## Testing Anti-Patterns\n\nWhen adding mocks or test utilities, read @testing-anti-patterns.md to avoid common pitfalls:\n- Testing mock behavior instead of real behavior\n- Adding test-only methods to production classes\n- Mocking without understanding dependencies\n\n## Final Rule\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\nNo exceptions without your human partner''s permission.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:03:04.187Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents and Development Assistants needing rigorous testing methodologies like Test-Driven Development (TDD)","zh":"适用于需要严格测试方法的代码审查和开发助手，如测试驱动开发（TDD）","ja":"コードレビュー代理と開発アシスタントが厳格なテスト方法論、たとえばテスト駆動開発（TDD）を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트와 개발 도우미가 엄격한 테스트 방법론을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다. 예를 들어 테스트 주도 개발(TDD)","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisión de Código y Asistentes de Desarrollo que necesitan metodologías de prueba rigurosas como Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD)","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Révision de Code et les Assistants de Développement ayant besoin de méthodologies de test rigoureuses comme le Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD)","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agenten und Entwicklungsassistenten, die strenge Testmethoden wie testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código e Assistentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de metodologias de teste rigorosas como Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD)","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов проверки кода и помощников разработки, требующих строгих методологий тестирования, таких как разработка, управляемая тестами (TDD)","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الشفرة ومساعدي التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى منهجيات اختبار صارمة مثل التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write reliable code by enforcing a test-first approach, ensuring core principles like watching tests fail are upheld, and supporting behaviors such as new feature development, bug fixing, and refactoring through minimal code implementations","zh":"使代理能够通过强制执行测试优先的方法编写可靠的代码，确保核心原则得到遵守，例如确保测试失败，并支持通过最少代码实现来进行新功能开发、错误修复和重构等行为","ja":"エージェントが信頼性の高いコードを書くことを可能にし、テスト優先のアプローチを強制的に実施し、コア原則を遵守し、新しい機能の開発、バグの修正、リファクタリングなどの振る舞いを最小限のコード実装を通じてサポートする","ko":"에이전트가 테스트 우선 접근 방식을 시행함으로써 안정적인 코드를 작성할 수 있도록 하며 핵심 원칙을 준수하고 새로운 기능 개발, 버그 수정 및 리팩토링과 같은 행동을 최소한의 코드 구현을 통해 지원하는 것을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes escribir código confiable al aplicar un enfoque de prueba primero, garantizando principios básicos como asegurarse de que las pruebas fallen y apoyando comportamientos como el desarrollo de nuevas características, la corrección de errores y la reestructuración a través de implementaciones de código mínimas","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire du code fiable en appliquant une approche de test en premier, en garantissant les principes de base tels que s''assurer que les tests échouent et en soutenant des comportements tels que le développement de nouvelles fonctionnalités, la correction de bogues et la réorganisation à l''aide de mises en œuvre de code minimales","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, zuverlässigen Code zu schreiben, indem sie einen testgetriebenen Ansatz durchsetzen, grundlegende Prinzipien wie das Beobachten von fehlgeschlagenen Tests aufrechterhalten und Verhaltensweisen wie die Entwicklung neuer Funktionen, die Fehlerbehebung und die Refaktorierung durch minimale Codeimplementierungen unterstützen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escreverem código confiável, aplicando uma abordagem de teste em primeiro lugar, garantindo princípios fundamentais como assistir a falhas de testes sejam mantidos e apoiando comportamentos como desenvolvimento de novas funcionalidades, correção de bugs e refatoração por meio de implementações de código mínimas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать надежный код, применяя подход тестирования в первую очередь, гарантируя, что основные принципы, такие как наблюдение за неудачами тестов, соблюдаются, и поддерживая поведение, такое как разработка новых функций, исправление ошибок и рефакторинг посредством минимальных реализаций кода","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من كتابة Код موثوق به من خلال تطبيق نهج الاختبار أولاً، وضمان مبادئ أساسية مثل مشاهدة فشل الاختبارات يتم الحفاظ عليها، ودعم سلوكيات مثل تطوير ميزات جديدة وتصحيح الأخطاء وإعادة هيكلة الكود من خلال تنفيذات код دقيقة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating unit tests for new features","Debugging existing codebases through targeted test creation","Refactoring legacy code with confidence using TDD"],"zh":["为新功能自动化单元测试","通过有针对性的测试创建调试现有代码库","使用TDD以信心重构遗留代码"],"ja":["新しい機能の単体テストを自動化する","ターゲットを絞ったテスト作成を通じて既存のコードベースをデバッグする","TDDを使用してレガシーコードを自信を持ってリファクタリングする"],"ko":["새로운 기능의 단위 테스트를 자동화하는 것","목표를 좁혀 테스트를 생성하여 기존 코드베이스를 디버깅하는 것","TDD를 사용하여 레거시 코드를 자신감 있게 리팩토링하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas unitarias para nuevas características","Depuración de códigobases existentes a través de la creación de pruebas dirigidas","Reestructuración de código heredado con confianza utilizando TDD"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests unitaires pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités","Débogage des bases de code existantes via la création de tests ciblés","Réorganisation de code hérité avec confiance en utilisant le TDD"],"de":["Automatisierung von Einheitstests für neue Funktionen","Fehlerbehebung in bestehenden Codebasen durch gezielte Testerstellung","Refaktorierung von Legacy-Code mit Vertrauen unter Verwendung von TDD"],"pt":["Automação de testes unitários para novas funcionalidades","Depuração de código existente por meio da criação de testes direcionados","Reconstrução de código legado com confiança usando TDD"],"ru":["Автоматизация юнит-тестов для новых функций","Отладка существующих кодовых баз посредством создания целенаправленных тестов","Рефакторинг устаревшего кода с уверенностью, используя TDD"],"ar":["أتمتة اختبارات الوحدات لملحقات جديدة","تصحيح أخطاء قاعدة الكود الحالية من خلال إنشاء اختبارات مستهدفة","إعادة بناء كود قديم بالثقة باستخدام TDD"]},"limitations":{"en":["May not be suitable for throwaway prototypes or generated code","Requires discipline to follow the TDD cycle","Exceptions may apply to configuration files or certain types of generated code, requiring human oversight"],"zh":["可能不适合一次性原型或生成的代码","需要纪律来遵循TDD循环","配置文件或某些类型的生成代码可能需要人工监督"],"ja":["使い捨てのプロトタイプや生成されたコードには適さない可能性がある","TDDサイクルに従うための規律が必要","コンフィギュレーションファイルまたは特定のタイプの生成コードには、例外が適用される可能性があり、人間の監視が必要"],"ko":["일회용 프로토 타입이나 생성 된 코드에는 적합하지 않을 수 있음","TDD 주기를 따르기 위한 규율이 필요함","구성 파일 또는 특정 유형의 생성 된 코드에는 예외가 적용될 수 있으며, 인간의 감시가 필요함"],"es":["Puede no ser adecuado para prototipos desechables o código generado","Requiere disciplina para seguir el ciclo de TDD","Se pueden aplicar excepciones a archivos de configuración o ciertos tipos de código generado, lo que requiere supervisión humana"],"fr":["Peut ne pas convenir aux prototypes jetables ou au code généré","Nécessite de la discipline pour suivre le cycle du TDD","Des exceptions peuvent s''appliquer aux fichiers de configuration ou à certains types de code généré, nécessitant une surveillance humaine"],"de":["Kann für wegwerffähige Prototypen oder generierten Code nicht geeignet sein","Benötigt Disziplin, um den TDD-Zyklus zu befolgen","Ausnahmen können für Konfigurationsdateien oder bestimmte Arten von generiertem Code gelten, was menschliche Überwachung erfordert"],"pt":["Pode não ser adequado para protótipos descartáveis ou código gerado","Exige disciplina para seguir o ciclo TDD","Exceções podem aplicar-se a arquivos de configuração ou certos tipos de código gerado, exigindo supervisão humana"],"ru":["Не может подходить для одноразовых прототипов или сгенерированного кода","Требует дисциплины для соблюдения цикла TDD","Исключения могут применяться к файлам конфигурации или определенным типам сгенерированного кода, требующим человеческого надзора"],"ar":[" قد لا يكون مناسبًا للنماذج الأولية القابلة للقذف أو الكود المولد","يتطلب انضباطًا لاتباع دورة TDD","استثناءات قد تنطبق على ملفات التكوين أو أنواع معينة من الكود المولد، يتطلب إشرافًا بشريًا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
