本原則について紹介し、スプライトシステムやタイルマップデザインなどの核心概念を解説します","ko":"이 문서는 2D 게임 개발의 기본 원리를 소개하며, 스프라이트 시스템과 타일 맵 디자인 등의 핵심 개념을 다룹니다","es":"El desarrollo de juegos 2D implica el diseño de sistemas de sprites y mapas de baldosas. Aprende los principios básicos para crear juegos 2D","fr":"Le développement de jeux 2D implique la conception de systèmes de sprites et de cartes de tuiles. Découvrez les principes de base pour créer des jeux 2D","de":"Die 2D-Spiele-Entwicklung beinhaltet das Design von Sprite-Systemen und Tilemaps. Erfahren Sie die Grundlagen für die Erstellung von 2D-Spielen","pt":"O desenvolvimento de jogos 2D envolve princípios como sistemas de sprites e design de tilemaps","ru":"Разработка 2D-игр включает принципы, такие как системы спрайтов и дизайн тайлмапов","ar":"تطوير ألعاب 2D يتضمن مبادئ مثل أنظمة السبرايتس وتصميم التايل ماب","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro..."},"definition":{"en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"features":{"zh":["精灵系统","瓦片地图设计","动画原则","层次控制","帧率优化"],"ja":["スプライトシステム","タイルマップデザイン","アニメーション原則","レイヤー制御","フレームレート最適化"],"ko":["스프라이트 시스템","타일 맵 디자인","애니메이션 원리","레이어 제어","프레임 레이트 최적화"],"es":["Sistemas de sprites","Diseño de mapas de baldosas","Animación y efectos visuales","Control de capas y orden Z","Optimización de rendimiento"],"fr":["Systèmes de sprites","Conception de cartes de tuiles","Animation et effets visuels","Contrôle des couches et ordre Z","Optimisation des performances"],"de":["Sprite-Systeme","Tilemap-Design","Animation und visuelle Effekte","Schichtsteuerung und Z-Order","Leistungsoptimierung"],"pt":["Sistemas de sprites","Design de tilemaps","Princípios de animação","Controle de camadas","Otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["Системы спрайтов","Дизайн тайлмапов","Принципы анимации","Контроль слоев","Оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["أنظمة السبرايتس","تصميم التايل ماب","مبادئ Animation","التحكم في الطبقات","تحسين الأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["2D游戏开发","精灵系统","瓦片地图设计","游戏开发工具","游戏引擎","游戏优化"],"ja":["2Dゲーム開発","スプライトシステム","タイルマップデザイン","ゲーム開発ツール","ゲームエンジン","ゲーム最適化"],"ko":["2D 게임 개발","스프라이트 시스템","타일 맵 디자인","게임 개발 도구","게임 엔진","게임 최적화"],"es":["desarrollo de juegos 2D","sistemas de sprites","diseño de mapas de baldosas","animación 2D","efectos visuales","optimización de rendimiento"],"fr":["développement de jeux 2D","systèmes de sprites","conception de cartes de tuiles","animation 2D","effets visuels","optimisation des performances"],"de":["2D-Spiele-Entwicklung","Sprite-Systeme","Tilemap-Design","2D-Animation","visuelle Effekte","Leistungsoptimierung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de jogos 2D","sistemas de sprites","design de tilemaps","princípios de animação","controle de camadas","otimização de desempenho","jogos 2D","gráficos 2D"],"ru":["разработка 2D-игр","системы спрайтов","дизайн тайлмапов","принципы анимации","контроль слоев","оптимизация производительности","2D-игры","2D-графика"],"ar":["تطوير ألعاب 2D","أنظمة السبرايتس","تصميم التايل ماب","مبادئ Animation","التحكم في الطبقات","تحسين الأداء","ألعاب 2D","رسومات 2D"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:58:18.472Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"2d-games","description":"2D game development principles. Sprites, tilemaps, physics, camera.","bodyPreview":"# 2D Game Development\n\n> Principles for 2D game systems.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Sprite Systems\n\n### Sprite Organization\n\n| Component | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Atlas** | Combine textures, reduce draw calls |\n| **Animation** | Frame sequences |\n| **Pivot** | Rotation/scale origin |\n| **Layering** | Z-order control |\n\n### Animation Principles\n\n- Frame rate: 8-24 FPS typical\n- Squash and stretch for impact\n- Anticipation before action\n- Follow-through after action\n\n---\n\n## 2. Tilemap Design\n\n###","body":"# 2D Game Development\n\n> Principles for 2D game systems.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Sprite Systems\n\n### Sprite Organization\n\n| Component | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Atlas** | Combine textures, reduce draw calls |\n| **Animation** | Frame sequences |\n| **Pivot** | Rotation/scale origin |\n| **Layering** | Z-order control |\n\n### Animation Principles\n\n- Frame rate: 8-24 FPS typical\n- Squash and stretch for impact\n- Anticipation before action\n- Follow-through after action\n\n---\n\n## 2. Tilemap Design\n\n### Tile Considerations\n\n| Factor | Recommendation |\n|--------|----------------|\n| **Size** | 16x16, 32x32, 64x64 |\n| **Auto-tiling** | Use for terrain |\n| **Collision** | Simplified shapes |\n\n### Layers\n\n| Layer | Content |\n|-------|---------|\n| Background | Non-interactive scenery |\n| Terrain | Walkable ground |\n| Props | Interactive objects |\n| Foreground | Parallax overlay |\n\n---\n\n## 3. 2D Physics\n\n### Collision Shapes\n\n| Shape | Use Case |\n|-------|----------|\n| Box | Rectangular objects |\n| Circle | Balls, rounded |\n| Capsule | Characters |\n| Polygon | Complex shapes |\n\n### Physics Considerations\n\n- Pixel-perfect vs physics-based\n- Fixed timestep for consistency\n- Layers for filtering\n\n---\n\n## 4. Camera Systems\n\n### Camera Types\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| **Follow** | Track player |\n| **Look-ahead** | Anticipate movement |\n| **Multi-target** | Two-player |\n| **Room-based** | Metroidvania |\n\n### Screen Shake\n\n- Short duration (50-200ms)\n- Diminishing intensity\n- Use sparingly\n\n---\n\n## 5. Genre Patterns\n\n### Platformer\n\n- Coyote time (leniency after edge)\n- Jump buffering\n- Variable jump height\n\n### Top-down\n\n- 8-directional or free movement\n- Aim-based or auto-aim\n- Consider rotation or not\n\n---\n\n## 6. Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ Don''t | ✅ Do |\n|----------|-------|\n| Separate textures | Use atlases |\n| Complex collision shapes | Simplified collision |\n| Jittery camera | Smooth following |\n| Pixel-perfect on physics | Choose one approach |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** 2D is about clarity. Every pixel should communicate.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T20:54:24.210Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","zh":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","ja":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","ko":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","es":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","fr":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","de":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","pt":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","ru":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design.","ar":"Ideal for Game Development Agents requiring expertise in 2D game systems, sprite animation, and tilemap design."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","zh":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","ja":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","ko":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","es":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","fr":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","de":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","pt":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","ru":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance.","ar":"Empowers agents to create engaging 2D game experiences using sprite systems with atlas texture combination, animation principles like squash and stretch, and tilemap design for immersive gameplay, all while leveraging frame rates between 8-24 FPS for optimal performance."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"zh":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"ja":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"ko":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"es":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"fr":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"de":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"pt":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management","Implementing animation principles for realistic character movements","Creating immersive tilemap designs for 2D game environments"],"ru":["Designing sprite systems with efficient atlas management"