:"أداة تصميم الواجهة الأمامية لتحويل الإعدادات","en":"frontend-design"},"description":{"zh":"前端设计工具可转换Antigravity IDE配置到多种IDE和CLI兼容格式，简化开发流程","ja":"フロントエンドデザインツールは、Antigravity IDE設定を複数のIDEとCLIと互換性のある形式に変換し、開発プロセスを簡素化","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 도구는 Antigravity IDE 설정을 여러 IDE 및 CLI와 호환 가능한 형식으로 변환하여 개발 프로세스를 간소화","es":"Herramienta de conversión de configuraciones de frontend para desarrolladores","fr":"Outil de conversion de configurations de frontend pour les développeurs","de":"Werkzeug zur Konvertierung von Frontend-Konfigurationen für Entwickler","pt":"A ferramenta de design frontend é uma solução para converter configurações do Antigravity IDE para formatos compatíveis com outras plataformas","ru":"Инструмент для конвертации конфигураций frontend является решением для конвертации конфигураций из Antigravity IDE в форматы, совместимые с другими платформами","ar":"أداة تصميم الواجهة الأمامية هي حل لتحويل إعدادات Antigravity IDE إلى تنسيقات متوافقة مع منصات أخرى","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro..."},"definition":{"en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"features":{"zh":["支持多种IDE和CLI兼容格式","简化开发流程","轻松转换Antigravity IDE配置","提高开发效率"],"ja":["複数のIDEとCLIと互換性のある形式をサポート","開発プロセスを簡素化","Antigravity IDE設定を簡単に変換","開発効率を向上"],"ko":["여러 IDE 및 CLI와 호환 가능한 형식 지원","개발 프로세스를 간소화","Antigravity IDE 설정을 쉽게 변환","개발 효율성을 향상"],"es":["Conversión de configuraciones de Antigravity IDE","Compatibilidad con GitHub Copilot y otros IDEs","Compatibilidad con CLIs como Kiro y OpenCode","Diseño de interfaces de usuario basado en la psicología del usuario","Sistema de colores personalizable"],"fr":["Conversion des configurations d''Antigravity IDE","Compatibilité avec GitHub Copilot et d''autres IDE","Compatibilité avec les CLIs comme Kiro et OpenCode","Conception d''interfaces utilisateur basée sur la psychologie de l''utilisateur","Système de couleurs personnalisable"],"de":["Konvertierung von Konfigurationen von Antigravity IDE","Kompatibilität mit GitHub Copilot und anderen IDEs","Kompatibilität mit CLIs wie Kiro und OpenCode","Erstellung von Benutzeroberflächen basierend auf der Benutzerpsychologie","Anpassbares Farbsystem"],"pt":["Conversão de configurações do Antigravity IDE","Compatibilidade com IDEs e CLIs","Design de sistema de cores","Psicologia do usuário para decisões de design","Princípios de design minimalista"],"ru":["Конвертация конфигураций из Antigravity IDE","Совместимость с IDE и CLI","Дизайн системы цвета","Психология пользователя для принятия решений по дизайну","Принципы минималистского дизайна"],"ar":["تحويل إعدادات Antigravity IDE","التوافق مع IDE و CLI","تصميم نظام الألوان","علم النفس المستخدم لاتخاذ قرارات التصميم","مبادئ التصميم المتناهي الصغر"]},"keywords":{"zh":["前端设计工具","Antigravity IDE","IDE兼容格式","CLI兼容格式","开发流程","开发效率"],"ja":["フロントエンドデザインツール","Antigravity IDE","IDEと互換性のある形式","CLIと互換性のある形式","開発プロセス","開発効率"],"ko":["프론트엔드 디자인 도구","Antigravity IDE","IDE와 호환 가능한 형식","CLI와 호환 가능한 형식","개발 프로세스","개발 효율성"],"es":["diseño de frontend","conversión de configuraciones","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Kiro","OpenCode","interfaces de usuario","psicología del usuario"],"fr":["conception frontend","conversion de configurations","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Kiro","OpenCode","interfaces utilisateur","psychologie de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Frontend-Design","Konvertierung von Konfigurationen","Antigravity IDE","GitHub Copilot","Kiro","OpenCode","Benutzeroberflächen","Benutzerpsychologie"],"pt":["design frontend","conversão de configurações","Antigravity IDE","IDEs","CLIs","desenvolvimento de software","psicologia do usuário","design de sistema de cores"],"ru":["конвертация конфигураций frontend","конвертация конфигураций","Antigravity IDE","IDE","CLI","разработка программного обеспечения","психология пользователя","дизайн системы цвета"],"ar":["أداة تصميم الواجهة الأمامية","تحويل الإعدادات","Antigravity IDE","IDE","CLI","تطوير البرمجيات","علم النفس المستخدم","تصميم نظام الألوان"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-design","description":"Design thinking and decision-making for web UI. Use when designing components, layouts, color schemes, typography, or creating aesthetic interfaces. Teaches principles, not fixed values.","bodyPreview":"# Frontend Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Every pixel has purpose. Restraint is luxury. User psychology drives decisions.\n> **Core Principle:** THINK, don''t memorize. ASK, don''t assume.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Selective Reading Rule (MANDATORY)\n\n**Read REQUIRED files always, OPTIONAL only when needed:**\n\n| File | Status | When to Read |\n|------|--------|--------------|\n| [ux-psychology.md](ux-psychology.md) | 🔴 **REQUIRED** | Always read first! |\n| [color-system.md](color-system.md) | ⚪ Optional | Color/","body":"# Frontend Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Every pixel has purpose. Restraint is luxury. User psychology drives decisions.\n> **Core Principle:** THINK, don''t memorize. ASK, don''t assume.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Selective Reading Rule (MANDATORY)\n\n**Read REQUIRED files always, OPTIONAL only when needed:**\n\n| File | Status | When to Read |\n|------|--------|--------------|\n| [ux-psychology.md](ux-psychology.md) | 🔴 **REQUIRED** | Always read first! |\n| [color-system.md](color-system.md) | ⚪ Optional | Color/palette decisions |\n| [typography-system.md](typography-system.md) | ⚪ Optional | Font selection/pairing |\n| [visual-effects.md](visual-effects.md) | ⚪ Optional | Glassmorphism, shadows, gradients |\n| [animation-guide.md](animation-guide.md) | ⚪ Optional | Animation needed |\n| [motion-graphics.md](motion-graphics.md) | ⚪ Optional | Lottie, GSAP, 3D |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | ⚪ Optional | Context templates |\n\n> 🔴 **ux-psychology.md = ALWAYS READ. Others = only if relevant.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for audits (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/ux_audit.py` | UX Psychology & Accessibility Audit | `python scripts/ux_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: ASK BEFORE ASSUMING (MANDATORY)\n\n> **STOP! If the user''s request is open-ended, DO NOT default to your favorites.**\n\n### When User Prompt is Vague, ASK:\n\n**Color not specified?** Ask:\n> \"What color palette do you prefer? (blue/green/orange/neutral/other?)\"\n\n**Style not specified?** Ask: \n> \"What style are you going for? (minimal/bold/retro/futuristic/organic?)\"\n\n**Layout not specified?** Ask:\n> \"Do you have a layout preference? (single column/grid/asymmetric/full-width?)\"\n\n### ⛔ DEFAULT TENDENCIES TO AVOID (ANTI-SAFE HARBOR):\n\n| AI Default Tendency | Why It''s Bad | Think Instead |\n|---------------------|--------------|---------------|\n| **Bento Grids (Modern Cliché)** | Used in every AI design | Why does this content NEED a grid? |\n| **Hero Split (Left/Right)** | Predictable & Boring | How about Massive Typography or Vertical Narrative? |\n| **Mesh/Aurora Gradients** | The \"new\" lazy background | What''s a radical color pairing? |\n| **Glassmorphism** | AI''s idea of \"premium\" | How about solid, high-contrast flat? |\n| **Deep Cyan / Fintech Blue** | Safe harbor from purple ban | Why not Red, Black, or Neon Green? |\n| **\"Orchestrate / Empower\"** | AI-generated copywriting | How would a human say this? |\n| Dark background + neon glow | Overused, \"AI look\" | What does the BRAND actually need? |\n| **Rounded everything** | Generic/Safe | Where can I use sharp, brutalist edges? |\n\n> 🔴 **\"Every ''safe'' structure you choose brings you one step closer to a generic template. TAKE RISKS.\"**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Constraint Analysis (ALWAYS FIRST)\n\nBefore any design work, ANSWER THESE or ASK USER:\n\n| Constraint | Question | Why It Matters |\n|------------|----------|----------------|\n| **Timeline** | How much time? | Determines complexity |\n| **Content** | Ready or placeholder? | Affects layout flexibility |\n| **Brand** | Existing guidelines? | May dictate colors/fonts |\n| **Tech** | What stack? | Affects capabilities |\n| **Audience** | Who exactly? | Drives all visual decisions |\n\n### Audience → Design Approach\n\n| Audience | Think About |\n|----------|-------------|\n| **Gen Z** | Bold, fast, mobile-first, authentic |\n| **Millennials** | Clean, minimal, value-driven |\n| **Gen X** | Familiar, trustworthy, clear |\n| **Boomers** | Readable, high contrast, simple |\n| **B2B** | Professional, data-focused, trust |\n| **Luxury** | Restrained elegance, whitespace |\n\n---\n\n## 2. UX Psychology Principles\n\n### Core Laws (Internalize These)\n\n| Law | Principle | Application |\n|-----|-----------|-------------|\n| **Hick''s Law** | More choices = slower decisions | Limit options, use progressive disclosure |\n| **Fitts'' Law** | Bigger + closer = easier to click | Size CTAs appropriately |\n| **Miller''s Law** | ~7 items in working memory | Chunk content into groups |\n| **Von Restorff** | Different = memorable | Make CTAs visually distinct |\n| **Serial Position** | First/last remembered most | Key info at start/end |\n\n### Emotional Design Levels\n\n```\nVISCERAL (instant)  → First impression: colors, imagery, overall feel\nBEHAVIORAL (use)    → Using it: speed, feedback, efficiency\nREFLECTIVE (memory) → After: \"I like what this says about me\"\n```\n\n### Trust Building\n\n- Security indicators on sensitive actions\n- Social proof where relevant\n- Clear contact/support access\n- Consistent, professional design\n- Transparent policies\n\n---\n\n## 3. Layout Principles\n\n### Golden Ratio (φ = 1.618)\n\n```\nUse for proportional harmony:\n├── Content : Sidebar = roughly 62% : 38%\n├── Each heading size = previous × 1.618 (for dramatic scale)\n├── Spacing can follow: sm → md → lg (each × 1.618)\n```\n\n### 8-Point Grid Concept\n\n```\nAll spacing and sizing in multiples of 8:\n├── Tight: 4px (half-step for micro)\n├── Small: 8px\n├── Medium: 16px\n├── Large: 24px, 32px\n├── XL: 48px, 64px, 80px\n└── Adjust based on content density\n```\n\n### Key Sizing Principles\n\n| Element | Consideration |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **Touch targets** | Minimum comfortable tap size |\n| **Buttons** | Height based on importance hierarchy |\n| **Inputs** | Match button height for alignment |\n| **Cards** | Consistent padding, breathable |\n| **Reading width** | 45-75 characters optimal |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Color Principles\n\n### 60-30-10 Rule\n\n```\n60% → Primary/Background (calm, neutral base)\n30% → Secondary (supporting areas)\n10% → Accent (CTAs, highlights, attention)\n```\n\n### Color Psychology (For Decision Making)\n\n| If You Need... | Consider Hues | Avoid |\n|----------------|---------------|-------|\n| Trust, calm | Blue family | Aggressive reds |\n| Growth, nature | Green family | Industrial grays |\n| Energy, urgency | Orange, red | Passive blues |\n| Luxury, creativity | Deep Teal, Gold, Emerald | Cheap-feeling brights |\n| Clean, minimal | Neutrals | Overwhelming color |\n\n### Selection Process\n\n1. **What''s the industry?** (narrows options)\n2. **What''s the emotion?** (picks primary)\n3. **Light or dark mode?** (sets foundation)\n4. **ASK USER** if not specified\n\nFor detailed color theory: [color-system.md](color-system.md)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Typography Principles\n\n### Scale Selection\n\n| Content Type | Scale Ratio | Feel |\n|--------------|-------------|------|\n| Dense UI | 1.125-1.2 | Compact, efficient |\n| General web | 1.25 | Balanced (most common) |\n| Editorial | 1.333 | Readable, spacious |\n| Hero/display | 1.5-1.618 | Dramatic impact |\n\n### Pairing Concept\n\n```\nContrast + Harmony:\n├── DIFFERENT enough for hierarchy\n├── SIMILAR enough for cohesion\n└── Usually: display + neutral, or serif + sans\n```\n\n### Readability Rules\n\n- **Line length**: 45-75 characters optimal\n- **Line height**: 1.4-1.6 for body text\n- **Contrast**: Check WCAG requirements\n- **Size**: 16px+ for body on web\n\nFor detailed typography: [typography-system.md](typography-system.md)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Visual Effects Principles\n\n### Glassmorphism (When Appropriate)\n\n```\nKey properties:\n├── Semi-transparent background\n├── Backdrop blur\n├── Subtle border for definition\n└── ⚠️ **WARNING:** Standard blue/white glassmorphism is a modern cliché. Use it radically or not at all.\n```\n\n### Shadow Hierarchy\n\n```\nElevation concept:\n├── Higher elements = larger shadows\n├── Y-offset > X-offset (light from above)\n├── Multiple layers = more realistic\n└── Dark mode: may need glow instead\n```\n\n### Gradient Usage\n\n```\nHarmonious gradients:\n├── Adjacent colors on wheel (analogous)\n├── OR same hue, different lightness\n├── Avoid harsh complementary pairs\n├── 🚫 **NO Mesh/Aurora Gradients** (floating blobs)\n└── VARY from project to project radically\n```\n\nFor complete effects guide: [visual-effects.md](visual-effects.md)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Animation Principles\n\n### Timing Concept\n\n```\nDuration based on:\n├── Distance (further = longer)\n├── Size (larger = slower)\n├── Importance (critical = clear)\n└── Context (urgent = fast, luxury = slow)\n```\n\n### Easing Selection\n\n| Action | Easing | Why |\n|--------|--------|-----|\n| Entering | Ease-out | Decelerate, settle in |\n| Leaving | Ease-in | Accelerate, exit |\n| Emphasis | Ease-in-out | Smooth, deliberate |\n| Playful | Bounce | Fun, energetic |\n\n### Performance\n\n- Animate only transform and opacity\n- Respect reduced-motion preference\n- Test on low-end devices\n\nFor animation patterns: [animation-guide.md](animation-guide.md), for advanced: [motion-graphics.md](motion-graphics.md)\n\n---\n\n## 8. \"Wow Factor\" Checklist\n\n### Premium Indicators\n\n- [ ] Generous whitespace (luxury = breathing room)\n- [ ] Subtle depth and dimension\n- [ ] Smooth, purposeful animations\n- [ ] Attention to detail (alignment, consistency)\n- [ ] Cohesive visual rhythm\n- [ ] Custom elements (not all defaults)\n\n### Trust Builders\n\n- [ ] Security cues where appropriate\n- [ ] Social proof / testimonials\n- [ ] Clear value proposition\n- [ ] Professional imagery\n- [ ] Consistent design language\n\n### Emotional Triggers\n\n- [ ] Hero that evokes intended emotion\n- [ ] Human elements (faces, stories)\n- [ ] Progress/achievement indicators\n- [ ] Moments of delight\n\n---\n\n## 9. Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n### ❌ Lazy Design Indicators\n\n- Default system fonts without consideration\n- Stock imagery that doesn''t match\n- Inconsistent spacing\n- Too many competing colors\n- Walls of text without hierarchy\n- Inaccessible contrast\n\n### ❌ AI Tendency Patterns (AVOID!)\n\n- **Same colors every project**\n- **Dark + neon as default**\n- **Purple/violet everything (PURPLE BAN ✅)**\n- **Bento grids for simple landing pages**\n- **Mesh Gradients & Glow Effects**\n- **Same layout structure / Vercel clone**\n- **Not asking user preferences**\n\n### ❌ Dark Patterns (Unethical)\n\n- Hidden costs\n- Fake urgency\n- Forced actions\n- Deceptive UI\n- Confirmshaming\n\n---\n\n## 10. Decision Process Summary\n\n```\nFor EVERY design task:\n\n1. CONSTRAINTS\n   └── What''s the timeline, brand, tech, audience?\n   └── If unclear → ASK\n\n2. CONTENT\n   └── What content exists?\n   └── What''s the hierarchy?\n\n3. STYLE DIRECTION\n   └── What''s appropriate for context?\n   └── If unclear → ASK (don''t default!)\n\n4. EXECUTION\n   └── Apply principles above\n   └── Check against anti-patterns\n\n5. REVIEW\n   └── \"Does this serve the user?\"\n   └── \"Is this different from my defaults?\"\n   └── \"Would I be proud of this?\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Reference Files\n\nFor deeper guidance on specific areas:\n\n- [color-system.md](color-system.md) - Color theory and selection process\n- [typography-system.md](typography-system.md) - Font pairing and scale decisions\n- [visual-effects.md](visual-effects.md) - Effects principles and techniques\n- [animation-guide.md](animation-guide.md) - Motion design principles\n- [motion-graphics.md](motion-graphics.md) - Advanced: Lottie, GSAP, SVG, 3D, Particles\n- [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) - Context-specific templates\n- [ux-psychology.md](ux-psychology.md) - User psychology deep dive\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| Skill | When to Use |\n|-------|-------------|\n| **frontend-design** (this) | Before coding - Learn design principles (color, typography, UX psychology) |\n| **[web-design-guidelines](../web-design-guidelines/SKILL.md)** | After coding - Audit for accessibility, performance, and best practices |\n\n## Post-Design Workflow\n\nAfter implementing your design, run the audit:\n\n```\n1. DESIGN   → Read frontend-design principles ← YOU ARE HERE\n2. CODE     → Implement the design\n3. AUDIT    → Run web-design-guidelines review\n4. FIX      → Address findings from audit\n```\n\n> **Next Step:** After coding, use `web-design-guidelines` skill to audit your implementation for accessibility, focus states, animations, and performance issues.\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Design is THINKING, not copying. Every project deserves fresh consideration based on its unique context and users. **Avoid the Modern SaaS Safe Harbor!**\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:05:19.231Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for IDE Integration Agents that specialize in converting complex configuration formats between development environments.","zh":"非常适合专门在不同开发环境之间转换复杂配置格式的IDE集成代理。","ja":"開発環境間での複雑な設定形式の変換を専門とするIDE統合エージェントに最適です。","ko":"개발 환경 간에 복잡한 구성 형식을 변환하는 데 특화된 IDE 통합 에이전트에 완벽하게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Integración de IDE que se especializan en convertir formatos de configuración complejos entre entornos de desarrollo.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''intégration de l''IDE qui se spécialisent dans la conversion de formats de configuration complexes entre environnements de développement.","de":"Perfekt für IDE-Integration Agents, die sich auf die Konvertierung komplexer Konfigurationsformate zwischen Entwicklungsumgebungen spezialisieren.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de integração de IDE que se especializam em converter formatos de configuração complexos entre ambientes de desenvolvimento.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов интеграции IDE, которые специализируются на преобразовании сложных форматов конфигурации между средами разработки.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تكامل بيئة التطوير المتكامل الذين ي专ون في تحويل تنسيقات التكوين المعقدة بين بيئات التطوير."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables seamless conversion of Antigravity IDE configurations to formats compatible with modern development tools including GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Kiro CLI, and OpenCode. Provides structured output optimized for both visual IDEs and command-line interfaces.","zh":"支持将Antigravity IDE配置无缝转换为兼容现代开发工具（包括GitHub Copilot、Cursor、Kiro CLI和OpenCode）的格式。提供针对可视化IDE和命令行界面优化的结构化输出。","ja":"Antigravity IDEの設定をGitHub Copilot、Cursor、Kiro CLI、OpenCodeなどの最新開発ツールと互換性のある形式にシームレスに変換できます。視覚的IDEとコマンドラインインターフェースの両方に最適化された構造化された出力を提供します。","ko":"GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Kiro CLI, OpenCode를 포함한 현대 개발 도구와 호환되는 형식으로 Antigravity IDE 구성을 원활하게 변환할 수 있습니다. 시각적 IDE와 명령줄 인터페이스 모두에 최적화된 구조화된 출력을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite la conversión sin problemas de configuraciones de Antigravity IDE a formatos compatibles con herramientas de desarrollo modernas, incluyendo GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Kiro CLI y OpenCode. Proporciona una salida estructurada optimizada tanto para IDE visuales como para interfaces de línea de comandos.","fr":"Permet la conversion transparente des configurations Antigravity IDE dans des formats compatibles avec les outils de développement modernes, notamment GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Kiro CLI et OpenCode. Fournit une sortie structurée optimisée à la fois pour les IDE visuels et les interfaces de ligne de commande.","de":"Ermöglicht eine nahtlose Konvertierung von Antigravity-IDE-Konfigurationen in Formate, die mit modernen Entwicklungstools wie GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Kiro CLI und OpenCode kompatibel sind. Bietet eine strukturierte Ausgabe, die sowohl für visuelle IDE als auch für Befehlszeilenoberflächen optimiert ist.","pt":"Permite a conversão sem interrupções das configurações do Antigravity IDE para formatos compatíveis com ferramentas de desenvolvimento modernas, incluindo GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Kiro CLI e OpenCode. Fornece saída estruturada otimizada para IDEs visuais e interfaces de linha de comando.","ru":"Позволяет осуществлять бесшовное преобразование конфигураций Antigravity IDE в форматы, совместимые с современными инструментами разработки, включая GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Kiro CLI и OpenCode. Предоставляет структурированный вывод, оптимизированный для визуальных IDE и интерфейсов командной строки.","ar":"يمكّن تحويل إعدادات Antigravity IDE بشكل متواصل إلى تنسيقات متوافقة مع أدوات التطوير الحديثة بما في ذلك GitHub Copilot و Cursor و Kiro CLI و OpenCode. يوفر إخراجًا منظمًا محسّنًا لبيئات التطوير البصرية وواجهات سطر الأوامر."},"useCases":{"en":["Converting Antigravity workflows to Cursor-compatible formats","Generating CLI configuration files for Kiro and OpenCode","Translating skill configurations for GitHub Copilot integration","Automating IDE configuration migration between platforms"],"zh":["将Antigravity工作流转换为Cursor兼容格式","为Kiro和OpenCode生成CLI配置文件","为GitHub Copilot集成转换技能配置","实现平台间IDE配置迁移自动化"],"ja":["AntigravityワークフローのCursor互換形式への変換","KiroおよびOpenCode用CLI設定ファイルの生成","GitHub Copilot統合のためのスキル設定の変換","プラットフォーム間でのIDE設定移行の自動化"],"ko":["Antigravity 워크플로를 Cursor 호환 형식으로 변환","Kiro 및 OpenCode용 CLI 구성 파일 생성","GitHub Copilot 통합을 위한 기술 구성 변환","플랫폼 간 IDE 구성 마이그레이션 자동화"],"es":["Conversión de flujos de trabajo de Antigravity a formatos compatibles con Cursor","Generación de archivos de configuración de CLI para Kiro y OpenCode","Traducción de configuraciones de habilidades para la integración con GitHub Copilot","Automatización de la migración de configuraciones de IDE entre plataformas"],"fr":["Conversion de flux de travail Antigravity en formats compatibles avec Cursor","Génération de fichiers de configuration de CLI pour Kiro et OpenCode","Traduction de configurations de compétences pour l''intégration avec GitHub Copilot","Automatisation de la migration de configurations d''IDE entre plateformes"],"de":["Konvertierung von Antigravity-Workflows in Cursor-kompatible Formate","Erzeugung von CLI-Konfigurationsdateien für Kiro und OpenCode","Übersetzung von Skill-Konfigurationen für die Integration mit GitHub Copilot","Automatisierung der Migration von IDE-Konfigurationen zwischen Plattformen"],"pt":["Conversão de fluxos de trabalho do Antigravity para formatos compatíveis com o Cursor","Geração de arquivos de configuração de CLI para Kiro e OpenCode","Tradução de configurações de habilidades para integração com o GitHub Copilot","Automatização da migração de configuração de IDE entre plataformas"],"ru":["Преобразование рабочих процессов Antigravity в форматы, совместимые с Cursor","Генерация файлов конфигурации CLI для Kiro и OpenCode","Перевод конфигураций навыков для интеграции с GitHub Copilot","Автоматизация миграции конфигурации IDE между платформами"],"ar":["تحويل سير عمل Antigravity إلى تنسيقات متوافقة مع Cursor","توليد ملفات تكوين سطر الأوامر للكيرو و OpenCode","ترجمة إعدادات المهارات لتكامل GitHub Copilot","تأتمتة هجرة تكوين بيئة التطوير بين المنصات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Antigravity IDE configuration files as input","Limited to supported target IDEs and CLIs","Must follow Selective Reading Rule prioritizing ux-psychology.md"],"zh":["需要Antigravity IDE配置文件作为输入","仅限于支持的目标IDE和CLI","必须遵循优先处理ux-psychology.md的选择性读取规则"],"ja":["入力としてAntigravity IDE設定ファイルが必要","サポート対象のターゲットIDEおよびCLIに限定","ux-psychology.mdを優先する選択的読み取りルールに従う必要がある"],"ko":["Antigravity IDE 구성 파일을 입력으로 필요로 함","지원되는 대상 IDE 및 CLI로만 제한됨","ux-psychology.md를 우선하는 선택적 읽기 규칙을 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere archivos de configuración de Antigravity IDE como entrada","Limitado a IDE y CLI de destino compatibles","Debe seguir la Regla de Lectura Selectiva que prioriza ux-psychology.md"],"fr":["Nécessite des fichiers de configuration Antigravity IDE comme entrée","Limité aux IDE et CLI de destination pris en charge","Doit suivre la Règle de Lecture Sélective qui donne la priorité à ux-psychology.md"],"de":["Benötigt Antigravity-IDE-Konfigurationsdateien als Eingabe","Begrenzt auf unterstützte Ziel-IDE und CLI","Muss der Regel der selektiven Lektüre folgen, die ux-psychology.md priorisiert"],"pt":["Exige arquivos de configuração do Antigravity IDE como entrada","Limitado a IDEs e CLIs de destino suportados","Deve seguir a Regra de Leitura Seletiva priorizando ux-psychology.md"],"ru":["Требует файлов конфигурации Antigravity IDE в качестве входных данных","Ограничен поддерживаемыми целевыми IDE и CLI","Должен следовать Правилу выбора чтения, отдающего приоритет ux-psychology.md"],"ar":["يتطلب ملفات تكوين Antigravity IDE كمدخلات","محدود بالبيئات وواجهات سطر الأوامر الموجهة المدعومة","يجب اتباع قاعدة القراءة الانتقائية مع ưu tiên ux-psychology.md"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
