ct组件的技术，提供编译时保证和自信的重构","ja":"React TypeScriptは型安全なReactコンポーネントを構築するための技術であり、コンパイル時保証と自信を持ってリファクタリングを行うことができます","ko":"React TypeScript는 타입 안전한 React 컴포넌트를 구축하기 위한 기술로 컴파일 타임 보장과 안심하고 리팩토링할 수 있습니다","es":"React con TypeScript ofrece garantías de seguridad en tiempo de compilación para un refactoring confiable. Aprende a crear componentes de React con tipos seg...","fr":"React avec TypeScript offre des garanties de sécurité au moment de la compilation pour un refactoring fiable. Apprenez à créer des composants React avec des ...","de":"React mit TypeScript bietet Sicherheitsgarantien zur Kompilierungszeit für ein zuverlässiges Refactoring. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie React-Komponenten mit sichere...","pt":"React Dev é uma habilidade que permite criar componentes React com TypeScript, fornecendo garantias de tempo de compilação para refatoração confiante","ru":"React Dev — это навык, который позволяет создавать компоненты React с помощью TypeScript, обеспечивая гарантии компиляции для уверенного рефакторинга","ar":"رياكت ديف هو مهارة تسمح بإنشاء مكونات رياكت باستخدام تايب سكريبت، وتوفر ضمانات وقت الترجمة للتعديل الموثوق","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["类型安全的React组件","编译时保证","自信的重构","支持React 19特性","路由器集成","自定义hook"],"ja":["型安全のReactコンポーネント","コンパイル時保証","自信を持ってリファクタリング","React 19特性のサポート","ルーター統合","カスタムhook"],"ko":["타입 안전한 React 컴포넌트","컴파일 타임 보장","안심하고 리팩토링","React 19 기능 지원","라우터 통합","커스텀 hook"],"es":["Componentes de React con tipos seguros","Implementación de componentes genéricos","Tipado de controladores de eventos y formularios","Uso de características de React 19","Integración con enrutadores como TanStack Router y React Router","Creación de ganchos personalizados con tipado adecuado"],"fr":["Composants React avec des types sécurisés","Implémentation de composants génériques","Typage de gestionnaires d''événements et de formulaires","Utilisation des fonctionnalités de React 19","Intégration avec des routeurs tels que TanStack Router et React Router","Création de crochets personnalisés avec un typage approprié"],"de":["React-Komponenten mit sicheren Typen","Implementierung von generischen Komponenten","Typisierung von Ereignishandlern und Formularen","Verwendung von React-19-Funktionen","Integration mit Routern wie TanStack Router und React Router","Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Hooks mit geeigneten Typen"],"pt":["Criação de componentes React com TypeScript","Implementação de componentes genéricos","Tipagem de manipuladores de eventos, formulários e referências","Uso de recursos do React 19","Integração com roteadores como TanStack Router e React Router","Criação de hooks personalizados com tipagem adequada"],"ru":["Создание компонентов React с помощью TypeScript","Реализация генерических компонентов","Типизация обработчиков событий, форм и ссылок","Использование функций React 19","Интеграция с маршрутизаторами, такими как TanStack Router и React Router","Создание пользовательских хуков с правильной типизацией"],"ar":["إنشاء مكونات رياكت باستخدام تايب سكريبت","تنفيذ مكونات عامة","تحديد tipos لمنشئي الأحداث والاستمارات والمراجع","استخدام ميزات رياكت 19","التكامل مع الموجهات مثل TanStack Router ورياكت روتر","إنشاء hooks مخصصة مع تحديد tipos مناسب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["React TypeScript","类型安全","编译时保证","React 19","路由器集成","自定义hook","React开发","TypeScript"],"ja":["React TypeScript","型安全","コンパイル時保証","React 19","ルーター統合","カスタムhook","React開発","TypeScript"],"ko":["React TypeScript","타입 안전","컴파일 타임 보장","React 19","라우터 통합","커스텀 hook","React 개발","TypeScript"],"es":["React con TypeScript","Desarrollo de React","TypeScript para React","Componentes de React seguros","React 19 características","Integración de enrutadores en React","Creación de ganchos personalizados en React","Tipado de eventos en React","Formularios en React con TypeScript"],"fr":["React avec TypeScript","Développement React","TypeScript pour React","Composants React sécurisés","Fonctionnalités de React 19","Intégration de routeurs dans React","Création de crochets personnalisés dans React","Typage d''événements dans React","Formulaires dans React avec TypeScript"],"de":["React mit TypeScript","React-Entwicklung","TypeScript für React","Sichere React-Komponenten","React-19-Funktionen","Integration von Routern in React","Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Hooks in React","Typisierung von Ereignissen in React","Formulare in React mit TypeScript"],"pt":["React Dev","TypeScript para React","Desenvolvimento de componentes React","Tipagem de componentes React","React 19","TanStack Router","React Router","Hooks personalizados"],"ru":["React Dev","TypeScript для React","Разработка компонентов React","Типизация компонентов React","React 19","TanStack Router","React Router","Пользовательские хуки"],"ar":["رياكت ديف","تايب سكريبت لرياكت","تطوير مكونات رياكت","تحديد tipos لمكونات رياكت","رياكت 19","TanStack Router","رياكت روتر","hooks مخصصة"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"react-dev","description":"This skill should be used when building React components with TypeScript, typing hooks, handling events, or when React TypeScript, React 19, Server Components are mentioned. Covers type-safe patterns for React 18-19 including generic components, proper event typing, and routing integration (TanStack Router, React Router).","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# React TypeScript\n\nType-safe React = compile-time guarantees = confident refactoring.\n\n<when_to_use>\n\n- Building typed React components\n- Implementing generic components\n- Typing event handlers, forms, refs\n- Using React 19 features (Actions, Server Components, use())\n- Router integration (TanStack Router, React Router)\n- Custom hooks with proper typing\n\nNOT for: non-React TypeScript, vanilla JS React\n\n</when_to_use>\n\n<react_19_changes>\n\nReact 19 breaking changes require migration. Key patterns","body":"# React TypeScript\n\nType-safe React = compile-time guarantees = confident refactoring.\n\n<when_to_use>\n\n- Building typed React components\n- Implementing generic components\n- Typing event handlers, forms, refs\n- Using React 19 features (Actions, Server Components, use())\n- Router integration (TanStack Router, React Router)\n- Custom hooks with proper typing\n\nNOT for: non-React TypeScript, vanilla JS React\n\n</when_to_use>\n\n<react_19_changes>\n\nReact 19 breaking changes require migration. Key patterns:\n\n**ref as prop** - forwardRef deprecated:\n\n```typescript\n// React 19 - ref as regular prop\ntype ButtonProps = {\n  ref?: React.Ref<HTMLButtonElement>;\n} & React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<''button''>;\n\nfunction Button({ ref, children, ...props }: ButtonProps) {\n  return <button ref={ref} {...props}>{children}</button>;\n}\n```\n\n**useActionState** - replaces useFormState:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useActionState } from ''react'';\n\ntype FormState = { errors?: string[]; success?: boolean };\n\nfunction Form() {\n  const [state, formAction, isPending] = useActionState(submitAction, {});\n  return <form action={formAction}>...</form>;\n}\n```\n\n**use()** - unwraps promises/context:\n\n```typescript\nfunction UserProfile({ userPromise }: { userPromise: Promise<User> }) {\n  const user = use(userPromise); // Suspends until resolved\n  return <div>{user.name}</div>;\n}\n```\n\nSee [react-19-patterns.md](references/react-19-patterns.md) for useOptimistic, useTransition, migration checklist.\n\n</react_19_changes>\n\n<component_patterns>\n\n**Props** - extend native elements:\n\n```typescript\ntype ButtonProps = {\n  variant: ''primary'' | ''secondary'';\n} & React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<''button''>;\n\nfunction Button({ variant, children, ...props }: ButtonProps) {\n  return <button className={variant} {...props}>{children}</button>;\n}\n```\n\n**Children typing**:\n\n```typescript\ntype Props = {\n  children: React.ReactNode;          // Anything renderable\n  icon: React.ReactElement;           // Single element\n  render: (data: T) => React.ReactNode;  // Render prop\n};\n```\n\n**Discriminated unions** for variant props:\n\n```typescript\ntype ButtonProps =\n  | { variant: ''link''; href: string }\n  | { variant: ''button''; onClick: () => void };\n\nfunction Button(props: ButtonProps) {\n  if (props.variant === ''link'') {\n    return <a href={props.href}>Link</a>;\n  }\n  return <button onClick={props.onClick}>Button</button>;\n}\n```\n\n</component_patterns>\n\n<event_handlers>\n\nUse specific event types for accurate target typing:\n\n```typescript\n// Mouse\nfunction handleClick(e: React.MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) {\n  e.currentTarget.disabled = true;\n}\n\n// Form\nfunction handleSubmit(e: React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>) {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  const formData = new FormData(e.currentTarget);\n}\n\n// Input\nfunction handleChange(e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) {\n  console.log(e.target.value);\n}\n\n// Keyboard\nfunction handleKeyDown(e: React.KeyboardEvent<HTMLInputElement>) {\n  if (e.key === ''Enter'') e.currentTarget.blur();\n}\n```\n\nSee [event-handlers.md](references/event-handlers.md) for focus, drag, clipboard, touch, wheel events.\n\n</event_handlers>\n\n<hooks_typing>\n\n**useState** - explicit for unions/null:\n\n```typescript\nconst [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\nconst [status, setStatus] = useState<''idle'' | ''loading''>(''idle'');\n```\n\n**useRef** - null for DOM, value for mutable:\n\n```typescript\nconst inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);  // DOM - use ?.\nconst countRef = useRef<number>(0);               // Mutable - direct access\n```\n\n**useReducer** - discriminated unions for actions:\n\n```typescript\ntype Action =\n  | { type: ''increment'' }\n  | { type: ''set''; payload: number };\n\nfunction reducer(state: State, action: Action): State {\n  switch (action.type) {\n    case ''set'': return { ...state, count: action.payload };\n    default: return state;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Custom hooks** - tuple returns with as const:\n\n```typescript\nfunction useToggle(initial = false) {\n  const [value, setValue] = useState(initial);\n  const toggle = () => setValue(v => !v);\n  return [value, toggle] as const;\n}\n```\n\n**useContext** - null guard pattern:\n\n```typescript\nconst UserContext = createContext<User | null>(null);\n\nfunction useUser() {\n  const user = useContext(UserContext);\n  if (!user) throw new Error(''useUser outside UserProvider'');\n  return user;\n}\n```\n\nSee [hooks.md](references/hooks.md) for useCallback, useMemo, useImperativeHandle, useSyncExternalStore.\n\n</hooks_typing>\n\n<generic_components>\n\nGeneric components infer types from props - no manual annotations at call site.\n\n**Pattern** - keyof T for column keys, render props for custom rendering:\n\n```typescript\ntype Column<T> = {\n  key: keyof T;\n  header: string;\n  render?: (value: T[keyof T], item: T) => React.ReactNode;\n};\n\ntype TableProps<T> = {\n  data: T[];\n  columns: Column<T>[];\n  keyExtractor: (item: T) => string | number;\n};\n\nfunction Table<T>({ data, columns, keyExtractor }: TableProps<T>) {\n  return (\n    <table>\n      <thead>\n        <tr>{columns.map(col => <th key={String(col.key)}>{col.header}</th>)}</tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        {data.map(item => (\n          <tr key={keyExtractor(item)}>\n            {columns.map(col => (\n              <td key={String(col.key)}>\n                {col.render ? col.render(item[col.key], item) : String(item[col.key])}\n              </td>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Constrained generics** for required properties:\n\n```typescript\ntype HasId = { id: string | number };\n\nfunction List<T extends HasId>({ items }: { items: T[] }) {\n  return <ul>{items.map(item => <li key={item.id}>...</li>)}</ul>;\n}\n```\n\nSee [generic-components.md](examples/generic-components.md) for Select, List, Modal, FormField patterns.\n\n</generic_components>\n\n<server_components>\n\nReact 19 Server Components run on server, can be async.\n\n**Async data fetching**:\n\n```typescript\nexport default async function UserPage({ params }: { params: { id: string } }) {\n  const user = await fetchUser(params.id);\n  return <div>{user.name}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n**Server Actions** - ''use server'' for mutations:\n\n```typescript\n''use server'';\n\nexport async function updateUser(userId: string, formData: FormData) {\n  await db.user.update({ where: { id: userId }, data: { ... } });\n  revalidatePath(`/users/${userId}`);\n}\n```\n\n**Client + Server Action**:\n\n```typescript\n''use client'';\n\nimport { useActionState } from ''react'';\nimport { updateUser } from ''@/actions/user'';\n\nfunction UserForm({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const [state, formAction, isPending] = useActionState(\n    (prev, formData) => updateUser(userId, formData), {}\n  );\n  return <form action={formAction}>...</form>;\n}\n```\n\n**use() for promise handoff**:\n\n```typescript\n// Server: pass promise without await\nasync function Page() {\n  const userPromise = fetchUser(''123'');\n  return <UserProfile userPromise={userPromise} />;\n}\n\n// Client: unwrap with use()\n''use client'';\nfunction UserProfile({ userPromise }: { userPromise: Promise<User> }) {\n  const user = use(userPromise);\n  return <div>{user.name}</div>;\n}\n```\n\nSee [server-components.md](examples/server-components.md) for parallel fetching, streaming, error boundaries.\n\n</server_components>\n\n<routing>\n\nBoth TanStack Router and React Router v7 provide type-safe routing solutions.\n\n**TanStack Router** - Compile-time type safety with Zod validation:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createRoute } from ''@tanstack/react-router'';\nimport { z } from ''zod'';\n\nconst userRoute = createRoute({\n  path: ''/users/$userId'',\n  component: UserPage,\n  loader: async ({ params }) => ({ user: await fetchUser(params.userId) }),\n  validateSearch: z.object({\n    tab: z.enum([''profile'', ''settings'']).optional(),\n    page: z.number().int().positive().default(1),\n  }),\n});\n\nfunction UserPage() {\n  const { user } = useLoaderData({ from: userRoute.id });\n  const { tab, page } = useSearch({ from: userRoute.id });\n  const { userId } = useParams({ from: userRoute.id });\n}\n```\n\n**React Router v7** - Automatic type generation with Framework Mode:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { Route } from \"./+types/user\";\n\nexport async function loader({ params }: Route.LoaderArgs) {\n  return { user: await fetchUser(params.userId) };\n}\n\nexport default function UserPage({ loaderData }: Route.ComponentProps) {\n  const { user } = loaderData; // Typed from loader\n  return <h1>{user.name}</h1>;\n}\n```\n\nSee [tanstack-router.md](references/tanstack-router.md) for TanStack patterns and [react-router.md](references/react-router.md) for React Router patterns.\n\n</routing>\n\n<rules>\n\nALWAYS:\n- Specific event types (MouseEvent, ChangeEvent, etc)\n- Explicit useState for unions/null\n- ComponentPropsWithoutRef for native element extension\n- Discriminated unions for variant props\n- as const for tuple returns\n- ref as prop in React 19 (no forwardRef)\n- useActionState for form actions\n- Type-safe routing patterns (see routing section)\n\nNEVER:\n- any for event handlers\n- JSX.Element for children (use ReactNode)\n- forwardRef in React 19+\n- useFormState (deprecated)\n- Forget null handling for DOM refs\n- Mix Server/Client components in same file\n- Await promises when passing to use()\n\n</rules>\n\n<references>\n\n- [hooks.md](references/hooks.md) - useState, useRef, useReducer, useContext, custom hooks\n- [event-handlers.md](references/event-handlers.md) - all event types, generic handlers\n- [react-19-patterns.md](references/react-19-patterns.md) - useActionState, use(), useOptimistic, migration\n- [generic-components.md](examples/generic-components.md) - Table, Select, List, Modal patterns\n- [server-components.md](examples/server-components.md) - async components, Server Actions, streaming\n- [tanstack-router.md](references/tanstack-router.md) - TanStack Router typed routes, search params, navigation\n- [react-router.md](references/react-router.md) - React Router v7 loaders, actions, type generation, forms\n\n</references>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:05:59.268Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Development Agents requiring type-safe React component generation and modern framework integration.","zh":"非常适合需要类型安全的 React 组件生成和现代框架集成的前端开发智能体。","ja":"型安全なReactコンポーネント生成とモダンフレームワーク統合を必要とするフロントエンド開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"타입 안전한 React 컴포넌트 생성과 현대적 프레임워크 통합이 필요한 프론트엔드 개발 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo frontend que requieren generación de componentes de React seguros con tipos y una integración moderna de frameworks.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement frontend nécessitant une génération de composants React sécurisés par type et une intégration de framework moderne.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine typsichere Generierung von React-Komponenten und eine moderne Framework-Integration erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Frontend que exigem geração de componentes React seguros em termos de tipo e integração com frameworks modernos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов фронтенд-разработки, требующих генерации компонентов React с безопасностью типов и интеграции с современными фреймворками.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الأمامي الذي يتطلب إنشاء مكونات رياكت آمنة من النوع وتكامل الإطارات الحديثة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables compile-time type guarantees for React components, supporting React 19 features like Actions and Server Components while integrating with TanStack Router and React Router. Provides robust typing for event handlers, forms, refs, and custom hooks.","zh":"为 React 组件提供编译时类型保证，支持 Actions 和服务器组件等 React 19 功能，同时与 TanStack Router 和 React Router 集成。为事件处理程序、表单、引用和自定义钩子提供强大的类型支持。","ja":"Reactコンポーネントにコンパイル時の型保証を可能にし、ActionsやサーバーコンポーネントなどのReact 19機能をサポートしながら、TanStack RouterおよびReact Routerと統合します。イベントハンドラ、フォーム、ref、カスタムフックに対して堅牢な型付けを提供します。","ko":"React 컴포넌트에 컴파일 타임 타입 보장을 제공하며, Actions 및 서버 컴포넌트와 같은 React 19 기능을 지원하고 TanStack Router 및 React Router와 통합합니다. 이벤트 핸들러, 폼, ref, 커스텀 훅에 대한 강력한 타이핑을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita garantías de tipo en tiempo de compilación para componentes de React, compatible con características de React 19 como Acciones y Componentes de servidor, mientras se integra con TanStack Router y React Router. Proporciona una tipificación robusta para controladores de eventos, formularios, referencias y ganchos personalizados.","fr":"Permet des garanties de type à la compilation pour les composants React, prenant en charge les fonctionnalités React 19 telles que les Actions et les Composants de serveur, tout en s''intégrant à TanStack Router et React Router. Fournit une typage robuste pour les gestionnaires d''événements, les formulaires, les références et les crochets personnalisés.","de":"Ermöglicht Typgarantien zur Kompilierzeit für React-Komponenten, unterstützt React-19-Features wie Aktionen und Serverkomponenten, während es sich in TanStack Router und React Router integriert. Bietet eine robuste Typisierung für Ereignishandler, Formulare, Referenzen und benutzerdefinierte Haken.","pt":"Habilita garantias de tipo em tempo de compilação para componentes React, suportando recursos do React 19 como Ações e Componentes de Servidor, enquanto se integra com TanStack Router e React Router. Fornece digitação robusta para manipuladores de eventos, formulários, referências e ganchos personalizados.","ru":"Предоставляет гарантии типов во время компиляции для компонентов React, поддерживая функции React 19, такие как Действия и Компоненты сервера, а также интегрируется с TanStack Router и React Router. Предоставляет прочную типизацию для обработчиков событий, форм, ссылок и пользовательских крючков.","ar":"تمكّن من ضمانات время الترجمة للنوع لمكونات رياكت، مع دعم ميزات رياكت 19 مثل الإجراءات ومكونات الخادم، في حين يتكامل مع TanStack Router ورياكت روتر. يوفر كتابة قوية لمعالجين الأحداث والنماذج والمراجع والسنارات المخصصة."},"useCases":{"en":["Building typed React components with TypeScript","Implementing generic components with proper type constraints","Migrating codebases to React 19 with breaking changes","Integrating type-safe routing with TanStack Router","Creating custom hooks with complete type definitions"],"zh":["使用 TypeScript 构建类型化的 React 组件","使用适当的类型约束实现通用组件","将代码库迁移到具有重大变更的 React 19","与 TanStack Router 集成类型安全的路由","创建具有完整类型定义的自定义钩子"],"ja":["TypeScriptを使用した型付けされたReactコンポーネントの構築","適切な型制約を用いた汎用コンポーネントの実装","破壊的変更を伴うReact 19へのコードベースの移行","TanStack Routerを用いた型安全なルーティングの統合","完全な型定義を持つカスタムフックの作成"],"ko":["TypeScript로 타입이 지정된 React 컴포넌트 구축","적절한 타입 제약 조건으로 제네릭 컴포넌트 구현","주요 변경 사항이 있는 React 19로 코드베이스 마이그레이션","TanStack Router와 타입 안전한 라우팅 통합","완전한 타입 정의를 갖춘 커스텀 훅 생성"],"es":["Crear componentes de React con TypeScript tipados","Implementar componentes genéricos con restricciones de tipo adecuadas","Migrar bases de código a React 19 con cambios importantes","Integrar enrutamiento seguro con tipo con TanStack Router","Crear ganchos personalizados con definiciones de tipo completas"],"fr":["Construire des composants React typés avec TypeScript","Mettre en œuvre des composants génériques avec des contraintes de type appropriées","Migration de bases de code vers React 19 avec des changements importants","Intégrer un routage sécurisé par type avec TanStack Router","Créer des crochets personnalisés avec des définitions de type complètes"],"de":["Erstellen von typsicheren React-Komponenten mit TypeScript","Implementieren von generischen Komponenten mit geeigneten Typbeschränkungen","Migration von Codebasen zu React 19 mit brechenden Änderungen","Integrieren von typsicherer Routing mit TanStack Router","Erstellen von benutzerdefinierten Haken mit vollständigen Typdefinitionen"],"pt":["Construção de componentes React tipados com TypeScript","Implementação de componentes genéricos com restrições de tipo adequadas","Migração de código para React 19 com alterações de quebra","Integração de roteamento seguro em termos de tipo com TanStack Router","Criação de ganchos personalizados com definições de tipo completas"],"ru":["Создание типизированных компонентов React с помощью TypeScript","Реализация.generic компонентов с правильными ограничениями типов","Миграция кодовой базы на React 19 с изменениями, нарушающими совместимость","Интеграция типобезопасного маршрутизации с TanStack Router","Создание пользовательских крючков с полными определениями типов"],"ar":["بناء مكونات رياكت المُصنّفة مع TypeScript","تنفيذ مكونات جينيكة مع قيود نوعية مناسبة","هجرة قواعد الكود إلى رياكت 19 مع تغييرات كاسرة","تكامل التوجيه الآمن من النوع مع TanStack Router","إنشاء سنارات مخصصة مع تعريفات نوعية كاملة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for non-React TypeScript projects","Cannot be used with vanilla JavaScript React applications","Requires adaptation for React 19 breaking changes"],"zh":["不适用于非 React 的 TypeScript 项目","不能用于纯 JavaScript React 应用程序","需要适配 React 19 的重大变更"],"ja":["React非依存のTypeScriptプロジェクトには不向き","バニラJavaScriptのReactアプリケーションでは使用不可","React 19の破壊的変更への適応が必要"],"ko":["React가 아닌 TypeScript 프로젝트에는 적합하지 않음","순수 JavaScript React 애플리케이션에서는 사용할 수 없음","React 19의 주요 변경 사항에 대한 적응이 필요함"],"es":["No es adecuado para proyectos de TypeScript que no sean de React","No se puede utilizar con aplicaciones de React de JavaScript vanilla","Requiere adaptación para los cambios importantes de React 19"],"fr":["N''est pas adapté pour les projets TypeScript non React","Ne peut pas être utilisé avec des applications React JavaScript vanilla","Nécessite une adaptation pour les changements importants de React 19"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für nicht-React-TypeScript-Projekte","Kann nicht mit React-Anwendungen aus Vanilla-JavaScript verwendet werden","Erfordert eine Anpassung für die brechenden Änderungen von React 19"],"pt":["Não é adequado para projetos TypeScript que não sejam do React","Não pode ser usado com aplicativos React de JavaScript vanilla","Exige adaptação para alterações de quebra do React 19"],"ru":["Не подходит для проектов TypeScript, не являющихся React","Не может быть использовано с приложениями React на ванильном JavaScript","Требует адаптации для изменений, нарушающих совместимость, в React 19"],"ar":["لا يتناسب مع مشاريع TypeScript التي ليست من رياكت","لا يمكن استخدامه مع تطبيقات رياكت الجافا سكريبت الفانيليا","يتطلب التكيف مع التغييرات الكاسرة في رياكت 19"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/canvas-design', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'canvas-design', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z', '2026-02-18T14:06:40.957Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/canvas-design","name":"canvas-design","description":{"zh":"Canvas设计技能是一种创建视觉设计哲学并在Canvas上表达的技术，输出md、pdf和png文件","ja":"キャンバス デザイン スキルは、視覚的なデザイン哲学を作成してキャンバス上で表現する技術です。md、pdf、pngファイルを出力します","ko":"캔버스 디자인 기술은 캔버스에서 시각적 디자인 철학을 생성하고 표현하는 기술입니다. md, pdf, png 파일을 출력합니다","es":"El diseño de canvas es el proceso de crear filosofías visuales que se expresan a través de la forma, el espacio, el color y la composición.","fr":"La conception de canvas est le processus de création de philosophies visuelles qui s''expriment à travers la forme, l''espace, la couleur et la composition.","de":"Das Canvas-Design ist der Prozess der Erstellung visueller Philosophien, die durch Form, Raum, Farbe und Komposition ausgedrückt werden.","pt":"Crie filosofias de design visuais expressas por meio de form, espaço, cor e composição","ru":"Создавайте визуальные философии дизайна, выраженные через форму, пространство, цвет и композицию","ar":"إنشاء فلسفات التصميم البصرية المعبرة من خلال الشكل والفضاء واللون والتركيب","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Canvas 设计技能","ja":"キャンバス デザイン スキル","ko":"캔버스 디자인 기술","es":"Diseño de Canvas: Crea Filosofías Visuales","fr":"Conception de Canvas: Créez des Philosophies Visuelles","de":"Canvas-Design: Erstelle Visuelle Philosophien","pt":"Crie Filosofias de Design com Canvas","ru":"Создание философии дизайна с помощью Canvas","ar":"إنشاء فلسفة التصميم مع Canvas","en":"canvas-design"},"description":{"zh":"Canvas设计技能是一种创建视觉设计哲学并在Canvas上表达的技术，输出md、pdf和png文件","ja":"キャンバス デザイン スキルは、視覚的なデザイン哲学を作成してキャンバス上で表現する技術です。md、pdf、pngファイルを出力します","ko":"캔버스 디자인 기술은 캔버스에서 시각적 디자인 철학을 생성하고 표현하는 기술입니다. md, pdf, png 파일을 출력합니다","es":"El diseño de canvas es el proceso de crear filosofías visuales que se expresan a través de la forma, el espacio, el color y la composición.","fr":"La conception de canvas est le processus de création de philosophies visuelles qui s''expriment à travers la forme, l''espace, la couleur et la composition.","de":"Das Canvas-Design ist der Prozess der Erstellung visueller Philosophien, die durch Form, Raum, Farbe und Komposition ausgedrückt werden.","pt":"Crie filosofias de design visuais expressas por meio de form, espaço, cor e composição","ru":"Создавайте визуальные философии дизайна, выраженные через форму, пространство, цвет и композицию","ar":"إنشاء فلسفات التصميم البصرية المعبرة من خلال الشكل والفضاء واللون والتركيب","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["创建视觉设计哲学","在Canvas上表达设计哲学","输出md、pdf和png文件","使用Form、Space、Color、Composition等元素","使用Images和Graphics等媒体"],"ja":["視覚的なデザイン哲学を作成する","キャンバス上でデザイン哲学を表現する","md、pdf、pngファイルを出力する","Form、Space、Color、Compositionなどの要素を使用する","ImagesとGraphicsなどのメディアを使用する"],"ko":["시각적 디자인 철학을 생성한다","캔버스에서 디자인 철학을 표현한다","md, pdf, png 파일을 출력한다","Form, Space, Color, Composition 등 요소를 사용한다","Images와 Graphics 등 미디어를 사용한다"],"es":["Creación de filosofías visuales","Expresión de ideas en un canvas","Diseño de conceptos visuales","Uso de elementos visuales como forma, espacio, color y composición","Creación de archivos .md, .pdf y .png"],"fr":["Création de philosophies visuelles","Expression d''idées sur un canvas","Conception de concepts visuels","Utilisation d''éléments visuels tels que la forme, l''espace, la couleur et la composition","Création de fichiers .md, .pdf et .png"],"de":["Erstellung visueller Philosophien","Ausdruck von Ideen auf einem Canvas","Entwurf visueller Konzepte","Verwendung visueller Elemente wie Form, Raum, Farbe und Komposition","Erstellung von Dateien .md, .pdf und .png"],"pt":["Criação de filosofias de design visuais","Expressão de filosofias em um canvas","Uso de form, espaço, cor e composição","Saída em formato .md, .pdf e .png","Desenvolvimento em duas etapas"],"ru":["Создание визуальных философий дизайна","Выражение философий на холсте","Использование формы, пространства, цвета и композиции","Вывод в форматах .md, .pdf и .png","Разработка в два этапа"],"ar":["إنشاء فلسفات التصميم البصرية","التعبير عن الفلسفات على لوحة","استخدام الشكل والفضاء واللون والتركيب","الإخراج في صيغ .md و .pdf و .png","التطوير في مرحلتين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Canvas设计","视觉设计哲学","设计表达","md文件","pdf文件","png文件","Form","Space","Color","Composition"],"ja":["キャンバス デザイン","視覚的なデザイン哲学","デザイン表現","mdファイル","pdfファイル","pngファイル","Form","Space","Color","Composition"],"ko":["캔버스 디자인","시각적 디자인 철학","디자인 표현","md 파일","pdf 파일","png 파일","Form","Space","Color","Composition"],"es":["diseño de canvas","filosofías visuales","concepción de canvas","expresión de ideas","diseño visual","creación de conceptos visuales"],"fr":["conception de canvas","philosophies visuelles","création de canvas","expression d''idées","conception visuelle","création de concepts visuels"],"de":["Canvas-Design","visuelle Philosophien","Erstellung von Canvas","Ausdruck von Ideen","visuelle Konzeption","Erstellung visueller Konzepte"],"pt":["filosofia de design","canvas design","design visual","criação de design","desenvolvimento de design","ferramentas de design"],"ru":["философия дизайна","дизайн холста","визуальный дизайн","создание дизайна","разработка дизайна","инструменты дизайна"],"ar":["فلسفة التصميم","تصميم لوحة","تصميم بصري","إنشاء تصميم","تطوير تصميم","أدوات التصميم"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"canvas-design","description":"Create beautiful visual art in .png and .pdf documents using design philosophy. You should use this skill when the user asks to create a poster, piece of art, design, or other static piece. Create original visual designs, never copying existing artists work to avoid copyright violations.","bodyPreview":"These are instructions for creating design philosophies - aesthetic movements that are then EXPRESSED VISUALLY. Output only .md files, .pdf files, and .png files.\n\nComplete this in two steps:\n1. Design Philosophy Creation (.md file)\n2. Express by creating it on a canvas (.pdf file or .png file)\n\nFirst, undertake this task:\n\n## DESIGN PHILOSOPHY CREATION\n\nTo begin, create a VISUAL PHILOSOPHY (not layouts or templates) that will be interpreted through:\n- Form, space, color, composition\n- Images, g","body":"These are instructions for creating design philosophies - aesthetic movements that are then EXPRESSED VISUALLY. Output only .md files, .pdf files, and .png files.\n\nComplete this in two steps:\n1. Design Philosophy Creation (.md file)\n2. Express by creating it on a canvas (.pdf file or .png file)\n\nFirst, undertake this task:\n\n## DESIGN PHILOSOPHY CREATION\n\nTo begin, create a VISUAL PHILOSOPHY (not layouts or templates) that will be interpreted through:\n- Form, space, color, composition\n- Images, graphics, shapes, patterns\n- Minimal text as visual accent\n\n### THE CRITICAL UNDERSTANDING\n- What is received: Some subtle input or instructions by the user that should be taken into account, but used as a foundation; it should not constrain creative freedom.\n- What is created: A design philosophy/aesthetic movement.\n- What happens next: Then, the same version receives the philosophy and EXPRESSES IT VISUALLY - creating artifacts that are 90% visual design, 10% essential text.\n\nConsider this approach:\n- Write a manifesto for an art movement\n- The next phase involves making the artwork\n\nThe philosophy must emphasize: Visual expression. Spatial communication. Artistic interpretation. Minimal words.\n\n### HOW TO GENERATE A VISUAL PHILOSOPHY\n\n**Name the movement** (1-2 words): \"Brutalist Joy\" / \"Chromatic Silence\" / \"Metabolist Dreams\"\n\n**Articulate the philosophy** (4-6 paragraphs - concise but complete):\n\nTo capture the VISUAL essence, express how the philosophy manifests through:\n- Space and form\n- Color and material\n- Scale and rhythm\n- Composition and balance\n- Visual hierarchy\n\n**CRITICAL GUIDELINES:**\n- **Avoid redundancy**: Each design aspect should be mentioned once. Avoid repeating points about color theory, spatial relationships, or typographic principles unless adding new depth.\n- **Emphasize craftsmanship REPEATEDLY**: The philosophy MUST stress multiple times that the final work should appear as though it took countless hours to create, was labored over with care, and comes from someone at the absolute top of their field. This framing is essential - repeat phrases like \"meticulously crafted,\" \"the product of deep expertise,\" \"painstaking attention,\" \"master-level execution.\"\n- **Leave creative space**: Remain specific about the aesthetic direction, but concise enough that the next Claude has room to make interpretive choices also at a extremely high level of craftmanship.\n\nThe philosophy must guide the next version to express ideas VISUALLY, not through text. Information lives in design, not paragraphs.\n\n### PHILOSOPHY EXAMPLES\n\n**\"Concrete Poetry\"**\nPhilosophy: Communication through monumental form and bold geometry.\nVisual expression: Massive color blocks, sculptural typography (huge single words, tiny labels), Brutalist spatial divisions, Polish poster energy meets Le Corbusier. Ideas expressed through visual weight and spatial tension, not explanation. Text as rare, powerful gesture - never paragraphs, only essential words integrated into the visual architecture. Every element placed with the precision of a master craftsman.\n\n**\"Chromatic Language\"**\nPhilosophy: Color as the primary information system.\nVisual expression: Geometric precision where color zones create meaning. Typography minimal - small sans-serif labels letting chromatic fields communicate. Think Josef Albers'' interaction meets data visualization. Information encoded spatially and chromatically. Words only to anchor what color already shows. The result of painstaking chromatic calibration.\n\n**\"Analog Meditation\"**\nPhilosophy: Quiet visual contemplation through texture and breathing room.\nVisual expression: Paper grain, ink bleeds, vast negative space. Photography and illustration dominate. Typography whispered (small, restrained, serving the visual). Japanese photobook aesthetic. Images breathe across pages. Text appears sparingly - short phrases, never explanatory blocks. Each composition balanced with the care of a meditation practice.\n\n**\"Organic Systems\"**\nPhilosophy: Natural clustering and modular growth patterns.\nVisual expression: Rounded forms, organic arrangements, color from nature through architecture. Information shown through visual diagrams, spatial relationships, iconography. Text only for key labels floating in space. The composition tells the story through expert spatial orchestration.\n\n**\"Geometric Silence\"**\nPhilosophy: Pure order and restraint.\nVisual expression: Grid-based precision, bold photography or stark graphics, dramatic negative space. Typography precise but minimal - small essential text, large quiet zones. Swiss formalism meets Brutalist material honesty. Structure communicates, not words. Every alignment the work of countless refinements.\n\n*These are condensed examples. The actual design philosophy should be 4-6 substantial paragraphs.*\n\n### ESSENTIAL PRINCIPLES\n- **VISUAL PHILOSOPHY**: Create an aesthetic worldview to be expressed through design\n- **MINIMAL TEXT**: Always emphasize that text is sparse, essential-only, integrated as visual element - never lengthy\n- **SPATIAL EXPRESSION**: Ideas communicate through space, form, color, composition - not paragraphs\n- **ARTISTIC FREEDOM**: The next Claude interprets the philosophy visually - provide creative room\n- **PURE DESIGN**: This is about making ART OBJECTS, not documents with decoration\n- **EXPERT CRAFTSMANSHIP**: Repeatedly emphasize the final work must look meticulously crafted, labored over with care, the product of countless hours by someone at the top of their field\n\n**The design philosophy should be 4-6 paragraphs long.** Fill it with poetic design philosophy that brings together the core vision. Avoid repeating the same points. Keep the design philosophy generic without mentioning the intention of the art, as if it can be used wherever. Output the design philosophy as a .md file.\n\n---\n\n## DEDUCING THE SUBTLE REFERENCE\n\n**CRITICAL STEP**: Before creating the canvas, identify the subtle conceptual thread from the original request.\n\n**THE ESSENTIAL PRINCIPLE**:\nThe topic is a **subtle, niche reference embedded within the art itself** - not always literal, always sophisticated. Someone familiar with the subject should feel it intuitively, while others simply experience a masterful abstract composition. The design philosophy provides the aesthetic language. The deduced topic provides the soul - the quiet conceptual DNA woven invisibly into form, color, and composition.\n\nThis is **VERY IMPORTANT**: The reference must be refined so it enhances the work''s depth without announcing itself. Think like a jazz musician quoting another song - only those who know will catch it, but everyone appreciates the music.\n\n---\n\n## CANVAS CREATION\n\nWith both the philosophy and the conceptual framework established, express it on a canvas. Take a moment to gather thoughts and clear the mind. Use the design philosophy created and the instructions below to craft a masterpiece, embodying all aspects of the philosophy with expert craftsmanship.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: For any type of content, even if the user requests something for a movie/game/book, the approach should still be sophisticated. Never lose sight of the idea that this should be art, not something that''s cartoony or amateur.\n\nTo create museum or magazine quality work, use the design philosophy as the foundation. Create one single page, highly visual, design-forward PDF or PNG output (unless asked for more pages). Generally use repeating patterns and perfect shapes. Treat the abstract philosophical design as if it were a scientific bible, borrowing the visual language of systematic observation—dense accumulation of marks, repeated elements, or layered patterns that build meaning through patient repetition and reward sustained viewing. Add sparse, clinical typography and systematic reference markers that suggest this could be a diagram from an imaginary discipline, treating the invisible subject with the same reverence typically reserved for documenting observable phenomena. Anchor the piece with simple phrase(s) or details positioned subtly, using a limited color palette that feels intentional and cohesive. Embrace the paradox of using analytical visual language to express ideas about human experience: the result should feel like an artifact that proves something ephemeral can be studied, mapped, and understood through careful attention. This is true art. \n\n**Text as a contextual element**: Text is always minimal and visual-first, but let context guide whether that means whisper-quiet labels or bold typographic gestures. A punk venue poster might have larger, more aggressive type than a minimalist ceramics studio identity. Most of the time, font should be thin. All use of fonts must be design-forward and prioritize visual communication. Regardless of text scale, nothing falls off the page and nothing overlaps. Every element must be contained within the canvas boundaries with proper margins. Check carefully that all text, graphics, and visual elements have breathing room and clear separation. This is non-negotiable for professional execution. **IMPORTANT: Use different fonts if writing text. Search the `./canvas-fonts` directory. Regardless of approach, sophistication is non-negotiable.**\n\nDownload and use whatever fonts are needed to make this a reality. Get creative by making the typography actually part of the art itself -- if the art is abstract, bring the font onto the canvas, not typeset digitally.\n\nTo push boundaries, follow design instinct/intuition while using the philosophy as a guiding principle. Embrace ultimate design freedom and choice. Push aesthetics and design to the frontier. \n\n**CRITICAL**: To achieve human-crafted quality (not AI-generated), create work that looks like it took countless hours. Make it appear as though someone at the absolute top of their field labored over every detail with painstaking care. Ensure the composition, spacing, color choices, typography - everything screams expert-level craftsmanship. Double-check that nothing overlaps, formatting is flawless, every detail perfect. Create something that could be shown to people to prove expertise and rank as undeniably impressive.\n\nOutput the final result as a single, downloadable .pdf or .png file, alongside the design philosophy used as a .md file.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL STEP\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The user ALREADY said \"It isn''t perfect enough. It must be pristine, a masterpiece if craftsmanship, as if it were about to be displayed in a museum.\"\n\n**CRITICAL**: To refine the work, avoid adding more graphics; instead refine what has been created and make it extremely crisp, respecting the design philosophy and the principles of minimalism entirely. Rather than adding a fun filter or refactoring a font, consider how to make the existing composition more cohesive with the art. If the instinct is to call a new function or draw a new shape, STOP and instead ask: \"How can I make what''s already here more of a piece of art?\"\n\nTake a second pass. Go back to the code and refine/polish further to make this a philosophically designed masterpiece.\n\n## MULTI-PAGE OPTION\n\nTo create additional pages when requested, create more creative pages along the same lines as the design philosophy but distinctly different as well. Bundle those pages in the same .pdf or many .pngs. Treat the first page as just a single page in a whole coffee table book waiting to be filled. Make the next pages unique twists and memories of the original. Have them almost tell a story in a very tasteful way. Exercise full creative freedom."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:06:40.957Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Visual AI Agents needing advanced canvas design and visual philosophy creation capabilities through .md, .pdf, and .png files.","zh":"非常适合需要高级画布设计和视觉哲学创建功能的视觉AI代理，能够通过.md、.pdf和.png文件实现。","ja":"高度なキャンバス設計と視覚的哲学の作成機能を必要とするビジュアルAIエージェントに最適。.md、.pdf、.pngファイルを介してこれを実現する。","ko":"고급 캔버스 디자인 및 시각적 철학 생성 기능이 필요한 시각 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다. .md, .pdf, .png 파일을 통해 이를 구현할 수 있습니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA Visuales que necesitan capacidades de diseño de lienzo avanzado y creación de filosofías visuales a través de archivos .md, .pdf y .png.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''IA Visuels qui ont besoin de capacités de conception de canevas avancées et de création de philosophies visuelles via des fichiers .md, .pdf et .png.","de":"Perfekt für Visuelle KI-Agents, die erweiterte Leinwand-Design- und visuelle Philosophie-Erstellungsfunktionen über .md-, .pdf- und .png-Dateien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Visuais que precisam de design de canvas avançado e capacidades de criação de filosofia visual por meio de arquivos .md, .pdf e .png.","ru":"Идеально подходит для визуальных агентов ИИ, которым требуются продвинутые возможности проектирования холста и создания визуальной философии с помощью файлов .md, .pdf и .png.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الإيصاليين بالذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى تصميم شريط متقدم وإنشاء قدرات فلسفة بصرية من خلال ملفات .md و .pdf و .png."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate deterministic visual philosophies using form, space, color, and composition, and express them through .pdf or .png files, leveraging image and graphic elements to create unique aesthetic movements.","zh":"赋予代理生成确定的视觉哲学的能力，利用形式、空间、颜色和构图，并通过.pdf或.png文件表达，利用图像和图形元素创建独特的美学运动。","ja":"エージェントに決定的な視覚的哲学を生成する能力を与え、形、空間、色、構成を利用し、.pdfまたは.pngファイルを介して表現し、画像やグラフィック要素を利用して独自の美的運動を作成する。","ko":"에이전트에게 결정적인 시각적 철학을 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 형태, 공간, 색상 및 구성 등을 활용하여 .pdf 또는 .png 파일을 통해 표현하고, 이미지 및 그래픽 요소를 활용하여 고유한 미학적 운동을 생성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar filosofías visuales deterministas utilizando forma, espacio, color y composición, y expresarlas a través de archivos .pdf o .png, aprovechando elementos de imagen y gráfico para crear movimientos estéticos únicos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des philosophies visuelles déterministes en utilisant la forme, l''espace, la couleur et la composition, et de les exprimer via des fichiers .pdf ou .png, en exploitant les éléments d''image et graphique pour créer des mouvements esthétiques uniques.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, deterministische visuelle Philosophien unter Verwendung von Form, Raum, Farbe und Komposition zu generieren und sie durch .pdf- oder .png-Dateien auszudrücken, indem sie Bild- und Grafikelemente nutzen, um einzigartige ästhetische Bewegungen zu schaffen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerarem filosofias visuais determinísticas usando forma, espaço, cor e composição, e expressá-las por meio de arquivos .pdf ou .png, aproveitando elementos de imagem e gráficos para criar movimentos estéticos únicos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать детерминированные визуальные философии с помощью формы, пространства, цвета и композиции, и выражать их через файлы .pdf или .png, используя изображения и графические элементы для создания уникальных эстетических движений.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على توليد فلسفات بصرية محددة باستخدام الشكل والفراغ واللون والتركيب، وعبر عنهم من خلال ملفات .pdf أو .png، واستخدام عناصر الصورة والرسومات لإنشاء حركات فنية فريدة."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating visual design philosophies for brand identities","Creating compositional layouts for digital art","Expressing aesthetic movements through .png files"],"zh":["为品牌身份生成视觉设计哲学","创建数字艺术的构图布局","通过.png文件表达美学运动"],"ja":["ブランドアイデンティティのための視覚的デザイン哲学の生成","デジタルアートのための構成レイアウトの作成",".pngファイルを介した美的運動の表現"],"ko":["브랜드 아이덴티티를 위한 시각적 디자인 철학 생성","디지털 아트를 위한 구성 레이아웃 생성",".png 파일을 통해 미학적 운동 표현"],"es":["Generar filosofías de diseño visual para identidades de marca","Crear diseños de composición para arte digital","Expresar movimientos estéticos a través de archivos .png"],"fr":["Générer des philosophies de conception visuelle pour les identités de marque","Créer des dispositions de composition pour l''art numérique","Exprimer des mouvements esthétiques via des fichiers .png"],"de":["Visuelle Designphilosophien für Markenidentitäten generieren","Kompositionslayouts für digitale Kunst erstellen","Ästhetische Bewegungen durch .png-Dateien ausdrücken"],"pt":["Geração de filosofias de design visual para identidades de marca","Criação de layouts compostos para arte digital","Expressar movimentos estéticos por meio de arquivos .png"],"ru":["Генерация философий визуального дизайна для бренд-идентичностей","Создание композиционных макетов для цифрового искусства","Выражение эстетических движений через файлы .png"],"ar":["توليد فلسفات للتصميم البصري لهويات العلامة التجارية","إنشاء تصاميم تركيبية للفن الرقمي","التعبير عن الحركات الفنية من خلال ملفات .png"]},"limitations":{"en":["Output limited to .md, .pdf, and .png files","Requires interpretation of visual elements like form, space, and color"],"zh":["输出仅限于.md、.pdf和.png文件","需要解释视觉元素，如形式、空间和颜色"],"ja":["出力は.md、.pdf、.pngファイルに限定される","形、空間、色などの視覚的要素の解釈が必要"],"ko":["출력은 .md, .pdf, .png 파일로만 제한됨","형태, 공간, 색상 등의 시각적 요소에 대한 해석이 필요"],"es":["La salida está limitada a archivos .md, .pdf y .png","Requiere la interpretación de elementos visuales como forma, espacio y color"],"fr":["La sortie est limitée aux fichiers .md, .pdf et .png","Nécessite l''interprétation d''éléments visuels tels que la forme, l''espace et la couleur"],"de":["Die Ausgabe ist auf .md-, .pdf- und .png-Dateien beschränkt","Erfordert die Interpretation visueller Elemente wie Form, Raum und Farbe"],"pt":["Saída limitada a arquivos .md, .pdf e .png","Requer interpretação de elementos visuais como forma, espaço e cor"],"ru":["Выход ограничен файлами .md, .pdf и .png","Требует интерпретации визуальных элементов, таких как форма, пространство и цвет"],"ar":["الإخراج مقيد بملفات .md و .pdf و .png","يتطلب تفسير للعناصر المرئية مثل الشكل والفراغ واللون"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
