ento em nível de projeto ou usuário"],"ru":["Создание пользовательских команд","Повторно используемые рабочие процессы","Идеально подходит для повторяющихся процессов","Поддержка многоэтапных процессов","Файлы markdown для команд","Хранение на уровне проекта или пользователя"],"ar":["إنشاء أوامر مخصصة","تدفقات عمل قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","مثالية للعمليات المتكررة","دعم العمليات متعددة المراحل","ملفات markdown للأوامر","تخزين على مستوى المشروع أو المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["命令创建者","Claude Code 命令","可重用命令","工作流程简化","多步骤过程","开发者工具"],"ja":["コマンドクリエーター","Claude Code コマンド","再利用可能なコマンド","ワークフロー簡素化","複数ステップのプロセス","開発者ツール"],"ko":["명령 생성기","Claude Code 명령","재사용 가능한 명령","워크플로우 단순화","다중 단계 프로세스","개발자 도구"],"es":["creador de comandos","claude code","automatización de flujos de trabajo","comandos personalizados","markdown","productividad","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["créateur de commandes","claude code","automatisation de workflows","commandes personnalisées","markdown","productivité","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Befehlsersteller","claude code","Automatisierung von Workflows","benutzerdefinierte Befehle","Markdown","Produktivität","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["comandos personalizados","fluxos de trabalho reutilizáveis","Command Creator","comandos reutilizáveis","processos repetitivos","multi-etapas","arquivos markdown","projeto","usuário"],"ru":["пользовательские команды","повторно используемые рабочие процессы","Command Creator","повторно используемые команды","повторяющиеся процессы","многоэтапные процессы","файлы markdown","проект","пользователь"],"ar":["أوامر مخصصة","تدفقات عمل قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","Command Creator","أوامر قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","عمليات متكررة","عمليات متعددة المراحل","ملفات markdown","مستوى المشروع","مستوى المستخدم"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"command-creator","description":"This skill should be used when creating a Claude Code slash command. Use when users ask to create a command, make a slash command, add a command, or want to document a workflow as a reusable command. Essential for creating optimized, agent-executable slash commands with proper structure and best practices.","bodyPreview":"# Command Creator\n\nThis skill guides the creation of Claude Code slash commands - reusable workflows that can be invoked with `/command-name` in Claude Code conversations.\n\n## About Slash Commands\n\nSlash commands are markdown files stored in `.claude/commands/` (project-level) or `~/.claude/commands/` (global/user-level) that get expanded into prompts when invoked. They''re ideal for:\n\n- Repetitive workflows (code review, PR submission, CI fixing)\n- Multi-step processes that need consistency\n- Ag","body":"# Command Creator\n\nThis skill guides the creation of Claude Code slash commands - reusable workflows that can be invoked with `/command-name` in Claude Code conversations.\n\n## About Slash Commands\n\nSlash commands are markdown files stored in `.claude/commands/` (project-level) or `~/.claude/commands/` (global/user-level) that get expanded into prompts when invoked. They''re ideal for:\n\n- Repetitive workflows (code review, PR submission, CI fixing)\n- Multi-step processes that need consistency\n- Agent delegation patterns\n- Project-specific automation\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nInvoke this skill when users:\n\n- Ask to \"create a command\" or \"make a slash command\"\n- Want to automate a repetitive workflow\n- Need to document a consistent process for reuse\n- Say \"I keep doing X, can we make a command for it?\"\n- Want to create project-specific or global commands\n\n## Bundled Resources\n\nThis skill includes reference documentation for detailed guidance:\n\n- **references/patterns.md** - Command patterns (workflow automation, iterative fixing, agent delegation, simple execution)\n- **references/examples.md** - Real command examples with full source (submit-stack, ensure-ci, create-implementation-plan)\n- **references/best-practices.md** - Quality checklist, common pitfalls, writing guidelines, template structure\n\nLoad these references as needed when creating commands to understand patterns, see examples, or ensure quality.\n\n## Command Structure Overview\n\nEvery slash command is a markdown file with:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Brief description shown in /help (required)\nargument-hint: <placeholder> (optional, if command takes arguments)\n---\n\n# Command Title\n\n[Detailed instructions for the agent to execute autonomously]\n```\n\n## Command Creation Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Determine Location\n\n**Auto-detect the appropriate location:**\n\n1. Check git repository status: `git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree 2>/dev/null`\n2. Default location:\n   - If in git repo → Project-level: `.claude/commands/`\n   - If not in git repo → Global: `~/.claude/commands/`\n3. Allow user override:\n   - If user explicitly mentions \"global\" or \"user-level\" → Use `~/.claude/commands/`\n   - If user explicitly mentions \"project\" or \"project-level\" → Use `.claude/commands/`\n\nReport the chosen location to the user before proceeding.\n\n### Step 2: Show Command Patterns\n\nHelp the user understand different command types. Load **references/patterns.md** to see available patterns:\n\n- **Workflow Automation** - Analyze → Act → Report (e.g., submit-stack)\n- **Iterative Fixing** - Run → Parse → Fix → Repeat (e.g., ensure-ci)\n- **Agent Delegation** - Context → Delegate → Iterate (e.g., create-implementation-plan)\n- **Simple Execution** - Run command with args (e.g., codex-review)\n\nAsk the user: \"Which pattern is closest to what you want to create?\" This helps frame the conversation.\n\n### Step 3: Gather Command Information\n\nAsk the user for key information:\n\n#### A. Command Name and Purpose\n\nAsk:\n\n- \"What should the command be called?\" (for filename)\n- \"What does this command do?\" (for description field)\n\nGuidelines:\n\n- Command names MUST be kebab-case (hyphens, NOT underscores)\n  - ✅ CORRECT: `submit-stack`, `ensure-ci`, `create-from-plan`\n  - ❌ WRONG: `submit_stack`, `ensure_ci`, `create_from_plan`\n- File names match command names: `my-command.md` → invoked as `/my-command`\n- Description should be concise, action-oriented (appears in `/help` output)\n\n#### B. Arguments\n\nAsk:\n\n- \"Does this command take any arguments?\"\n- \"Are arguments required or optional?\"\n- \"What should arguments represent?\"\n\nIf command takes arguments:\n\n- Add `argument-hint: <placeholder>` to frontmatter\n- Use `<angle-brackets>` for required arguments\n- Use `[square-brackets]` for optional arguments\n\n#### C. Workflow Steps\n\nAsk:\n\n- \"What are the specific steps this command should follow?\"\n- \"What order should they happen in?\"\n- \"What tools or commands should be used?\"\n\nGather details about:\n\n- Initial analysis or checks to perform\n- Main actions to take\n- How to handle results\n- Success criteria\n- Error handling approach\n\n#### D. Tool Restrictions and Guidance\n\nAsk:\n\n- \"Should this command use any specific agents or tools?\"\n- \"Are there any tools or operations it should avoid?\"\n- \"Should it read any specific files for context?\"\n\n### Step 4: Generate Optimized Command\n\nCreate the command file with agent-optimized instructions. Load **references/best-practices.md** for:\n\n- Template structure\n- Best practices for agent execution\n- Writing style guidelines\n- Quality checklist\n\nKey principles:\n\n- Use imperative/infinitive form (verb-first instructions)\n- Be explicit and specific\n- Include expected outcomes\n- Provide concrete examples\n- Define clear error handling\n\n### Step 5: Create the Command File\n\n1. Determine full file path:\n   - Project: `.claude/commands/[command-name].md`\n   - Global: `~/.claude/commands/[command-name].md`\n\n2. Ensure directory exists:\n\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p [directory-path]\n   ```\n\n3. Write the command file using the Write tool\n\n4. Confirm with user:\n   - Report the file location\n   - Summarize what the command does\n   - Explain how to use it: `/command-name [arguments]`\n\n### Step 6: Test and Iterate (Optional)\n\nIf the user wants to test:\n\n1. Suggest testing: `You can test this command by running: /command-name [arguments]`\n2. Be ready to iterate based on feedback\n3. Update the file with improvements as needed\n\n## Quick Tips\n\n**For detailed guidance, load the bundled references:**\n\n- Load **references/patterns.md** when designing the command workflow\n- Load **references/examples.md** to see how existing commands are structured\n- Load **references/best-practices.md** before finalizing to ensure quality\n\n**Common patterns to remember:**\n\n- Use Bash tool for `pytest`, `pyright`, `ruff`, `prettier`, `make`, `gt` commands\n- Use Task tool to invoke subagents for specialized tasks\n- Check for specific files first (e.g., `.PLAN.md`) before proceeding\n- Mark todos complete immediately, not in batches\n- Include explicit error handling instructions\n- Define clear success criteria\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen creating a command:\n\n1. **Detect location** (project vs global)\n2. **Show patterns** to frame the conversation\n3. **Gather information** (name, purpose, arguments, steps, tools)\n4. **Generate optimized command** with agent-executable instructions\n5. **Create file** at appropriate location\n6. **Confirm and iterate** as needed\n\nFocus on creating commands that agents can execute autonomously, with clear steps, explicit tool usage, and proper error handling.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:06:47.015Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code needing reusable workflow automation through slash commands","zh":"非常适合像 Claude Code 这样的 AI 代理，它需要通过斜杠命令实现可重用的工作流自动化","ja":"Claude Code のような AI エージェントに最適で、スラッシュコマンドを使用した再利用可能なワークフローの自動化が必要","ko":"Claude Code 와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 슬래시 명령을 통해 재사용 가능한 워크플로 자동화를 필요로 함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code que necesitan automatización de flujos de trabajo reutilizables a través de comandos de barra","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude Code qui ont besoin d''une automatisation de flux de travail réutilisable via des commandes de barre oblique","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, die eine wiederverwendbare Workflow-Automatisierung über Schrägstrichbefehle benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude Code que precisam de automação de fluxo de trabalho reutilizável por meio de comandos de barra","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, требующих многоразовой автоматизации рабочего процесса через команды с косой чертой","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code الذين يحتاجون إلى أتمتة تدفق العمل القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام من خلال أوامر البار"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and invoke custom workflows using markdown files stored in `.claude/commands/`, streamlining repetitive tasks and multi-step processes through consistent and expandable prompts, leveraging slash commands like `/command-name`","zh":"赋予代理创建和调用自定义工作流的能力，使用存储在 `.claude/commands/` 中的 markdown 文件，通过一致且可扩展的提示简化重复性任务和多步骤过程，利用类似 `/command-name` 的斜杠命令","ja":"エージェントが `.claude/commands/` に保存されたマークダウンファイルを使用してカスタムワークフローを作成して呼び出す能力を提供し、繰り返しのタスクや複数ステップのプロセスを一貫して拡張可能なプロンプトを使用して簡素化する、`/command-name` のようなスラッシュコマンドを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 `.claude/commands/`에 저장된 마크다운 파일을 사용하여 사용자 지정 워크플ローを作成하고 호출할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 반복적인 작업과 다단계 프로세스를 일관되게 확장 가능한 프롬프트를 사용하여 단순화하며, `/command-name`과 같은 슬래시 명령을 활용함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear e invocar flujos de trabajo personalizados utilizando archivos markdown almacenados en `.claude/commands/`, simplificando tareas repetitivas y procesos de varios pasos a través de solicitudes consistentes y ampliables, aprovechando comandos de barra como `/command-name`","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et d''appeler des flux de travail personnalisés en utilisant des fichiers markdown stockés dans `.claude/commands/`, rationalisant les tâches répétitives et les processus multétapes via des invites cohérentes et extensibles, en exploitant des commandes de barre oblique comme `/command-name`","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, benutzerdefinierte Workflows zu erstellen und aufzurufen, indem sie Markdown-Dateien verwenden, die in `.claude/commands/` gespeichert sind, wiederkehrende Aufgaben und mehrschrittige Prozesse durch konsistente und erweiterbare Prompts rationalisierend, indem Schrägstrichbefehle wie `/command-name` genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e invocar fluxos de trabalho personalizados usando arquivos markdown armazenados em `.claude/commands/`, simplificando tarefas repetitivas e processos em vários passos por meio de prompts consistentes e expansíveis, aproveitando comandos de barra como `/command-name`","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и вызывать пользовательские рабочие процессы, используя файлы markdown, хранящиеся в `.claude/commands/`, оптимизируя повторяющиеся задачи и многоступенчатые процессы посредством последовательных и расширяемых подсказок, используя команды с косой чертой, такие как `/command-name`","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء وتنفيذ تدفقات عمل مخصصة باستخدام ملفات markdown المخزنة في `.claude/commands/`، وتبسيط المهام المتكررة والعمليات متعددة الخطوات من خلال إشارات متسقة وقابلة للتوسيع، واستغلال أوامر البار مثل `/command-name`"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code review workflows","Generating consistent PR submission templates","Simplifying CI fixing processes"],"zh":["自动化代码审查工作流","生成一致的 PR 提交模板","简化 CI 修复过程"],"ja":["コードレビューのワークフローを自動化する","一貫した PR 提出テンプレートを生成する","CI の修復プロセスを簡素化する"],"ko":["코드 리뷰 워크플ロー 자동화","일관된 PR 제출 템플릿 생성","CI 수정 프로세스 단순화"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo de revisión de código","Generación de plantillas de presentación de PR consistentes","Simplificación de procesos de corrección de CI"],"fr":["Automatisation des flux de travail de révision de code","Génération de modèles de soumission de PR cohérents","Simplification des processus de correction de CI"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Review-Workflows","Erzeugung konsistenter PR-Vorlagen","Vereinfachung von CI-Korrekturprozessen"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de revisão de código","Gerar modelos de envio de PR consistentes","Simplificar processos de correção de CI"],"ru":["Автоматизировать рабочие процессы проверки кода","Генерировать последовательные шаблоны отправки PR","Упрощать процессы исправления CI"],"ar":["أتمتة تدفقات العمل لمراجعة الشفرة","توليد قوالب إرسال متسقة ل-PR","تبسيط عمليات إصلاح CI"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `.claude/commands/` directory","Limited to Claude Code conversations","Dependent on markdown file format"],"zh":["需要访问 `.claude/commands/` 目录","仅限 Claude Code 会话","依赖于 markdown 文件格式"],"ja":["`.claude/commands/` ディレクトリへのアクセスが必要","Claude Code 会話のみ","マークダウンファイル形式に依存"],"ko":["`.claude/commands/` 디렉토리에 대한 액세스가 필요","Claude Code 채팅만 해당","마크다운 파일 형식에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso al directorio `.claude/commands/`","Limitado a conversaciones de Claude Code","Dependiente del formato de archivo markdown"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au répertoire `.claude/commands/`","Limité aux conversations de Claude Code","Dépendant du format de fichier markdown"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Verzeichnis `.claude/commands/`","Begrenzt auf Claude-Code-Konversationen","Abhängig vom Markdown-Dateiformat"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao diretório `.claude/commands/`","Limitado a conversas do Claude Code","Dependente do formato de arquivo markdown"],"ru":["Требует доступа к каталогу `.claude/commands/`","Ограничен разговорами Claude Code","Зависит от формата файла markdown"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الدليل `.claude/commands/`","محدود لمحادثات Claude Code","يعتمد على تنسيق ملف markdown"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
