 semântica e por palavra-chave"],"ru":["Реализация семантического поиска","Оптимизация задержки поиска","Масштабирование до миллионов векторов","Объединение семантического и поиска по ключевым словам"],"ar":["تنفيذ عمليات بحث семантиكي","تحسين تأخير البحث","توسيع النطاق لآلاف الآف من المتجهات","دمج البحث Семантиكي والبحث بالكلمات المفتاحية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["相似搜索","语义搜索","推荐系统","搜索优化","距离度量","大规模搜索","自然语言处理","机器学习"],"ja":["類似検索","語義検索","レコメンデーション","検索最適化","距離度量","大規模検索","自然言語処理","機械学習"],"ko":["유사 검색","의미 검색","추천 시스템","검색 최적화","거리 측정","대규모 검색","자연어 처리","기계 학습"],"es":["búsqueda de similitud","búsqueda semántica","recomendación de contenido","optimización de búsqueda","scalabilidad de búsqueda","vectores de búsqueda"],"fr":["recherche de similarité","recherche sémantique","recommandation de contenu","optimisation de recherche","évolutivité de recherche","vecteurs de recherche"],"de":["Ähnlichkeitssuche","semantische Suche","Inhalts-Empfehlung","Suchoptimierung","Skalierbarkeit der Suche","Suchvektoren"],"pt":["busca semântica","padrões de busca por semelhança","sistemas de produção","otimização de busca","escalabilidade","vetores"],"ru":["семантический поиск","шаблоны поиска по подобию","производственные системы","оптимизация поиска","масштабируемость","векторы"],"ar":["البحث Семантиكي","نماذج البحث عن التشابه","أنظمة الإنتاج","تحسين البحث","توسيع النطاق","المتجهات"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"similarity-search-patterns","description":"Implement efficient similarity search with vector databases. Use when building semantic search, implementing nearest neighbor queries, or optimizing retrieval performance.","bodyPreview":"# Similarity Search Patterns\n\nPatterns for implementing efficient similarity search in production systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building semantic search systems\n- Implementing RAG retrieval\n- Creating recommendation engines\n- Optimizing search latency\n- Scaling to millions of vectors\n- Combining semantic and keyword search\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Distance Metrics\n\n| Metric             | Formula            | Best For              |\n| ------------------ | ------------------ | ----------","body":"# Similarity Search Patterns\n\nPatterns for implementing efficient similarity search in production systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building semantic search systems\n- Implementing RAG retrieval\n- Creating recommendation engines\n- Optimizing search latency\n- Scaling to millions of vectors\n- Combining semantic and keyword search\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Distance Metrics\n\n| Metric             | Formula            | Best For              |\n| ------------------ | ------------------ | --------------------- | --- | -------------- |\n| **Cosine**         | 1 - (A·B)/(‖A‖‖B‖) | Normalized embeddings |\n| **Euclidean (L2)** | √Σ(a-b)²           | Raw embeddings        |\n| **Dot Product**    | A·B                | Magnitude matters     |\n| **Manhattan (L1)** | Σ                  | a-b                   |     | Sparse vectors |\n\n### 2. Index Types\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 Index Types                      │\n├─────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────────┤\n│    Flat     │     HNSW      │    IVF+PQ         │\n│ (Exact)     │ (Graph-based) │ (Quantized)       │\n├─────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────┤\n│ O(n) search │ O(log n)      │ O(√n)             │\n│ 100% recall │ ~95-99%       │ ~90-95%           │\n│ Small data  │ Medium-Large  │ Very Large        │\n└─────────────┴───────────────┴───────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Pinecone Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom pinecone import Pinecone, ServerlessSpec\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional\nimport hashlib\n\nclass PineconeVectorStore:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        api_key: str,\n        index_name: str,\n        dimension: int = 1536,\n        metric: str = \"cosine\"\n    ):\n        self.pc = Pinecone(api_key=api_key)\n\n        # Create index if not exists\n        if index_name not in self.pc.list_indexes().names():\n            self.pc.create_index(\n                name=index_name,\n                dimension=dimension,\n                metric=metric,\n                spec=ServerlessSpec(cloud=\"aws\", region=\"us-east-1\")\n            )\n\n        self.index = self.pc.Index(index_name)\n\n    def upsert(\n        self,\n        vectors: List[Dict],\n        namespace: str = \"\"\n    ) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Upsert vectors.\n        vectors: [{\"id\": str, \"values\": List[float], \"metadata\": dict}]\n        \"\"\"\n        # Batch upsert\n        batch_size = 100\n        total = 0\n\n        for i in range(0, len(vectors), batch_size):\n            batch = vectors[i:i + batch_size]\n            self.index.upsert(vectors=batch, namespace=namespace)\n            total += len(batch)\n\n        return total\n\n    def search(\n        self,\n        query_vector: List[float],\n        top_k: int = 10,\n        namespace: str = \"\",\n        filter: Optional[Dict] = None,\n        include_metadata: bool = True\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Search for similar vectors.\"\"\"\n        results = self.index.query(\n            vector=query_vector,\n            top_k=top_k,\n            namespace=namespace,\n            filter=filter,\n            include_metadata=include_metadata\n        )\n\n        return [\n            {\n                \"id\": match.id,\n                \"score\": match.score,\n                \"metadata\": match.metadata\n            }\n            for match in results.matches\n        ]\n\n    def search_with_rerank(\n        self,\n        query: str,\n        query_vector: List[float],\n        top_k: int = 10,\n        rerank_top_n: int = 50,\n        namespace: str = \"\"\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Search and rerank results.\"\"\"\n        # Over-fetch for reranking\n        initial_results = self.search(\n            query_vector,\n            top_k=rerank_top_n,\n            namespace=namespace\n        )\n\n        # Rerank with cross-encoder or LLM\n        reranked = self._rerank(query, initial_results)\n\n        return reranked[:top_k]\n\n    def _rerank(self, query: str, results: List[Dict]) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Rerank results using cross-encoder.\"\"\"\n        from sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\n\n        model = CrossEncoder(''cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2'')\n\n        pairs = [(query, r[\"metadata\"][\"text\"]) for r in results]\n        scores = model.predict(pairs)\n\n        for result, score in zip(results, scores):\n            result[\"rerank_score\"] = float(score)\n\n        return sorted(results, key=lambda x: x[\"rerank_score\"], reverse=True)\n\n    def delete(self, ids: List[str], namespace: str = \"\"):\n        \"\"\"Delete vectors by ID.\"\"\"\n        self.index.delete(ids=ids, namespace=namespace)\n\n    def delete_by_filter(self, filter: Dict, namespace: str = \"\"):\n        \"\"\"Delete vectors matching filter.\"\"\"\n        self.index.delete(filter=filter, namespace=namespace)\n```\n\n### Template 2: Qdrant Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom qdrant_client import QdrantClient\nfrom qdrant_client.http import models\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional\n\nclass QdrantVectorStore:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        url: str = \"localhost\",\n        port: int = 6333,\n        collection_name: str = \"documents\",\n        vector_size: int = 1536\n    ):\n        self.client = QdrantClient(url=url, port=port)\n        self.collection_name = collection_name\n\n        # Create collection if not exists\n        collections = self.client.get_collections().collections\n        if collection_name not in [c.name for c in collections]:\n            self.client.create_collection(\n                collection_name=collection_name,\n                vectors_config=models.VectorParams(\n                    size=vector_size,\n                    distance=models.Distance.COSINE\n                ),\n                # Optional: enable quantization for memory efficiency\n                quantization_config=models.ScalarQuantization(\n                    scalar=models.ScalarQuantizationConfig(\n                        type=models.ScalarType.INT8,\n                        quantile=0.99,\n                        always_ram=True\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n\n    def upsert(self, points: List[Dict]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Upsert points.\n        points: [{\"id\": str/int, \"vector\": List[float], \"payload\": dict}]\n        \"\"\"\n        qdrant_points = [\n            models.PointStruct(\n                id=p[\"id\"],\n                vector=p[\"vector\"],\n                payload=p.get(\"payload\", {})\n            )\n            for p in points\n        ]\n\n        self.client.upsert(\n            collection_name=self.collection_name,\n            points=qdrant_points\n        )\n        return len(points)\n\n    def search(\n        self,\n        query_vector: List[float],\n        limit: int = 10,\n        filter: Optional[models.Filter] = None,\n        score_threshold: Optional[float] = None\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Search for similar vectors.\"\"\"\n        results = self.client.search(\n            collection_name=self.collection_name,\n            query_vector=query_vector,\n            limit=limit,\n            query_filter=filter,\n            score_threshold=score_threshold\n        )\n\n        return [\n            {\n                \"id\": r.id,\n                \"score\": r.score,\n                \"payload\": r.payload\n            }\n            for r in results\n        ]\n\n    def search_with_filter(\n        self,\n        query_vector: List[float],\n        must_conditions: List[Dict] = None,\n        should_conditions: List[Dict] = None,\n        must_not_conditions: List[Dict] = None,\n        limit: int = 10\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Search with complex filters.\"\"\"\n        conditions = []\n\n        if must_conditions:\n            conditions.extend([\n                models.FieldCondition(\n                    key=c[\"key\"],\n                    match=models.MatchValue(value=c[\"value\"])\n                )\n                for c in must_conditions\n            ])\n\n        filter = models.Filter(must=conditions) if conditions else None\n\n        return self.search(query_vector, limit=limit, filter=filter)\n\n    def search_with_sparse(\n        self,\n        dense_vector: List[float],\n        sparse_vector: Dict[int, float],\n        limit: int = 10,\n        dense_weight: float = 0.7\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Hybrid search with dense and sparse vectors.\"\"\"\n        # Requires collection with named vectors\n        results = self.client.search(\n            collection_name=self.collection_name,\n            query_vector=models.NamedVector(\n                name=\"dense\",\n                vector=dense_vector\n            ),\n            limit=limit\n        )\n        return [{\"id\": r.id, \"score\": r.score, \"payload\": r.payload} for r in results]\n```\n\n### Template 3: pgvector with PostgreSQL\n\n```python\nimport asyncpg\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional\nimport numpy as np\n\nclass PgVectorStore:\n    def __init__(self, connection_string: str):\n        self.connection_string = connection_string\n\n    async def init(self):\n        \"\"\"Initialize connection pool and extension.\"\"\"\n        self.pool = await asyncpg.create_pool(self.connection_string)\n\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            # Enable extension\n            await conn.execute(\"CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector\")\n\n            # Create table\n            await conn.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS documents (\n                    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n                    content TEXT,\n                    metadata JSONB,\n                    embedding vector(1536)\n                )\n            \"\"\")\n\n            # Create index (HNSW for better performance)\n            await conn.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS documents_embedding_idx\n                ON documents\n                USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops)\n                WITH (m = 16, ef_construction = 64)\n            \"\"\")\n\n    async def upsert(self, documents: List[Dict]):\n        \"\"\"Upsert documents with embeddings.\"\"\"\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            await conn.executemany(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO documents (id, content, metadata, embedding)\n                VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4)\n                ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET\n                    content = EXCLUDED.content,\n                    metadata = EXCLUDED.metadata,\n                    embedding = EXCLUDED.embedding\n                \"\"\",\n                [\n                    (\n                        doc[\"id\"],\n                        doc[\"content\"],\n                        doc.get(\"metadata\", {}),\n                        np.array(doc[\"embedding\"]).tolist()\n                    )\n                    for doc in documents\n                ]\n            )\n\n    async def search(\n        self,\n        query_embedding: List[float],\n        limit: int = 10,\n        filter_metadata: Optional[Dict] = None\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Search for similar documents.\"\"\"\n        query = \"\"\"\n            SELECT id, content, metadata,\n                   1 - (embedding <=> $1::vector) as similarity\n            FROM documents\n        \"\"\"\n\n        params = [query_embedding]\n\n        if filter_metadata:\n            conditions = []\n            for key, value in filter_metadata.items():\n                params.append(value)\n                conditions.append(f\"metadata->>''{key}'' = ${len(params)}\")\n            query += \" WHERE \" + \" AND \".join(conditions)\n\n        query += f\" ORDER BY embedding <=> $1::vector LIMIT ${len(params) + 1}\"\n        params.append(limit)\n\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            rows = await conn.fetch(query, *params)\n\n        return [\n            {\n                \"id\": row[\"id\"],\n                \"content\": row[\"content\"],\n                \"metadata\": row[\"metadata\"],\n                \"score\": row[\"similarity\"]\n            }\n            for row in rows\n        ]\n\n    async def hybrid_search(\n        self,\n        query_embedding: List[float],\n        query_text: str,\n        limit: int = 10,\n        vector_weight: float = 0.5\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Hybrid search combining vector and full-text.\"\"\"\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            rows = await conn.fetch(\n                \"\"\"\n                WITH vector_results AS (\n                    SELECT id, content, metadata,\n                           1 - (embedding <=> $1::vector) as vector_score\n                    FROM documents\n                    ORDER BY embedding <=> $1::vector\n                    LIMIT $3 * 2\n                ),\n                text_results AS (\n                    SELECT id, content, metadata,\n                           ts_rank(to_tsvector(''english'', content),\n                                   plainto_tsquery(''english'', $2)) as text_score\n                    FROM documents\n                    WHERE to_tsvector(''english'', content) @@ plainto_tsquery(''english'', $2)\n                    LIMIT $3 * 2\n                )\n                SELECT\n                    COALESCE(v.id, t.id) as id,\n                    COALESCE(v.content, t.content) as content,\n                    COALESCE(v.metadata, t.metadata) as metadata,\n                    COALESCE(v.vector_score, 0) * $4 +\n                    COALESCE(t.text_score, 0) * (1 - $4) as combined_score\n                FROM vector_results v\n                FULL OUTER JOIN text_results t ON v.id = t.id\n                ORDER BY combined_score DESC\n                LIMIT $3\n                \"\"\",\n                query_embedding, query_text, limit, vector_weight\n            )\n\n        return [dict(row) for row in rows]\n```\n\n### Template 4: Weaviate Implementation\n\n```python\nimport weaviate\nfrom weaviate.util import generate_uuid5\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional\n\nclass WeaviateVectorStore:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        url: str = \"http://localhost:8080\",\n        class_name: str = \"Document\"\n    ):\n        self.client = weaviate.Client(url=url)\n        self.class_name = class_name\n        self._ensure_schema()\n\n    def _ensure_schema(self):\n        \"\"\"Create schema if not exists.\"\"\"\n        schema = {\n            \"class\": self.class_name,\n            \"vectorizer\": \"none\",  # We provide vectors\n            \"properties\": [\n                {\"name\": \"content\", \"dataType\": [\"text\"]},\n                {\"name\": \"source\", \"dataType\": [\"string\"]},\n                {\"name\": \"chunk_id\", \"dataType\": [\"int\"]}\n            ]\n        }\n\n        if not self.client.schema.exists(self.class_name):\n            self.client.schema.create_class(schema)\n\n    def upsert(self, documents: List[Dict]):\n        \"\"\"Batch upsert documents.\"\"\"\n        with self.client.batch as batch:\n            batch.batch_size = 100\n\n            for doc in documents:\n                batch.add_data_object(\n                    data_object={\n                        \"content\": doc[\"content\"],\n                        \"source\": doc.get(\"source\", \"\"),\n                        \"chunk_id\": doc.get(\"chunk_id\", 0)\n                    },\n                    class_name=self.class_name,\n                    uuid=generate_uuid5(doc[\"id\"]),\n                    vector=doc[\"embedding\"]\n                )\n\n    def search(\n        self,\n        query_vector: List[float],\n        limit: int = 10,\n        where_filter: Optional[Dict] = None\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Vector search.\"\"\"\n        query = (\n            self.client.query\n            .get(self.class_name, [\"content\", \"source\", \"chunk_id\"])\n            .with_near_vector({\"vector\": query_vector})\n            .with_limit(limit)\n            .with_additional([\"distance\", \"id\"])\n        )\n\n        if where_filter:\n            query = query.with_where(where_filter)\n\n        results = query.do()\n\n        return [\n            {\n                \"id\": item[\"_additional\"][\"id\"],\n                \"content\": item[\"content\"],\n                \"source\": item[\"source\"],\n                \"score\": 1 - item[\"_additional\"][\"distance\"]\n            }\n            for item in results[\"data\"][\"Get\"][self.class_name]\n        ]\n\n    def hybrid_search(\n        self,\n        query: str,\n        query_vector: List[float],\n        limit: int = 10,\n        alpha: float = 0.5  # 0 = keyword, 1 = vector\n    ) -> List[Dict]:\n        \"\"\"Hybrid search combining BM25 and vector.\"\"\"\n        results = (\n            self.client.query\n            .get(self.class_name, [\"content\", \"source\"])\n            .with_hybrid(query=query, vector=query_vector, alpha=alpha)\n            .with_limit(limit)\n            .with_additional([\"score\"])\n            .do()\n        )\n\n        return [\n            {\n                \"content\": item[\"content\"],\n                \"source\": item[\"source\"],\n                \"score\": item[\"_additional\"][\"score\"]\n            }\n            for item in results[\"data\"][\"Get\"][self.class_name]\n        ]\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Use appropriate index** - HNSW for most cases\n- **Tune parameters** - ef_search, nprobe for recall/speed\n- **Implement hybrid search** - Combine with keyword search\n- **Monitor recall** - Measure search quality\n- **Pre-filter when possible** - Reduce search space\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t skip evaluation** - Measure before optimizing\n- **Don''t over-index** - Start with flat, scale up\n- **Don''t ignore latency** - P99 matters for UX\n- **Don''t forget costs** - Vector storage adds up\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Pinecone Docs](https://docs.pinecone.io/)\n- [Qdrant Docs](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/)\n- [pgvector](https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector)\n- [Weaviate Docs](https://weaviate.io/developers/weaviate)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:08:01.957Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring efficient similarity search capabilities for semantic search systems and recommendation engines","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 等 AI 代理，需要高效的相似性搜索功能以用于语义搜索系统和推荐引擎","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの AI エージェントに適しており、セマンティック検索システムやレコメンドエンジンで効率的な類似検索機能を必要とする","ko":"Claude Code와 AutoGPT 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 의미 검색 시스템과 추천 엔진을 위한 효율적인 유사성 검색 기능을 필요로 함","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren capacidades de búsqueda de similitud eficientes para sistemas de búsqueda semántica y motores de recomendación","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des capacités de recherche de similarité efficaces pour les systèmes de recherche sémantique et les moteurs de recommandation","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die effiziente Ähnlichkeitssuchfunktionen für semantische Suchsysteme und Empfehlungsmotoren erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code e AutoGPT que exigem capacidades de pesquisa de similaridade eficientes para sistemas de pesquisa semântica e motores de recomendação","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих эффективных возможностей поиска подобия для семантических систем поиска и двигателей рекомендаций","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT التي تتطلب قدرات بحث مماثلة فعالة لأنظمة البحث الدلالي ومحركات التوصية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement efficient similarity search using distance metrics such as cosine similarity and Euclidean distance, optimizing search latency and scaling to millions of vectors, while combining semantic and keyword search for robust information retrieval","zh":"赋予代理实现使用余弦相似度和欧几里得距离等距离度量的高效相似性搜索，优化搜索延迟，并将向量规模扩大到数百万，同时结合语义和关键词搜索以实现强大的信息检索","ja":"エージェントがコサイン類似度やユークリッド距離などの距離尺度を使用して効率的な類似検索を実装できるようにし、検索遅延を最適化し、数百万のベクトルにスケーリングしながら、セマンティック検索とキーワード検索を組み合わせて強力な情報検索を実現する","ko":"에이전트가 코사인 유사도와 유클리드 거리 같은 거리 측정을 사용하여 효율적인 유사성 검색을 구현할 수 있도록 하며, 검색 지연을 최적화하고 수백만개의 벡터로 확장하면서, 의미 검색과 키워드 검색을 결합하여 강력한 정보 검색을 가능하게 함","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar búsquedas de similitud eficientes utilizando métricas de distancia como la similitud coseno y la distancia euclidiana, optimizando la latencia de búsqueda y escalando a millones de vectores, al mismo tiempo que combina la búsqueda semántica y de palabras clave para una recuperación de información robusta","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des recherches de similarité efficaces en utilisant des métriques de distance telles que la similarité cosinus et la distance euclidienne, en optimisant la latence de recherche et en échelle à des millions de vecteurs, tout en combinant la recherche sémantique et la recherche de mots clés pour une récupération d''informations robuste","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, effiziente Ähnlichkeitssuchen unter Verwendung von Distanzmetriken wie Kosinusähnlichkeit und euklidischer Distanz zu implementieren, wodurch die Suchlatenz optimiert und auf Millionen von Vektoren skaliert wird, während semantische und Schlüsselwortsuche für eine robuste Informationsrückgewinnung kombiniert werden","pt":"Permite que os agentes implementem uma pesquisa de similaridade eficiente usando métricas de distância, como similaridade coseno e distância euclidiana, otimizando a latência de pesquisa e dimensionando para milhões de vetores, ao mesmo tempo em que combina pesquisa semântica e de palavras-chave para uma recuperação robusta de informações","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать эффективный поиск подобия с использованием метрик расстояния, таких как косинусная подобие и евклидово расстояние, оптимизируя задержку поиска и масштабируя до миллионов векторов, а также сочетая семантический и ключевой поиск для надежного извлечения информации","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من تنفيذ بحث مماثلة فعال باستخدام مقاييس المسافة مثل الميلان الكوسيني والمسافة الأوكليديا، وتحسين زمن البحث وتوسيع نطاق البحث لآلاف الألف من المتجهات، مع الجمع بين بحث الدلالي والبحث بالكلمات الرئيسية لاسترجاع المعلومات بقوة"},"useCases":{"en":["Building semantic search systems with RAG retrieval","Creating recommendation engines with optimized similarity search","Scaling vector search to millions of records for large-scale applications","Combining semantic and keyword search for hybrid search systems"],"zh":["使用 RAG 检索构建语义搜索系统","创建使用优化的相似性搜索的推荐引擎","将向量搜索扩大到数百万条记录以适应大规模应用","将语义和关键词搜索结合用于混合搜索系统"],"ja":["RAG 検索を使用してセマンティック検索システムを構築する","最適化された類似検索を使用してレコメンドエンジンを作成する","ベクトル検索を数百万のレコードにスケーリングして大規模なアプリケーションに対応する","セマンティック検索とキーワード検索を組み合わせてハイブリッド検索システムを実現する"],"ko":["RAG 검색을 사용하여 의미 검색 시스템을 구축함","최적화된 유사성 검색을 사용하여 추천 엔진을 생성함","벡터 검색을 수백만개의 레코드로 확장하여 대규모 애플리케이션에 적합함","의미 검색과 키워드 검색을 결합하여 하이브리드 검색 시스템을 구현함"],"es":["Construir sistemas de búsqueda semántica con recuperación RAG","Crear motores de recomendación con búsqueda de similitud optimizada","Escalado de la búsqueda de vectores a millones de registros para aplicaciones de gran escala","Combinar búsqueda semántica y de palabras clave para sistemas de búsqueda híbrida"],"fr":["Construire des systèmes de recherche sémantique avec récupération RAG","Créer des moteurs de recommandation avec recherche de similarité optimisée","Mettre à l''échelle la recherche de vecteurs à des millions d''enregistrements pour des applications à grande échelle","Combiner la recherche sémantique et la recherche de mots clés pour des systèmes de recherche hybride"],"de":["Aufbau von semantischen Suchsystemen mit RAG-Wiederherstellung","Erstellung von Empfehlungsmotoren mit optimierter Ähnlichkeitssuche","Skalierung der Vektorsuche auf Millionen von Datensätzen für groß angelegte Anwendungen","Kombination von semantischer und Schlüsselwortsuche für hybride Suchsysteme"],"pt":["Construir sistemas de pesquisa semântica com recuperação RAG","Criar motores de recomendação com pesquisa de similaridade otimizada","Dimensionar a pesquisa de vetores para milhões de registros para aplicações em larga escala","Combinar pesquisa semântica e de palavras-chave para sistemas de pesquisa híbrida"],"ru":["Построение семантических систем поиска с извлечением RAG","Создание двигателей рекомендаций с оптимизированным поиском подобия","Масштабирование поиска векторов до миллионов записей для крупномасштабных приложений","Сочетание семантического и ключевого поиска для гибридных систем поиска"],"ar":["بناء أنظمة بحث دلالي مع استرجاع RAG","إنشاء محركات توصية مع بحث مماثلة محسّن","توسيع نطاق بحث المتجهات لآلاف الألف من السجلات لتطبيقات على نطاق واسع","الجمع بين بحث الدلالي والبحث بالكلمات الرئيسية لأنظمة بحث هجينة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of distance metrics and vector operations","Optimized for production systems with large-scale vector search requirements"],"zh":["需要理解距离度量和向量操作","针对具有大规模向量搜索需求的生产系统进行优化"],"ja":["距離尺度とベクトル操作の理解が必要","大規模なベクトル検索の要件を持つプロダクションシステム向けに最適化"],"ko":["거리 측정과 벡터 연산을 이해해야 함","대규모 벡터 검색 요구 사항이 있는 프로덕션 시스템을 위한 최적화"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de métricas de distancia y operaciones de vectores","Optimizado para sistemas de producción con requisitos de búsqueda de vectores de gran escala"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des métriques de distance et des opérations de vecteurs","Optimisé pour les systèmes de production avec des exigences de recherche de vecteurs à grande échelle"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis von Distanzmetriken und Vektoroperationen","Optimiert für Produktionsysteme mit groß angelegten Vektorsuchanforderungen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de métricas de distância e operações de vetores","Otimizado para sistemas de produção com requisitos de pesquisa de vetores em larga escala"],"ru":["Требует понимания метрик расстояния и операций с векторами","Оптимизирован для производственных систем с требованиями крупномасштабного поиска векторов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مقاييس المسافة وعمليات المتجهات","مُحسّن لمنظومات الإنتاج ذات متطلبات بحث متجهات على نطاق واسع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/crafting-effective-readmes', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'crafting-effective-readmes', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z', '2026-02-18T14:08:43.635Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/crafting-effective-readmes","name":"crafting-effective-readmes","description":{"zh":"README ","ja":"README","ko":"README ","es":"Crear READMEs efectivos es crucial para proporcionar información esencial a diferentes audiencias, desde contribuyentes hasta usuarios finales.","fr":"La création de READMEs efficaces est cruciale pour fournir des informations essentielles à différents publics, des contributeurs aux utilisateurs finaux.","de":"Das Erstellen von effektiven READMEs ist entscheidend, um wesentliche Informationen für unterschiedliche Zielgruppen bereitzustellen, von Mitwirkenden bis hin zu Endnutzern.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"README ","ja":"README","ko":"README ","es":"Crear READMEs Efectivos","fr":"Créer des READMEs Efficaces","de":"Erstellen von Effektiven READMEs","en":"crafting-effective-readmes"},"description":{"zh":"README ","ja":"README","ko":"README ","es":"Crear READMEs efectivos es crucial para proporcionar información esencial a diferentes audiencias, desde contribuyentes hasta usuarios finales.","fr":"La création de READMEs efficaces est cruciale pour fournir des informations essentielles à différents publics, des contributeurs aux utilisateurs finaux.","de":"Das Erstellen von effektiven READMEs ist entscheidend, um wesentliche Informationen für unterschiedliche Zielgruppen bereitzustellen, von Mitwirkenden bis hi...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["README","OSS","","README","Git","README"],"ja":["README","OSS","","README","Git","README"],"ko":["README","OSS","","README","Git","README"],"es":["Identificar al público objetivo","Determinar las necesidades de información","Estructurar contenido de manera clara","Incluir instrucciones de uso","Mantener actualizado el contenido"],"fr":["Identifier le public cible","Déterminer les besoins d''information","Structurer le contenu de manière claire","Inclure des instructions d''utilisation","Maintenir le contenu à jour"],"de":["Zielgruppe identifizieren","Informationsbedürfnisse bestimmen","Inhalt klar strukturieren","Nutzungsanweisungen einbeziehen","Inhalt auf dem neuesten Stand halten"]},"keywords":{"zh":["README","OSS","Git","README","README","README"],"ja":["README","OSS","Git","README","README","README"],"ko":["README","OSS","Git","README","README","README"],"es":["README efectivo","documentación de software","desarrollo de software","comunicación técnica","experiencia del usuario","proyecto de código abierto"],"fr":["README efficace","documentation de logiciel","développement de logiciel","communication technique","expérience utilisateur","projet de code source ouvert"],"de":["effektives README","Software-Dokumentation","Software-Entwicklung","technische Kommunikation","Benutzererfahrung","Open-Source-Projekt"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"crafting-effective-readmes","description":"Use when writing or improving README files. Not all READMEs are the same — provides templates and guidance matched to your audience and project type.","bodyPreview":"# Crafting Effective READMEs\n\n## Overview\n\nREADMEs answer questions your audience will have. Different audiences need different information - a contributor to an OSS project needs different context than future-you opening a config folder.\n\n**Always ask:** Who will read this, and what do they need to know?\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Task\n\n**Ask:** \"What README task are you working on?\"\n\n| Task | When |\n|------|------|\n| **Creating** | New project, no README yet |\n| **Adding** | Need to","body":"# Crafting Effective READMEs\n\n## Overview\n\nREADMEs answer questions your audience will have. Different audiences need different information - a contributor to an OSS project needs different context than future-you opening a config folder.\n\n**Always ask:** Who will read this, and what do they need to know?\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Task\n\n**Ask:** \"What README task are you working on?\"\n\n| Task | When |\n|------|------|\n| **Creating** | New project, no README yet |\n| **Adding** | Need to document something new |\n| **Updating** | Capabilities changed, content is stale |\n| **Reviewing** | Checking if README is still accurate |\n\n### Step 2: Task-Specific Questions\n\n**Creating initial README:**\n1. What type of project? (see Project Types below)\n2. What problem does this solve in one sentence?\n3. What''s the quickest path to \"it works\"?\n4. Anything notable to highlight?\n\n**Adding a section:**\n1. What needs documenting?\n2. Where should it go in the existing structure?\n3. Who needs this info most?\n\n**Updating existing content:**\n1. What changed?\n2. Read current README, identify stale sections\n3. Propose specific edits\n\n**Reviewing/refreshing:**\n1. Read current README\n2. Check against actual project state (package.json, main files, etc.)\n3. Flag outdated sections\n4. Update \"Last reviewed\" date if present\n\n### Step 3: Always Ask\n\nAfter drafting, ask: **\"Anything else to highlight or include that I might have missed?\"**\n\n## Project Types\n\n| Type | Audience | Key Sections | Template |\n|------|----------|--------------|----------|\n| **Open Source** | Contributors, users worldwide | Install, Usage, Contributing, License | `templates/oss.md` |\n| **Personal** | Future you, portfolio viewers | What it does, Tech stack, Learnings | `templates/personal.md` |\n| **Internal** | Teammates, new hires | Setup, Architecture, Runbooks | `templates/internal.md` |\n| **Config** | Future you (confused) | What''s here, Why, How to extend, Gotchas | `templates/xdg-config.md` |\n\n**Ask the user** if unclear. Don''t assume OSS defaults for everything.\n\n## Essential Sections (All Types)\n\nEvery README needs at minimum:\n\n1. **Name** - Self-explanatory title\n2. **Description** - What + why in 1-2 sentences  \n3. **Usage** - How to use it (examples help)\n\n## References\n\n- `section-checklist.md` - Which sections to include by project type\n- `style-guide.md` - Common README mistakes and prose guidance\n- `using-references.md` - Guide to deeper reference materials\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:08:43.635Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Documentation Agents tasked with creating informative and audience-specific README files","zh":"适用于负责创建信息丰富且面向特定受众的README文件的文档代理","ja":"情報豊富で対象者に特化したREADMEファイルを作成するドキュメントエージェントに適しています","ko":"정보가 풍부하고 대상자에 특화된 README 파일을 생성하는 문서 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de documentación encargados de crear archivos README informativos y específicos para la audiencia","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de documentation chargés de créer des fichiers README informatifs et spécifiques au public","de":"Ideal für Dokumentationsagenten, die mit der Erstellung von informativen und zielgruppenspezifischen README-Dateien betraut sind","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Documentação encarregados de criar arquivos README informativos e específicos para o público-alvo","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов документации, которым поручено создавать информативные и ориентированные на аудиторию файлы README","ar":"مثالي لعميل الوثائق المكلف بإنشاء ملفات README إعلامية ومتوافقة مع الجمهور المستهدف"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft effective READMEs by identifying target audiences and their information needs, utilizing Markdown formatting and task-oriented content creation, and applying best practices for contributor and user engagement","zh":"通过识别目标受众及其信息需求，利用Markdown格式和面向任务的内容创建，并应用贡献者和用户参与的最佳实践，赋予代理创建有效README的能力","ja":"ターゲットオーディエンスとその情報ニーズを特定し、Markdown形式とタスク指向のコンテンツ作成を利用し、貢献者とユーザーの関与のベストプラクティスを適用することで、エージェントが効果的なREADMEを作成できるようにします","ko":"대상자와 их 정보 필요를 식별하고, 마크다운 형식과 작업 지향적 콘텐츠 생성을 활용하며, 기여자와 사용자 참여의 최선의 관행을 적용함으로써 에이전트가 효과적인 README를 작성할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes crear README efectivos al identificar a las audiencias objetivo y sus necesidades de información, utilizando la formación de Markdown y la creación de contenido orientada a tareas, y aplicando las mejores prácticas para la participación de contribuyentes y usuarios","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des README efficaces en identifiant les publics cibles et leurs besoins d''information, en utilisant la mise en forme Markdown et la création de contenu orientée vers les tâches, et en appliquant les meilleures pratiques pour l''engagement des contributeurs et des utilisateurs","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, effektive READMEs zu erstellen, indem sie Zielgruppen und deren Informationsbedürfnisse identifizieren, Markdown-Formatierung und inhaltsorientierte Aufgabenstellung verwenden und bewährte Verfahren für die Einbindung von Mitwirkenden und Benutzern anwenden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar READMEs eficazes, identificando os públicos-alvo e suas necessidades de informação, utilizando formatação Markdown e criação de conteúdo orientada por tarefas, e aplicando as melhores práticas para engajamento de contribuintes e usuários","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать эффективные файлы README, определяя целевую аудиторию и их информационные потребности, используя форматирование Markdown и создание контента, ориентированного на задачи, и применяя лучшие практики для взаимодействия с участниками и пользователями","ar":"تمكّن العملاء من إنشاء ملفات README فعالة عن طريق تحديد الجمهور المستهدف واحتياجاتهم للمعلومات، واستخدام تنسيق Markdown وإنشاء محتوى موجه بالمهام، وتطبيق أفضل الممارسات للتفاعل بين المساهمين والمستخدمين"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating project-specific READMEs for open-source repositories","Creating configuration guides for technical audiences","Developing contributor guidelines for collaborative projects"],"zh":["为开源存储库生成项目特定的README","为技术受众创建配置指南","为协作项目开发贡献者指南"],"ja":["オープンソースリポジトリのプロジェクト固有のREADMEを生成する","技術的なオーディエンスのために設定ガイドを作成する","共同プロジェクトのために貢献者ガイドを開発する"],"ko":["오픈소스 저장소의 프로젝트 특정 README 생성","기술적인 대상자들을 위한 구성 가이드 작성","공동 프로젝트를 위한 기여자 가이드 개발"],"es":["Generación de archivos README específicos de proyecto para repositorios de código abierto","Creación de guías de configuración para audiencias técnicas","Desarrollo de directrices para contribuyentes en proyectos colaborativos"],"fr":["Génération de fichiers README spécifiques au projet pour les référentiels de code source ouvert","Création de guides de configuration pour les publics techniques","Développement de lignes directrices pour les contributeurs dans les projets collaboratifs"],"de":["Generierung von projektspezifischen README-Dateien für Open-Source-Repositorys","Erstellung von Konfigurationshandbüchern für technische Zielgruppen","Entwicklung von Richtlinien für Mitwirkende in kollaborativen Projekten"],"pt":["Geração de arquivos README específicos para projetos em repositórios de código aberto","Criação de guias de configuração para públicos técnicos","Desenvolvimento de diretrizes para contribuintes em projetos colaborativos"],"ru":["Генерация проектных файлов README для репозиториев с открытым исходным кодом","Создание руководств по конфигурации для технической аудитории","Разработка руководств для участников в совместных проектах"],"ar":["إنشاء ملفات README محددة للمشاريع في مستودعات الشفرة المفتوحة","إنشاء دليـل إعدادات للمستخدمين التقنيين","تطوير إرشادات للمساهمين في المشاريع التعاونية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Markdown syntax","Audience analysis and content customization needed"],"zh":["需要理解Markdown语法","需要受众分析和内容定制"],"ja":["Markdown構文の理解が必要","オーディエンス分析とコンテンツカスタマイズが必要"],"ko":["마크다운 구문 이해 필요","대상자 분석 및 콘텐츠 맞춤 필요"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la sintaxis Markdown","Análisis de la audiencia y personalización de contenido necesarios"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la syntaxe Markdown","Analyse de la audience et personnalisation du contenu nécessaires"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für Markdown-Syntax","Zielgruppenanalyse und Inhaltsanpassung erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da sintaxe Markdown","Análise de público e personalização de conteúdo necessárias"],"ru":["Требует понимания синтаксиса Markdown","Необходимы анализ аудитории и настройка контента"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم بنية Markdown","تحليل الجمهور وتخصيص المحتوى ضروريان"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/cloudflare-durable-objects', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'cloudflare-durable-objects', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z', '2026-02-18T14:08:15.411Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/cloudflare-durable-objects","name":"cloudflare-durable-objects","description":{"zh":"Cloudflare Durable Objects ","ja":"Cloudflare Durable Objects","ko":"Cloudflare Durable Objects ","es":"Cloudflare Durable Objects es una tecnología que permite a los desarrolladores crear aplicaciones escalables y seguras en la plataforma Cloudflare.","fr":"Cloudflare Durable Objects est une technologie qui permet aux développeurs de créer des applications évolutives et sécurisées sur la plateforme Cloudflare.","de":"Cloudflare Durable Objects ist eine Technologie, die es Entwicklern ermöglicht, skalierbare und sichere Anwendungen auf der Cloudflare-Plattform zu erstellen.","pt":"Cloudflare Durable Objects é uma tecnologia de armazenamento de dados que permite criar aplicativos escaláveis e seguros. Com ele, você pode melhorar a performance e a segurança dos seus aplicativos","ru":"Cloudflare Durable Objects — это технология хранения данных, которая позволяет создавать масштабируемые и безопасные приложения. С ее помощью вы можете улучшить производительность и безопасность своих приложений","ar":"أوامر Cloudflare الدائمة هي تقنية تخزين البيانات التي تمكنك من إنشاء تطبيقات قابلة للتوسع وأمنة. يمكنك تحسين الأداء والأمان لتطبيقاتك مع هذه التقنية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Cloudflare Durable Objects","ja":"Cloudflare","ko":"Cloudflare ","es":"Objetos Duraderos de Cloudflare: Desarrollo de Aplicaciones","fr":"Objets Durables Cloudflare: Développement d''Applications","de":"Cloudflare Durable Objects: Entwicklung von Anwendungen","pt":"Cloudflare Durable Objects: Desenvolvimento de Aplicativo...","ru":"Clo