 local de trabalho","Feedback sensível para colegas ou gerentes","Discussão de tópicos sensíveis, como salário ou promoção"],"ru":["Структурированный подход к сложным разговорам","Решение конфликтов на рабочем месте","Деликатная обратная связь для коллег или руководителей","Обсуждение деликатных тем, таких как зарплата или повышение"],"ar":["نهج منظم للمحادثات الصعبة","حل النزاعات في مكان العمل","تغذية الرأي الحساسة لأصحاب العمل أو المدراء","مناقشة المواضيع الحساسة، مثل الراتب أو الترقية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["工作场所对话","冲突解决","绩效问题","敏感反馈","情绪化讨论","结构化框架","开发者"],"ja":["職場での会話","衝突解決","パフォーマンスの問題","デリケートなフィードバック","感情的議論","構造化フレームワーク","開発者"],"ko":["직장 대화","충돌 해결","성과 문제","민감한 피드백","감정적인 논의","구조화된 프레임워크","개발자"],"es":["conversaciones difíciles en el lugar de trabajo","resolución de conflictos","problemas de rendimiento","retroalimentación sensible","preparación para conversaciones difíciles","navegación de conflictos","comunicación efectiva en el lugar de trabajo"],"fr":["conversations difficiles sur le lieu de travail","résolution des conflits","problèmes de performance","rétroaction sensible","préparation pour les conversations difficiles","navigation des conflits","communication efficace sur le lieu de travail"],"de":["schwierige Gespräche am Arbeitsplatz","Konfliktlösung","Leistungsprobleme","sensible Rückmeldungen","Vorbereitung auf schwierige Gespräche","Navigation von Konflikten","effektive Kommunikation am Arbeitsplatz"],"pt":["conversas difíceis no local de trabalho","resolução de conflitos","feedback sensível","gestão de conflitos","comunicação no local de trabalho","desenvolvimento profissional"],"ru":["трудные разговоры на рабочем месте","решение конфликтов","деликатная обратная связь","управление конфликтами","коммуникация на рабочем месте","профессиональное развитие"],"ar":["المحادثات الصعبة في مكان العمل","حل النزاعات","تغذية الرأي الحساسة","إدارة النزاعات","التواصل في مكان العمل","التطوير المهني"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"difficult-workplace-conversations","description":"Structured approach to workplace conflicts, performance discussions, and challenging feedback using preparation-delivery-followup framework. Use when preparing for tough conversations, addressing conflicts, giving critical feedback, or navigating sensitive workplace discussions.","bodyPreview":"# Difficult Conversations Skill\n\nA structured framework for approaching challenging workplace conversations including conflicts, performance issues, sensitive feedback, and emotionally charged discussions.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Preparing for a challenging conversation with a colleague\n- Addressing performance issues with a team member\n- Delivering difficult feedback to a peer or manager\n- Navigating conflict between team members\n- Discussing sensitive topics (salary, promotion, terminati","body":"# Difficult Conversations Skill\n\nA structured framework for approaching challenging workplace conversations including conflicts, performance issues, sensitive feedback, and emotionally charged discussions.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Preparing for a challenging conversation with a colleague\n- Addressing performance issues with a team member\n- Delivering difficult feedback to a peer or manager\n- Navigating conflict between team members\n- Discussing sensitive topics (salary, promotion, termination)\n- Handling emotional or defensive reactions\n- Following up after difficult discussions\n\n## Core Framework: Preparation-Delivery-Followup\n\nDifficult conversations succeed or fail based on three phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Preparation (Before)\n\n**Purpose:** Set yourself up for a productive conversation\n\n1. **Clarify the Issue**\n   - What specifically happened? (Observable facts only)\n   - What is the impact? (On you, team, work)\n   - What do you need to change?\n\n2. **Check Your Emotions**\n   - What am I feeling? Why?\n   - Am I calm enough to have this conversation?\n   - What might trigger me during this conversation?\n\n3. **Consider Their Perspective**\n   - How might they see this situation?\n   - What constraints or pressures might they have?\n   - What do they care about that I can acknowledge?\n\n4. **Define Your Goal**\n   - What outcome do I want?\n   - What is the minimum acceptable result?\n   - What am I willing to compromise on?\n\n### Phase 2: Delivery (During)\n\n**Purpose:** Have the conversation effectively\n\n1. **Open Neutrally**\n   - Start with facts, not judgments\n   - Express intent to understand, not accuse\n   - Create psychological safety\n\n2. **Share Your Perspective**\n   - Describe behavior, not character\n   - Focus on impact, not intention\n   - Use \"I\" statements, not \"you always\"\n\n3. **Listen Actively**\n   - Ask clarifying questions\n   - Acknowledge their viewpoint\n   - Look for shared interests\n\n4. **Seek Resolution**\n   - Propose specific actions\n   - Agree on next steps\n   - Set check-in timeline\n\n### Phase 3: Followup (After)\n\n**Purpose:** Ensure lasting resolution\n\n1. **Document Agreements**\n   - What was agreed?\n   - Who does what by when?\n   - How will you measure success?\n\n2. **Check Progress**\n   - Follow up as promised\n   - Acknowledge improvements\n   - Address continued issues promptly\n\n3. **Maintain Relationship**\n   - Separate issue from person\n   - Rebuild trust over time\n   - Watch for regression\n\n## Key Principles\n\n### Separate Impact from Intent\n\n**What happened:** Observable behavior\n**What I felt:** Your emotional response\n**What I assume:** Their intention (often wrong)\n\nFocus conversation on behavior and impact, not assumed intentions.\n\n### The SBI Model\n\n**Situation:** When and where did this happen?\n**Behavior:** What specifically did they do/say?\n**Impact:** What was the effect on you, the team, or the work?\n\n### Managing Emotions\n\n| If You Feel | Before Acting |\n| ----------- | ------------- |\n| Angry | Wait 24 hours, write but don''t send |\n| Hurt | Talk to neutral party first |\n| Anxious | Practice the conversation |\n| Defensive | Identify your contribution |\n\n### When to Escalate\n\nEscalate when:\n\n- Safety is at risk\n- Legal issues involved\n- Repeated conversations haven''t worked\n- Power dynamics prevent resolution\n- You need documentation\n\n## Conversation Types\n\n### Performance Feedback\n\n- Lead with specific examples\n- Connect to expectations/standards\n- Focus on future improvement\n- Offer support and resources\n\n### Conflict Resolution\n\n- Hear both sides separately first\n- Identify underlying interests\n- Look for win-win solutions\n- Document agreements\n\n### Sensitive Topics\n\n- Choose private, neutral setting\n- Allow time for processing\n- Be direct but compassionate\n- Respect confidentiality\n\n### Receiving Feedback\n\n- Thank them for feedback\n- Ask clarifying questions\n- Don''t defend immediately\n- Reflect before responding\n\n## References (Load When Needed)\n\n### Detailed Frameworks\n\n- **[Conversation Framework](references/conversation-framework.md)**: Complete three-phase framework with scripts and examples\n- **[Preparation Template](references/preparation-template.md)**: Worksheet for preparing before difficult conversations\n- **[Delivery Scripts](references/delivery-scripts.md)**: Opening lines, response handling, reframing techniques\n- **[Emotional Regulation](references/emotional-regulation.md)**: Managing your own emotions before and during\n\n## See Also\n\n- `feedback-mastery` skill - SBI feedback model (overlaps but more feedback-focused)\n- `professional-effective-communication` skill - General communication patterns\n\n## Example Scenarios\n\n### Scenario 1: Addressing Missed Deadlines\n\n```markdown\n**Issue:** Team member missed 3 deadlines in past month\n**Impact:** Project delayed, others blocked\n**Goal:** Understand root cause, agree on prevention plan\n\n**Opening:** \"I wanted to check in about the recent deliverables. I''ve noticed\nthe last three have come in past deadline, and I''d like to understand what''s\nhappening and how we can address it together.\"\n```\n\n### Scenario 2: Peer Conflict\n\n```markdown\n**Issue:** Colleague publicly criticized your work in meeting\n**Impact:** Embarrassed, trust damaged\n**Goal:** Address behavior, rebuild working relationship\n\n**Opening:** \"I''d like to talk about what happened in yesterday''s standup.\nWhen you said my code ''missed obvious issues,'' I felt called out in front\nof the team. I''d like to understand your concerns and find a better way\nto handle code quality feedback.\"\n```\n\n### Scenario 3: Asking Manager for Raise\n\n```markdown\n**Issue:** Feel underpaid relative to market/contribution\n**Impact:** Demotivation, considering leaving\n**Goal:** Discuss compensation, get timeline or adjustment\n\n**Opening:** \"I''d like to discuss my compensation. I''ve been here two years,\ntaken on the payments project leadership, and want to make sure my salary\nreflects my contributions and the current market.\"\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n### In Preparation\n\n- **Scripting every word** - You''ll sound robotic; prepare themes, not scripts\n- **Building a case** - This isn''t a trial; seek understanding, not winning\n- **Waiting too long** - Issues compound; address promptly\n\n### In Delivery\n\n- **Starting with \"You always...\"** - Triggers defensiveness immediately\n- **Burying the lead** - Get to the point; don''t soften excessively\n- **Asking leading questions** - \"Don''t you think...\" isn''t asking\n\n### In Followup\n\n- **Forgetting to check in** - Without follow-up, nothing changes\n- **Holding grudges** - Issue resolved means relationship continues\n- **Over-documenting** - Not everything needs written record\n\n## Success Metrics\n\nA successful difficult conversation:\n\n- Both parties feel heard\n- Specific actions are agreed\n- Relationship is preserved or improved\n- The issue doesn''t recur (or has clear escalation)\n- Neither party is blindsided later\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:08:20.883Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents requiring structured frameworks for navigating conflicts, performance issues, and sensitive feedback in workplace conversations.","zh":"适合需要结构化框架来处理冲突、性能问题和敏感反馈的对话式AI代理的工作场景。","ja":"対話型AIエージェントが衝突、パフォーマンスの問題、職場での会話におけるデリケートなフィードバックをナビゲートするために構造化フレームワークを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"대화형 AI 에이전트가 충돌, 성능 문제, 직장での 대화에서 민감한 피드백을 탐색하기 위한 구조화된 프레임워크를 필요로 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial conversacional que requieren marcos estructurados para navegar conflictos, problemas de rendimiento y comentarios sensibles en conversaciones laborales.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle conversationnelle qui nécessitent des cadres structurés pour naviguer dans les conflits, les problèmes de performance et les commentaires sensibles dans les conversations de travail.","de":"Ideal für Conversational-AI-Agents, die strukturierte Rahmenbedingungen für die Navigation von Konflikten, Leistungsproblemen und sensiblen Feedback in Arbeitsplatzgesprächen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Conversacional que requerem estruturas organizadas para navegar conflitos, problemas de desempenho e feedback sensível em conversas de local de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разговорного ИИ, требующих структурированных рамок для навигации по конфликтам, проблемам производительности и деликатной обратной связи на рабочем месте.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي التفاعلي الذين يحتاجون إلى إطارات منظمة للتنقل في النزاعات ومشكلات الأداء والتعليقات الحساسة في محادثات مكان العمل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to facilitate emotionally charged discussions, address performance issues, and deliver difficult feedback using a structured framework, leveraging protocols like active listening and conflict resolution methodologies.","zh":"赋予代理以结构化框架来促进情绪化讨论、解决性能问题、使用主动倾听和冲突解决方法等协议来提供困难的反馈。","ja":"エージェントに構造化フレームワークを使用して感情的な議論を促進し、パフォーマンスの問題に対処し、アクティブリスニングや紛争解決方法などのプロトコルを利用して難しいフィードバックを提供する機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 구조화된 프레임워크를 사용하여 감정적인 토론을 촉진하고 성능 문제를 해결하며 활성倾听 및 분쟁 해결 방법과 같은 프로토콜을 활용하여 어려운 피드백을 제공할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a facilitar discusiones emocionalmente cargadas, abordar problemas de rendimiento y entregar comentarios difíciles utilizando un marco estructurado, aprovechando protocolos como la escucha activa y las metodologías de resolución de conflictos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de faciliter des discussions chargées émotionnellement, d''aborder les problèmes de performance et de fournir des commentaires difficiles en utilisant un cadre structuré, en exploitant des protocoles tels que l''écoute active et les méthodologies de résolution de conflits.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, emotionale Diskussionen zu erleichtern, Leistungsprobleme anzusprechen und schwieriges Feedback unter Verwendung eines strukturierten Rahmens zu liefern, der Protokolle wie aktives Zuhören und Konfliktlösungsmethoden nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a facilitar discussões carregadas de emoção, abordar problemas de desempenho e fornecer feedback difícil usando uma estrutura organizada, aproveitando protocolos como escuta ativa e metodologias de resolução de conflitos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью облегчить эмоционально заряженные обсуждения, решить проблемы производительности и передать трудную обратную связь, используя структурированную основу, опираясь на протоколы, такие как активное слушание и методологии разрешения конфликтов.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تسهيل المناقشات المحملة عاطفياً، ومعالجة مشكلات الأداء، وتقديم تعليقات صعبة باستخدام إطار منظم، مستفيداً من بروتوكولات مثل الاستماع النشط ومنهجيات حل النزاعات."},"useCases":{"en":["Navigating inter-team conflicts","Delivering performance improvement feedback","Discussing sensitive topics like salary and promotion"],"zh":["处理团队间冲突","提供绩效改进反馈","讨论薪水和晋升等敏感话题"],"ja":["チーム間の対立を解決する","パフォーマンス改善のフィードバックを提供する","給与や昇進などのデリケートな話題を議論する"],"ko":["팀 간의 충돌을 해결하는こと","성과 개선 피드백을 제공하는 것","급여 및 승진 등 민감한 주제를 토론하는 것"],"es":["Navegación de conflictos interequipo","Entrega de comentarios de mejora del rendimiento","Discusión de temas sensibles como salario y promoción"],"fr":["Navigation de conflits interéquipes","Fourniture de commentaires d''amélioration de la performance","Discussion de sujets sensibles tels que le salaire et la promotion"],"de":["Navigation von Teamkonflikten","Lieferung von Leistungsverbesserungsfeedback","Diskussion sensibler Themen wie Gehalt und Beförderung"],"pt":["Navegação de conflitos entre equipes","Fornecimento de feedback de melhoria de desempenho","Discussão de tópicos sensíveis como salário e promoção"],"ru":["Навигация в межкомандных конфликтах","Предоставление обратной связи по улучшению производительности","Обсуждение деликатных тем, таких как зарплата и продвижение"],"ar":["تنقل النزاعات بين الفرق","تقديم تعليقات لتحسين الأداء","مناقشة مواضيع حساسة مثل الراتب والترقية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of workplace dynamics and human resources protocols","May not be applicable in all cultural or organizational contexts"],"zh":["需要了解职场动态和人力资源协议","可能不适用于所有文化或组织环境"],"ja":["職場のダイナミクスと人事プロトコルを理解する必要がある","すべての文化や組織の環境に適用できない場合がある"],"ko":["직장 동态와 인적 자원 프로토콜을 이해해야 함","모든 문화나 조직 환경에 적용할 수 없는 경우가 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la dinámica laboral y los protocolos de recursos humanos","Puede que no sea aplicable en todos los contextos culturales o organizacionales"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la dynamique de travail et des protocoles des ressources humaines","Peut ne pas être applicable dans tous les contextes culturels ou organisationnels"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Arbeitsplatzdynamik und der Personalprotokolle","Kann möglicherweise nicht in allen kulturellen oder organisatorischen Kontexten anwendbar sein"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da dinâmica do local de trabalho e protocolos de recursos humanos","Pode não ser aplicável em todos os contextos culturais ou organizacionais"],"ru":["Требует понимания динамики рабочего места и протоколов управления человеческими ресурсами","Может быть не применим во всех культурных или организационных контекстах"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم ديناميكية مكان العمل وبروتوكولات الموارد البشرية","يمكن ألا يكون قابلاً للتطبيق في جميع السياقات الثقافية أو التنظيمية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
