"测试验证","选项呈现","工作流执行","代码清理","开发分支管理","软件开发"],"ja":["開発ブランチ","テストの検証","オプションの提示","ワークフローの実行","コードのクリーンアップ","開発ブランチの管理","ソフトウェア開発"],"ko":["개발 브랜치","테스트 검증","옵션 제공","워크플로우 처리","코드 정리","개발 브랜치 관리","소프트웨어 개발"],"es":["finalizar rama de desarrollo","desarrollo de software","pruebas de software","gestión de desarrollo","eficiencia en el desarrollo","calidad en el desarrollo"],"fr":["terminer une branche de développement","développement de logiciels","tests de logiciels","gestion de développement","efficacité dans le développement","qualité dans le développement"],"de":["Entwicklungszweig abschließen","Softwareentwicklung","Softwaretests","Entwicklungsmanagement","Effizienz in der Entwicklung","Qualität in der Entwicklung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de software","ramos de desenvolvimento","verificação de testes","workflows","eficiência","desenvolvedores"],"ru":["разработка программного обеспечения","ветки разработки","проверка тестов","рабочие процессы","эффективность","разработчики"],"ar":["تطوير البرمجيات","فروع التطوير","التحقق من الاختبارات","سير العمل","الكفاءة","المطوّرون"]}},"owner":"dwalleck","repo":"kiro-starter-kit","repoPath":"dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"finishing-a-development-branch","description":"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup","bodyPreview":"# Finishing a Development Branch\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide completion of development work by presenting clear options and handling chosen workflow.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify tests → Present options → Execute choice → Clean up.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Verify Tests\n\n**Before presenting options, verify tests pass:**\n\n```bash\n# Run project''s test suite\nnpm test / cargo test / pytest / go test ./...\n`","body":"# Finishing a Development Branch\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide completion of development work by presenting clear options and handling chosen workflow.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify tests → Present options → Execute choice → Clean up.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Verify Tests\n\n**Before presenting options, verify tests pass:**\n\n```bash\n# Run project''s test suite\nnpm test / cargo test / pytest / go test ./...\n```\n\n**If tests fail:**\n```\nTests failing (<N> failures). Must fix before completing:\n\n[Show failures]\n\nCannot proceed with merge/PR until tests pass.\n```\n\nStop. Don''t proceed to Step 2.\n\n**If tests pass:** Continue to Step 2.\n\n### Step 2: Determine Base Branch\n\n```bash\n# Try common base branches\ngit merge-base HEAD main 2>/dev/null || git merge-base HEAD master 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nOr ask: \"This branch split from main - is that correct?\"\n\n### Step 3: Present Options\n\nPresent exactly these 4 options:\n\n```\nImplementation complete. What would you like to do?\n\n1. Merge back to <base-branch> locally\n2. Push and create a Pull Request\n3. Keep the branch as-is (I''ll handle it later)\n4. Discard this work\n\nWhich option?\n```\n\n**Don''t add explanation** - keep options concise.\n\n### Step 4: Execute Choice\n\n#### Option 1: Merge Locally\n\n```bash\n# Switch to base branch\ngit checkout <base-branch>\n\n# Pull latest\ngit pull\n\n# Merge feature branch\ngit merge <feature-branch>\n\n# Verify tests on merged result\n<test command>\n\n# If tests pass\ngit branch -d <feature-branch>\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n#### Option 2: Push and Create PR\n\n```bash\n# Push branch\ngit push -u origin <feature-branch>\n\n# Create PR\ngh pr create --title \"<title>\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n<2-3 bullets of what changed>\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] <verification steps>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n#### Option 3: Keep As-Is\n\nReport: \"Keeping branch <name>. Worktree preserved at <path>.\"\n\n**Don''t cleanup worktree.**\n\n#### Option 4: Discard\n\n**Confirm first:**\n```\nThis will permanently delete:\n- Branch <name>\n- All commits: <commit-list>\n- Worktree at <path>\n\nType ''discard'' to confirm.\n```\n\nWait for exact confirmation.\n\nIf confirmed:\n```bash\ngit checkout <base-branch>\ngit branch -D <feature-branch>\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n### Step 5: Cleanup Worktree\n\n**For Options 1, 2, 4:**\n\nCheck if in worktree:\n```bash\ngit worktree list | grep $(git branch --show-current)\n```\n\nIf yes:\n```bash\ngit worktree remove <worktree-path>\n```\n\n**For Option 3:** Keep worktree.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Option | Merge | Push | Keep Worktree | Cleanup Branch |\n|--------|-------|------|---------------|----------------|\n| 1. Merge locally | ✓ | - | - | ✓ |\n| 2. Create PR | - | ✓ | ✓ | - |\n| 3. Keep as-is | - | - | ✓ | - |\n| 4. Discard | - | - | - | ✓ (force) |\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**Skipping test verification**\n- **Problem:** Merge broken code, create failing PR\n- **Fix:** Always verify tests before offering options\n\n**Open-ended questions**\n- **Problem:** \"What should I do next?\" → ambiguous\n- **Fix:** Present exactly 4 structured options\n\n**Automatic worktree cleanup**\n- **Problem:** Remove worktree when might need it (Option 2, 3)\n- **Fix:** Only cleanup for Options 1 and 4\n\n**No confirmation for discard**\n- **Problem:** Accidentally delete work\n- **Fix:** Require typed \"discard\" confirmation\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Proceed with failing tests\n- Merge without verifying tests on result\n- Delete work without confirmation\n- Force-push without explicit request\n\n**Always:**\n- Verify tests before offering options\n- Present exactly 4 options\n- Get typed confirmation for Option 4\n- Clean up worktree for Options 1 & 4 only\n\n## Integration\n\n**Called by:**\n- **subagent-driven-development** (Step 7) - After all tasks complete\n- **executing-plans** (Step 5) - After all batches complete\n\n**Pairs with:**\n- **using-git-worktrees** - Cleans up worktree created by that skill\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:09:55.630Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing streamlined workflow management and test verification.","zh":"非常适合需要简化工作流管理和测试验证的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントがワークフローの管理とテストの検証を簡素化する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 워크플로 관리와 테스트 검증을 간소화해야 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una gestión de flujo de trabajo simplificada y verificación de pruebas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une gestion de flux de travail simplifiée et de vérification de tests.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine vereinfachte Workflow-Verwaltung und Testverifizierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho simplificado e verificação de testes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходим упрощенный менеджмент рабочего процесса и проверка тестов.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تطوير الوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة تدفق عمل مبسطة وتحقق من الاختبارات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute a development branch completion workflow by verifying tests with npm, cargo, pytest, or go test, presenting clear options, and handling chosen workflow execution and cleanup.","zh":"赋予代理执行开发分支完成工作流的能力，通过使用npm、cargo、pytest或go test验证测试，并提供清晰的选项，处理所选工作流的执行和清理。","ja":"エージェントが開発ブランチの完了ワークフローを実行する能力を付与し、npm、cargo、pytest、またはgo testを使用してテストを検証し、明確なオプションを提示し、選択されたワークフローの実行とクリーンアップを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 개발 브랜치 완성 워크플로를 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 npm, cargo, pytest 또는 go test를 사용하여 테스트를 검증하고 명확한 옵션을 제공하며 선택한 워크플로의 실행 및 정리를 처리합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes ejecutar un flujo de trabajo de finalización de rama de desarrollo verificando pruebas con npm, cargo, pytest o go test, presentando opciones claras y manejando la ejecución y limpieza del flujo de trabajo elegido.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter un flux de travail de finalisation de branche de développement en vérifiant les tests avec npm, cargo, pytest ou go test, en présentant des options claires et en gérant l''exécution et le nettoyage du flux de travail choisi.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, einen Entwicklungszweig-Abschluss-Workflow auszuführen, indem Tests mit npm, cargo, pytest oder go test verifiziert werden, klare Optionen präsentiert werden und die Ausführung und Bereinigung des gewählten Workflows gehandhabt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar um fluxo de trabalho de conclusão de ramo de desenvolvimento, verificando testes com npm, cargo, pytest ou go test, apresentando opções claras e tratando a execução e limpeza do fluxo de trabalho escolhido.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять рабочий процесс завершения ветки разработки, проверяя тесты с помощью npm, cargo, pytest или go test, предлагая ясные варианты и обрабатывая выполнение и очистку выбранного рабочего процесса.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنفيذ تدفق عمل إكمال فرع التطوير عن طريق التحقق من الاختبارات باستخدام npm و cargo و pytest أو go test ، مع تقديم خيارات واضحة ومعالجة تنفيذ تدفق العمل والتنظيف المحدد."},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying tests before deployment","Automating workflow execution with npm test or cargo test","Cleaning up development branches after completion"],"zh":["部署前验证测试","使用npm test或cargo test自动执行工作流","完成后清理开发分支"],"ja":["デプロイ前のテストの検証","npm testまたはcargo testを使用してワークフローの自動実行","完了後の開発ブランチのクリーンアップ"],"ko":["배포 전 테스트 검증","npm test 또는 cargo test를 사용하여 워크플로 자동 실행","완료 후 개발 브랜치 정리"],"es":["Verificar pruebas antes de la implementación","Automatizar la ejecución de flujo de trabajo con npm test o cargo test","Limpiar ramas de desarrollo después de la finalización"],"fr":["Vérifier les tests avant le déploiement","Automatiser l''exécution du flux de travail avec npm test ou cargo test","Nettoyer les branches de développement après l''achèvement"],"de":["Tests vor der Bereitstellung überprüfen","Workflow-Ausführung mit npm test oder cargo test automatisieren","Entwicklungszweige nach Abschluss bereinigen"],"pt":["Verificar testes antes da implantação","Automatizar a execução do fluxo de trabalho com npm test ou cargo test","Limpar ramos de desenvolvimento após a conclusão"],"ru":["Проверка тестов перед развертыванием","Автоматизация выполнения рабочего процесса с помощью npm test или cargo test","Очистка веток разработки после завершения"],"ar":["التحقق من الاختبارات قبل النشر","تأتمتة تنفيذ تدفق العمل باستخدام npm test أو cargo test","تنظيف فروع التطوير بعد الإكمال"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires project test suite setup with npm, cargo, pytest, or go test","Limited to development branch completion workflow"],"zh":["需要使用npm、cargo、pytest或go test设置项目测试套件","仅限开发分支完成工作流"],"ja":["npm、cargo、pytest、またはgo testを使用してプロジェクトのテストスイートを設定する必要がある","開発ブランチの完了ワークフローに限定される"],"ko":["npm, cargo, pytest 또는 go test를 사용하여 프로젝트 테스트套件을 설정해야 함","개발 브랜치 완성 워크플로에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere configuración del conjunto de pruebas del proyecto con npm, cargo, pytest o go test","Limitado al flujo de trabajo de finalización de rama de desarrollo"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration du jeu de tests du projet avec npm, cargo, pytest ou go test","Limité au flux de travail de finalisation de branche de développement"],"de":["Benötigt eine Einrichtung des Projekttestsatzes mit npm, cargo, pytest oder go test","Begrenzt auf den Workflow für die Fertigstellung des Entwicklungszweigs"],"pt":["Exige configuração do conjunto de testes do projeto com npm, cargo, pytest ou go test","Limitado ao fluxo de trabalho de conclusão de ramo de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Требует настройки набора тестов проекта с помощью npm, cargo, pytest или go test","Ограничен рабочим процессом завершения ветки разработки"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مجموعة اختبارات المشروع باستخدام npm و cargo و pytest أو go test ","محدود بتدفق عمل إكمال فرع التطوير"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/qa-test-planner', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'qa-test-planner', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z', '2026-02-18T14:10:05.880Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/qa-test-planner","name":"qa-test-planner","description":{"zh":"QA测试计划器是一种综合技能，用于创建测试计划、生成手动测试用例、构建回归测试套件和记录缺陷","ja":"QAテストプランナーは、テスト計画を作成し、手動テストケースを生成し、回帰テストスイートを構築し、バグを記録するための包括的なスキルです","ko":"QA 테스트 플래너는 테스트 계획을 생성하고 수동 테스트 케이스를 생성하며 회귀 테스트套件을 구축하고 결함을 기록하는 데 사용되는 포괄적인 기술입니다","es":"El planificador de pruebas QA es una habilidad integral para ingenieros de QA que crea planes de pruebas, genera casos de prueba manuales y valida diseños.","fr":"Le planificateur de tests QA est une compétence globale pour les ingénieurs QA qui crée des plans de tests, génère des cas de test manuels et valide les conceptions.","de":"Der QA-Testplaner ist eine umfassende Fähigkeit für QA-Ingenieure, die Testpläne erstellt, manuelle Testfälle generiert und Entwürfe validiert.","pt":"O Planejador de Testes de QA é uma habilidade abrangente para engenheiros de QA criarem planos de teste, gerarem casos de teste manuais e construírem suites de teste de regressão","ru":"Планировщик тестирования QA - это всесторонняя способность для инженеров QA создавать планы тестирования, генерировать ручные тестовые случаи и строить наборы тестирования регрессии","ar":"مخطط اختبار جودة QA هو مهارة شاملة لمهندسي جودة QA لإنشاء خطط اختبار وإنشاء حالات اختبار يدوي وتحديث مجموعات اختبار الانحدار","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"QA测试计划器 - 自动生成测试用例","ja":"QAテストプランナー - テストケースを自動生成","ko":"QA 테스트 플래너 - 자동 테스트 케이스 생성","es":"Planificador de pruebas QA: crea planes y casos de prueba","fr":"Planificateur de tests QA : créez des plans et des cas de...","de":"QA-Testplaner: Erstellen von Testplänen und -fällen","pt":"Planejador de Testes de QA: crie planos de teste personal...","ru":"Планировщик тестирования QA: создавайте индивидуальные пл...","ar":"مخطط اختبار جودة QA: أنشئ خطط اختبار مخصصة","en":"qa-test-planner"},"description":{"zh":"QA测试计划器是一种综合技能，用于创建测试计划、生成手动测试用例、构建回归测试套件和记录缺陷","ja":"QAテストプランナーは、テスト計画を作成し、手動テストケースを生成し、回帰テストスイートを構築し、バグを記録するための包括的なスキルです","ko":"QA 테스트 플래너는 테스트 계획을 생성하고 수동 테스트 케이스를 생성하며 회귀 테스트套件을 구축하고 결함을 기록하는 데 사용되는 포괄적인 기술입니다","es":"El planificador de pruebas QA es una habilidad integral para ingenieros de QA que crea planes de pruebas, genera casos de prueba manuales y valida diseños.","fr":"Le planificateur de tests QA est une compétence globale pour les ingénieurs QA qui crée des plans de tests, génère des cas de test manuels et valide les conc...","de":"Der QA-Testplaner ist eine umfassende Fähigkeit für QA-Ingenieure, die Testpläne erstellt, manuelle Testfälle generiert und Entwürfe validiert.","pt":"O Planejador de Testes de QA é uma habilidade abrangente para engenheiros de QA criarem planos de teste, gerarem casos de teste manuais e construírem suites ...","ru":"Планировщик тестирования QA - это всесторонняя способность для инженеров QA создавать планы тестирования, генерировать ручные тестовые случаи и строить набор...","ar":"مخطط اختبار جودة QA هو مهارة شاملة لمهندسي جودة QA لإنشاء خطط اختبار وإنشاء حالات اختبار يدوي وتحديث مجموعات اختبار الانحدار","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["创建测试计划","生成手动测试用例","构建回归测试套件","验证设计与Figma","记录缺陷"],"ja":["テスト計画を作成","手動テストケースを生成","回帰テストスイートを構築","デザインをFigmaと検証","バグを記録"],"ko":["테스트 계획 생성","수동 테스트 케이스 생성","회귀 테스트套件 구축","디자인을 Figma와 검증","결함 기록"],"es":["Creación de planes de pruebas","Generación de casos de prueba manuales","Validación de diseños con Figma","Creación de suites de pruebas de regresión","Documentación de errores de manera efectiva"],"fr":["Création de plans de tests","Génération de cas de test manuels","Validation des conceptions avec Figma","Création de suites de tests de régression","Documentation des erreurs de manière efficace"],"de":["Erstellung von Testplänen","Generierung von manuellen Testfällen","Validierung von Entwürfen mit Figma","Erstellung von Regressions-Test-Suiten","Dokumentation von Fehlern auf effektive Weise"],"pt":["Crie planos de teste personalizados","Gere casos de teste manuais","Construa suites de teste de regressão","Valide designs contra Figma","Documente bugs de forma eficaz"],"ru":["Создавайте индивидуальные планы тестирования","Генерируйте ручные тестовые случаи","Стройте наборы тестирования регрессии","Валидируйте дизайны против Figma","Документируйте ошибки эффективно"],"ar":["أنشئ خطط اختبار مخصصة","أنشئ حالات اختبار يدوي","ابني مجموعات اختبار الانحدار","검증 التصاميم مقابل Figma","وثق الأخطاء بفعالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["QA测试","测试计划","手动测试用例","回归测试","Figma","缺陷记录"],"ja":["QAテスト","テスト計画","手動テストケース","回帰テスト","Figma","バグ記録"],"ko":["QA 테스트","테스트 계획","수동 테스트 케이스","회귀 테스트","Figma","결함 기록"],"es":["planificador de pruebas QA","pruebas de software","ingenieros de QA","casos de prueba","validación de diseños","Figma","pruebas de regresión"],"fr":["planificateur de tests QA","tests de logiciel","ingénieurs QA","cas de test","validation des conceptions","Figma","tests de régression"],"de":["QA-Testplaner","Software-Tests","QA-Ingenieure","Testfälle","Validierung von Entwürfen","Figma","Regressions-Tests"],"pt":["planejador de testes de QA","testes de software","engenharia de QA","planos de teste personalizados","casos de teste manuais","suites de teste de regressão"],"ru":["Планировщик тестирования QA","тестирование программного обеспечения","инженерия QA","индивидуальные планы тестирования","ручные тестовые случаи","наборы тестирования регрессии"],"ar":["مخطط اختبار جودة QA","اختبار البرمجيات","هندسة جودة QA","خطط اختبار مخصصة","حالات اختبار يدوي","مجموعات اختبار الانحدار"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"qa-test-planner","description":"Generate comprehensive test plans, manual test cases, regression test suites, and bug reports for QA engineers. Includes Figma MCP integration for design validation.","bodyPreview":"# QA Test Planner\n\nA comprehensive skill for QA engineers to create test plans, generate manual test cases, build regression test suites, validate designs against Figma, and document bugs effectively.\n\n> **Activation:** This skill is triggered only when explicitly called by name (e.g., `/qa-test-planner`, `qa-test-planner`, or `use the skill qa-test-planner`).\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Create a test plan:**\n```\n\"Create a test plan for the user authentication feature\"\n```\n\n**Generate test cases:**","body":"# QA Test Planner\n\nA comprehensive skill for QA engineers to create test plans, generate manual test cases, build regression test suites, validate designs against Figma, and document bugs effectively.\n\n> **Activation:** This skill is triggered only when explicitly called by name (e.g., `/qa-test-planner`, `qa-test-planner`, or `use the skill qa-test-planner`).\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Create a test plan:**\n```\n\"Create a test plan for the user authentication feature\"\n```\n\n**Generate test cases:**\n```\n\"Generate manual test cases for the checkout flow\"\n```\n\n**Build regression suite:**\n```\n\"Build a regression test suite for the payment module\"\n```\n\n**Validate against Figma:**\n```\n\"Compare the login page against the Figma design at [URL]\"\n```\n\n**Create bug report:**\n```\n\"Create a bug report for the form validation issue\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | What You Get | Time |\n|------|--------------|------|\n| Test Plan | Strategy, scope, schedule, risks | 10-15 min |\n| Test Cases | Step-by-step instructions, expected results | 5-10 min each |\n| Regression Suite | Smoke tests, critical paths, execution order | 15-20 min |\n| Figma Validation | Design-implementation comparison, discrepancy list | 10-15 min |\n| Bug Report | Reproducible steps, environment, evidence | 5 min |\n\n---\n\n## How It Works\n\n```\nYour Request\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. ANALYZE                                          │\n│    • Parse feature/requirement                      │\n│    • Identify test types needed                     │\n│    • Determine scope and priorities                 │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. GENERATE                                         │\n│    • Create structured deliverables                 │\n│    • Apply templates and best practices             │\n│    • Include edge cases and variations              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. VALIDATE                                         │\n│    • Check completeness                             │\n│    • Verify traceability                            │\n│    • Ensure actionable steps                        │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\nQA Deliverable Ready\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\n### Interactive Scripts\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `./scripts/generate_test_cases.sh` | Create test cases interactively | Step-by-step prompts |\n| `./scripts/create_bug_report.sh` | Generate bug reports | Guided input collection |\n\n### Natural Language\n\n| Request | Output |\n|---------|--------|\n| \"Create test plan for {feature}\" | Complete test plan document |\n| \"Generate {N} test cases for {feature}\" | Numbered test cases with steps |\n| \"Build smoke test suite\" | Critical path tests |\n| \"Compare with Figma at {URL}\" | Visual validation checklist |\n| \"Document bug: {description}\" | Structured bug report |\n\n---\n\n## Core Deliverables\n\n### 1. Test Plans\n- Test scope and objectives\n- Testing approach and strategy\n- Environment requirements\n- Entry/exit criteria\n- Risk assessment\n- Timeline and milestones\n\n### 2. Manual Test Cases\n- Step-by-step instructions\n- Expected vs actual results\n- Preconditions and setup\n- Test data requirements\n- Priority and severity\n\n### 3. Regression Suites\n- Smoke tests (15-30 min)\n- Full regression (2-4 hours)\n- Targeted regression (30-60 min)\n- Execution order and dependencies\n\n### 4. Figma Validation\n- Component-by-component comparison\n- Spacing and typography checks\n- Color and visual consistency\n- Interactive state validation\n\n### 5. Bug Reports\n- Clear reproduction steps\n- Environment details\n- Evidence (screenshots, logs)\n- Severity and priority\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Avoid | Why | Instead |\n|-------|-----|---------|\n| Vague test steps | Can''t reproduce | Specific actions + expected results |\n| Missing preconditions | Tests fail unexpectedly | Document all setup requirements |\n| No test data | Tester blocked | Provide sample data or generation |\n| Generic bug titles | Hard to track | Specific: \"[Feature] issue when [action]\" |\n| Skip edge cases | Miss critical bugs | Include boundary values, nulls |\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n**Test Plan:**\n- [ ] Scope clearly defined (in/out)\n- [ ] Entry/exit criteria specified\n- [ ] Risks identified with mitigations\n- [ ] Timeline realistic\n\n**Test Cases:**\n- [ ] Each step has expected result\n- [ ] Preconditions documented\n- [ ] Test data available\n- [ ] Priority assigned\n\n**Bug Reports:**\n- [ ] Reproducible steps\n- [ ] Environment documented\n- [ ] Screenshots/evidence attached\n- [ ] Severity/priority set\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [Test Case Templates](references/test_case_templates.md) - Standard formats for all test types\n- [Bug Report Templates](references/bug_report_templates.md) - Documentation templates\n- [Regression Testing Guide](references/regression_testing.md) - Suite building and execution\n- [Figma Validation Guide](references/figma_validation.md) - Design-implementation validation\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Test Case Structure</strong></summary>\n\n### Standard Test Case Format\n\n```markdown\n## TC-001: [Test Case Title]\n\n**Priority:** High | Medium | Low\n**Type:** Functional | UI | Integration | Regression\n**Status:** Not Run | Pass | Fail | Blocked\n\n### Objective\n[What are we testing and why]\n\n### Preconditions\n- [Setup requirement 1]\n- [Setup requirement 2]\n- [Test data needed]\n\n### Test Steps\n1. [Action to perform]\n   **Expected:** [What should happen]\n\n2. [Action to perform]\n   **Expected:** [What should happen]\n\n3. [Action to perform]\n   **Expected:** [What should happen]\n\n### Test Data\n- Input: [Test data values]\n- User: [Test account details]\n- Configuration: [Environment settings]\n\n### Post-conditions\n- [System state after test]\n- [Cleanup required]\n\n### Notes\n- [Edge cases to consider]\n- [Related test cases]\n- [Known issues]\n```\n\n### Test Types\n\n| Type | Focus | Example |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| Functional | Business logic | Login with valid credentials |\n| UI/Visual | Appearance, layout | Button matches Figma design |\n| Integration | Component interaction | API returns data to frontend |\n| Regression | Existing functionality | Previous features still work |\n| Performance | Speed, load handling | Page loads under 3 seconds |\n| Security | Vulnerabilities | SQL injection prevented |\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Test Plan Template</strong></summary>\n\n### Test Plan Structure\n\n```markdown\n# Test Plan: [Feature/Release Name]\n\n## Executive Summary\n- Feature/product being tested\n- Testing objectives\n- Key risks\n- Timeline overview\n\n## Test Scope\n\n**In Scope:**\n- Features to be tested\n- Test types (functional, UI, performance)\n- Platforms and environments\n- User flows and scenarios\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Features not being tested\n- Known limitations\n- Third-party integrations (if applicable)\n\n## Test Strategy\n\n**Test Types:**\n- Manual testing\n- Exploratory testing\n- Regression testing\n- Integration testing\n- User acceptance testing\n\n**Test Approach:**\n- Black box testing\n- Positive and negative testing\n- Boundary value analysis\n- Equivalence partitioning\n\n## Test Environment\n- Operating systems\n- Browsers and versions\n- Devices (mobile, tablet, desktop)\n- Test data requirements\n- Backend/API environments\n\n## Entry Criteria\n- [ ] Requirements documented\n- [ ] Designs finalized\n- [ ] Test environment ready\n- [ ] Test data prepared\n- [ ] Build deployed\n\n## Exit Criteria\n- [ ] All high-priority test cases executed\n- [ ] 90%+ test case pass rate\n- [ ] All critical bugs fixed\n- [ ] No open high-severity bugs\n- [ ] Regression suite passed\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Probability | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|-------------|--------|------------|\n| [Risk 1] | H/M/L | H/M/L | [Mitigation] |\n\n## Test Deliverables\n- Test plan document\n- Test cases\n- Test execution reports\n- Bug reports\n- Test summary report\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Bug Reporting</strong></summary>\n\n### Bug Report Template\n\n```markdown\n# BUG-[ID]: [Clear, specific title]\n\n**Severity:** Critical | High | Medium | Low\n**Priority:** P0 | P1 | P2 | P3\n**Type:** Functional | UI | Performance | Security\n**Status:** Open | In Progress | Fixed | Closed\n\n## Environment\n- **OS:** [Windows 11, macOS 14, etc.]\n- **Browser:** [Chrome 120, Firefox 121, etc.]\n- **Device:** [Desktop, iPhone 15, etc.]\n- **Build:** [Version/commit]\n- **URL:** [Page where bug occurs]\n\n## Description\n[Clear, concise description of the issue]\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n1. [Specific step]\n2. [Specific step]\n3. [Specific step]\n\n## Expected Behavior\n[What should happen]\n\n## Actual Behavior\n[What actually happens]\n\n## Visual Evidence\n- Screenshot: [attached]\n- Video: [link if applicable]\n- Console errors: [paste errors]\n\n## Impact\n- **User Impact:** [How many users affected]\n- **Frequency:** [Always, Sometimes, Rarely]\n- **Workaround:** [If one exists]\n\n## Additional Context\n- Related to: [Feature/ticket]\n- Regression: [Yes/No]\n- Figma design: [Link if UI bug]\n```\n\n### Severity Definitions\n\n| Level | Criteria | Examples |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| **Critical (P0)** | System crash, data loss, security | Payment fails, login broken |\n| **High (P1)** | Major feature broken, no workaround | Search not working |\n| **Medium (P2)** | Feature partial, workaround exists | Filter missing one option |\n| **Low (P3)** | Cosmetic, rare edge cases | Typo, minor alignment |\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Figma MCP Integration</strong></summary>\n\n### Design Validation Workflow\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n- Figma MCP server configured\n- Access to Figma design files\n- Figma URLs for components/pages\n\n**Process:**\n\n1. **Get Design Specs from Figma**\n```\n\"Get the button specifications from Figma file [URL]\"\n\nResponse includes:\n- Dimensions (width, height)\n- Colors (background, text, border)\n- Typography (font, size, weight)\n- Spacing (padding, margin)\n- Border radius\n- States (default, hover, active, disabled)\n```\n\n2. **Compare Implementation**\n```\nTC: Primary Button Visual Validation\n1. Inspect primary button in browser dev tools\n2. Compare against Figma specs:\n   - Dimensions: 120x40px\n   - Border-radius: 8px\n   - Background color: #0066FF\n   - Font: 16px Medium #FFFFFF\n3. Document discrepancies\n```\n\n3. **Create Bug if Mismatch**\n```\nBUG: Primary button color doesn''t match design\nSeverity: Medium\nExpected (Figma): #0066FF\nActual (Implementation): #0052CC\nScreenshot: [attached]\nFigma link: [specific component]\n```\n\n### What to Validate\n\n| Element | What to Check | Tool |\n|---------|---------------|------|\n| Colors | Hex values exact | Browser color picker |\n| Spacing | Padding/margin px | DevTools computed styles |\n| Typography | Font, size, weight | DevTools font panel |\n| Layout | Width, height, position | DevTools box model |\n| States | Hover, active, focus | Manual interaction |\n| Responsive | Breakpoint behavior | DevTools device mode |\n\n### Example Queries\n```\n\"Get button specifications from Figma design [URL]\"\n\"Compare navigation menu implementation against Figma design\"\n\"Extract spacing values for dashboard layout from Figma\"\n\"List all color tokens used in Figma design system\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Regression Testing</strong></summary>\n\n### Suite Structure\n\n| Suite Type | Duration | Frequency | Coverage |\n|------------|----------|-----------|----------|\n| Smoke | 15-30 min | Daily | Critical paths only |\n| Targeted | 30-60 min | Per change | Affected areas |\n| Full | 2-4 hours | Weekly/Release | Comprehensive |\n| Sanity | 10-15 min | After hotfix | Quick validation |\n\n### Building a Regression Suite\n\n**Step 1: Identify Critical Paths**\n- What can users NOT live without?\n- What generates revenue?\n- What handles sensitive data?\n- What''s used most frequently?\n\n**Step 2: Prioritize Test Cases**\n\n| Priority | Description | Must Run |\n|----------|-------------|----------|\n| P0 | Business-critical, security | Always |\n| P1 | Major features, common flows | Weekly+ |\n| P2 | Minor features, edge cases | Releases |\n\n**Step 3: Execution Order**\n1. Smoke first - if fails, stop and fix build\n2. P0 tests next - must pass before proceeding\n3. P1 then P2 - track all failures\n4. Exploratory - find unexpected issues\n\n### Pass/Fail Criteria\n\n**PASS:**\n- All P0 tests pass\n- 90%+ P1 tests pass\n- No critical bugs open\n\n**FAIL (Block Release):**\n- Any P0 test fails\n- Critical bug discovered\n- Security vulnerability\n- Data loss scenario\n\n**CONDITIONAL:**\n- P1 failures with workarounds\n- Known issues documented\n- Fix plan in place\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Deep Dive: Test Execution Tracking</strong></summary>\n\n### Test Run Report Template\n\n```markdown\n# Test Run: [Release Version]\n\n**Date:** 2024-01-15\n**Build:** v2.5.0-rc1\n**Tester:** [Name]\n**Environment:** Staging\n\n## Summary\n- Total Test Cases: 150\n- Executed: 145\n- Passed: 130\n- Failed: 10\n- Blocked: 5\n- Not Run: 5\n- Pass Rate: 90%\n\n## Test Cases by Priority\n\n| Priority | Total | Pass | Fail | Blocked |\n|----------|-------|------|------|---------|\n| P0 (Critical) | 25 | 23 | 2 | 0 |\n| P1 (High) | 50 | 45 | 3 | 2 |\n| P2 (Medium) | 50 | 45 | 3 | 2 |\n| P3 (Low) | 25 | 17 | 2 | 1 |\n\n## Critical Failures\n- TC-045: Payment processing fails\n  - Bug: BUG-234\n  - Status: Open\n\n## Blocked Tests\n- TC-112: Dashboard widget (API endpoint down)\n\n## Risks\n- 2 critical bugs blocking release\n- Payment integration needs attention\n\n## Next Steps\n- Retest after BUG-234 fix\n- Complete remaining 5 test cases\n- Run full regression before sign-off\n```\n\n### Coverage Tracking\n\n```markdown\n## Coverage Matrix\n\n| Feature | Requirements | Test Cases | Status | Gaps |\n|---------|--------------|------------|--------|------|\n| Login | 8 | 12 | Complete | None |\n| Checkout | 15 | 10 | Partial | Payment errors |\n| Dashboard | 12 | 15 | Complete | None |\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>QA Process Workflow</strong></summary>\n\n### Phase 1: Planning\n- [ ] Review requirements and designs\n- [ ] Create test plan\n- [ ] Identify test scenarios\n- [ ] Estimate effort and timeline\n- [ ] Set up test environment\n\n### Phase 2: Test Design\n- [ ] Write test cases\n- [ ] Review test cases with team\n- [ ] Prepare test data\n- [ ] Build regression suite\n- [ ] Get Figma design access\n\n### Phase 3: Execution\n- [ ] Execute test cases\n- [ ] Log bugs with clear steps\n- [ ] Validate against Figma (UI tests)\n- [ ] Track test progress\n- [ ] Communicate blockers\n\n### Phase 4: Reporting\n- [ ] Compile test results\n- [ ] Analyze coverage\n- [ ] Document risks\n- [ ] Provide go/no-go recommendation\n- [ ] Archive test artifacts\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Best Practices</strong></summary>\n\n### Test Case Writing\n\n**DO:**\n- Be specific and unambiguous\n- Include expected results for each step\n- Test one thing per test case\n- Use consistent naming conventions\n- Keep test cases maintainable\n\n**DON''T:**\n- Assume knowledge\n- Make test cases too long\n- Skip preconditions\n- Forget edge cases\n- Leave expected results vague\n\n### Bug Reporting\n\n**DO:**\n- Provide clear reproduction steps\n- Include screenshots/videos\n- Specify exact environment details\n- Describe impact on users\n- Link to Figma for UI bugs\n\n**DON''T:**\n- Report without reproduction steps\n- Use vague descriptions\n- Skip environment details\n- Forget to assign priority\n- Duplicate existing bugs\n\n### Regression Testing\n\n**DO:**\n- Automate repetitive tests when possible\n- Maintain regression suite regularly\n- Prioritize critical paths\n- Run smoke tests frequently\n- Update suite after each release\n\n**DON''T:**\n- Skip regression before releases\n- Let suite become outdated\n- Test everything every time\n- Ignore failed regression tests\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n## Examples\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Example: Login Flow Test Case</strong></summary>\n\n```markdown\n## TC-LOGIN-001: Valid User Login\n\n**Priority:** P0 (Critical)\n**Type:** Functional\n**Estimated Time:** 2 minutes\n\n### Objective\nVerify users can successfully login with valid credentials\n\n### Preconditions\n- User account exists (test@example.com / Test123!)\n- User is not already logged in\n- Browser cookies cleared\n\n### Test Steps\n1. Navigate to https://app.example.com/login\n   **Expected:** Login page displays with email and password fields\n\n2. Enter email: test@example.com\n   **Expected:** Email field accepts input\n\n3. Enter password: Test123!\n   **Expected:** Password field shows masked characters\n\n4. Click \"Login\" button\n   **Expected:**\n   - Loading indicator appears\n   - User redirected to /dashboard\n   - Welcome message shown: \"Welcome back, Test User\"\n   - Avatar/profile image displayed in header\n\n### Post-conditions\n- User session created\n- Auth token stored\n- Analytics event logged\n\n### Edge Cases to Consider\n- TC-LOGIN-002: Invalid password\n- TC-LOGIN-003: Non-existent email\n- TC-LOGIN-004: SQL injection attempt\n- TC-LOGIN-005: Very long password\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Example: Responsive Design Test Case</strong></summary>\n\n```markdown\n## TC-UI-045: Mobile Navigation Menu\n\n**Priority:** P1 (High)\n**Type:** UI/Responsive\n**Devices:** Mobile (iPhone, Android)\n\n### Objective\nVerify navigation menu works correctly on mobile devices\n\n### Preconditions\n- Access from mobile device or responsive mode\n- Viewport width: 375px (iPhone SE) to 428px (iPhone Pro Max)\n\n### Test Steps\n1. Open homepage on mobile device\n   **Expected:** Hamburger menu icon visible (top-right)\n\n2. Tap hamburger icon\n   **Expected:**\n   - Menu slides in from right\n   - Overlay appears over content\n   - Close (X) button visible\n\n3. Tap menu item\n   **Expected:** Navigate to section, menu closes\n\n4. Compare against Figma mobile design [link]\n   **Expected:**\n   - Menu width: 280px\n   - Slide animation: 300ms ease-out\n   - Overlay opacity: 0.5, color #000000\n   - Font size: 16px, line-height 24px\n\n### Breakpoints to Test\n- 375px (iPhone SE)\n- 390px (iPhone 14)\n- 428px (iPhone 14 Pro Max)\n- 360px (Galaxy S21)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n**\"Testing shows the presence, not the absence of bugs.\" - Edsger Dijkstra**\n\n**\"Quality is not an act, it is a habit.\" - Aristotle**\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:10:05.880Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Automation Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain needing comprehensive test planning and validation capabilities against designs in Figma.","zh":"适用于像 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的自动化代理，需要对 Figma 中的设计进行全面测试规划和验证能力。","ja":"AutoGPTやLangChainのような自動化エージェントに適しており、Figma内のデザインに対する包括的なテスト計画と検証機能が必要です。","ko":"AutoGPT와 LangChain 같은 자동화 에이전트에 적합하며, Figma의 디자인에 대한 포괄적인 테스트 계획 및 검증 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de automatización como AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan capacidades de planificación y validación de pruebas comprehensivas contra diseños en Figma.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''automatisation comme AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant une planification et une validation de tests complètes contre les conceptions dans Figma.","de":"Ideal für Automatisierungsagenten wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die umfassende Testplanungs- und Validierungsfunktionen gegen Designs in Figma benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Automação, como AutoGPT e LangChain, que necessitam de capacidades de planejamento e validação de testes abrangentes contra designs no Figma.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, которым необходимы комплексные возможности планирования и проверки тестов по дизайну в Figma.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل التutomatiوn مثل AutoGPT و LangChain التي تحتاج إلى إمكانيات مخططة و_VALIDATION الشاملة للاختبار ضد التصاميم في Figma."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create detailed test plans, generate manual test cases, and build regression test suites, while validating designs against Figma and effectively documenting bugs using protocols like regression testing.","zh":"使代理能够创建详细的测试计划，生成手动测试用例，并构建回归测试套件，同时验证Figma中的设计并使用诸如回归测试之类的协议有效地记录错误。","ja":"エージェントが詳細なテスト計画を作成し、手動テストケースを生成し、回帰テストスイートを構築することを可能にし、Figma内のデザインを検証し、回帰テストなどのプロトコルを使用してバグを効果的にドキュメント化します。","ko":"에이전트가 자세한 테스트 계획을 만들고, 수동 테스트 케이스를 생성하고, 회귀 테스트 세트를 구축할 수 있도록 하며, Figma의 디자인을 검증하고, 회귀 테스트와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 오류를 효과적으로 문서화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear planes de prueba detallados, generar casos de prueba manuales y construir suites de pruebas de regresión, mientras valida diseños contra Figma y documenta efectivamente errores utilizando protocolos como pruebas de regresión.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des plans de test détaillés, de générer des cas de test manuels et de construire des suites de test de régression, tout en validant les conceptions contre Figma et en documentant efficacement les bogues à l''aide de protocoles tels que les tests de régression.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, detaillierte Testpläne zu erstellen, manuelle Testfälle zu generieren und Regressions-Test-Suiten zu erstellen, während Designs gegen Figma validiert und Fehler mithilfe von Protokollen wie Regressions tests effektiv dokumentiert werden.","pt":"Habilita agentes a criar planos de teste detalhados, gerar casos de teste manuais e construir conjuntos de teste de regressão, enquanto valida designs contra o Figma e documenta efetivamente bugs usando protocolos como teste de regressão.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать подробные планы тестирования, генерировать ручные тестовые случаи и строить наборы тестов регрессии, а также проверять дизайны против Figma и эффективно документировать ошибки с помощью протоколов, таких как регрессионное тестирование.","ar":"يمكن للعاملين من خلاله إنشاء خطط اختبار مفصلة وتوليد حالات اختبار يدوية وبناء مجموعات اختبار الانحدار، مع التحقق من التصاميم مقابل Figma وتوثيق الأخطاء بشكل فعال باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل اختبار الانحدار."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating test plans for new feature releases","Generating manual test cases for user authentication features","Validating UI designs against Figma specifications"],"zh":["为新功能发布创建测试计划","为用户身份验证功能生成手动测试用例","验证UI设计是否符合Figma规范"],"ja":["新機能リリースのテスト計画を作成する","ユーザー認証機能の手動テストケースを生成する","UIデザインをFigmaの仕様と比較して検証する"],"ko":["새로운 기능 릴리즈를 위한 테스트 계획을 생성하는 것","사용자 인증 기능을 위한 수동 테스트 케이스를 생성하는 것","UI 디자인을 Figma 사양과 비교하여 검증하는 것"],"es":["Creación de planes de prueba para nuevas versiones de características","Generación de casos de prueba manuales para características de autenticación de usuario","Validación de diseños de interfaz de usuario contra especificaciones de Figma"],"fr":["Création de plans de test pour de nouvelles versions de fonctionnalités","Génération de cas de test manuels pour les fonctionnalités d''authentification des utilisateurs","Validation des conceptions d''interface utilisateur contre les spécifications de Figma"],"de":["Erstellung von Testplänen für neue Feature-Veröffentlichungen","Generierung von manuellen Testfällen für Benutzer-Authentifizierungs-Features","Validierung von Benutzeroberflächendesigns gegen Figma-Spezifikationen"],"pt":["Criar planos de teste para lançamentos de novos recursos","Gerar casos de teste manuais para recursos de autenticação de usuário","Validar designs de UI contra especificações do Figma"],"ru":["Создание планов тестирования для выпусков новых функций","Генерация ручных тестовых случаев для функций аутентификации пользователей","Проверка дизайнов пользовательского интерфейса против спецификаций Figma"],"ar":["إنشاء خطط اختبار للوصول إلى إصدارات الميزات الجديدة","توليد حالات اختبار يدوية لميزات التحقق من هوية المستخدم","التحقق من تصاميم الواجهة المستخدمة مقابل مواصفات Figma"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires explicit activation by name","Limited to QA test planning and validation"],"zh":["需要明确地通过名称激活","仅限于QA测试规划和验证"],"ja":["名前で明示的にアクティブ化する必要がある","QAテスト計画および検証にのみ限定される"],"ko":["명시적으로 이름으로 활성화해야 함","QA 테스트 계획 및 검증에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere activación explícita por nombre","Limitado a la planificación y validación de pruebas de QA"],"fr":["Nécessite une activation explicite par nom","Limité à la planification et à la validation des tests de QA"],"de":["Benötigt eine explizite Aktivierung durch Namen","Begrenzt auf QA-Testplanung und -validierung"],"pt":["Requer ativação explícita por nome","Limitado ao planejamento e validação de testes de QA"],"ru":["Требует явной активации по имени","Ограничен планированием и проверкой тестов QA"],"ar":["يتطلب تنشيطًا صريحًا بالاسم","محدود بالتخطيط والتحقق من اختبارات جودة المؤسسة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
