 Оптимизация конверсии для разработчиков","ar":"Onboarding CRO: تحسين معدل التحويل للمطورين","en":"onboarding-cro"},"description":{"zh":"Onboarding CRO ","ja":"Onboarding CRO","ko":"Onboarding CRO ","es":"El onboarding CRO se centra en ayudar a los usuarios a alcanzar su momento ''aha'' lo más rápido posible y establecer hábitos que conduzcan a la retención a la...","fr":"L''onboarding CRO se concentre sur l''aide aux utilisateurs pour atteindre leur moment ''aha'' le plus rapidement possible et établir des habitudes qui conduisen...","de":"Das Onboarding CRO konzentriert sich darauf, den Benutzern zu helfen, ihren ''aha''-Moment so schnell wie möglich zu erreichen und Gewohnheiten zu etablieren, ...","pt":"Ferramenta especializada em Conversion Rate Optimization para processos de onboarding, focada em ajudar usuários a alcançar valor rapidamente e estabelecer h...","ru":"Специализированный инструмент для оптимизации конверсии процессов онбординга, помогающий пользователям быстро получить ценность и установить привычки для дол...","ar":"أداة متخصصة في تحسين معدل التحويل لعمليات التشغيل، تركز على مساعدة المستخدمين في تحقيق القيمة بسرعة وإنشاء عادات تؤدي إلى الاحتفاظ طويل الأمد.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Onboarding CRO"," "," ","API","SDK"],"ja":["Onboarding CRO","","","API","SDK"],"ko":["Onboarding CRO","","","API","SDK"],"es":["Análisis de la experiencia de usuario","Optimización del proceso de onboarding","Creación de hábitos para la retención a largo plazo","Medición del éxito del onboarding","Personalización de la experiencia de usuario"],"fr":["Analyse de l''expérience utilisateur","Optimisation du processus d''onboarding","Création d''habitudes pour la rétention à long terme","Mesure du succès de l''onboarding","Personnalisation de l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Analyse der Benutzererfahrung","Optimierung des Onboarding-Prozesses","Erstellung von Gewohnheiten für die langfristige Bindung","Messung des Erfolgs des Onboarding","Personalisierung der Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["Análise contextual de marketing de produto","Identificação do \"momento aha\" do usuário","Estratégias de formação de hábitos para retenção","Otimização baseada em dados de fluxos de onboarding","Integração com documentação de contexto existente","Avaliação inicial personalizada para cada produto"],"ru":["Контекстный анализ продуктового маркетинга","Идентификация \"момента озарения\" пользователя","Стратегии формирования привычек для удержания","Оптимизация потоков онбординга на основе данных","Интеграция с существующей документацией контекста","Персонализированная первоначальная оценка для каждого продукта"],"ar":["تحليل سياق تسويق المنتج","تحديد \"لحظة الإدراك\" للمستخدم","استراتيجيات تكوين العادات للاحتفاظ","تحسين تدفقات التشغيل بناءً على البيانات","التكامل مع وثائق السياق الموجودة","تقييم أولي مخصص لكل منتج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Onboarding CRO"," "," "," ","API","SDK"],"ja":["Onboarding CRO","","","","API","SDK"],"ko":["Onboarding CRO","","","","API","SDK"],"es":["onboarding CRO","optimización de la experiencia de usuario","retención a largo plazo","análisis de la experiencia de usuario","creación de hábitos","medición del éxito del onboarding","personalización de la experiencia de usuario","desarrollo de software","experiencia de usuario"],"fr":["onboarding CRO","amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","rétention à long terme","analyse de l''expérience utilisateur","création d''habitudes","mesure du succès de l''onboarding","personnalisation de l''expérience utilisateur","développement de logiciels","expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Onboarding CRO","Optimierung der Benutzererfahrung","langfristige Bindung","Analyse der Benutzererfahrung","Erstellung von Gewohnheiten","Messung des Erfolgs des Onboarding","Personalisierung der Benutzererfahrung","Software-Entwicklung","Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["otimização taxa conversão onboarding","CRO para desenvolvedores","ativação usuários produtos digitais","momento aha desenvolvimento","retenção longo prazo UX","onboarding técnico otimização","habits formation development","product activation framework"],"ru":["оптимизация конверсии онбординг","CRO для разработчиков","активация пользователей цифровых продуктов","момент озарения разработка","долгосрочное удержание UX","технический онбординг оптимизация","формирование привычек разработка","фреймворк активации продукта"],"ar":["تحسين معدل التحويل للتشغيل","CRO للمطورين","تفعيل مستخدمي المنتجات الرقمية","لحظة الإدراك في التطوير","الاحتفاظ طويل الأمد UX","التشغيل التقني والتحسين","تشكيل العادات في التطوير","إطار تفعيل المنتج"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"onboarding-cro","description":"When the user wants to optimize post-signup onboarding, user activation, first-run experience, or time-to-value. Also use when the user mentions onboarding flow, activation rate, user activation, first-run experience, empty states, onboarding checklist, aha moment, or new user experience. For signup/registration optimization, see signup-flow-cro. For ongoing email sequences, see email-sequence.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Onboarding CRO\n\nYou are an expert in user onboarding and activation. Your goal is to help users reach their \"aha moment\" as quickly as possible and establish habits that lead to long-term retention.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **","body":"# Onboarding CRO\n\nYou are an expert in user onboarding and activation. Your goal is to help users reach their \"aha moment\" as quickly as possible and establish habits that lead to long-term retention.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Product Context** - What type of product? B2B or B2C? Core value proposition?\n2. **Activation Definition** - What''s the \"aha moment\"? What action indicates a user \"gets it\"?\n3. **Current State** - What happens after signup? Where do users drop off?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Time-to-Value Is Everything\nRemove every step between signup and experiencing core value.\n\n### 2. One Goal Per Session\nFocus first session on one successful outcome. Save advanced features for later.\n\n### 3. Do, Don''t Show\nInteractive > Tutorial. Doing the thing > Learning about the thing.\n\n### 4. Progress Creates Motivation\nShow advancement. Celebrate completions. Make the path visible.\n\n---\n\n## Defining Activation\n\n### Find Your Aha Moment\n\nThe action that correlates most strongly with retention:\n- What do retained users do that churned users don''t?\n- What''s the earliest indicator of future engagement?\n\n**Examples by product type:**\n- Project management: Create first project + add team member\n- Analytics: Install tracking + see first report\n- Design tool: Create first design + export/share\n- Marketplace: Complete first transaction\n\n### Activation Metrics\n- % of signups who reach activation\n- Time to activation\n- Steps to activation\n- Activation by cohort/source\n\n---\n\n## Onboarding Flow Design\n\n### Immediate Post-Signup (First 30 Seconds)\n\n| Approach | Best For | Risk |\n|----------|----------|------|\n| Product-first | Simple products, B2C, mobile | Blank slate overwhelm |\n| Guided setup | Products needing personalization | Adds friction before value |\n| Value-first | Products with demo data | May not feel \"real\" |\n\n**Whatever you choose:**\n- Clear single next action\n- No dead ends\n- Progress indication if multi-step\n\n### Onboarding Checklist Pattern\n\n**When to use:**\n- Multiple setup steps required\n- Product has several features to discover\n- Self-serve B2B products\n\n**Best practices:**\n- 3-7 items (not overwhelming)\n- Order by value (most impactful first)\n- Start with quick wins\n- Progress bar/completion %\n- Celebration on completion\n- Dismiss option (don''t trap users)\n\n### Empty States\n\nEmpty states are onboarding opportunities, not dead ends.\n\n**Good empty state:**\n- Explains what this area is for\n- Shows what it looks like with data\n- Clear primary action to add first item\n- Optional: Pre-populate with example data\n\n### Tooltips and Guided Tours\n\n**When to use:** Complex UI, features that aren''t self-evident, power features users might miss\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Max 3-5 steps per tour\n- Dismissable at any time\n- Don''t repeat for returning users\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Channel Onboarding\n\n### Email + In-App Coordination\n\n**Trigger-based emails:**\n- Welcome email (immediate)\n- Incomplete onboarding (24h, 72h)\n- Activation achieved (celebration + next step)\n- Feature discovery (days 3, 7, 14)\n\n**Email should:**\n- Reinforce in-app actions, not duplicate them\n- Drive back to product with specific CTA\n- Be personalized based on actions taken\n\n---\n\n## Handling Stalled Users\n\n### Detection\nDefine \"stalled\" criteria (X days inactive, incomplete setup)\n\n### Re-engagement Tactics\n\n1. **Email sequence** - Reminder of value, address blockers, offer help\n2. **In-app recovery** - Welcome back, pick up where left off\n3. **Human touch** - For high-value accounts, personal outreach\n\n---\n\n## Measurement\n\n### Key Metrics\n\n| Metric | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| Activation rate | % reaching activation event |\n| Time to activation | How long to first value |\n| Onboarding completion | % completing setup |\n| Day 1/7/30 retention | Return rate by timeframe |\n\n### Funnel Analysis\n\nTrack drop-off at each step:\n```\nSignup → Step 1 → Step 2 → Activation → Retention\n100%      80%       60%       40%         25%\n```\n\nIdentify biggest drops and focus there.\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Onboarding Audit\nFor each issue: Finding → Impact → Recommendation → Priority\n\n### Onboarding Flow Design\n- Activation goal\n- Step-by-step flow\n- Checklist items (if applicable)\n- Empty state copy\n- Email sequence triggers\n- Metrics plan\n\n---\n\n## Common Patterns by Product Type\n\n| Product Type | Key Steps |\n|--------------|-----------|\n| B2B SaaS | Setup wizard → First value action → Team invite → Deep setup |\n| Marketplace | Complete profile → Browse → First transaction → Repeat loop |\n| Mobile App | Permissions → Quick win → Push setup → Habit loop |\n| Content Platform | Follow/customize → Consume → Create → Engage |\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Ideas\n\nWhen recommending experiments, consider tests for:\n- Flow simplification (step count, ordering)\n- Progress and motivation mechanics\n- Personalization by role or goal\n- Support and help availability\n\n**For comprehensive experiment ideas**: See [references/experiments.md](references/experiments.md)\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What action most correlates with retention?\n2. What happens immediately after signup?\n3. Where do users currently drop off?\n4. What''s your activation rate target?\n5. Do you have cohort analysis on successful vs. churned users?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **signup-flow-cro**: For optimizing the signup before onboarding\n- **email-sequence**: For onboarding email series\n- **paywall-upgrade-cro**: For converting to paid during/after onboarding\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing onboarding changes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:12:16.291Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for User Experience Agents needing advanced onboarding and activation strategies to boost user retention.","zh":"适合需要高级入职和激活策略来提高用户留存率的用户体验代理。","ja":"高度なオンボーディングとアクティベーション戦略が必要なユーザーエクスペリエンスエージェントに最適。","ko":"고급 온보딩 및 활성화 전략이 필요한 사용자 경험 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Experiencia de Usuario que necesitan estrategias de incorporación y activación avanzadas para mejorar la retención de usuarios.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''expérience utilisateur ayant besoin de stratégies d''intégration et d''activation avancées pour améliorer la rétention des utilisateurs.","de":"Perfekt für Benutzererfahrungsagenten, die erweiterte Onboarding- und Aktivierungsstrategien benötigen, um die Benutzerrate zu verbessern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Experiência do Usuário que necessitam de estratégias avançadas de integração e ativação para aumentar a retenção de usuários.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов пользовательского опыта, требующих продвинутых стратегий интеграции и активации для повышения удержания пользователей.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تجربة المستخدم الذين يحتاجون إلى استراتيجيات متقدمة للدمج والتفعيل لتعزيز احتفاظ المستخدمين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design personalized onboarding flows using product marketing context, accelerating users'' path to their ''aha moment'' through targeted activation and habit formation, leveraging files like `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` for context-aware recommendations.","zh":"赋予代理人使用产品营销背景设计个性化入职流程的能力，通过有针对性的激活和习惯形成加速用户达到他们的‘啊哈’时刻，并利用类似`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`的文件进行背景感知推荐。","ja":"エージェントが製品マーケティングコンテキストを使用してパーソナライズされたオンボーディングフローを設計できるようにし、ターゲットを絞ったアクティベーションと習慣形成を通じてユーザーの『アハ！』の瞬間への道を加速し、`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`のようなファイルを使用してコンテキストに応じたRecommendationを行う。","ko":"에이전트가 제품 마케팅 콘텍스트를 사용하여 개인화된 온보딩 흐름을 설계할 수 있도록 하여, 대상에 따른 활성화 및 습관 형성을 통해 사용자의 ''아하!'' 순간에 대한 경로를 가속화하고, `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`와 같은 파일을 사용하여 콘텍스트 인식 추천을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar flujos de incorporación personalizados utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos, acelerando el camino de los usuarios hacia su ''momento aha'' a través de la activación y la formación de hábitos dirigidas, aprovechando archivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para recomendaciones conscientes del contexto.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des flux d''intégration personnalisés en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits, en accélérant le parcours des utilisateurs vers leur ''moment aha'' à travers l''activation et la formation d''habitudes ciblées, en exploitant des fichiers tels que `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` pour des recommandations conscientes du contexte.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, personalisierte Onboarding-Flows unter Verwendung des Produktmarketing-Kontexts zu entwerfen, beschleunigt den Weg der Benutzer zu ihrem ''Aha''-Moment durch gezielte Aktivierung und Habit-Bildung, indem Dateien wie `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` für kontextbewusste Empfehlungen genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar fluxos de integração personalizados usando o contexto de marketing de produto, acelerando o caminho dos usuários para o seu ''momento aha'' por meio de ativação e formação de hábitos direcionados, utilizando arquivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para recomendações cientes de contexto.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать персонализированные потоки интеграции с использованием контекста маркетинга продукта, ускоряя путь пользователей к их ''моменту ага'' посредством целенаправленной активации и формирования привычек, используя файлы типа `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` для контекстно-зависимых рекомендаций.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تصميم تدفقات دمج مخصصة باستخدام سياق تسويق المنتج، وتسريع مسار المستخدمين إلى لحظة ''آها'' من خلال التنشيط والتشكيل الموجه، واستخدام الملفات مثل `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` لتوصيات ت意识 بالسياق."},"useCases":{"en":["Streamlining user onboarding processes","Creating habit-forming activation strategies","Analyzing product marketing context for personalized user experiences"],"zh":["简化用户入职流程","创建习惯形成的激活策略","分析产品营销背景以提供个性化的用户体验"],"ja":["ユーザーオンボーディングプロセスの最適化","習慣形成のためのアクティベーション戦略の作成","製品マーケティングコンテキストの分析によるパーソナライズされたユーザーエクスペリエンスの提供"],"ko":["사용자 온보딩 프로세스 최적화","습관 형성 활성화 전략 생성","제품 마케팅 콘텍스트 분석을 통한 개인화된 사용자 경험 제공"],"es":["Optimización de los procesos de incorporación de usuarios","Creación de estrategias de activación que generan hábitos","Análisis del contexto de marketing de productos para experiencias de usuario personalizadas"],"fr":["Optimisation des processus d''intégration des utilisateurs","Création de stratégies d''activation qui créent des habitudes","Analyse du contexte de marketing de produits pour des expériences utilisateur personnalisées"],"de":["Optimierung der Onboarding-Prozesse für Benutzer","Erstellung von Aktivierungsstrategien, die Gewohnheiten bilden","Analyse des Produktmarketing-Kontexts für personalisierte Benutzererfahrungen"],"pt":["Otimizando processos de integração do usuário","Criando estratégias de ativação que formam hábitos","Analisando contexto de marketing de produto para experiências de usuário personalizadas"],"ru":["Оптимизация процессов интеграции пользователей","Создание стратегий активации, формирующих привычки","Анализ контекста маркетинга продукта для персонализированных пользовательских опытов"],"ar":["تحسين عمليات دمج المستخدم","إنشاء استراتيجيات تفعيل لتكوين العادات","تحليل سياق تسويق المنتج لتجارب المستخدمين المخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existence of `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` for optimal performance","Context-specific to product marketing"],"zh":["需要`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`文件以实现最佳性能","特定于产品营销背景"],"ja":["`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`ファイルが必要なので、最適なパフォーマンスが得られます","製品マーケティングコンテキストに特有"],"ko":["`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 파일이 필요하여 최적의 성능을 발휘합니다","제품 마케팅 콘텍스트에 특정"],"es":["Requiere la existencia de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para un rendimiento óptimo","Específico del contexto de marketing de productos"],"fr":["Nécessite l''existence de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` pour des performances optimales","Spécifique au contexte de marketing de produits"],"de":["Erfordert die Existenz von `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` für optimale Leistung","Kontextspezifisch für Produktmarketing"],"pt":["Exige a existência de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para desempenho ótimo","Específico de contexto para marketing de produto"],"ru":["Требует существования `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` для оптимальной производительности","Контекстно-зависимый для маркетинга продукта"],"ar":["يتطلب وجود `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` لأداء مثالي","محدد بالسياق لتسويق المنتج"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/next-upgrade', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'next-upgrade', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z', '2026-02-18T14:11:59.648Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/next-upgrade","name":"next-upgrade","description":{"zh":"升级 Next.js 项目到最新版本，确保项目的稳定性和安全性","ja":"Next.js プロジェクトを最新バージョンにアップグレードして、安定性とセキュリティを確保する","ko":"Next.js 프로젝트를 최신 버전으로 업그레이드 하여 안정성과 보안을 확보합니다","es":"La habilidad next-upgrade actualiza tu proyecto a la última versión de Next.js siguiendo las guías oficiales de migración. Automatiza el proceso de detección de la versión actual y la actualización a la última versión","fr":"La compétence next-upgrade met à niveau votre projet vers la dernière version de Next.js en suivant les guides de migration officiels. Elle automatise le processus de détection de la version actuelle et de mise à niveau vers la dernière version","de":"Die Fähigkeit next-upgrade aktualisiert Ihr Projekt auf die neueste Version von Next.js, indem sie die offiziellen Migrationsleitfäden befolgt. Sie automatisiert den Prozess der Erkennung der aktuellen Version und der Aktualisierung auf die neueste Version","pt":"Atualize seu projeto Next.js para a versão mais recente com as guias oficiais de migração","ru":"Обновите свой проект Next.js до последней версии с помощью официальных рекомендаций по миграции","ar":"ترقية مشروع Next.js إلى الإصدار الأحدث باستخدام إرشادات الترقية الرسمية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Next.js Upgrade 指南","ja":"Next.js アップグレード ガイド","ko":"Next.js 업그레이드 가이드","es":"Actualiza a Next.js con next-upgrade","fr":"Mettre à niveau vers Next.js avec next-upgrade","de":"Auf Next.js mit next-upgrade aktualisieren","pt":"Atualize para Next.js mais recente","ru":"Обновите до последней версии Next.js","ar":"ترقية إلى إصدار Next.js الأحدث","en":"next-upgrade"},"description":{"zh":"升级 Next.js 项目到最新版本，确保项目的稳定性和安全性","ja":"Next.js プロジェクトを最新バージョンにアップグレードして、安定性とセキュリティを確保する","ko":"Next.js 프로젝트를 최신 버전으로 업그레이드 하여 안정성과 보안을 확보합니다","es":"La habilidad next-upgrade actualiza tu proyecto a la última versión de Next.js siguiendo las guías oficiales de migración. Automatiza el proceso de detección...","fr":"La compétence next-upgrade met à niveau votre projet vers la dernière version de Next.js en suivant les guides de migration officiels. Elle automatise le pro...","de":"Die Fähigkeit next-upgrade aktualisiert Ihr Projekt auf die neueste Version von Next.js, indem sie die offiziellen Migrationsleitfäden befolgt. Sie automatis...","pt":"Atualize seu projeto Next.js para a versão mais recente com as guias oficiais de migração","ru":"Обновите свой проект Next.js до последней версии с помощью официальных рекомендаций по миграции","ar":"ترقية مشروع Next.js إلى الإصدار الأحدث باستخدام إرشادات الترقية الرسمية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["检测当前 Next.js 版本","获取最新升级指南","使用 Codemods 进行升级","升级 React 和 React DOM","确保项目兼容性"],"ja":["現在の Next.js バージョンの検出","最新のアップグレード ガイドの取得","Codemods を使用したアップグレード","React と React DOM のアップグレード","プロジェクトの互換性の確保"],"ko":["현재 Next.js 버전 검출","최신 업그레이드 가이드 얻기","Codemods 사용 업그레이드","React 및 React DOM 업그레이드","프로젝트 호환성 보장"],"es":["Detección de la versión actual de Next.js","Actualización a la última versión de Next.js","Seguimiento de las guías oficiales de migración","Automatización del proceso de actualización","Compatibilidad con codemods y guías de versión específica"],"fr":["Détection de la version actuelle de Next.js","Mise à niveau vers la dernière version de Next.js","Suivi des guides de migration officiels","Automatisation du processus de mise à niveau","Compatibilité avec les codemods et les guides de version spécifique"],"de":["Erkennung der aktuellen Version von Next.js","Aktualisierung auf die neueste Version von Next.js","Befolgen der offiziellen Migrationsleitfäden","Automatisierung des Aktualisierungsprozesses","Kompatibilität mit Codemods und versionspezifischen Leitfäden"],"pt":["Detecção da versão atual do Next.js","Fetch da documentação de upgrade oficial","Suporte a codemods","Guia de upgrade personalizado para cada versão","Integração com WebFetch","Suporte a React e React DOM"],"ru":["Определение текущей версии Next.js","Получение официальной документации по обновлению","Поддержка codemods","Пользовательское руководство по обновлению для каждой версии","Интеграция с WebFetch","Поддержка React и React DOM"],"ar":["اكتشاف الإصدار الحالي من Next.js","استرجاع وثائق الترقية الرسمية","دعم codemods","دليل الترقية المخصص لكل إصدار","التكامل مع WebFetch","دعم React و React DOM"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Next.js 升级","Next.js 迁移","最新版本","官方升级指南","Codemods","React 升级","React DOM 升级"],"ja":["Next.js アップグレード","Next.js 移行","最新バージョン","公式アップグレードガイド","Codemods","React アップグレード","React DOM アップグレード"],"ko":["Next.js 업그레이드","Next.js 이주","최신 버전","공식 업그레이드 가이드","Codemods","React 업그레이드","React DOM 업그레이드"],"es":["Next.js","actualización","migración","automatización","codemods","guías de versión","desarrollo web","JavaScript","React"],"fr":["Next.js","mise à niveau","migration","automatisation","codemods","guides de version","développement web","JavaScript","React"],"de":["Next.js","Aktualisierung","Migration","Automatisierung","Codemods","Versionsleitfäden","Webentwicklung","JavaScript","React"],"pt":["Next.js","atualização","migração","React","React DOM","codemods","WebFetch","desenvolvimento web","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Next.js","обновление","миграция","React","React DOM","codemods","WebFetch","веб-разработка","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["Next.js","ترقية","هجرة","React","React DOM","codemods","WebFetch","تطوير الويب","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"next-upgrade","description":"Upgrade Next.js to the latest version following official migration guides and codemods","bodyPreview":"# Upgrade Next.js\n\nUpgrade the current project to the latest Next.js version following official migration guides.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. **Detect current version**: Read `package.json` to identify the current Next.js version and related dependencies (React, React DOM, etc.)\n\n2. **Fetch the latest upgrade guide**: Use WebFetch to get the official upgrade documentation:\n   - Codemods: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/upgrading/codemods\n   - Version-specific guides (adjust versio","body":"# Upgrade Next.js\n\nUpgrade the current project to the latest Next.js version following official migration guides.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. **Detect current version**: Read `package.json` to identify the current Next.js version and related dependencies (React, React DOM, etc.)\n\n2. **Fetch the latest upgrade guide**: Use WebFetch to get the official upgrade documentation:\n   - Codemods: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/upgrading/codemods\n   - Version-specific guides (adjust version as needed):\n     - https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/upgrading/version-15\n     - https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/upgrading/version-14\n\n3. **Determine upgrade path**: Based on current version, identify which migration steps apply. For major version jumps, upgrade incrementally (e.g., 13 → 14 → 15).\n\n4. **Run codemods first**: Next.js provides codemods to automate breaking changes:\n   ```bash\n   npx @next/codemod@latest <transform> <path>\n   ```\n   Common transforms:\n   - `next-async-request-api` - Updates async Request APIs (v15)\n   - `next-request-geo-ip` - Migrates geo/ip properties (v15)\n   - `next-dynamic-access-named-export` - Transforms dynamic imports (v15)\n\n5. **Update dependencies**: Upgrade Next.js and peer dependencies together:\n   ```bash\n   npm install next@latest react@latest react-dom@latest\n   ```\n\n6. **Review breaking changes**: Check the upgrade guide for manual changes needed:\n   - API changes (e.g., async params in v15)\n   - Configuration changes in `next.config.js`\n   - Deprecated features being removed\n\n7. **Update TypeScript types** (if applicable):\n   ```bash\n   npm install @types/react@latest @types/react-dom@latest\n   ```\n\n8. **Test the upgrade**:\n   - Run `npm run build` to check for build errors\n   - Run `npm run dev` and test key functionality\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:11:59.648Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for DevOps and Code Maintenance Agents automating Next.js project upgrades.","zh":"适用于DevOps和代码维护代理自动升级Next.js项目。","ja":"DevOpsとコードメンテナンスエージェントがNext.jsプロジェクトを自動アップグレードするために不可欠です。","ko":"DevOps와 코드 유지 보수 에이전트가 Next.js 프로젝트를 자동 업그레이드하는 데 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de DevOps y mantenimiento de código que automatizan las actualizaciones de proyectos de Next.js.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents DevOps et de maintenance de code qui automatisent les mises à jour des projets Next.js.","de":"Wesentlich für DevOps- und Code-Wartungsagenten, die Next.js-Projekt-Upgrades automatisieren.","pt":"Essencial para os agentes de DevOps e Manutenção de Código que automatizam as atualizações de projetos Next.js.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов DevOps и обслуживания кода, автоматизирующих обновления проектов Next.js.","ar":"ضروري لعميل DevOps و صيانة الشفرة التي تلقم تحديثات مشاريع Next.js."},"recommendation":{"en":"Automates the entire Next.js version migration process by detecting current dependencies, fetching official upgrade guides, and executing codemods. Provides systematic version-specific upgrades while maintaining compatibility with React and React DOM dependencies.","zh":"通过检测当前依赖项、获取官方升级指南并执行codemods来自动执行整个Next.js版本迁移过程。提供系统的版本特定升级，同时保持与React和React DOM依赖项的兼容性。","ja":"現在の依存関係の検出、公式のアップグレードガイドの取得、codemodsの実行によってNext.jsのバージョン移行プロセスを自動化します。ReactおよびReact DOMの依存関係との互換性を維持しながら、バージョン固有のアップグレードを提供します。","ko":"현재 종속 항목을 감지하고 공식 업그레이드 가이드를 가져오고 코드 모드를 실행하여 Next.js 버전 마이그레이션 프로세스를 자동화합니다. React 및 React DOM 종속 항목과의 호환성을 유지하면서 버전별 업그레이드를 제공합니다.","es":"Automatiza todo el proceso de migración de versión de Next.js detectando las dependencias actuales, recuperando las guías de actualización oficiales y ejecutando codemods. Proporciona actualizaciones sistemáticas de versión específica mientras mantiene la compatibilidad con las dependencias de React y React DOM.","fr":"Automatise l''ensemble du processus de migration de version de Next.js en détectant les dépendances actuelles, en récupérant les guides de mise à jour officiels et en exécutant des codemods. Fournit des mises à jour systématiques de version spécifique tout en maintenant la compatibilité avec les dépendances React et React DOM.","de":"Automatisiert den gesamten Next.js-Version-Migrationsprozess, indem es die aktuellen Abhängigkeiten erkennt, offizielle Upgrade-Anleitungen abruft und Codemods ausführt. Bietet systematische versionsspezifische Upgrades, während die Kompatibilität mit React- und React-DOM-Abhängigkeiten aufrechterhalten wird.","pt":"Automatiza todo o processo de migração de versão do Next.js, detectando as dependências atuais, buscando guias de atualização oficiais e executando codemods. Fornece atualizações sistemáticas de versão específica, mantendo a compatibilidade com as dependências do React e React DOM.","ru":"Автоматизирует весь процесс миграции версии Next.js, обнаруживая текущие зависимости, получая официальные руководства по обновлению и выполняя codemods. Обеспечивает систематические обновления версии, сохраняя совместимость с зависимостями React и React DOM.","ar":"يتوفر على عملية الهجرة الكاملة لنسخة Next.js من خلال الكشف عن الاعتماديات الحالية و الحصول على أدلة التحديث الرسمية و تنفيذ codemods. يوفر تحديثات إصدار محددة و ي维持 التوافق مع الاعتماديات React و React DOM."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating version detection from package.json","Executing official Next.js codemods","Managing dependency version alignment","Following version-specific migration guides"],"zh":["自动从package.json检测版本","执行官方Next.js代码变更","管理依赖版本对齐","遵循版本特定迁移指南"],"ja":["package.jsonからバージョンを自動検出する","公式のNext.js codemodsを実行する","依存関係バージョンの整列を管理する","バージョン特有の移行ガイドに従う"],"ko":["package.json에서 버전을 자동으로 감지","공식 Next.js 코드 모드를 실행","의존성 버전 정렬 관리","버전 특정 마이그레이션 가이드 따라"],"es":["Automatizar la detección de versión desde package.json","Ejecutar codemods oficiales de Next.js","Gestionar la alineación de la versión de dependencias","Seguir guías de migración específicas de la versión"],"fr":["Automatiser la détection de version à partir de package.json","Exécuter des codemods officiels de Next.js","Gérer l''alignement de la version des dépendances","Suivre les guides de migration spécifiques à la version"],"de":["Automatisieren der Versionserkennung aus package.json","Ausführen von offiziellen Next.js-Codemods","Verwalten der Abhängigkeitsversionen-Ausrichtung","Befolgen versionsspezifischer Migrationsleitfäden"],"pt":["Automatizar a detecção de versão do package.json","Executar codemods oficiais do Next.js","Gerenciar alinhamento de versão de dependência","Seguir guias de migração de versão específica"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обнаружение версии в package.json","Выполнять официальные codemods Next.js","Управлять выравниванием версий зависимостей","Следовать руководствам по миграции версии"],"ar":["التلقم الكشف عن إصدار package.json","تنفيذ codemods الرسمية لـ Next.js","إدارة محاذاة إصدار الاعتماديات","متابعة إرشادات الهجرة الخاصة بالإصدار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires filesystem access to read package.json","Dependent on Next.js official documentation availability","May require manual intervention for complex breaking changes"],"zh":["需要文件系统访问权限来读取package.json","依赖Next.js官方文档的可用性","可能需要手动干预复杂的破坏性变化"],"ja":["package.jsonを読み取るためにファイルシステムへのアクセス権が必要","Next.js公式ドキュメントの可用性に依存","複雑な破壊的な変更の場合、手動での介入が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["package.json을 읽기 위해 파일 시스템 액세스 권한이 필요","Next.js 공식 문서의 가용성에 의존","복잡한 破壊적인 변경의 경우 수동 개입이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere acceso al sistema de archivos para leer package.json","Depende de la disponibilidad de la documentación oficial de Next.js","Puede requerir intervención manual para cambios complejos de ruptura"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au système de fichiers pour lire package.json","Dépend de la disponibilité de la documentation officielle de Next.js","Peut nécessiter une intervention manuelle pour des changements de rupture complexes"],"de":["Benötigt Dateizugriff, um package.json zu lesen","Hängt von der Verfügbarkeit der offiziellen Next.js-Dokumentation ab","Kann manuelles Eingreifen für komplexe Umbrechungen erfordern"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao sistema de arquivos para ler package.json","Depende da disponibilidade da documentação oficial do Next.js","Pode requerer intervenção manual para alterações complexas de quebra"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файловой системе для чтения package.json","Зависит от наличия официальной документации Next.js","Может требовать ручного вмешательства для сложных изменений, нарушающих совместимость"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام الملفات لقراءة package.json","يعتمد على توافر الوثائق الرسمية لبرنامج Next.js","يمكن أن يتطلب تدخل يدوي لتحديثات كسر معقدة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/writing-skills', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'writing-skills', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z', '2026-02-18T14:12:12.278Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/writing-skills","name":"writing-skills","description":{"zh":"写作技能是将测试驱动开发应用于过程文档，通过测试和重构实现高质量文档","ja":"ライティングスキルは、テスト駆動開発をプロセス文書に適用し、テストとリファクタリングを通じて高品質な文書を実現する","ko":"작성 스킬은 테스트 주도 개발을 프로세스 문서에 적용하여 테스트와 리팩토링을 통해 고품질 문서를 구현","es":"Las habilidades de escritura aplican el desarrollo guiado por pruebas a la documentación de procesos","fr":"Les compétences en écriture appliquent le développement piloté par les tests à la documentation des processus","de":"Die Schreibfähigkeiten wenden die testgetriebene Entwicklung auf die Prozessdokumentation an","pt":"As habilidades de escrita de código são uma abordagem de Test-Driven Development aplicada à documentação de processos","ru":"Навыки написания кода - это подход Test-Driven Development, примененный к документации процессов","ar":"مهارات الكتابة البرمجية هي نهج التطوير القائم على الاختبار الموجهة إلى وثائق العمليات","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"写作技能：测试驱动开发文档","ja":"ライティングスキル：テスト駆動開発による文書化","ko":"작성 스킬: 테스트 주도 개발을 적용한 문서화","es":"Habilidades de escritura para desarrolladores","fr":"Compétences en écriture pour les développeurs","de":"Schreibfähigkeiten für Entwickler","pt":"Habilidades de Escrita de Código","ru":"Навыки написания кода","ar":"مهارات الكتابة البرمجية","en":"writing-skills"},"description":{"zh":"写作技能是将测试驱动开发应用于过程文档，通过测试和重构实现高质量文档","ja":"ライティングスキルは、テスト駆動開発をプロセス文書に適用し、テストとリファクタリングを通じて高品質な文書を実現する","ko":"작성 스킬은 테스트 주도 개발을 프로세스 문서에 적용하여 테스트와 리팩토링을 통해 고품질 문서를 구현","es":"Las habilidades de escritura aplican el desarrollo guiado por pruebas a la documentación de procesos","fr":"Les compétences en écriture appliquent le développement piloté par les tests à la documentation des processus","de":"Die Schreibfähigkeiten wenden die testgetriebene Entwicklung auf die Prozessdokumentation an","pt":"As habilidades de escrita de código são uma abordagem de Test-Driven Development aplicada à documentação de processos","ru":"Навыки написания кода - это подход Test-Driven Development, примененный к документации процессов","ar":"مهارات الكتابة البرمجية هي نهج التطوير القائم على الاختبار الموجهة إلى وثائق العمليات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","过程文档","测试和重构","高质量文档","Agent-specific 目录"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","プロセス文書","テストとリファクタリング","高品質な文書","エージェント固有のディレクトリ"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","프로세스 문서","테스트와 리팩토링","고품질 문서","에이전트 고유 디렉토리"],"es":["Aplicación de TDD en documentación","Escritura de casos de prueba","Observación de fallos y refactorización","Documentación de procesos","Integración con agentes específicos"],"fr":["Application du TDD dans la documentation","Rédaction de cas de test","Observation des échecs et refactoring","Documentation des processus","Intégration avec des agents spécifiques"],"de":["Anwendung von TDD in der Dokumentation","Erstellung von Testfällen","Beobachtung von Fehlern und Refactoring","Dokumentation von Prozessen","Integration mit agentspezifischen Verzeichnissen"],"pt":["Test-Driven Development aplicado à documentação","Criação de casos de teste com subagentes","Refatoração de código para fechar lacunas","Desenvolvimento de habilidades de escrita de código personalizadas","Integração com agentes específicos","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Test-Driven Development, примененный к документации","Создание тестовых случаев с субагентами","Рефакторинг кода для закрытия лазеек","Разработка индивидуальных навыков написания кода","Интеграция с конкретными агентами","Повышение качества кода"],"ar":["التطوير القائم على الاختبار الموجهة إلى وثائق العمليات","إنشاء حالات اختبار مع وكالات فرعية","إعادة هيكلة الكود لإغلاق الثغرات","تطوير مهارات الكتابة البرمجية المخصصة","التكامل مع الوكالات المحددة","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["写作技能","测试驱动开发","过程文档","文档化","Agent-specific 目录","测试和重构"],"ja":["ライティングスキル","テスト駆動開発","プロセス文書","文書化","エージェント固有のディレクトリ","テストとリファクタリング"],"ko":["작성 스킬","테스트 주도 개발","프로세스 문서","문서화","에이전트 고유 디렉토리","테스트와 리팩토링"],"es":["habilidades de escritura","desarrollo guiado por pruebas","documentación de procesos","TDD","pruebas de software","documentación técnica"],"fr":["compétences en écriture","développement piloté par les tests","documentation des processus","TDD","tests de logiciel","documentation technique"],"de":["Schreibfähigkeiten","testgetriebene Entwicklung","Prozessdokumentation","TDD","Softwaretests","technische Dokumentation"],"pt":["habilidades de escrita de código","Test-Driven Development","documentação de processos","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade de código","refatoração de código","casos de teste","subagentes","agentes específicos"],"ru":["навыки написания кода","Test-Driven Development","документация процессов","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","рефакторинг кода","тестовые случаи","субагенты","конкретные агенты"],"ar":["مهارات الكتابة البرمجية","التطوير القائم على الاختبار","وثائق العمليات","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود","إعادة هيكلة الكود","حالات الاختبار","الوكالات الفرعية","الوكالات المحددة"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"writing-skills","description":"Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment","bodyPreview":"# Writing Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal skills live in agent-specific directories (`~/.claude/skills` for Claude Code, `~/.codex/skills` for Codex)** \n\nYou write test cases (pressure scenarios with subagents), watch them fail (baseline behavior), write the skill (documentation), watch tests pass (agents comply), and refactor (close loopholes).\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch an agent fail without the skil","body":"# Writing Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal skills live in agent-specific directories (`~/.claude/skills` for Claude Code, `~/.codex/skills` for Codex)** \n\nYou write test cases (pressure scenarios with subagents), watch them fail (baseline behavior), write the skill (documentation), watch tests pass (agents comply), and refactor (close loopholes).\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch an agent fail without the skill, you don''t know if the skill teaches the right thing.\n\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand superpowers:test-driven-development before using this skill. That skill defines the fundamental RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle. This skill adapts TDD to documentation.\n\n**Official guidance:** For Anthropic''s official skill authoring best practices, see anthropic-best-practices.md. This document provides additional patterns and guidelines that complement the TDD-focused approach in this skill.\n\n## What is a Skill?\n\nA **skill** is a reference guide for proven techniques, patterns, or tools. Skills help future Claude instances find and apply effective approaches.\n\n**Skills are:** Reusable techniques, patterns, tools, reference guides\n\n**Skills are NOT:** Narratives about how you solved a problem once\n\n## TDD Mapping for Skills\n\n| TDD Concept | Skill Creation |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| **Test case** | Pressure scenario with subagent |\n| **Production code** | Skill document (SKILL.md) |\n| **Test fails (RED)** | Agent violates rule without skill (baseline) |\n| **Test passes (GREEN)** | Agent complies with skill present |\n| **Refactor** | Close loopholes while maintaining compliance |\n| **Write test first** | Run baseline scenario BEFORE writing skill |\n| **Watch it fail** | Document exact rationalizations agent uses |\n| **Minimal code** | Write skill addressing those specific violations |\n| **Watch it pass** | Verify agent now complies |\n| **Refactor cycle** | Find new rationalizations → plug → re-verify |\n\nThe entire skill creation process follows RED-GREEN-REFACTOR.\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\n**Create when:**\n- Technique wasn''t intuitively obvious to you\n- You''d reference this again across projects\n- Pattern applies broadly (not project-specific)\n- Others would benefit\n\n**Don''t create for:**\n- One-off solutions\n- Standard practices well-documented elsewhere\n- Project-specific conventions (put in CLAUDE.md)\n- Mechanical constraints (if it''s enforceable with regex/validation, automate it—save documentation for judgment calls)\n\n## Skill Types\n\n### Technique\nConcrete method with steps to follow (condition-based-waiting, root-cause-tracing)\n\n### Pattern\nWay of thinking about problems (flatten-with-flags, test-invariants)\n\n### Reference\nAPI docs, syntax guides, tool documentation (office docs)\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n\n```\nskills/\n  skill-name/\n    SKILL.md              # Main reference (required)\n    supporting-file.*     # Only if needed\n```\n\n**Flat namespace** - all skills in one searchable namespace\n\n**Separate files for:**\n1. **Heavy reference** (100+ lines) - API docs, comprehensive syntax\n2. **Reusable tools** - Scripts, utilities, templates\n\n**Keep inline:**\n- Principles and concepts\n- Code patterns (< 50 lines)\n- Everything else\n\n## SKILL.md Structure\n\n**Frontmatter (YAML):**\n- Only two fields supported: `name` and `description`\n- Max 1024 characters total\n- `name`: Use letters, numbers, and hyphens only (no parentheses, special chars)\n- `description`: Third-person, describes ONLY when to use (NOT what it does)\n  - Start with \"Use when...\" to focus on triggering conditions\n  - Include specific symptoms, situations, and contexts\n  - **NEVER summarize the skill''s process or workflow** (see CSO section for why)\n  - Keep under 500 characters if possible\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: Skill-Name-With-Hyphens\ndescription: Use when [specific triggering conditions and symptoms]\n---\n\n# Skill Name\n\n## Overview\nWhat is this? Core principle in 1-2 sentences.\n\n## When to Use\n[Small inline flowchart IF decision non-obvious]\n\nBullet list with SYMPTOMS and use cases\nWhen NOT to use\n\n## Core Pattern (for techniques/patterns)\nBefore/after code comparison\n\n## Quick Reference\nTable or bullets for scanning common operations\n\n## Implementation\nInline code for simple patterns\nLink to file for heavy reference or reusable tools\n\n## Common Mistakes\nWhat goes wrong + fixes\n\n## Real-World Impact (optional)\nConcrete results\n```\n\n\n## Claude Search Optimization (CSO)\n\n**Critical for discovery:** Future Claude needs to FIND your skill\n\n### 1. Rich Description Field\n\n**Purpose:** Claude reads description to decide which skills to load for a given task. Make it answer: \"Should I read this skill right now?\"\n\n**Format:** Start with \"Use when...\" to focus on triggering conditions\n\n**CRITICAL: Description = When to Use, NOT What the Skill Does**\n\nThe description should ONLY describe triggering conditions. Do NOT summarize the skill''s process or workflow in the description.\n\n**Why this matters:** Testing revealed that when a description summarizes the skill''s workflow, Claude may follow the description instead of reading the full skill content. A description saying \"code review between tasks\" caused Claude to do ONE review, even though the skill''s flowchart clearly showed TWO reviews (spec compliance then code quality).\n\nWhen the description was changed to just \"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks\" (no workflow summary), Claude correctly read the flowchart and followed the two-stage review process.\n\n**The trap:** Descriptions that summarize workflow create a shortcut Claude will take. The skill body becomes documentation Claude skips.\n\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD: Summarizes workflow - Claude may follow this instead of reading skill\ndescription: Use when executing plans - dispatches subagent per task with code review between tasks\n\n# ❌ BAD: Too much process detail\ndescription: Use for TDD - write test first, watch it fail, write minimal code, refactor\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Just triggering conditions, no workflow summary\ndescription: Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Triggering conditions only\ndescription: Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code\n```\n\n**Content:**\n- Use concrete triggers, symptoms, and situations that signal this skill applies\n- Describe the *problem* (race conditions, inconsistent behavior) not *language-specific symptoms* (setTimeout, sleep)\n- Keep triggers technology-agnostic unless the skill itself is technology-specific\n- If skill is technology-specific, make that explicit in the trigger\n- Write in third person (injected into system prompt)\n- **NEVER summarize the skill''s process or workflow**\n\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD: Too abstract, vague, doesn''t include when to use\ndescription: For async testing\n\n# ❌ BAD: First person\ndescription: I can help you with async tests when they''re flaky\n\n# ❌ BAD: Mentions technology but skill isn''t specific to it\ndescription: Use when tests use setTimeout/sleep and are flaky\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Starts with \"Use when\", describes problem, no workflow\ndescription: Use when tests have race conditions, timing dependencies, or pass/fail inconsistently\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Technology-specific skill with explicit trigger\ndescription: Use when using React Router and handling authentication redirects\n```\n\n### 2. Keyword Coverage\n\nUse words Claude would search for:\n- Error messages: \"Hook timed out\", \"ENOTEMPTY\", \"race condition\"\n- Symptoms: \"flaky\", \"hanging\", \"zombie\", \"pollution\"\n- Synonyms: \"timeout/hang/freeze\", \"cleanup/teardown/afterEach\"\n- Tools: Actual commands, library names, file types\n\n### 3. Descriptive Naming\n\n**Use active voice, verb-first:**\n- ✅ `creating-skills` not `skill-creation`\n- ✅ `condition-based-waiting` not `async-test-helpers`\n\n### 4. Token Efficiency (Critical)\n\n**Problem:** getting-started and frequently-referenced skills load into EVERY conversation. Every token counts.\n\n**Target word counts:**\n- getting-started workflows: <150 words each\n- Frequently-loaded skills: <200 words total\n- Other skills: <500 words (still be concise)\n\n**Techniques:**\n\n**Move details to tool help:**\n```bash\n# ❌ BAD: Document all flags in SKILL.md\nsearch-conversations supports --text, --both, --after DATE, --before DATE, --limit N\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Reference --help\nsearch-conversations supports multiple modes and filters. Run --help for details.\n```\n\n**Use cross-references:**\n```markdown\n# ❌ BAD: Repeat workflow details\nWhen searching, dispatch subagent with template...\n[20 lines of repeated instructions]\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Reference other skill\nAlways use subagents (50-100x context savings). REQUIRED: Use [other-skill-name] for workflow.\n```\n\n**Compress examples:**\n```markdown\n# ❌ BAD: Verbose example (42 words)\nyour human partner: \"How did we handle authentication errors in React Router before?\"\nYou: I''ll search past conversations for React Router authentication patterns.\n[Dispatch subagent with search query: \"React Router authentication error handling 401\"]\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Minimal example (20 words)\nPartner: \"How did we handle auth errors in React Router?\"\nYou: Searching...\n[Dispatch subagent → synthesis]\n```\n\n**Eliminate redundancy:**\n- Don''t repeat what''s in cross-referenced skills\n- Don''t explain what''s obvious from command\n- Don''t include multiple examples of same pattern\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\nwc -w skills/path/SKILL.md\n# getting-started workflows: aim for <150 each\n# Other frequently-loaded: aim for <200 total\n```\n\n**Name by what you DO or core insight:**\n- ✅ `condition-based-waiting` > `async-test-helpers`\n- ✅ `using-skills` not `skill-usage`\n- ✅ `flatten-with-flags` > `data-structure-refactoring`\n- ✅ `root-cause-tracing` > `debugging-techniques`\n\n**Gerunds (-ing) work well for processes:**\n- `creating-skills`, `testing-skills`, `debugging-with-logs`\n- Active, describes the action you''re taking\n\n### 4. Cross-Referencing Other Skills\n\n**When writing documentation that references other skills:**\n\nUse skill name only, with explicit requirement markers:\n- ✅ Good: `**REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:test-driven-development`\n- ✅ Good: `**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand superpowers:systematic-debugging`\n- ❌ Bad: `See skills/testing/test-driven-development` (unclear if required)\n- ❌ Bad: `@skills/testing/test-driven-development/SKILL.md` (force-loads, burns context)\n\n**Why no @ links:** `@` syntax force-loads files immediately, consuming 200k+ context before you need them.\n\n## Flowchart Usage\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_flowchart {\n    \"Need to show information?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Use markdown\" [shape=box];\n    \"Small inline flowchart\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Need to show information?\" -> \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" -> \"Small inline flowchart\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" -> \"Use markdown\" [label=\"no\"];\n}\n```\n\n**Use flowcharts ONLY for:**\n- Non-obvious decision points\n- Process loops where you might stop too early\n- \"When to use A vs B\" decisions\n\n**Never use flowcharts for:**\n- Reference material → Tables, lists\n- Code examples → Markdown blocks\n- Linear instructions → Numbered lists\n- Labels without semantic meaning (step1, helper2)\n\nSee @graphviz-conventions.dot for graphviz style rules.\n\n**Visualizing for your human partner:** Use `render-graphs.js` in this directory to render a skill''s flowcharts to SVG:\n```bash\n./render-graphs.js ../some-skill           # Each diagram separately\n./render-graphs.js ../some-skill --combine # All diagrams in one SVG\n```\n\n## Code Examples\n\n**One excellent example beats many mediocre ones**\n\nChoose most relevant language:\n- Testing techniques → TypeScript/JavaScript\n- System debugging → Shell/Python\n- Data processing → Python\n\n**Good example:**\n- Complete and runnable\n- Well-commented explaining WHY\n- From real scenario\n- Shows pattern clearly\n- Ready to adapt (not generic template)\n\n**Don''t:**\n- Implement in 5+ languages\n- Create fill-in-the-blank templates\n- Write contrived examples\n\nYou''re good at porting - one great example is enough.\n\n## File Organization\n\n### Self-Contained Skill\n```\ndefense-in-depth/\n  SKILL.md    # Everything inline\n```\nWhen: All content fits, no heavy reference needed\n\n### Skill with Reusable Tool\n```\ncondition-based-waiting/\n  SKILL.md    # Overview + patterns\n  example.ts  # Working helpers to adapt\n```\nWhen: Tool is reusable code, not just narrative\n\n### Skill with Heavy Reference\n```\npptx/\n  SKILL.md       # Overview + workflows\n  pptxgenjs.md   # 600 lines API reference\n  ooxml.md       # 500 lines XML structure\n  scripts/       # Executable tools\n```\nWhen: Reference material too large for inline\n\n## The Iron Law (Same as TDD)\n\n```\nNO SKILL WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nThis applies to NEW skills AND EDITS to existing skills.\n\nWrite skill before testing? Delete it. Start over.\nEdit skill without testing? Same violation.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Not for \"simple additions\"\n- Not for \"just adding a section\"\n- Not for \"documentation updates\"\n- Don''t keep untested changes as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" while running tests\n- Delete means delete\n\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** The superpowers:test-driven-development skill explains why this matters. Same principles apply to documentation.\n\n## Testing All Skill Types\n\nDifferent skill types need different test approaches:\n\n### Discipline-Enforcing Skills (rules/requirements)\n\n**Examples:** TDD, verification-before-completion, designing-before-coding\n\n**Test with:**\n- Academic questions: Do they understand the rules?\n- Pressure scenarios: Do they comply under stress?\n- Multiple pressures combined: time + sunk cost + exhaustion\n- Identify rationalizations and add explicit counters\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent follows rule under maximum pressure\n\n### Technique Skills (how-to guides)\n\n**Examples:** condition-based-waiting, root-cause-tracing, defensive-programming\n\n**Test with:**\n- Application scenarios: Can they apply the technique correctly?\n- Variation scenarios: Do they handle edge cases?\n- Missing information tests: Do instructions have gaps?\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent successfully applies technique to new scenario\n\n### Pattern Skills (mental models)\n\n**Examples:** reducing-complexity, information-hiding concepts\n\n**Test with:**\n- Recognition scenarios: Do they recognize when pattern applies?\n- Application scenarios: Can they use the mental model?\n- Counter-examples: Do they know when NOT to apply?\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent correctly identifies when/how to apply pattern\n\n### Reference Skills (documentation/APIs)\n\n**Examples:** API documentation, command references, library guides\n\n**Test with:**\n- Retrieval scenarios: Can they find the right information?\n- Application scenarios: Can they use what they found correctly?\n- Gap testing: Are common use cases covered?\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent finds and correctly applies reference information\n\n## Common Rationalizations for Skipping Testing\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Skill is obviously clear\" | Clear to you ≠ clear to other agents. Test it. |\n| \"It''s just a reference\" | References can have gaps, unclear sections. Test retrieval. |\n| \"Testing is overkill\" | Untested skills have issues. Always. 15 min testing saves hours. |\n| \"I''ll test if problems emerge\" | Problems = agents can''t use skill. Test BEFORE deploying. |\n| \"Too tedious to test\" | Testing is less tedious than debugging bad skill in production. |\n| \"I''m confident it''s good\" | Overconfidence guarantees issues. Test anyway. |\n| \"Academic review is enough\" | Reading ≠ using. Test application scenarios. |\n| \"No time to test\" | Deploying untested skill wastes more time fixing it later. |\n\n**All of these mean: Test before deploying. No exceptions.**\n\n## Bulletproofing Skills Against Rationalization\n\nSkills that enforce discipline (like TDD) need to resist rationalization. Agents are smart and will find loopholes when under pressure.\n\n**Psychology note:** Understanding WHY persuasion techniques work helps you apply them systematically. See persuasion-principles.md for research foundation (Cialdini, 2021; Meincke et al., 2025) on authority, commitment, scarcity, social proof, and unity principles.\n\n### Close Every Loophole Explicitly\n\nDon''t just state the rule - forbid specific workarounds:\n\n<Bad>\n```markdown\nWrite code before test? Delete it.\n```\n</Bad>\n\n<Good>\n```markdown\nWrite code before test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n```\n</Good>\n\n### Address \"Spirit vs Letter\" Arguments\n\nAdd foundational principle early:\n\n```markdown\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n```\n\nThis cuts off entire class of \"I''m following the spirit\" rationalizations.\n\n### Build Rationalization Table\n\nCapture rationalizations from baseline testing (see Testing section below). Every excuse agents make goes in the table:\n\n```markdown\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n```\n\n### Create Red Flags List\n\nMake it easy for agents to self-check when rationalizing:\n\n```markdown\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n```\n\n### Update CSO for Violation Symptoms\n\nAdd to description: symptoms of when you''re ABOUT to violate the rule:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code\n```\n\n## RED-GREEN-REFACTOR for Skills\n\nFollow the TDD cycle:\n\n### RED: Write Failing Test (Baseline)\n\nRun pressure scenario with subagent WITHOUT the skill. Document exact behavior:\n- What choices did they make?\n- What rationalizations did they use (verbatim)?\n- Which pressures triggered violations?\n\nThis is \"watch the test fail\" - you must see what agents naturally do before writing the skill.\n\n### GREEN: Write Minimal Skill\n\nWrite skill that addresses those specific rationalizations. Don''t add extra content for hypothetical cases.\n\nRun same scenarios WITH skill. Agent should now comply.\n\n### REFACTOR: Close Loopholes\n\nAgent found new rationalization? Add explicit counter. Re-test until bulletproof.\n\n**Testing methodology:** See @testing-skills-with-subagents.md for the complete testing methodology:\n- How to write pressure scenarios\n- Pressure types (time, sunk cost, authority, exhaustion)\n- Plugging holes systematically\n- Meta-testing techniques\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Narrative Example\n\"In session 2025-10-03, we found empty projectDir caused...\"\n**Why bad:** Too specific, not reusable\n\n### ❌ Multi-Language Dilution\nexample-js.js, example-py.py, example-go.go\n**Why bad:** Mediocre quality, maintenance burden\n\n### ❌ Code in Flowcharts\n```dot\nstep1 [label=\"import fs\"];\nstep2 [label=\"read file\"];\n```\n**Why bad:** Can''t copy-paste, hard to read\n\n### ❌ Generic Labels\nhelper1, helper2, step3, pattern4\n**Why bad:** Labels should have semantic meaning\n\n## STOP: Before Moving to Next Skill\n\n**After writing ANY skill, you MUST STOP and complete the deployment process.**\n\n**Do NOT:**\n- Create multiple skills in batch without testing each\n- Move to next skill before current one is verified\n- Skip testing because \"batching is more efficient\"\n\n**The deployment checklist below is MANDATORY for EACH skill.**\n\nDeploying untested skills = deploying untested code. It''s a violation of quality standards.\n\n## Skill Creation Checklist (TDD Adapted)\n\n**IMPORTANT: Use TodoWrite to create todos for EACH checklist item below.**\n\n**RED Phase - Write Failing Test:**\n- [ ] Create pressure scenarios (3+ combined pressures for discipline skills)\n- [ ] Run scenarios WITHOUT skill - document baseline behavior verbatim\n- [ ] Identify patterns in rationalizations/failures\n\n**GREEN Phase - Write Minimal Skill:**\n- [ ] Name uses only letters, numbers, hyphens (no parentheses/special chars)\n- [ ] YAML frontmatter with only name and description (max 1024 chars)\n- [ ] Description starts with \"Use when...\" and includes specific triggers/symptoms\n- [ ] Description written in third person\n- [ ] Keywords throughout for search (errors, symptoms, tools)\n- [ ] Clear overview with core principle\n- [ ] Address specific baseline failures identified in RED\n- [ ] Code inline OR link to separate file\n- [ ] One excellent example (not multi-language)\n- [ ] Run scenarios WITH skill - verify agents now comply\n\n**REFACTOR Phase - Close Loopholes:**\n- [ ] Identify NEW rationalizations from testing\n- [ ] Add explicit counters (if discipline skill)\n- [ ] Build rationalization table from all test iterations\n- [ ] Create red flags list\n- [ ] Re-test until bulletproof\n\n**Quality Checks:**\n- [ ] Small flowchart only if decision non-obvious\n- [ ] Quick reference table\n- [ ] Common mistakes section\n- [ ] No narrative storytelling\n- [ ] Supporting files only for tools or heavy reference\n\n**Deployment:**\n- [ ] Commit skill to git and push to your fork (if configured)\n- [ ] Consider contributing back via PR (if broadly useful)\n\n## Discovery Workflow\n\nHow future Claude finds your skill:\n\n1. **Encounters problem** (\"tests are flaky\")\n3. **Finds SKILL** (description matches)\n4. **Scans overview** (is this relevant?)\n5. **Reads patterns** (quick reference table)\n6. **Loads example** (only when implementing)\n\n**Optimize for this flow** - put searchable terms early and often.\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**Creating skills IS TDD for process documentation.**\n\nSame Iron Law: No skill without failing test first.\nSame cycle: RED (baseline) → GREEN (write skill) → REFACTOR (close loopholes).\nSame benefits: Better quality, fewer surprises, bulletproof results.\n\nIf you follow TDD for code, follow it for skills. It''s the same discipline applied to documentation.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:12:12.278Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and Codex requiring advanced process documentation through Test-Driven Development","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 和 Codex 等需要通过测试驱动开发进行高级流程文档化的 AI 代理","ja":"Claude CodeやCodexなどの高度なプロセス文書化をテスト駆動開発を通じて要求するAIエージェントに最適","ko":"테스트 주도 개발을 통해 고급 프로세스 문서화를 요구하는 Claude Code 및 Codex와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code y Codex que requieren documentación avanzada de procesos mediante Desarrollo Guiado por Pruebas","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents IA comme Claude Code et Codex nécessitant une documentation de processus avancée via le Développement Piloté par les Tests","de":"Ideal für KI-Agenten wie Claude Code und Codex, die eine erweiterte Prozessdokumentation durch testgetriebene Entwicklung benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e Codex que exigem documentação de processo avançada por meio do Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и Codex, требующих расширенной документации процесса через разработку, управляемую тестами","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و Codex الذين يتطلبون توثيق عملية متقدم من خلال التطوير القائم على الاختبار"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to comply with documentation standards by applying test cases, watching baseline behavior, and refactoring to close loopholes, utilizing agent-specific directories like ~/.claude/skills and ~/.codex/skills","zh":"通过应用测试用例、观察基线行为和重构以关闭漏洞，赋予代理遵守文档标准的能力，利用代理特定目录如 ~/.claude/skills 和 ~/.codex/skills","ja":"テストケースの適用、ベースライン動作の監視、ループホールの閉じるためのリファクタリングを行い、文書化規格に準拠するエージェントを作成することができる。エージェント固有のディレクトリ such as ~/.claude/skills および ~/.codex/skills を利用","ko":"테스트 케이스를 적용하고, 기준 行동을 관찰하고, 리팩토링을 통해 루프홀을 닫는 등, 에이전트별 디렉토리 such as ~/.claude/skills 및 ~/.codex/skills를 활용하여 문서화 표준을 준수하도록 에이전트를 강화하는 것","es":"Permite a los agentes cumplir con los estándares de documentación aplicando casos de prueba, observando el comportamiento base y refactorizando para cerrar lagunas, utilizando directorios específicos de agentes como ~/.claude/skills y ~/.codex/skills","fr":"Permet aux agents de se conformer aux normes de documentation en appliquant des cas de test, en observant le comportement de base et en refactorisant pour combler les lacunes, en utilisant des répertoires spécifiques aux agents comme ~/.claude/skills et ~/.codex/skills","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Dokumentationsstandards einzuhalten, indem Testfälle angewendet, Basisverhalten beobachtet und refaktorisiert werden, um Lücken zu schließen, unter Verwendung agentspezifischer Verzeichnisse wie ~/.claude/skills und ~/.codex/skills","pt":"Habilita os agentes a cumprir os padrões de documentação aplicando casos de teste, observando o comportamento de baseline e reestruturando para fechar lacunas, utilizando diretórios específicos do agente, como ~/.claude/skills e ~/.codex/skills","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью соблюдать стандарты документации, применяя тестовые случаи, наблюдая за базовым поведением и рефакторингом для закрытия лазеек, используя агент-специфические директории, такие как ~/.claude/skills и ~/.codex/skills","ar":"يتمكّن الوكلاء من الامتثال لمعايير التوثيق من خلال تطبيق الحالات التجريبية، مراقبة السلوك الأساسي وإعادة هيكلة الإغلاق للثغرات، باستخدام الدلائل الخاصة بالوكيل، مثل ~/.claude/skills و ~/.codex/skills"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating process documentation testing","Generating compliant documentation","Debugging agent behavior through test-driven development"],"zh":["自动化流程文档测试","生成兼容文档","通过测试驱动开发调试代理行为"],"ja":["プロセス文書化テストの自動化","準拠文書の生成","テスト駆動開発によるエージェント動作のデバッグ"],"ko":["프로세스 문서화 테스트 자동화","준수 문서 생성","테스트 주도 개발을 통한 에이전트 행동 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas de documentación de procesos","Generación de documentación compatible","Depuración del comportamiento del agente mediante desarrollo guiado por pruebas"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests de documentation des processus","Génération d''une documentation conforme","Débogage du comportement de l''agent via le développement piloté par les tests"],"de":["Automatisierung von Prozessdokumentationstests","Erstellung konformer Dokumentation","Debugging des Agentenverhaltens durch testgetriebene Entwicklung"],"pt":["Automatizar testes de documentação de processo","Gerar documentação compatível","Depurar comportamento de agente por meio do desenvolvimento orientado a testes"],"ru":["Автоматизация тестирования документации процесса","Генерация соответствующей документации","Отладка поведения агента с помощью разработки, управляемой тестами"],"ar":["تحسين اختبارات توثيق العملية","إنتاج توثيق متوافق","تصحيح سلوك العميل من خلال التطوير القائم على الاختبار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires agent-specific directory access","Limited to agents with test-driven development capabilities"],"zh":["需要代理特定目录访问","仅限具有测试驱动开发能力的代理"],"ja":["エージェント固有のディレクトリへのアクセスが必要","テスト駆動開発機能を持つエージェントに限定"],"ko":["에이전트별 디렉토리 액세스가 필요","테스트 주도 개발 기능을 갖춘 에이전트로 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso a directorios específicos del agente","Limitado a agentes con capacidades de desarrollo guiado por pruebas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au répertoire spécifique de l''agent","Limité aux agents ayant des capacités de développement piloté par les tests"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf agentspezifische Verzeichnisse","Beschränkt auf Agenten mit Fähigkeiten zur testgetriebenen Entwicklung"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao diretório específico do agente","Limitado a agentes com capacidades de desenvolvimento dirigido por testes"],"ru":["Требует доступа к агент-специфической директории","Ограничен агентами с возможностями разработки, управляемой тестами"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الدليل الخاص بالوكيل","محدود بالوكلاء الذين لديهم القدرات على التطوير القائم على الاختبار"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
