,"pt":"O Gerador de Manifestos Kubernetes fornece orientação abrangente para criar manifestos bem estruturados e seguros","ru":"Генератор манифестов Kubernetes предоставляет всестороннее руководство для создания хорошо структурированных и безопасных манифестов","ar":"مُولِد مаниفستات كوبيرنتس يوفر إرشادات شاملة لإنشاء مانيفستات منظمة وأمنة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["K8s","K8s","K8sConfigMaps","K8sSecrets","K8sPersistentVolumeClaims"],"ja":["K8s","K8s","K8sConfigMaps","K8sSecrets","K8sPersistentVolumeClaims"],"ko":["K8s","K8s","K8sConfigMaps","K8sSecrets","K8sPersistentVolumeClaims"],"es":["Generación de manifiestos de despliegue","Creación de servicios y configuraciones","Soporte para ConfigMaps y Secretos","Generación de reclamaciones de volumen persistente","Seguridad y mejores prácticas de Kubernetes"],"fr":["Génération de manifestes de déploiement","Création de services et de configurations","Prise en charge de ConfigMaps et de secrets","Génération de revendications de volume persistant","Sécurité et meilleures pratiques de Kubernetes"],"de":["Generierung von Deploy-Manifesten","Erstellung von Diensten und Konfigurationen","Unterstützung für ConfigMaps und Geheimnisse","Generierung von PersistentVolumeClaims","Sicherheit und Best Practices für Kubernetes"],"pt":["Criação de manifestos de implantação","Suporte a Serviços, ConfigMaps, Segredos e Reivindicações de Volume Persistente","Orientação passo a passo para manifestos prontos para produção","Seguimento de práticas recomendadas de cloud-native e convenções do Kubernetes","Geração de manifestos bem estruturados e seguros"],"ru":["Создание манифестов развертывания","Поддержка Сервисов, ConfigMaps, Секретов и Заявок на постоянный объем","Пошаговое руководство для манифестов, готовых к производству","Соблюдение рекомендованных практик cloud-native и конвенций Kubernetes","Генерация хорошо структурированных и безопасных манифестов"],"ar":["إنشاء مانيفستات النشر","دعم الخدمات، ConfigMaps، الأسرار وإقتراحات الحجم الثابت","دليل خطوة بخطوة لمانيفستات جاهزة للإنتاج","التعاون مع ممارسات السحاب الأصلية وتقاليد كوبيرنتس","إنشاء مانيفستات منظمة وأمنة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["K8s","K8s","K8sConfigMaps","K8sSecrets","K8sPersistentVolumeClaims","K8s","K8s"],"ja":["K8s","K8s","K8sConfigMaps","K8sSecrets","K8sPersistentVolumeClaims","K8s","K8s"],"ko":["K8s","K8s","K8sConfigMaps","K8sSecrets","K8sPersistentVolumeClaims","K8s","K8s"],"es":["Kubernetes","manifiestos de Kubernetes","despliegue de Kubernetes","seguridad de Kubernetes","mejores prácticas de Kubernetes","ConfigMaps","Secretos","PersistentVolumeClaims"],"fr":["Kubernetes","manifestes Kubernetes","déploiement Kubernetes","sécurité Kubernetes","meilleures pratiques Kubernetes","ConfigMaps","secrets","revendications de volume persistant"],"de":["Kubernetes","Kubernetes-Manifeste","Kubernetes-Deploy","Kubernetes-Sicherheit","Kubernetes-Best-Practices","ConfigMaps","Geheimnisse","PersistentVolumeClaims"],"pt":["Kubernetes","Manifestos Kubernetes","Gerador de Manifestos","Implantação de Kubernetes","Serviços de Kubernetes","ConfigMaps","Segredos","Reivindicações de Volume Persistente"],"ru":["Kubernetes","Манифесты Kubernetes","Генератор манифестов","Развертывание Kubernetes","Сервисы Kubernetes","ConfigMaps","Секреты","Заявки на постоянный объем"],"ar":["كوبيرنتس","مаниفستات كوبيرنتس","مُولِد مانيفستات","نشر كوبيرنتس","خدمات كوبيرنتس","ConfigMaps","أسرار","إقتراحات الحجم الثابت"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"k8s-manifest-generator","description":"Create production-ready Kubernetes manifests for Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, and Secrets following best practices and security standards. Use when generating Kubernetes YAML manifests, creating K8s resources, or implementing production-grade Kubernetes configurations.","bodyPreview":"# Kubernetes Manifest Generator\n\nStep-by-step guidance for creating production-ready Kubernetes manifests including Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets, and PersistentVolumeClaims.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive guidance for generating well-structured, secure, and production-ready Kubernetes manifests following cloud-native best practices and Kubernetes conventions.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n\n- Create new Kubernetes Deployment manifests\n-","body":"# Kubernetes Manifest Generator\n\nStep-by-step guidance for creating production-ready Kubernetes manifests including Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets, and PersistentVolumeClaims.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive guidance for generating well-structured, secure, and production-ready Kubernetes manifests following cloud-native best practices and Kubernetes conventions.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n\n- Create new Kubernetes Deployment manifests\n- Define Service resources for network connectivity\n- Generate ConfigMap and Secret resources for configuration management\n- Create PersistentVolumeClaim manifests for stateful workloads\n- Follow Kubernetes best practices and naming conventions\n- Implement resource limits, health checks, and security contexts\n- Design manifests for multi-environment deployments\n\n## Step-by-Step Workflow\n\n### 1. Gather Requirements\n\n**Understand the workload:**\n\n- Application type (stateless/stateful)\n- Container image and version\n- Environment variables and configuration needs\n- Storage requirements\n- Network exposure requirements (internal/external)\n- Resource requirements (CPU, memory)\n- Scaling requirements\n- Health check endpoints\n\n**Questions to ask:**\n\n- What is the application name and purpose?\n- What container image and tag will be used?\n- Does the application need persistent storage?\n- What ports does the application expose?\n- Are there any secrets or configuration files needed?\n- What are the CPU and memory requirements?\n- Does the application need to be exposed externally?\n\n### 2. Create Deployment Manifest\n\n**Follow this structure:**\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: <app-name>\n  namespace: <namespace>\n  labels:\n    app: <app-name>\n    version: <version>\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: <app-name>\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: <app-name>\n        version: <version>\n    spec:\n      containers:\n        - name: <container-name>\n          image: <image>:<tag>\n          ports:\n            - containerPort: <port>\n              name: http\n          resources:\n            requests:\n              memory: \"256Mi\"\n              cpu: \"250m\"\n            limits:\n              memory: \"512Mi\"\n              cpu: \"500m\"\n          livenessProbe:\n            httpGet:\n              path: /health\n              port: http\n            initialDelaySeconds: 30\n            periodSeconds: 10\n          readinessProbe:\n            httpGet:\n              path: /ready\n              port: http\n            initialDelaySeconds: 5\n            periodSeconds: 5\n          env:\n            - name: ENV_VAR\n              value: \"value\"\n          envFrom:\n            - configMapRef:\n                name: <app-name>-config\n            - secretRef:\n                name: <app-name>-secret\n```\n\n**Best practices to apply:**\n\n- Always set resource requests and limits\n- Implement both liveness and readiness probes\n- Use specific image tags (never `:latest`)\n- Apply security context for non-root users\n- Use labels for organization and selection\n- Set appropriate replica count based on availability needs\n\n**Reference:** See `references/deployment-spec.md` for detailed deployment options\n\n### 3. Create Service Manifest\n\n**Choose the appropriate Service type:**\n\n**ClusterIP (internal only):**\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: <app-name>\n  namespace: <namespace>\n  labels:\n    app: <app-name>\nspec:\n  type: ClusterIP\n  selector:\n    app: <app-name>\n  ports:\n    - name: http\n      port: 80\n      targetPort: 8080\n      protocol: TCP\n```\n\n**LoadBalancer (external access):**\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: <app-name>\n  namespace: <namespace>\n  labels:\n    app: <app-name>\n  annotations:\n    service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-type: nlb\nspec:\n  type: LoadBalancer\n  selector:\n    app: <app-name>\n  ports:\n    - name: http\n      port: 80\n      targetPort: 8080\n      protocol: TCP\n```\n\n**Reference:** See `references/service-spec.md` for service types and networking\n\n### 4. Create ConfigMap\n\n**For application configuration:**\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: <app-name>-config\n  namespace: <namespace>\ndata:\n  APP_MODE: production\n  LOG_LEVEL: info\n  DATABASE_HOST: db.example.com\n  # For config files\n  app.properties: |\n    server.port=8080\n    server.host=0.0.0.0\n    logging.level=INFO\n```\n\n**Best practices:**\n\n- Use ConfigMaps for non-sensitive data only\n- Organize related configuration together\n- Use meaningful names for keys\n- Consider using one ConfigMap per component\n- Version ConfigMaps when making changes\n\n**Reference:** See `assets/configmap-template.yaml` for examples\n\n### 5. Create Secret\n\n**For sensitive data:**\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Secret\nmetadata:\n  name: <app-name>-secret\n  namespace: <namespace>\ntype: Opaque\nstringData:\n  DATABASE_PASSWORD: \"changeme\"\n  API_KEY: \"secret-api-key\"\n  # For certificate files\n  tls.crt: |\n    -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\n    ...\n    -----END CERTIFICATE-----\n  tls.key: |\n    -----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n    ...\n    -----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n```\n\n**Security considerations:**\n\n- Never commit secrets to Git in plain text\n- Use Sealed Secrets, External Secrets Operator, or Vault\n- Rotate secrets regularly\n- Use RBAC to limit secret access\n- Consider using Secret type: `kubernetes.io/tls` for TLS secrets\n\n### 6. Create PersistentVolumeClaim (if needed)\n\n**For stateful applications:**\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: <app-name>-data\n  namespace: <namespace>\nspec:\n  accessModes:\n    - ReadWriteOnce\n  storageClassName: gp3\n  resources:\n    requests:\n      storage: 10Gi\n```\n\n**Mount in Deployment:**\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  template:\n    spec:\n      containers:\n        - name: app\n          volumeMounts:\n            - name: data\n              mountPath: /var/lib/app\n      volumes:\n        - name: data\n          persistentVolumeClaim:\n            claimName: <app-name>-data\n```\n\n**Storage considerations:**\n\n- Choose appropriate StorageClass for performance needs\n- Use ReadWriteOnce for single-pod access\n- Use ReadWriteMany for multi-pod shared storage\n- Consider backup strategies\n- Set appropriate retention policies\n\n### 7. Apply Security Best Practices\n\n**Add security context to Deployment:**\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  template:\n    spec:\n      securityContext:\n        runAsNonRoot: true\n        runAsUser: 1000\n        fsGroup: 1000\n        seccompProfile:\n          type: RuntimeDefault\n      containers:\n        - name: app\n          securityContext:\n            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n            capabilities:\n              drop:\n                - ALL\n```\n\n**Security checklist:**\n\n- [ ] Run as non-root user\n- [ ] Drop all capabilities\n- [ ] Use read-only root filesystem\n- [ ] Disable privilege escalation\n- [ ] Set seccomp profile\n- [ ] Use Pod Security Standards\n\n### 8. Add Labels and Annotations\n\n**Standard labels (recommended):**\n\n```yaml\nmetadata:\n  labels:\n    app.kubernetes.io/name: <app-name>\n    app.kubernetes.io/instance: <instance-name>\n    app.kubernetes.io/version: \"1.0.0\"\n    app.kubernetes.io/component: backend\n    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: <system-name>\n    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: kubectl\n```\n\n**Useful annotations:**\n\n```yaml\nmetadata:\n  annotations:\n    description: \"Application description\"\n    contact: \"team@example.com\"\n    prometheus.io/scrape: \"true\"\n    prometheus.io/port: \"9090\"\n    prometheus.io/path: \"/metrics\"\n```\n\n### 9. Organize Multi-Resource Manifests\n\n**File organization options:**\n\n**Option 1: Single file with `---` separator**\n\n```yaml\n# app-name.yaml\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\n...\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Secret\n...\n---\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\n...\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\n...\n```\n\n**Option 2: Separate files**\n\n```\nmanifests/\n├── configmap.yaml\n├── secret.yaml\n├── deployment.yaml\n├── service.yaml\n└── pvc.yaml\n```\n\n**Option 3: Kustomize structure**\n\n```\nbase/\n├── kustomization.yaml\n├── deployment.yaml\n├── service.yaml\n└── configmap.yaml\noverlays/\n├── dev/\n│   └── kustomization.yaml\n└── prod/\n    └── kustomization.yaml\n```\n\n### 10. Validate and Test\n\n**Validation steps:**\n\n```bash\n# Dry-run validation\nkubectl apply -f manifest.yaml --dry-run=client\n\n# Server-side validation\nkubectl apply -f manifest.yaml --dry-run=server\n\n# Validate with kubeval\nkubeval manifest.yaml\n\n# Validate with kube-score\nkube-score score manifest.yaml\n\n# Check with kube-linter\nkube-linter lint manifest.yaml\n```\n\n**Testing checklist:**\n\n- [ ] Manifest passes dry-run validation\n- [ ] All required fields are present\n- [ ] Resource limits are reasonable\n- [ ] Health checks are configured\n- [ ] Security context is set\n- [ ] Labels follow conventions\n- [ ] Namespace exists or is created\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Simple Stateless Web Application\n\n**Use case:** Standard web API or microservice\n\n**Components needed:**\n\n- Deployment (3 replicas for HA)\n- ClusterIP Service\n- ConfigMap for configuration\n- Secret for API keys\n- HorizontalPodAutoscaler (optional)\n\n**Reference:** See `assets/deployment-template.yaml`\n\n### Pattern 2: Stateful Database Application\n\n**Use case:** Database or persistent storage application\n\n**Components needed:**\n\n- StatefulSet (not Deployment)\n- Headless Service\n- PersistentVolumeClaim template\n- ConfigMap for DB configuration\n- Secret for credentials\n\n### Pattern 3: Background Job or Cron\n\n**Use case:** Scheduled tasks or batch processing\n\n**Components needed:**\n\n- CronJob or Job\n- ConfigMap for job parameters\n- Secret for credentials\n- ServiceAccount with RBAC\n\n### Pattern 4: Multi-Container Pod\n\n**Use case:** Application with sidecar containers\n\n**Components needed:**\n\n- Deployment with multiple containers\n- Shared volumes between containers\n- Init containers for setup\n- Service (if needed)\n\n## Templates\n\nThe following templates are available in the `assets/` directory:\n\n- `deployment-template.yaml` - Standard deployment with best practices\n- `service-template.yaml` - Service configurations (ClusterIP, LoadBalancer, NodePort)\n- `configmap-template.yaml` - ConfigMap examples with different data types\n- `secret-template.yaml` - Secret examples (to be generated, not committed)\n- `pvc-template.yaml` - PersistentVolumeClaim templates\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\n- `references/deployment-spec.md` - Detailed Deployment specification\n- `references/service-spec.md` - Service types and networking details\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Always set resource requests and limits** - Prevents resource starvation\n2. **Implement health checks** - Ensures Kubernetes can manage your application\n3. **Use specific image tags** - Avoid unpredictable deployments\n4. **Apply security contexts** - Run as non-root, drop capabilities\n5. **Use ConfigMaps and Secrets** - Separate config from code\n6. **Label everything** - Enables filtering and organization\n7. **Follow naming conventions** - Use standard Kubernetes labels\n8. **Validate before applying** - Use dry-run and validation tools\n9. **Version your manifests** - Keep in Git with version control\n10. **Document with annotations** - Add context for other developers\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**Pods not starting:**\n\n- Check image pull errors: `kubectl describe pod <pod-name>`\n- Verify resource availability: `kubectl get nodes`\n- Check events: `kubectl get events --sort-by=''.lastTimestamp''`\n\n**Service not accessible:**\n\n- Verify selector matches pod labels: `kubectl get endpoints <service-name>`\n- Check service type and port configuration\n- Test from within cluster: `kubectl run debug --rm -it --image=busybox -- sh`\n\n**ConfigMap/Secret not loading:**\n\n- Verify names match in Deployment\n- Check namespace\n- Ensure resources exist: `kubectl get configmap,secret`\n\n## Next Steps\n\nAfter creating manifests:\n\n1. Store in Git repository\n2. Set up CI/CD pipeline for deployment\n3. Consider using Helm or Kustomize for templating\n4. Implement GitOps with ArgoCD or Flux\n5. Add monitoring and observability\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- `helm-chart-scaffolding` - For templating and packaging\n- `gitops-workflow` - For automated deployments\n- `k8s-security-policies` - For advanced security configurations\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:16:00.106Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Native Agents requiring automated generation of production-ready Kubernetes manifests","zh":"适用于需要自动生成生产就绪 Kubernetes 清单的云原生代理","ja":"クラウドネイティブエージェントが自動生成されたプロダクションレディのKubernetesマニフェストを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"생산 준비가 된 Kubernetes 매니페스트를 자동으로 생성해야 하는 클라우드 네이티브 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes nativos de la nube que requieren generación automatizada de manifiestos de Kubernetes listos para producción","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Cloud Natifs nécessitant une génération automatisée de manifests Kubernetes prêts pour la production","de":"Ideal für Cloud Native Agents, die eine automatisierte Generierung von produktionsreifen Kubernetes-Manifests erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Cloud Native que requerem geração automatizada de manifestos Kubernetes prontos para produção","ru":"Идеально подходит для Cloud Native агентов, требующих автоматизированного создания готовых к эксплуатации манифестов Kubernetes","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء السحابة الأصلية التي تتطلب إنشاءً آليًا لبيانات الضبط Kubernetes الجاهزة للإنتاج"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate well-structured, secure, and production-ready Kubernetes manifests following cloud-native best practices and Kubernetes conventions, including Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets, and PersistentVolumeClaims","zh":"赋予代理生成结构良好、安全且生产就绪的Kubernetes清单的能力，遵循云原生最佳实践和Kubernetes惯例，包括Deployments、Services、ConfigMaps、Secrets和PersistentVolumeClaims","ja":"クラウドネイティブのベストプラクティスおよびKubernetesの規約に従い、構造化された、安全で、プロダクションレディのKubernetesマニフェストを生成するエージェントの能力を提供する。Deployments、Services、ConfigMaps、Secrets、PersistentVolumeClaimsなど","ko":"클라우드 네이티브 에이전트가 구조적으로 잘 정리되어 있고, 보안이 되고, 프로덕션 준비가 된 쿠버네티스 매니페스트를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여한다. 클라우드 네이티브의最佳实践 및 쿠버네티스 관례를 따르며, Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets 및 PersistentVolumeClaims 등을 포함","es":"Permite a los agentes generar manifiestos de Kubernetes bien estructurados, seguros y listos para producción, siguiendo las mejores prácticas nativas de la nube y las convenciones de Kubernetes, incluyendo Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets y PersistentVolumeClaims","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des manifests Kubernetes bien structurés, sécurisés et prêts pour la production, en suivant les meilleures pratiques cloud natives et les conventions Kubernetes, y compris les Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets et PersistentVolumeClaims","de":"Ermöglicht Agents die Generierung von gut strukturierten, sicheren und produktionsreifen Kubernetes-Manifests nach Cloud-nativen Best Practices und Kubernetes-Konventionen, einschließlich Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets und PersistentVolumeClaims","pt":"Capacita os agentes a gerar manifestos Kubernetes bem estruturados, seguros e prontos para produção, seguindo as melhores práticas cloud-native e as convenções do Kubernetes, incluindo Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets e PersistentVolumeClaims","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать хорошо структурированные, безопасные и готовые к эксплуатации манифесты Kubernetes в соответствии с лучшими практиками cloud-native и соглашениями Kubernetes, включая Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets и PersistentVolumeClaims","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء بيانات ضبط Kubernetes منظمة جيدًا وآمنة وجاهزة للإنتاج وفقًا لأفضل ممارسات السحابة الأصلية وأعراف Kubernetes، بما في ذلك النشرات Deployments والخدمات Services وخرائط التهيئة ConfigMaps والأسرار Secrets ومطالبات الحجم الدائم PersistentVolumeClaims"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating new Kubernetes Deployment manifests","Creating secure ConfigMaps and Secrets","Automating PersistentVolumeClaims for stateful applications"],"zh":["生成新的Kubernetes部署清单","创建安全的ConfigMaps和Secrets","为有状态应用程序自动化PersistentVolumeClaims"],"ja":["新しいKubernetesデプロイマニフェストを生成する","セキュアなConfigMapsとSecretsを作成する","ステートフルアプリケーションのPersistentVolumeClaimsを自動化する"],"ko":["新的 쿠버네티스 배포 매니페스트 생성","보안 ConfigMaps 및 Secrets 생성","상태가 있는 애플리케이션을 위한 PersistentVolumeClaims 자동화"],"es":["Generar nuevos manifiestos de Kubernetes Deployment","Crear ConfigMaps y Secrets seguros","Automatizar PersistentVolumeClaims para aplicaciones con estado"],"fr":["Génération de nouveaux manifests Kubernetes Deployment","Création de ConfigMaps et Secrets sécurisés","Automatisation des PersistentVolumeClaims pour applications stateful"],"de":["Generieren neuer Kubernetes Deployment-Manifests","Erstellen sicherer ConfigMaps und Secrets","Automatisieren von PersistentVolumeClaims für Stateful Applications"],"pt":["Gerar novos manifestos de Kubernetes Deployment","Criar ConfigMaps e Secrets seguros","Automatizar PersistentVolumeClaims para aplicações stateful"],"ru":["Создание новых манифестов развертывания Kubernetes (Deployment)","Создание безопасных ConfigMaps и Secrets","Автоматизация создания PersistentVolumeClaims для stateful-приложений"],"ar":["إنشاء بيانات ضبط نشر Kubernetes جديدة","إنشاء خرائط تهيئة ConfigMaps وأسرار Secrets آمنة","أتمتة مطالب الحجم الدائم PersistentVolumeClaims للتطبيقات ذات الحالة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Kubernetes conventions and cloud-native best practices","Limited to generating manifests for Kubernetes resources"],"zh":["需要了解Kubernetes惯例和云原生最佳实践","仅限生成Kubernetes资源的清单"],"ja":["Kubernetesの規約およびクラウドネイティブのベストプラクティスについての知識が必要","Kubernetesリソースのマニフェストの生成のみ"],"ko":["쿠버네티스 관례 및 클라우드 네이티브의最佳实践에 대한 지식이 필요","쿠버네티스 리소스의 매니페스트 생성만 가능"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de las convenciones de Kubernetes y las mejores prácticas nativas de la nube","Limitado a generar manifiestos para recursos de Kubernetes"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des conventions Kubernetes et des meilleures pratiques cloud natives","Limité à la génération de manifests pour les ressources Kubernetes"],"de":["Erfordert Kenntnisse der Kubernetes-Konventionen und Cloud-nativen Best Practices","Beschränkt auf die Generierung von Manifests für Kubernetes-Ressourcen"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento das convenções do Kubernetes e das melhores práticas cloud-native","Limitado à geração de manifestos para recursos do Kubernetes"],"ru":["Требует знания соглашений Kubernetes и лучших практик cloud-native","Ограничено созданием манифестов только для ресурсов Kubernetes"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بأعراف Kubernetes وأفضل ممارسات السحابة الأصلية","يقتصر على إنشاء بيانات الضبط لموارد Kubernetes فقط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
