lines 및 Remote bindings 등의 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Cloudflare R2 es un almacenamiento de objetos en la nube que ofrece escalabilidad y seguridad para aplicaciones modernas","fr":"Cloudflare R2 est un stockage d''objets en ligne qui offre une évolutivité et une sécurité pour les applications modernes","de":"Cloudflare R2 ist ein Objektspeicher in der Cloud, der Skalierbarkeit und Sicherheit für moderne Anwendungen bietet","pt":"O Cloudflare R2 é um armazenamento de objetos produção pronto, com recursos como R2 SQL e Pipelines","ru":"Cloudflare R2 — производственное объектное хранилище, с функциями như R2 SQL и Pipelines","ar":"Cloudflare R2 هو تخزين كائنات جاهز للإنتاج ، مع ميزات مثل R2 SQL و Pipelines","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["R2 SQL 开放测试","Pipelines 一般可用性","Remote bindings 一般可用性","Serverless 查询引擎","实时流数据摄取","本地开发连接部署的 R2"],"ja":["R2 SQL オープンベータ","Pipelines 一般提供","Remote bindings 一般提供","サーバーレス クエリ エンジン","リアルタイム ストリーム データ インジェスト","ローカル開発接続デプロイされた R2"],"ko":["R2 SQL 오픈 베타","Pipelines 일반 제공","Remote bindings 일반 제공","서버리스 쿼리 엔진","실시간 스트림 데이터 수집","로컬 개발 연결 배포된 R2"],"es":["Almacenamiento de objetos escalable","Motor de consulta servidorless R2 SQL","Ingesta de flujo en tiempo real con Pipelines","Enlaces remotos para desarrollo local","Integración con Cloudflare Worker"],"fr":["Stockage d''objets évolutif","Moteur de requête serveurless R2 SQL","Ingestion de flux en temps réel avec Pipelines","Liens distants pour le développement local","Intégration avec Cloudflare Worker"],"de":["Skalierbarer Objektspeicher","Serverloser Abfragemotor R2 SQL","Echtzeit-Stream-Ingesta mit Pipelines","Remote-Bindings für lokale Entwicklung","Integration mit Cloudflare Worker"],"pt":["Armazenamento de objetos escalável","R2 SQL para consultas serverless","Pipelines para ingestão de fluxos em tempo real","Ligações remotas para desenvolvimento local","Integração com Cloudflare Worker"],"ru":["Масштабируемое объектное хранилище","R2 SQL для серверных запросов","Pipelines для реального времени потоковой ингестии","Удаленные привязки для локальной разработки","Интеграция с Cloudflare Worker"],"ar":["تخزين كائنات قابل للتوسيع","R2 SQL للاستفسارات بدون خادم","Pipelines لاستقبال تدفقات الوقت الفعلي","الترابط عن بعد للتنمية المحلية","التكامل مع Cloudflare Worker"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cloudflare R2","对象存储","R2 SQL","Pipelines","Remote bindings","Serverless 查询引擎","实时流数据摄取"],"ja":["Cloudflare R2","オブジェクトストレージ","R2 SQL","Pipelines","Remote bindings","サーバーレス クエリ エンジン","リアルタイム ストリーム データ インジェスト"],"ko":["Cloudflare R2","객체 저장소","R2 SQL","Pipelines","Remote bindings","서버리스 쿼리 엔진","실시간 스트림 데이터 수집"],"es":["almacenamiento de objetos en la nube","Cloudflare R2","desarrollo de aplicaciones modernas","escalabilidad y seguridad","motor de consulta servidorless","ingesta de flujo en tiempo real"],"fr":["stockage d''objets en ligne","Cloudflare R2","développement d''applications modernes","évolutivité et sécurité","moteur de requête serveurless","ingestion de flux en temps réel"],"de":["Objektspeicher in der Cloud","Cloudflare R2","Entwicklung moderner Anwendungen","Skalierbarkeit und Sicherheit","serverloser Abfragemotor","Echtzeit-Stream-Ingesta"],"pt":["Cloudflare R2","armazenamento de objetos","R2 SQL","Pipelines","desenvolvimento de software","tutoriais de Cloudflare","recursos de Cloudflare"],"ru":["Cloudflare R2","объектное хранилище","R2 SQL","Pipelines","разработка программного обеспечения","уроки Cloudflare","функции Cloudflare"],"ar":["Cloudflare R2","تخزين كائنات","R2 SQL","Pipelines","تنمية البرمجيات","دروس Cloudflare","ميزات Cloudflare"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cloudflare-r2","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Cloudflare R2 Object Storage\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0, aws4fetch@1.0.20\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **September 2025**: R2 SQL open beta (serverless query engine for Apache Iceberg), Pipelines GA (real-time stream ingestion), Remote bindings GA (local dev connects to deployed R2)\n- **May 2025**: Dashboard redesign (deepli","body":"# Cloudflare R2 Object Storage\n\n**Status**: Production Ready ✅\n**Last Updated**: 2026-01-20\n**Dependencies**: cloudflare-worker-base (for Worker setup)\n**Latest Versions**: wrangler@4.59.2, @cloudflare/workers-types@4.20260109.0, aws4fetch@1.0.20\n\n**Recent Updates (2025)**:\n- **September 2025**: R2 SQL open beta (serverless query engine for Apache Iceberg), Pipelines GA (real-time stream ingestion), Remote bindings GA (local dev connects to deployed R2)\n- **May 2025**: Dashboard redesign (deeplink support, bucket settings centralization), Super Slurper 5x faster (rebuilt with Workers/Queues/Durable Objects)\n- **April 2025**: R2 Data Catalog open beta (managed Apache Iceberg catalog), Event Notifications open beta (5,000 msg/s per Queue)\n- **2025**: Bucket limits increased (1 million max), CRC-64/NVME checksums, Server-side encryption with customer keys, Infrequent Access storage class (beta), Oceania region, S3 API enhancements (sha256/sha1 checksums, ListParts, conditional CopyObject)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (5 Minutes)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create bucket\nnpx wrangler r2 bucket create my-bucket\n\n# 2. Add binding to wrangler.jsonc\n# {\n#   \"r2_buckets\": [{\n#     \"binding\": \"MY_BUCKET\",\n#     \"bucket_name\": \"my-bucket\",\n#     \"preview_bucket_name\": \"my-bucket-preview\"  // Optional: separate dev/prod\n#   }]\n# }\n\n# 3. Upload/download from Worker\ntype Bindings = { MY_BUCKET: R2Bucket };\n\n// Upload\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''file.txt'', data, {\n  httpMetadata: { contentType: ''text/plain'' }\n});\n\n// Download\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''file.txt'');\nif (!object) return c.json({ error: ''Not found'' }, 404);\n\nreturn new Response(object.body, {\n  headers: {\n    ''Content-Type'': object.httpMetadata?.contentType || ''application/octet-stream'',\n    ''ETag'': object.httpEtag,\n  },\n});\n\n# 4. Deploy\nnpx wrangler deploy\n```\n\n---\n\n## R2 Workers API\n\n### Core Methods\n\n```typescript\n// put() - Upload objects\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''file.txt'', data, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''text/plain'',\n    cacheControl: ''public, max-age=3600'',\n  },\n  customMetadata: { userId: ''123'' },\n  md5: await crypto.subtle.digest(''MD5'', data),  // Checksum verification\n});\n\n// Conditional upload (prevent overwrites)\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.put(''file.txt'', data, {\n  onlyIf: { uploadedBefore: new Date(''2020-01-01'') }\n});\nif (!object) return c.json({ error: ''File already exists'' }, 409);\n\n// get() - Download objects\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''file.txt'');\nif (!object) return c.json({ error: ''Not found'' }, 404);\n\nconst text = await object.text();           // As string\nconst json = await object.json();           // As JSON\nconst buffer = await object.arrayBuffer();  // As ArrayBuffer\n\n// Range requests (partial downloads)\nconst partial = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''video.mp4'', {\n  range: { offset: 0, length: 1024 * 1024 }  // First 1MB\n});\n\n// head() - Get metadata only (no body download)\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.head(''file.txt'');\nconsole.log(object.size, object.etag, object.customMetadata);\n\n// delete() - Delete objects\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.delete(''file.txt'');  // Single delete (idempotent)\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.delete([''file1.txt'', ''file2.txt'']);  // Bulk delete (max 1000)\n\n// list() - List objects\nconst listed = await env.MY_BUCKET.list({\n  prefix: ''images/'',  // Filter by prefix\n  limit: 100,\n  cursor: cursor,     // Pagination\n  delimiter: ''/'',     // Folder-like listing\n  include: [''httpMetadata'', ''customMetadata''],  // IMPORTANT: Opt-in for metadata\n});\n\nfor (const object of listed.objects) {\n  console.log(`${object.key}: ${object.size} bytes`);\n  console.log(object.httpMetadata?.contentType);  // Now populated with include parameter\n  console.log(object.customMetadata);             // Now populated with include parameter\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Multipart Uploads\n\nFor files >100MB or resumable uploads. Use when: large files, browser uploads, parallelization needed.\n\n```typescript\n// 1. Create multipart upload\nconst multipart = await env.MY_BUCKET.createMultipartUpload(''large-file.zip'', {\n  httpMetadata: { contentType: ''application/zip'' }\n});\n\n// 2. Upload parts (5MB-100MB each, max 10,000 parts)\nconst multipart = env.MY_BUCKET.resumeMultipartUpload(key, uploadId);\nconst part1 = await multipart.uploadPart(1, chunk1);\nconst part2 = await multipart.uploadPart(2, chunk2);\n\n// 3. Complete upload\nconst object = await multipart.complete([\n  { partNumber: 1, etag: part1.etag },\n  { partNumber: 2, etag: part2.etag },\n]);\n\n// 4. Abort if needed\nawait multipart.abort();\n```\n\n**Limits**: Parts 5MB-100MB, max 10,000 parts per upload. Don''t use for files <5MB (overhead).\n\n---\n\n## Presigned URLs\n\nAllow clients to upload/download directly to/from R2 (bypasses Worker). Use aws4fetch library.\n\n```typescript\nimport { AwsClient } from ''aws4fetch'';\n\nconst r2Client = new AwsClient({\n  accessKeyId: env.R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID,\n  secretAccessKey: env.R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,\n});\n\nconst url = new URL(\n  `https://${bucketName}.${accountId}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/${filename}`\n);\nurl.searchParams.set(''X-Amz-Expires'', ''3600'');  // 1 hour expiry\n\nconst signed = await r2Client.sign(\n  new Request(url, { method: ''PUT'' }),  // or ''GET'' for downloads\n  { aws: { signQuery: true } }\n);\n\n// Client uploads directly to R2\nawait fetch(signed.url, { method: ''PUT'', body: file });\n```\n\n**CRITICAL Security:**\n- ❌ **NEVER** expose R2 access keys in client-side code\n- ✅ **ALWAYS** generate presigned URLs server-side\n- ✅ **ALWAYS** set expiry times (1-24 hours typical)\n- ✅ **ALWAYS** add authentication before generating URLs\n- ✅ **CONSIDER** scoping to user folders: `users/${userId}/${filename}`\n\n### Presigned URL Domain Requirements\n\n**CRITICAL**: Presigned URLs **ONLY work with the S3 API domain**, not custom domains.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG - Presigned URLs don''t work with custom domains\nconst url = new URL(`https://cdn.example.com/${filename}`);\nconst signed = await r2Client.sign(\n  new Request(url, { method: ''PUT'' }),\n  { aws: { signQuery: true } }\n);\n// This URL will fail - presigning requires S3 domain\n\n// ✅ CORRECT - Use R2 storage domain for presigned URLs\nconst url = new URL(\n  `https://${accountId}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/${filename}`\n);\nconst signed = await r2Client.sign(\n  new Request(url, { method: ''PUT'' }),\n  { aws: { signQuery: true } }\n);\n\n// Pattern: Upload via presigned S3 URL, serve via custom domain\nasync function generateUploadUrl(filename: string) {\n  const uploadUrl = new URL(\n    `https://${accountId}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/${filename}`\n  );\n  const signed = await r2Client.sign(\n    new Request(uploadUrl, { method: ''PUT'' }),\n    { aws: { signQuery: true } }\n  );\n\n  return {\n    uploadUrl: signed.url,  // For client upload (S3 domain)\n    publicUrl: `https://cdn.example.com/${filename}`  // For serving (custom domain)\n  };\n}\n```\n\n**Source**: [Community Knowledge](https://ruanmartinelli.com/blog/cloudflare-r2-pre-signed-urls/)\n\n### API Token Requirements for Wrangler\n\n⚠️ **Wrangler CLI requires \"Admin Read & Write\" permissions**, not \"Object Read & Write\".\n\nWhen creating API tokens for wrangler operations:\n- ✅ **Use**: R2 → Admin Read & Write\n- ❌ **Don''t use**: R2 → Object Read & Write (causes 403 Forbidden errors)\n\n**Why**: \"Object Read & Write\" is for S3 API direct access only. Wrangler needs admin-level permissions for bucket operations.\n\n```bash\n# With wrong permissions:\nexport CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=\"token_with_object_readwrite\"\nwrangler r2 object put my-bucket/file.txt --file=./file.txt --remote\n# ✘ [ERROR] Failed to fetch - 403: Forbidden\n\n# With correct permissions (Admin Read & Write):\nwrangler r2 object put my-bucket/file.txt --file=./file.txt --remote\n# ✔ Success\n```\n\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #9235](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/9235)\n\n---\n\n## CORS Configuration\n\nConfigure CORS in bucket settings (Dashboard → R2 → Bucket → Settings → CORS Policy) before browser access.\n\n### Dashboard Format vs CLI Format\n\n⚠️ **The wrangler CLI and Dashboard UI use DIFFERENT CORS formats**. This commonly causes confusion.\n\n**Dashboard Format** (works in UI only):\n```json\n[{\n  \"AllowedOrigins\": [\"https://example.com\"],\n  \"AllowedMethods\": [\"GET\", \"PUT\"],\n  \"AllowedHeaders\": [\"*\"],\n  \"ExposeHeaders\": [\"ETag\"],\n  \"MaxAgeSeconds\": 3600\n}]\n```\n\n**CLI Format** (required for `wrangler r2 bucket cors`):\n```json\n{\n  \"rules\": [{\n    \"allowed\": {\n      \"origins\": [\"https://www.example.com\"],\n      \"methods\": [\"GET\", \"PUT\"],\n      \"headers\": [\"Content-Type\", \"Authorization\"]\n    },\n    \"exposeHeaders\": [\"ETag\", \"Content-Length\"],\n    \"maxAgeSeconds\": 8640\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n```bash\n# Using CLI format\nwrangler r2 bucket cors set my-bucket --file cors-config.json\n\n# Error if using Dashboard format:\n# \"The CORS configuration file must contain a ''rules'' array\"\n```\n\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #10076](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10076)\n\n### Custom Domain CORS\n\nWhen using custom domains with R2, CORS is handled in **two layers**:\n\n1. **R2 Bucket CORS**: Applies to all access methods (presigned URLs, direct S3 access)\n2. **Transform Rules CORS**: Additional CORS headers via Cloudflare Cache settings on custom domain\n\n```typescript\n// Bucket CORS (set via dashboard or wrangler)\n{\n  \"rules\": [{\n    \"allowed\": {\n      \"origins\": [\"https://app.example.com\"],\n      \"methods\": [\"GET\", \"PUT\"],\n      \"headers\": [\"Content-Type\"]\n    },\n    \"maxAgeSeconds\": 3600\n  }]\n}\n\n// Additional CORS via Transform Rules (Dashboard → Rules → Transform Rules)\n// Modify Response Header: Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://app.example.com\n\n// Order of CORS evaluation:\n// 1. R2 bucket CORS (if presigned URL or direct R2 access)\n// 2. Transform Rules CORS (if via custom domain)\n```\n\n**Source**: [Community Knowledge](https://mikeesto.medium.com/pre-signed-urls-cors-on-cloudflare-r2-c90d43370dc4)\n\n**For presigned URLs**: CORS handled by R2 directly (configure on bucket, not Worker).\n\n---\n\n## HTTP Metadata & Custom Metadata\n\n```typescript\n// HTTP metadata (standard headers)\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''file.pdf'', data, {\n  httpMetadata: {\n    contentType: ''application/pdf'',\n    cacheControl: ''public, max-age=31536000, immutable'',\n    contentDisposition: ''attachment; filename=\"report.pdf\"'',\n    contentEncoding: ''gzip'',\n  },\n  customMetadata: {\n    userId: ''12345'',\n    version: ''1.0'',\n  }  // Max 2KB total, keys/values must be strings\n});\n\n// Read metadata\nconst object = await env.MY_BUCKET.head(''file.pdf'');\nconsole.log(object.httpMetadata, object.customMetadata);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Common R2 Errors\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  await env.MY_BUCKET.put(key, data);\n} catch (error: any) {\n  const message = error.message;\n\n  if (message.includes(''R2_ERROR'')) {\n    // Generic R2 error\n  } else if (message.includes(''exceeded'')) {\n    // Quota exceeded\n  } else if (message.includes(''precondition'')) {\n    // Conditional operation failed\n  } else if (message.includes(''multipart'')) {\n    // Multipart upload error\n  }\n\n  console.error(''R2 Error:'', message);\n  return c.json({ error: ''Storage operation failed'' }, 500);\n}\n```\n\n### Retry Logic\n\nR2 experienced two major outages in Q1 2025 (February 6: 59 minutes, March 21: 1h 7min) due to operational issues. Implement robust retry logic with exponential backoff for platform errors.\n\n```typescript\nasync function r2WithRetry<T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  maxRetries = 5\n): Promise<T> {\n  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < maxRetries; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      return await operation();\n    } catch (error: any) {\n      const message = error.message;\n\n      // Retry on transient errors and platform issues\n      const is5xxError =\n        message.includes(''500'') ||\n        message.includes(''502'') ||\n        message.includes(''503'') ||\n        message.includes(''504'');\n\n      const isRetryable =\n        is5xxError ||\n        message.includes(''network'') ||\n        message.includes(''timeout'') ||\n        message.includes(''temporarily unavailable'');\n\n      if (!isRetryable || attempt === maxRetries - 1) {\n        throw error;\n      }\n\n      // Exponential backoff (longer for platform errors)\n      // 5xx errors: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s (up to 31s total)\n      // Other errors: 1s, 2s, 4s, 5s, 5s (up to 17s total)\n      const delay = is5xxError\n        ? Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, attempt), 16000)\n        : Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, attempt), 5000);\n\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));\n    }\n  }\n\n  throw new Error(''Max retries exceeded'');\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst object = await r2WithRetry(() =>\n  env.MY_BUCKET.get(''important-file.txt'')\n);\n```\n\n**Platform Reliability**: While R2 is generally reliable, the 2025 Q1 outages demonstrate the importance of retry logic for production applications. All 5xx errors should be retried with exponential backoff.\n\n**Sources**:\n- [February 6 Incident](https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-incident-on-february-6-2025/)\n- [March 21 Incident](https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-incident-march-21-2025/)\n\n---\n\n## Performance Optimization\n\n```typescript\n// Batch delete (up to 1000 keys)\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.delete([''file1.txt'', ''file2.txt'', ''file3.txt'']);\n\n// Range requests for large files\nconst partial = await env.MY_BUCKET.get(''video.mp4'', {\n  range: { offset: 0, length: 10 * 1024 * 1024 }  // First 10MB\n});\n\n// Cache headers for immutable assets\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''static/app.abc123.js'', jsData, {\n  httpMetadata: { cacheControl: ''public, max-age=31536000, immutable'' }\n});\n\n// Checksums for data integrity\nconst md5Hash = await crypto.subtle.digest(''MD5'', fileData);\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(''important.dat'', fileData, { md5: md5Hash });\n```\n\n### Concurrent Write Rate Limits\n\n⚠️ **High-frequency concurrent writes to the same object key will trigger HTTP 429 rate limiting**.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD: Multiple Workers writing to same key rapidly\nasync function logToSharedFile(env: Env, logEntry: string) {\n  const existing = await env.LOGS.get(''global-log.txt'');\n  const content = (await existing?.text()) || '''';\n  await env.LOGS.put(''global-log.txt'', content + logEntry);\n  // High write frequency to same key = 429 errors\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Shard by timestamp or ID (distribute writes)\nasync function logWithSharding(env: Env, logEntry: string) {\n  const timestamp = Date.now();\n  const shard = Math.floor(timestamp / 60000); // 1-minute shards\n\n  await env.LOGS.put(`logs/${shard}.txt`, logEntry, {\n    customMetadata: { timestamp: timestamp.toString() }\n  });\n  // Different keys = no rate limiting\n}\n\n// ✅ ALTERNATIVE: Use Durable Objects for append operations\n// Durable Objects can handle high-frequency updates to same state\n\n// ✅ ALTERNATIVE: Use Queues + batch processing\n// Buffer writes and batch them with unique keys\n```\n\n**Source**: [R2 Limits Documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/platform/limits/)\n\n### R2.dev Domain Rate Limiting\n\n🚨 **CRITICAL**: The `{bucket}.{account}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com` (r2.dev) domain is **NOT for production use**.\n\n**r2.dev limitations:**\n- ❌ Variable rate limiting (starts at ~hundreds of requests/second)\n- ❌ Bandwidth throttling\n- ❌ No SLA or performance guarantees\n- ❌ You''ll receive 429 Too Many Requests under load\n\n**For production: ALWAYS use custom domains**\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ NOT for production - r2.dev endpoint\nconst publicUrl = `https://${bucketName}.${accountId}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/${key}`;\n// This will be rate limited in production\n\n// ✅ Production: Custom domain\nconst productionUrl = `https://cdn.example.com/${key}`;\n\n// Setup custom domain:\n// 1. Dashboard → R2 → Bucket → Settings → Custom Domains\n// 2. Add your domain (e.g., cdn.example.com)\n// 3. Benefits:\n//    - No rate limiting beyond account limits\n//    - Cloudflare Cache support\n//    - Custom cache rules via Workers\n//    - Full CDN features\n```\n\n**r2.dev is ONLY for testing/development. Custom domains are required for production.**\n\n**Source**: [R2 Limits Documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/platform/limits/)\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n**Always Do:**\n- Set `contentType` for all uploads\n- Use batch delete for multiple objects (up to 1000)\n- Set cache headers for static assets\n- Use presigned URLs for large client uploads (S3 domain only)\n- Use multipart for files >100MB\n- Set CORS before browser uploads (use CLI format for wrangler)\n- Set expiry times on presigned URLs (1-24 hours)\n- Use `head()` when you only need metadata\n- Use conditional operations to prevent overwrites\n- Use custom domains for production (never r2.dev)\n- Shard writes across keys to avoid rate limits\n- Use `include` parameter with `list()` to get metadata\n- Implement retry logic with exponential backoff for 5xx errors\n\n**Never Do:**\n- Never expose R2 access keys in client-side code\n- Never skip `contentType` (files download as binary)\n- Never delete in loops (use batch delete)\n- Never skip CORS for browser uploads\n- Never use multipart for small files (<5MB)\n- Never delete >1000 keys in single call\n- Never skip presigned URL expiry (security risk)\n- Never use r2.dev domain for production (rate limited)\n- Never use presigned URLs with custom domains (use S3 domain)\n- Never write to same key at high frequency (causes 429)\n- Never use \"Object Read & Write\" tokens for wrangler (use \"Admin Read & Write\")\n\n### Multi-Tenant Architecture\n\nWith the bucket limit increased to **1 million buckets per account**, per-tenant buckets are now viable for large-scale applications.\n\n```typescript\n// Option 1: Per-tenant buckets (now scalable to 1M tenants)\nconst bucketName = `tenant-${tenantId}`;\nconst bucket = env[bucketName]; // Dynamic binding\n\n// Option 2: Key prefixing (still preferred for most use cases)\nawait env.MY_BUCKET.put(`tenants/${tenantId}/file.txt`, data);\n\n// Choose based on:\n// - Per-tenant buckets: Strong isolation, separate billing/quotas\n// - Key prefixing: Simpler, fewer resources, easier to manage\n```\n\n**Source**: [R2 Limits Documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/platform/limits/)\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues Prevented\n\nThis skill prevents **13** documented issues:\n\n| Issue # | Issue | Error | Prevention |\n|---------|-------|-------|------------|\n| **#1** | **CORS errors in browser** | Browser can''t upload/download | Configure CORS in bucket settings, use correct CLI format |\n| **#2** | **Files download as binary** | Missing content-type | Always set `httpMetadata.contentType` on upload |\n| **#3** | **Presigned URL expiry** | URLs never expire | Always set `X-Amz-Expires` (1-24 hours) |\n| **#4** | **Multipart upload limits** | Parts exceed limits | Keep parts 5MB-100MB, max 10,000 parts |\n| **#5** | **Bulk delete limits** | >1000 keys fails | Chunk deletes into batches of 1000 |\n| **#6** | **Custom metadata overflow** | Exceeds 2KB limit | Keep custom metadata under 2KB |\n| **#7** | **list() metadata missing** | `httpMetadata` undefined | Use `include: [''httpMetadata'', ''customMetadata'']` parameter ([Issue #10870](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10870)) |\n| **#8** | **CORS format confusion** | \"Must contain ''rules'' array\" | Use CLI format with `rules` wrapper for wrangler ([Issue #10076](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10076)) |\n| **#9** | **API token 403 errors** | \"Failed to fetch - 403\" | Use \"Admin Read & Write\" not \"Object Read & Write\" for wrangler ([Issue #9235](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/9235)) |\n| **#10** | **r2.dev rate limiting** | HTTP 429 in production | Use custom domains, never r2.dev for production ([R2 Limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/platform/limits/)) |\n| **#11** | **Concurrent write 429s** | Same key written frequently | Shard writes across different keys ([R2 Limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/platform/limits/)) |\n| **#12** | **Presigned URL domain error** | Presigned URLs fail | Use S3 domain only, not custom domains ([Community](https://ruanmartinelli.com/blog/cloudflare-r2-pre-signed-urls/)) |\n| **#13** | **Platform outages** | 5xx errors during outages | Implement retry logic with exponential backoff ([Feb 6](https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-incident-on-february-6-2025/), [Mar 21](https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-incident-march-21-2025/)) |\n\n---\n\n## Development Best Practices\n\n### Local R2 Storage Cleanup\n\n⚠️ **Local R2 DELETE operations don''t cleanup blob files**. When using `wrangler dev`, deleted objects remain in `.wrangler/state/v3/r2/{bucket-name}/blobs/`, causing local storage to grow indefinitely.\n\n```bash\n# Symptom: .wrangler/state grows large during development\ndu -sh .wrangler/state/v3/r2/\n\n# Fix: Manually cleanup local R2 storage\nrm -rf .wrangler/state/v3/r2/\n\n# Alternative: Use remote R2 for development\nwrangler dev --remote\n```\n\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #10795](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/10795)\n\n### Remote R2 Access Issues\n\n⚠️ **Local dev with `--remote` can have unreliable `.get()` operations**. Some users report `get()` returning undefined despite `put()` working correctly.\n\n```bash\n# If experiencing issues with remote R2 in local dev:\n\n# Option 1: Use local buckets instead (recommended)\nwrangler dev  # No --remote flag\n\n# Option 2: Deploy to preview environment for testing\nwrangler deploy --env preview\n\n# Option 3: Add retry logic if must use --remote\nasync function safeGet(bucket: R2Bucket, key: string) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    const obj = await bucket.get(key);\n    if (obj && obj.body) return obj;\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000));\n  }\n  throw new Error(''Failed to get object after retries'');\n}\n```\n\n**Source**: [GitHub Issue #8868](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/8868) (Community-sourced)\n\n---\n\n## Wrangler Commands Reference\n\n```bash\n# Bucket management\nwrangler r2 bucket create <BUCKET_NAME>\nwrangler r2 bucket list\nwrangler r2 bucket delete <BUCKET_NAME>\n\n# Object management\nwrangler r2 object put <BUCKET_NAME>/<KEY> --file=<FILE_PATH>\nwrangler r2 object get <BUCKET_NAME>/<KEY> --file=<OUTPUT_PATH>\nwrangler r2 object delete <BUCKET_NAME>/<KEY>\n\n# List objects\nwrangler r2 object list <BUCKET_NAME>\nwrangler r2 object list <BUCKET_NAME> --prefix=\"folder/\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Official Documentation\n\n- **R2 Overview**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/\n- **Get Started**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/get-started/\n- **Workers API**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/workers/workers-api-reference/\n- **Multipart Upload**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/workers/workers-multipart-usage/\n- **Presigned URLs**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/s3/presigned-urls/\n- **CORS Configuration**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/buckets/cors/\n- **Public Buckets**: https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/buckets/public-buckets/\n\n---\n\n**Ready to store with R2!** 🚀\n\n**Last verified**: 2026-01-20 | **Skill version**: 2.0.0 | **Changes**: Added 7 new known issues from community research (list() metadata, CORS format confusion, API token permissions, r2.dev rate limiting, concurrent write limits, presigned URL domain requirements, platform outage retry patterns). Enhanced retry logic for 5xx errors, added development best practices section, documented bucket limit increase to 1M.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:18:24.169Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud-Native Agents needing scalable object storage and serverless query capabilities with Cloudflare R2","zh":"非常适合需要可扩展对象存储和 Cloudflare R2 服务器端查询能力的云原生代理","ja":"Cloudflare R2 を使用したスケーラブルなオブジェクトストレージとサーバーレス クエリ機能が必要なクラウドネイティブ エージェントに最適","ko":"클라우드플레어 R2를 사용한 확장 가능한 객체 저장소 및 서버리스 쿼리 기능이 필요한 클라우드 네이티브 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes Cloud-Native que necesitan almacenamiento de objetos escalable y capacidades de consulta sin servidor con Cloudflare R2","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Cloud-Native nécessitant un stockage d''objets évolutif et des capacités de requête sans serveur avec Cloudflare R2","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Native-Agents, die skaliertes Objekt-Speicher und serverlose Abfragefunktionen mit Cloudflare R2 benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Nativos em Nuvem que necessitam de armazenamento de objetos escalável e capacidades de consulta sem servidor com Cloudflare R2","ru":"Идеально подходит для облачных агентов, которым необходим масштабируемое хранилище объектов и возможности серверных запросов с Cloudflare R2","ar":"مثالي untuk وكلاء السحабية الذين يحتاجون إلى تخزين كائنات قابل للتحجيم وقدرات استعلام بدون خادم مع Cloudflare R2"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Cloudflare Worker setup with cloudflare-worker-base, utilizing wrangler and @cloudflare/workers-types for seamless integration with R2 Object Storage, and tapping into R2 SQL for serverless query engine capabilities with Apache Iceberg","zh":"赋予代理使用 cloudflare-worker-base 设置 Cloudflare Worker，利用 wrangler 和 @cloudflare/workers-types 实现与 R2 对象存储的无缝集成，并通过 Apache Iceberg 使用 R2 SQL 的服务器端查询引擎功能","ja":"cloudflare-worker-base を使用した Cloudflare Worker の設定を可能にし、wrangler および @cloudflare/workers-types を使用して R2 オブジェクトストレージとのシームレスな統合を実現し、Apache Iceberg を使用した R2 SQL のサーバーレス クエリ エンジンの機能を利用できる","ko":"클라우드플레어 워커 설정을 위한 cloudflare-worker-base를 사용하여 에이전트를 활성화하고, wrangler 및 @cloudflare/workers-types를 사용하여 R2 객체 저장소와의無縫한 통합을 구현하고, 아파치 아이스버그를 사용하여 R2 SQL의 서버리스 쿼리 엔진 기능을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar la configuración de Cloudflare Worker con cloudflare-worker-base, utilizando wrangler y @cloudflare/workers-types para una integración sin problemas con R2 Object Storage, y aprovechando R2 SQL para capacidades de motor de consulta sin servidor con Apache Iceberg","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter la configuration de Cloudflare Worker avec cloudflare-worker-base, en utilisant wrangler et @cloudflare/workers-types pour une intégration transparente avec R2 Object Storage, et en exploitant R2 SQL pour des capacités de moteur de requête sans serveur avec Apache Iceberg","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, die Cloudflare-Worker-Konfiguration mit cloudflare-worker-base zu nutzen, indem sie wrangler und @cloudflare/workers-types verwenden, um eine nahtlose Integration mit R2-Objektspeicher zu ermöglichen und R2 SQL für serverlose Abfrage-Engine-Funktionen mit Apache Iceberg zu nutzen","pt":"Permite que os agentes aproveitem a configuração do Cloudflare Worker com cloudflare-worker-base, utilizando wrangler e @cloudflare/workers-types para integração transparente com o Armazenamento de Objetos R2 e aproveitando o R2 SQL para capacidades de motor de consulta sem servidor com Apache Iceberg","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать настройку Cloudflare Worker с cloudflare-worker-base, используя wrangler и @cloudflare/workers-types для бесшовной интеграции с хранилищем объектов R2 и использования R2 SQL для возможностей серверного запроса с Apache Iceberg","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الاستفادة من إعداد Cloudflare Worker مع cloudflare-worker-base ، باستخدام wrangler و @cloudflare/workers-types للاندماج السلس مع تخزين الكائنات R2 وتapping إلى R2 SQL لسمات محرك الاستعلام الخالي من الخادم مع Apache Iceberg"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating data ingestion with Pipelines for real-time stream processing","Generating insights with R2 SQL for data analysis","Debugging remote bindings for local development connectivity to deployed R2 instances"],"zh":["使用管道自动执行数据摄取以进行实时流处理","使用 R2 SQL 生成分析数据的见解","调试远程绑定以实现本地开发连接到已部署的 R2 实例"],"ja":["パイプラインを使用してリアルタイム ストリーム処理のためのデータの取り込みを自動化する","R2 SQL を使用してデータ分析のための洞察を生成する","リモート バインドをデバッグして、ローカル開発をデプロイされた R2 インスタンスに接続する"],"ko":["파이프라인을 사용하여 실시간 스트림 처리를 위한 데이터 수집 자동화","R2 SQL을 사용하여 데이터 분석을 위한 인사이트 생성","원격 바인딩 디버깅을 통해 로컬 개발을 배포된 R2 인스턴스에 연결"],"es":["Automatizar la ingesta de datos con Pipelines para el procesamiento de flujos de datos en tiempo real","Generar información con R2 SQL para el análisis de datos","Depurar enlaces remotos para la conectividad de desarrollo local a instancias de R2 implementadas"],"fr":["Automatiser l''ingestion de données avec Pipelines pour le traitement de flux de données en temps réel","Générer des informations avec R2 SQL pour l''analyse de données","Déboguer les liaisons à distance pour la connectivité de développement local aux instances de R2 déployées"],"de":["Automatisieren der Datenübernahme mit Pipelines für die Echtzeit-Stream-Verarbeitung","Erzeugen von Erkenntnissen mit R2 SQL für die Datenanalyse","Fehlerbehebung von Remote-Bindings für die lokale Entwicklungskonnektivität zu bereitgestellten R2-Instanzen"],"pt":["Automatizar a ingestão de dados com Pipelines para processamento de fluxo em tempo real","Gerar informações com R2 SQL para análise de dados","Depurar ligações remotas para conectividade de desenvolvimento local com instâncias R2 implantadas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать прием данных с помощью Pipelines для обработки потоков в реальном времени","Генерировать информацию с помощью R2 SQL для анализа данных","Отлаживать удаленные привязки для подключения локального развития к развернутым экземплярам R2"],"ar":["تأتمة استيعاب البيانات مع Pipelines لمعالجة التدفق في الوقت الفعلي","توليد معلومات مع R2 SQL لتحليل البيانات","تصحيح الأواصر البعيدة للتواصل التطويري المحلي مع مثيلات R2 المثبتة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires cloudflare-worker-base for Worker setup","Dependent on wrangler and @cloudflare/workers-types versions"],"zh":["需要 cloudflare-worker-base 来设置 Worker","依赖于 wrangler 和 @cloudflare/workers-types 的版本"],"ja":["Worker の設定には cloudflare-worker-base が必要","wrangler および @cloudflare/workers-types のバージョンに依存する"],"ko":["워커 설정을 위해 cloudflare-worker-base가 필요","wrangler 및 @cloudflare/workers-types 버전에 의존"],"es":["Requiere cloudflare-worker-base para la configuración de Worker","Depende de las versiones de wrangler y @cloudflare/workers-types"],"fr":["Nécessite cloudflare-worker-base pour la configuration de Worker","Dépend des versions de wrangler et @cloudflare/workers-types"],"de":["Benötigt cloudflare-worker-base für die Worker-Konfiguration","Hängt von den Versionen von wrangler und @cloudflare/workers-types ab"],"pt":["Exige cloudflare-worker-base para configuração do Worker","Dependente das versões do wrangler e @cloudflare/workers-types"],"ru":["Требует cloudflare-worker-base для настройки Worker","Зависит от версий wrangler и @cloudflare/workers-types"],"ar":["يتطلب cloudflare-worker-base لإعداد Worker","يعتمد على إصدارات wrangler و @cloudflare/workers-types"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/rag-implementation', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'rag-implementation', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z', '2026-02-18T14:18:43.302Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/rag-implementation","name":"rag-implementation","description":{"zh":"RAG 实现使开发者能够构建提供准确、有根据的响应的 LLM 应用，利用外部知识源","ja":"RAG 実装により、開発者は外部知識ソースを利用して正確で裏付けられた応答を提供する LLM アプリケーションを構築できます","ko":"RAG 구현을 통해 개발자는 외부 지식 소스를 사용하여 정확하고 근거 있는 응답을 제공하는 LLM 애플리케이션을 구축","es":"La implementación RAG permite a los desarrolladores crear aplicaciones LLM con respuestas precisas y basadas en conocimientos externos. Aprende a dominar esta técnica para mejorar tus aplicaciones","fr":"La mise en œuvre RAG permet aux développeurs de créer des applications LLM avec des réponses précises et basées sur des connaissances externes. Apprenez à maîtriser cette technique pour améliorer vos applications","de":"Die RAG-Implementierung ermöglicht es Entwicklern, LLM-Anwendungen mit genauen und auf externen Wissen basierenden Antworten zu erstellen. Lernen Sie, diese Technik zu meistern, um Ihre Anwendungen zu verbessern","pt":"Masterize a implementação RAG para criar aplicações LLM com respostas precisas e baseadas em conhecimento externo","ru":"Освойте реализацию RAG для создания приложений LLM с точными и основанными на внешних знаниях ответами","ar":"استخدم تنفيذ RAG لإنشاء تطبيقات LLM ذات استجابات دقيقة ومستندة إلى مصادر معرفة خارجية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"RAG 实现 - 精确响应和外部知识集成","ja":"RAG 実装 - 正確な応答と外部知識ソースの統合","ko":"RAG 구현 - 정확한 응답과 외부 지식 통합","es":"Implementación RAG para LLM","fr":"Mise en œuvre RAG pour les applications LLM","de":"RAG-Implementierung für LLM-Anwendungen","pt":"Implementação RAG para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Реализация RAG для разработчиков","ar":"تنفيذ RAG ل्मطورين","en":"rag-implementation"},"description":{"zh":"RAG 实现使开发者能够构建提供准确、有根据的响应的 LLM 应用，利用外部知识源","ja":"RAG 実装により、開発者は外部知識ソースを利用して正確で裏付けられた応答を提供する LLM アプリケーションを構築できます","ko":"RAG 구현을 통해 개발자는 외부 지식 소스를 사용하여 정확하고 근거 있는 응답을 제공하는 LLM 애플리케이션을 구축","es":"La implementación RAG permite a los desarrolladores crear aplicaciones LLM con respuestas precisas y basadas en conocimientos externos. Aprende a dominar est...","fr":"La mise en œuvre RAG permet aux développeurs de créer des applications LLM avec des réponses précises et basées sur des connaissances externes. Apprenez à ma...","de":"Die RAG-Implementierung ermöglicht es Entwicklern, LLM-Anwendungen mit genauen und auf externen Wissen basierenden Antworten zu erstellen. Lernen Sie, diese ...","pt":"Masterize a implementação RAG para criar aplicações LLM com respostas precisas e baseadas em conhecimento externo","ru":"Освойте реализацию RAG для создания приложений LLM с точными и основанными на внешних знаниях ответами","ar":"استخدم تنفيذ RAG لإنشاء تطبيقات LLM ذات استجابات دقيقة ومستندة إلى مصادر معرفة خارجية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["构建 Q&A 系统","创建聊天机器人","实现语义搜索","减少幻觉","启用 LLM 访问域特定知识"],"ja":["Q&A システムの構築","チャットボットの作成","セマンティック検索の実装","幻覚の減少","LLM によるドメイン固有の知識へのアクセス"],"ko":["Q&A 시스템 구축","채팅봇 생성","의미 검색 구현","환각 감소","LLM을 통한 도메인 특정 지식 액세스"],"es":["Respuestas precisas y basadas en conocimientos externos","Acceso a conocimientos específicos del dominio","Reducción de alucinaciones con respuestas basadas en hechos","Implementación de búsqueda semántica con consultas de lenguaje natural","Creación de asistentes de documentación","Desarrollo de sistemas de preguntas y respuestas sobre documentos propietarios"],"fr":["Réponses précises et basées sur des connaissances externes","Accès à des connaissances spécifiques au domaine","Réduction des hallucinations avec des réponses basées sur des faits","Mise en œuvre de la recherche sémantique avec des requêtes de langage naturel","Création d''assistants de documentation","Développement de systèmes de questions et réponses sur des documents propriétaires"],"de":["Genaue und auf externen Wissen basierende Antworten","Zugriff auf domänenspezifisches Wissen","Reduzierung von Halluzinationen mit faktengestützten Antworten","Implementierung von semantischer Suche mit natürlichen Sprachabfragen","Erstellung von Dokumentationsassistenten","Entwicklung von Frage- und Antwortsystemen über eigene Dokumente"],"pt":["Criação de sistemas de Q&A sobre documentos proprietários","Desenvolvimento de chatbots com informações atuais e factuais","Implementação de busca semântica com consultas de linguagem natural","Redução de alucinações com respostas baseadas em conhecimento","Habilitação de LLMs para acessar conhecimento específico de domínio","Criação de assistentes de documentação"],"ru":["Создание систем вопросов и ответов над собственными документами","Разработка чат-ботов с актуальной и фактической информацией","Реализация семантического поиска с естественно-языковыми запросами","Снижение галлюцинаций с ответами, основанными на знаниях","Включение LLM для доступа к знаниям конкретного домена","Создание помощников документации"],"ar":["إنشاء أنظمة أسئلة وأجوبة على وثائق مملوكة","تطوير محادثات مع معلومات حديثة وحقيقية","تنفيذ بحث دلالية بالاستفسارات اللغوية الطبيعية","تقليل الهلوسات بالاستجابات المعتمدة على المعرفة","تمكين LLMs من الوصول إلى معرفة محددة المجال","إنشاء مساعدين للتوثيق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["RAG","LLM","外部知识源","准确响应","自然语言处理","语义搜索"],"ja":["RAG","LLM","外部知識ソース","正確な応答","自然言語処理","セマンティック検索"],"ko":["RAG","LLM","외부 지식 소스","정확한 응답","자연어 처리","의미 검색"],"es":["RAG","LLM","generación de lenguaje","recuperación de información","respuestas precisas","conocimientos externos","desarrollo de aplicaciones","inteligencia artificial","procesamiento de lenguaje natural"],"fr":["RAG","LLM","génération de langage","récupération d''informations","réponses précises","connaissances externes","développement d''applications","intelligence artificielle","traitement du langage naturel"],"de":["RAG","LLM","Sprachgenerierung","Informationsabruf","genaue Antworten","externes Wissen","Anwendungsentwicklung","künstliche Intelligenz","natürliche Sprachverarbeitung"],"pt":["RAG","LLM","conhecimento externo","sistemas de Q&A","chatbots","busca semântica","respostas baseadas em conhecimento","desenvolvimento de aplicações","modelos de linguagem"],"ru":["RAG","LLM","внешнее знание","системы вопросов и ответов","чат-боты","семантический поиск","ответы, основанные на знаниях","разработка приложений","модели языка"],"ar":["RAG","LLM","معرفة خارجية","أنظمة أسئلة وأجوبة","محادثات","بحث دلالية","استجابات معتمدة على المعرفة","تطوير تطبيقات","نماذج اللغة"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.527Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rag-implementation","description":"Build Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems for LLM applications with vector databases and semantic search. Use when implementing knowledge-grounded AI, building document Q&A systems, or integrating LLMs with external knowledge bases.","bodyPreview":"# RAG Implementation\n\nMaster Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to build LLM applications that provide accurate, grounded responses using external knowledge sources.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building Q&A systems over proprietary documents\n- Creating chatbots with current, factual information\n- Implementing semantic search with natural language queries\n- Reducing hallucinations with grounded responses\n- Enabling LLMs to access domain-specific knowledge\n- Building documentation assistants\n-","body":"# RAG Implementation\n\nMaster Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to build LLM applications that provide accurate, grounded responses using external knowledge sources.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building Q&A systems over proprietary documents\n- Creating chatbots with current, factual information\n- Implementing semantic search with natural language queries\n- Reducing hallucinations with grounded responses\n- Enabling LLMs to access domain-specific knowledge\n- Building documentation assistants\n- Creating research tools with source citation\n\n## Core Components\n\n### 1. Vector Databases\n\n**Purpose**: Store and retrieve document embeddings efficiently\n\n**Options:**\n\n- **Pinecone**: Managed, scalable, serverless\n- **Weaviate**: Open-source, hybrid search, GraphQL\n- **Milvus**: High performance, on-premise\n- **Chroma**: Lightweight, easy to use, local development\n- **Qdrant**: Fast, filtered search, Rust-based\n- **pgvector**: PostgreSQL extension, SQL integration\n\n### 2. Embeddings\n\n**Purpose**: Convert text to numerical vectors for similarity search\n\n**Models (2026):**\n| Model | Dimensions | Best For |\n|-------|------------|----------|\n| **voyage-3-large** | 1024 | Claude apps (Anthropic recommended) |\n| **voyage-code-3** | 1024 | Code search |\n| **text-embedding-3-large** | 3072 | OpenAI apps, high accuracy |\n| **text-embedding-3-small** | 1536 | OpenAI apps, cost-effective |\n| **bge-large-en-v1.5** | 1024 | Open source, local deployment |\n| **multilingual-e5-large** | 1024 | Multi-language support |\n\n### 3. Retrieval Strategies\n\n**Approaches:**\n\n- **Dense Retrieval**: Semantic similarity via embeddings\n- **Sparse Retrieval**: Keyword matching (BM25, TF-IDF)\n- **Hybrid Search**: Combine dense + sparse with weighted fusion\n- **Multi-Query**: Generate multiple query variations\n- **HyDE**: Generate hypothetical documents for better retrieval\n\n### 4. Reranking\n\n**Purpose**: Improve retrieval quality by reordering results\n\n**Methods:**\n\n- **Cross-Encoders**: BERT-based reranking (ms-marco-MiniLM)\n- **Cohere Rerank**: API-based reranking\n- **Maximal Marginal Relevance (MMR)**: Diversity + relevance\n- **LLM-based**: Use LLM to score relevance\n\n## Quick Start with LangGraph\n\n```python\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph, START, END\nfrom langchain_anthropic import ChatAnthropic\nfrom langchain_voyageai import VoyageAIEmbeddings\nfrom langchain_pinecone import PineconeVectorStore\nfrom langchain_core.documents import Document\nfrom langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\nfrom langchain_text_splitters import RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter\nfrom typing import TypedDict, Annotated\n\nclass RAGState(TypedDict):\n    question: str\n    context: list[Document]\n    answer: str\n\n# Initialize components\nllm = ChatAnthropic(model=\"claude-sonnet-4-5\")\nembeddings = VoyageAIEmbeddings(model=\"voyage-3-large\")\nvectorstore = PineconeVectorStore(index_name=\"docs\", embedding=embeddings)\nretriever = vectorstore.as_retriever(search_kwargs={\"k\": 4})\n\n# RAG prompt\nrag_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\n    \"\"\"Answer based on the context below. If you cannot answer, say so.\n\n    Context:\n    {context}\n\n    Question: {question}\n\n    Answer:\"\"\"\n)\n\nasync def retrieve(state: RAGState) -> RAGState:\n    \"\"\"Retrieve relevant documents.\"\"\"\n    docs = await retriever.ainvoke(state[\"question\"])\n    return {\"context\": docs}\n\nasync def generate(state: RAGState) -> RAGState:\n    \"\"\"Generate answer from context.\"\"\"\n    context_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(doc.page_content for doc in state[\"context\"])\n    messages = rag_prompt.format_messages(\n        context=context_text,\n        question=state[\"question\"]\n    )\n    response = await llm.ainvoke(messages)\n    return {\"answer\": response.content}\n\n# Build RAG graph\nbuilder = StateGraph(RAGState)\nbuilder.add_node(\"retrieve\", retrieve)\nbuilder.add_node(\"generate\", generate)\nbuilder.add_edge(START, \"retrieve\")\nbuilder.add_edge(\"retrieve\", \"generate\")\nbuilder.add_edge(\"generate\", END)\n\nrag_chain = builder.compile()\n\n# Use\nresult = await rag_chain.ainvoke({\"question\": \"What are the main features?\"})\nprint(result[\"answer\"])\n```\n\n## Advanced RAG Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Hybrid Search with RRF\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_community.retrievers import BM25Retriever\nfrom langchain.retrievers import EnsembleRetriever\n\n# Sparse retriever (BM25 for keyword matching)\nbm25_retriever = BM25Retriever.from_documents(documents)\nbm25_retriever.k = 10\n\n# Dense retriever (embeddings for semantic search)\ndense_retriever = vectorstore.as_retriever(search_kwargs={\"k\": 10})\n\n# Combine with Reciprocal Rank Fusion weights\nensemble_retriever = EnsembleRetriever(\n    retrievers=[bm25_retriever, dense_retriever],\n    weights=[0.3, 0.7]  # 30% keyword, 70% semantic\n)\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Multi-Query Retrieval\n\n```python\nfrom langchain.retrievers.multi_query import MultiQueryRetriever\n\n# Generate multiple query perspectives for better recall\nmulti_query_retriever = MultiQueryRetriever.from_llm(\n    retriever=vectorstore.as_retriever(search_kwargs={\"k\": 5}),\n    llm=llm\n)\n\n# Single query → multiple variations → combined results\nresults = await multi_query_retriever.ainvoke(\"What is the main topic?\")\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Contextual Compression\n\n```python\nfrom langchain.retrievers import ContextualCompressionRetriever\nfrom langchain.retrievers.document_compressors import LLMChainExtractor\n\n# Compressor extracts only relevant portions\ncompressor = LLMChainExtractor.from_llm(llm)\n\ncompression_retriever = ContextualCompressionRetriever(\n    base_compressor=compressor,\n    base_retriever=vectorstore.as_retriever(search_kwargs={\"k\": 10})\n)\n\n# Returns only relevant parts of documents\ncompressed_docs = await compression_retriever.ainvoke(\"specific query\")\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Parent Document Retriever\n\n```python\nfrom langchain.retrievers import ParentDocumentRetriever\nfrom langchain.storage import InMemoryStore\nfrom langchain_text_splitters import RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter\n\n# Small chunks for precise retrieval, large chunks for context\nchild_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=400, chunk_overlap=50)\nparent_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=2000, chunk_overlap=200)\n\n# Store for parent documents\ndocstore = InMemoryStore()\n\nparent_retriever = ParentDocumentRetriever(\n    vectorstore=vectorstore,\n    docstore=docstore,\n    child_splitter=child_splitter,\n    parent_splitter=parent_splitter\n)\n\n# Add documents (splits children, stores parents)\nawait parent_retriever.aadd_documents(documents)\n\n# Retrieval returns parent documents with full context\nresults = await parent_retriever.ainvoke(\"query\")\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: HyDE (Hypothetical Document Embeddings)\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\n\nclass HyDEState(TypedDict):\n    question: str\n    hypothetical_doc: str\n    context: list[Document]\n    answer: str\n\nhyde_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\n    \"\"\"Write a detailed passage that would answer this question:\n\n    Question: {question}\n\n    Passage:\"\"\"\n)\n\nasync def generate_hypothetical(state: HyDEState) -> HyDEState:\n    \"\"\"Generate hypothetical document for better retrieval.\"\"\"\n    messages = hyde_prompt.format_messages(question=state[\"question\"])\n    response = await llm.ainvoke(messages)\n    return {\"hypothetical_doc\": response.content}\n\nasync def retrieve_with_hyde(state: HyDEState) -> HyDEState:\n    \"\"\"Retrieve using hypothetical document.\"\"\"\n    # Use hypothetical doc for retrieval instead of original query\n    docs = await retriever.ainvoke(state[\"hypothetical_doc\"])\n    return {\"context\": docs}\n\n# Build HyDE RAG graph\nbuilder = StateGraph(HyDEState)\nbuilder.add_node(\"hypothetical\", generate_hypothetical)\nbuilder.add_node(\"retrieve\", retrieve_with_hyde)\nbuilder.add_node(\"generate\", generate)\nbuilder.add_edge(START, \"hypothetical\")\nbuilder.add_edge(\"hypothetical\", \"retrieve\")\nbuilder.add_edge(\"retrieve\", \"generate\")\nbuilder.add_edge(\"generate\", END)\n\nhyde_rag = builder.compile()\n```\n\n## Document Chunking Strategies\n\n### Recursive Character Text Splitter\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_text_splitters import RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter\n\nsplitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(\n    chunk_size=1000,\n    chunk_overlap=200,\n    length_function=len,\n    separators=[\"\\n\\n\", \"\\n\", \". \", \" \", \"\"]  # Try in order\n)\n\nchunks = splitter.split_documents(documents)\n```\n\n### Token-Based Splitting\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_text_splitters import TokenTextSplitter\n\nsplitter = TokenTextSplitter(\n    chunk_size=512,\n    chunk_overlap=50,\n    encoding_name=\"cl100k_base\"  # OpenAI tiktoken encoding\n)\n```\n\n### Semantic Chunking\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_experimental.text_splitter import SemanticChunker\n\nsplitter = SemanticChunker(\n    embeddings=embeddings,\n    breakpoint_threshold_type=\"percentile\",\n    breakpoint_threshold_amount=95\n)\n```\n\n### Markdown Header Splitter\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_text_splitters import MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter\n\nheaders_to_split_on = [\n    (\"#\", \"Header 1\"),\n    (\"##\", \"Header 2\"),\n    (\"###\", \"Header 3\"),\n]\n\nsplitter = MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter(\n    headers_to_split_on=headers_to_split_on,\n    strip_headers=False\n)\n```\n\n## Vector Store Configurations\n\n### Pinecone (Serverless)\n\n```python\nfrom pinecone import Pinecone, ServerlessSpec\nfrom langchain_pinecone import PineconeVectorStore\n\n# Initialize Pinecone client\npc = Pinecone(api_key=os.environ[\"PINECONE_API_KEY\"])\n\n# Create index if needed\nif \"my-index\" not in pc.list_indexes().names():\n    pc.create_index(\n        name=\"my-index\",\n        dimension=1024,  # voyage-3-large dimensions\n        metric=\"cosine\",\n        spec=ServerlessSpec(cloud=\"aws\", region=\"us-east-1\")\n    )\n\n# Create vector store\nindex = pc.Index(\"my-index\")\nvectorstore = PineconeVectorStore(index=index, embedding=embeddings)\n```\n\n### Weaviate\n\n```python\nimport weaviate\nfrom langchain_weaviate import WeaviateVectorStore\n\nclient = weaviate.connect_to_local()  # or connect_to_weaviate_cloud()\n\nvectorstore = WeaviateVectorStore(\n    client=client,\n    index_name=\"Documents\",\n    text_key=\"content\",\n    embedding=embeddings\n)\n```\n\n### Chroma (Local Development)\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_chroma import Chroma\n\nvectorstore = Chroma(\n    collection_name=\"my_collection\",\n    embedding_function=embeddings,\n    persist_directory=\"./chroma_db\"\n)\n```\n\n### pgvector (PostgreSQL)\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_postgres.vectorstores import PGVector\n\nconnection_string = \"postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@localhost:5432/vectordb\"\n\nvectorstore = PGVector(\n    embeddings=embeddings,\n    collection_name=\"documents\",\n    connection=connection_string,\n)\n```\n\n## Retrieval Optimization\n\n### 1. Metadata Filtering\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_core.documents import Document\n\n# Add metadata during indexing\ndocs_with_metadata = []\nfor doc in documents:\n    doc.metadata.update({\n        \"source\": doc.metadata.get(\"source\", \"unknown\"),\n        \"category\": determine_category(doc.page_content),\n        \"date\": datetime.now().isoformat()\n    })\n    docs_with_metadata.append(doc)\n\n# Filter during retrieval\nresults = await vectorstore.asimilarity_search(\n    \"query\",\n    filter={\"category\": \"technical\"},\n    k=5\n)\n```\n\n### 2. Maximal Marginal Relevance (MMR)\n\n```python\n# Balance relevance with diversity\nresults = await vectorstore.amax_marginal_relevance_search(\n    \"query\",\n    k=5,\n    fetch_k=20,  # Fetch 20, return top 5 diverse\n    lambda_mult=0.5  # 0=max diversity, 1=max relevance\n)\n```\n\n### 3. Reranking with Cross-Encoder\n\n```python\nfrom sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\n\nreranker = CrossEncoder(''cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2'')\n\nasync def retrieve_and_rerank(query: str, k: int = 5) -> list[Document]:\n    # Get initial results\n    candidates = await vectorstore.asimilarity_search(query, k=20)\n\n    # Rerank\n    pairs = [[query, doc.page_content] for doc in candidates]\n    scores = reranker.predict(pairs)\n\n    # Sort by score and take top k\n    ranked = sorted(zip(candidates, scores), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n    return [doc for doc, score in ranked[:k]]\n```\n\n### 4. Cohere Rerank\n\n```python\nfrom langchain.retrievers import CohereRerank\nfrom langchain_cohere import CohereRerank\n\nreranker = CohereRerank(model=\"rerank-english-v3.0\", top_n=5)\n\n# Wrap retriever with reranking\nreranked_retriever = ContextualCompressionRetriever(\n    base_compressor=reranker,\n    base_retriever=vectorstore.as_retriever(search_kwargs={\"k\": 20})\n)\n```\n\n## Prompt Engineering for RAG\n\n### Contextual Prompt with Citations\n\n```python\nrag_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\n    \"\"\"Answer the question based on the context below. Include citations using [1], [2], etc.\n\n    If you cannot answer based on the context, say \"I don''t have enough information.\"\n\n    Context:\n    {context}\n\n    Question: {question}\n\n    Instructions:\n    1. Use only information from the context\n    2. Cite sources with [1], [2] format\n    3. If uncertain, express uncertainty\n\n    Answer (with citations):\"\"\"\n)\n```\n\n### Structured Output for RAG\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass RAGResponse(BaseModel):\n    answer: str = Field(description=\"The answer based on context\")\n    confidence: float = Field(description=\"Confidence score 0-1\")\n    sources: list[str] = Field(description=\"Source document IDs used\")\n    reasoning: str = Field(description=\"Brief reasoning for the answer\")\n\n# Use with structured output\nstructured_llm = llm.with_structured_output(RAGResponse)\n```\n\n## Evaluation Metrics\n\n```python\nfrom typing import TypedDict\n\nclass RAGEvalMetrics(TypedDict):\n    retrieval_precision: float  # Relevant docs / retrieved docs\n    retrieval_recall: float     # Retrieved relevant / total relevant\n    answer_relevance: float     # Answer addresses question\n    faithfulness: float         # Answer grounded in context\n    context_relevance: float    # Context relevant to question\n\nasync def evaluate_rag_system(\n    rag_chain,\n    test_cases: list[dict]\n) -> RAGEvalMetrics:\n    \"\"\"Evaluate RAG system on test cases.\"\"\"\n    metrics = {k: [] for k in RAGEvalMetrics.__annotations__}\n\n    for test in test_cases:\n        result = await rag_chain.ainvoke({\"question\": test[\"question\"]})\n\n        # Retrieval metrics\n        retrieved_ids = {doc.metadata[\"id\"] for doc in result[\"context\"]}\n        relevant_ids = set(test[\"relevant_doc_ids\"])\n\n        precision = len(retrieved_ids & relevant_ids) / len(retrieved_ids)\n        recall = len(retrieved_ids & relevant_ids) / len(relevant_ids)\n\n        metrics[\"retrieval_precision\"].append(precision)\n        metrics[\"retrieval_recall\"].append(recall)\n\n        # Use LLM-as-judge for quality metrics\n        quality = await evaluate_answer_quality(\n            question=test[\"question\"],\n            answer=result[\"answer\"],\n            context=result[\"context\"],\n            expected=test.get(\"expected_answer\")\n        )\n        metrics[\"answer_relevance\"].append(quality[\"relevance\"])\n        metrics[\"faithfulness\"].append(quality[\"faithfulness\"])\n        metrics[\"context_relevance\"].append(quality[\"context_relevance\"])\n\n    return {k: sum(v) / len(v) for k, v in metrics.items()}\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- [LangChain RAG Tutorial](https://python.langchain.com/docs/tutorials/rag/)\n- [LangGraph RAG Examples](https://langchain-ai.github.io/langgraph/tutorials/rag/)\n- [Pinecone Best Practices](https://docs.pinecone.io/guides/get-started/overview)\n- [Voyage AI Embeddings](https://docs.voyageai.com/)\n- [RAG Evaluation Guide](https://docs.ragas.io/)\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Chunk Size**: Balance between context (larger) and specificity (smaller) - typically 500-1000 tokens\n2. **Overlap**: Use 10-20% overlap to preserve context at boundaries\n3. **Metadata**: Include source, page, timestamp for filtering and debugging\n4. **Hybrid Search**: Combine semantic and keyword search for best recall\n5. **Reranking**: Use cross-encoder reranking for precision-critical applications\n6. **Citations**: Always return source documents for transparency\n7. **Evaluation**: Continuously test retrieval quality and answer accuracy\n8. **Monitoring**: Track retrieval metrics and latency in production\n\n## Common Issues\n\n- **Poor Retrieval**: Check embedding quality, chunk size, query formulation\n- **Irrelevant Results**: Add metadata filtering, use hybrid search, rerank\n- **Missing Information**: Ensure documents are properly indexed, check chunking\n- **Slow Queries**: Optimize vector store, use caching, reduce k\n- **Hallucinations**: Improve grounding prompt, add verification step\n- **Context Too Long**: Use compression or parent document retriever\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:18:43.302Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Language Agents seeking to integrate Retrieval-Augmented Generation for accurate and informed responses.","zh":"适合高级语言代理，旨在集成检索增强生成以实现准确和明智的响应。","ja":"高度な言語エージェントが、正確で情報に基づいた応答を生成するために、検索増強生成を統合するのに適しています。","ko":"정확하고 정보에 기반한 응답을 생성하기 위해 검색 증강 생성을 통합하려는 고급 언어 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Lenguaje Avanzados que buscan integrar Generación con Recuperación para respuestas precisas y informadas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de langage avancés souhaitant intégrer la génération avec récupération pour des réponses précises et éclairées.","de":"Ideal für fortgeschrittene Sprachagenten, die Retrieval-Augmented-Generation für genaue und informative Antworten integrieren möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem Avançados que buscam integrar Geração com Recuperação Aumentada para respostas precisas e informadas.","ru":"Идеально для передовых языковых агентов, стремящихся интегрировать генерацию с дополненной извлечением для точных и информированных ответов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين المتقدمين الذين يسعون إلى دمج الإنتاج مع الاسترجاع المعزز للحصول على استجابات دقيقة ومستنيرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to access domain-specific knowledge and reduce hallucinations by leveraging external knowledge sources through Retrieval-Augmented Generation, utilizing natural language queries and semantic search protocols.","zh":"赋予代理访问特定领域知识的能力，并通过检索增强生成利用外部知识源，减少幻觉，使用自然语言查询和语义搜索协议。","ja":"エージェントに、特定のドメインの知識にアクセスする能力を与え、自然言語クエリとセマンティック検索プロトコルを使用して、外部の知識源を活用することで、検索増強生成を実現し、幻覚を減らします。","ko":"에이전트가 특정 도메인의 지식에 접근할 수 있는 능력을 부여하고, 자연어 쿼리 및 의미 검색 프로토콜을 사용하여 외부 지식원을 활용하여 검색 증강 생성을 구현하고, 환상을 줄입니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes acceder a conocimientos específicos del dominio y reducir alucinaciones aprovechando fuentes de conocimiento externas a través de la Generación con Recuperación, utilizando consultas de lenguaje natural y protocolos de búsqueda semántica.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''accéder à des connaissances spécifiques au domaine et de réduire les hallucinations en exploitant des sources de connaissances externes via la génération avec récupération, en utilisant des requêtes de langage naturel et des protocoles de recherche sémantique.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, auf domänen-spezifisches Wissen zuzugreifen und Halluzinationen durch die Nutzung externer Wissensquellen über Retrieval-Augmented-Generation zu reduzieren, indem sie natürliche Sprachabfragen und semantische Suchprotokolle verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a acessar conhecimento específico de domínio e reduzir alucinações ao aproveitar fontes de conhecimento externas por meio da Geração com Recuperação Aumentada, utilizando consultas de linguagem natural e protocolos de pesquisa semântica.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью доступа к домен-специфичным знаниям и снижает риск галлюцинаций путем использования внешних источников знаний через генерацию с дополненной извлечением, используя запросы естественного языка и семантические протоколы поиска.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من الوصول إلى المعرفة المحددة للنطاق وتقليل الهلوسة من خلال الاستفادة من مصادر المعرفة الخارجية من خلال الإنتاج مع الاسترجاع المعزز، باستخدام استفسارات اللغة الطبيعية وبروتوكولات البحث الدلالي."},"useCases":{"en":["Building Q&A systems over proprietary documents","Creating chatbots with current factual information","Implementing semantic search with natural language queries"],"zh":["基于专有文档构建问答系统","创建具有当前事实信息的聊天机器人","使用自然语言查询实现语义搜索"],"ja":["独自のドキュメントを使用してQ&Aシステムを構築する","現在の事実情報を備えたチャットボットを作成する","自然言語クエリを使用してセマンティック検索を実装する"],"ko":["비공개 문서를 사용하여 Q&A 시스템을 구축하는 것","현재 사실 정보를 갖춘 챗봇을 생성하는 것","자연어 쿼리를 사용하여 의미 검색을 구현하는 것"],"es":["Construir sistemas de preguntas y respuestas sobre documentos propiedad","Crear chatbots con información factual actualizada","Implementar búsqueda semántica con consultas de lenguaje natural"],"fr":["Construire des systèmes de questions et réponses sur des documents propriétaires","Créer des chatbots avec des informations factuelles actuelles","Mettre en œuvre une recherche sémantique avec des requêtes de langage naturel"],"de":["Aufbau von Q&A-Systemen über eigene Dokumente","Erstellung von Chatbots mit aktuellen faktischen Informationen","Implementierung von semantischer Suche mit natürlichen Sprachabfragen"],"pt":["Construir sistemas de Perguntas e Respostas sobre documentos proprietários","Criar chatbots com informações factuais atuais","Implementar pesquisa semântica com consultas de linguagem natural"],"ru":["Создание систем вопросов и ответов на основе проприетарных документов","Разработка чат-ботов с актуальной фактической информацией","Реализация семантического поиска с запросами естественного языка"],"ar":["بناء أنظمة الأسئلة والإجابات على وثائق مملوكة","إنشاء محادثات روبوتات مع معلومات фактиة حالية","تنفيذ بحث دلالي باستخدام استفسارات اللغة الطبيعية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to external knowledge sources","Dependent on quality of training data for Retrieval-Augmented Generation"],"zh":["需要访问外部知识源","依赖于检索增强生成的训练数据质量"],"ja":["外部の知識源へのアクセスが必要","検索増強生成のトレーニングデータの品質に依存する"],"ko":["외부 지식원에 접근할 수 있어야 함","검색 증강 생성을 위한 훈련 데이터의 품질에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a fuentes de conocimiento externas","Depende de la calidad de los datos de entrenamiento para la Generación con Recuperación"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à des sources de connaissances externes","Dépend de la qualité des données de formation pour la génération avec récupération"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf externe Wissensquellen","Hängt von der Qualität der Trainingsdaten für die Retrieval-Augmented-Generation ab"],"pt":["Exige acesso a fontes de conhecimento externas","Depende da qualidade dos dados de treinamento para Geração com Recuperação Aumentada"],"ru":["Требует доступа к внешним источникам знаний","Зависит от качества данных для обучения генерации с дополненной извлечением"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مصادر المعرفة الخارجية","يعتمد على جودة بيانات التدريب لإنشاء الاسترجاع المعزز"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('khushparag/agentic_learning_coach/mermaid-diagrams', 'community', 'khushparag', 'agentic_learning_coach', 'khushparag/agentic_learning_coach', 'mermaid-diagrams', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:18:43.130Z', NULL, '{"id":"khushparag/agentic_learning_coach/mermaid-diagrams","name":"mermaid-diagrams","description":{"zh":"MermaidMermaid","ja":"MermaidMermaid","ko":"MermaidMermaid","es":"Mermaid es una herramienta para crear diagramas de software utilizando una sintaxis basada en texto. Permite renderizar diagramas desde definiciones de texto simples","fr":"Mermaid est un outil pour créer des diagrammes de logiciel en utilisant une syntaxe basée sur le texte. Il permet de rendre des diagrammes à partir de définitions de texte simples","de":"Mermaid ist ein Tool zur Erstellung von Software-Diagrammen mithilfe einer textbasierten Syntax. Es ermöglicht die Renderung von Diagrammen aus einfachen Textdefinitionen","pt":"O Mermaid é uma ferramenta para criar diagramas de software profissionais com sintaxe baseada em texto. Ele renderiza diagramas a partir de definições de texto simples, tornando-os fáceis de atualizar e manter ao lado do código.","ru":"Mermaid - это инструмент для создания профессиональных диаграмм программного обеспечения с помощью текстовой синтаксиса. Он отображает диаграммы из простых текстовых определений, что делает их легко обновляемыми и поддерживаемыми вместе с кодом.","ar":"مرميد هو أداة لإنشاء رسومات برمجيات احترافية باستخدام بناء الجملة النصي. يقوم بتحويل الرسومات من تعريفات نصية بسيطة، مما يجعلها سهلة التحديث والصيانة إلى جانب الكود.","en":"Intelligent multi-agent system for personalized coding education. Features 7 AI agents, adaptive learning, secure code execution, gamification, and social learning. Built with FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL, and Docker. 356 tests, 90%+ coverage. Spec-driven development with Kiro CLI."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Mermaid Diagrams ","ja":"Mermaid","ko":"Mermaid ","es":"Diagramas Mermaid: Creación de diagramas de software","fr":"Diagrammes Mermaid: Création de diagrammes de logiciel","de":"Mermaid-Diagramme: Erstellung von Software-Diagrammen","pt":"Diagramas Mermaid: Crie Diagramas Profissionais","ru":"Mermaid Диаграммы: Создайте Профессиональные Диаграммы","ar":"رسومات ميرميد: أنشئ رسومات محترفة","en":"mermaid-diagrams"},"description":{"zh":"MermaidMermaid","ja":"MermaidMermaid","ko":"MermaidMermaid","es":"Mermaid es una herramienta para crear diagramas de software utilizando una sintaxis basada en texto. Permite renderizar diagramas desde definiciones de texto...","fr":"Mermaid est un outil pour créer des diagrammes de logiciel en utilisant une syntaxe basée sur le texte. Il permet de rendre des diagrammes à partir de défini...","de":"Mermaid ist ein Tool zur Erstellung von Software-Diagrammen mithilfe einer textbasierten Syntax. Es ermöglicht die Renderung von Diagrammen aus einfachen Tex...","pt":"O Mermaid é uma ferramenta para criar diagramas de software profissionais com sintaxe baseada em texto. Ele renderiza diagramas a partir de definições de tex...","ru":"Mermaid - это инструмент для создания профессиональных диаграмм программного обеспечения с помощью текстовой синтаксиса. Он отображает диаграммы из простых т...","ar":"مرميد هو أداة لإنشاء رسومات برمجيات احترافية باستخدام بناء الجملة النصي. يقوم بتحويل الرسومات من تعريفات نصية بسيطة، مما يجعلها سهلة التحديث والصيانة إلى جان...","en":"Intelligent multi-agent system for personalized coding education. Features 7 AI agents, adaptive learning, secure code execution, gamification, and social le..."},"definition":{"en":"Intelligent multi-agent system for personalized coding education. Features 7 AI agents, adaptive learning, secure code execution, gamification, and social learning. Built with FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL, and Docker. 356 tests, 90%+ coverage. Spec-driven development with Kiro CLI."},"features":{"zh":["Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid"],"ja":["Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid"],"ko":["Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid"],"es":["Sintaxis basada en texto","Renderizado de diagramas desde definiciones de texto","Versionamiento y actualización fácil de los diagramas","Compatibilidad con diferentes tipos de diagramas"],"fr":["Syntaxe basée sur le texte","Rendu de diagrammes à partir de définitions de texte","Versionnage et mise à jour facile des diagrammes","Compatibilité avec différents types de diagrammes"],"de":["Textbasierte Syntax","Renderung von Diagrammen aus Textdefinitionen","Versionierung und einfache Aktualisierung von Diagrammen","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Diagrammtypen"],"pt":["Sintaxe baseada em texto para criar diagramas","Renderização de diagramas a partir de definições de texto simples","Fácil atualização e manutenção de diagramas","Integração com código","Suporte a vários tipos de diagramas","Comentários com `%%`"],"ru":["Текстовая синтаксис для создания диаграмм","Отображение диаграмм из простых текстовых определений","Легкое обновление и поддержка диаграмм","Интеграция с кодом","Поддержка нескольких типов диаграмм","Комментарии с `%%`"],"ar":["بناء الجملة النصي لإنشاء رسومات","عرض الرسومات من تعريفات نصية بسيطة","تحديث وتصحيح رسومات سهل","التكامل مع الكود","دعم أنواع متعددة من الرسومات","تعليقات باستخدام `%%`"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid"],"ja":["Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid"],"ko":["Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid","Mermaid"],"es":["mermaid","diagramas de software","sintaxis basada en texto","renderizado de diagramas","versionamiento de diagramas","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["mermaid","diagrammes de logiciel","syntaxe basée sur le texte","rendu de diagrammes","versionnage de diagrammes","développement de logiciel"],"de":["mermaid","software-diagramme","textbasierte syntax","renderung von diagrammen","versionierung von diagrammen","software-entwicklung"],"pt":["mermaid","diagramas de software","sintaxe baseada em texto","renderização de diagramas","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de diagramação","integração com código","desenho de diagramas","diagramas profissionais"],"ru":["mermaid","диаграммы программного обеспечения","текстовая синтаксис","отображение диаграмм","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты диаграммирования","интеграция с кодом","создание диаграмм","профессиональные диаграммы"],"ar":["مرميد","رسومات برمجيات","بناء الجملة النصي","عرض الرسومات","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات الرسم البياني","التكامل مع الكود","إنشاء رسومات","رسومات احترافية"]}},"owner":"khushparag","repo":"agentic_learning_coach","repoPath":"khushparag/agentic_learning_coach","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mermaid-diagrams","description":"Comprehensive guide for creating software diagrams using Mermaid syntax. Use when users need to create, visualize, or document software through diagrams including class diagrams (domain modeling, object-oriented design), sequence diagrams (application flows, API interactions, code execution), flowcharts (processes, algorithms, user journeys), entity relationship diagrams (database schemas), C4 architecture diagrams (system context, containers, components), state diagrams, git graphs, pie charts, gantt charts, or any other diagram type. Triggers include requests to diagram, visualize, model, map out, show the flow, or when explaining system architecture, database design, code structure, or user/application flows.","bodyPreview":"# Mermaid Diagramming\n\nCreate professional software diagrams using Mermaid''s text-based syntax. Mermaid renders diagrams from simple text definitions, making diagrams version-controllable, easy to update, and maintainable alongside code.\n\n## Core Syntax Structure\n\nAll Mermaid diagrams follow this pattern:\n\n```mermaid\ndiagramType\n  definition content\n```\n\n**Key principles:**\n- First line declares diagram type (e.g., `classDiagram`, `sequenceDiagram`, `flowchart`)\n- Use `%%` for comments\n- Line br","body":"# Mermaid Diagramming\n\nCreate professional software diagrams using Mermaid''s text-based syntax. Mermaid renders diagrams from simple text definitions, making diagrams version-controllable, easy to update, and maintainable alongside code.\n\n## Core Syntax Structure\n\nAll Mermaid diagrams follow this pattern:\n\n```mermaid\ndiagramType\n  definition content\n```\n\n**Key principles:**\n- First line declares diagram type (e.g., `classDiagram`, `sequenceDiagram`, `flowchart`)\n- Use `%%` for comments\n- Line breaks and indentation improve readability but aren''t required\n- Unknown words break diagrams; parameters fail silently\n\n## Diagram Type Selection Guide\n\n**Choose the right diagram type:**\n\n1. **Class Diagrams** - Domain modeling, OOP design, entity relationships\n   - Domain-driven design documentation\n   - Object-oriented class structures\n   - Entity relationships and dependencies\n\n2. **Sequence Diagrams** - Temporal interactions, message flows\n   - API request/response flows\n   - User authentication flows\n   - System component interactions\n   - Method call sequences\n\n3. **Flowcharts** - Processes, algorithms, decision trees\n   - User journeys and workflows\n   - Business processes\n   - Algorithm logic\n   - Deployment pipelines\n\n4. **Entity Relationship Diagrams (ERD)** - Database schemas\n   - Table relationships\n   - Data modeling\n   - Schema design\n\n5. **C4 Diagrams** - Software architecture at multiple levels\n   - System Context (systems and users)\n   - Container (applications, databases, services)\n   - Component (internal structure)\n   - Code (class/interface level)\n\n6. **State Diagrams** - State machines, lifecycle states\n7. **Git Graphs** - Version control branching strategies\n8. **Gantt Charts** - Project timelines, scheduling\n9. **Pie/Bar Charts** - Data visualization\n\n## Quick Start Examples\n\n### Class Diagram (Domain Model)\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n    Title -- Genre\n    Title *-- Season\n    Title *-- Review\n    User --> Review : creates\n    \n    class Title {\n        +string name\n        +int releaseYear\n        +play()\n    }\n    \n    class Genre {\n        +string name\n        +getTopTitles()\n    }\n```\n\n### Sequence Diagram (API Flow)\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant API\n    participant Database\n    \n    User->>API: POST /login\n    API->>Database: Query credentials\n    Database-->>API: Return user data\n    alt Valid credentials\n        API-->>User: 200 OK + JWT token\n    else Invalid credentials\n        API-->>User: 401 Unauthorized\n    end\n```\n\n### Flowchart (User Journey)\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Start([User visits site]) --> Auth{Authenticated?}\n    Auth -->|No| Login[Show login page]\n    Auth -->|Yes| Dashboard[Show dashboard]\n    Login --> Creds[Enter credentials]\n    Creds --> Validate{Valid?}\n    Validate -->|Yes| Dashboard\n    Validate -->|No| Error[Show error]\n    Error --> Login\n```\n\n### ERD (Database Schema)\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    USER ||--o{ ORDER : places\n    ORDER ||--|{ LINE_ITEM : contains\n    PRODUCT ||--o{ LINE_ITEM : includes\n    \n    USER {\n        int id PK\n        string email UK\n        string name\n        datetime created_at\n    }\n    \n    ORDER {\n        int id PK\n        int user_id FK\n        decimal total\n        datetime created_at\n    }\n```\n\n## Detailed References\n\nFor in-depth guidance on specific diagram types, see:\n\n- **[references/class-diagrams.md](references/class-diagrams.md)** - Domain modeling, relationships (association, composition, aggregation, inheritance), multiplicity, methods/properties\n- **[references/sequence-diagrams.md](references/sequence-diagrams.md)** - Actors, participants, messages (sync/async), activations, loops, alt/opt/par blocks, notes\n- **[references/flowcharts.md](references/flowcharts.md)** - Node shapes, connections, decision logic, subgraphs, styling\n- **[references/erd-diagrams.md](references/erd-diagrams.md)** - Entities, relationships, cardinality, keys, attributes\n- **[references/c4-diagrams.md](references/c4-diagrams.md)** - System context, container, component diagrams, boundaries\n- **[references/advanced-features.md](references/advanced-features.md)** - Themes, styling, configuration, layout options\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Start Simple** - Begin with core entities/components, add details incrementally\n2. **Use Meaningful Names** - Clear labels make diagrams self-documenting\n3. **Comment Extensively** - Use `%%` comments to explain complex relationships\n4. **Keep Focused** - One diagram per concept; split large diagrams into multiple focused views\n5. **Version Control** - Store `.mmd` files alongside code for easy updates\n6. **Add Context** - Include titles and notes to explain diagram purpose\n7. **Iterate** - Refine diagrams as understanding evolves\n\n## Configuration and Theming\n\nConfigure diagrams using frontmatter:\n\n```mermaid\n---\nconfig:\n  theme: base\n  themeVariables:\n    primaryColor: \"#ff6b6b\"\n---\nflowchart LR\n    A --> B\n```\n\n**Available themes:** default, forest, dark, neutral, base\n\n**Layout options:**\n- `layout: dagre` (default) - Classic balanced layout\n- `layout: elk` - Advanced layout for complex diagrams (requires integration)\n\n**Look options:**\n- `look: classic` - Traditional Mermaid style\n- `look: handDrawn` - Sketch-like appearance\n\n## Exporting and Rendering\n\n**Native support in:**\n- GitHub/GitLab - Automatically renders in Markdown\n- VS Code - With Markdown Mermaid extension\n- Notion, Obsidian, Confluence - Built-in support\n\n**Export options:**\n- [Mermaid Live Editor](https://mermaid.live) - Online editor with PNG/SVG export\n- Mermaid CLI - `npm install -g @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli` then `mmdc -i input.mmd -o output.png`\n- Docker - `docker run --rm -v $(pwd):/data minlag/mermaid-cli -i /data/input.mmd -o /data/output.png`\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Breaking characters** - Avoid `{}` in comments, use proper escape sequences for special characters\n- **Syntax errors** - Misspellings break diagrams; validate syntax in Mermaid Live\n- **Overcomplexity** - Split complex diagrams into multiple focused views\n- **Missing relationships** - Document all important connections between entities\n\n## When to Create Diagrams\n\n**Always diagram when:**\n- Starting new projects or features\n- Documenting complex systems\n- Explaining architecture decisions\n- Designing database schemas\n- Planning refactoring efforts\n- Onboarding new team members\n\n**Use diagrams to:**\n- Align stakeholders on technical decisions\n- Document domain models collaboratively\n- Visualize data flows and system interactions\n- Plan before coding\n- Create living documentation that evolves with code\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:18:43.130Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing advanced diagramming and documentation capabilities using Mermaid''s text-based syntax.","zh":"非常适合需要使用Mermaid的文本语法进行高级图表和文档创建的开发代理。","ja":"Mermaidのテキストベースの構文を使用した高度な図表とドキュメント作成機能が必要な開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Mermaid의 텍스트 기반 구문으로 고급 도표 및 문서 생성 기능이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan capacidades de diagramación y documentación avanzadas utilizando la sintaxis basada en texto de Mermaid.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de fonctionnalités de diagramme et de documentation avancées utilisant la syntaxe basée sur du texte de Mermaid.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsagenten, die erweiterte Diagramm- und Dokumentationsfunktionen mit Mermaids textbasierter Syntax benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de diagramação e documentação usando a sintaxe baseada em texto do Mermaid.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходимы расширенные возможности диаграммирования и документирования с использованием текстовой синтаксиса Mermaid.","ar":"مثالي لخوادم التطوير التي تحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لإنشاء مخططات وتوثيق باستخدام بناء الجملة النصي لبرنامج Mermaid."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create professional software diagrams using Mermaid, enabling version-controllable, easy to update, and maintainable diagrams alongside code, leveraging FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL, and Docker for secure and adaptive learning environments, with features like spec-driven development and Kiro CLI.","zh":"赋予代理创建专业软件图表的能力，使用Mermaid实现版本控制、易于更新和维护的图表，且可以与代码一起使用，利用FastAPI、React、PostgreSQL和Docker实现安全且适应性强的学习环境，具有特性驱动开发和Kiro CLI等功能。","ja":"エージェントがMermaidを使用してプロフェッショナルなソフトウェア図表を作成できるようにし、FastAPI、React、PostgreSQL、Dockerを使用して、バージョン管理、簡単に更新、保守可能な図表をコードと一緒に使用できるようにします。また、SpecDriven開発やKiro CLIなどの機能を備えた安全で適応性の高い学習環境を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 Mermaid를 사용하여 전문 소프트웨어 도표를 생성할 수 있도록 하여 코드와 함께 버전 관리, 쉽게 업데이트하고 유지 관리할 수 있는 도표를 만들 수 있도록 합니다. 또한 FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL 및 Docker를 사용하여 보안 및 적응性 있는 학습 환경을 구축하고 특성 주도 개발 및 Kiro CLIなどの 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear diagramas de software profesionales con Mermaid, lo que permite diagramas controlados por versiones, fáciles de actualizar y mantenibles junto con el código, aprovechando FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL y Docker para entornos de aprendizaje seguros y adaptativos, con características como desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones y Kiro CLI.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des diagrammes de logiciels professionnels avec Mermaid, ce qui permet des diagrammes contrôlés par version, faciles à mettre à jour et maintenables aux côtés du code, en exploitant FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL et Docker pour des environnements d''apprentissage sécurisés et adaptatifs, avec des fonctionnalités comme le développement piloté par des spécifications et Kiro CLI.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, professionelle Software-Diagramme mit Mermaid zu erstellen, wodurch versionierbare, leicht zu aktualisierende und wartbare Diagramme neben dem Code ermöglicht werden, indem FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL und Docker für sichere und adaptive Lernumgebungen genutzt werden, mit Funktionen wie spezifikationsgetriebenem Entwicklung und Kiro CLI.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar diagramas de software profissionais usando o Mermaid, permitindo diagramas controláveis por versão, fáceis de atualizar e manter ao lado do código, aproveitando o FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL e Docker para ambientes de aprendizado seguros e adaptáveis, com recursos como desenvolvimento orientado por especificações e Kiro CLI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать профессиональные программные диаграммы с помощью Mermaid, что позволяет создавать версионно-контролируемые, легко обновляемые и поддерживаемые диаграммы вместе с кодом, используя FastAPI, React, PostgreSQL и Docker для безопасных и адаптивных сред обучения, с функциями, такими как разработка, управляемая спецификациями, и Kiro CLI.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية إنشاء مخططات برنامج محترفة باستخدام Mermaid، مما يتيح إنشاء مخططات قابلة للتحكم الإصدار، سهلة التحديث والصيانة جنبًا إلى جنب مع الشفرة، مستفيدًا من FastAPI و React و PostgreSQL و Docker لإنشاء بيئات تعلم آمنة وملائمة، مع ميزات مثل التطوير الموجه بالمواصفات وواجهة سطر أوامر Kiro."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating class diagrams for object-oriented programming","Creating sequence diagrams for complex system interactions","Debugging flowcharts for logical program flows"],"zh":["为面向对象编程生成类图表","为复杂系统交互创建序列图表","为逻辑程序流调试流程图"],"ja":["オブジェクト指向プログラミングのクラス図表を生成する","複雑なシステム相互作用のシーケンス図表を作成する","論理プログラムフローのデバッグフローチャート"],"ko":["객체 지향 프로그래밍을 위한 클래스 도표 생성","복잡한 시스템 상호 작용을 위한 시퀀스 도표 생성","논리 프로그램 흐름을 위한 디버깅 흐름도"],"es":["Generación de diagramas de clases para la programación orientada a objetos","Creación de diagramas de secuencia para interacciones de sistemas complejos","Depuración de diagramas de flujo para flujos de programas lógicos"],"fr":["Génération de diagrammes de classes pour la programmation orientée objet","Création de diagrammes de séquence pour les interactions de systèmes complexes","Débogage de diagrammes de flux pour les flux de programmes logiques"],"de":["Erstellung von Klassendiagrammen für die objektorientierte Programmierung","Erstellung von Sequenzdiagrammen für komplexe Systeminteraktionen","Fehlerbehebung von Flussdiagrammen für logische Programmflüsse"],"pt":["Gerar diagramas de classes para programação orientada a objetos","Criar diagramas de sequência para interações de sistemas complexos","Depurar fluxogramas para fluxos de programas lógicos"],"ru":["Генерировать диаграммы классов для объектно-ориентированного программирования","Создавать диаграммы последовательности для сложных взаимодействий систем","Отлаживать блок-схемы для логических потоков программ"],"ar":["إنشاء مخططات فئات للبرمجة الموجهة بالكائنات","إنشاء مخططات تسلسل للتفاعلات الأنظمة المعقدة","تصحيح أخطاء المخططات الانسيابية للتدفقات البرمجية المنطقية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Mermaid syntax knowledge","Limited to diagram types supported by Mermaid (e.g., classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, flowchart)"],"zh":["需要Mermaid语法知识","仅限Mermaid支持的图表类型（例如，classDiagram，sequenceDiagram，flowchart）"],"ja":["Mermaidの構文の知識が必要","Mermaidでサポートされている図表の種類のみ（たとえば、classDiagram、sequenceDiagram、flowchart）"],"ko":["Mermaid 구문 지식 필요","Mermaid에서 지원하는 도표 유형만 해당(예: classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, flowchart)"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de la sintaxis de Mermaid","Limitado a los tipos de diagramas compatibles con Mermaid (por ejemplo, classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, flowchart)"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en syntaxe Mermaid","Limité aux types de diagrammes pris en charge par Mermaid (par exemple, classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, flowchart)"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Mermaid-Syntax","Begrenzt auf die von Mermaid unterstützten Diagrammtypen (z. B. classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, flowchart)"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento da sintaxe do Mermaid","Limitado a tipos de diagramas suportados pelo Mermaid (por exemplo, classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, flowchart)"],"ru":["Требует знания синтаксиса Mermaid","Ограничен типами диаграмм, поддерживаемыми Mermaid (например, classDiagram, sequenceDiagram, flowchart)"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بناء الجملة لبرنامج Mermaid","محدود بنوعيات المخططات المدعومة من برنامج Mermaid (على سبيل المثال، مخطط الفئة، مخطط التسلسل، مخطط الانسياب)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HugoCL/round-robin-rmpe/web-design-guidelines', 'community', 'HugoCL', 'round-robin-rmpe', 'HugoCL/round-robin-rmpe', 'web-design-guidelines', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:19:01.459Z', NULL, '{"id":"HugoCL/round-robin-rmpe/web-design-guidelines","name":"web-design-guidelines","description":{"zh":"Web 设计指南提供了一套自动化代码审查的工具，帮助开发者确保代码符合最新的 Web 接口标准","ja":"Web デザイン ガイドラインは、開発者がコードが最新の Web インターフェイス標準に準拠していることを確認するための自動化コードレビュー ツールを提供します","ko":"웹 디자인 가이드라인은 개발자가 코드가 최신 웹 인터페이스 표준에 준수하는지 확인할 수 있는 자동화된 코드 리뷰 도구를 제공합니다","es":"Las pautas de diseño web ofrecen una guía para crear interfaces web accesibles y fáciles de usar. Aprende a aplicarlas","fr":"Les guidelines de conception web fournissent un cadre pour créer des interfaces web accessibles et utilisables. Découvrez comment les appliquer","de":"Die Web-Design-Richtlinien bieten einen Leitfaden für die Erstellung von benutzerfreundlichen Web-Oberflächen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie anwenden","pt":"O skill de diretrizes de design web ajuda a garantir a conformidade com as diretrizes de interface. Ele verifica arquivos e fornece relatórios de conformidade.","ru":"Навык руководства по веб-дизайну помогает обеспечить соответствие рекомендациям по интерфейсу. Он проверяет файлы и предоставляет отчеты о соответствии.","ar":"مهارة إرشادات تصميم الويب تساعد على ضمان المطابقة مع إرشادات الواجهة. أنها تحقق من الملفات وتقدم تقارير حول المطابقة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Web 设计指南：简化开发流程","ja":"Web デザイン ガイドライン：開発の効率化","ko":"웹 디자인 가이드ライン: 개발 프로세스 최적화","es":"Pautas de diseño web: Guías para interfaces web","fr":"Guidelines de conception web : Interfaces web","de":"Web-Design-Richtlinien: Leitfaden für Web-Oberflächen","pt":"Diretrizes de Design Web: Guia de Interface","ru":"Руководство по веб-дизайну: рекомендации по интерфейсу","ar":"إرشادات تصميم الويب: دليل الواجهة","en":"web-design-guidelines"},"description":{"zh":"Web 设计指南提供了一套自动化代码审查的工具，帮助开发者确保代码符合最新的 Web 接口标准","ja":"Web デザイン ガイドラインは、開発者がコードが最新の Web インターフェイス標準に準拠していることを確認するための自動化コードレビュー ツールを提供します","ko":"웹 디자인 가이드라인은 개발자가 코드가 최신 웹 인터페이스 표준에 준수하는지 확인할 수 있는 자동화된 코드 리뷰 도구를 제공합니다","es":"Las pautas de diseño web ofrecen una guía para crear interfaces web accesibles y fáciles de usar. Aprende a aplicarlas","fr":"Les guidelines de conception web fournissent un cadre pour créer des interfaces web accessibles et utilisables. Découvrez comment les appliquer","de":"Die Web-Design-Richtlinien bieten einen Leitfaden für die Erstellung von benutzerfreundlichen Web-Oberflächen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie anwenden","pt":"O skill de diretrizes de design web ajuda a garantir a conformidade com as diretrizes de interface. Ele verifica arquivos e fornece relatórios de conformidade.","ru":"Навык руководства по веб-дизайну помогает обеспечить соответствие рекомендациям по интерфейсу. Он проверяет файлы и предоставляет отчеты о соответствии.","ar":"مهارة إرشادات تصميم الويب تساعد على ضمان المطابقة مع إرشادات الواجهة. أنها تحقق من الملفات وتقدم تقارير حول المطابقة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动化代码审查","支持最新 Web 接口标准","简化开发流程","提高代码质量","减少手动审查错误"],"ja":["自動化コードレビュー","最新の Web インターフェイス標準のサポート","開発プロセスの簡素化","コード品質の向上","手動レビューのエラー削減"],"ko":["자동화된 코드 리뷰","최신 웹 인터페이스 표준 지원","개발 프로세스 최적화","코드 품질 향상","수동 리뷰 오류 감소"],"es":["Revisión de archivos para cumplimiento con las pautas","Verificación de reglas y recomendaciones","Salida de resultados en formato conciso","Actualización automática de las pautas","Compatibilidad con varios formatos de archivo"],"fr":["Vérification des fichiers pour la conformité aux guidelines","Vérification des règles et des recommandations","Sortie des résultats dans un format concis","Mise à jour automatique des guidelines","Compatibilité avec plusieurs formats de fichiers"],"de":["Überprüfung von Dateien auf Einhaltung der Richtlinien","Überprüfung von Regeln und Empfehlungen","Ausgabe der Ergebnisse im knappen Format","Automatische Aktualisierung der Richtlinien","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Dateiformaten"],"pt":["Verificação de arquivos de conformidade","Relatórios de conformidade em formato conciso","Integração com fontes de diretrizes de design web","Verificação de regras de acessibilidade e usabilidade","Suporte a múltiplos arquivos e padrões"],"ru":["Проверка файлов на соответствие","Отчеты о соответствии в кратком формате","Интеграция с источниками руководства по веб-дизайну","Проверка правил доступности и удобства использования","Поддержка нескольких файлов и шаблонов"],"ar":["فحص الملفات للتأكد من المطابقة","تقارير المطابقة بالتنسيق الموجز","التكامل مع مصادر إرشادات تصميم الويب","فحص قواعد إمكانية الوصول وسهولة الاستخدام","دعم الملفات المتعددة والأنماط"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Web 设计指南","自动化代码审查","Web 接口标准","开发效率","代码质量","Web 开发工具"],"ja":["Web デザイン ガイドライン","自動化コードレビュー","Web インターフェイス標準","開発効率","コード品質","Web 開発ツール"],"ko":["웹 디자인 가이드라인","자동화된 코드 리뷰","웹 인터페이스 표준","개발 효율성","코드 품질","웹 개발 도구"],"es":["pautas de diseño web","interfaces web","accesibilidad web","usabilidad web","diseño de interfaces","guias de diseño","web design guidelines","desarrollo web","frontend development"],"fr":["guidelines de conception web","interfaces web","accessibilité web","expérience utilisateur","conception d''interfaces","guides de conception","web design guidelines","développement web","frontend development"],"de":["Web-Design-Richtlinien","Web-Oberflächen","Barrierefreiheit","Benutzerfreundlichkeit","Oberflächengestaltung","Designleitfäden","Web-Entwicklung","Frontend-Entwicklung","Usability-Engineering"],"pt":["diretrizes de design web","interface de usuário","acessibilidade web","usabilidade web","desenvolvimento web","guias de design"],"ru":["руководство по веб-дизайну","интерфейс пользователя","доступность веб","удобство использования веб","разработка веб","гайды по дизайну"],"ar":["إرشادات تصميم الويب","واجهة المستخدم","إمكانية الوصول إلى الويب","سهولة استخدام الويب","تطوير الويب","دلائل التصميم"]}},"owner":"HugoCL","repo":"round-robin-rmpe","repoPath":"HugoCL/round-robin-rmpe","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"web-design-guidelines","description":"Review UI code for Web Interface Guidelines compliance. Use when asked to review my UI, check accessibility, audit design, review UX, or check my site against best practices.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Web Interface Guidelines\n\nReview files for compliance with Web Interface Guidelines.\n\n## How It Works\n\n1. Fetch the latest guidelines from the source URL below\n2. Read the specified files (or prompt user for files/pattern)\n3. Check against all rules in the fetched guidelines\n4. Output findings in the terse `file:line` format\n\n## Guidelines Source\n\nFetch fresh guidelines before each review:\n\n```\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines/main/command.md\n```\n\nUse WebF","body":"# Web Interface Guidelines\n\nReview files for compliance with Web Interface Guidelines.\n\n## How It Works\n\n1. Fetch the latest guidelines from the source URL below\n2. Read the specified files (or prompt user for files/pattern)\n3. Check against all rules in the fetched guidelines\n4. Output findings in the terse `file:line` format\n\n## Guidelines Source\n\nFetch fresh guidelines before each review:\n\n```\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines/main/command.md\n```\n\nUse WebFetch to retrieve the latest rules. The fetched content contains all the rules and output format instructions.\n\n## Usage\n\nWhen a user provides a file or pattern argument:\n1. Fetch guidelines from the source URL above\n2. Read the specified files\n3. Apply all rules from the fetched guidelines\n4. Output findings using the format specified in the guidelines\n\nIf no files specified, ask the user which files to review.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:19:01.459Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing automated web interface compliance checking with Web Interface Guidelines.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化Web接口合规性检查的前端代理，符合Web接口指南。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントがWebインターフェイスのガイドラインに準拠した自動化されたWebインターフェイスのコンプライアンスチェックを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"自動화된 웹 인터페이스 컴플라이언스 체크가 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합하며, 웹 인터페이스 가이드라인을 준수합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan una comprobación automática de la conformidad de la interfaz web con las Directrices de la Interfaz Web.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin d''une vérification automatisée de la conformité de l''interface web avec les Directives d''Interface Web.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die eine automatisierte Überprüfung der Webinterface-Konformität mit den Webinterface-Richtlinien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de verificação automática de conformidade de interface web com as Diretrizes de Interface Web.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым требуется автоматическая проверка соответствия веб-интерфейса руководящим принципам веб-интерфейса.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الذي يحتاج إلى التحقق التلقائي من مطابقة واجهة الويب لمرشد واجهة الويب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to review files for compliance with the latest web interface guidelines from Vercel Labs, utilizing Markdown files and outputting findings in a terse `file:line` format, all via HTTPS protocol from the source URL.","zh":"赋予代理审查文件以确保其符合Vercel Labs最新的Web接口指南的能力，使用Markdown文件，并以简洁的`文件：行`格式输出结果，全部通过HTTPS协议从源URL获取。","ja":"Vercel Labsからの最新のWebインターフェイスガイドラインに従ってファイルを審査するエージェントの能力を提供します。Markdownファイルを使用し、`ファイル：行`形式で結果を出力します。すべてのプロセスはHTTPSプロトコルを使用して、ソースURLから実行されます。","ko":"에이전트가 Vercel Labs의 최신 웹 인터페이스 가이드라인에 따라 파일을 검토할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 마크다운 파일을 사용하고, 결과를 `파일:行` 형식으로 출력하며, 모든 처리는 HTTPS 프로토콜을 통해 소스 URL에서 수행됩니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a revisar archivos para asegurarse de que cumplan con las últimas directrices de interfaz web de Vercel Labs, utilizando archivos Markdown y generando resultados en un formato conciso `archivo:línea`, todo a través del protocolo HTTPS desde la URL de origen.","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier les fichiers pour garantir leur conformité avec les dernières directives d''interface web de Vercel Labs, en utilisant des fichiers Markdown et en produisant des résultats dans un format concis `fichier:ligne`, le tout via le protocole HTTPS à partir de l''URL source.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Dateien auf Konformität mit den neuesten Webinterface-Richtlinien von Vercel Labs zu überprüfen, indem Markdown-Dateien verwendet und Ergebnisse in einem knappen `Datei:Zeile`-Format ausgegeben werden, alles über das HTTPS-Protokoll von der Quell-URL.","pt":"Permite que os agentes revisem arquivos para garantir a conformidade com as últimas diretrizes de interface web da Vercel Labs, utilizando arquivos Markdown e exibindo os resultados em um formato conciso `arquivo:linha`, tudo via protocolo HTTPS a partir da URL de origem.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять файлы на соответствие последним руководящим принципам веб-интерфейса от Vercel Labs, используя файлы Markdown и выводя результаты в кратком формате `файл:строка`, все через протокол HTTPS из исходного URL.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على مراجعة الملفات للتأكد من مطابقتها لأحدث إرشادات واجهة الويب من Vercel Labs، باستخدام ملفات Markdown وعرض النتائج في تنسيق مقتضب `ملف:سطر`، وكل ذلك عبر بروتوكول HTTPS من عنوان URL الأصلي."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating web interface reviews for compliance","Generating reports on guideline violations in Markdown files","Debugging web interface issues based on Vercel Labs guidelines"],"zh":["自动化Web接口审查以确保合规性","生成关于指南违规的报告，使用Markdown文件","根据Vercel Labs指南调试Web接口问题"],"ja":["コンプライアンスを確保するためのWebインターフェイスの審査を自動化する","マークダウンファイルを使用してガイドライン違反の報告書を生成する","Vercel Labsのガイドラインに基づいてWebインターフェイスの問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["컴플라이언스를 보장하기 위한 웹 인터페이스의 검토를 자동화한다","마크다운 파일을 사용하여 가이드라인 위반에 대한 보고서를 생성한다","Vercel Labs의 가이드라인을 기준으로 웹 인터페이스의 문제를 디버깅한다"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de la interfaz web para la conformidad","Generación de informes sobre violaciones de las directrices en archivos Markdown","Depuración de problemas de la interfaz web en función de las directrices de Vercel Labs"],"fr":["Automatisation des vérifications d''interface web pour la conformité","Génération de rapports sur les violations des directives dans les fichiers Markdown","Débogage des problèmes d''interface web en fonction des directives de Vercel Labs"],"de":["Automatisierung von Webinterface-Überprüfungen für die Konformität","Erstellung von Berichten über Richtlinienverletzungen in Markdown-Dateien","Fehlerbehebung von Webinterface-Problemen auf der Grundlage der Richtlinien von Vercel Labs"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de interface web para garantir a conformidade","Gerar relatórios sobre violações de diretrizes em arquivos Markdown","Depurar problemas de interface web com base nas diretrizes da Vercel Labs"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверки веб-интерфейса на соответствие","Генерировать отчеты о нарушениях руководящих принципов в файлах Markdown","Отлаживать проблемы веб-интерфейса на основе руководящих принципов Vercel Labs"],"ar":["توفير تلقائي لعمليات فحص واجهة الويب للتأكد من المطابقة","توليد تقارير عن انتهاكات الإرشادات في ملفات Markdown","تصحيح أخطاء في واجهة المستخدم بناءً على إرشادات Vercel Labs"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires internet access for fetching guidelines from GitHub","Limited to guidelines provided by Vercel Labs at the specified source URL"],"zh":["需要互联网访问以从GitHub获取指南","仅限于Vercel Labs在指定源URL处提供的指南"],"ja":["ガイドラインをGitHubから取得するためにインターネットアクセスが必要","指定されたソースURLにあるVercel Labsが提供するガイドラインのみに限定される"],"ko":["가이드라인을 GitHub에서 가져오기 위해 인터넷 액세스가 필요합니다","지정된 소스 URL에 있는 Vercel Labs가 제공하는 가이드라인으로만 제한됩니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso a Internet para recuperar las directrices de GitHub","Limitado a las directrices proporcionadas por Vercel Labs en la URL de origen especificada"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à Internet pour récupérer les directives depuis GitHub","Limité aux directives fournies par Vercel Labs à l''URL source spécifiée"],"de":["Benötigt Internetzugang, um Richtlinien von GitHub abzurufen","Begrenzt auf die von Vercel Labs zur angegebenen Quell-URL bereitgestellten Richtlinien"],"pt":["Requer acesso à internet para buscar diretrizes do GitHub","Limitado às diretrizes fornecidas pela Vercel Labs no URL de origem especificado"],"ru":["Требует доступа к интернету для получения руководящих принципов из GitHub","Ограничен руководящими принципами, предоставленными Vercel Labs по указанному исходному URL"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الإنترنت للبحث عن الإرشادات من GitHub","محدود بالإرشادات المقدمة من Vercel Labs في عنوان URL الأصلي المحدد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
