Sie kohärente und zugängliche visuelle Systeme mit den Grundlagen der Typografie, Farbe und Abstand","pt":"Desenvolva sistemas visuais coesos e acessíveis com fundamentos de design visual","ru":"Создавайте сплоченные и доступные визуальные системы с помощью основ визуального дизайна","ar":"ابني أنظمة بصرية متكاملة وسهلة الوصول مع أساسيات التصميم البصري","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["建立设计令牌","创建或完善间距和大小系统","选择和配对字体","构建可访问的颜色调色板","设计图标系统和视觉资产","改善视觉层次和可读性"],"ja":["デザイントークンを確立","間隔とサイズのシステムを作成または改善","フォントを選択してペアにする","アクセシブルなカラーパレットを構築","アイコンシステムと視覚的なアセットを設計","視覚的な階層と可読性を改善"],"ko":["디자인 토큰을 설정","간격과 크기 시스템을 생성 또는 개선","폰트를 선택하고 페어링","접근 가능한 색상 팔레트를 구축","아이콘 시스템과 시각적 자산을 설계","시각적 계층과 가독성을 개선"],"es":["Creación de tokens de diseño","Sistemas de espaciado y tamaño","Selección y emparejamiento de fuentes","Paletas de color accesibles","Diseño de sistemas de iconos","Mejora de la jerarquía visual y la legibilidad"],"fr":["Création de jetons de conception","Systèmes d''espacement et de taille","Sélection et appariement de polices","Palettes de couleurs accessibles","Conception de systèmes d''icônes","Amélioration de la hiérarchie visuelle et de la lisibilité"],"de":["Erstellung von Design-Tokens","Abstands- und Größensysteme","Auswahl und Kombination von Schriftarten","Zugängliche Farbpaletten","Entwurf von Ikonensystemen","Verbesserung der visuellen Hierarchie und Lesbarkeit"],"pt":["Tipografia","Cores e paletas","Espaçamento e tamanho","Iconografia e ativos visuais","Hierarquia visual e legibilidade","Modo escuro e temas"],"ru":["Типография","Цвета и палитры","Интервал и размер","Иконография и визуальные активы","Визуальная иерархия и читаемость","Темный режим и темы"],"ar":["الطباعة","الألوان والpalette","المسافة والحجم","الرموز والعناصر البصرية","الترتيب البصري والقراءة","الوضع الداكن والأشكال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["视觉设计","排版","颜色","间距","图标","设计令牌","可访问性","视觉系统"],"ja":["ビジュアルデザイン","フォント","カラー","間隔","アイコン","デザイントークン","アクセシビリティ","視覚システム"],"ko":["시각 디자인","폰트","색상","간격","아이콘","디자인 토큰","접근성","시각 시스템"],"es":["diseño visual","tipografía","color","espaciado","iconografía","accesibilidad","sistemas visuales","tokens de diseño","paletas de color"],"fr":["conception visuelle","typographie","couleur","espacement","icône","accessibilité","systèmes visuels","jetons de conception","palettes de couleurs"],"de":["visuelles Design","Typografie","Farbe","Abstand","Ikonografie","Zugänglichkeit","visuelle Systeme","Design-Tokens","Farbpaletten"],"pt":["design visual","tipografia","cor e paleta","espaçamento e tamanho","iconografia","acessibilidade","sistemas visuais","legibilidade","modo escuro"],"ru":["визуальный дизайн","типография","цвет и палитра","интервал и размер","иконография","доступность","визуальные системы","читаемость","темный режим"],"ar":["التصميم البصري","الطباعة","اللون والpalette","المسافة والحجم","الرموز","السهولة في الوصول","النظم البصرية","القراءة","الوضع الداكن"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"visual-design-foundations","description":"Apply typography, color theory, spacing systems, and iconography principles to create cohesive visual designs. Use when establishing design tokens, building style guides, or improving visual hierarchy and consistency.","bodyPreview":"# Visual Design Foundations\n\nBuild cohesive, accessible visual systems using typography, color, spacing, and iconography fundamentals.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Establishing design tokens for a new project\n- Creating or refining a spacing and sizing system\n- Selecting and pairing typefaces\n- Building accessible color palettes\n- Designing icon systems and visual assets\n- Improving visual hierarchy and readability\n- Auditing designs for visual consistency\n- Implementing dark mode or theming\n\n#","body":"# Visual Design Foundations\n\nBuild cohesive, accessible visual systems using typography, color, spacing, and iconography fundamentals.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Establishing design tokens for a new project\n- Creating or refining a spacing and sizing system\n- Selecting and pairing typefaces\n- Building accessible color palettes\n- Designing icon systems and visual assets\n- Improving visual hierarchy and readability\n- Auditing designs for visual consistency\n- Implementing dark mode or theming\n\n## Core Systems\n\n### 1. Typography Scale\n\n**Modular Scale** (ratio-based sizing):\n\n```css\n:root {\n  --font-size-xs: 0.75rem; /* 12px */\n  --font-size-sm: 0.875rem; /* 14px */\n  --font-size-base: 1rem; /* 16px */\n  --font-size-lg: 1.125rem; /* 18px */\n  --font-size-xl: 1.25rem; /* 20px */\n  --font-size-2xl: 1.5rem; /* 24px */\n  --font-size-3xl: 1.875rem; /* 30px */\n  --font-size-4xl: 2.25rem; /* 36px */\n  --font-size-5xl: 3rem; /* 48px */\n}\n```\n\n**Line Height Guidelines**:\n| Text Type | Line Height |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Headings | 1.1 - 1.3 |\n| Body text | 1.5 - 1.7 |\n| UI labels | 1.2 - 1.4 |\n\n### 2. Spacing System\n\n**8-point grid** (industry standard):\n\n```css\n:root {\n  --space-1: 0.25rem; /* 4px */\n  --space-2: 0.5rem; /* 8px */\n  --space-3: 0.75rem; /* 12px */\n  --space-4: 1rem; /* 16px */\n  --space-5: 1.25rem; /* 20px */\n  --space-6: 1.5rem; /* 24px */\n  --space-8: 2rem; /* 32px */\n  --space-10: 2.5rem; /* 40px */\n  --space-12: 3rem; /* 48px */\n  --space-16: 4rem; /* 64px */\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Color System\n\n**Semantic color tokens**:\n\n```css\n:root {\n  /* Brand */\n  --color-primary: #2563eb;\n  --color-primary-hover: #1d4ed8;\n  --color-primary-active: #1e40af;\n\n  /* Semantic */\n  --color-success: #16a34a;\n  --color-warning: #ca8a04;\n  --color-error: #dc2626;\n  --color-info: #0891b2;\n\n  /* Neutral */\n  --color-gray-50: #f9fafb;\n  --color-gray-100: #f3f4f6;\n  --color-gray-200: #e5e7eb;\n  --color-gray-300: #d1d5db;\n  --color-gray-400: #9ca3af;\n  --color-gray-500: #6b7280;\n  --color-gray-600: #4b5563;\n  --color-gray-700: #374151;\n  --color-gray-800: #1f2937;\n  --color-gray-900: #111827;\n}\n```\n\n## Quick Start: Design Tokens in Tailwind\n\n```js\n// tailwind.config.js\nmodule.exports = {\n  theme: {\n    extend: {\n      fontFamily: {\n        sans: [\"Inter\", \"system-ui\", \"sans-serif\"],\n        mono: [\"JetBrains Mono\", \"monospace\"],\n      },\n      fontSize: {\n        xs: [\"0.75rem\", { lineHeight: \"1rem\" }],\n        sm: [\"0.875rem\", { lineHeight: \"1.25rem\" }],\n        base: [\"1rem\", { lineHeight: \"1.5rem\" }],\n        lg: [\"1.125rem\", { lineHeight: \"1.75rem\" }],\n        xl: [\"1.25rem\", { lineHeight: \"1.75rem\" }],\n        \"2xl\": [\"1.5rem\", { lineHeight: \"2rem\" }],\n      },\n      colors: {\n        brand: {\n          50: \"#eff6ff\",\n          500: \"#3b82f6\",\n          600: \"#2563eb\",\n          700: \"#1d4ed8\",\n        },\n      },\n      spacing: {\n        // Extends default with custom values\n        18: \"4.5rem\",\n        88: \"22rem\",\n      },\n    },\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Typography Best Practices\n\n### Font Pairing\n\n**Safe combinations**:\n\n- Heading: **Inter** / Body: **Inter** (single family)\n- Heading: **Playfair Display** / Body: **Source Sans Pro** (contrast)\n- Heading: **Space Grotesk** / Body: **IBM Plex Sans** (geometric)\n\n### Responsive Typography\n\n```css\n/* Fluid typography using clamp() */\nh1 {\n  font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw + 1rem, 3.5rem);\n  line-height: 1.1;\n}\n\np {\n  font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw + 0.5rem, 1.125rem);\n  line-height: 1.6;\n  max-width: 65ch; /* Optimal reading width */\n}\n```\n\n### Font Loading\n\n```css\n/* Prevent layout shift */\n@font-face {\n  font-family: \"Inter\";\n  src: url(\"/fonts/Inter.woff2\") format(\"woff2\");\n  font-display: swap;\n  font-weight: 400 700;\n}\n```\n\n## Color Theory\n\n### Contrast Requirements (WCAG)\n\n| Element            | Minimum Ratio |\n| ------------------ | ------------- |\n| Body text          | 4.5:1 (AA)    |\n| Large text (18px+) | 3:1 (AA)      |\n| UI components      | 3:1 (AA)      |\n| Enhanced           | 7:1 (AAA)     |\n\n### Dark Mode Strategy\n\n```css\n:root {\n  --bg-primary: #ffffff;\n  --bg-secondary: #f9fafb;\n  --text-primary: #111827;\n  --text-secondary: #6b7280;\n  --border: #e5e7eb;\n}\n\n[data-theme=\"dark\"] {\n  --bg-primary: #111827;\n  --bg-secondary: #1f2937;\n  --text-primary: #f9fafb;\n  --text-secondary: #9ca3af;\n  --border: #374151;\n}\n```\n\n### Color Accessibility\n\n```tsx\n// Check contrast programmatically\nfunction getContrastRatio(foreground: string, background: string): number {\n  const getLuminance = (hex: string) => {\n    const rgb = hexToRgb(hex);\n    const [r, g, b] = rgb.map((c) => {\n      c = c / 255;\n      return c <= 0.03928 ? c / 12.92 : Math.pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, 2.4);\n    });\n    return 0.2126 * r + 0.7152 * g + 0.0722 * b;\n  };\n\n  const l1 = getLuminance(foreground);\n  const l2 = getLuminance(background);\n  const lighter = Math.max(l1, l2);\n  const darker = Math.min(l1, l2);\n\n  return (lighter + 0.05) / (darker + 0.05);\n}\n```\n\n## Spacing Guidelines\n\n### Component Spacing\n\n```\nCard padding:      16-24px (--space-4 to --space-6)\nSection gap:       32-64px (--space-8 to --space-16)\nForm field gap:    16-24px (--space-4 to --space-6)\nButton padding:    8-16px vertical, 16-24px horizontal\nIcon-text gap:     8px (--space-2)\n```\n\n### Visual Rhythm\n\n```css\n/* Consistent vertical rhythm */\n.prose > * + * {\n  margin-top: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n.prose > h2 + * {\n  margin-top: var(--space-2);\n}\n\n.prose > * + h2 {\n  margin-top: var(--space-8);\n}\n```\n\n## Iconography\n\n### Icon Sizing System\n\n```css\n:root {\n  --icon-xs: 12px;\n  --icon-sm: 16px;\n  --icon-md: 20px;\n  --icon-lg: 24px;\n  --icon-xl: 32px;\n}\n```\n\n### Icon Component\n\n```tsx\ninterface IconProps {\n  name: string;\n  size?: \"xs\" | \"sm\" | \"md\" | \"lg\" | \"xl\";\n  className?: string;\n}\n\nconst sizeMap = {\n  xs: 12,\n  sm: 16,\n  md: 20,\n  lg: 24,\n  xl: 32,\n};\n\nexport function Icon({ name, size = \"md\", className }: IconProps) {\n  return (\n    <svg\n      width={sizeMap[size]}\n      height={sizeMap[size]}\n      className={cn(\"inline-block flex-shrink-0\", className)}\n      aria-hidden=\"true\"\n    >\n      <use href={`/icons.svg#${name}`} />\n    </svg>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Establish Constraints**: Limit choices to maintain consistency\n2. **Document Decisions**: Create a living style guide\n3. **Test Accessibility**: Verify contrast, sizing, touch targets\n4. **Use Semantic Tokens**: Name by purpose, not appearance\n5. **Design Mobile-First**: Start with constraints, add complexity\n6. **Maintain Vertical Rhythm**: Consistent spacing creates harmony\n7. **Limit Font Weights**: 2-3 weights per family is sufficient\n\n## Common Issues\n\n- **Inconsistent Spacing**: Not using a defined scale\n- **Poor Contrast**: Failing WCAG requirements\n- **Font Overload**: Too many families or weights\n- **Magic Numbers**: Arbitrary values instead of tokens\n- **Missing States**: Forgetting hover, focus, disabled\n- **No Dark Mode Plan**: Retrofitting is harder than planning\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Tailwind CSS Documentation](https://tailwindcss.com/docs)\n- [Type Scale Calculator](https://typescale.com/)\n- [Contrast Checker](https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/)\n- [Material Design Color System](https://m3.material.io/styles/color/overview)\n- [Radix Colors](https://www.radix-ui.com/colors)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:19:11.766Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UI/UX Agents needing advanced visual design capabilities for typography, color, and spacing fundamentals.","zh":"非常适合需要高级视觉设计能力的UI/UX代理，特别是在排版、颜色和间距基本方面。","ja":"UI/UXエージェントがタイポグラフィ、色、間隔の基本的な視覚的なデザイン能力を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"タイポグラフィ、색상 및 여백 기본에 대한 고급 시각 디자인 기능이 필요한 UI/UX 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de UI/UX que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de diseño visual para fundamentos de tipografía, color y espaciado.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents UI/UX ayant besoin de capacités avancées en conception visuelle pour les fondamentaux de la typographie, de la couleur et de l''espacement.","de":"Perfekt für UI/UX-Agenten, die erweiterte Fähigkeiten im visuellen Design für die Grundlagen von Typografie, Farbe und Abständen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de UI/UX que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de design visual para fundamentos de tipografia, cor e espaçamento.","ru":"Идеально для агентов UI/UX, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности визуального дизайна для типографики, цвета и основ пространственного расположения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم / تجربة المستخدم الذي يحتاج إلى قابليات تصميم مرئي متقدم لأساسيات الطباعة ، واللون ، ومسافات التباعد."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create cohesive visual systems using design tokens, typography fundamentals, and accessible color palettes, while also implementing dark mode or theming using protocols like CSS and file formats like .svg.","zh":"赋予代理创建连贯的视觉系统的能力，使用设计令牌、排版基础和可访问的颜色调色板，同时使用CSS等协议和.svg等文件格式实现暗黑模式或主题。","ja":"デザイントークン、タイポグラフィの基礎、及びアクセシブルなカラーパレットを使用して一貫した視覚システムを作成するエージェントを可能にし、CSSなどのプロトコルと.svgなどのファイル形式を使用してダークモードまたはテーミングを実装します。","ko":"디자인 토큰, 타이포그래피 기본 및 접근 가능한 색상 팔레트를 사용하여 일관된 시각적 시스템을 생성 할 수있는 에이전트를 강화하며 CSS와 같은 프로토콜 및 .svg와 같은 파일 형식을 사용하여 다크 모드 또는 테마를 구현합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear sistemas visuales cohesivos utilizando tokens de diseño, fundamentos de tipografía y paletas de colores accesibles, además de implementar modo oscuro o tematización utilizando protocolos como CSS y formatos de archivo como .svg.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des systèmes visuels cohérents en utilisant des tokens de conception, les fondamentaux de la typographie et des palettes de couleurs accessibles, tout en implémentant le mode sombre ou le theming à l''aide de protocoles comme CSS et de formats de fichier comme .svg.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, kohärente visuelle Systeme mit Design-Tokens, Typografie-Grundlagen und barrierefreien Farbpaletten zu erstellen und dabei auch den Dunkelmodus oder Theming mit Protokollen wie CSS und Dateiformaten wie .svg zu implementieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem sistemas visuais coesos usando tokens de design, fundamentos de tipografia e paletas de cores acessíveis, além de implementar o modo escuro ou tema usando protocolos como CSS e formatos de arquivo como .svg.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать целостные визуальные системы с помощью дизайн-токенов, основ типографики и доступных цветовых палитр, а также реализовывать темный режим или темизацию с использованием протоколов như CSS и форматов файлов как .svg.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية إنشاء أنظمة مرئية متسقة باستخدام رموز التصميم وأسس الطباعة والرسومات الألوان المترجمة ، بالإضافة إلى تنفيذ الوضع الداكن أو التهيئة باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل CSS وتنسيقات الملفات مثل .svg."},"useCases":{"en":["Establishing design tokens for new projects","Generating accessible color palettes for web applications","Refining spacing and sizing systems for improved visual hierarchy"],"zh":["为新项目建立设计令牌","为Web应用程序生成可访问的颜色调色板","改进视觉层次结构的间距和尺寸系统"],"ja":["新規プロジェクトのためのデザイントークンの確立","Webアプリケーションのためのアクセシブルなカラーパレットの生成","視覚的な階層構造の向上のための間隔とサイズのシステムの改良"],"ko":["새로운 프로젝트를 위한 디자인 토큰의 설정","웹 애플리케이션을 위한 접근 가능한 색상 팔레트 생성","시각적 계층 구조 개선을 위한 간격 및 크기 시스템의 개선"],"es":["Establecer tokens de diseño para nuevos proyectos","Generar paletas de colores accesibles para aplicaciones web","Refinar sistemas de espaciado y dimensionamiento para mejorar la jerarquía visual"],"fr":["Établir des tokens de conception pour de nouveaux projets","Générer des palettes de couleurs accessibles pour des applications web","Affiner les systèmes d''espacement et de dimensionnement pour améliorer la hiérarchie visuelle"],"de":["Etablieren von Design-Tokens für neue Projekte","Erzeugen barrierefreier Farbpaletten für Webanwendungen","Verfeinern von Abstands- und Größensystemen zur Verbesserung der visuellen Hierarchie"],"pt":["Estabelecer tokens de design para novos projetos","Gerar paletas de cores acessíveis para aplicações web","Aperfeiçoar sistemas de espaçamento e dimensionamento para melhor hierarquia visual"],"ru":["Установка токенов дизайна для новых проектов","Генерация доступных цветовых палитр для веб-приложений","Уточнение систем间距 и размеров для улучшения визуальной иерархии"],"ar":["تحديد رموز التصميم لمشاريع جديدة","genera paletas الألوان المترجمة للتطبيقات الويب","تحسين أنظمة المسافات والحجم لتحسين التسلسل الهرمي المرئي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of design principles and human-computer interaction","Limited to visual design applications, not suitable for backend development"],"zh":["需要设计原则和人机交互的知识","仅限于视觉设计应用，不适合后端开发"],"ja":["デザインの原則と人間コンピュータ相互作用の知識が必要","視覚的なデザインアプリケーションに限定され、バックエンド開発には適していない"],"ko":["디자인 원칙 및 인간-컴퓨터 상호 작용에 대한 지식이 필요","시각적 디자인 애플리케이션에만 국한되며 백엔드 개발에는 적합하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere conocimientos de principios de diseño e interacción humano-computadora","Limitado a aplicaciones de diseño visual, no es adecuado para desarrollo backend"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des principes de conception et de l''interaction homme-machine","Limité aux applications de conception visuelle, ne convient pas au développement backend"],"de":["Erfordert Kenntnisse in Designprinzipien und Mensch-Computer-Interaktion","Beschränkt auf Anwendungen im visuellen Design, nicht geeignet für Backend-Entwicklung"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de princípios de design e interação homem-computador","Limitado a aplicações de design visual, não adequado para desenvolvimento backend"],"ru":["Требует знания принципов дизайна и взаимодействия человека с компьютером","Ограничен для приложений визуального дизайна, не подходит для разработки бэкенда"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة مبادئ التصميم والتفاعل بين الإنسان والحاسوب","محدود للتطبيقات التصميم المرئي ، وليس مناسبا لتنمية الخلفية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('LeeCuongg/stock-flow-qt-food/vercel-composition-patterns', 'community', 'LeeCuongg', 'stock-flow-qt-food', 'LeeCuongg/stock-flow-qt-food', 'vercel-composition-patterns', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:19:38.414Z', NULL, '{"id":"LeeCuongg/stock-flow-qt-food/vercel-composition-patterns","name":"vercel-composition-patterns","description":{"zh":"Vercel组合模式提供了一种构建灵活、可维护的React组件的方法，通过避免布尔属性过度膨胀","ja":"Vercelコンポジションパターンは、柔軟でメンテナンス可能なReactコンポーネントを構築する方法を提供","ko":"버셀 컴포지션 패턴은 유연하고 유지 보수 가능한 리액트 컴포넌트를 구축하는 방법을 제공","es":"Los patrones de composición de Vercel permiten crear componentes de React flexibles y mantenibles. Evita la proliferación de propiedades booleanas con componentes compuestos y estado elevado.","fr":"Les modèles de composition Vercel permettent de créer des composants React flexibles et maintenables. Évitez la prolifération des propriétés booléennes avec des composants composés et un état élevé.","de":"Die Vercel-Zusammensetzungs-Muster ermöglichen die Erstellung flexibler und wartbarer React-Komponenten. Vermeiden Sie die Ausbreitung von booleschen Eigenschaften mit zusammengesetzten Komponenten und angehobenem Zustand.","pt":"Padrões de composição para construir componentes React flexíveis e manuteníveis.","ru":"Шаблоны композиции для построения гибких и поддерживаемых компонентов React.","ar":"نماذج التكوين لبناء مكونات React مرنة وقابلة للصيانة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Vercel组合模式：构建灵活React组件","ja":"Vercelコンポジションパターン：柔軟なReactコンポーネントを構築","ko":"버셀 컴포지션 패턴: 유연한 리액트 컴포넌트 구축","es":"Patrones de composición de Vercel para React","fr":"Modèles de composition Vercel pour React","de":"Vercel-Zusammensetzungs-Muster für React","pt":"Padrões de Composição Vercel para React","ru":"Шаблоны композиции Vercel для React","ar":"نماذج التكوين Vercel ل React","en":"vercel-composition-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"Vercel组合模式提供了一种构建灵活、可维护的React组件的方法，通过避免布尔属性过度膨胀","ja":"Vercelコンポジションパターンは、柔軟でメンテナンス可能なReactコンポーネントを構築する方法を提供","ko":"버셀 컴포지션 패턴은 유연하고 유지 보수 가능한 리액트 컴포넌트를 구축하는 방법을 제공","es":"Los patrones de composición de Vercel permiten crear componentes de React flexibles y mantenibles. Evita la proliferación de propiedades booleanas con compon...","fr":"Les modèles de composition Vercel permettent de créer des composants React flexibles et maintenables. Évitez la prolifération des propriétés booléennes avec ...","de":"Die Vercel-Zusammensetzungs-Muster ermöglichen die Erstellung flexibler und wartbarer React-Komponenten. Vermeiden Sie die Ausbreitung von booleschen Eigensc...","pt":"Padrões de composição para construir componentes React flexíveis e manuteníveis.","ru":"Шаблоны композиции для построения гибких и поддерживаемых компонентов React.","ar":"نماذج التكوين لبناء مكونات React مرنة وقابلة للصيانة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["避免布尔属性过度膨胀","使用复合组件","提升状态","组合内部组件","构建可维护的代码库","提高代码可读性"],"ja":["ブール属性の増加を避ける","コンポジットコンポーネントを使用","ステートを昇格する","内部コンポーネントを合成する","メンテナンス可能なコードベースを構築","コードの可読性を向上させる"],"ko":["불리언 속성의 증가를 방지","합성 컴포넌트 사용","상태 상승","내부 컴포넌트 합성","유지 보수 가능한 코드베이스 구축","코드의 가독성을 향상"],"es":["Componentes compuestos","Estado elevado","Composición de internos","Evitación de la proliferación de propiedades booleanas","Código más legible y mantenible","Mejora de la escalabilidad"],"fr":["Composants composés","État élevé","Composition d''internes","Évitement de la prolifération des propriétés booléennes","Code plus lisible et maintenable","Amélioration de la mise à l''échelle"],"de":["Zusammengesetzte Komponenten","Angehobener Zustand","Zusammensetzung von Interna","Vermeidung der Ausbreitung von booleschen Eigenschaften","Bessere Lesbarkeit und Wartbarkeit des Codes","Verbesserung der Skalierbarkeit"],"pt":["Componentes compostos","Elevação de estado","Composição de internos","Evitar propriedades booleanas","Criação de bibliotecas de componentes reutilizáveis","Design de APIs de componentes flexíveis"],"ru":["Составные компоненты","Подъем состояния","Композиция внутренних компонентов","Избегание булевых свойств","Создание библиотек повторно используемых компонентов","Проектирование гибких API компонентов"],"ar":["المكونات المركبة","رفع الحالة","تكوين المكونات الداخلية","تجنب الخواص المنطقية","إنشاء مكتبات المكونات القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","تصميم واجهات برمجة تطبيقات المكونات المرنة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Vercel组合模式","React组件设计","灵活组件","可维护代码","布尔属性过度膨胀","复合组件","状态提升","组合内部组件"],"ja":["Vercelコンポジションパターン","Reactコンポーネント設計","柔軟なコンポーネント","メンテナンス可能なコード","ブール属性の増加","コンポジットコンポーネント","ステートの昇格","内部コンポーネントの合成"],"ko":["버셀 컴포지션 패턴","리액트 컴포넌트 디자인","유연한 컴포넌트","유지 보수 가능한 코드","불리언 속성의 증가","합성 컴포넌트","상태 상승","내부 컴포넌트 합성"],"es":["patrones de composición de Vercel","React","componentes flexibles","mantenimiento de código","escalabilidad","desarrollo de software","programación","JavaScript"],"fr":["modèles de composition Vercel","React","composants flexibles","maintenance de code","mise à l''échelle","développement de logiciels","programmation","JavaScript"],"de":["Vercel-Zusammensetzungs-Muster","React","flexible Komponenten","Code-Wartung","Skalierbarkeit","Software-Entwicklung","Programmierung","JavaScript"],"pt":["React Composition Patterns","Componentes React flexíveis","Manutenção de componentes","Padrões de composição","Componentes compostos","Elevação de estado","Desenvolvimento de software","Engenharia de software"],"ru":["Шаблоны композиции React","Гибкие компоненты React","Поддержка компонентов","Шаблоны композиции","Составные компоненты","Подъем состояния","Разработка программного обеспечения","Инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["نماذج التكوين React","مكونات React مرنة","صيانة المكونات","نماذج التكوين","المكونات المركبة","رفع الحالة","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"LeeCuongg","repo":"stock-flow-qt-food","repoPath":"LeeCuongg/stock-flow-qt-food","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vercel-composition-patterns","description":"","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# React Composition Patterns\n\nComposition patterns for building flexible, maintainable React components. Avoid\nboolean prop proliferation by using compound components, lifting state, and\ncomposing internals. These patterns make codebases easier for both humans and AI\nagents to work with as they scale.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Refactoring components with many boolean props\n- Building reusable component libraries\n- Designing flexible component APIs\n- Reviewing compone","body":"# React Composition Patterns\n\nComposition patterns for building flexible, maintainable React components. Avoid\nboolean prop proliferation by using compound components, lifting state, and\ncomposing internals. These patterns make codebases easier for both humans and AI\nagents to work with as they scale.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Refactoring components with many boolean props\n- Building reusable component libraries\n- Designing flexible component APIs\n- Reviewing component architecture\n- Working with compound components or context providers\n\n## Rule Categories by Priority\n\n| Priority | Category                | Impact | Prefix          |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ------ | --------------- |\n| 1        | Component Architecture  | HIGH   | `architecture-` |\n| 2        | State Management        | MEDIUM | `state-`        |\n| 3        | Implementation Patterns | MEDIUM | `patterns-`     |\n| 4        | React 19 APIs           | MEDIUM | `react19-`      |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### 1. Component Architecture (HIGH)\n\n- `architecture-avoid-boolean-props` - Don''t add boolean props to customize\n  behavior; use composition\n- `architecture-compound-components` - Structure complex components with shared\n  context\n\n### 2. State Management (MEDIUM)\n\n- `state-decouple-implementation` - Provider is the only place that knows how\n  state is managed\n- `state-context-interface` - Define generic interface with state, actions, meta\n  for dependency injection\n- `state-lift-state` - Move state into provider components for sibling access\n\n### 3. Implementation Patterns (MEDIUM)\n\n- `patterns-explicit-variants` - Create explicit variant components instead of\n  boolean modes\n- `patterns-children-over-render-props` - Use children for composition instead\n  of renderX props\n\n### 4. React 19 APIs (MEDIUM)\n\n> **⚠️ React 19+ only.** Skip this section if using React 18 or earlier.\n\n- `react19-no-forwardref` - Don''t use `forwardRef`; use `use()` instead of `useContext()`\n\n## How to Use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and code examples:\n\n```\nrules/architecture-avoid-boolean-props.md\nrules/state-context-interface.md\n```\n\nEach rule file contains:\n\n- Brief explanation of why it matters\n- Incorrect code example with explanation\n- Correct code example with explanation\n- Additional context and references\n\n## Full Compiled Document\n\nFor the complete guide with all rules expanded: `AGENTS.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:19:38.414Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing advanced React component composition and state management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 React 组件组合和状态管理能力的前端代理。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントが高度な React コンポーネントの構成と状態管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 React 컴포넌트 구성 및 상태 관리 기능이 필요한 프런트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de composición de componentes y gestión de estado de React.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin de capacités avancées de composition de composants et de gestion d''état React.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die erweiterte React-Komponenten-Zusammensetzung und Statusverwaltungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de composição e gerenciamento de estado de componentes React.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности композиции и управления состоянием компонентов React.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الأمامي التي تحتاج إلى سمات متقدمة لتركيبات وتحكم حالة مكونات React."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build flexible and maintainable React components by utilizing compound components, lifting state, and composing internals, making codebases easier to scale and maintain with features like boolean prop proliferation avoidance and reusable component libraries.","zh":"通过利用复合组件、提升状态和组成内部，实现构建灵活且易于维护的 React 组件，使代码库更容易扩展和维护，并具有布尔属性扩散避免和可重用组件库等功能。","ja":"複合コンポーネント、状態の昇格、内部の構成を利用することで、柔軟かつ保守可能な React コンポーネントを構築し、コードベースをスケールしやすく保守しやすくする機能を提供します。ブール値のプロパティの拡散の回避や再利用可能なコンポーネント ライブラリなど。","ko":"복합 컴포넌트, 상태 상승, 내부 구성 등을 활용하여 유연하고 유지 보수하기 쉬운 React 컴포넌트를 구축함으로써 코드베이스를 확장하고 유지 보수하기 쉽게 만들며, 불리언 속성 확산 방지 및 재사용 가능한 컴포넌트 라이브러리 등의 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear componentes de React flexibles y mantenibles mediante el uso de componentes compuestos, elevación de estado y composición de elementos internos, lo que hace que las bases de código sean más fáciles de escalar y mantener con características como la evitación de la proliferación de propiedades booleanas y bibliotecas de componentes reutilizables.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des composants React flexibles et maintenables en utilisant des composants composés, en soulevant l''état et en composant les éléments internes, ce qui rend les bases de code plus faciles à mettre à l''échelle et à maintenir avec des fonctionnalités comme l''évitement de la prolifération des propriétés booléennes et les bibliothèques de composants réutilisables.","de":"Ermöglich es den Agenten, flexible und wartbare React-Komponenten zu erstellen, indem sie zusammengesetzte Komponenten, Statusanhebung und Zusammensetzung von Interna nutzen, wodurch Codebasen einfacher zu skalieren und zu warten sind, mit Funktionen wie der Vermeidung der Ausbreitung von booleschen Eigenschaften und wiederverwendbaren Komponentenbibliotheken.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir componentes React flexíveis e mantenedores, utilizando componentes compostos, elevando o estado e compondo internos, tornando as bases de código mais fáceis de dimensionar e manter com recursos como evasão de proliferação de propriedades booleanas e bibliotecas de componentes reutilizáveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать гибкие и поддерживаемые компоненты React, используя составные компоненты, подъем состояния и компоновку внутренних компонентов, что делает кодовые базы более легкими в масштабировании и поддержке с функциями, такими как избежание распространения булевых свойств и библиотеки повторно используемых компонентов.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من بناء مكونات React مرنة وقابلة للصيانة من خلال استخدام المكونات المركبة ورفع الحالة وتركيب الداخلي، مما يجعلهم يسهل توسيعها وضبطها مع الميزات مثل تجنب انتشار الخواص المنطقية وقواعد المكونات القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام."},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring components with multiple boolean props","Building reusable component libraries with flexible APIs","Designing component architectures that scale with compound components"],"zh":["重构具有多个布尔属性的组件","使用灵活的 API 构建可重用组件库","使用复合组件设计可扩展的组件架构"],"ja":["複数のブール値プロパティを持つコンポーネントのリファクタリング","柔軟な API を使用した再利用可能なコンポーネント ライブラリの構築","複合コンポーネントを使用したスケーラブルなコンポーネント アーキテクチャの設計"],"ko":["여러 개의 불리언 속성을 가진 컴포넌트의 리팩토링","유연한 API를 사용한 재사용 가능한 컴포넌트 라이브러리의 구축","복합 컴포넌트를 사용한 확장 가능한 컴포넌트 아키텍처의 설계"],"es":["Reestructuración de componentes con varias propiedades booleanas","Creación de bibliotecas de componentes reutilizables con APIs flexibles","Diseño de arquitecturas de componentes que se escalan con componentes compuestos"],"fr":["Réorganisation de composants avec plusieurs propriétés booléennes","Création de bibliothèques de composants réutilisables avec des API flexibles","Conception d''architectures de composants qui s''adaptent avec des composants composés"],"de":["Umstrukturierung von Komponenten mit mehreren booleschen Eigenschaften","Erstellung von wiederverwendbaren Komponentenbibliotheken mit flexiblen APIs","Entwurf von Komponentenarchitekturen, die mit zusammengesetzten Komponenten skaliert werden"],"pt":["Reestruturação de componentes com várias propriedades booleanas","Construção de bibliotecas de componentes reutilizáveis com APIs flexíveis","Projeto de arquiteturas de componentes que dimensionam com componentes compostos"],"ru":["Рефакторинг компонентов с несколькими булевыми свойствами","Построение библиотек повторно используемых компонентов с гибкими API","Проектирование архитектур компонентов, которые масштабируются с составными компонентами"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة المكونات ذات الخواص المنطقية المتعددة","بناء مكتبات المكونات القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام مع واجهات برمجة تطبيقات مرنة","تصميم هندسة المكونات التي يمكن توسيعها مع المكونات المركبة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React component development context","Focused on React composition patterns, not applicable to other frontend frameworks"],"zh":["需要 React 组件开发的上下文","专注于 React 组合模式，不适用于其他前端框架"],"ja":["React コンポーネントの開発コンテキストが必要","React の構成パターンに焦点を当てており、他のフロントエンド フレームワークには適用できない"],"ko":["React 컴포넌트 개발의 컨텍스트가 필요","React의 구성 패턴에 초점을 맞추고 있으며 다른 프론트엔드 프레임워크에는 적용할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere contexto de desarrollo de componentes de React","Se centra en patrones de composición de React, no aplicable a otros frameworks de frontend"],"fr":["Nécessite un contexte de développement de composants React","Se concentre sur les modèles de composition React, non applicable à d''autres frameworks frontend"],"de":["Benötigt Kontext für die Entwicklung von React-Komponenten","Konzentriert sich auf React-Zusammensetzungsmodelle, nicht anwendbar auf andere Frontend-Frameworks"],"pt":["Requer contexto de desenvolvimento de componentes React","Focado em padrões de composição React, não aplicável a outros frameworks de frontend"],"ru":["Требует контекста разработки компонентов React","Сосредоточен на паттернах композиции React, не применим к другим фронтенд-фреймворкам"],"ar":["يتطلب سياق تطوير مكونات React","مركز على أنماط تركيب React، لا ينطبق على إطارات أمامية أخرى"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/postgresql-table-design', 'community', 'yashvinthan', 'DuskSpendr', 'yashvinthan/DuskSpendr', 'postgresql-table-design', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:19:45.214Z', NULL, '{"id":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/postgresql-table-design","name":"postgresql-table-design","description":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计是数据库性能优化的关键，了解如何定义主键、规范化和反规范化表设计","ja":"PostgreSQLテーブル設計はデータベースのパフォーマンスを最適化するために重要です。主キーを定義し、正規化と反正規化のテーブル設計を理解しましょう","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 설계는 데이터베이스 성능 최적화를 위한 핵심입니다. 주キー 정의, 정규화 및 비정규화에 대해 알아보세요","es":"Aprende a diseñar tablas PostgreSQL de manera efectiva para mejorar el rendimiento y la escalabilidad de tus bases de datos","fr":"Découvrez comment concevoir des tables PostgreSQL de manière efficace pour améliorer les performances et la scalabilité de vos bases de données","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie PostgreSQL-Tabellen effektiv entwerfen, um die Leistung und Skalierbarkeit Ihrer Datenbanken zu verbessern","pt":"O design de tabela PostgreSQL envolve a definição de chaves primárias e a normalização para eliminar a redundância de dados.","ru":"Дизайн таблицы PostgreSQL включает определение первичных ключей и нормализацию для исключения избыточности данных.","ar":"تصميم جدول PostgreSQL يتضمن تعريف المفاتيح الأساسية والتنسيق لإزالة التكرار في البيانات","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计最佳实践","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計のベストプラクティス","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 설계 최적화","es":"Diseño de Tablas PostgreSQL","fr":"Conception de Tables PostgreSQL","de":"PostgreSQL-Tabellendesign","pt":"Design de Tabela PostgreSQL: Melhores Práticas","ru":"Дизайн таблицы PostgreSQL: лучшие практики","ar":"تصميم جدول PostgreSQL: أفضل الممارسات","en":"postgresql-table-design"},"description":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计是数据库性能优化的关键，了解如何定义主键、规范化和反规范化表设计","ja":"PostgreSQLテーブル設計はデータベースのパフォーマンスを最適化するために重要です。主キーを定義し、正規化と反正規化のテーブル設計を理解しましょう","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 설계는 데이터베이스 성능 최적화를 위한 핵심입니다. 주キー 정의, 정규화 및 비정규화에 대해 알아보세요","es":"Aprende a diseñar tablas PostgreSQL de manera efectiva para mejorar el rendimiento y la escalabilidad de tus bases de datos","fr":"Découvrez comment concevoir des tables PostgreSQL de manière efficace pour améliorer les performances et la scalabilité de vos bases de données","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie PostgreSQL-Tabellen effektiv entwerfen, um die Leistung und Skalierbarkeit Ihrer Datenbanken zu verbessern","pt":"O design de tabela PostgreSQL envolve a definição de chaves primárias e a normalização para eliminar a redundância de dados.","ru":"Дизайн таблицы PostgreSQL включает определение первичных ключей и нормализацию для исключения избыточности данных.","ar":"تصميم جدول PostgreSQL يتضمن تعريف المفاتيح الأساسية والتنسيق لإزالة التكرار في البيانات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["定义主键","规范化表设计","反规范化表设计","使用BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","使用UUID保证全局唯一性","优化查询性能"],"ja":["主キーを定義する","テーブル設計の正規化","テーブル設計の反正規化","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITYを使用する","UUIDを使用して全局的一意性を保証する","クエリのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["주키 정의","테이블 설계의 정규화","테이블 설계의 비정규화","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY 사용","UUID 사용하여 전역 고유성 보장","쿼리 성능 최적화"],"es":["Definir claves primarias para tablas de referencia","Normalizar datos para eliminar redundancias","Denormalizar datos para mejorar el rendimiento de lectura","Utilizar BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY para claves primarias","Utilizar UUID para garantizar la unicidad global"],"fr":["Définir des clés primaires pour les tables de référence","Normaliser les données pour éliminer les redondances","Dénormaliser les données pour améliorer les performances de lecture","Utiliser BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY pour les clés primaires","Utiliser UUID pour garantir l''unicité globale"],"de":["Definieren von Primärschlüsseln für Referenztabelle","Normalisieren von Daten zum Eliminieren von Redundanz","Denormalisieren von Daten zur Verbesserung der Leseleistung","Verwenden von BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY für Primärschlüssel","Verwenden von UUID zur Gewährleistung der globalen Eindeutigkeit"],"pt":["Definição de chave primária","Normalização para eliminar redundância de dados","Denormalização para melhorar o desempenho","Uso de BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","Uso de UUID para garantir a singularidade global","Otimização do desempenho de leitura"],"ru":["Определение первичного ключа","Нормализация для исключения избыточности данных","Денормализация для улучшения производительности","Использование BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","Использование UUID для обеспечения глобальной уникальности","Оптимизация производительности чтения"],"ar":["تعريف المفتاح الأساسي","التنسيق لإزالة التكرار في البيانات","إزالة التنسيق لتحسين الأداء","استخدام BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","استخدام UUID لضمان الفردية العالمية","تحسين أداء القراءة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PostgreSQL 表设计","数据库性能优化","主键设计","规范化","反规范化","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","查询性能优化"],"ja":["PostgreSQLテーブル設計","データベースのパフォーマンスを最適化する","主キー設計","正規化","反正規化","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","クエリのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 테이블 설계","데이터베이스 성능 최적화","주키 설계","정규화","비정규화","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","쿼리 성능 최적화"],"es":["diseño de tablas postgresql","normalización de datos","denormalización de datos","claves primarias","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","bases de datos relacionales","rendimiento de bases de datos"],"fr":["conception de tables postgresql","normalisation de données","dénormalisation de données","clés primaires","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","bases de données relationnelles","performances de bases de données"],"de":["PostgreSQL-Tabellendesign","Datennormalisierung","Daten-denormalisierung","Primärschlüssel","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","relationale Datenbanken","Datenbankleistung"],"pt":["design de tabela postgresql","chave primária","normalização","denormalização","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","otimização de desempenho","leitura de banco de dados"],"ru":["дизайн таблицы postgresql","первичный ключ","нормализация","денормализация","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","оптимизация производительности","чтение базы данных"],"ar":["تصميم جدول postgresql","المفتاح الأساسي","التنسيق","إزالة التنسيق","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","تحسين الأداء","قراءة قاعدة البيانات"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"postgresql-table-design","description":"Design a PostgreSQL-specific schema. Covers best-practices, data types, indexing, constraints, performance patterns, and advanced features","bodyPreview":"# PostgreSQL Table Design\n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenanc","body":"# PostgreSQL Table Design\n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenance burden.\n- Add **NOT NULL** everywhere it’s semantically required; use **DEFAULT**s for common values.\n- Create **indexes for access paths you actually query**: PK/unique (auto), **FK columns (manual!)**, frequent filters/sorts, and join keys.\n- Prefer **TIMESTAMPTZ** for event time; **NUMERIC** for money; **TEXT** for strings; **BIGINT** for integer values, **DOUBLE PRECISION** for floats (or `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic).\n\n## PostgreSQL “Gotchas”\n\n- **Identifiers**: unquoted → lowercased. Avoid quoted/mixed-case names. Convention: use `snake_case` for table/column names.\n- **Unique + NULLs**: UNIQUE allows multiple NULLs. Use `UNIQUE (...) NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+) to restrict to one NULL.\n- **FK indexes**: PostgreSQL **does not** auto-index FK columns. Add them.\n- **No silent coercions**: length/precision overflows error out (no truncation). Example: inserting 999 into `NUMERIC(2,0)` fails with error, unlike some databases that silently truncate or round.\n- **Sequences/identity have gaps** (normal; don''t \"fix\"). Rollbacks, crashes, and concurrent transactions create gaps in ID sequences (1, 2, 5, 6...). This is expected behavior—don''t try to make IDs consecutive.\n- **Heap storage**: no clustered PK by default (unlike SQL Server/MySQL InnoDB); `CLUSTER` is one-off reorganization, not maintained on subsequent inserts. Row order on disk is insertion order unless explicitly clustered.\n- **MVCC**: updates/deletes leave dead tuples; vacuum handles them—design to avoid hot wide-row churn.\n\n## Data Types\n\n- **IDs**: `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` preferred (`GENERATED BY DEFAULT` also fine); `UUID` when merging/federating/used in a distributed system or for opaque IDs. Generate with `uuidv7()` (preferred if using PG18+) or `gen_random_uuid()` (if using an older PG version).\n- **Integers**: prefer `BIGINT` unless storage space is critical; `INTEGER` for smaller ranges; avoid `SMALLINT` unless constrained.\n- **Floats**: prefer `DOUBLE PRECISION` over `REAL` unless storage space is critical. Use `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic.\n- **Strings**: prefer `TEXT`; if length limits needed, use `CHECK (LENGTH(col) <= n)` instead of `VARCHAR(n)`; avoid `CHAR(n)`. Use `BYTEA` for binary data. Large strings/binary (>2KB default threshold) automatically stored in TOAST with compression. TOAST storage: `PLAIN` (no TOAST), `EXTENDED` (compress + out-of-line), `EXTERNAL` (out-of-line, no compress), `MAIN` (compress, keep in-line if possible). Default `EXTENDED` usually optimal. Control with `ALTER TABLE tbl ALTER COLUMN col SET STORAGE strategy` and `ALTER TABLE tbl SET (toast_tuple_target = 4096)` for threshold. Case-insensitive: for locale/accent handling use non-deterministic collations; for plain ASCII use expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` (preferred unless column needs case-insensitive PK/FK/UNIQUE) or `CITEXT`.\n- **Money**: `NUMERIC(p,s)` (never float).\n- **Time**: `TIMESTAMPTZ` for timestamps; `DATE` for date-only; `INTERVAL` for durations. Avoid `TIMESTAMP` (without timezone). Use `now()` for transaction start time, `clock_timestamp()` for current wall-clock time.\n- **Booleans**: `BOOLEAN` with `NOT NULL` constraint unless tri-state values are required.\n- **Enums**: `CREATE TYPE ... AS ENUM` for small, stable sets (e.g. US states, days of week). For business-logic-driven and evolving values (e.g. order statuses) → use TEXT (or INT) + CHECK or lookup table.\n- **Arrays**: `TEXT[]`, `INTEGER[]`, etc. Use for ordered lists where you query elements. Index with **GIN** for containment (`@>`, `<@`) and overlap (`&&`) queries. Access: `arr[1]` (1-indexed), `arr[1:3]` (slicing). Good for tags, categories; avoid for relations—use junction tables instead. Literal syntax: `''{val1,val2}''` or `ARRAY[val1,val2]`.\n- **Range types**: `daterange`, `numrange`, `tstzrange` for intervals. Support overlap (`&&`), containment (`@>`), operators. Index with **GiST**. Good for scheduling, versioning, numeric ranges. Pick a bounds scheme and use it consistently; prefer `[)` (inclusive/exclusive) by default.\n- **Network types**: `INET` for IP addresses, `CIDR` for network ranges, `MACADDR` for MAC addresses. Support network operators (`<<`, `>>`, `&&`).\n- **Geometric types**: `POINT`, `LINE`, `POLYGON`, `CIRCLE` for 2D spatial data. Index with **GiST**. Consider **PostGIS** for advanced spatial features.\n- **Text search**: `TSVECTOR` for full-text search documents, `TSQUERY` for search queries. Index `tsvector` with **GIN**. Always specify language: `to_tsvector(''english'', col)` and `to_tsquery(''english'', ''query'')`. Never use single-argument versions. This applies to both index expressions and queries.\n- **Domain types**: `CREATE DOMAIN email AS TEXT CHECK (VALUE ~ ''^[^@]+@[^@]+$'')` for reusable custom types with validation. Enforces constraints across tables.\n- **Composite types**: `CREATE TYPE address AS (street TEXT, city TEXT, zip TEXT)` for structured data within columns. Access with `(col).field` syntax.\n- **JSONB**: preferred over JSON; index with **GIN**. Use only for optional/semi-structured attrs. ONLY use JSON if the original ordering of the contents MUST be preserved.\n- **Vector types**: `vector` type by `pgvector` for vector similarity search for embeddings.\n\n### Do not use the following data types\n\n- DO NOT use `timestamp` (without time zone); DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `char(n)` or `varchar(n)`; DO use `text` instead.\n- DO NOT use `money` type; DO use `numeric` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timetz` type; DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timestamptz(0)` or any other precision specification; DO use `timestamptz` instead\n- DO NOT use `serial` type; DO use `generated always as identity` instead.\n\n## Table Types\n\n- **Regular**: default; fully durable, logged.\n- **TEMPORARY**: session-scoped, auto-dropped, not logged. Faster for scratch work.\n- **UNLOGGED**: persistent but not crash-safe. Faster writes; good for caches/staging.\n\n## Row-Level Security\n\nEnable with `ALTER TABLE tbl ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`. Create policies: `CREATE POLICY user_access ON orders FOR SELECT TO app_users USING (user_id = current_user_id())`. Built-in user-based access control at the row level.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **PK**: implicit UNIQUE + NOT NULL; creates a B-tree index.\n- **FK**: specify `ON DELETE/UPDATE` action (`CASCADE`, `RESTRICT`, `SET NULL`, `SET DEFAULT`). Add explicit index on referencing column—speeds up joins and prevents locking issues on parent deletes/updates. Use `DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED` for circular FK dependencies checked at transaction end.\n- **UNIQUE**: creates a B-tree index; allows multiple NULLs unless `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+). Standard behavior: `(1, NULL)` and `(1, NULL)` are allowed. With `NULLS NOT DISTINCT`: only one `(1, NULL)` allowed. Prefer `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` unless you specifically need duplicate NULLs.\n- **CHECK**: row-local constraints; NULL values pass the check (three-valued logic). Example: `CHECK (price > 0)` allows NULL prices. Combine with `NOT NULL` to enforce: `price NUMERIC NOT NULL CHECK (price > 0)`.\n- **EXCLUDE**: prevents overlapping values using operators. `EXCLUDE USING gist (room_id WITH =, booking_period WITH &&)` prevents double-booking rooms. Requires appropriate index type (often GiST).\n\n## Indexing\n\n- **B-tree**: default for equality/range queries (`=`, `<`, `>`, `BETWEEN`, `ORDER BY`)\n- **Composite**: order matters—index used if equality on leftmost prefix (`WHERE a = ? AND b > ?` uses index on `(a,b)`, but `WHERE b = ?` does not). Put most selective/frequently filtered columns first.\n- **Covering**: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (id) INCLUDE (name, email)` - includes non-key columns for index-only scans without visiting table.\n- **Partial**: for hot subsets (`WHERE status = ''active''` → `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (user_id) WHERE status = ''active''`). Any query with `status = ''active''` can use this index.\n- **Expression**: for computed search keys (`CREATE INDEX ON tbl (LOWER(email))`). Expression must match exactly in WHERE clause: `WHERE LOWER(email) = ''user@example.com''`.\n- **GIN**: JSONB containment/existence, arrays (`@>`, `?`), full-text search (`@@`)\n- **GiST**: ranges, geometry, exclusion constraints\n- **BRIN**: very large, naturally ordered data (time-series)—minimal storage overhead. Effective when row order on disk correlates with indexed column (insertion order or after `CLUSTER`).\n\n## Partitioning\n\n- Use for very large tables (>100M rows) where queries consistently filter on partition key (often time/date).\n- Alternate use: use for tables where data maintenance tasks dictates e.g. data pruned or bulk replaced periodically\n- **RANGE**: common for time-series (`PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at)`). Create partitions: `CREATE TABLE logs_2024_01 PARTITION OF logs FOR VALUES FROM (''2024-01-01'') TO (''2024-02-01'')`. **TimescaleDB** automates time-based or ID-based partitioning with retention policies and compression.\n- **LIST**: for discrete values (`PARTITION BY LIST (region)`). Example: `FOR VALUES IN (''us-east'', ''us-west'')`.\n- **HASH**: for even distribution when no natural key (`PARTITION BY HASH (user_id)`). Creates N partitions with modulus.\n- **Constraint exclusion**: requires `CHECK` constraints on partitions for query planner to prune. Auto-created for declarative partitioning (PG10+).\n- Prefer declarative partitioning or hypertables. Do NOT use table inheritance.\n- **Limitations**: no global UNIQUE constraints—include partition key in PK/UNIQUE. FKs from partitioned tables not supported; use triggers.\n\n## Special Considerations\n\n### Update-Heavy Tables\n\n- **Separate hot/cold columns**—put frequently updated columns in separate table to minimize bloat.\n- **Use `fillfactor=90`** to leave space for HOT updates that avoid index maintenance.\n- **Avoid updating indexed columns**—prevents beneficial HOT updates.\n- **Partition by update patterns**—separate frequently updated rows in a different partition from stable data.\n\n### Insert-Heavy Workloads\n\n- **Minimize indexes**—only create what you query; every index slows inserts.\n- **Use `COPY` or multi-row `INSERT`** instead of single-row inserts.\n- **UNLOGGED tables** for rebuildable staging data—much faster writes.\n- **Defer index creation** for bulk loads—>drop index, load data, recreate indexes.\n- **Partition by time/hash** to distribute load. **TimescaleDB** automates partitioning and compression of insert-heavy data.\n- **Use a natural key for primary key** such as a (timestamp, device_id) if enforcing global uniqueness is important many insert-heavy tables don''t need a primary key at all.\n- If you do need a surrogate key, **Prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` over `UUID`**.\n\n### Upsert-Friendly Design\n\n- **Requires UNIQUE index** on conflict target columns—`ON CONFLICT (col1, col2)` needs exact matching unique index (partial indexes don''t work).\n- **Use `EXCLUDED.column`** to reference would-be-inserted values; only update columns that actually changed to reduce write overhead.\n- **`DO NOTHING` faster** than `DO UPDATE` when no actual update needed.\n\n### Safe Schema Evolution\n\n- **Transactional DDL**: most DDL operations can run in transactions and be rolled back—`BEGIN; ALTER TABLE...; ROLLBACK;` for safe testing.\n- **Concurrent index creation**: `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` avoids blocking writes but can''t run in transactions.\n- **Volatile defaults cause rewrites**: adding `NOT NULL` columns with volatile defaults (e.g., `now()`, `gen_random_uuid()`) rewrites entire table. Non-volatile defaults are fast.\n- **Drop constraints before columns**: `ALTER TABLE DROP CONSTRAINT` then `DROP COLUMN` to avoid dependency issues.\n- **Function signature changes**: `CREATE OR REPLACE` with different arguments creates overloads, not replacements. DROP old version if no overload desired.\n\n## Generated Columns\n\n- `... GENERATED ALWAYS AS (<expr>) STORED` for computed, indexable fields. PG18+ adds `VIRTUAL` columns (computed on read, not stored).\n\n## Extensions\n\n- **`pgcrypto`**: `crypt()` for password hashing.\n- **`uuid-ossp`**: alternative UUID functions; prefer `pgcrypto` for new projects.\n- **`pg_trgm`**: fuzzy text search with `%` operator, `similarity()` function. Index with GIN for `LIKE ''%pattern%''` acceleration.\n- **`citext`**: case-insensitive text type. Prefer expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` unless you need case-insensitive constraints.\n- **`btree_gin`/`btree_gist`**: enable mixed-type indexes (e.g., GIN index on both JSONB and text columns).\n- **`hstore`**: key-value pairs; mostly superseded by JSONB but useful for simple string mappings.\n- **`timescaledb`**: essential for time-series—automated partitioning, retention, compression, continuous aggregates.\n- **`postgis`**: comprehensive geospatial support beyond basic geometric types—essential for location-based applications.\n- **`pgvector`**: vector similarity search for embeddings.\n- **`pgaudit`**: audit logging for all database activity.\n\n## JSONB Guidance\n\n- Prefer `JSONB` with **GIN** index.\n- Default: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col);` → accelerates:\n  - **Containment** `jsonb_col @> ''{\"k\":\"v\"}''`\n  - **Key existence** `jsonb_col ? ''k''`, **any/all keys** `?\\|`, `?&`\n  - **Path containment** on nested docs\n  - **Disjunction** `jsonb_col @> ANY(ARRAY[''{\"status\":\"active\"}'', ''{\"status\":\"pending\"}''])`\n- Heavy `@>` workloads: consider opclass `jsonb_path_ops` for smaller/faster containment-only indexes:\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col jsonb_path_ops);`\n  - **Trade-off**: loses support for key existence (`?`, `?|`, `?&`) queries—only supports containment (`@>`)\n- Equality/range on a specific scalar field: extract and index with B-tree (generated column or expression):\n  - `ALTER TABLE tbl ADD COLUMN price INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS ((jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT) STORED;`\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (price);`\n  - Prefer queries like `WHERE price BETWEEN 100 AND 500` (uses B-tree) over `WHERE (jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT BETWEEN 100 AND 500` without index.\n- Arrays inside JSONB: use GIN + `@>` for containment (e.g., tags). Consider `jsonb_path_ops` if only doing containment.\n- Keep core relations in tables; use JSONB for optional/variable attributes.\n- Use constraints to limit allowed JSONB values in a column e.g. `config JSONB NOT NULL CHECK(jsonb_typeof(config) = ''object'')`\n\n## Examples\n\n### Users\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  user_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX ON users (LOWER(email));\nCREATE INDEX ON users (created_at);\n```\n\n### Orders\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  order_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  user_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''PENDING'' CHECK (status IN (''PENDING'',''PAID'',''CANCELED'')),\n  total NUMERIC(10,2) NOT NULL CHECK (total > 0),\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (user_id);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (created_at);\n```\n\n### JSONB\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE profiles (\n  user_id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  attrs JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT ''{}'',\n  theme TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (attrs->>''theme'') STORED\n);\nCREATE INDEX profiles_attrs_gin ON profiles USING GIN (attrs);\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:19:45.214Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Data Modeling Agents requiring efficient database schema creation with PostgreSQL table design expertise.","zh":"适用于需要高效数据库架构创建以及PostgreSQL表设计专业知识的数据建模代理。","ja":"PostgreSQLテーブル設計の専門知識を必要とするデータモデリングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 설계 전문 지식을 필요로 하는 데이터 모델링 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de modelado de datos que requieren una creación eficiente de esquemas de bases de datos con experiencia en el diseño de tablas de PostgreSQL.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de modélisation de données nécessitant une création efficace de schémas de base de données avec une expertise en conception de tables PostgreSQL.","de":"Ideal für Data Modeling Agents, die eine effiziente Erstellung von Datenbankschemas mit Expertise im PostgreSQL-Tabellendesign benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Modelagem de Dados que exigem criação eficiente de esquema de banco de dados com especialização em design de tabelas PostgreSQL.","ru":"Идеально для агентов моделирования данных, требующих эффективного создания схемы базы данных с опытом проектирования таблиц PostgreSQL.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء نمذجة البيانات التي تتطلب إنشاء فعال لSTRUCTURE قاعدة البيانات مع خبرة في تصميم جداول PostgreSQL."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define robust PRIMARY KEY structures using BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY and UUID for global uniqueness, while applying normalization rules to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies, leveraging techniques like denormalization for high-ROI reads.","zh":"赋予代理定义强大的主键结构，使用BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY和UUID实现全局唯一性，同时应用规范化规则消除数据冗余和更新异常，利用反规范化技术提高读取效率。","ja":"エージェントが強力な主キー構造を定義できるようにし、BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITYとUUIDを使用してグローバルな一意性を実現し、規範化規則を適用してデータの冗長性と更新の異常を排除し、反規範化技術を使用して読み取りの効率を高める。","ko":"에이전트가 강력한 기본 키 구조를 정의하도록 하여 BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY와 UUID를 사용하여 전역 고유성을 구현하며, 규정화 규칙을 적용하여 데이터 중복과 업데이트 이상을 제거하고, 비규정화 기술을 사용하여 읽기 효율을 높입니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes definir estructuras robustas de CLAVE PRIMARIA utilizando BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY y UUID para la unicidad global, mientras aplica reglas de normalización para eliminar la redundancia de datos y las anomalías de actualización, aprovechando técnicas como la desnormalización para lecturas de alto ROI.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des structures robustes de CLÉ PRIMAIRE en utilisant BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY et UUID pour l''unicité globale, tout en appliquant des règles de normalisation pour éliminer la redondance des données et les anomalies de mise à jour, en tirant parti de techniques comme la dénormalisation pour des lectures à haut ROI.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, robuste PRIMARY KEY-Strukturen unter Verwendung von BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY und UUID für globale Eindeutigkeit zu definieren, während Normalisierungsregeln angewendet werden, um Datenredundanz und Aktualisierungsanomalien zu beseitigen, und Techniken wie Denormalisierung für Reads mit hohem ROI nutzt.","pt":"Habilita agentes a definir estruturas de CHAVE PRIMÁRIA robustas usando BIGINT GERADO SEMPRE COMO IDENTIDADE e UUID para unicidade global, aplicando regras de normalização para eliminar redundância de dados e anomalias de atualização, aproveitando técnicas como desnormalização para leituras de alto ROI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью определять прочные структуры ПЕРВИЧНОГО КЛЮЧА с использованием BIGINT СГЕНЕРИРОВАННОГО ВСЕГДА КАК ИДЕНТИЧНОСТЬ и UUID для глобальной уникальности, применяя правила нормализации для устранения избыточности данных и аномалий обновления, используя техники, такие как денормализация для чтений с высоким ROI.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تعريف هياكل المفتاح الأساسي القوية باستخدام BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY و UUID للفردية العالمية، مع تطبيق قواعد التطبيع لإزالة ازدواجية البيانات وشذوذ التحديث، واستخدام تقنيات مثل إعادة التطبيع للقراءات عالية العائد على الاستثمار."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing normalized database tables to 3NF","Implementing efficient PRIMARY KEY structures for reference tables","Denormalizing tables for measured, high-ROI reads"],"zh":["设计规范化的数据库表至3NF","为参考表实现高效的主键结构","为测量的高ROI读取而反规范化表"],"ja":["3NFまでの規範化されたデータベーステーブルを設計する","参照テーブルに効率的な主キー構造を実装する","測定された高ROI読み取りのためにテーブルを反規範化する"],"ko":["3NF까지의 정규화된 데이터베이스 테이블을 설계한다","참조 테이블에 효율적인 기본 키 구조를 구현한다","측정된 높은 ROI 읽기 위해 테이블을 비정규화한다"],"es":["Diseñar tablas de bases de datos normalizadas hasta la 3FN","Implementar estructuras eficientes de CLAVE PRIMARIA para tablas de referencia","Desnormalizar tablas para lecturas medidas y de alto ROI"],"fr":["Concevoir des tables de base de données normalisées jusqu''à la 3FN","Mettre en œuvre des structures efficaces de CLÉ PRIMAIRE pour les tables de référence","Dénormaliser les tables pour des lectures mesurées et à haut ROI"],"de":["Entwurf normalisierter Datenbanktabellen bis zur 3NF","Implementierung effizienter PRIMARY KEY-Strukturen für Referenztabellen","Denormalisierung von Tabellen für gemessene Reads mit hohem ROI"],"pt":["Projeto de tabelas de banco de dados normalizadas para 3NF","Implementação de estruturas de CHAVE PRIMÁRIA eficientes para tabelas de referência","Desnormalização de tabelas para leituras medidas de alto ROI"],"ru":["Проектирование нормализованных таблиц базы данных до 3NF","Реализация эффективных структур ПЕРВИЧНОГО КЛЮЧА для таблиц ссылок","Денормализация таблиц для измеренных чтений с высоким ROI"],"ar":["تصميم جداول قاعدة البيانات المُعاد تطبيعها إلى 3NF","تنفيذ هياكل المفتاح الأساسي الفعالة لأجلة المراجع","إعادة تطبيع الجداول للقراءات المقاسة عالية العائد على الاستثمار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of database normalization principles","PostgreSQL-specific syntax and features"],"zh":["需要理解数据库规范化原则","PostgreSQL特有的语法和特性"],"ja":["データベースの規範化原則の理解が必要","PostgreSQL固有の構文と機能"],"ko":["데이터베이스 정규화 원리의 이해가 필요하다","PostgreSQL 고유의 구문 및 기능"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de normalización de bases de datos","Sintaxis y características específicas de PostgreSQL"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de normalisation des bases de données","Syntaxe et fonctionnalités spécifiques à PostgreSQL"],"de":["Erfordert ein Verständnis der Prinzipien der Datenbanknormalisierung","PostgreSQL-spezifische Syntax und Funktionen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de normalização de banco de dados","Sintaxe e recursos específicos do PostgreSQL"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов нормализации базы данных","Синтаксис и функции, специфичные для PostgreSQL"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تطبيع قاعدة البيانات","التركيبة النحوية والميزات المحددة لبرنامج PostgreSQL"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
