ции","ar":"العملات التصميمية: خبير في التنفيذ","en":"design-tokens"},"description":{"zh":"设计令牌专家提供专业指导，帮助您掌握设计令牌的最佳实践，包括令牌类型、结构、验证等","ja":"デザイントークン専門家は、デザイントークンのベストプラクティスをマスターするための専門家の指導を提供します","ko":"디자인 토큰 전문가는 디자인 토큰의最佳实践을 마스터하는 데 필요한 전문가의 지침을 제공합니다","es":"La guía técnica para trabajar con tokens de diseño según la especificación del Grupo de Trabajo de Tokens de Diseño (DTCG).","fr":"Le guide technique pour travailler avec des jetons de conception selon la spécification du Groupe de Travail des Jetons de Conception (DTCG).","de":"Die technische Anleitung für die Arbeit mit Design-Tokens gemäß der Spezifikation der Design-Tokens-Arbeitsgruppe (DTCG).","pt":"O Design Tokens é uma ferramenta para implementar a especificação do Design Tokens Community Group, permitindo a criação de tokens de design consistentes e e...","ru":"Дизайн-токены - это инструмент для реализации спецификации Design Tokens Community Group, позволяющий создавать последовательные и масштабируемые дизайн-токены.","ar":"العملات التصميمية هي أداة لتنفيذ مواصفات مجموعة عملات التصميم المجتمعية، مما يسمح بإنشاء عملات تصميم متسقة وقابلة للتوسعة.","en":"Project implementation of the legal and investigation project for Gemini 3 Hackathon 2026"},"definition":{"en":"Project implementation of the legal and investigation project for Gemini 3 Hackathon 2026"},"features":{"zh":["令牌类型、结构、验证","颜色空间、组件、alpha值","集合、修饰符、解析顺序","jq、JSONata、Figma集成"],"ja":["トークンの種類、構造、検証","色空間、コンポーネント、アルファ値","セット、修飾子、解決順序","jq、JSONata、Figma統合"],"ko":["토큰 유형, 구조, 검증","색상 공간, 구성 요소, 알파 값","집합, 수정자, 해결 순서","jq, JSONata, Figma 통합"],"es":["Tipos y estructura de tokens","Validación y resolución de tokens","Espacios de color y componentes","Modificadores y orden de resolución","Integración con herramientas como Figma"],"fr":["Types et structure des jetons","Validation et résolution des jetons","Espaces de couleur et composants","Modificateurs et ordre de résolution","Intégration avec des outils comme Figma"],"de":["Typen und Struktur von Design-Tokens","Validierung und Auflösung von Design-Tokens","Farbräume und Komponenten","Modifikatoren und Auflösungsreihenfolge","Integration mit Tools wie Figma"],"pt":["Token types, structure, validation","Color spaces, components, alpha, erros comuns","Sets, modifiers, resolution order","Suporte a jq, JSONata, Figma expo"],"ru":["Типы токенов, структура, валидация","Цветовые пространства, компоненты, альфа, распространенные ошибки","Наборы, модификаторы, порядок разрешения","Поддержка jq, JSONata, Figma expo"],"ar":["أنواع العملات، الهيكل، التحقق","فضاءات الألوان، المكونات، ألفا، الأخطاء الشائعة","مجموعات، Modifiers، ترتيب الحل","دعم jq، JSONata، Figma expo"]},"keywords":{"zh":["设计令牌","DTCG规范","令牌类型","颜色空间","jq","JSONata","Figma","设计系统","开发最佳实践"],"ja":["デザイントークン","DTCG規格","トークンの種類","色空間","jq","JSONata","Figma","デザインシステム","開発ベストプラクティス"],"ko":["디자인 토큰","DTCG 규격","토큰 유형","색상 공간","jq","JSONata","Figma","디자인 시스템","개발最佳实践"],"es":["tokens de diseño","desarrollo de interfaz de usuario","diseño de interfaz de usuario","especificación DTCG","validación de tokens","resolución de tokens"],"fr":["jetons de conception","développement d''interface utilisateur","conception d''interface utilisateur","spécification DTCG","validation des jetons","résolution des jetons"],"de":["Design-Tokens","Entwicklung von Benutzeroberflächen","Design von Benutzeroberflächen","DTCG-Spezifikation","Validierung von Design-Tokens","Auflösung von Design-Tokens"],"pt":["design tokens","especificação DTCG","tokens de design","consistência visual","variáveis de design","cores","tipografia"],"ru":["дизайн-токены","спецификация DTCG","токены дизайна","визуальная согласованность","переменные дизайна","цвета","типография"],"ar":["العملات التصميمية","مواصفات DTCG","عملات التصميم","الاتساق البصري","متغيرات التصميم","الألوان","الطباعة"]}},"owner":"Siddharth-Khattar","repo":"holmes","repoPath":"Siddharth-Khattar/holmes","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"design-tokens","description":"Expert in design tokens using the DTCG specification. Use this skill when users ask about design tokens, DTCG format, token validation, formatting, transformation, color spaces (sRGB, Display P3, OKLCH), references and aliasing, resolvers, theming with modifiers/contexts, multi-platform design systems, accessibility, or working with tools like jq, jsonata, and terrazzo. Helps with token file creation, resolver configuration, structure, naming conventions, and best practices.","bodyPreview":"# Design Tokens Expert\n\nExpert guidance for working with design tokens following the Design Tokens Community Group (DTCG) specification.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Topic | Reference |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Token types, structure, validation | [reference/format.md](reference/format.md) |\n| Color spaces, components, alpha, **common mistakes** | [reference/color.md](reference/color.md) |\n| Sets, modifiers, resolution order | [reference/resolver.md](reference/resolver.md) |\n| jq, JSONata, **Figma expo","body":"# Design Tokens Expert\n\nExpert guidance for working with design tokens following the Design Tokens Community Group (DTCG) specification.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Topic | Reference |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Token types, structure, validation | [reference/format.md](reference/format.md) |\n| Color spaces, components, alpha, **common mistakes** | [reference/color.md](reference/color.md) |\n| Sets, modifiers, resolution order | [reference/resolver.md](reference/resolver.md) |\n| jq, JSONata, **Figma export**, **Terrazzo config** | [reference/tools.md](reference/tools.md) |\n| Common patterns and examples | [examples/use-cases.md](examples/use-cases.md) |\n\n**Getting Started:** See [Getting Started Guides](#getting-started-guides) for step-by-step workflows.\n\n## Specification Sources\n\nBased on the latest DTCG Draft Community Group Reports:\n- [Format Module](https://www.designtokens.org/tr/drafts/format/)\n- [Color Module](https://www.designtokens.org/tr/drafts/color/)\n- [Resolver Module](https://www.designtokens.org/tr/drafts/resolver/)\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Token Structure\n\nA token is a JSON object with `$value`. Special properties use `$` prefix:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"brand-blue\": {\n    \"$type\": \"color\",\n    \"$value\": {\n      \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\",\n      \"components\": [0.15, 0.39, 0.92],\n      \"hex\": \"#2563eb\"\n    },\n    \"$description\": \"Primary brand color\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Token Types\n\n**Atomic:** color, dimension, fontFamily, fontWeight, duration, cubicBezier, number\n\n**Composite:** strokeStyle, border, shadow, gradient, typography, transition\n\nSee [reference/format.md](reference/format.md) for complete type definitions.\n\n### Color Format\n\nColors use structured objects (not hex strings):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$type\": \"color\",\n  \"$value\": {\n    \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\",\n    \"components\": [1, 0, 0.5],\n    \"alpha\": 0.8,\n    \"hex\": \"#ff0080\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSupported spaces: srgb, display-p3, oklch, oklab, hsl, hwb, lab, lch, and more. See [reference/color.md](reference/color.md).\n\n### References (Aliasing)\n\n**Two syntaxes supported:**\n\n1. **Curly braces** - Token-level references: `\"{path.to.token}\"`\n2. **JSON Pointer (`$ref`)** - Property-level access: `{\"$ref\": \"#/path/to/$value/property\"}`\n\nToken reference example:\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": {\n    \"primary\": {\"$type\": \"color\", \"$value\": {\"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [0, 0.4, 0.8]}}\n  },\n  \"button\": {\n    \"background\": {\"$type\": \"color\", \"$value\": \"{color.primary}\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\nJSON Pointer example (accessing array elements):\n```json\n{\n  \"blue\": {\n    \"$type\": \"color\",\n    \"$value\": {\"colorSpace\": \"okhsl\", \"components\": [0.733, 0.8, 0.5]}\n  },\n  \"blue-hue\": {\n    \"$type\": \"number\",\n    \"$ref\": \"#/blue/$value/components/0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [reference/format.md](reference/format.md) for complete reference syntax details.\n\n### Groups and Type Inheritance\n\nGroups organize tokens. `$type` on a group applies to all children:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"spacing\": {\n    \"$type\": \"dimension\",\n    \"sm\": {\"$value\": {\"value\": 8, \"unit\": \"px\"}},\n    \"md\": {\"$value\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit\": \"px\"}},\n    \"lg\": {\"$value\": {\"value\": 24, \"unit\": \"px\"}}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Resolvers for Theming\n\nResolvers manage tokens across contexts (themes, platforms, densities):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-system\",\n  \"version\": \"2025.10\",\n  \"sets\": {\n    \"core\": {\"sources\": [{\"$ref\": \"tokens/base.json\"}]}\n  },\n  \"modifiers\": {\n    \"theme\": {\n      \"contexts\": {\n        \"light\": [{\"$ref\": \"themes/light.json\"}],\n        \"dark\": [{\"$ref\": \"themes/dark.json\"}]\n      },\n      \"default\": \"light\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"resolutionOrder\": [\n    {\"$ref\": \"#/sets/core\"},\n    {\"$ref\": \"#/modifiers/theme\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nSee [reference/resolver.md](reference/resolver.md) for complete documentation.\n\n## Getting Started Guides\n\n### Quick Start: Convert CSS Variables to DTCG\n\n**Starting point:** Existing CSS custom properties\n```css\n:root {\n  --color-primary: #2563eb;\n  --color-background: #ffffff;\n  --spacing-sm: 8px;\n  --spacing-md: 16px;\n}\n```\n\n**Step 1:** Create primitives.tokens.json\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": {\n    \"primitive\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"blue-500\": {\n        \"$value\": { \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [0.145, 0.388, 0.922], \"hex\": \"#2563eb\" }\n      },\n      \"white\": {\n        \"$value\": { \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [1, 1, 1], \"hex\": \"#ffffff\" }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"spacing\": {\n    \"$type\": \"dimension\",\n    \"scale\": {\n      \"sm\": { \"$value\": { \"value\": 8, \"unit\": \"px\" } },\n      \"md\": { \"$value\": { \"value\": 16, \"unit\": \"px\" } }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Step 2:** Create semantic.tokens.json with references\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": {\n    \"interactive\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"primary\": { \"$value\": \"{color.primitive.blue-500}\" }\n    },\n    \"background\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"page\": { \"$value\": \"{color.primitive.white}\" }\n    }\n  },\n  \"spacing\": {\n    \"$type\": \"dimension\",\n    \"component\": {\n      \"padding\": { \"$value\": \"{spacing.scale.sm}\" },\n      \"gap\": { \"$value\": \"{spacing.scale.md}\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Conversion tips:**\n- RGB hex to sRGB: divide each channel by 255 (e.g., `37/255 = 0.145`)\n- Keep hex as fallback in the `hex` property\n- Create semantic layer for purpose-driven naming\n\n---\n\n### Quick Start: Set Up Terrazzo with Dark Mode\n\n**Step 1:** Install dependencies\n```bash\nnpm install -D @terrazzo/cli @terrazzo/plugin-css\n```\n\n**Step 2:** Create token files with mode extensions\n\ntokens/themes/light.tokens.json:\n```json\n{\n  \"$extensions\": { \"mode\": \"light\" },\n  \"color\": {\n    \"background\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"page\": { \"$value\": { \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [1, 1, 1], \"hex\": \"#ffffff\" } }\n    },\n    \"text\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"primary\": { \"$value\": { \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [0.07, 0.07, 0.07], \"hex\": \"#121212\" } }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\ntokens/themes/dark.tokens.json:\n```json\n{\n  \"$extensions\": { \"mode\": \"dark\" },\n  \"color\": {\n    \"background\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"page\": { \"$value\": { \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [0.07, 0.07, 0.07], \"hex\": \"#121212\" } }\n    },\n    \"text\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"primary\": { \"$value\": { \"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [0.95, 0.95, 0.95], \"hex\": \"#f2f2f2\" } }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Step 3:** Create terrazzo.config.mjs\n```javascript\nimport { defineConfig } from \"@terrazzo/cli\";\nimport pluginCSS from \"@terrazzo/plugin-css\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  tokens: [\n    \"./tokens/primitives.tokens.json\",\n    \"./tokens/themes/light.tokens.json\",\n    \"./tokens/themes/dark.tokens.json\"\n  ],\n  outDir: \"./dist/\",\n  plugins: [\n    pluginCSS({\n      filename: \"tokens.css\",\n      modeSelectors: [\n        { mode: \"light\", selectors: [\":root\", \"[data-theme=''light'']\"] },\n        { mode: \"dark\", selectors: [\"[data-theme=''dark'']\", \"@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"] }\n      ]\n    })\n  ]\n});\n```\n\n**Step 4:** Build and use\n```bash\nnpx terrazzo build\n```\n\nIn your HTML:\n```html\n<html data-theme=\"light\"><!-- or \"dark\" -->\n```\n\n---\n\n### Quick Start: Import Figma Variables Export\n\n**Step 1:** Export from Figma\n- Open Variables panel in Figma\n- Use a DTCG export plugin or Figma''s built-in export\n- Save as `figma-export.json`\n\n**Step 2:** Validate the export\n```bash\n# Check JSON is valid\njq ''.'' figma-export.json > /dev/null && echo \"Valid JSON\"\n\n# List all token paths\njq -r ''paths(has(\"$value\")) | join(\".\")'' figma-export.json\n```\n\n**Step 3:** Add mode extensions if needed\n\nIf Figma exported separate mode files, add `$extensions.mode`:\n```bash\n# Add mode to light theme file\njq ''. + {\"$extensions\": {\"mode\": \"light\"}}'' light.json > light.tokens.json\n```\n\n**Step 4:** Add hex fallbacks (if missing)\n\nFigma exports sRGB components but may omit hex:\n```bash\n# Quick check if hex values exist\njq ''.. | objects | select(.colorSpace == \"srgb\") | select(.hex == null)'' figma-export.json\n```\n\n**Step 5:** Configure Terrazzo\n\nCreate `terrazzo.config.mjs` pointing to your imported files and build.\n\n**Common Figma export issues:**\n- Flat structure (no primitives/semantic separation) - reorganize manually\n- Space in token names - use jq to convert to kebab-case\n- Missing `$type` on groups - add type inheritance\n\n---\n\n## Workflows\n\n### Creating a Token File\n\n```\nToken File Creation:\n- [ ] Step 1: Define file structure (primitives → semantic → components)\n- [ ] Step 2: Create primitive tokens with explicit types\n- [ ] Step 3: Create semantic tokens referencing primitives\n- [ ] Step 4: Validate structure and references\n- [ ] Step 5: Test with target tools (Terrazzo, etc.)\n```\n\n**Step 1: Define structure**\n\nOrganize into layers:\n```\ntokens/\n├── primitives.tokens.json   # Raw values (colors, spacing scales)\n├── semantic.tokens.json     # Purpose-driven aliases\n└── components.tokens.json   # Component-specific tokens\n```\n\n**Step 2: Create primitives**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": {\n    \"primitive\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"blue\": {\n        \"500\": {\"$value\": {\"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [0.15, 0.39, 0.92], \"hex\": \"#2563eb\"}}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Step 3: Create semantic tokens**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": {\n    \"interactive\": {\n      \"$type\": \"color\",\n      \"default\": {\"$value\": \"{color.primitive.blue.500}\"}\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Step 4: Validate**\n\nCheck for:\n- All tokens have resolvable `$type`\n- No circular references\n- Valid value formats for each type\n- Names don''t contain `{`, `}`, `.` or start with `$`\n\n**Step 5: Test with tools**\n\n```bash\nterrazzo validate tokens.json\nterrazzo build --input tokens.json --output test.css --format css\n```\n\n---\n\n### Setting Up a Theme Resolver\n\n```\nResolver Setup:\n- [ ] Step 1: Organize token files by concern\n- [ ] Step 2: Create resolver.json with version and sets\n- [ ] Step 3: Define theme modifier with contexts\n- [ ] Step 4: Configure resolution order\n- [ ] Step 5: Test with different inputs\n```\n\n**Step 1: Organize files**\n\n```\ntokens/\n├── resolver.json\n├── base.tokens.json\n└── themes/\n    ├── light.tokens.json\n    └── dark.tokens.json\n```\n\n**Step 2: Create resolver**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-design-system\",\n  \"version\": \"2025.10\",\n  \"sets\": {\n    \"foundation\": {\n      \"sources\": [{\"$ref\": \"base.tokens.json\"}]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Step 3: Define theme modifier**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"modifiers\": {\n    \"theme\": {\n      \"contexts\": {\n        \"light\": [{\"$ref\": \"themes/light.tokens.json\"}],\n        \"dark\": [{\"$ref\": \"themes/dark.tokens.json\"}]\n      },\n      \"default\": \"light\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Step 4: Set resolution order**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"resolutionOrder\": [\n    {\"$ref\": \"#/sets/foundation\"},\n    {\"$ref\": \"#/modifiers/theme\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Step 5: Test**\n\n```bash\nterrazzo build --resolver resolver.json --output light.css\nterrazzo build --resolver resolver.json --input theme=dark --output dark.css\n```\n\n---\n\n### Validating Token Files\n\n```\nValidation Checklist:\n- [ ] Step 1: Check JSON syntax\n- [ ] Step 2: Verify type declarations\n- [ ] Step 3: Validate value formats\n- [ ] Step 4: Check reference resolution\n- [ ] Step 5: Verify naming constraints\n```\n\n**Step 1: JSON syntax**\n\n```bash\njq ''.'' tokens.json > /dev/null && echo \"Valid JSON\"\n```\n\n**Step 2: Type declarations**\n\nEvery token needs a resolvable `$type` (explicit or inherited from parent group).\n\n**Step 3: Value formats**\n\n| Type | Valid Format |\n|------|--------------|\n| color | `{colorSpace, components, [alpha], [hex]}` |\n| dimension | `{value: number, unit: \"px\"|\"rem\"}` |\n| duration | `{value: number, unit: \"ms\"|\"s\"}` |\n| cubicBezier | `[P1x, P1y, P2x, P2y]` where P1x, P2x ∈ [0,1] |\n| fontWeight | 1-1000 or string (\"normal\", \"bold\", etc.) |\n\n**Step 4: References**\n\n- All `{path.to.token}` references must resolve\n- No circular references (A → B → A)\n- No self-references\n\n**Step 5: Naming**\n\n- Names cannot start with `$`\n- Names cannot contain `{`, `}`, `.`\n\n---\n\n### Migrating from Other Formats\n\n```\nMigration Workflow:\n- [ ] Step 1: Export existing tokens to JSON\n- [ ] Step 2: Map types to DTCG equivalents\n- [ ] Step 3: Convert color values to structured format\n- [ ] Step 4: Update reference syntax\n- [ ] Step 5: Validate and test\n```\n\n**Common conversions:**\n\n| From | To DTCG |\n|------|---------|\n| `\"#ff0000\"` | `{colorSpace: \"srgb\", components: [1,0,0], hex: \"#ff0000\"}` |\n| `\"16px\"` | `{value: 16, unit: \"px\"}` |\n| `\"$colors.primary\"` or `{colors.primary}` | `\"{colors.primary}\"` |\n\n**Terrazzo conversion:**\n\n```bash\nterrazzo convert --from style-dictionary --to dtcg input.json output.tokens.json\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Token Layers\n\n1. **Primitives** - Raw values without semantic meaning\n2. **Semantic** - Purpose-driven tokens referencing primitives\n3. **Component** - Specific component tokens referencing semantic\n\n### Naming Conventions\n\n- Use lowercase with hyphens: `color.brand.primary`\n- Structure: `[category].[subcategory].[variant].[state]`\n- Semantic over appearance: `color.interactive.default` not `color.blue-500`\n\n### Theming Strategy\n\nUse resolvers for themes (recommended over group extension):\n- Cleaner separation of concerns\n- Token paths stay consistent across themes\n- Easy to compose themes (e.g., dark + high-contrast)\n- Standardized input handling for build tools\n\n### Accessibility\n\n**Color contrast:** Document contrast ratios in `$extensions`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$extensions\": {\n    \"com.example.a11y\": {\"contrastRatio\": 7.5, \"wcagLevel\": \"AA\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Reduced motion:** Use resolver modifier:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"modifiers\": {\n    \"motion\": {\n      \"contexts\": {\n        \"full\": [{\"$ref\": \"motion/full.json\"}],\n        \"reduced\": [{\"$ref\": \"motion/reduced.json\"}]\n      },\n      \"default\": \"full\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### File Conventions\n\n- Token files: `.tokens` or `.tokens.json`\n- Resolver files: `.resolver.json`\n- Encoding: UTF-8\n\n## Common Tasks\n\n| Task | Approach |\n|------|----------|\n| Format validation | Check against DTCG spec, use Terrazzo validate |\n| Structure optimization | Organize into primitive → semantic → component layers |\n| Alias resolution | Trace references, check for circular dependencies |\n| Resolver configuration | Define sets, modifiers, resolution order |\n| Theme implementation | Use resolver modifiers with context files |\n| Multi-context builds | Generate outputs per theme/platform/density |\n| Tool integration | Use jq for queries, Terrazzo for transforms |\n| Migration | Convert colors to structured format, update references |\n\n## Your Role\n\nWhen helping with design tokens:\n\n1. **Verify before claiming** - Check reference files before stating what DTCG does/doesn''t support. Never assume spec limitations.\n2. **Use latest DTCG spec** - Structured color format, proper types\n3. **Validate structure** - Check `$value`, `$type`, references\n4. **Suggest best practices** - Naming, organization, layering\n5. **Help with tools** - jq queries, Terrazzo commands, JSONata transforms\n6. **Consider platforms** - Web, iOS, Android via `$extensions`\n7. **Think about scale** - Design for maintainability\n8. **Prioritize accessibility** - Contrast, motion, focus indicators\n9. **Connect design and code** - Bridge tools and implementation\n\n**Important:** When asked about spec capabilities (what syntax is valid, what features exist), always read the relevant reference file first. Do not rely on assumptions or prior knowledge about the spec.\n\nAlways provide clear examples and explain reasoning behind recommendations.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:20:24.369Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing advanced design token management and validation following the Design Tokens Community Group (DTCG) specification.","zh":"非常适合需要高级设计令牌管理和验证的前端代理，特别是遵循设计令牌社区小组（DTCG）规格的代理。","ja":"デザイントークン管理および検証に高度な機能が必要なフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。特に、Design Tokens Community Group (DTCG) の仕様に従ったエージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 디자인 토큰 관리 및 확인이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합하며, 특히 디자인 토큰 커뮤니티 그룹(DTCG) 사양을 따르는 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes frontend que necesitan una gestión avanzada de tokens de diseño y validación siguiendo la especificación del Grupo de Trabajo de Tokens de Diseño (DTCG).","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin d''une gestion avancée des jetons de conception et de validation suivant la spécification du Groupe de travail sur les jetons de conception (DTCG).","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die eine erweiterte Design-Token-Verwaltung und -Validierung gemäß der Spezifikation der Design-Tokens-Community-Gruppe (DTCG) benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de gerenciamento avançado de tokens de design e validação seguindo a especificação do Design Tokens Community Group (DTCG).","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым необходим продвинутый менеджмент токенов дизайна и валидация в соответствии с спецификацией Design Tokens Community Group (DTCG).","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الواجهة الأمامية التي تحتاج إلى إدارة متقدمة لأشكال التصميم والتحقق من صحتها وفقًا لمواصفات مجموعة مجتمع رموز التصميم (DTCG)."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to work with design tokens, including token types, structure, validation, color spaces, and resolution order, using standards like JSONata and leveraging tools such as Figma for seamless integration and analysis of design components.","zh":"赋予代理使用设计令牌的能力，包括令牌类型、结构、验证、颜色空间和解析顺序，使用JSONata等标准，并利用Figma等工具实现设计组件的无缝集成和分析。","ja":"エージェントがデザイントークンを使用できるようにします。トークンの種類、構造、検証、色空間、解決順序などを、JSONataなどの規格を使用して、Figmaなどのツールを利用して設計コンポーネントのシームレスな統合と分析を行います。","ko":"에이전트가 디자인 토큰을 사용할 수 있도록 해줍니다. 토큰 유형, 구조, 확인, 색상 공간 및 해결 순서 등을 JSONata와 같은 표준을 사용하여, Figma와 같은 도구를 사용하여 디자인 구성 요소의 無縫な統合 및 분석을 수행할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a trabajar con tokens de diseño, incluidos tipos de tokens, estructura, validación, espacios de color y orden de resolución, utilizando estándares como JSONata y aprovechando herramientas como Figma para una integración y análisis sin problemas de componentes de diseño.","fr":"Permet aux agents de travailler avec des jetons de conception, y compris les types de jetons, la structure, la validation, les espaces de couleur et l''ordre de résolution, en utilisant des normes telles que JSONata et en exploitant des outils tels que Figma pour une intégration et une analyse sans problème des composants de conception.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, mit Design-Tokens zu arbeiten, einschließlich Tokentypen, Struktur, Validierung, Farbräumen und Auflösungsreihenfolge, unter Verwendung von Standards wie JSONata und Nutzung von Tools wie Figma für eine nahtlose Integration und Analyse von Designkomponenten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a trabalhar com tokens de design, incluindo tipos de tokens, estrutura, validação, espaços de cor e ordem de resolução, usando padrões como JSONata e aproveitando ferramentas como Figma para integração e análise sem problemas de componentes de design.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью работать с токенами дизайна, включая типы токенов, структуру, валидацию, цветовые пространства и порядок разрешения, используя стандарты như JSONata и利用ая инструменты seperti Figma для бесшовной интеграции и анализа компонентов дизайна.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من العمل مع رموز التصميم، بما في ذلك أنواع الرموز، والهيكل، والتحقق من الصحة، ومساحات الألوان، وترتيب القرار، باستخدام معايير مثل JSONata وتحقيق أدوات مثل Figma للتكامل السلس والتحليل المكونات التصميمية."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating design token formats","Resolving color space inconsistencies","Automating design token sets and modifiers"],"zh":["验证设计令牌格式","解决颜色空间不一致问题","自动化设计令牌集和修饰符"],"ja":["デザイントークンの形式を検証する","色空間の不一致を解決する","デザイントークンセットと修飾子を自動化する"],"ko":["디자인 토큰 형식 확인","색상 공간 불일치 해결","디자인 토큰 세트 및 수정자 자동화"],"es":["Validar formatos de tokens de diseño","Resolver inconsistencias en el espacio de color","Automatizar conjuntos de tokens de diseño y modificadores"],"fr":["Valider les formats de jetons de conception","Résoudre les incohérences dans l''espace de couleur","Automatiser les ensembles de jetons de conception et les modificateurs"],"de":["Design-Token-Formate validieren","Farbraum-Inkonsistenzen auflösen","Design-Token-Sätze und Modifikatoren automatisieren"],"pt":["Validar formatos de tokens de design","Resolver inconsistências de espaços de cor","Automatizar conjuntos de tokens de design e modificadores"],"ru":["Валидировать форматы токенов дизайна","Разрешать несоответствия цветовых пространств","Автоматизировать наборы токенов дизайна и модификаторы"],"ar":["التحقق من صحة تنسيقات رموز التصميم","حل عدم الاتساق في مساحات الألوان","تأتميم مجموعات رموز التصميم والمنظمات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of DTCG specification","Limited to design token management and related workflows"],"zh":["需要了解DTCG规格","仅限于设计令牌管理和相关工作流"],"ja":["DTCGの仕様を理解する必要がある","デザイントークン管理および関連ワークフローに限定される"],"ko":["DTCG 사양을 이해해야 함","디자인 토큰 관리 및 관련 워크플로에 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la especificación DTCG","Limitado a la gestión de tokens de diseño y flujos de trabajo relacionados"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la spécification DTCG","Limité à la gestion des jetons de conception et aux flux de travail associés"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis der DTCG-Spezifikation","Begrenzt auf Design-Token-Verwaltung und damit verbundene Workflows"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da especificação DTCG","Limitado ao gerenciamento de tokens de design e workflows relacionados"],"ru":["Требует понимания спецификации DTCG","Ограничен менеджментом токенов дизайна и связанными с ним рабочими процессами"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لمواصفات مجموعة مجتمع رموز التصميم (DTCG)","محدود بإدارة رموز التصميم والعمليات المرتبطة بها"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/pdf', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'pdf', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:20:24.306Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/pdf","name":"pdf","description":{"zh":"PDF Python","ja":"PDF JavaScript","ko":"PDF ","es":"Guía de procesamiento de PDF que cubre operaciones esenciales con bibliotecas de Python y herramientas de línea de comandos","fr":"Guide de traitement de PDF qui couvre les opérations essentielles avec des bibliothèques Python et des outils de ligne de commande","de":"PDF-Verarbeitungs-Anleitung, die grundlegende Operationen mit Python-Bibliotheken und Kommandozeilen-Tools abdeckt","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"PDF ","ja":"PDF","ko":"PDF ","es":"Procesamiento de PDF con Python","fr":"Traitement de PDF avec Python","de":"PDF-Verarbeitung mit Python","en":"pdf"},"description":{"zh":"PDF Python","ja":"PDF JavaScript","ko":"PDF ","es":"Guía de procesamiento de PDF que cubre operaciones esenciales con bibliotecas de Python y herramientas de línea de comandos","fr":"Guide de traitement de PDF qui couvre les opérations essentielles avec des bibliothèques Python et des outils de ligne de commande","de":"PDF-Verarbeitungs-Anleitung, die grundlegende Operationen mit Python-Bibliotheken und Kommandozeilen-Tools abdeckt","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Python","JavaScript","PDF","PDF","PDF"],"ja":["Python","JavaScript","PDF","PDF","PDF"],"ko":["Python","JavaScript","PDF","PDF","PDF"],"es":["Lectura de PDF con PyPDF","Escritura de PDF con PyPDF","Extracción de texto de PDF","Uso de herramientas de línea de comandos para PDF"],"fr":["Lecture de PDF avec PyPDF","Écriture de PDF avec PyPDF","Extraction de texte de PDF","Utilisation d''outils de ligne de commande pour PDF"],"de":["Lesen von PDF mit PyPDF","Schreiben von PDF mit PyPDF","Textextraktion aus PDF","Verwendung von Kommandozeilen-Tools für PDF"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PDF","Python PDF","JavaScript PDF","PDF","PDF","PDF"],"ja":["PDF","Python PDF","JavaScript PDF","PDF","PDF","PDF"],"ko":["PDF","Python PDF","JavaScript PDF","PDF","PDF","PDF"],"es":["procesamiento de pdf","python pdf","bibliotecas de python para pdf","herramientas de línea de comandos para pdf","pdf con python","manipulación de pdf"],"fr":["traitement de pdf","python pdf","bibliothèques python pour pdf","outils de ligne de commande pour pdf","pdf avec python","manipulation de pdf"],"de":["pdf-verarbeitung","python pdf","python-bibliotheken für pdf","kommandozeilen-tools für pdf","pdf mit python","manipulation von pdf"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pdf","description":"Comprehensive PDF manipulation toolkit for extracting text and tables, creating new PDFs, merging/splitting documents, and handling forms. When Claude needs to fill in a PDF form or programmatically process, generate, or analyze PDF documents at scale.","bodyPreview":"# PDF Processing Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nThis guide covers essential PDF processing operations using Python libraries and command-line tools. For advanced features, JavaScript libraries, and detailed examples, see reference.md. If you need to fill out a PDF form, read forms.md and follow its instructions.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\n# Read a PDF\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nprint(f\"Pages: {len(reader.pages)}\")\n\n# Extract text\ntext = \"\"\nfor page in reader.","body":"# PDF Processing Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nThis guide covers essential PDF processing operations using Python libraries and command-line tools. For advanced features, JavaScript libraries, and detailed examples, see reference.md. If you need to fill out a PDF form, read forms.md and follow its instructions.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\n# Read a PDF\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nprint(f\"Pages: {len(reader.pages)}\")\n\n# Extract text\ntext = \"\"\nfor page in reader.pages:\n    text += page.extract_text()\n```\n\n## Python Libraries\n\n### pypdf - Basic Operations\n\n#### Merge PDFs\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfWriter, PdfReader\n\nwriter = PdfWriter()\nfor pdf_file in [\"doc1.pdf\", \"doc2.pdf\", \"doc3.pdf\"]:\n    reader = PdfReader(pdf_file)\n    for page in reader.pages:\n        writer.add_page(page)\n\nwith open(\"merged.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n#### Split PDF\n```python\nreader = PdfReader(\"input.pdf\")\nfor i, page in enumerate(reader.pages):\n    writer = PdfWriter()\n    writer.add_page(page)\n    with open(f\"page_{i+1}.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n        writer.write(output)\n```\n\n#### Extract Metadata\n```python\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nmeta = reader.metadata\nprint(f\"Title: {meta.title}\")\nprint(f\"Author: {meta.author}\")\nprint(f\"Subject: {meta.subject}\")\nprint(f\"Creator: {meta.creator}\")\n```\n\n#### Rotate Pages\n```python\nreader = PdfReader(\"input.pdf\")\nwriter = PdfWriter()\n\npage = reader.pages[0]\npage.rotate(90)  # Rotate 90 degrees clockwise\nwriter.add_page(page)\n\nwith open(\"rotated.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n### pdfplumber - Text and Table Extraction\n\n#### Extract Text with Layout\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\nwith pdfplumber.open(\"document.pdf\") as pdf:\n    for page in pdf.pages:\n        text = page.extract_text()\n        print(text)\n```\n\n#### Extract Tables\n```python\nwith pdfplumber.open(\"document.pdf\") as pdf:\n    for i, page in enumerate(pdf.pages):\n        tables = page.extract_tables()\n        for j, table in enumerate(tables):\n            print(f\"Table {j+1} on page {i+1}:\")\n            for row in table:\n                print(row)\n```\n\n#### Advanced Table Extraction\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\nwith pdfplumber.open(\"document.pdf\") as pdf:\n    all_tables = []\n    for page in pdf.pages:\n        tables = page.extract_tables()\n        for table in tables:\n            if table:  # Check if table is not empty\n                df = pd.DataFrame(table[1:], columns=table[0])\n                all_tables.append(df)\n\n# Combine all tables\nif all_tables:\n    combined_df = pd.concat(all_tables, ignore_index=True)\n    combined_df.to_excel(\"extracted_tables.xlsx\", index=False)\n```\n\n### reportlab - Create PDFs\n\n#### Basic PDF Creation\n```python\nfrom reportlab.lib.pagesizes import letter\nfrom reportlab.pdfgen import canvas\n\nc = canvas.Canvas(\"hello.pdf\", pagesize=letter)\nwidth, height = letter\n\n# Add text\nc.drawString(100, height - 100, \"Hello World!\")\nc.drawString(100, height - 120, \"This is a PDF created with reportlab\")\n\n# Add a line\nc.line(100, height - 140, 400, height - 140)\n\n# Save\nc.save()\n```\n\n#### Create PDF with Multiple Pages\n```python\nfrom reportlab.lib.pagesizes import letter\nfrom reportlab.platypus import SimpleDocTemplate, Paragraph, Spacer, PageBreak\nfrom reportlab.lib.styles import getSampleStyleSheet\n\ndoc = SimpleDocTemplate(\"report.pdf\", pagesize=letter)\nstyles = getSampleStyleSheet()\nstory = []\n\n# Add content\ntitle = Paragraph(\"Report Title\", styles[''Title''])\nstory.append(title)\nstory.append(Spacer(1, 12))\n\nbody = Paragraph(\"This is the body of the report. \" * 20, styles[''Normal''])\nstory.append(body)\nstory.append(PageBreak())\n\n# Page 2\nstory.append(Paragraph(\"Page 2\", styles[''Heading1'']))\nstory.append(Paragraph(\"Content for page 2\", styles[''Normal'']))\n\n# Build PDF\ndoc.build(story)\n```\n\n## Command-Line Tools\n\n### pdftotext (poppler-utils)\n```bash\n# Extract text\npdftotext input.pdf output.txt\n\n# Extract text preserving layout\npdftotext -layout input.pdf output.txt\n\n# Extract specific pages\npdftotext -f 1 -l 5 input.pdf output.txt  # Pages 1-5\n```\n\n### qpdf\n```bash\n# Merge PDFs\nqpdf --empty --pages file1.pdf file2.pdf -- merged.pdf\n\n# Split pages\nqpdf input.pdf --pages . 1-5 -- pages1-5.pdf\nqpdf input.pdf --pages . 6-10 -- pages6-10.pdf\n\n# Rotate pages\nqpdf input.pdf output.pdf --rotate=+90:1  # Rotate page 1 by 90 degrees\n\n# Remove password\nqpdf --password=mypassword --decrypt encrypted.pdf decrypted.pdf\n```\n\n### pdftk (if available)\n```bash\n# Merge\npdftk file1.pdf file2.pdf cat output merged.pdf\n\n# Split\npdftk input.pdf burst\n\n# Rotate\npdftk input.pdf rotate 1east output rotated.pdf\n```\n\n## Common Tasks\n\n### Extract Text from Scanned PDFs\n```python\n# Requires: pip install pytesseract pdf2image\nimport pytesseract\nfrom pdf2image import convert_from_path\n\n# Convert PDF to images\nimages = convert_from_path(''scanned.pdf'')\n\n# OCR each page\ntext = \"\"\nfor i, image in enumerate(images):\n    text += f\"Page {i+1}:\\n\"\n    text += pytesseract.image_to_string(image)\n    text += \"\\n\\n\"\n\nprint(text)\n```\n\n### Add Watermark\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\n# Create watermark (or load existing)\nwatermark = PdfReader(\"watermark.pdf\").pages[0]\n\n# Apply to all pages\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nwriter = PdfWriter()\n\nfor page in reader.pages:\n    page.merge_page(watermark)\n    writer.add_page(page)\n\nwith open(\"watermarked.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n### Extract Images\n```bash\n# Using pdfimages (poppler-utils)\npdfimages -j input.pdf output_prefix\n\n# This extracts all images as output_prefix-000.jpg, output_prefix-001.jpg, etc.\n```\n\n### Password Protection\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader, PdfWriter\n\nreader = PdfReader(\"input.pdf\")\nwriter = PdfWriter()\n\nfor page in reader.pages:\n    writer.add_page(page)\n\n# Add password\nwriter.encrypt(\"userpassword\", \"ownerpassword\")\n\nwith open(\"encrypted.pdf\", \"wb\") as output:\n    writer.write(output)\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Best Tool | Command/Code |\n|------|-----------|--------------|\n| Merge PDFs | pypdf | `writer.add_page(page)` |\n| Split PDFs | pypdf | One page per file |\n| Extract text | pdfplumber | `page.extract_text()` |\n| Extract tables | pdfplumber | `page.extract_tables()` |\n| Create PDFs | reportlab | Canvas or Platypus |\n| Command line merge | qpdf | `qpdf --empty --pages ...` |\n| OCR scanned PDFs | pytesseract | Convert to image first |\n| Fill PDF forms | pdf-lib or pypdf (see forms.md) | See forms.md |\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- For advanced pypdfium2 usage, see reference.md\n- For JavaScript libraries (pdf-lib), see reference.md\n- If you need to fill out a PDF form, follow the instructions in forms.md\n- For troubleshooting guides, see reference.md\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:20:24.306Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Document Analysis Agents needing advanced PDF processing capabilities using Python libraries like pypdf.","zh":"非常适合需要使用Python库（如pypdf）进行高级PDF处理的文档分析代理。","ja":"Pythonライブラリ（pypdfなど）を使用した高度なPDF処理機能を必要とするドキュメント分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Python 라이브러리(pypdf 등)를 사용하여 고급 PDF 처리 기능이 필요한 문서 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Análisis de Documentos que necesitan capacidades de procesamiento de PDF avanzadas utilizando bibliotecas de Python como pypdf.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''Analyse de Documents nécessitant des capacités de traitement de PDF avancées en utilisant des bibliothèques Python comme pypdf.","de":"Perfekt für Dokumentenanalyse-Agenten, die erweiterte PDF-Verarbeitungsfähigkeiten unter Verwendung von Python-Bibliotheken wie pypdf benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Documentos que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de processamento de PDF usando bibliotecas Python como pypdf.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа документов, которым необходимы расширенные возможности обработки PDF с помощью библиотек Python, таких как pypdf.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء قائم على تحليل المستندات الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لمعالجة PDF باستخدام مكتبات Python مثل pypdf."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to extract text, read PDF pages, and perform essential PDF operations using command-line tools and JavaScript libraries, enabling seamless integration with various workflows and protocols.","zh":"赋予代理提取文本、阅读PDF页面和执行基本PDF操作的能力，使用命令行工具和JavaScript库，实现与各类工作流和协议的无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントにテキストの抽出、PDFページの読み取り、基本的なPDF操作を実行する機能を付与し、コマンドラインツールとJavaScriptライブラリを使用して、様々なワークフローとプロトコルとのシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 텍스트를 추출하고 PDF 페이지를 읽고 기본 PDF 작업을 수행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 명령줄 도구와 JavaScript 라이브러리를 사용하여 다양한 워크플ロー와 프로토콜과의无缝한 통합을实现합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a extraer texto, leer páginas de PDF y realizar operaciones de PDF esenciales utilizando herramientas de línea de comandos y bibliotecas de JavaScript, lo que permite una integración fluida con varios flujos de trabajo y protocolos.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''extraire du texte, de lire des pages de PDF et d''exécuter des opérations de PDF essentielles en utilisant des outils de ligne de commande et des bibliothèques JavaScript, ce qui permet une intégration fluide avec différents flux de travail et protocoles.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Text zu extrahieren, PDF-Seiten zu lesen und wesentliche PDF-Operationen unter Verwendung von Befehlszeilenwerkzeugen und JavaScript-Bibliotheken durchzuführen, was eine nahtlose Integration mit verschiedenen Workflows und Protokollen ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a extrair texto, ler páginas de PDF e realizar operações de PDF essenciais usando ferramentas de linha de comando e bibliotecas JavaScript, permitindo uma integração perfeita com vários fluxos de trabalho e protocolos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью извлекать текст, читать страницы PDF и выполнять основные операции с PDF с помощью инструментов командной строки и библиотек JavaScript, обеспечивая бесшовную интеграцию с различными рабочими процессами и протоколами.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء استخراج النص، قراءة صفحات PDF، وأداء عمليات PDF الأساسية باستخدام أدوات سطر الأوامر ومكتبات JavaScript، مما يسمح بالتكامل السلس مع سير عمل وبروتوكولات مختلفة."},"useCases":{"en":["Extracting text from PDF documents","Automating PDF form filling using Python","Debugging PDF page structure and content"],"zh":["从PDF文档中提取文本","使用Python自动填写PDF表单","调试PDF页面结构和内容"],"ja":["PDFドキュメントからテキストを抽出する","Pythonを使用してPDFフォームを自動的に埋める","PDFページの構造と内容をデバッグする"],"ko":["PDF 문서에서 텍스트 추출","Python을 사용하여 PDF 양식을 자동으로 채우기","PDF 페이지 구조 및 내용 디버깅"],"es":["Extracción de texto de documentos de PDF","Automatización del llenado de formularios de PDF utilizando Python","Depuración de la estructura y el contenido de la página de PDF"],"fr":["Extraction de texte de documents de PDF","Automatisation du remplissage de formulaires de PDF en utilisant Python","Débogage de la structure et du contenu de la page de PDF"],"de":["Extraktion von Text aus PDF-Dokumenten","Automatisierung des Ausfüllens von PDF-Formularen unter Verwendung von Python","Fehlerbehebung der Struktur und des Inhalts von PDF-Seiten"],"pt":["Extração de texto de documentos PDF","Automação de preenchimento de formulários PDF usando Python","Depuração da estrutura e conteúdo da página PDF"],"ru":["Извлечение текста из документов PDF","Автоматизация заполнения форм PDF с помощью Python","Отладка структуры и содержания страницы PDF"],"ar":["استخراج النص من مستندات PDF","الآلية التلقائية لتعبئة نماذج PDF باستخدام Python","تصحيح الهياكل والمحتوى لصفحات PDF"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires pypdf library installation","Python compatibility required","Limited to PDF file format"],"zh":["需要安装pypdf库","需要Python兼容性","仅限PDF文件格式"],"ja":["pypdfライブラリのインストールが必要","Pythonの互換性が必要","PDFファイル形式のみに制限される"],"ko":["pypdf 라이브러리 설치 필요","Python 호환성 필요","PDF 파일 형식만 해당"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de la biblioteca pypdf","Se requiere compatibilidad con Python","Limitado al formato de archivo de PDF"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de la bibliothèque pypdf","Compatibilité Python requise","Limité au format de fichier de PDF"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation der pypdf-Bibliothek","Python-Kompatibilität erforderlich","Begrenzt auf das PDF-Dateiformat"],"pt":["Requer instalação da biblioteca pypdf","Compatibilidade com Python necessária","Limitado ao formato de arquivo PDF"],"ru":["Требуется установка библиотеки pypdf","Требуется совместимость с Python","Ограничен форматом файла PDF"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت مكتبة pypdf","مطلوب توافق مع Python","محدود بنظام ملف PDF"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
