hlen mit Sicherheitskontrollen","Konfiguration von erlaubten und verbotenen Pfaden","Kompatibilität mit erweiterten Lese- und Schreibmodi"],"pt":["Leitura e escrita de arquivos com fs_read e fs_write","Execução de comandos do shell com execute_bash","Configuração de caminhos permitidos e negados","Suporte a modos de leitura e escrita diferentes","Segurança com controles de acesso e fallback"],"ru":["Чтение и запись файлов с помощью fs_read и fs_write","Выполнение команд оболочки с помощью execute_bash","Настройка разрешенных и запрещенных путей","Поддержка различных режимов чтения и записи","Безопасность с помощью контроля доступа и fallback"],"ar":["قراءة وكتابة الملفات باستخدام fs_read و fs_write","تنفيذ أوامر Shell باستخدام execute_bash","ضبط المسارات المسموح بها والمنعها","دعم أوضاع قراءة وكتابة مختلفة","أمان مع التحكم في الوصول والallback"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kiro 工具","文件读写","bash 命令","安全检查","配置选项","开发者工具"],"ja":["Kiro ツール","ファイルの読み書き","bash コマンド","セキュリティチェック","設定オプション","開発者ツール"],"ko":["Kiro 도구","파일 읽기/쓰기","bash 명령어","보안 점검","설정 옵션","개발자 도구"],"es":["herramientas de kiro","desarrollo de software","lectura y escritura de archivos","ejecución de comandos de shell","seguridad de desarrollo","configuración de rutas"],"fr":["outils kiro","développement de logiciels","lecture et écriture de fichiers","exécution de commandes shell","sécurité de développement","configuration des chemins"],"de":["kiro-tools","software-entwicklung","lesen und schreiben von dateien","ausführen von shell-befehlen","sicherheit in der entwicklung","konfiguration von pfaden"],"pt":["Kiro","ferramentas built-in","fs_read","fs_write","execute_bash","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","segurança","controle de acesso"],"ru":["Kiro","встроенные инструменты","fs_read","fs_write","execute_bash","разработка приложений","безопасность","контроль доступа"],"ar":["Kiro","أدوات مدمجة","fs_read","fs_write","execute_bash","تطوير التطبيقات","أمان","تحكم الوصول"]}},"owner":"ryolambert","repo":"kiro-wiz","repoPath":"ryolambert/kiro-wiz","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kiro-tools-reference","description":"Reference for all Kiro built-in tools and their configuration. Use when configuring toolsSettings in agents.","bodyPreview":"# Kiro Built-in Tools Reference\n\n## fs_read\nRead files, directories, images. Modes: Line, Directory, Search, Image.\nConfig: `allowedPaths`, `deniedPaths`\n\n## fs_write\nCreate/modify files. Commands: create, str_replace, insert, append.\nConfig: `allowedPaths`, `deniedPaths`, `fallbackAction` (interactive|deny)\n\n## execute_bash\nRun shell commands with safety checks.\nConfig: `allowedCommands` (regex), `deniedCommands` (regex), `autoAllowReadonly`, `denyByDefault`\nRead-only commands: ls, cat, echo, p","body":"# Kiro Built-in Tools Reference\n\n## fs_read\nRead files, directories, images. Modes: Line, Directory, Search, Image.\nConfig: `allowedPaths`, `deniedPaths`\n\n## fs_write\nCreate/modify files. Commands: create, str_replace, insert, append.\nConfig: `allowedPaths`, `deniedPaths`, `fallbackAction` (interactive|deny)\n\n## execute_bash\nRun shell commands with safety checks.\nConfig: `allowedCommands` (regex), `deniedCommands` (regex), `autoAllowReadonly`, `denyByDefault`\nRead-only commands: ls, cat, echo, pwd, which, head, tail, find, grep\n\n## grep\nRegex search across files. Respects .gitignore.\nModes: content, files_with_matches, count\nParams: pattern, path, include, case_sensitive, output_mode, max_matches_per_file, max_files\n\n## glob\nFind files by glob pattern. Respects .gitignore.\nParams: pattern, path, limit, max_depth\n\n## code\nLSP-powered code intelligence: search_symbols, lookup_symbols, get_document_symbols, pattern_search, pattern_rewrite\n\n## use_aws\nAWS CLI integration.\nConfig: `allowedServices`, `autoAllowReadonly`\n\n## introspect\nSearch Kiro documentation. Used by help agent.\n\n## knowledge\nKnowledge base search (requires `chat.enableKnowledge` setting)\n\n## thinking\nExtended reasoning (requires `chat.enableThinking` setting)\n\n## todo_list\nTask management (requires `chat.enableTodoList` setting)\n\n## delegate\nSubagent delegation (requires `chat.enableDelegate` setting)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:20:29.814Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced System Agents requiring secure file system interactions and bash command execution.","zh":"适用于需要安全文件系统交互和bash命令执行的高级系统代理。","ja":"セキュアなファイルシステムの相互作用とbashコマンドの実行を必要とする高度なシステムエージェントに適しています。","ko":"보안 파일 시스템 상호 작용 및 bash 명령 실행이 필요한 고급 시스템 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Sistemas Avanzados que requieren interacciones de sistema de archivos seguras y ejecución de comandos bash.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de système avancés nécessitant des interactions de système de fichiers sécurisées et une exécution de commande bash.","de":"Ideal für erweiterte Systemagenten, die sichere Dateisysteminteraktionen und die Ausführung von Bash-Befehlen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Sistema Avançados que exigem interações de sistema de arquivos seguras e execução de comandos bash.","ru":"Идеален для продвинутых системных агентов, требующих безопасного взаимодействия с файловой системой и выполнения команд bash.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النيابة المتقدمة الذين يتطلبون تفاعلات نظام ملفات آمنة وتحكم في تنفيذ أوامر الباش."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to read files, directories, and images with configurable modes, while also enabling safe bash command execution with allowed and denied command lists, and securely creating or modifying files with fallback actions.","zh":"赋予代理读取文件、目录和图像的能力，具有可配置的模式，同时也允许安全的bash命令执行，具有允许和拒绝的命令列表，并使用回退操作安全地创建或修改文件。","ja":"エージェントにファイル、ディレクトリ、画像を読み取る機能を提供し、可構成モードを備えながら、安全なbashコマンドの実行も可能にします。許可されたコマンドと拒否されたコマンドのリストを使用し、フォールバックアクションを使用してファイルを安全に作成または変更します。","ko":"에이전트가 파일, 디렉토리 및 이미지를 읽을 수 있도록 구성 가능한 모드와 함께 안전한 bash 명령 실행을 가능하게 하며, 허용 및 거부 명령 목록을 사용하여 파일을 보안으로 생성 또는 수정할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a leer archivos, directorios e imágenes con modos configurables, y también permite la ejecución segura de comandos bash con listas de comandos permitidos y denegados, y la creación o modificación segura de archivos con acciones de reserva.","fr":"Permet aux agents de lire des fichiers, des répertoires et des images avec des modes configurables, tout en permettant l''exécution sécurisée de commandes bash avec des listes de commandes autorisées et refusées, et la création ou la modification sécurisée de fichiers avec des actions de secours.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Dateien, Verzeichnisse und Bilder mit konfigurierbaren Modi zu lesen, ermöglicht auch die sichere Ausführung von Bash-Befehlen mit zulässigen und verbotenen Befehlslisten und die sichere Erstellung oder Änderung von Dateien mit Fallback-Aktionen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a ler arquivos, diretórios e imagens com modos configuráveis, além de permitir a execução segura de comandos bash com listas de comandos permitidos e negados, e criar ou modificar arquivos com ações de fallback de forma segura.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью читать файлы, директории и изображения с настраиваемыми режимами, а также обеспечивает безопасное выполнение команд bash с помощью списков разрешенных и запрещенных команд, и безопасно создает или изменяет файлы с настройками действий по умолчанию.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من قراءة الملفات والتوجيهات والصور مع أوضاع يمكن تكوينها، بالإضافة إلى تمكين تشغيل أوامر الباش بأمان باستخدام قوائم الأوامر المسموحة والمرفوضة، وإنشاء أو تعديل الملفات بأمان مع إعدادات الإجراءات الافتراضية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating file system operations with configurable allowed and denied paths","Executing bash commands with safety checks and read-only command support","Generating files with specific content using str_replace, insert, and append commands"],"zh":["使用可配置的允许和拒绝路径自动执行文件系统操作","使用安全检查和只读命令支持执行bash命令","使用str_replace、插入和追加命令生成具有特定内容的文件"],"ja":["許可されたパスと拒否されたパスの構成を使用してファイルシステム操作を自動化する","安全性のチェックと読み取り専用のコマンドサポートを使用してbashコマンドを実行する","str_replace、挿入、追加コマンドを使用して特定の内容を持つファイルを生成する"],"ko":["허용 및 거부 경로를 구성하여 파일 시스템 운영을 자동화하는 것","안전성 점검 및 읽기 전용 명령 지원을 사용하여 bash 명령을 실행하는 것","특정 내용을 갖는 파일을 생성하기 위해 str_replace, 삽입 및追加 명령을 사용하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar operaciones de sistema de archivos con rutas permitidas y denegadas configurables","Ejecutar comandos bash con comprobaciones de seguridad y soporte de comando de solo lectura","Generar archivos con contenido específico utilizando comandos str_replace, insertar y agregar"],"fr":["Automatiser les opérations de système de fichiers avec des chemins autorisés et refusés configurables","Exécuter des commandes bash avec des vérifications de sécurité et un support de commande en lecture seule","Générer des fichiers avec un contenu spécifique en utilisant des commandes str_replace, insérer et ajouter"],"de":["Automatisieren von Dateisystemoperationen mit konfigurierbaren erlaubten und verbotenen Pfaden","Ausführen von Bash-Befehlen mit Sicherheitsprüfungen und Unterstützung von nur-Lese-Befehlen","Erstellen von Dateien mit spezifischem Inhalt unter Verwendung von Befehlen str_replace, einfügen und anhängen"],"pt":["Automatizar operações de sistema de arquivos com caminhos permitidos e negados configuráveis","Executar comandos bash com verificações de segurança e suporte a comandos somente leitura","Gerar arquivos com conteúdo específico usando comandos str_replace, insert e append"],"ru":["Автоматизировать операции с файловой системой с настраиваемыми разрешенными и запрещенными путями","Выполнять команды bash с проверками безопасности и поддержкой команд только для чтения","Генерировать файлы с конкретным содержимым, используя команды str_replace, insert и append"],"ar":["أتمتة عمليات نظام الملفات مع مسارات يمكن تكوينها مسموح بها ومرفوضة","تشغيل أوامر الباش مع فحص الأمان ودعم الأوامر للقراءة فقط","إنشاء ملفات بمحتوى محدد باستخدام أوامر استبدال السلسلة وإدراج والتعليمات الإضافية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires configuration of allowed and denied paths for file system operations","Bash command execution limited by allowed and denied command lists","File system write operations subject to fallback action configuration"],"zh":["需要配置允许和拒绝的路径用于文件系统操作","bash命令执行受到允许和拒绝的命令列表的限制","文件系统写入操作受到回退操作配置的限制"],"ja":["ファイルシステム操作のために許可されたパスと拒否されたパスの構成が必要","bashコマンドの実行は許可されたコマンドと拒否されたコマンドのリストによって制限される","ファイルシステムの書き込み操作はフォールバックアクションの構成によって制限される"],"ko":["파일 시스템 운영을 위해 허용 및 거부 경로의 구성이 필요함","bash 명령의 실행이 허용 및 거부 명령 목록에 의해 제한됨","파일 시스템 쓰기 작업이 폴백 동작 구성에 의해 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere configuración de rutas permitidas y denegadas para operaciones de sistema de archivos","La ejecución de comandos bash está limitada por listas de comandos permitidos y denegados","Las operaciones de escritura del sistema de archivos están sujetas a la configuración de acciones de reserva"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de chemins autorisés et refusés pour les opérations de système de fichiers","L''exécution de commandes bash est limitée par des listes de commandes autorisées et refusées","Les opérations d''écriture du système de fichiers sont soumises à la configuration d''actions de secours"],"de":["Erfordert Konfiguration von erlaubten und verbotenen Pfaden für Dateisystemoperationen","Die Ausführung von Bash-Befehlen ist durch zulässige und verbotene Befehlslisten beschränkt","Dateisystem-Schreiboperationen unterliegen der Konfiguration von Fallback-Aktionen"],"pt":["Exige a configuração de caminhos permitidos e negados para operações de sistema de arquivos","A execução de comandos bash é limitada por listas de comandos permitidos e negados","Operações de gravação de sistema de arquivos estão sujeitas à configuração de ações de fallback"],"ru":["Требует настройки разрешенных и запрещенных путей для операций с файловой системой","Выполнение команд bash ограничено списками разрешенных и запрещенных команд","Операции записи файловой системы подлежат настройке действий по умолчанию"],"ar":["يتطلب تكوين مسارات يمكن تكوينها مسموح بها ومرفوضة لعمليات نظام الملفات","تنفيذ أوامر الباش مقيد بقوائم الأوامر المسموحة والمرفوضة","عمليات كتابة نظام الملفات خاضعة لإعدادات الإجراءات الافتراضية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/Backend Models Standards', 'community', 'yashvinthan', 'DuskSpendr', 'yashvinthan/DuskSpendr', 'Backend Models Standards', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:20:35.547Z', NULL, '{"id":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr/Backend Models Standards","name":"Backend Models Standards","description":{"zh":"后端模型标准定义数据结构和完整性，保持模型专注于数据表示","ja":"バックエンドモデル標準はデータ構造と整合性を定義し、モデルをデータ表現に集中させる","ko":"백엔드 모델 표준은 데이터 구조와 무결성을 정의하고 모델을 데이터 표현에 집중시킵니다","es":"Los modelos de datos definidos correctamente son fundamentales para un proyecto backend sólido. Aprende a estructurar tus datos de manera efectiva","fr":"Les modèles de données correctement définis sont fondamentaux pour un projet backend solide. Apprenez à structurer vos données de manière efficace","de":"Richtig definierte Datenmodelle sind für ein solides Backend-Projekt von entscheidender Bedeutung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Ihre Daten effektiv strukturieren","pt":"Os modelos de backend definem a estrutura de dados e a integridade, mantendo-se focados na representação de dados, não na lógica de negócios.","ru":"Модели бэкенда определяют структуру данных и целостность, сохраняя фокус на представлении данных, а не на логике бизнеса.","ar":"تنص نماذج الخلفية على بنية البيانات والسلامة، مع التركيز على تمثيل البيانات وليس منطق الأعمال.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"后端模型标准","ja":"バックエンドモデル標準","ko":"백엔드 모델 표준","es":"Estándares de Modelos Backend","fr":"Normes de Modèles Backend","de":"Backend-Modellstandards","pt":"Padrões de Modelos de Backend","ru":"Стандарты моделей бэкенда","ar":"معايير نماذج الخلفية","en":"Backend Models Standards"},"description":{"zh":"后端模型标准定义数据结构和完整性，保持模型专注于数据表示","ja":"バックエンドモデル標準はデータ構造と整合性を定義し、モデルをデータ表現に集中させる","ko":"백엔드 모델 표준은 데이터 구조와 무결성을 정의하고 모델을 데이터 표현에 집중시킵니다","es":"Los modelos de datos definidos correctamente son fundamentales para un proyecto backend sólido. Aprende a estructurar tus datos de manera efectiva","fr":"Les modèles de données correctement définis sont fondamentaux pour un projet backend solide. Apprenez à structurer vos données de manière efficace","de":"Richtig definierte Datenmodelle sind für ein solides Backend-Projekt von entscheidender Bedeutung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Ihre Daten effektiv strukturieren","pt":"Os modelos de backend definem a estrutura de dados e a integridade, mantendo-se focados na representação de dados, não na lógica de negócios.","ru":"Модели бэкенда определяют структуру данных и целостность, сохраняя фокус на представлении данных, а не на логике бизнеса.","ar":"تنص نماذج الخلفية على بنية البيانات والسلامة، مع التركيز على تمثيل البيانات وليس منطق الأعمال.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["定义数据结构","保持模型专注于数据表示","配置外键和索引","建立表关系","优化数据完整性"],"ja":["データ構造の定義","モデルをデータ表現に集中させる","外键と索引の設定","テーブル関係の確立","データ整合性の最適化"],"ko":["데이터 구조 정의","모델을 데이터 표현에 집중시키기","외부 키 및 인덱스 구성","테이블 관계 설정","데이터 무결성 최적화"],"es":["Definición de la estructura de datos","Establecimiento de relaciones entre tablas","Configuración de claves foráneas e índices","Implementación de comportamientos en cascada","Uso de ORM y ActiveRecord","Creación de esquemas de bases de datos"],"fr":["Définition de la structure des données","Établissement de relations entre les tables","Configuration des clés étrangères et des index","Mise en œuvre de comportements en cascade","Utilisation d''ORM et d''ActiveRecord","Création de schémas de bases de données"],"de":["Definition der Datenstruktur","Herstellung von Beziehungen zwischen Tabellen","Konfiguration von Fremdschlüsseln und Indizes","Implementierung von Cascade-Verhaltensweisen","Verwendung von ORM und ActiveRecord","Erstellung von Datenbankschemata"],"pt":["Definição de estrutura de dados","Manutenção da integridade dos dados","Separação da lógica de negócios","Configuração de chaves estrangeiras e índices","Definição de relacionamentos entre tabelas"],"ru":["Определение структуры данных","Поддержание целостности данных","Отделение логики бизнеса","Настройка внешних ключей и индексов","Определение отношений между таблицами"],"ar":["تعريف بنية البيانات","الحفاظ على سلامة البيانات","فصل منطق الأعمال","تكوين المفاتيح الخارجية والفهرس","تعريف العلاقات بين الجداول"]},"keywords":{"zh":["后端模型","数据结构","数据完整性","模型设计","数据库设计","后端开发"],"ja":["バックエンドモデル","データ構造","データ整合性","モデル設計","データベース設計","バックエンド開発"],"ko":["백엔드 모델","데이터 구조","데이터 무결성","모델 설계","데이터베이스 설계","백엔드 개발"],"es":["modelos de datos","backend","ORM","ActiveRecord","bases de datos","esquemas de datos","integridad de datos","estructura de datos","relaciones entre tablas"],"fr":["modèles de données","backend","ORM","ActiveRecord","bases de données","schémas de données","intégrité des données","structure des données","relations entre les tables"],"de":["Datenmodelle","Backend","ORM","ActiveRecord","Datenbanken","Datenbankschemata","Datenintegrität","Datenstruktur","Beziehungen zwischen Tabellen"],"pt":["modelos de backend","padrões de modelos","estrutura de dados","integridade de dados","lógica de negócios","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["модели бэкенда","стандарты моделей","структура данных","целостность данных","логика бизнеса","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["نماذج الخلفية","معايير النماذج","بنية البيانات","سلامة البيانات","منطق الأعمال","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Backend Models Standards","description":"Define database models with clear naming, appropriate data types, constraints, relationships, and validation at multiple layers. Use this skill when creating or modifying database model files, ORM classes, schema definitions, or data model relationships. Apply when working with model files (e.g., models.py, models/, ActiveRecord classes, Prisma schema, Sequelize models), defining table structures, setting up foreign keys and relationships, configuring cascade behaviors, implementing model validations, adding timestamps, or working with database constraints (NOT NULL, UNIQUE, foreign keys). Use for any task involving data integrity enforcement, relationship definitions, or model-level data validation.","bodyPreview":"# Backend Models Standards\n\n**Core Rule:** Models define data structure and integrity. Keep them focused on data representation, not business logic.\n\n## When to use this skill\n\n- When creating or modifying database model files (models.py, models/, schema.prisma, etc.)\n- When defining ORM classes or ActiveRecord models for database tables\n- When establishing table relationships (one-to-many, many-to-many, has-many, belongs-to)\n- When configuring foreign keys, indexes, and cascade behaviors\n- When","body":"# Backend Models Standards\n\n**Core Rule:** Models define data structure and integrity. Keep them focused on data representation, not business logic.\n\n## When to use this skill\n\n- When creating or modifying database model files (models.py, models/, schema.prisma, etc.)\n- When defining ORM classes or ActiveRecord models for database tables\n- When establishing table relationships (one-to-many, many-to-many, has-many, belongs-to)\n- When configuring foreign keys, indexes, and cascade behaviors\n- When implementing model-level validation rules\n- When adding timestamp fields (created_at, updated_at) for auditing\n- When setting database constraints (NOT NULL, UNIQUE, CHECK constraints)\n- When choosing appropriate data types for model fields\n- When balancing normalization with query performance needs\n- When defining model methods or scopes for common queries\n\nThis Skill provides Claude Code with specific guidance on how to adhere to coding standards as they relate to how it should handle backend models.\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n**Models:** Singular, PascalCase (`User`, `OrderItem`, `PaymentMethod`)\n\n**Tables:** Plural, snake_case (`users`, `order_items`, `payment_methods`)\n\n**Relationships:** Descriptive and clear\n- `user.orders` (one-to-many)\n- `order.items` (one-to-many)\n- `product.categories` (many-to-many)\n\n**Avoid generic names:** `data`, `info`, `record`, `entity`\n\n## Required Fields\n\n**Timestamps on every model:**\n```python\ncreated_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=False, default=datetime.utcnow)\nupdated_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=False, default=datetime.utcnow, onupdate=datetime.utcnow)\n```\n\n**Primary keys:** Always explicit, prefer UUIDs for distributed systems or auto-incrementing integers for simplicity\n\n**Why:** Auditing, debugging, data lineage tracking, soft deletes\n\n## Data Integrity - Database Level\n\n**Use constraints, not just application validation:**\n\n```python\n# NOT NULL for required fields\nemail = Column(String(255), nullable=False)\n\n# UNIQUE constraints\nemail = Column(String(255), unique=True, nullable=False)\n\n# CHECK constraints for business rules\nage = Column(Integer, CheckConstraint(''age >= 18''))\n\n# Foreign keys with explicit cascade behavior\nuser_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(''users.id'', ondelete=''CASCADE''))\n```\n\n**Why:** Database enforces rules even if application code bypassed. Defense in depth.\n\n## Data Types - Choose Appropriately\n\n| Data       | Type               | Avoid       |\n| ---------- | ------------------ | ----------- |\n| Email, URL | VARCHAR(255)       | TEXT        |\n| Short text | VARCHAR(n)         | TEXT        |\n| Long text  | TEXT               | VARCHAR     |\n| Money      | DECIMAL(10,2)      | FLOAT       |\n| Boolean    | BOOLEAN            | TINYINT     |\n| Timestamps | TIMESTAMP/DATETIME | VARCHAR     |\n| JSON data  | JSON/JSONB         | TEXT        |\n| UUIDs      | UUID               | VARCHAR(36) |\n\n**Why:** Correct types enable database optimizations, constraints, and prevent data corruption.\n\n## Indexes - Performance Critical\n\n**Always index:**\n- Primary keys (automatic)\n- Foreign keys (manual in most ORMs)\n- Columns in WHERE clauses\n- Columns in JOIN conditions\n- Columns in ORDER BY clauses\n\n**Example:**\n```python\nclass Order(Base):\n    __tablename__ = ''orders''\n    \n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n    user_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(''users.id''), index=True)\n    status = Column(String(50), index=True)  # Frequently filtered\n    created_at = Column(DateTime, index=True)  # Frequently sorted\n```\n\n**Don''t over-index:** Each index slows writes. Index only queried columns.\n\n## Relationships - Explicit Configuration\n\n**Define both sides of relationships:**\n\n```python\n# One-to-many\nclass User(Base):\n    orders = relationship(''Order'', back_populates=''user'', cascade=''all, delete-orphan'')\n\nclass Order(Base):\n    user_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(''users.id''))\n    user = relationship(''User'', back_populates=''orders'')\n```\n\n**Cascade behaviors:**\n- `CASCADE`: Delete related records (user deleted → orders deleted)\n- `SET NULL`: Nullify foreign key (category deleted → product.category_id = NULL)\n- `RESTRICT`: Prevent deletion if related records exist\n- `NO ACTION`: Database default, usually same as RESTRICT\n\n**Choose based on business logic, not convenience.**\n\n## Validation - Two Layers\n\n**Model-level validation (application):**\n```python\n@validates(''email'')\ndef validate_email(self, key, email):\n    if not re.match(r''^[^@]+@[^@]+\\.[^@]+$'', email):\n        raise ValueError(''Invalid email format'')\n    return email\n```\n\n**Database-level constraints (see Data Integrity section)**\n\n**Why both:** Model validation provides clear error messages. Database constraints prevent data corruption if application bypassed.\n\n## What Belongs in Models\n\n**YES:**\n- Field definitions and types\n- Relationships to other models\n- Simple property methods (`@property def full_name`)\n- Data validation rules\n- Database constraints\n\n**NO:**\n- Business logic (move to service layer)\n- External API calls\n- Complex calculations (move to service methods)\n- Email sending, file uploads, etc.\n\n**Models represent data structure, not behavior.**\n\n## Normalization vs Performance\n\n**Normalize when:**\n- Data has clear entity boundaries\n- Updates need to propagate (user email changes once)\n- Avoiding data duplication is critical\n\n**Denormalize when:**\n- Read performance critical (analytics, reporting)\n- Data rarely changes (historical snapshots)\n- Joins become too expensive\n\n**Default to normalized. Denormalize only with evidence of performance issues.**\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n**Soft deletes:**\n```python\ndeleted_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=True, index=True)\n\n# Query only active records\nquery = session.query(User).filter(User.deleted_at.is_(None))\n```\n\n**Polymorphic associations:**\n```python\n# Avoid if possible - complex and hard to maintain\n# Prefer separate relationship fields or inheritance\n```\n\n**Enums for fixed values:**\n```python\nfrom enum import Enum\n\nclass OrderStatus(str, Enum):\n    PENDING = ''pending''\n    PAID = ''paid''\n    SHIPPED = ''shipped''\n    DELIVERED = ''delivered''\n\nstatus = Column(Enum(OrderStatus), nullable=False, default=OrderStatus.PENDING)\n```\n\n## Testing Models\n\n**Test constraints and validation:**\n```python\ndef test_user_email_required():\n    with pytest.raises(IntegrityError):\n        user = User(name=''Test'')\n        session.add(user)\n        session.commit()\n\ndef test_user_email_unique():\n    user1 = User(email=''test@example.com'')\n    user2 = User(email=''test@example.com'')\n    session.add(user1)\n    session.commit()\n    \n    with pytest.raises(IntegrityError):\n        session.add(user2)\n        session.commit()\n```\n\n**Test relationships:**\n```python\ndef test_user_orders_cascade_delete():\n    user = User(email=''test@example.com'')\n    order = Order(user=user)\n    session.add(user)\n    session.commit()\n    \n    session.delete(user)\n    session.commit()\n    \n    assert session.query(Order).count() == 0\n```\n\n## Checklist for New Models\n\n- [ ] Singular model name, plural table name\n- [ ] Primary key defined\n- [ ] `created_at` and `updated_at` timestamps\n- [ ] NOT NULL on required fields\n- [ ] UNIQUE constraints where appropriate\n- [ ] Foreign keys with explicit cascade behavior\n- [ ] Indexes on foreign keys and queried columns\n- [ ] Appropriate data types (not all VARCHAR)\n- [ ] Validation at model and database levels\n- [ ] Relationships defined on both sides\n- [ ] Tests for constraints and validation\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:20:35.547Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Model-Driven Agents requiring standardized backend data structures and integrity","zh":"适用于需要标准化后端数据结构和完整性的模型驱动代理","ja":"標準化されたバックエンドデータ構造と整合性が必要なモデル駆動エージェントに適しています","ko":"표준화된 백엔드 데이터 구조와 완전성이 필요한 모델 기반 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes basados en modelos que requieren estructuras de datos de backend estandarizadas y integridad","fr":"Idéal pour les agents basés sur des modèles nécessitant des structures de données de backend standardisées et une intégrité","de":"Ideal für modellbasierte Agenten, die standardisierte Backend-Datensstrukturen und Integrität erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Dirigidos por Modelo que exigem estruturas de dados de backend padronizadas e integridade","ru":"Идеально для агентов, управляемых моделью, требующих стандартизированных структур данных бэкенда и целостности","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الموجهين بالنموذج الذين يتطلبون هيكلات بيانات خلفية معيارية وسلامة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define robust data representations using ORM classes and ActiveRecord models, establishing relationships and configuring foreign keys, indexes, and cascade behaviors with precision, leveraging models.py, schema.prisma, and other database model files","zh":"赋予代理定义使用ORM类和ActiveRecord模型的强大的数据表示，建立关系并配置外键、索引和级联行