,"CLI","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode"],"ja":["レッドチーム戦術","MITRE ATT&CK","対抗シミュレーション","設定変換","IDE","CLI","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode"],"ko":["레드 팀 전술","MITRE ATT&CK","적대자 시뮬레이션","설정 변환","IDE","CLI","GitHub Copilot","Cursor","Kiro","OpenCode"],"es":["tácticas de equipo rojo","simulación de adversarios","MITRE ATT&CK","seguridad informática","pruebas de seguridad","desarrollo de software","IDEs","CLIs","GitHub Copilot","Kiro"],"fr":["tactiques d''équipe rouge","simulation d''adversaires","MITRE ATT&CK","sécurité informatique","tests de sécurité","développement de logiciels","IDE","CLIs","GitHub Copilot","Kiro"],"de":["Rote-Team-Taktiken","Adversary-Simulation","MITRE-ATT&CK","IT-Sicherheit","Sicherheitstests","Software-Entwicklung","IDEs","CLIs","GitHub Copilot","Kiro"],"pt":["Red Team Tactics","MITRE ATT&CK","Simulação de ameaças","Conversão de configurações","Segurança cibernética","Testes de segurança","Otimização de configurações"],"ru":["Тактика Красной Команды","MITRE ATT&CK","Симуляция угроз","Конвертация конфигураций","Кибербезопасность","Тестирование безопасности","Оптимизация конфигураций"],"ar":["تكتيكات الفريق الأحمر","MITRE ATT&CK","محاكاة التهديدات","تحويل التكوينات","أمن المعلومات","اختبار الأمان","تحسين التكوينات"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"red-team-tactics","description":"Red team tactics principles based on MITRE ATT&CK. Attack phases, detection evasion, reporting.","bodyPreview":"# Red Team Tactics\n\n> Adversary simulation principles based on MITRE ATT&CK framework.\n\n---\n\n## 1. MITRE ATT&CK Phases\n\n### Attack Lifecycle\n\n```\nRECONNAISSANCE → INITIAL ACCESS → EXECUTION → PERSISTENCE\n       ↓              ↓              ↓            ↓\n   PRIVILEGE ESC → DEFENSE EVASION → CRED ACCESS → DISCOVERY\n       ↓              ↓              ↓            ↓\nLATERAL MOVEMENT → COLLECTION → C2 → EXFILTRATION → IMPACT\n```\n\n### Phase Objectives\n\n| Phase | Objective |\n|-------|-----------|\n|","body":"# Red Team Tactics\n\n> Adversary simulation principles based on MITRE ATT&CK framework.\n\n---\n\n## 1. MITRE ATT&CK Phases\n\n### Attack Lifecycle\n\n```\nRECONNAISSANCE → INITIAL ACCESS → EXECUTION → PERSISTENCE\n       ↓              ↓              ↓            ↓\n   PRIVILEGE ESC → DEFENSE EVASION → CRED ACCESS → DISCOVERY\n       ↓              ↓              ↓            ↓\nLATERAL MOVEMENT → COLLECTION → C2 → EXFILTRATION → IMPACT\n```\n\n### Phase Objectives\n\n| Phase | Objective |\n|-------|-----------|\n| **Recon** | Map attack surface |\n| **Initial Access** | Get first foothold |\n| **Execution** | Run code on target |\n| **Persistence** | Survive reboots |\n| **Privilege Escalation** | Get admin/root |\n| **Defense Evasion** | Avoid detection |\n| **Credential Access** | Harvest credentials |\n| **Discovery** | Map internal network |\n| **Lateral Movement** | Spread to other systems |\n| **Collection** | Gather target data |\n| **C2** | Maintain command channel |\n| **Exfiltration** | Extract data |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Reconnaissance Principles\n\n### Passive vs Active\n\n| Type | Trade-off |\n|------|-----------|\n| **Passive** | No target contact, limited info |\n| **Active** | Direct contact, more detection risk |\n\n### Information Targets\n\n| Category | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Technology stack | Attack vector selection |\n| Employee info | Social engineering |\n| Network ranges | Scanning scope |\n| Third parties | Supply chain attack |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Initial Access Vectors\n\n### Selection Criteria\n\n| Vector | When to Use |\n|--------|-------------|\n| **Phishing** | Human target, email access |\n| **Public exploits** | Vulnerable services exposed |\n| **Valid credentials** | Leaked or cracked |\n| **Supply chain** | Third-party access |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Privilege Escalation Principles\n\n### Windows Targets\n\n| Check | Opportunity |\n|-------|-------------|\n| Unquoted service paths | Write to path |\n| Weak service permissions | Modify service |\n| Token privileges | Abuse SeDebug, etc. |\n| Stored credentials | Harvest |\n\n### Linux Targets\n\n| Check | Opportunity |\n|-------|-------------|\n| SUID binaries | Execute as owner |\n| Sudo misconfiguration | Command execution |\n| Kernel vulnerabilities | Kernel exploits |\n| Cron jobs | Writable scripts |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Defense Evasion Principles\n\n### Key Techniques\n\n| Technique | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| LOLBins | Use legitimate tools |\n| Obfuscation | Hide malicious code |\n| Timestomping | Hide file modifications |\n| Log clearing | Remove evidence |\n\n### Operational Security\n\n- Work during business hours\n- Mimic legitimate traffic patterns\n- Use encrypted channels\n- Blend with normal behavior\n\n---\n\n## 6. Lateral Movement Principles\n\n### Credential Types\n\n| Type | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| Password | Standard auth |\n| Hash | Pass-the-hash |\n| Ticket | Pass-the-ticket |\n| Certificate | Certificate auth |\n\n### Movement Paths\n\n- Admin shares\n- Remote services (RDP, SSH, WinRM)\n- Exploitation of internal services\n\n---\n\n## 7. Active Directory Attacks\n\n### Attack Categories\n\n| Attack | Target |\n|--------|--------|\n| Kerberoasting | Service account passwords |\n| AS-REP Roasting | Accounts without pre-auth |\n| DCSync | Domain credentials |\n| Golden Ticket | Persistent domain access |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Reporting Principles\n\n### Attack Narrative\n\nDocument the full attack chain:\n1. How initial access was gained\n2. What techniques were used\n3. What objectives were achieved\n4. Where detection failed\n\n### Detection Gaps\n\nFor each successful technique:\n- What should have detected it?\n- Why didn''t detection work?\n- How to improve detection\n\n---\n\n## 9. Ethical Boundaries\n\n### Always\n\n- Stay within scope\n- Minimize impact\n- Report immediately if real threat found\n- Document all actions\n\n### Never\n\n- Destroy production data\n- Cause denial of service (unless scoped)\n- Access beyond proof of concept\n- Retain sensitive data\n\n---\n\n## 10. Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ Don''t | ✅ Do |\n|----------|-------|\n| Rush to exploitation | Follow methodology |\n| Cause damage | Minimize impact |\n| Skip reporting | Document everything |\n| Ignore scope | Stay within boundaries |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Red team simulates attackers to improve defenses, not to cause harm.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:21:02.351Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cybersecurity Agents needing advanced threat simulation and MITRE ATT&CK framework integration.","zh":"非常适合需要高级威胁模拟和MITRE ATT&CK框架集成的网络安全代理。","ja":"高度な脅威シミュレーションとMITRE ATT&CKフレームワークの統合が必要なサイバーセキュリティエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 위협 시뮬레이션 및 MITRE ATT&CK 프레임워크 통합이 필요한 사이버 보안 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Cybersecurity Agents needing advanced threat simulation and MITRE ATT&CK framework integration.","fr":"Perfect for Cybersecurity Agents needing advanced threat simulation and MITRE ATT&CK framework integration.","de":"Perfect for Cybersecurity Agents needing advanced threat simulation and MITRE ATT&CK framework integration.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Cibersegurança que necessitam de simulação de ameaças avançadas e integração do framework MITRE ATT&CK.","ru":"Идеально для агентов кибербезопасности, которым требуются продвинутые симуляции угроз и интеграция с фреймворком MITRE ATT&CK.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الأمن السيبراني الذين يحتاجون إلى محاكاة تهديد متقدم وتكامل إطار عمل MITRE ATT&CK."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to simulate adversary attacks using the MITRE ATT&CK framework, providing comprehensive threat modeling and red teaming capabilities, including reconnaissance, initial access, and lateral movement tactics, all while utilizing CLIs like Kiro and OpenCode.","zh":"赋予代理模拟对手攻击的能力，使用MITRE ATT&CK框架，提供全面性的威胁建模和红队攻击能力，包括侦察、初始访问和横向移动策略，同时利用Kiro和OpenCode等命令行接口。","ja":"MITRE ATT&CKフレームワークを使用して対象の攻撃をシミュレートする機能をエージェントに与え、総合的な脅威モデリングとレッドチーム攻撃能力を提供し、偵察、初期アクセス、横方向移動戦術などを含み、KiroやOpenCodeなどのCLIを利用します。","ko":"MITRE ATT&CK 프레임워크를 사용하여 대응 공격을 시뮬레이션하는 기능을 에이전트에 부여하여 종합적인 위협 모델링 및 레드 팀 공격 기능을 제공하며, 정찰, 초기 접근 및 횡단 이동 전략 등을 포함하여 Kiro 및 OpenCode와 같은 CLI를 활용합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to simulate adversary attacks using the MITRE ATT&CK framework, providing comprehensive threat modeling and red teaming capabilities, including reconnaissance, initial access, and lateral movement tactics, all while utilizing CLIs like Kiro and OpenCode.","fr":"Empowers agents to simulate adversary attacks using the MITRE ATT&CK framework, providing comprehensive threat modeling and red teaming capabilities, including reconnaissance, initial access, and lateral movement tactics, all while utilizing CLIs like Kiro and OpenCode.","de":"Empowers agents to simulate adversary attacks using the MITRE ATT&CK framework, providing comprehensive threat modeling and red teaming capabilities, including reconnaissance, initial access, and lateral movement tactics, all while utilizing CLIs like Kiro and OpenCode.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a simular ataques de adversários usando o framework MITRE ATT&CK, fornecendo modelagem de ameaças abrangente e capacidades de red teaming, incluindo táticas de reconhecimento, acesso inicial e movimento lateral, tudo isso utilizando CLIs como Kiro e OpenCode.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью симулировать атаки противников с использованием фреймворка MITRE ATT&CK, обеспечивая комплексное моделирование угроз и возможности команды красных, включая тактику разведки, первоначального доступа и латерального движения, все это при использовании CLI, таких как Kiro и OpenCode.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من محاكاة هجمات المعارضين باستخدام إطار عمل MITRE ATT&CK، وتوفير نمذجة التهديد الشاملة وقدرات فريق الأحمر، بما في ذلك تكتيكات الاستطلاع والوصول الأولي والحركة الجانبية، وكل ذلك باستخدام واجهات سطر الأوامر مثل Kiro و OpenCode."},"useCases":{"en":["Simulating advanced threat scenarios using MITRE ATT&CK phases","Converting Antigravity IDE configurations for compatibility with GitHub Copilot and Cursor","Enhancing threat detection with red team tactics and techniques"],"zh":["使用MITRE ATT&CK阶段模拟高级威胁场景","将Antigravity IDE配置转换为与GitHub Copilot和Cursor兼容","使用红队战术和技术增强威胁检测"],"ja":["MITRE ATT&CKの段階を使用して高度な脅威シナリオをシミュレートする","Antigravity IDEの設定をGitHub CopilotおよびCursorと互換性のある形式に変換する","レッドチームの戦術とテクニックを使用して脅威検出を強化する"],"ko":["MITRE ATT&CK 단계를 사용하여 고급 위협 시나리오를 시뮬레이션하는 것","Antigravity IDE 설정을 GitHub Copilot 및 Cursor와 호환되는 형식으로 변환하는 것","레드 팀 전술 및 기술을 사용하여 위협 감지를 강화하는 것"],"es":["Simulating advanced threat scenarios using MITRE ATT&CK phases","Converting Antigravity IDE configurations for compatibility with GitHub Copilot and Cursor","Enhancing threat detection with red team tactics and techniques"],"fr":["Simulating advanced threat scenarios using MITRE ATT&CK phases","Converting Antigravity IDE configurations for compatibility with GitHub Copilot and Cursor","Enhancing threat detection with red team tactics and techniques"],"de":["Simulating advanced threat scenarios using MITRE ATT&CK phases","Converting Antigravity IDE configurations for compatibility with GitHub Copilot and Cursor","Enhancing threat detection with red team tactics and techniques"],"pt":["Simulando cenários de ameaças avançadas usando fases MITRE ATT&CK","Convertendo configurações do Antigravity IDE para compatibilidade com GitHub Copilot e Cursor","Melhorando a detecção de ameaças com táticas e técnicas de red teaming"],"ru":["Симулирование продвинутых сценариев угроз с использованием фаз MITRE ATT&CK","Преобразование конфигураций Antigravity IDE для совместимости с GitHub Copilot и Cursor","Улучшение обнаружения угроз с помощью тактик и техник команды красных"],"ar":["محاكاة سيناريوهات التهديد المتقدمة باستخدام مراحل MITRE ATT&CK","تحويل-configurations من Antigravity IDE للتوافق مع GitHub Copilot و Cursor","تحسين كشف التهديدات باستخدام تكتيكات و تقنيات فريق الأحمر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of MITRE ATT&CK framework","Limited to compatibility with specified IDEs and CLIs"],"zh":["需要了解MITRE ATT&CK框架","仅限与指定IDE和CLI兼容"],"ja":["MITRE ATT&CKフレームワークの知識が必要","指定されたIDEおよびCLIとの互換性のみ"],"ko":["MITRE ATT&CK 프레임워크에 대한 이해가 필요","지정된 IDE 및 CLI와의 호환성만"],"es":["Requires knowledge of MITRE ATT&CK framework","Limited to compatibility with specified IDEs and CLIs"],"fr":["Requires knowledge of MITRE ATT&CK framework","Limited to compatibility with specified IDEs and CLIs"],"de":["Requires knowledge of MITRE ATT&CK framework","Limited to compatibility with specified IDEs and CLIs"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento do framework MITRE ATT&CK","Limitado à compatibilidade com IDEs e CLIs especificados"],"ru":["Требуется знание фреймворка MITRE ATT&CK","Ограничен совместимостью с указанными IDE и CLI"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بإطار عمل MITRE ATT&CK","محدود بالتوافق مع IDEs و CLIs المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/dbt-transformation-patterns', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'dbt-transformation-patterns', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:21:11.240Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/dbt-transformation-patterns","name":"dbt-transformation-patterns","description":{"zh":"dbt, dbt","ja":"dbt, dbt","ko":"dbt, dbt","es":"Patrones de transformación dbt para desarrolladores, incluyendo organización de modelos, estrategias de testing y procesamiento incremental","fr":"Modèles de transformation dbt pour les développeurs, incluant l''organisation de modèles, les stratégies de test et le traitement incrémental","de":"dbt-Transformationsmuster für Entwickler, einschließlich Modellorganisation, Teststrategien und inkrementalem Verarbeiten","pt":"Padrões de transformação dbt para pipelines de dados escaláveis e organizados","ru":"Шаблоны преобразования dbt для масштабируемых и организованных конвейеров данных","ar":"أنماط تحويل dbt لتحويلات بيانات قابلة للتوسيع والمنظمة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"dbt ","ja":"dbt","ko":"dbt ","es":"Patrones de transformación dbt para desarrolladores","fr":"Modèles de transformation dbt pour les développeurs","de":"dbt-Transformationsmuster für Entwickler","pt":"Padrões de Transformação dbt","ru":"Шаблоны преобразования dbt","ar":"أنماط تحويل dbt","en":"dbt-transformation-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"dbt, dbt","ja":"dbt, dbt","ko":"dbt, dbt","es":"Patrones de transformación dbt para desarrolladores, incluyendo organización de modelos, estrategias de testing y procesamiento incremental","fr":"Modèles de transformation dbt pour les développeurs, incluant l''organisation de modèles, les stratégies de test et le traitement incrémental","de":"dbt-Transformationsmuster für Entwickler, einschließlich Modellorganisation, Teststrategien und inkrementalem Verarbeiten","pt":"Padrões de transformação dbt para pipelines de dados escaláveis e organizados","ru":"Шаблоны преобразования dbt для масштабируемых и организованных конвейеров данных","ar":"أنماط تحويل dbt لتحويلات بيانات قابلة للتوسيع والمنظمة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt"],"ja":["dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt"],"ko":["dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt"],"es":["Organización de modelos en capas de staging, intermedia e intermediate","Estrategias de testing para garantizar la calidad de los datos","Procesamiento incremental para grandes conjuntos de datos","Documentación de modelos de datos y linaje","Configuración de la estructura del proyecto dbt"],"fr":["Organisation de modèles en couches de staging, intermédiaire et mart","Stratégies de test pour garantir la qualité des données","Traitement incrémental pour les grands ensembles de données","Documentation des modèles de données et de la lignée","Configuration de la structure du projet dbt"],"de":["Modellorganisation in Staging-, Intermediate- und Mart-Schichten","Teststrategien für die Gewährleistung der Datenqualität","Inkrementelles Verarbeiten für große Datensätze","Dokumentation von Datenmodellen und -linie","Einrichtung der dbt-Projektstruktur"],"pt":["Organização de modelos em camadas","Estratégias de teste de qualidade de dados","Processamento incremental para grandes conjuntos de dados","Documentação de modelos de dados e linhagem","Configuração de estrutura de projeto dbt"],"ru":["Организация моделей в слоях","Стратегии тестирования качества данных","Инкрементальная обработка для больших наборов данных","Документация моделей данных и родословной","Настройка структуры проекта dbt"],"ar":["تنظيم النماذج في طبقات","استراتيجيات اختبار جودة البيانات","المعالجة التكرارية لل مجموعات البيانات الكبيرة","توثيق نماذج البيانات والنسل","تكوين هيكل مشروع dbt"]},"keywords":{"zh":["dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt"],"ja":["dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt"],"ko":["dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt","dbt"],"es":["dbt","transformación de datos","pipelines de datos","modelos de datos","testing de datos","procesamiento incremental","documentación de datos"],"fr":["dbt","transformation de données","pipelines de données","modèles de données","test de données","traitement incrémental","documentation de données"],"de":["dbt","DatenTransformation","Datenpipelines","Datenmodelle","DatenTesting","inkrementelles Verarbeiten","Dokumentation von Daten"],"pt":["dbt","transformação de dados","pipelines de dados","organização de modelos","testes de qualidade de dados","processamento incremental","documentação de dados"],"ru":["dbt","преобразование данных","конвейеры данных","организация моделей","тестирование качества данных","инкрементальная обработка","документация данных"],"ar":["dbt","تحويل البيانات","أنابيب البيانات","تنظيم النماذج","اختبار جودة البيانات","المعالجة التكرارية","توثيق البيانات"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dbt-transformation-patterns","description":"Master dbt (data build tool) for analytics engineering with model organization, testing, documentation, and incremental strategies. Use when building data transformations, creating data models, or implementing analytics engineering best practices.","bodyPreview":"# dbt Transformation Patterns\n\nProduction-ready patterns for dbt (data build tool) including model organization, testing strategies, documentation, and incremental processing.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building data transformation pipelines with dbt\n- Organizing models into staging, intermediate, and marts layers\n- Implementing data quality tests\n- Creating incremental models for large datasets\n- Documenting data models and lineage\n- Setting up dbt project structure\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1.","body":"# dbt Transformation Patterns\n\nProduction-ready patterns for dbt (data build tool) including model organization, testing strategies, documentation, and incremental processing.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Building data transformation pipelines with dbt\n- Organizing models into staging, intermediate, and marts layers\n- Implementing data quality tests\n- Creating incremental models for large datasets\n- Documenting data models and lineage\n- Setting up dbt project structure\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Model Layers (Medallion Architecture)\n\n```\nsources/          Raw data definitions\n    ↓\nstaging/          1:1 with source, light cleaning\n    ↓\nintermediate/     Business logic, joins, aggregations\n    ↓\nmarts/            Final analytics tables\n```\n\n### 2. Naming Conventions\n\n| Layer        | Prefix         | Example                       |\n| ------------ | -------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Staging      | `stg_`         | `stg_stripe__payments`        |\n| Intermediate | `int_`         | `int_payments_pivoted`        |\n| Marts        | `dim_`, `fct_` | `dim_customers`, `fct_orders` |\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```yaml\n# dbt_project.yml\nname: \"analytics\"\nversion: \"1.0.0\"\nprofile: \"analytics\"\n\nmodel-paths: [\"models\"]\nanalysis-paths: [\"analyses\"]\ntest-paths: [\"tests\"]\nseed-paths: [\"seeds\"]\nmacro-paths: [\"macros\"]\n\nvars:\n  start_date: \"2020-01-01\"\n\nmodels:\n  analytics:\n    staging:\n      +materialized: view\n      +schema: staging\n    intermediate:\n      +materialized: ephemeral\n    marts:\n      +materialized: table\n      +schema: analytics\n```\n\n```\n# Project structure\nmodels/\n├── staging/\n│   ├── stripe/\n│   │   ├── _stripe__sources.yml\n│   │   ├── _stripe__models.yml\n│   │   ├── stg_stripe__customers.sql\n│   │   └── stg_stripe__payments.sql\n│   └── shopify/\n│       ├── _shopify__sources.yml\n│       └── stg_shopify__orders.sql\n├── intermediate/\n│   └── finance/\n│       └── int_payments_pivoted.sql\n└── marts/\n    ├── core/\n    │   ├── _core__models.yml\n    │   ├── dim_customers.sql\n    │   └── fct_orders.sql\n    └── finance/\n        └── fct_revenue.sql\n```\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Source Definitions\n\n```yaml\n# models/staging/stripe/_stripe__sources.yml\nversion: 2\n\nsources:\n  - name: stripe\n    description: Raw Stripe data loaded via Fivetran\n    database: raw\n    schema: stripe\n    loader: fivetran\n    loaded_at_field: _fivetran_synced\n    freshness:\n      warn_after: { count: 12, period: hour }\n      error_after: { count: 24, period: hour }\n    tables:\n      - name: customers\n        description: Stripe customer records\n        columns:\n          - name: id\n            description: Primary key\n            tests:\n              - unique\n              - not_null\n          - name: email\n            description: Customer email\n          - name: created\n            description: Account creation timestamp\n\n      - name: payments\n        description: Stripe payment transactions\n        columns:\n          - name: id\n            tests:\n              - unique\n              - not_null\n          - name: customer_id\n            tests:\n              - not_null\n              - relationships:\n                  to: source(''stripe'', ''customers'')\n                  field: id\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Staging Models\n\n```sql\n-- models/staging/stripe/stg_stripe__customers.sql\nwith source as (\n    select * from {{ source(''stripe'', ''customers'') }}\n),\n\nrenamed as (\n    select\n        -- ids\n        id as customer_id,\n\n        -- strings\n        lower(email) as email,\n        name as customer_name,\n\n        -- timestamps\n        created as created_at,\n\n        -- metadata\n        _fivetran_synced as _loaded_at\n\n    from source\n)\n\nselect * from renamed\n```\n\n```sql\n-- models/staging/stripe/stg_stripe__payments.sql\n{{\n    config(\n        materialized=''incremental'',\n        unique_key=''payment_id'',\n        on_schema_change=''append_new_columns''\n    )\n}}\n\nwith source as (\n    select * from {{ source(''stripe'', ''payments'') }}\n\n    {% if is_incremental() %}\n    where _fivetran_synced > (select max(_loaded_at) from {{ this }})\n    {% endif %}\n),\n\nrenamed as (\n    select\n        -- ids\n        id as payment_id,\n        customer_id,\n        invoice_id,\n\n        -- amounts (convert cents to dollars)\n        amount / 100.0 as amount,\n        amount_refunded / 100.0 as amount_refunded,\n\n        -- status\n        status as payment_status,\n\n        -- timestamps\n        created as created_at,\n\n        -- metadata\n        _fivetran_synced as _loaded_at\n\n    from source\n)\n\nselect * from renamed\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Intermediate Models\n\n```sql\n-- models/intermediate/finance/int_payments_pivoted_to_customer.sql\nwith payments as (\n    select * from {{ ref(''stg_stripe__payments'') }}\n),\n\ncustomers as (\n    select * from {{ ref(''stg_stripe__customers'') }}\n),\n\npayment_summary as (\n    select\n        customer_id,\n        count(*) as total_payments,\n        count(case when payment_status = ''succeeded'' then 1 end) as successful_payments,\n        sum(case when payment_status = ''succeeded'' then amount else 0 end) as total_amount_paid,\n        min(created_at) as first_payment_at,\n        max(created_at) as last_payment_at\n    from payments\n    group by customer_id\n)\n\nselect\n    customers.customer_id,\n    customers.email,\n    customers.created_at as customer_created_at,\n    coalesce(payment_summary.total_payments, 0) as total_payments,\n    coalesce(payment_summary.successful_payments, 0) as successful_payments,\n    coalesce(payment_summary.total_amount_paid, 0) as lifetime_value,\n    payment_summary.first_payment_at,\n    payment_summary.last_payment_at\n\nfrom customers\nleft join payment_summary using (customer_id)\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Mart Models (Dimensions and Facts)\n\n```sql\n-- models/marts/core/dim_customers.sql\n{{\n    config(\n        materialized=''table'',\n        unique_key=''customer_id''\n    )\n}}\n\nwith customers as (\n    select * from {{ ref(''int_payments_pivoted_to_customer'') }}\n),\n\norders as (\n    select * from {{ ref(''stg_shopify__orders'') }}\n),\n\norder_summary as (\n    select\n        customer_id,\n        count(*) as total_orders,\n        sum(total_price) as total_order_value,\n        min(created_at) as first_order_at,\n        max(created_at) as last_order_at\n    from orders\n    group by customer_id\n),\n\nfinal as (\n    select\n        -- surrogate key\n        {{ dbt_utils.generate_surrogate_key([''customers.customer_id'']) }} as customer_key,\n\n        -- natural key\n        customers.customer_id,\n\n        -- attributes\n        customers.email,\n        customers.customer_created_at,\n\n        -- payment metrics\n        customers.total_payments,\n        customers.successful_payments,\n        customers.lifetime_value,\n        customers.first_payment_at,\n        customers.last_payment_at,\n\n        -- order metrics\n        coalesce(order_summary.total_orders, 0) as total_orders,\n        coalesce(order_summary.total_order_value, 0) as total_order_value,\n        order_summary.first_order_at,\n        order_summary.last_order_at,\n\n        -- calculated fields\n        case\n            when customers.lifetime_value >= 1000 then ''high''\n            when customers.lifetime_value >= 100 then ''medium''\n            else ''low''\n        end as customer_tier,\n\n        -- timestamps\n        current_timestamp as _loaded_at\n\n    from customers\n    left join order_summary using (customer_id)\n)\n\nselect * from final\n```\n\n```sql\n-- models/marts/core/fct_orders.sql\n{{\n    config(\n        materialized=''incremental'',\n        unique_key=''order_id'',\n        incremental_strategy=''merge''\n    )\n}}\n\nwith orders as (\n    select * from {{ ref(''stg_shopify__orders'') }}\n\n    {% if is_incremental() %}\n    where updated_at > (select max(updated_at) from {{ this }})\n    {% endif %}\n),\n\ncustomers as (\n    select * from {{ ref(''dim_customers'') }}\n),\n\nfinal as (\n    select\n        -- keys\n        orders.order_id,\n        customers.customer_key,\n        orders.customer_id,\n\n        -- dimensions\n        orders.order_status,\n        orders.fulfillment_status,\n        orders.payment_status,\n\n        -- measures\n        orders.subtotal,\n        orders.tax,\n        orders.shipping,\n        orders.total_price,\n        orders.total_discount,\n        orders.item_count,\n\n        -- timestamps\n        orders.created_at,\n        orders.updated_at,\n        orders.fulfilled_at,\n\n        -- metadata\n        current_timestamp as _loaded_at\n\n    from orders\n    left join customers on orders.customer_id = customers.customer_id\n)\n\nselect * from final\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Testing and Documentation\n\n```yaml\n# models/marts/core/_core__models.yml\nversion: 2\n\nmodels:\n  - name: dim_customers\n    description: Customer dimension with payment and order metrics\n    columns:\n      - name: customer_key\n        description: Surrogate key for the customer dimension\n        tests:\n          - unique\n          - not_null\n\n      - name: customer_id\n        description: Natural key from source system\n        tests:\n          - unique\n          - not_null\n\n      - name: email\n        description: Customer email address\n        tests:\n          - not_null\n\n      - name: customer_tier\n        description: Customer value tier based on lifetime value\n        tests:\n          - accepted_values:\n              values: [\"high\", \"medium\", \"low\"]\n\n      - name: lifetime_value\n        description: Total amount paid by customer\n        tests:\n          - dbt_utils.expression_is_true:\n              expression: \">= 0\"\n\n  - name: fct_orders\n    description: Order fact table with all order transactions\n    tests:\n      - dbt_utils.recency:\n          datepart: day\n          field: created_at\n          interval: 1\n    columns:\n      - name: order_id\n        tests:\n          - unique\n          - not_null\n      - name: customer_key\n        tests:\n          - not_null\n          - relationships:\n              to: ref(''dim_customers'')\n              field: customer_key\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Macros and DRY Code\n\n```sql\n-- macros/cents_to_dollars.sql\n{% macro cents_to_dollars(column_name, precision=2) %}\n    round({{ column_name }} / 100.0, {{ precision }})\n{% endmacro %}\n\n-- macros/generate_schema_name.sql\n{% macro generate_schema_name(custom_schema_name, node) %}\n    {%- set default_schema = target.schema -%}\n    {%- if custom_schema_name is none -%}\n        {{ default_schema }}\n    {%- else -%}\n        {{ default_schema }}_{{ custom_schema_name }}\n    {%- endif -%}\n{% endmacro %}\n\n-- macros/limit_data_in_dev.sql\n{% macro limit_data_in_dev(column_name, days=3) %}\n    {% if target.name == ''dev'' %}\n        where {{ column_name }} >= dateadd(day, -{{ days }}, current_date)\n    {% endif %}\n{% endmacro %}\n\n-- Usage in model\nselect * from {{ ref(''stg_orders'') }}\n{{ limit_data_in_dev(''created_at'') }}\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: Incremental Strategies\n\n```sql\n-- Delete+Insert (default for most warehouses)\n{{\n    config(\n        materialized=''incremental'',\n        unique_key=''id'',\n        incremental_strategy=''delete+insert''\n    )\n}}\n\n-- Merge (best for late-arriving data)\n{{\n    config(\n        materialized=''incremental'',\n        unique_key=''id'',\n        incremental_strategy=''merge'',\n        merge_update_columns=[''status'', ''amount'', ''updated_at'']\n    )\n}}\n\n-- Insert Overwrite (partition-based)\n{{\n    config(\n        materialized=''incremental'',\n        incremental_strategy=''insert_overwrite'',\n        partition_by={\n            \"field\": \"created_date\",\n            \"data_type\": \"date\",\n            \"granularity\": \"day\"\n        }\n    )\n}}\n\nselect\n    *,\n    date(created_at) as created_date\nfrom {{ ref(''stg_events'') }}\n\n{% if is_incremental() %}\nwhere created_date >= dateadd(day, -3, current_date)\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n## dbt Commands\n\n```bash\n# Development\ndbt run                          # Run all models\ndbt run --select staging         # Run staging models only\ndbt run --select +fct_orders     # Run fct_orders and its upstream\ndbt run --select fct_orders+     # Run fct_orders and its downstream\ndbt run --full-refresh           # Rebuild incremental models\n\n# Testing\ndbt test                         # Run all tests\ndbt test --select stg_stripe     # Test specific models\ndbt build                        # Run + test in DAG order\n\n# Documentation\ndbt docs generate                # Generate docs\ndbt docs serve                   # Serve docs locally\n\n# Debugging\ndbt compile                      # Compile SQL without running\ndbt debug                        # Test connection\ndbt ls --select tag:critical     # List models by tag\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Use staging layer** - Clean data once, use everywhere\n- **Test aggressively** - Not null, unique, relationships\n- **Document everything** - Column descriptions, model descriptions\n- **Use incremental** - For tables > 1M rows\n- **Version control** - dbt project in Git\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t skip staging** - Raw → mart is tech debt\n- **Don''t hardcode dates** - Use `{{ var(''start_date'') }}`\n- **Don''t repeat logic** - Extract to macros\n- **Don''t test in prod** - Use dev target\n- **Don''t ignore freshness** - Monitor source data\n\n## Resources\n\n- [dbt Documentation](https://docs.getdbt.com/)\n- [dbt Best Practices](https://docs.getdbt.com/guides/best-practices)\n- [dbt-utils Package](https://hub.getdbt.com/dbt-labs/dbt_utils/latest/)\n- [dbt Discourse](https://discourse.getdbt.com/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:21:11.240Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Engineering Agents needing advanced dbt transformation pipeline capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 dbt 转换管道功能的数据工程代理。","ja":"高度な dbt 変換パイプライン機能を必要とするデータエンジニアリングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 dbt 변환 파이프라인 기능이 필요한 데이터 엔지니어링 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Ingeniería de Datos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de transformación de pipeline dbt.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''ingénierie de données nécessitant des capacités de pipeline de transformation dbt avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Engineering-Agents, die erweiterte dbt-Transformationspipeline-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Engenharia de Dados que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de pipeline de transformação dbt.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов инженерии данных, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности конвейера преобразования dbt.","ar":"مثالي لعميل هندسة البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحويل أنابيب dbt."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement production-ready dbt patterns, including model organization, testing strategies, and incremental processing, while ensuring data quality and documentation using dbt''s data build tool.","zh":"赋予代理实现生产就绪的 dbt 模式，包括模型组织、测试策略、增量处理，同时确保使用 dbt 的数据构建工具进行数据质量和文档编制。","ja":"エージェントに、モデル構成、テスト戦略、インクリメンタル処理を含む生産就緒の dbt パターンを実装する力を与え、dbt のデータビルドツールを使用してデータ品質とドキュメント化を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 모델 조직, 테스트 전략, 증분 처리를 포함한 프로덕션 준비된 dbt 패턴을 구현할 수 있도록 하며, dbt의 데이터 빌드 도구를 사용하여 데이터 품질과 문서화를 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar patrones de dbt listos para producción, incluyendo la organización de modelos, estrategias de prueba y procesamiento incremental, garantizando al mismo tiempo la calidad y documentación de los datos utilizando la herramienta de compilación de datos dbt.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des modèles dbt prêts pour la production, y compris l''organisation des modèles, les stratégies de test et le traitement incrémentiel, tout en assurant la qualité et la documentation des données à l''aide de l''outil de construction de données dbt.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, produktionsreife dbt-Muster zu implementieren, einschließlich Modellorganisation, Teststrategien und inkrementeller Verarbeitung, während gleichzeitig die Datenqualität und -dokumentation unter Verwendung des dbt-Datentools sichergestellt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar padrões de produção prontos dbt, incluindo organização de modelo, estratégias de teste e processamento incremental, garantindo a qualidade e a documentação dos dados usando a ferramenta de construção de dados dbt.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать padrões производственных dbt, включая организацию модели, стратегии тестирования и инкрементальную обработку, обеспечивая качество и документацию данных с помощью инструмента построения данных dbt.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء تمكين تنفيذ أنماط جاهزة للإنتاج dbt، بما في ذلك تنظيم النموذج وстрategies اختبار والمعالجة التكرارية، مع ضمان جودة الوثائق ووثائق البيانات باستخدام أداة بناء البيانات dbt."},"useCases":{"en":["Building scalable data transformation pipelines with dbt","Organizing models into staging, intermediate, and marts layers for efficient data processing","Implementing data quality tests and incremental models for large datasets","Documenting data models and lineage for transparency and auditing"],"zh":["使用 dbt 构建可扩展的数据转换管道","将模型组织到分阶段、中间和商店层以实现高效的数据处理","为大型数据集实现数据质量测试和增量模型","记录数据模型和血统以实现透明度和审计"],"ja":["dbt を使用してスケーラブルなデータ変換パイプラインを構築する","モデルをステージング、Intermediate、Mart のレイヤーに組織して効率的なデータ処理を実現する","大規模なデータセットに対してデータ品質テストとインクリメンタルモデルを実装する","データモデルと血統を文書化して透明性と監査を実現する"],"ko":["dbt를 사용하여 확장 가능한 데이터 변환 파이프라인을 구축한다","모델을 스테이징, 중간, 마트 레이어로 조직하여 효율적인 데이터 처리를 실현한다","대규모 데이터셋에 대한 데이터 품질 테스트와 증분 모델을 구현한다","데이터 모델과 血統을 문서화하여 투명성과 감사성을 실현한다"],"es":["Creación de pipelines de transformación de datos escalables con dbt","Organización de modelos en capas de staging, intermedias y marts para un procesamiento de datos eficiente","Implementación de pruebas de calidad de datos y modelos incrementales para grandes conjuntos de datos","Documentación de modelos y linaje de datos para transparencia y auditoría"],"fr":["Création de pipelines de transformation de données évolutifs avec dbt","Organisation de modèles en couches de staging, intermédiaires et marts pour un traitement de données efficace","Mise en œuvre de tests de qualité de données et de modèles incrémentiels pour de grands ensembles de données","Documentation de modèles et de lignée de données pour la transparence et l''audit"],"de":["Erstellung von skalierbaren Daten-Transformationspipelines mit dbt","Organisation von Modellen in Staging-, Zwischen- und Marts-Schichten für effizientes Datenverarbeiten","Implementierung von Datenqualitätstests und inkrementellen Modellen für große Datensätze","Dokumentation von Datenmodellen und -abstammung für Transparenz und Audit"],"pt":["Construir pipelines de transformação de dados escaláveis com dbt","Organizar modelos em camadas de staging, intermediárias e marts para processamento de dados eficiente","Implementar testes de qualidade de dados e modelos incrementais para conjuntos de dados grandes","Documentar modelos de dados e linhagem para transparência e auditoria"],"ru":["Построение масштабируемых конвейеров преобразования данных с помощью dbt","Организация моделей в слоях staging, промежуточных и marts для эффективной обработки данных","Реализация тестов качества данных и инкрементальных моделей для больших наборов данных","Документирование моделей данных и происхождения для прозрачности и аудита"],"ar":["بناء أنابيب تحويل البيانات القابلة للتوسع مع dbt","تنظيم النماذج في طبقات من مرحلة ما قبل الإنتاج وطبقات متوسطة ومتاجر لعمليات معالجة البيانات الفعالة","تنفيذ اختبارات جودة البيانات والنماذج التكرارية لل مجموعات البيانات الكبيرة","توثيق نماذج البيانات والنسب للشفافية والتدقيق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires dbt installation and configuration","Limited to dbt-supported data sources and warehouses"],"zh":["需要 dbt 安装和配置","仅限于 dbt 支持的数据源和仓库"],"ja":["dbt のインストールと設定が必要","dbt でサポートされているデータソースと倉庫に限定される"],"ko":["dbt 설치 및 구성이 필요하다","dbt에서 지원하는 데이터 소스 및 저장소에 제한된다"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de dbt","Limitado a fuentes de datos y almacenes compatibles con dbt"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de dbt","Limité aux sources de données et entrepôts pris en charge par dbt"],"de":["Benötigt dbt-Installation und -Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf dbt-Unterstützung von Datenquellen und -warehouses"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do dbt","Limitado a fontes de dados e armazéns suportados pelo dbt"],"ru":["Требует установки и настройки dbt","Ограничен источниками данных и хранилищами, поддерживаемыми dbt"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين dbt","محدود بمصادر البيانات والمخازن المدعومة من قِبل dbt"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
