s performances et de la scalabilité dans Node.js"],"de":["Informierte Entscheidungsfindung bei der Node.js-Entwicklung","Auswahl geeigneter Frameworks und Muster","Prinzipien für die Konfiguration von Node.js-Projekten","Best Practices für die Zusammenarbeit und die Team-Entwicklung","Optimierung der Leistung und Skalierbarkeit in Node.js"],"pt":["Princípios de tomada de decisão","Seleção de framework","Padrões de desenvolvimento","Desenvolvimento de aplicações escaláveis","Boas práticas de codificação"],"ru":["Принципы принятия решений","Выбор фреймворка","Паттерны разработки","Разработка масштабируемых приложений","Хорошие практики кодирования"],"ar":["مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات","اختيار الإطار","أنماط التطوير","تطوير التطبيقات القابلة للتحجيم","أفضل الممارسات للبرمجة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Node.js","最佳实践","开发原则","框架选择","代码质量","开发效率"],"ja":["Node.js","ベストプラクティス","開発原則","フレームワーク選択","コード品質","開発効率"],"ko":["Node.js","최적의 실践","개발 원칙","프레임워크 선택","코드 품질","개발 효율"],"es":["nodejs","desarrollo de nodejs","mejores prácticas de nodejs","principios de desarrollo de nodejs","frameworks de nodejs","patrones de nodejs","colaboración en nodejs","optimización de nodejs"],"fr":["nodejs","développement nodejs","bonnes pratiques nodejs","principes de développement nodejs","frameworks nodejs","modèles nodejs","collaboration nodejs","optimisation nodejs"],"de":["nodejs","nodejs-entwicklung","nodejs-best-practices","entwicklungsprinzipien für nodejs","nodejs-frameworks","nodejs-muster","zusammenarbeit in nodejs","optimierung von nodejs"],"pt":["Node.js","desenvolvimento Node.js","melhores práticas Node.js","padrões de desenvolvimento","desenvolvimento de aplicações","escalabilidade"],"ru":["Node.js","разработка на Node.js","лучшие практики Node.js","паттерны разработки","разработка приложений","масштабируемость"],"ar":["Node.js","تطوير Node.js","أفضل الممارسات لندجس","أنماط التطوير","تطوير التطبيقات","القدرة على التحجيم"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nodejs-best-practices","description":"Node.js development principles and decision-making. Framework selection, async patterns, security, and architecture. Teaches thinking, not copying.","bodyPreview":"# Node.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles and decision-making for Node.js development in 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize code patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for preferences when unclear\n- Choose framework/pattern based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same solution every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── Edge/Serverless (Cloudflare","body":"# Node.js Best Practices\n\n> Principles and decision-making for Node.js development in 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize code patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for preferences when unclear\n- Choose framework/pattern based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same solution every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── Edge/Serverless (Cloudflare, Vercel)\n│   └── Hono (zero-dependency, ultra-fast cold starts)\n│\n├── High Performance API\n│   └── Fastify (2-3x faster than Express)\n│\n├── Enterprise/Team familiarity\n│   └── NestJS (structured, DI, decorators)\n│\n├── Legacy/Stable/Maximum ecosystem\n│   └── Express (mature, most middleware)\n│\n└── Full-stack with frontend\n    └── Next.js API Routes or tRPC\n```\n\n### Comparison Principles\n\n| Factor | Hono | Fastify | Express |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| **Best for** | Edge, serverless | Performance | Legacy, learning |\n| **Cold start** | Fastest | Fast | Moderate |\n| **Ecosystem** | Growing | Good | Largest |\n| **TypeScript** | Native | Excellent | Good |\n| **Learning curve** | Low | Medium | Low |\n\n### Selection Questions to Ask:\n1. What''s the deployment target?\n2. Is cold start time critical?\n3. Does team have existing experience?\n4. Is there legacy code to maintain?\n\n---\n\n## 2. Runtime Considerations (2025)\n\n### Native TypeScript\n\n```\nNode.js 22+: --experimental-strip-types\n├── Run .ts files directly\n├── No build step needed for simple projects\n└── Consider for: scripts, simple APIs\n```\n\n### Module System Decision\n\n```\nESM (import/export)\n├── Modern standard\n├── Better tree-shaking\n├── Async module loading\n└── Use for: new projects\n\nCommonJS (require)\n├── Legacy compatibility\n├── More npm packages support\n└── Use for: existing codebases, some edge cases\n```\n\n### Runtime Selection\n\n| Runtime | Best For |\n|---------|----------|\n| **Node.js** | General purpose, largest ecosystem |\n| **Bun** | Performance, built-in bundler |\n| **Deno** | Security-first, built-in TypeScript |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Architecture Principles\n\n### Layered Structure Concept\n\n```\nRequest Flow:\n│\n├── Controller/Route Layer\n│   ├── Handles HTTP specifics\n│   ├── Input validation at boundary\n│   └── Calls service layer\n│\n├── Service Layer\n│   ├── Business logic\n│   ├── Framework-agnostic\n│   └── Calls repository layer\n│\n└── Repository Layer\n    ├── Data access only\n    ├── Database queries\n    └── ORM interactions\n```\n\n### Why This Matters:\n- **Testability**: Mock layers independently\n- **Flexibility**: Swap database without touching business logic\n- **Clarity**: Each layer has single responsibility\n\n### When to Simplify:\n- Small scripts → Single file OK\n- Prototypes → Less structure acceptable\n- Always ask: \"Will this grow?\"\n\n---\n\n## 4. Error Handling Principles\n\n### Centralized Error Handling\n\n```\nPattern:\n├── Create custom error classes\n├── Throw from any layer\n├── Catch at top level (middleware)\n└── Format consistent response\n```\n\n### Error Response Philosophy\n\n```\nClient gets:\n├── Appropriate HTTP status\n├── Error code for programmatic handling\n├── User-friendly message\n└── NO internal details (security!)\n\nLogs get:\n├── Full stack trace\n├── Request context\n├── User ID (if applicable)\n└── Timestamp\n```\n\n### Status Code Selection\n\n| Situation | Status | When |\n|-----------|--------|------|\n| Bad input | 400 | Client sent invalid data |\n| No auth | 401 | Missing or invalid credentials |\n| No permission | 403 | Valid auth, but not allowed |\n| Not found | 404 | Resource doesn''t exist |\n| Conflict | 409 | Duplicate or state conflict |\n| Validation | 422 | Schema valid but business rules fail |\n| Server error | 500 | Our fault, log everything |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Async Patterns Principles\n\n### When to Use Each\n\n| Pattern | Use When |\n|---------|----------|\n| `async/await` | Sequential async operations |\n| `Promise.all` | Parallel independent operations |\n| `Promise.allSettled` | Parallel where some can fail |\n| `Promise.race` | Timeout or first response wins |\n\n### Event Loop Awareness\n\n```\nI/O-bound (async helps):\n├── Database queries\n├── HTTP requests\n├── File system\n└── Network operations\n\nCPU-bound (async doesn''t help):\n├── Crypto operations\n├── Image processing\n├── Complex calculations\n└── → Use worker threads or offload\n```\n\n### Avoiding Event Loop Blocking\n\n- Never use sync methods in production (fs.readFileSync, etc.)\n- Offload CPU-intensive work\n- Use streaming for large data\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation Principles\n\n### Validate at Boundaries\n\n```\nWhere to validate:\n├── API entry point (request body/params)\n├── Before database operations\n├── External data (API responses, file uploads)\n└── Environment variables (startup)\n```\n\n### Validation Library Selection\n\n| Library | Best For |\n|---------|----------|\n| **Zod** | TypeScript first, inference |\n| **Valibot** | Smaller bundle (tree-shakeable) |\n| **ArkType** | Performance critical |\n| **Yup** | Existing React Form usage |\n\n### Validation Philosophy\n\n- Fail fast: Validate early\n- Be specific: Clear error messages\n- Don''t trust: Even \"internal\" data\n\n---\n\n## 7. Security Principles\n\n### Security Checklist (Not Code)\n\n- [ ] **Input validation**: All inputs validated\n- [ ] **Parameterized queries**: No string concatenation for SQL\n- [ ] **Password hashing**: bcrypt or argon2\n- [ ] **JWT verification**: Always verify signature and expiry\n- [ ] **Rate limiting**: Protect from abuse\n- [ ] **Security headers**: Helmet.js or equivalent\n- [ ] **HTTPS**: Everywhere in production\n- [ ] **CORS**: Properly configured\n- [ ] **Secrets**: Environment variables only\n- [ ] **Dependencies**: Regularly audited\n\n### Security Mindset\n\n```\nTrust nothing:\n├── Query params → validate\n├── Request body → validate\n├── Headers → verify\n├── Cookies → validate\n├── File uploads → scan\n└── External APIs → validate response\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Testing Principles\n\n### Test Strategy Selection\n\n| Type | Purpose | Tools |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| **Unit** | Business logic | node:test, Vitest |\n| **Integration** | API endpoints | Supertest |\n| **E2E** | Full flows | Playwright |\n\n### What to Test (Priorities)\n\n1. **Critical paths**: Auth, payments, core business\n2. **Edge cases**: Empty inputs, boundaries\n3. **Error handling**: What happens when things fail?\n4. **Not worth testing**: Framework code, trivial getters\n\n### Built-in Test Runner (Node.js 22+)\n\n```\nnode --test src/**/*.test.ts\n├── No external dependency\n├── Good coverage reporting\n└── Watch mode available\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n### ❌ DON''T:\n- Use Express for new edge projects (use Hono)\n- Use sync methods in production code\n- Put business logic in controllers\n- Skip input validation\n- Hardcode secrets\n- Trust external data without validation\n- Block event loop with CPU work\n\n### ✅ DO:\n- Choose framework based on context\n- Ask user for preferences when unclear\n- Use layered architecture for growing projects\n- Validate all inputs\n- Use environment variables for secrets\n- Profile before optimizing\n\n---\n\n## 11. Decision Checklist\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- [ ] **Asked user about stack preference?**\n- [ ] **Chosen framework for THIS context?** (not just default)\n- [ ] **Considered deployment target?**\n- [ ] **Planned error handling strategy?**\n- [ ] **Identified validation points?**\n- [ ] **Considered security requirements?**\n\n---\n\n> **Remember**: Node.js best practices are about decision-making, not memorizing patterns. Every project deserves fresh consideration based on its requirements.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:21:03.213Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing advanced Node.js development best practices and compatibility with modern IDEs like GitHub Copilot and CLIs.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Node.js 开发最佳实践和兼容现代 IDE（如 GitHub Copilot 和 CLI）的全栈代理。","ja":"Node.js開発のベストプラクティスと、GitHub CopilotやCLIなどの最新のIDEとの互換性が必要なフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 Node.js 개발 최적화 및 GitHub Copilot 및 CLI와 같은 최신 IDE와의 호환성을 필요로 하는 풀스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Full Stack que necesitan prácticas avanzadas de desarrollo de Node.js y compatibilidad con IDEs modernas como GitHub Copilot y CLIs.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin de bonnes pratiques de développement avancées Node.js et de compatibilité avec des IDE modernes comme GitHub Copilot et CLIs.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die erweiterte Node.js-Entwicklungsbest-Practices und Kompatibilität mit modernen IDEs wie GitHub Copilot und CLIs benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que necessitam de práticas avançadas de desenvolvimento Node.js e compatibilidade com IDEs modernas como GitHub Copilot e CLIs.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full Stack, которым требуются передовые практики разработки Node.js и совместимость с современными IDE, такими как GitHub Copilot и CLI.","ar":"يتماشى تمامًا مع احتياجات وكلاء الويب الكامل الذين يحتاجون إلى ممارسات متقدمة لتنمية Node.js ومتوافقة مع IDEs الحديثة مثل GitHub Copilot و CLIs."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply decision-making principles for Node.js development, choosing the right framework and patterns based on context, and leveraging tools like Antigravity IDE for configuration conversions, ensuring compatibility with various CLIs and IDEs, including Kiro, OpenCode, and Cursor.","zh":"赋予代理应用 Node.js 开发的决策原则，根据上下文选择合适的框架和模式，并利用 Antigravity IDE 等工具进行配置转换，确保与各种 CLI 和 IDE（包括 Kiro、OpenCode 和 Cursor）兼容。","ja":"エージェントに、Node.js開発の意思決定原則を適用し、コンテキストに基づいて適切なフレームワークとパターンを選択し、Antigravity IDEなどのツールを使用して構成の変換を行い、Kiro、OpenCode、Cursorを含む様々なCLIとIDEとの互換性を確保する力を与えます。","ko":"에이전트가 Node.js 개발의 의사 결정 원칙을 적용하고, 문脈에 따라 적절한 프레임워크와 패턴을 선택하며, Antigravity IDE와 같은 도구를 사용하여 구성 변환을 수행하고, Kiro, OpenCode, Cursor를 포함한 다양한 CLI 및 IDE와의 호환성을 보장하는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar principios de toma de decisiones para el desarrollo de Node.js, eligiendo el marco y los patrones adecuados según el contexto, y aprovechando herramientas como Antigravity IDE para conversiones de configuración, garantizando la compatibilidad con varios CLIs y IDEs, incluyendo Kiro, OpenCode y Cursor.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des principes de prise de décision pour le développement Node.js, en choisissant le bon cadre et les modèles en fonction du contexte, et en exploitant des outils comme Antigravity IDE pour des conversions de configuration, en garantissant la compatibilité avec divers CLIs et IDE, y compris Kiro, OpenCode et Cursor.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Entscheidungsprinzipien für die Node.js-Entwicklung anzuwenden, indem sie den richtigen Rahmen und Muster basierend auf dem Kontext wählen und Tools wie Antigravity IDE für Konfigurationskonvertierungen nutzen, um die Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen CLIs und IDEs sicherzustellen, einschließlich Kiro, OpenCode und Cursor.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar princípios de tomada de decisão para o desenvolvimento Node.js, escolhendo o framework e os padrões certos com base no contexto e utilizando ferramentas como Antigravity IDE para conversões de configuração, garantindo a compatibilidade com várias CLIs e IDEs, incluindo Kiro, OpenCode e Cursor.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять принципы принятия решений для разработки Node.js, выбирая правильный фреймворк и шаблоны на основе контекста, и использует инструменты, такие как Antigravity IDE, для конверсии конфигураций, обеспечивая совместимость с различными CLI и IDE, включая Kiro, OpenCode и Cursor.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تطبيق مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات لتنمية Node.js، واختيار الإطار والأنماط المناسبة بناءً على السياق، واستخدام أدوات مثل Antigravity IDE للتحويلات التكوينية، مما يضمن التوافق مع مختلف CLIs و IDEs، بما في ذلك Kiro و OpenCode و Cursor."},"useCases":{"en":["Converting Agent and Skill configurations for compatibility with multiple IDEs","Applying framework selection decision trees for Edge/Serverless and Cloudflare environments","Implementing best practices for Node.js development in 2025, considering context and user preferences"],"zh":["为兼容多个IDE而转换代理和技能配置","应用框架选择决策树用于Edge/Serverless和Cloudflare环境","在2025年实施Node.js开发最佳实践，考虑上下文和用户偏好"],"ja":["複数のIDEとの互換性のためにエージェントとスキルの構成を変換する","Edge/ServerlessおよびCloudflare環境向けにフレームワークの選択の意思決定ツリーを適用する","2025年に、コンテキストとユーザー偏好を考慮してNode.js開発のベストプラクティスを実施する"],"ko":["여러 IDE와의 호환성을 위해 에이전트 및 스킬 구성 변환","Edge/Serverless 및 Cloudflare 환경을 위한 프레임워크 선택 의사 결정 트리 적용","2025년에 문脈 및 사용자 선호도를 고려하여 Node.js 개발 최적화 수행"],"es":["Conversión de configuraciones de Agentes y Habilidades para la compatibilidad con varios IDE","Aplicación de árboles de decisión para la selección de marcos en entornos Edge/Serverless y Cloudflare","Implementación de prácticas recomendadas para el desarrollo de Node.js en 2025, teniendo en cuenta el contexto y las preferencias del usuario"],"fr":["Conversion des configurations d''agents et de compétences pour la compatibilité avec plusieurs IDE","Application d''arbres de décision pour la sélection de cadres dans les environnements Edge/Serverless et Cloudflare","Mise en œuvre de bonnes pratiques pour le développement Node.js en 2025, en tenant compte du contexte et des préférences de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Konvertierung von Agenten- und Fähigkeitskonfigurationen für die Kompatibilität mit mehreren IDEs","Anwendung von Entscheidungsbäumen für die Rahmenauswahl in Edge/Serverless- und Cloudflare-Umgebungen","Implementierung von Best-Practices für die Node.js-Entwicklung im Jahr 2025, unter Berücksichtigung des Kontexts und der Benutzervorlieben"],"pt":["Converter configurações de Agente e Habilidade para compatibilidade com várias IDEs","Aplicar árvores de decisão de seleção de framework para ambientes Edge/Serverless e Cloudflare","Implementar práticas recomendadas para o desenvolvimento Node.js em 2025, considerando o contexto e as preferências do usuário"],"ru":["Преобразование конфигураций агента и навыков для совместимости с несколькими IDE","Применение деревьев решений для выбора фреймворка для сред Edge/Serverless и Cloudflare","Реализация рекомендуемых практик для разработки Node.js в 2025 году, учитывая контекст и предпочтения пользователя"],"ar":["تحويل تكوينات الوكيل والمهارة لتوافقها مع عدة IDEs","تطبيق أشجار القرارات لاختيار الإطار في بيئات Edge/Serverless و Cloudflare","تنفيذ أفضل الممارسات لتنمية Node.js في عام 2025، مع مراعاة السياق وتفضيلات المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Node.js development principles and decision-making","Limited to conversions and compatibility with specified IDEs and CLIs","Context-dependent, requiring analysis of user preferences and project requirements"],"zh":["需要了解 Node.js 开发原则和决策","仅限于指定 IDE 和 CLI 的转换和兼容性","依赖于上下文，需要分析用户偏好和项目需求"],"ja":["Node.js開発の原則と意思決定の理解が必要","指定されたIDEとCLIの変換と互換性に限定される","コンテキストに依存し、ユーザー偏好とプロジェクト要件の分析が必要"],"ko":["Node.js 개발 원칙 및 의사 결정 이해 필요","지정된 IDE 및 CLI의 변환 및 호환성에 한정됨","문脈에 의존하며, 사용자 선호도 및 프로젝트 요구 사항 분석 필요"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de desarrollo de Node.js y la toma de decisiones","Limitado a conversiones y compatibilidad con los IDE y CLIs especificados","Dependiente del contexto, requiriendo análisis de las preferencias del usuario y los requisitos del proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de développement Node.js et de la prise de décision","Limité aux conversions et à la compatibilité avec les IDE et CLIs spécifiés","Dépendant du contexte, nécessitant une analyse des préférences de l''utilisateur et des exigences du projet"],"de":["Benötigt ein Verständnis der Node.js-Entwicklungsprinzipien und der Entscheidungsfindung","Begrenzt auf Konvertierungen und Kompatibilität mit den angegebenen IDEs und CLIs","Kontextabhängig, erfordert eine Analyse der Benutzervorlieben und der Projektanforderungen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de desenvolvimento Node.js e tomada de decisão","Limitado a conversões e compatibilidade com IDEs e CLIs especificados","Dependente do contexto, exigindo análise das preferências do usuário e requisitos do projeto"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов разработки Node.js и принятия решений","Ограничен преобразованиями и совместимостью с указанными IDE и CLI","Зависит от контекста, требует анализа предпочтений пользователя и требований проекта"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تطور Node.js وعمليات اتخاذ القرارات","محدود بالتحويلات والتوافق مع IDEs و CLIs المحددة","يعتمد على السياق، يتطلب تحليل تفضيلات المستخدم ومتطلبات المشروع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit/mobile-games', 'community', 'HaoNgo232', 'agent-bridge-kit', 'HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit', 'mobile-games', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:21:19.389Z', NULL, '{"id":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit/mobile-games","name":"mobile-games","description":{"zh":"移动游戏开发需要考虑平台约束和优化原则，包括触摸输入、电池寿命、温度、屏幕尺寸和中断等因素","ja":"モバイルゲーム開発では、プラットフォームの制約と最適化原則を考慮する必要があります。これには、タッチ入力、バッテリー寿命、温度、画面サイズ、断絶などが含まれます","ko":"모바일 게임 개발에서는 플랫폼 제약과 최적화 원리를 고려해야 합니다. 이는 터치 입력, 배터리 수명, 온도, 화면 크기, 중단 등이 포함됩니다","es":"El desarrollo de juegos móviles implica superar limitaciones de plataforma. Aprende a optimizar tus juegos con estrategias efectivas.","fr":"Le développement de jeux mobiles implique de surmonter les limites de la plateforme. Apprenez à optimiser vos jeux avec des stratégies efficaces.","de":"Die Entwicklung von Mobile Games beinhaltet die Überwindung von Plattformbeschränkungen. Lernen Sie, Ihre Spiele mit effektiven Strategien zu optimieren.","pt":"O desenvolvimento de jogos móveis envolve considerações de plataforma e otimização. Aprenda sobre estratégias de plataforma e princípios de entrada por toque.","ru":"Разработка мобильных игр включает в себя рассмотрение платформы и оптимизацию. Узнайте о стратегиях платформы и принципах касания.","ar":"تطوير ألعاب الجوال يتضمن مراعاة المنصة وتحسينها. تعلم عن استراتيجيات المنصة ومبادئ الإدخال باللمس.","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"移动游戏开发优化","ja":"モバイルゲーム開発の最適化","ko":"모바일 게임 개발 최적화","es":"Desarrollo de Juegos Móviles: Optimización y Principios","fr":"Développement de Jeux Mobiles: Optimisation et Principes","de":"Mobile Game Entwicklung: Optimierung und Prinzipien","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Jogos Móveis: Otimização e Princípios","ru":"Разработка Мобильных Игр: Оптимизация и Принципы","ar":"تطوير ألعاب الجوال: تحسين والمبادئ","en":"mobile-games"},"description":{"zh":"移动游戏开发需要考虑平台约束和优化原则，包括触摸输入、电池寿命、温度、屏幕尺寸和中断等因素","ja":"モバイルゲーム開発では、プラットフォームの制約と最適化原則を考慮する必要があります。これには、タッチ入力、バッテリー寿命、温度、画面サイズ、断絶などが含まれます","ko":"모바일 게임 개발에서는 플랫폼 제약과 최적화 원리를 고려해야 합니다. 이는 터치 입력, 배터리 수명, 온도, 화면 크기, 중단 등이 포함됩니다","es":"El desarrollo de juegos móviles implica superar limitaciones de plataforma. Aprende a optimizar tus juegos con estrategias efectivas.","fr":"Le développement de jeux mobiles implique de surmonter les limites de la plateforme. Apprenez à optimiser vos jeux avec des stratégies efficaces.","de":"Die Entwicklung von Mobile Games beinhaltet die Überwindung von Plattformbeschränkungen. Lernen Sie, Ihre Spiele mit effektiven Strategien zu optimieren.","pt":"O desenvolvimento de jogos móveis envolve considerações de plataforma e otimização. Aprenda sobre estratégias de plataforma e princípios de entrada por toque.","ru":"Разработка мобильных игр включает в себя рассмотрение платформы и оптимизацию. Узнайте о стратегиях платформы и принципах касания.","ar":"تطوير ألعاب الجوال يتضمن مراعاة المنصة وتحسينها. تعلم عن استراتيجيات المنصة ومبادئ الإدخال باللمس.","en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro..."},"definition":{"en":"Tool for converting Agent, Skill and Workfows configurations from Antigravity IDE to a format compatible with IDEs (GitHub Copilot, Cursor,..) and CLIs (Kiro, OpenCode,..)."},"features":{"zh":["触摸输入优化","电池寿命优化","温度控制","响应式UI设计","中断处理"],"ja":["タッチ入力の最適化","バッテリー寿命の最適化","温度制御","レスポンシブUIデザイン","断絶処理"],"ko":["터치 입력 최적화","배터리 수명 최적화","온도 제어","반응형 UI 디자인","중단 처리"],"es":["Optimización para entrada táctil","Estrategias para reducir el consumo de batería","Principios de diseño para pantallas pequeñas","Gestión de interrupciones y pausas","Diseño de interfaces de usuario responsivas"],"fr":["Optimisation pour les entrées tactiles","Stratégies pour réduire la consommation de batterie","Principes de conception pour les écrans de petite taille","Gestion des interruptions et des pauses","Conception d''interfaces utilisateur responsives"],"de":["Optimierung für Touch-Eingabe","Strategien zur Reduzierung des Batterieverbrauchs","Prinzipien für das Design von kleinen Bildschirmen","Verwaltung von Unterbrechungen und Pausen","Entwurf von responsiven Benutzeroberflächen"],"pt":["Otimização de plataforma","Princípios de entrada por toque","Estratégias de bateria e termal","Interface do usuário responsiva","Gestos e áreas de toque grandes"],"ru":["Оптимизация платформы","Принципы касания","Стратегии батареи и термала","Отзывчивый пользовательский интерфейс","Жесты и большие области касания"],"ar":["تحسين المنصة","مبادئ الإدخال باللمس","استراتيجيات البطارية والحرارة","واجهة المستخدم المستجيبة","الإشارات والإلكترونات الكبيرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["移动游戏开发","平台约束","优化原则","触摸输入","电池寿命","温度","屏幕尺寸","中断"],"ja":["モバイルゲーム開発","プラットフォームの制約","最適化原則","タッチ入力","バッテリー寿命","温度","画面サイズ","断絶"],"ko":["모바일 게임 개발","플랫폼 제약","최적화 원리","터치 입력","배터리 수명","온도","화면 크기","중단"],"es":["desarrollo de juegos móviles","optimización de juegos","entrada táctil","consumo de batería","diseño de interfaces de usuario","interrupciones en juegos","principios de diseño para móviles","juegos para dispositivos móviles"],"fr":["développement de jeux mobiles","optimisation de jeux","entrées tactiles","consommation de batterie","conception d''interfaces utilisateur","interruptions dans les jeux","principes de conception pour les mobiles","jeux pour appareils mobiles"],"de":["Mobile Game Entwicklung","Spieloptimierung","Touch-Eingabe","Batterieverbrauch","Benutzeroberflächendesign","Unterbrechungen in Spielen","Prinzipien für das Mobile-Design","Spiele für mobile Geräte"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de jogos móveis","otimização de plataforma","princípios de entrada por toque","estratégias de bateria","interface do usuário responsiva","jogos móveis","desenvolvimento de jogos"],"ru":["разработка мобильных игр","оптимизация платформы","принципы касания","стратегии батареи","отзывчивый пользовательский интерфейс","мобильные игры","разработка игр"],"ar":["تطوير ألعاب الجوال","تحسين المنصة","مبادئ الإدخال باللمس","استراتيجيات البطارية","واجهة المستخدم المستجيبة","ألعاب الجوال","تطوير الألعاب"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"agent-bridge-kit","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/agent-bridge-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mobile-games","description":"Mobile game development principles. Touch input, battery, performance, app stores.","bodyPreview":"# Mobile Game Development\n\n> Platform constraints and optimization principles.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Platform Considerations\n\n### Key Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Strategy |\n|------------|----------|\n| **Touch input** | Large hit areas, gestures |\n| **Battery** | Limit CPU/GPU usage |\n| **Thermal** | Throttle when hot |\n| **Screen size** | Responsive UI |\n| **Interruptions** | Pause on background |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Touch Input Principles\n\n### Touch vs Controller\n\n| Touch | Desktop/Console |\n|-------|-----------","body":"# Mobile Game Development\n\n> Platform constraints and optimization principles.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Platform Considerations\n\n### Key Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Strategy |\n|------------|----------|\n| **Touch input** | Large hit areas, gestures |\n| **Battery** | Limit CPU/GPU usage |\n| **Thermal** | Throttle when hot |\n| **Screen size** | Responsive UI |\n| **Interruptions** | Pause on background |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Touch Input Principles\n\n### Touch vs Controller\n\n| Touch | Desktop/Console |\n|-------|-----------------|\n| Imprecise | Precise |\n| Occludes screen | No occlusion |\n| Limited buttons | Many buttons |\n| Gestures available | Buttons/sticks |\n\n### Best Practices\n\n- Minimum touch target: 44x44 points\n- Visual feedback on touch\n- Avoid precise timing requirements\n- Support both portrait and landscape\n\n---\n\n## 3. Performance Targets\n\n### Thermal Management\n\n| Action | Trigger |\n|--------|---------|\n| Reduce quality | Device warm |\n| Limit FPS | Device hot |\n| Pause effects | Critical temp |\n\n### Battery Optimization\n\n- 30 FPS often sufficient\n- Sleep when paused\n- Minimize GPS/network\n- Dark mode saves OLED battery\n\n---\n\n## 4. App Store Requirements\n\n### iOS (App Store)\n\n| Requirement | Note |\n|-------------|------|\n| Privacy labels | Required |\n| Account deletion | If account creation exists |\n| Screenshots | For all device sizes |\n\n### Android (Google Play)\n\n| Requirement | Note |\n|-------------|------|\n| Target API | Current year''s SDK |\n| 64-bit | Required |\n| App bundles | Recommended |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Monetization Models\n\n| Model | Best For |\n|-------|----------|\n| **Premium** | Quality games, loyal audience |\n| **Free + IAP** | Casual, progression-based |\n| **Ads** | Hyper-casual, high volume |\n| **Subscription** | Content updates, multiplayer |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ Don''t | ✅ Do |\n|----------|-------|\n| Desktop controls on mobile | Design for touch |\n| Ignore battery drain | Monitor thermals |\n| Force landscape | Support player preference |\n| Always-on network | Cache and sync |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Mobile is the most constrained platform. Respect battery and attention.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:21:19.389Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Game Development Agents needing insights into mobile platform constraints and optimization principles.","zh":"非常适合需要了解移动平台约束和优化原则的游戏开发代理。","ja":"モバイルプラットフォームの制約と最適化原則の洞察が必要なゲーム開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"모바일 플랫폼의 제약과 최적화 원리를 이해해야 하는 게임 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de juegos que necesitan información sobre las limitaciones de la plataforma móvil y los principios de optimización.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement de jeux ayant besoin d''informations sur les contraintes de la plate-forme mobile et les principes d''optimisation.","de":"Perfekt für Game-Development-Agents, die Einblicke in die Einschränkungen der mobilen Plattform und die Optimierungsprinzipien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Jogos que necessitam de insights sobre restrições de plataforma móvel e princípios de otimização.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по разработке игр, которым необходимы идеи о ограничениях мобильной платформы и принципах оптимизации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير الألعاب الذي يحتاج إلى رؤى حول قيود منصة الهاتف المحمول ومبادئ التحسين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop responsive and efficient mobile games by considering touch input principles, battery and thermal constraints, and screen size limitations, utilizing strategies like large hit areas, gestures, and throttling to ensure seamless gameplay.","zh":"通过考虑触摸输入原则、电池和热约束以及屏幕尺寸限制，利用大型点击区域、手势和节流等策略，赋予代理开发响应迅速和高效的移动游戏的能力，以确保无缝的游戏体验。","ja":"タッチ入力の原則、バッテリーと熱の制約、画面サイズの制限を考慮し、大きなヒットエリア、ジェスチャー、スロットルなどの戦略を使用して、エージェントがレスポンシブで効率的なモバイルゲームを開発できるようにし、シームレスなゲームプレイを実現します。","ko":"터치 입력 원리, 배터리 및 열 제약, 화면 크기 제한 등을 고려하고, 큰 히트 영역, 제스처, 스로틀링 등의 전략을 활용하여, 에이전트가 반응성이 뛰어난 모바일 게임을 개발할 수 있도록 하여, 무결점의 게임 플레이를 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desarrollar juegos móviles responsivos y eficientes considerando principios de entrada táctil, restricciones de batería y térmicas, y limitaciones de tamaño de pantalla, utilizando estrategias como áreas de golpeo grandes, gestos y reducción de velocidad para garantizar una experiencia de juego sin interrupciones.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer des jeux mobiles responsives et efficaces en considérant les principes de saisie tactile, les contraintes de batterie et thermiques, et les limitations de taille d''écran, en utilisant des stratégies comme des zones de touche importantes, des gestes et une régulation pour assurer un gameplay fluide.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, responsive und effiziente Mobile-Spiele zu entwickeln, indem sie Prinzipien der Touch-Eingabe, Batterie- und thermische Einschränkungen sowie Bildschirmgrößenbeschränkungen berücksichtigen und Strategien wie große Trefferflächen, Gesten und Drosselung verwenden, um ein nahtloses Gameplay zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver jogos móveis responsivos e eficientes, considerando princípios de entrada por toque, restrições de bateria e termal, e limitações de tamanho de tela, utilizando estratégias como áreas de toque grandes, gestos e limitação para garantir uma jogabilidade sem interrupções.","ru":"Наделяет агентов способностью создавать отзывчивые и эффективные мобильные игры, учитывая принципы ввода с помощью сенсорного экрана, ограничения батареи и термические ограничения, а также ограничения размера экрана, используя стратегии, такие как большие активные области, жесты и ограничение, чтобы обеспечить бесперебойную игру.","ar":"يُمكن العميل من تطوير ألعاب محمولة استجابة وفعالة من خلال مراعاة مبادئ الإدخال باللمس والقيود الحرارية والكهربائية وتقييدات حجم الشاشة، واستخدام استراتيجيات مثل مساحات اللمس الكبيرة والإشارات وتقليل الحد الأقصى لضمان لعب سلس."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing responsive UI for varying screen sizes","Optimizing game performance for battery and thermal efficiency","Implementing touch input principles for intuitive gameplay"],"zh":["为不同屏幕尺寸设计响应迅速的UI","优化游戏性能以实现电池和热效率","实现触摸输入原则以实现直观的游戏体验"],"ja":["さまざまな画面サイズに対応したレスポンシブUIの設計","バッテリーと熱の効率を向上させるゲームパフォーマンスの最適化","直感的なゲームプレイを実現するタッチ入力の原則の実装"],"ko":["다양한 화면 크기에 맞는 반응성 UI 설계","배터리 및 열 효율성을 위한 게임 성능 최적화","직관적인 게임 플레이를 위한 터치 입력 원리의 구현"],"es":["Diseñar una interfaz de usuario responsable para tamaños de pantalla variables","Optimizar el rendimiento del juego para la eficiencia de la batería y el calor","Implementar principios de entrada táctil para una experiencia de juego intuitiva"],"fr":["Concevoir une interface utilisateur réactive pour des tailles d''écran variables","Optimiser les performances du jeu pour l''efficacité de la batterie et la thermique","Mettre en œuvre des principes de saisie tactile pour un gameplay intuitif"],"de":["Entwerfen einer responsiven Benutzeroberfläche für variable Bildschirmgrößen","Optimieren der Spielperformance für Batterie- und thermische Effizienz","Implementieren von Touch-Eingabegrundsätzen für eine intuitive Spielsteuerung"],"pt":["Projetar interface do usuário responsiva para tamanhos de tela variados","Otimizar o desempenho do jogo para eficiência de bateria e termal","Implementar princípios de entrada por toque para jogabilidade intuitiva"],"ru":["Разработка отзывчивого пользовательского интерфейса для различных размеров экрана","Оптимизация производительности игры для эффективности батареи и термической эффективности","Реализация принципов ввода с помощью сенсорного экрана для интуитивной игры"],"ar":["تصميم واجهة مستخدم استجابة لأحجام شاشات مختلفة","تحسين أداء اللعبة للكفاءة الكهربائية والحرارية","تطبيق مبادئ الإدخال باللمس للعب المثيرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires consideration of platform-specific constraints","Limited to mobile game development"],"zh":["需要考虑平台特定的约束","仅限于移动游戏开发"],"ja":["プラットフォーム固有の制約を考慮する必要がある","モバイルゲーム開発のみに限定される"],"ko":["플랫폼 고유의 제약을 고려해야 함","모바일 게임 개발에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la consideración de restricciones específicas de la plataforma","Limitado al desarrollo de juegos móviles"],"fr":["Nécessite la prise en compte de contraintes spécifiques à la plate-forme","Limité au développement de jeux mobiles"],"de":["Erfordert die Berücksichtigung von plattformspezifischen Einschränkungen","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von Mobile-Spielen"],"pt":["Exige consideração de restrições específicas da plataforma","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de jogos móveis"],"ru":["Требует учета ограничений платформы","Ограничен разработкой мобильных игр"],"ar":["يتطلب مراعاة قيود منصة محددة","محدود بتطوير ألعاب الهاتف المحمول"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
