ADR）の作成、維持、管理のための包括的なパターンを提供します。","ko":"중요한 기술 결정의 맥락과 근거를 포착하는 아키텍처 결정 기록(ADR)을 생성, 유지 및 관리하기 위한 포괄적인 패턴을 제공합니다.","es":"Los Registros de Decisiones de Arquitectura capturan el contexto y la justificación de decisiones técnicas importantes","fr":"Les Enregistrements de Décisions d''Architecture capturent le contexte et la justification des décisions techniques importantes","de":"Die Architekturentscheidungsaufzeichnungen erfassen den Kontext und die Begründung wichtiger technischer Entscheidungen","pt":"Registros de Decisões de Arquitetura são padrões abrangentes para capturar o contexto e a lógica por trás de decisões técnicas importantes","ru":"Записи решений по архитектуре являются полными шаблонами для захвата контекста и логики за важными техническими решениями","ar":"سجلات قرارات الهندسة المعمارية هي أنماط شاملة لتقديم سياق و논理 لقرارات تقنية مهمة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["ADR创建与模板指南","决策背景与理由记录模式","ADR版本管理与维护流程","技术选择与设计权衡文档化","团队协作与决策流程标准化","历史决策回顾与审计支持"],"ja":["ADR作成とテンプレートガイド","決定の背景と理論記録パターン","ADRバージョン管理と維持プロセス","技術選択と設計トレードオフの文書化","チーム協力と意思決定プロセスの標準化","履歴決定のレビューと監査サポート"],"ko":["ADR 생성 및 템플릿 가이드","결정 배경 및 근거 기록 패턴","ADR 버전 관리 및 유지 관리 프로세스","기술 선택 및 설계 트레이드오프 문서화","팀 협업 및 의사 결정 프로세스 표준화","역사적 결정 검토 및 감사 지원"],"es":["Patrones para crear y mantener Registros de Decisiones de Arquitectura","Documentación de decisiones técnicas","Registro de elecciones tecnológicas","Revisión de decisiones históricas","Establecimiento de procesos de toma de decisiones"],"fr":["Modèles pour créer et maintenir des Enregistrements de Décisions d''Architecture","Documentation des décisions techniques","Enregistrement des choix technologiques","Révision des décisions historiques","Établissement de processus de prise de décision"],"de":["Muster für die Erstellung und Pflege von Architekturentscheidungsaufzeichnungen","Dokumentation von technischen Entscheidungen","Aufzeichnung von Technologieentscheidungen","Überprüfung von historischen Entscheidungen","Einrichtung von Entscheidungsprozessen"],"pt":["Padrões abrangentes para criar e gerenciar Registros de Decisões de Arquitetura","Captura do contexto e da lógica por trás de decisões técnicas importantes","Documentação de tecnologias e design","Revisão de decisões históricas","Estabelecimento de processos de tomada de decisão"],"ru":["Полные шаблоны для создания и управления Записями решений по архитектуре","Захват контекста и логики за важными техническими решениями","Документирование технологий и дизайна","Просмотр исторических решений","Установление процессов принятия решений"],"ar":["أنماط شاملة لإنشاء وإدارة سجلات قرارات الهندسة المعمارية","تقديم سياق و논理 لقرارات تقنية مهمة","توثيق التكنولوجيا والتصميم","استعراض القرارات التاريخية","إنشاء عمليات اتخاذ القرارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["架构决策记录","ADR模板","技术决策文档","设计权衡记录","团队决策流程","架构治理","ADR管理最佳实践","软件架构文档"],"ja":["アーキテクチャ決定記録","ADRテンプレート","技術的決定文書","設計トレードオフ記録","チーム意思決定プロセス","アーキテクチャガバナンス","ADR管理ベストプラクティス","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ文書"],"ko":["아키텍처 결정 기록","ADR 템플릿","기술 결정 문서화","설계 트레이드오프 기록","팀 의사 결정 프로세스","아키텍처 거버넌스","ADR 관리 최적 사례","소프트웨어 아키텍처 문서"],"es":["Registros de Decisiones de Arquitectura","decisiones técnicas","documentación de tecnología","patrones de arquitectura","toma de decisiones","gestión de decisiones"],"fr":["Enregistrements de Décisions d''Architecture","décisions techniques","documentation de technologie","modèles d''architecture","prise de décision","gestion de décisions"],"de":["Architekturentscheidungsaufzeichnungen","technische Entscheidungen","Dokumentation von Technologie","Architekturmuster","Entscheidungsfindung","Entscheidungsmanagement"],"pt":["Registros de Decisões de Arquitetura","ADR","Decisões técnicas","Documentação de tecnologias","Revisão de decisões","Processos de tomada de decisão"],"ru":["Записи решений по архитектуре","ADR","Технические решения","Документирование технологий","Просмотр решений","Процессы принятия решений"],"ar":["سجلات قرارات الهندسة المعمارية","ADR","قرارات تقنية","توثيق التكنولوجيا","استعراض القرارات","عمليات اتخاذ القرارات"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"architecture-decision-records","description":"Write and maintain Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) following best practices for technical decision documentation. Use when documenting significant technical decisions, reviewing past architectural choices, or establishing decision processes.","bodyPreview":"# Architecture Decision Records\n\nComprehensive patterns for creating, maintaining, and managing Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) that capture the context and rationale behind significant technical decisions.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Making significant architectural decisions\n- Documenting technology choices\n- Recording design trade-offs\n- Onboarding new team members\n- Reviewing historical decisions\n- Establishing decision-making processes\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. What is an ADR?\n\nAn Ar","body":"# Architecture Decision Records\n\nComprehensive patterns for creating, maintaining, and managing Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) that capture the context and rationale behind significant technical decisions.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Making significant architectural decisions\n- Documenting technology choices\n- Recording design trade-offs\n- Onboarding new team members\n- Reviewing historical decisions\n- Establishing decision-making processes\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. What is an ADR?\n\nAn Architecture Decision Record captures:\n\n- **Context**: Why we needed to make a decision\n- **Decision**: What we decided\n- **Consequences**: What happens as a result\n\n### 2. When to Write an ADR\n\n| Write ADR                  | Skip ADR               |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| New framework adoption     | Minor version upgrades |\n| Database technology choice | Bug fixes              |\n| API design patterns        | Implementation details |\n| Security architecture      | Routine maintenance    |\n| Integration patterns       | Configuration changes  |\n\n### 3. ADR Lifecycle\n\n```\nProposed → Accepted → Deprecated → Superseded\n              ↓\n           Rejected\n```\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Standard ADR (MADR Format)\n\n```markdown\n# ADR-0001: Use PostgreSQL as Primary Database\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nWe need to select a primary database for our new e-commerce platform. The system\nwill handle:\n\n- ~10,000 concurrent users\n- Complex product catalog with hierarchical categories\n- Transaction processing for orders and payments\n- Full-text search for products\n- Geospatial queries for store locator\n\nThe team has experience with MySQL, PostgreSQL, and MongoDB. We need ACID\ncompliance for financial transactions.\n\n## Decision Drivers\n\n- **Must have ACID compliance** for payment processing\n- **Must support complex queries** for reporting\n- **Should support full-text search** to reduce infrastructure complexity\n- **Should have good JSON support** for flexible product attributes\n- **Team familiarity** reduces onboarding time\n\n## Considered Options\n\n### Option 1: PostgreSQL\n\n- **Pros**: ACID compliant, excellent JSON support (JSONB), built-in full-text\n  search, PostGIS for geospatial, team has experience\n- **Cons**: Slightly more complex replication setup than MySQL\n\n### Option 2: MySQL\n\n- **Pros**: Very familiar to team, simple replication, large community\n- **Cons**: Weaker JSON support, no built-in full-text search (need\n  Elasticsearch), no geospatial without extensions\n\n### Option 3: MongoDB\n\n- **Pros**: Flexible schema, native JSON, horizontal scaling\n- **Cons**: No ACID for multi-document transactions (at decision time),\n  team has limited experience, requires schema design discipline\n\n## Decision\n\nWe will use **PostgreSQL 15** as our primary database.\n\n## Rationale\n\nPostgreSQL provides the best balance of:\n\n1. **ACID compliance** essential for e-commerce transactions\n2. **Built-in capabilities** (full-text search, JSONB, PostGIS) reduce\n   infrastructure complexity\n3. **Team familiarity** with SQL databases reduces learning curve\n4. **Mature ecosystem** with excellent tooling and community support\n\nThe slight complexity in replication is outweighed by the reduction in\nadditional services (no separate Elasticsearch needed).\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- Single database handles transactions, search, and geospatial queries\n- Reduced operational complexity (fewer services to manage)\n- Strong consistency guarantees for financial data\n- Team can leverage existing SQL expertise\n\n### Negative\n\n- Need to learn PostgreSQL-specific features (JSONB, full-text search syntax)\n- Vertical scaling limits may require read replicas sooner\n- Some team members need PostgreSQL-specific training\n\n### Risks\n\n- Full-text search may not scale as well as dedicated search engines\n- Mitigation: Design for potential Elasticsearch addition if needed\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Use JSONB for flexible product attributes\n- Implement connection pooling with PgBouncer\n- Set up streaming replication for read replicas\n- Use pg_trgm extension for fuzzy search\n\n## Related Decisions\n\n- ADR-0002: Caching Strategy (Redis) - complements database choice\n- ADR-0005: Search Architecture - may supersede if Elasticsearch needed\n\n## References\n\n- [PostgreSQL JSON Documentation](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/datatype-json.html)\n- [PostgreSQL Full Text Search](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/textsearch.html)\n- Internal: Performance benchmarks in `/docs/benchmarks/database-comparison.md`\n```\n\n### Template 2: Lightweight ADR\n\n```markdown\n# ADR-0012: Adopt TypeScript for Frontend Development\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n**Date**: 2024-01-15\n**Deciders**: @alice, @bob, @charlie\n\n## Context\n\nOur React codebase has grown to 50+ components with increasing bug reports\nrelated to prop type mismatches and undefined errors. PropTypes provide\nruntime-only checking.\n\n## Decision\n\nAdopt TypeScript for all new frontend code. Migrate existing code incrementally.\n\n## Consequences\n\n**Good**: Catch type errors at compile time, better IDE support, self-documenting\ncode.\n\n**Bad**: Learning curve for team, initial slowdown, build complexity increase.\n\n**Mitigations**: TypeScript training sessions, allow gradual adoption with\n`allowJs: true`.\n```\n\n### Template 3: Y-Statement Format\n\n```markdown\n# ADR-0015: API Gateway Selection\n\nIn the context of **building a microservices architecture**,\nfacing **the need for centralized API management, authentication, and rate limiting**,\nwe decided for **Kong Gateway**\nand against **AWS API Gateway and custom Nginx solution**,\nto achieve **vendor independence, plugin extensibility, and team familiarity with Lua**,\naccepting that **we need to manage Kong infrastructure ourselves**.\n```\n\n### Template 4: ADR for Deprecation\n\n```markdown\n# ADR-0020: Deprecate MongoDB in Favor of PostgreSQL\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted (Supersedes ADR-0003)\n\n## Context\n\nADR-0003 (2021) chose MongoDB for user profile storage due to schema flexibility\nneeds. Since then:\n\n- MongoDB''s multi-document transactions remain problematic for our use case\n- Our schema has stabilized and rarely changes\n- We now have PostgreSQL expertise from other services\n- Maintaining two databases increases operational burden\n\n## Decision\n\nDeprecate MongoDB and migrate user profiles to PostgreSQL.\n\n## Migration Plan\n\n1. **Phase 1** (Week 1-2): Create PostgreSQL schema, dual-write enabled\n2. **Phase 2** (Week 3-4): Backfill historical data, validate consistency\n3. **Phase 3** (Week 5): Switch reads to PostgreSQL, monitor\n4. **Phase 4** (Week 6): Remove MongoDB writes, decommission\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- Single database technology reduces operational complexity\n- ACID transactions for user data\n- Team can focus PostgreSQL expertise\n\n### Negative\n\n- Migration effort (~4 weeks)\n- Risk of data issues during migration\n- Lose some schema flexibility\n\n## Lessons Learned\n\nDocument from ADR-0003 experience:\n\n- Schema flexibility benefits were overestimated\n- Operational cost of multiple databases was underestimated\n- Consider long-term maintenance in technology decisions\n```\n\n### Template 5: Request for Comments (RFC) Style\n\n```markdown\n# RFC-0025: Adopt Event Sourcing for Order Management\n\n## Summary\n\nPropose adopting event sourcing pattern for the order management domain to\nimprove auditability, enable temporal queries, and support business analytics.\n\n## Motivation\n\nCurrent challenges:\n\n1. Audit requirements need complete order history\n2. \"What was the order state at time X?\" queries are impossible\n3. Analytics team needs event stream for real-time dashboards\n4. Order state reconstruction for customer support is manual\n\n## Detailed Design\n\n### Event Store\n```\n\nOrderCreated { orderId, customerId, items[], timestamp }\nOrderItemAdded { orderId, item, timestamp }\nOrderItemRemoved { orderId, itemId, timestamp }\nPaymentReceived { orderId, amount, paymentId, timestamp }\nOrderShipped { orderId, trackingNumber, timestamp }\n\n```\n\n### Projections\n\n- **CurrentOrderState**: Materialized view for queries\n- **OrderHistory**: Complete timeline for audit\n- **DailyOrderMetrics**: Analytics aggregation\n\n### Technology\n\n- Event Store: EventStoreDB (purpose-built, handles projections)\n- Alternative considered: Kafka + custom projection service\n\n## Drawbacks\n\n- Learning curve for team\n- Increased complexity vs. CRUD\n- Need to design events carefully (immutable once stored)\n- Storage growth (events never deleted)\n\n## Alternatives\n\n1. **Audit tables**: Simpler but doesn''t enable temporal queries\n2. **CDC from existing DB**: Complex, doesn''t change data model\n3. **Hybrid**: Event source only for order state changes\n\n## Unresolved Questions\n\n- [ ] Event schema versioning strategy\n- [ ] Retention policy for events\n- [ ] Snapshot frequency for performance\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Prototype with single order type (2 weeks)\n2. Team training on event sourcing (1 week)\n3. Full implementation and migration (4 weeks)\n4. Monitoring and optimization (ongoing)\n\n## References\n\n- [Event Sourcing by Martin Fowler](https://martinfowler.com/eaaDev/EventSourcing.html)\n- [EventStoreDB Documentation](https://www.eventstore.com/docs)\n```\n\n## ADR Management\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\ndocs/\n├── adr/\n│   ├── README.md           # Index and guidelines\n│   ├── template.md         # Team''s ADR template\n│   ├── 0001-use-postgresql.md\n│   ├── 0002-caching-strategy.md\n│   ├── 0003-mongodb-user-profiles.md  # [DEPRECATED]\n│   └── 0020-deprecate-mongodb.md      # Supersedes 0003\n```\n\n### ADR Index (README.md)\n\n```markdown\n# Architecture Decision Records\n\nThis directory contains Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) for [Project Name].\n\n## Index\n\n| ADR                                   | Title                              | Status     | Date       |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------- | ---------- |\n| [0001](0001-use-postgresql.md)        | Use PostgreSQL as Primary Database | Accepted   | 2024-01-10 |\n| [0002](0002-caching-strategy.md)      | Caching Strategy with Redis        | Accepted   | 2024-01-12 |\n| [0003](0003-mongodb-user-profiles.md) | MongoDB for User Profiles          | Deprecated | 2023-06-15 |\n| [0020](0020-deprecate-mongodb.md)     | Deprecate MongoDB                  | Accepted   | 2024-01-15 |\n\n## Creating a New ADR\n\n1. Copy `template.md` to `NNNN-title-with-dashes.md`\n2. Fill in the template\n3. Submit PR for review\n4. Update this index after approval\n\n## ADR Status\n\n- **Proposed**: Under discussion\n- **Accepted**: Decision made, implementing\n- **Deprecated**: No longer relevant\n- **Superseded**: Replaced by another ADR\n- **Rejected**: Considered but not adopted\n```\n\n### Automation (adr-tools)\n\n```bash\n# Install adr-tools\nbrew install adr-tools\n\n# Initialize ADR directory\nadr init docs/adr\n\n# Create new ADR\nadr new \"Use PostgreSQL as Primary Database\"\n\n# Supersede an ADR\nadr new -s 3 \"Deprecate MongoDB in Favor of PostgreSQL\"\n\n# Generate table of contents\nadr generate toc > docs/adr/README.md\n\n# Link related ADRs\nadr link 2 \"Complements\" 1 \"Is complemented by\"\n```\n\n## Review Process\n\n```markdown\n## ADR Review Checklist\n\n### Before Submission\n\n- [ ] Context clearly explains the problem\n- [ ] All viable options considered\n- [ ] Pros/cons balanced and honest\n- [ ] Consequences (positive and negative) documented\n- [ ] Related ADRs linked\n\n### During Review\n\n- [ ] At least 2 senior engineers reviewed\n- [ ] Affected teams consulted\n- [ ] Security implications considered\n- [ ] Cost implications documented\n- [ ] Reversibility assessed\n\n### After Acceptance\n\n- [ ] ADR index updated\n- [ ] Team notified\n- [ ] Implementation tickets created\n- [ ] Related documentation updated\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Write ADRs early** - Before implementation starts\n- **Keep them short** - 1-2 pages maximum\n- **Be honest about trade-offs** - Include real cons\n- **Link related decisions** - Build decision graph\n- **Update status** - Deprecate when superseded\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t change accepted ADRs** - Write new ones to supersede\n- **Don''t skip context** - Future readers need background\n- **Don''t hide failures** - Rejected decisions are valuable\n- **Don''t be vague** - Specific decisions, specific consequences\n- **Don''t forget implementation** - ADR without action is waste\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Documenting Architecture Decisions (Michael Nygard)](https://cognitect.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-architecture-decisions)\n- [MADR Template](https://adr.github.io/madr/)\n- [ADR GitHub Organization](https://adr.github.io/)\n- [adr-tools](https://github.com/npryce/adr-tools)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:24:05.983Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Documentation Agents needing structured decision-tracking capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化决策跟踪功能的技术文档代理。","ja":"技術文書エージェントが構造化された意思決定の追跡機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"구조화된 의사 결정 추적 기능이 필요한 기술 문서 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Documentación Técnica que necesitan capacidades de seguimiento de decisiones estructuradas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Documentation Technique ayant besoin de capacités de suivi de décision structurées.","de":"Perfekt für technische Dokumentationsagenten, die strukturierte Entscheidungsverlaufsmöglichkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Documentação Técnica que necessitam de capacidades de rastreamento de decisões estruturadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов технической документации, которым необходимы структурированные возможности отслеживания решений.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الوثائق الفنية الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات تتبع قرارات منظم"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to capture and manage Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) using comprehensive patterns, facilitating informed decision-making and streamlined onboarding processes through structured context and rationale documentation.","zh":"赋予代理捕获和管理架构决策记录（ADRs）使用全面的模式，从而促进明智的决策和通过结构化的上下文和理由文档简化入职流程。","ja":"エージェントに、包括的なパターンを使用してアーキテクチャの意思決定レコード（ADRs）をキャプチャして管理する機能を提供し、構造化されたコンテキストと理由の文書化を通じて、情報に基づいた意思決定と入社手続きの合理化を促進します。","ko":"에이전트가 포괄적인 패턴을 사용하여 아키텍처 의사 결정 기록(ADRs)을 캡처하고 관리할 수 있도록 하여, 구조화된 컨텍스트와 이유의 문서를 통해 정보에 기반한 의사 결정과 입사 절차의 간소화를促進합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a capturar y gestionar Registros de Decisiones de Arquitectura (ADRs) utilizando patrones integrales, lo que facilita una toma de decisiones informada y procesos de incorporación simplificados a través de la documentación de contexto y justificación estructurada.","fr":"Permet aux agents de capturer et de gérer des Enregistrements de Décisions d''Architecture (ADRs) en utilisant des modèles complets, ce qui facilite une prise de décision éclairée et des processus d''intégration simplifiés grâce à la documentation de contexte et de justification structurée.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Architekturentscheidungsregister (ADRs) mithilfe umfassender Muster zu erfassen und zu verwalten, was eine fundierte Entscheidungsfindung und vereinfachte Onboarding-Prozesse durch strukturierte Kontext- und Begründungsdokumentation ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a capturar e gerenciar Registros de Decisões de Arquitetura (ADRs) usando padrões abrangentes, facilitando a tomada de decisões informadas e processos de integração simplificados por meio da documentação de contexto e justificativa estruturada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью захватить и управлять Архитектурными Записями Решений (ADRs) с помощью всеобъемлющих шаблонов, облегчая принятие обоснованных решений и оптимизируя процессы адаптации благодаря структурированной документации контекста и обоснования.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على الاستحواذ وإدارة سجلات قرارات الهندسة المعمارية (ADRs) باستخدام أنماط شاملة ، مما يسهل اتخاذ قرارات مستنيرة وعمليات التكامل الميسرة من خلال توثيق السياق والمنطق المنظم"},"useCases":{"en":["Documenting technology choices and design trade-offs","Creating and maintaining ADRs for significant architectural decisions","Onboarding new team members with access to historical decision records"],"zh":["记录技术选择和设计权衡","为重大架构决策创建和维护ADRs","使用历史决策记录为新团队成员提供入职支持"],"ja":["技術選択と設計トレードオフを文書化する","重要なアーキテクチャ上の意思決定のためにADRsを作成し維持する","歴史的な意思決定レコードへのアクセスを提供して新しいチームメンバーの入社をサポートする"],"ko":["기술 선택과 설계 트레이드 오프를 문서화하는 것","중요한 아키텍처 의사 결정에 대한 ADRs 생성 및 유지","신규 팀원에게 역사적인 의사 결정 기록에 대한 액세스를 제공하여 입사 지원"],"es":["Documentar elecciones tecnológicas y compensaciones de diseño","Crear y mantener ADR para decisiones arquitectónicas significativas","Incorporar nuevos miembros del equipo con acceso a registros históricos de decisiones"],"fr":["Documenter les choix technologiques et les compromis de conception","Créer et maintenir des ADR pour des décisions architecturales significatives","Intégrer de nouveaux membres d''équipe avec un accès aux enregistrements historiques de décisions"],"de":["Technologieauswahlen und Designkompromisse dokumentieren","ADR für bedeutende Architekturentscheidungen erstellen und pflegen","Neue Teammitglieder mit Zugang zu historischen Entscheidungsprotokollen onboarding"],"pt":["Documentar escolhas tecnológicas e compromissos de design","Criar e manter ADRs para decisões arquiteturais significativas","Integrar novos membros da equipe com acesso a registros históricos de decisões"],"ru":["Документирование технологических выборов и компромиссов по дизайну","Создание и поддержание ADR для значимых архитектурных решений","Адаптация новых участников команды с доступом к историческим записям решений"],"ar":["توثيق الخيارات التكنولوجية وتراجعات التصميم","إنشاء وسائل إدارة ADRs للقرارات الهندسية المعمارية المهمة","تكامل أعضاء الفريق الجدد مع الوصول إلى سجلات القرارات التاريخية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to established ADR patterns and templates","Effective use depends on consistent record-keeping and maintenance"],"zh":["需要遵守既定的ADR模式和模板","有效使用取决于一致的记录保存和维护"],"ja":["既存のADRパターンとテンプレートに従う必要がある","有効な使用は一貫したレコード保守とメンテナンスに依存する"],"ko":["既存의 ADR 패턴과 템플릿을 따라야 함","유효한 사용은 일관된 기록 보관 및 유지에 의존"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a patrones y plantillas de ADR establecidos","El uso efectivo depende de un registro y mantenimiento consistentes"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à des modèles et des modèles de ADR établis","L''utilisation efficace dépend d''un enregistrement et d''une maintenance constants"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung etablierter ADR-Muster und -Vorlagen","Der effektive Einsatz hängt von einem konsistenten Aufzeichnen und Warten ab"],"pt":["Exige adesão a padrões e modelos ADR estabelecidos","Uso eficaz depende de registro e manutenção consistentes"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения установленных шаблонов и шаблонов ADR","Эффективное использование зависит от последовательного ведения и поддержания записей"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام bằng أنماط و قوالب ADR المحددة","الاستخدام الفعال يعتمد على تسجيل و صيانة متسقة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
