":"Demander des revues de code est essentiel pour assurer la qualité du logiciel","de":"Code-Reviews anfordern ist entscheidend für die Qualität der Software","pt":"Revisão de código é uma prática essencial para garantir a qualidade do software. Saiba quando solicitar revisões e como fazer para melhorar a qualidade do se...","ru":"Код-ревью - это важная практика для обеспечения качества программного обеспечения. Узнайте, когда запрашивать обзоры и как это делать, чтобы улучшить качеств...","ar":"مراجعة الشفرة هي ممارسة أساسية لضمان جودة البرمجيات. تعلم متى تطلب المراجعات وكيف تفعل ذلك لتحسين جودة شفرتك","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["代码审查","问题发现","代码质量提高","开发协作","代码安全"],"ja":["コードレビュー","問題発見","コード品質向上","開発コラボレーション","コードセキュリティ"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","문제 발견","코드 품질 향상","개발 협업","코드 보안"],"es":["Revisión de código temprana y frecuente","Detección de errores antes de la implementación","Mejora de la calidad del software","Optimización del proceso de desarrollo","Colaboración entre desarrolladores"],"fr":["Revue de code précoce et fréquente","Détection des erreurs avant la mise en œuvre","Amélioration de la qualité du logiciel","Optimisation du processus de développement","Collaboration entre les développeurs"],"de":["Frühzeitige und häufige Code-Review","Fehlererkennung vor der Implementierung","Verbesserung der Softwarequalität","Optimierung des Entwicklungsprozesses","Zusammenarbeit zwischen Entwicklern"],"pt":["Revisão de código para garantir a qualidade","Detecção de erros e bugs","Melhoria da legibilidade e manutenção do código","Redução do tempo de depuração","Aumento da produtividade da equipe"],"ru":["Код-ревью для обеспечения качества","Обнаружение ошибок и багов","Улучшение читаемости и обслуживания кода","Сокращение времени отладки","Повышение производительности команды"],"ar":["مراجعة الشفرة لضمان الجودة","اكتشاف الأخطاء والعيوب","تحسين قراءة و صيانة الشفرة","تقليل وقت تصحيح الأخطاء","زيادة إنتاجية الفريق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码质量","开发协作","代码安全","代码review","开发流程"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード品質","開発コラボレーション","コードセキュリティ","コードreview","開発プロセス"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 品질","개발 협업","코드 보안","코드 review","개발 프로세스"],"es":["revisión de código","desarrollo de software","calidad del software","pruebas de código","colaboración entre desarrolladores","mejora de la calidad","optimización del proceso de desarrollo"],"fr":["revue de code","développement de logiciel","qualité du logiciel","tests de code","collaboration entre les développeurs","amélioration de la qualité","optimisation du processus de développement"],"de":["Code-Review","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Qualität","Code-Tests","Zusammenarbeit zwischen Entwicklern","Qualitätsverbesserung","Optimierung des Entwicklungsprozesses"],"pt":["revisão de código","qualidade de software","desenvolvimento de software","revisão de código preciso","melhoria da qualidade","redução de erros"],"ru":["код-ревью","качество программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения","ранний код-ревью","улучшение качества","уменьшение ошибок"],"ar":["مراجعة الشفرة","جودة البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات","مراجعة الشفرة المبكرة","تحسين الجودة","تقليل الأخطاء"]}},"owner":"dwalleck","repo":"kiro-starter-kit","repoPath":"dwalleck/kiro-starter-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"requesting-code-review","description":"Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements","bodyPreview":"# Requesting Code Review\n\nDispatch superpowers:code-reviewer subagent to catch issues before they cascade.\n\n**Core principle:** Review early, review often.\n\n## When to Request Review\n\n**Mandatory:**\n- After each task in subagent-driven development\n- After completing major feature\n- Before merge to main\n\n**Optional but valuable:**\n- When stuck (fresh perspective)\n- Before refactoring (baseline check)\n- After fixing complex bug\n\n## How to Request\n\n**1. Get git SHAs:**\n```bash\nBASE_SHA=$(git rev-pa","body":"# Requesting Code Review\n\nDispatch superpowers:code-reviewer subagent to catch issues before they cascade.\n\n**Core principle:** Review early, review often.\n\n## When to Request Review\n\n**Mandatory:**\n- After each task in subagent-driven development\n- After completing major feature\n- Before merge to main\n\n**Optional but valuable:**\n- When stuck (fresh perspective)\n- Before refactoring (baseline check)\n- After fixing complex bug\n\n## How to Request\n\n**1. Get git SHAs:**\n```bash\nBASE_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD~1)  # or origin/main\nHEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n```\n\n**2. Dispatch code-reviewer subagent:**\n\nUse Task tool with superpowers:code-reviewer type, fill template at `code-reviewer.md`\n\n**Placeholders:**\n- `{WHAT_WAS_IMPLEMENTED}` - What you just built\n- `{PLAN_OR_REQUIREMENTS}` - What it should do\n- `{BASE_SHA}` - Starting commit\n- `{HEAD_SHA}` - Ending commit\n- `{DESCRIPTION}` - Brief summary\n\n**3. Act on feedback:**\n- Fix Critical issues immediately\n- Fix Important issues before proceeding\n- Note Minor issues for later\n- Push back if reviewer is wrong (with reasoning)\n\n## Example\n\n```\n[Just completed Task 2: Add verification function]\n\nYou: Let me request code review before proceeding.\n\nBASE_SHA=$(git log --oneline | grep \"Task 1\" | head -1 | awk ''{print $1}'')\nHEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n\n[Dispatch superpowers:code-reviewer subagent]\n  WHAT_WAS_IMPLEMENTED: Verification and repair functions for conversation index\n  PLAN_OR_REQUIREMENTS: Task 2 from docs/plans/deployment-plan.md\n  BASE_SHA: a7981ec\n  HEAD_SHA: 3df7661\n  DESCRIPTION: Added verifyIndex() and repairIndex() with 4 issue types\n\n[Subagent returns]:\n  Strengths: Clean architecture, real tests\n  Issues:\n    Important: Missing progress indicators\n    Minor: Magic number (100) for reporting interval\n  Assessment: Ready to proceed\n\nYou: [Fix progress indicators]\n[Continue to Task 3]\n```\n\n## Integration with Workflows\n\n**Subagent-Driven Development:**\n- Review after EACH task\n- Catch issues before they compound\n- Fix before moving to next task\n\n**Executing Plans:**\n- Review after each batch (3 tasks)\n- Get feedback, apply, continue\n\n**Ad-Hoc Development:**\n- Review before merge\n- Review when stuck\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Skip review because \"it''s simple\"\n- Ignore Critical issues\n- Proceed with unfixed Important issues\n- Argue with valid technical feedback\n\n**If reviewer wrong:**\n- Push back with technical reasoning\n- Show code/tests that prove it works\n- Request clarification\n\nSee template at: requesting-code-review/code-reviewer.md\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:24:07.843Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing to catch issues before they cascade in subagent-driven development","zh":"非常适合需要在子代理驱动开发中捕捉问题的代码审查代理，防止问题在后续开发中被放大","ja":"サブエージェント駆動開発で問題を事前に発見する必要があるコードレビューエージェントに最適","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트가 서브 에이전트 주도 개발에서 문제를 사전에 포착해야 하는 경우에 적합함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan detectar problemas antes de que se propaguen en el desarrollo impulsado por subagentes","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code qui ont besoin de détecter les problèmes avant qu''ils ne se propagent dans le développement piloté par des sous-agents","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die Probleme erkennen müssen, bevor sie sich im subagentengesteuerten Entwicklungsumfeld ausbreiten","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam detectar problemas antes que eles sejam propagados no desenvolvimento impulsionado por subagentes","ru":"Идеально для агентов код-ревью, которым необходимо обнаруживать проблемы до того, как они станут распространяться в субагент-ориентированном развитии","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى التقاط المشكلات قبل أن تتسارع في التطوير القائم على وكيل فرعي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to dispatch subagents like code-reviewer for early and frequent review, utilizing git SHAs and ensuring adherence to core principles like reviewing after each task and before merge to main, facilitating a proactive approach to bug fixing and refactoring","zh":"赋予代理能力以派遣子代理，例如代码审查员，以便在早期和频繁地进行审查，利用git SHA并确保遵守每个任务后和合并到主分支前进行审查的核心原则，从而促进主动的错误修复和重构方法","ja":"エージェントにサブエージェントを派遣する機能を付与し、コードレビューアーを早期に頻繁にレビューを行うことができるようにし、git SHAを利用し、タスクごとにレビューを行い、メインブランチにマージする前にレビューを行うなどのコア原則に従うことを保証し、バグの修復とリファクタリングに主動的に取り組むことができる","ko":"에이전트에 서브 에이전트를派遣할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 코드 리뷰어와 같은 에이전트를 통해 초기에 빈번한 리뷰를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, git SHA를 활용하여 각 작업 후 및 메인 브랜치에 병합하기 전 리뷰를 수행하는 등의 핵심 원칙을 준수하도록 보장함으로써 버그 수정 및 리팩토링에 적극적으로 접근할 수 있는 방식을 권장함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a enviar subagentes como revisores de código para revisiones tempranas y frecuentes, utilizando SHAs de git y asegurando el cumplimiento de principios básicos como la revisión después de cada tarea y antes de la fusión con la rama principal, facilitando un enfoque proactivo para la solución de errores y refactorización","fr":"Permet aux agents d''envoyer des sous-agents comme des réviseurs de code pour des examens précoces et fréquents, en utilisant des SHAs Git et en assurant le respect de principes fondamentaux tels que l''examen après chaque tâche et avant la fusion avec la branche principale, facilitant une approche proactive pour la correction de bogues et la réorganisation","de":"Ermöglich es Agenten, Subagenten wie Code-Reviewer zu entsenden, um frühe und häufige Überprüfungen durchzuführen, indem sie git-SHAs nutzen und die Einhaltung von Grundprinzipien wie der Überprüfung nach jeder Aufgabe und vor dem Merge in den Hauptzweig sicherstellen, wodurch ein proaktiver Ansatz für die Fehlerbehebung und Refaktorisierung ermöglicht wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a enviar subagentes como revisor de código para revisão precoce e frequente, utilizando SHAs do git e garantindo a adesão a princípios fundamentais como revisar após cada tarefa e antes da mesclagem com o principal, facilitando uma abordagem proativa para solução de bugs e refatoração","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отправлять субагентов, такие как код-ревьюер, для раннего и частого обзора, используя SHA git и обеспечивая соблюдение основных принципов, таких как обзор после каждой задачи и до слияния с основным, облегчая активный подход к исправлению ошибок и рефакторингу","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من إرسال وكلاء فرعيين مثل مراجع الشفرة للاستعراض المبكر والمكرر، مع استخدام SHA Git وضمان الالتزام بمبادئ أساسية مثل المراجعة بعد كل مهمة وقبل الدمج في الرئيسي، مما يسهل المنهج النشط لصيانة الأخطاء وإعادة هيكلة البرنامج"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code review requests after completing major features","Generating baseline checks before refactoring","Debugging complex bugs with fresh perspectives"],"zh":["自动在完成主要功能后发起代码审查请求","在重构前生成基线检查","带着新鲜视角调试复杂错误"],"ja":["主要な機能を完了した後にコードレビューのリクエストを自動的に送信する","リファクタリング前にベースラインチェックを生成する","新しい視点で複雑なバグをデバッグする"],"ko":["주요 기능을 완료한 후 코드 리뷰 요청을 자동으로 발송함","리팩토링 전에 기준점 검사를 생성함","신선한 관점으로 복잡한 버그를 디버깅함"],"es":["Automatizar las solicitudes de revisión de código después de completar características principales","Generar controles de referencia antes de la refactorización","Depurar errores complejos con perspectivas frescas"],"fr":["Automatiser les demandes d''examen de code après avoir terminé les fonctionnalités principales","Générer des contrôles de base avant la réorganisation","Déboguer des bogues complexes avec des perspectives fraîches"],"de":["Automatisieren von Code-Review-Anfragen nach dem Abschließen von Hauptfunktionen","Erzeugen von Basisprüfungen vor der Refaktorisierung","Beheben komplexer Fehler mit frischen Perspektiven"],"pt":["Automatizar solicitações de revisão de código após a conclusão de recursos principais","Gerar verificações de baseline antes da refatoração","Depurar bugs complexos com perspectivas frescas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать запросы на код-ревью после завершения основных функций","Генерировать базовые проверки перед рефакторингом","Отладить сложные ошибки с свежими перспективами"],"ar":["الاستفادة من طلبات مراجعة الشفرة تلقائيًا بعد إكمال الميزات الرئيسية","توليد فحص الأساس قبل إعادة هيكلة البرنامج","تصحيح الأخطاء المعقدة من خلال منظورات جديدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git integration","Subagent-driven development environment needed","Adherence to specific review protocols mandatory"],"zh":["需要git集成","需要子代理驱动开发环境","必须遵守特定的审查协议"],"ja":["gitの統合が必要","サブエージェント駆動開発環境が必要","特定のレビュープロトコルに従うことが必須"],"ko":["git 통합이 필요함","서브 에이전트 주도 개발 환경이 필요함","특정 리뷰 프로토콜을 준수해야 함"],"es":["Requiere integración con git","Entorno de desarrollo impulsado por subagentes necesario","Cumplimiento de protocolos de revisión específicos obligatorio"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec Git","Environnement de développement piloté par des sous-agents nécessaire","Respect de protocoles d''examen spécifiques obligatoire"],"de":["Erfordert git-Integration","Subagentengesteuerte Entwicklungsumgebung erforderlich","Einhalten spezifischer Review-Protokolle obligatorisch"],"pt":["Requer integração com o git","Ambiente de desenvolvimento impulsionado por subagentes necessário","Adesão a protocolos de revisão específicos é obrigatória"],"ru":["Требуется интеграция с git","Необходимо окружение субагент-ориентированного развития","Соблюдение определенных протоколов обзора является обязательным"],"ar":["يحتاج إلى دمج مع Git","بيئة تطوير مدعومة بوكيل فرعي ضرورية","الالتزام ببروتوكولات مراجعة محددة إلزامي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('nrwl/nx/ci-monitor', 'community', 'nrwl', 'nx', 'nrwl/nx', 'ci-monitor', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:24:20.779Z', NULL, '{"id":"nrwl/nx/ci-monitor","name":"ci-monitor","description":{"zh":"CI 监控器是一种用于监控 Nx Cloud CI 流水线执行和处理自愈修复的工具","ja":"CI モニターは、Nx Cloud CI パイプラインの実行を監視し、セルフヒーリングの修復を処理するツール","ko":"CI 모니터는 Nx Cloud CI 파이프라인 실행을 모니터링하고 자가 치유 수정을 처리하는 도구","es":"La plataforma de monorepo que optimiza tus compilaciones, escala tu CI y soluciona automaticamente las PR fallidas","fr":"La plate-forme de monorepo qui optimise vos compilations, met à l''échelle votre CI et résout automatiquement les PR échouées","de":"Die Monorepo-Plattform, die Ihre Kompilierungen optimiert, Ihr CI skaliert und fehlgeschlagene PRs automatisch behebt","pt":"O CI Monitor é uma plataforma que otimiza builds e CI, permitindo que os desenvolvedores entreguem software em metade do tempo","ru":"CI Monitor — это платформа, которая оптимизирует сборки и CI, позволяя разработчикам доставлять программное обеспечение вдвое быстрее","ar":"CI Monitor هو منصة تحسن البناء والسي، مما يسمح للمطورين بتسليم البرامج في نصف الوقت","en":"The Monorepo Platform that amplifies both developers and AI agents. Nx optimizes your builds, scales your CI, and fixes failed PRs automatically. Ship in half the time."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"CI 监控器 - 加速开发和自动化","ja":"CI モニター - 開発と自動化の効率化","ko":"CI 모니터 - 개발과 자동화의 가속화","es":"Monitoreo de CI: Optimiza tus flujos de trabajo","fr":"Surveillance CI : Optimisez vos flux de travail","de":"CI-Überwachung: Optimieren Sie Ihre Arbeitsabläufe","pt":"CI Monitor: Otimização de Builds e CI","ru":"CI Monitor: оптимизация сборок и CI","ar":"CI Monitor: تحسين البناء والسي","en":"ci-monitor"},"description":{"zh":"CI 监控器是一种用于监控 Nx Cloud CI 流水线执行和处理自愈修复的工具","ja":"CI モニターは、Nx Cloud CI パイプラインの実行を監視し、セルフヒーリングの修復を処理するツール","ko":"CI 모니터는 Nx Cloud CI 파이프라인 실행을 모니터링하고 자가 치유 수정을 처리하는 도구","es":"La plataforma de monorepo que optimiza tus compilaciones, escala tu CI y soluciona automaticamente las PR fallidas","fr":"La plate-forme de monorepo qui optimise vos compilations, met à l''échelle votre CI et résout automatiquement les PR échouées","de":"Die Monorepo-Plattform, die Ihre Kompilierungen optimiert, Ihr CI skaliert und fehlgeschlagene PRs automatisch behebt","pt":"O CI Monitor é uma plataforma que otimiza builds e CI, permitindo que os desenvolvedores entreguem software em metade do tempo","ru":"CI Monitor — это платформа, которая оптимизирует сборки и CI, позволяя разработчикам доставлять программное обеспечение вдвое быстрее","ar":"CI Monitor هو منصة تحسن البناء والسي، مما يسمح للمطورين بتسليم البرامج في نصف الوقت","en":"The Monorepo Platform that amplifies both developers and AI agents. Nx optimizes your builds, scales your CI, and fixes failed PRs automatically. Ship in hal..."},"definition":{"en":"The Monorepo Platform that amplifies both developers and AI agents. Nx optimizes your builds, scales your CI, and fixes failed PRs automatically. Ship in half the time."},"features":{"zh":["自动监控 CI 流水线执行","处理自愈修复","优化构建和扩展 CI","自动修复失败的 PR","支持 Nx Cloud"],"ja":["CI パイプラインの実行を自動的に監視","セルフヒーリングの修復を処理","ビルドを最適化し、CI を拡張","失敗した PR を自動的に修復","Nx Cloud をサポート"],"ko":["CI 파이프라인 실행을 자동으로 모니터링","자가 치유 수정을 처리","빌드를 최적화하고 CI를 확장","실패한 PR을 자동으로 수정","Nx Cloud를 지원"],"es":["Optimización de compilaciones","Escalado de CI","Solución automática de PR fallidas","Integración con Nx Cloud","Monitoreo de estado de CI","Automatización de flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Optimisation des compilations","Mise à l''échelle de la CI","Résolution automatique des PR échouées","Intégration avec Nx Cloud","Surveillance de l''état de la CI","Automatisation des flux de travail"],"de":["Optimierung von Kompilierungen","Skalierung von CI","Automatische Behebung fehlgeschlagener PRs","Integration mit Nx Cloud","Überwachung des CI-Status","Automatisierung von Workflows"],"pt":["Otimização de builds","Escala de CI","Correção automática de PRs com falhas","Monitoramento de pipeline de CI","Integração com Nx Cloud"],"ru":["Оптимизация сборок","Масштабирование CI","Автоматическое исправление ошибок в PR","Мониторинг конвейера CI","Интеграция с Nx Cloud"],"ar":["تحسين البناء","توسيع نطاق السي","تصحيح تلقائي للبرامج الناقصة","مراقبة خط أنابيب السي","التكامل مع Nx Cloud"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CI 监控器","自动化","优化","CI 流水线","Nx Cloud","开发工具","自动修复"],"ja":["CI モニター","自動化","最適化","CI パイプライン","Nx Cloud","開発ツール","自動修復"],"ko":["CI 모니터","자동화","최적화","CI 파이프라인","Nx Cloud","개발 도구","자동 수정"],"es":["monorepo","ci monitor","nx cloud","desarrollo de software","automatización de flujos de trabajo","optimización de compilaciones","escalado de CI","solución de PR fallidas","integración con Nx Cloud"],"fr":["monorepo","surveillance ci","nx cloud","développement de logiciels","automatisation des flux de travail","optimisation des compilations","mise à l''échelle de la CI","résolution de PR échouées","intégration avec Nx Cloud"],"de":["monorepo","ci-überwachung","nx cloud","softwareentwicklung","automatisierung von workflows","optimierung von kompilierungen","skalierung von ci","behebung fehlgeschlagener prs","integration mit nx cloud"],"pt":["CI Monitor","Otimização de builds","Escala de CI","Desenvolvimento de software","Nx Cloud","Pipeline de CI","Correção automática de PRs"],"ru":["CI Monitor","Оптимизация сборок","Масштабирование CI","Разработка программного обеспечения","Nx Cloud","Конвейер CI","Автоматическое исправление ошибок в PR"],"ar":["CI Monitor","تحسين البناء","توسيع نطاق السي","تطوير البرامج","Nx Cloud","خط أنابيب السي","تصحيح تلقائي للبرامج الناقصة"]}},"owner":"nrwl","repo":"nx","repoPath":"nrwl/nx","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ci-monitor","description":"Monitor Nx Cloud CI pipeline and handle self-healing fixes automatically. Checks for Nx Cloud connection before starting.","bodyPreview":"# CI Monitor Command\n\nYou are the orchestrator for monitoring Nx Cloud CI pipeline executions and handling self-healing fixes. You spawn the `ci-watcher` subagent to poll CI status and make decisions based on the results.\n\n## Context\n\n- **Current Branch:** !`git branch --show-current`\n- **Current Commit:** !`git rev-parse --short HEAD`\n- **Remote Status:** !`git status -sb | head -1`\n\n## User Instructions\n\n$ARGUMENTS\n\n**Important:** If user provides specific instructions, respect them over defau","body":"# CI Monitor Command\n\nYou are the orchestrator for monitoring Nx Cloud CI pipeline executions and handling self-healing fixes. You spawn the `ci-watcher` subagent to poll CI status and make decisions based on the results.\n\n## Context\n\n- **Current Branch:** !`git branch --show-current`\n- **Current Commit:** !`git rev-parse --short HEAD`\n- **Remote Status:** !`git status -sb | head -1`\n\n## User Instructions\n\n$ARGUMENTS\n\n**Important:** If user provides specific instructions, respect them over default behaviors described below.\n\n## Configuration Defaults\n\n| Setting                   | Default       | Description                                                         |\n| ------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--max-cycles`            | 10            | Maximum CIPE cycles before timeout                                  |\n| `--timeout`               | 120           | Maximum duration in minutes                                         |\n| `--verbosity`             | medium        | Output level: minimal, medium, verbose                              |\n| `--branch`                | (auto-detect) | Branch to monitor                                                   |\n| `--subagent-timeout`      | 60            | Subagent polling timeout in minutes                                 |\n| `--fresh`                 | false         | Ignore previous context, start fresh                                |\n| `--auto-fix-workflow`     | false         | Attempt common fixes for pre-CIPE failures (e.g., lockfile updates) |\n| `--new-cipe-timeout`      | 10            | Minutes to wait for new CIPE after action                           |\n| `--local-verify-attempts` | 3             | Max local verification + enhance cycles before pushing to CI        |\n\nParse any overrides from `$ARGUMENTS` and merge with defaults.\n\n## Nx Cloud Connection Check\n\n**CRITICAL**: Before starting the monitoring loop, verify the workspace is connected to Nx Cloud.\n\n### Step 0: Verify Nx Cloud Connection\n\n1. **Check `nx.json`** at workspace root for `nxCloudId` or `nxCloudAccessToken`\n2. **If `nx.json` missing OR neither property exists** → exit with:\n   ```\n   [ci-monitor] Nx Cloud not connected. Unlock 70% faster CI and auto-fix broken PRs with https://nx.dev/nx-cloud\n   ```\n3. **If connected** → continue to main loop\n\n## Session Context Behavior\n\n**Important:** Within a Claude Code session, conversation context persists. If you Ctrl+C to interrupt the monitor and re-run `/ci-monitor`, Claude remembers the previous state and may continue from where it left off.\n\n- **To continue monitoring:** Just re-run `/ci-monitor` (context is preserved)\n- **To start fresh:** Use `/ci-monitor --fresh` to ignore previous context\n- **For a completely clean slate:** Exit Claude Code and restart `claude`\n\n## Default Behaviors by Status\n\nThe subagent returns with one of the following statuses. This table defines the **default behavior** for each status. User instructions can override any of these.\n\n| Status              | Default Behavior                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ci_success`        | Exit with success. Log \"CI passed successfully!\"                                                                                                                  |\n| `fix_auto_applying` | Fix will be auto-applied by self-healing. Do NOT call MCP. Record `last_cipe_url`, spawn new subagent in wait mode to poll for new CIPE.                          |\n| `fix_available`     | Compare `failedTaskIds` vs `verifiedTaskIds` to determine verification state. See **Fix Available Decision Logic** section below.                                 |\n| `fix_failed`        | Self-healing failed to generate fix. Attempt local fix based on `taskOutputSummary`. If successful → commit, push, loop. If not → exit with failure.              |\n| `environment_issue` | Call MCP to request rerun: `update_self_healing_fix({ shortLink, action: \"RERUN_ENVIRONMENT_STATE\" })`. New CIPE spawns automatically. Loop to poll for new CIPE. |\n| `no_fix`            | CI failed, no fix available (self-healing disabled or not executable). Attempt local fix if possible. Otherwise exit with failure.                                |\n| `no_new_cipe`       | Expected CIPE never spawned (CI workflow likely failed before Nx tasks). Report to user, attempt common fixes if configured, or exit with guidance.               |\n| `polling_timeout`   | Subagent polling timeout reached. Exit with timeout.                                                                                                              |\n| `cipe_canceled`     | CIPE was canceled. Exit with canceled status.                                                                                                                     |\n| `cipe_timed_out`    | CIPE timed out. Exit with timeout status.                                                                                                                         |\n| `error`             | Increment `no_progress_count`. If >= 3 → exit with circuit breaker. Otherwise wait 60s and loop.                                                                  |\n\n### Fix Available Decision Logic\n\nWhen subagent returns `fix_available`, main agent compares `failedTaskIds` vs `verifiedTaskIds`:\n\n#### Step 1: Categorize Tasks\n\n1. **Verified tasks** = tasks in both `failedTaskIds` AND `verifiedTaskIds`\n2. **Unverified tasks** = tasks in `failedTaskIds` but NOT in `verifiedTaskIds`\n3. **E2E tasks** = unverified tasks where target contains \"e2e\" (task format: `<project>:<target>` or `<project>:<target>:<config>`)\n4. **Verifiable tasks** = unverified tasks that are NOT e2e\n\n#### Step 2: Determine Path\n\n| Condition                               | Path                                     |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| No unverified tasks (all verified)      | Apply via MCP                            |\n| Unverified tasks exist, but ALL are e2e | Apply via MCP (treat as verified enough) |\n| Verifiable tasks exist                  | Local verification flow                  |\n\n#### Step 3a: Apply via MCP (fully/e2e-only verified)\n\n- Call `update_self_healing_fix({ shortLink, action: \"APPLY\" })`\n- Record `last_cipe_url`, spawn subagent in wait mode\n\n#### Step 3b: Local Verification Flow\n\nWhen verifiable (non-e2e) unverified tasks exist:\n\n1. **Detect package manager:**\n   - `pnpm-lock.yaml` exists → `pnpm nx`\n   - `yarn.lock` exists → `yarn nx`\n   - Otherwise → `npx nx`\n\n2. **Run verifiable tasks in parallel:**\n   - Spawn `general` subagents to run each task concurrently\n   - Each subagent runs: `<pm> nx run <taskId>`\n   - Collect pass/fail results from all subagents\n\n3. **Evaluate results:**\n\n| Result                    | Action                       |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| ALL verifiable tasks pass | Apply via MCP                |\n| ANY verifiable task fails | Apply-locally + enhance flow |\n\n4. **Apply-locally + enhance flow:**\n   - Run `nx apply-locally <shortLink>`\n   - Enhance the code to fix failing tasks\n   - Run failing tasks again to verify fix\n   - If still failing → increment `local_verify_count`, loop back to enhance\n   - If passing → commit and push, record `expected_commit_sha`, spawn subagent in wait mode\n\n5. **Track attempts** (wraps step 4):\n   - Increment `local_verify_count` after each enhance cycle\n   - If `local_verify_count >= local_verify_attempts` (default: 3):\n     - Get code in commit-able state\n     - Commit and push with message indicating local verification failed\n     - Report to user:\n       ```\n       [ci-monitor] Local verification failed after <N> attempts. Pushed to CI for final validation. Failed: <taskIds>\n       ```\n     - Record `expected_commit_sha`, spawn subagent in wait mode (let CI be final judge)\n\n#### Commit Message Format\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"fix(<projects>): <brief description>\n\nFailed tasks: <taskId1>, <taskId2>\nLocal verification: passed|enhanced|failed-pushing-to-ci\"\n```\n\n### Unverified Fix Flow (No Verification Attempted)\n\nWhen `verificationStatus` is `FAILED`, `NOT_EXECUTABLE`, or fix has `couldAutoApplyTasks != true` with no verification:\n\n- Analyze fix content (`suggestedFix`, `suggestedFixReasoning`, `taskOutputSummary`)\n- If fix looks correct → apply via MCP\n- If fix needs enhancement → use Apply Locally + Enhance Flow above\n- If fix is wrong → reject via MCP, fix from scratch, commit, push\n\n### Auto-Apply Eligibility\n\nThe `couldAutoApplyTasks` field indicates whether the fix is eligible for automatic application:\n\n- **`true`**: Fix is eligible for auto-apply. Subagent keeps polling while verification is in progress. Returns `fix_auto_applying` when verified, or `fix_available` if verification fails.\n- **`false`** or **`null`**: Fix requires manual action (apply via MCP, apply locally, or reject)\n\n**Key point**: When subagent returns `fix_auto_applying`, do NOT call MCP to apply - self-healing handles it. Just spawn a new subagent in wait mode.\n\n### Apply vs Reject vs Apply Locally\n\n- **Apply via MCP**: Calls `update_self_healing_fix({ shortLink, action: \"APPLY\" })`. Self-healing agent applies the fix in CI and a new CIPE spawns automatically. No local git operations needed.\n- **Apply Locally**: Runs `nx apply-locally <shortLink>`. Applies the patch to your local working directory and sets state to `APPLIED_LOCALLY`. Use this when you want to enhance the fix before pushing.\n- **Reject via MCP**: Calls `update_self_healing_fix({ shortLink, action: \"REJECT\" })`. Marks fix as rejected. Use only when the fix is completely wrong and you''ll fix from scratch.\n\n### Apply Locally + Enhance Flow\n\nWhen the fix needs enhancement (use `nx apply-locally`, NOT reject):\n\n1. Apply the patch locally: `nx apply-locally <shortLink>` (this also updates state to `APPLIED_LOCALLY`)\n2. Make additional changes as needed\n3. Commit and push:\n   ```bash\n   git add -A\n   git commit -m \"fix: resolve <failedTaskIds>\"\n   git push origin $(git branch --show-current)\n   ```\n4. Loop to poll for new CIPE\n\n### Reject + Fix From Scratch Flow\n\nWhen the fix is completely wrong:\n\n1. Call MCP to reject: `update_self_healing_fix({ shortLink, action: \"REJECT\" })`\n2. Fix the issue from scratch locally\n3. Commit and push:\n   ```bash\n   git add -A\n   git commit -m \"fix: resolve <failedTaskIds>\"\n   git push origin $(git branch --show-current)\n   ```\n4. Loop to poll for new CIPE\n\n### Environment Issue Handling\n\nWhen `failureClassification == ''ENVIRONMENT_STATE''`:\n\n1. Call MCP to request rerun: `update_self_healing_fix({ shortLink, action: \"RERUN_ENVIRONMENT_STATE\" })`\n2. New CIPE spawns automatically (no local git operations needed)\n3. Loop to poll for new CIPE with `previousCipeUrl` set\n\n### No-New-CIPE Handling\n\nWhen `status == ''no_new_cipe''`:\n\nThis means the expected CIPE was never created - CI likely failed before Nx tasks could run.\n\n1. **Report to user:**\n\n   ```\n   [ci-monitor] No CI attempt for <sha> after 10 min. Check CI provider for pre-Nx failures (install, checkout, auth). Last CI attempt: <previousCipeUrl>\n   ```\n\n2. **If user configured auto-fix attempts** (e.g., `--auto-fix-workflow`):\n   - Detect package manager: check for `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `yarn.lock`, `package-lock.json`\n   - Run install to update lockfile:\n     ```bash\n     pnpm install   # or npm install / yarn install\n     ```\n   - If lockfile changed:\n     ```bash\n     git add pnpm-lock.yaml  # or appropriate lockfile\n     git commit -m \"chore: update lockfile\"\n     git push origin $(git branch --show-current)\n     ```\n   - Record new commit SHA, loop to poll with `expectedCommitSha`\n\n3. **Otherwise:** Exit with `no_new_cipe` status, providing guidance for user to investigate\n\n## Exit Conditions\n\nExit the monitoring loop when ANY of these conditions are met:\n\n| Condition                                   | Exit Type        |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| CI passes (`cipeStatus == ''SUCCEEDED''`)     | Success          |\n| Max CIPE cycles reached                     | Timeout          |\n| Max duration reached                        | Timeout          |\n| 3 consecutive no-progress iterations        | Circuit breaker  |\n| No fix available and local fix not possible | Failure          |\n| No new CIPE and auto-fix not configured     | Pre-CIPE failure |\n| User cancels                                | Cancelled        |\n\n## Main Loop\n\n### Step 1: Initialize Tracking\n\n```\ncycle_count = 0\nstart_time = now()\nno_progress_count = 0\nlocal_verify_count = 0\nlast_state = null\nlast_cipe_url = null\nexpected_commit_sha = null\n```\n\n### Step 2: Spawn Subagent\n\nSpawn the `ci-watcher` subagent to poll CI status:\n\n**Fresh start (first spawn, no expected CIPE):**\n\n```\nTask(\n  agent: \"ci-watcher\",\n  prompt: \"Monitor CI for branch ''<branch>''.\n           Subagent timeout: <subagent-timeout> minutes.\n           New-CIPE timeout: <new-cipe-timeout> minutes.\n           Verbosity: <verbosity>.\"\n)\n```\n\n**After action that triggers new CIPE (wait mode):**\n\n```\nTask(\n  agent: \"ci-watcher\",\n  prompt: \"Monitor CI for branch ''<branch>''.\n           Subagent timeout: <subagent-timeout> minutes.\n           New-CIPE timeout: <new-cipe-timeout> minutes.\n           Verbosity: <verbosity>.\n\n           WAIT MODE: A new CIPE should spawn. Ignore old CIPE until new one appears.\n           Expected commit SHA: <expected_commit_sha>\n           Previous CIPE URL: <last_cipe_url>\"\n)\n```\n\n### Step 3: Handle Subagent Response\n\nWhen subagent returns:\n\n1. Check the returned status\n2. Look up default behavior in the table above\n3. Check if user instructions override the default\n4. Execute the appropriate action\n5. **If action expects new CIPE**, update tracking (see Step 3a)\n6. If action results in looping, go to Step 2\n\n### Step 3a: Track State for New-CIPE Detection\n\nAfter actions that should trigger a new CIPE, record state before looping:\n\n| Action                        | What to Track                                 | Subagent Mode |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| Fix auto-applying             | `last_cipe_url = current cipeUrl`             | Wait mode     |\n| Apply via MCP                 | `last_cipe_url = current cipeUrl`             | Wait mode     |\n| Apply locally + push          | `expected_commit_sha = $(git rev-parse HEAD)` | Wait mode     |\n| Reject + fix + push           | `expected_commit_sha = $(git rev-parse HEAD)` | Wait mode     |\n| Fix failed + local fix + push | `expected_commit_sha = $(git rev-parse HEAD)` | Wait mode     |\n| No fix + local fix + push     | `expected_commit_sha = $(git rev-parse HEAD)` | Wait mode     |\n| Environment rerun             | `last_cipe_url = current cipeUrl`             | Wait mode     |\n| No-new-CIPE + auto-fix + push | `expected_commit_sha = $(git rev-parse HEAD)` | Wait mode     |\n\n**CRITICAL**: When passing `expectedCommitSha` or `last_cipe_url` to the subagent, it enters **wait mode**:\n\n- Subagent will **completely ignore** the old/stale CIPE\n- Subagent will only wait for new CIPE to appear\n- Subagent will NOT return to main agent with stale CIPE data\n- Once new CIPE detected, subagent switches to normal polling\n\n**Why wait mode matters for context preservation**: Stale CIPE data can be very large (task output summaries, suggested fix patches, reasoning). If subagent returns this to main agent, it pollutes main agent''s context with useless data since we already processed that CIPE. Wait mode keeps stale data in the subagent, never sending it to main agent.\n\n### Step 4: Progress Tracking\n\nAfter each action:\n\n- If state changed significantly → reset `no_progress_count = 0`\n- If state unchanged → `no_progress_count++`\n- On new CI attempt detected → reset `local_verify_count = 0`\n\n## Status Reporting\n\nBased on verbosity level:\n\n| Level     | What to Report                                                             |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `minimal` | Only final result (success/failure/timeout)                                |\n| `medium`  | State changes + periodic updates (\"Cycle N \\| Elapsed: Xm \\| Status: ...\") |\n| `verbose` | All of medium + full subagent responses, git outputs, MCP responses        |\n\n## User Instruction Examples\n\nUsers can override default behaviors:\n\n| Instruction                                      | Effect                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| \"never auto-apply\"                               | Always prompt before applying any fix         |\n| \"always ask before git push\"                     | Prompt before each push                       |\n| \"reject any fix for e2e tasks\"                   | Auto-reject if `failedTaskIds` contains e2e   |\n| \"apply all fixes regardless of verification\"     | Skip verification check, apply everything     |\n| \"if confidence < 70, reject\"                     | Check confidence field before applying        |\n| \"run ''nx affected -t typecheck'' before applying\" | Add local verification step                   |\n| \"auto-fix workflow failures\"                     | Attempt lockfile updates on pre-CIPE failures |\n| \"wait 45 min for new CIPE\"                       | Override new-CIPE timeout (default: 10 min)   |\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Error                    | Action                                                                                |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Git rebase conflict      | Report to user, exit                                                                  |\n| `nx apply-locally` fails | Report to user, attempt manual patch or exit                                          |\n| MCP tool error           | Retry once, if fails report to user                                                   |\n| Subagent spawn failure   | Retry once, if fails exit with error                                                  |\n| No new CIPE detected     | If `--auto-fix-workflow`, try lockfile update; otherwise report to user with guidance |\n| Lockfile auto-fix fails  | Report to user, exit with guidance to check CI logs                                   |\n\n## Example Session\n\n### Example 1: Normal Flow with Self-Healing (medium verbosity)\n\n```\n[ci-monitor] Starting CI monitor for branch ''feature/add-auth''\n[ci-monitor] Config: max-cycles=5, timeout=120m, verbosity=medium\n\n[ci-monitor] Spawning subagent to poll CI status...\n[CI Monitor] CI attempt: IN_PROGRESS | Self-Healing: NOT_STARTED | Elapsed: 1m\n[CI Monitor] CI attempt: FAILED | Self-Healing: IN_PROGRESS | Elapsed: 3m\n[CI Monitor] CI attempt: FAILED | Self-Healing: COMPLETED | Elapsed: 5m\n\n[ci-monitor] Fix available! Verification: COMPLETED\n[ci-monitor] Applying fix via MCP...\n[ci-monitor] Fix applied in CI. Waiting for new CI attempt...\n\n[ci-monitor] Spawning subagent to poll CI status...\n[CI Monitor] New CI attempt detected!\n[CI Monitor] CI attempt: SUCCEEDED | Elapsed: 8m\n\n[ci-monitor] CI passed successfully!\n\n[ci-monitor] Summary:\n  - Total cycles: 2\n  - Total time: 12m 34s\n  - Fixes applied: 1\n  - Result: SUCCESS\n```\n\n### Example 2: Pre-CI Failure (medium verbosity)\n\n```\n[ci-monitor] Starting CI monitor for branch ''feature/add-products''\n[ci-monitor] Config: max-cycles=5, timeout=120m, auto-fix-workflow=true\n\n[ci-monitor] Spawning subagent to poll CI status...\n[CI Monitor] CI attempt: FAILED | Self-Healing: COMPLETED | Elapsed: 2m\n\n[ci-monitor] Applying fix locally, enhancing, and pushing...\n[ci-monitor] Committed: abc1234\n\n[ci-monitor] Spawning subagent to poll CI status...\n[CI Monitor] Waiting for new CI attempt... (expected SHA: abc1234)\n[CI Monitor] ⚠️  CI attempt timeout (10 min). Returning no_new_cipe.\n\n[ci-monitor] Status: no_new_cipe\n[ci-monitor] --auto-fix-workflow enabled. Attempting lockfile update...\n[ci-monitor] Lockfile updated. Committed: def5678\n\n[ci-monitor] Spawning subagent to poll CI status...\n[CI Monitor] New CI attempt detected!\n[CI Monitor] CI attempt: SUCCEEDED | Elapsed: 18m\n\n[ci-monitor] CI passed successfully!\n\n[ci-monitor] Summary:\n  - Total cycles: 3\n  - Total time: 22m 15s\n  - Fixes applied: 1 (self-healing) + 1 (lockfile)\n  - Result: SUCCESS\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:24:20.779Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for DevOps Agents requiring automated CI pipeline monitoring and self-healing capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要自动化CI管道监控和自我修复能力的DevOps代理。","ja":"DevOpsエージェントが自動CIパイプライン監視とセルフヒーリング機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"자동화된 CI 파이프라인 모니터링 및 자가 수리 기능을 필요로 하는 DevOps 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de DevOps que requieren un monitoreo automatizado de la canalización de CI y capacidades de autoreparación.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps nécessitant un suivi automatique de la canalisation de CI et des capacités d''auto-réparation.","de":"Ideal für DevOps-Agents, die ein automatisiertes Monitoring der CI-Pipeline und Selbstheilungsfähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes DevOps que exigem monitoramento automatizado de pipeline de CI e capacidades de autocura.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, требующих автоматизированного мониторинга конвейера CI и возможностей самоисцеления.","ar":"مثالي لعميل DevOps الذي يتطلب مراقبة تلقائية لخط أنابيب CI وقدرات الشفاء الذاتي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to monitor Nx Cloud CI pipeline executions, poll CI status, and perform automated fixes using the `ci-watcher` subagent, leveraging Git commands like `git branch` and `git rev-parse` for efficient pipeline management.","zh":"赋予代理监控Nx Cloud CI管道执行、轮询CI状态，并使用`ci-watcher`子代理执行自动化修复，利用Git命令如`git branch`和`git rev-parse`进行高效的管道管理。","ja":"エージェントにNx Cloud CIパイプラインの実行を監視し、CIステータスをポーリングし、`ci-watcher`サブエージェントを使用して自動修復を実行する能力を与え、Gitコマンド such as `git branch`と`git rev-parse`を使用してパイプラインを効率的に管理します。","ko":"에이전트가 Nx Cloud CI 파이프라인 실행을 모니터링하고 CI 상태를 폴링하며 `ci-watcher` 서브 에이전트를 사용하여 자동화된 수정을 수행할 수 있도록 하며 Git 명령어인 `git branch` 및 `git rev-parse`를 사용하여 파이프라인을 효율적으로 관리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a monitorear las ejecuciones de la canalización de CI de Nx Cloud, sondear el estado de CI y realizar arreglos automatizados utilizando el subagente `ci-watcher`, aprovechando comandos de Git como `git branch` y `git rev-parse` para una gestión de canalización eficiente.","fr":"Permet aux agents de surveiller les exécutions de la canalisation de CI de Nx Cloud, d''interroger l''état de CI et d''effectuer des corrections automatiques en utilisant le sous-agent `ci-watcher`, en exploitant des commandes Git comme `git branch` et `git rev-parse` pour une gestion de canalisation efficace.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, die Ausführungen der CI-Pipeline von Nx Cloud zu überwachen, den CI-Status abzufragen und automatisierte Korrekturen mithilfe des Subagents `ci-watcher` durchzuführen, indem Git-Befehle wie `git branch` und `git rev-parse` für eine effiziente Pipelinesteuerung genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a monitorar execuções de pipeline de CI do Nx Cloud, consultar o status do CI e realizar correções automatizadas usando o subagente `ci-watcher`, aproveitando comandos Git como `git branch` e `git rev-parse` para gerenciamento de pipeline eficiente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью мониторить выполнение конвейера CI Nx Cloud, опрашивать статус CI и выполнять автоматические исправления с помощью субагента `ci-watcher`, используя команды Git, такие как `git branch` и `git rev-parse`, для эффективного управления конвейером.","ar":"تمكين العميل من مراقبة تنفيذ خط أنابيب CI من Nx Cloud ، وطرح حالة CI ، وإجراء تصحيحات تلقائية باستخدام وكلاء فرعيين `ci-watcher` ، واستخدام أوامر Git مثل `git branch` و `git rev-parse` لإدارة خطوط أنابيب فعالة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating CI pipeline monitoring","Performing self-healing fixes for failed PRs","Optimizing build processes with Nx"],"zh":["自动化CI管道监控","为失败的PR执行自我修复修复","使用Nx优化构建过程"],"ja":["CIパイプライン監視の自動化","失敗したPRのセルフヒーリング修復の実行","Nxを使用したビルドプロセスの最適化"],"ko":["CI 파이프라인 모니터링 자동화","실패한 PR에 대한 자가 수리 수정 수행","Nx를 사용한 빌드 프로세스 최적화"],"es":["Automatización del monitoreo de la canalización de CI","Realización de arreglos de autoreparación para PR fallidas","Optimización de los procesos de compilación con Nx"],"fr":["Automatisation du suivi de la canalisation de CI","Réalisation de corrections d''auto-réparation pour les PR échouées","Optimisation des processus de construction avec Nx"],"de":["Automatisierung des Monitorings der CI-Pipeline","Durchführung von Selbstheilungsmaßnahmen für fehlgeschlagene PRs","Optimierung der Buildprozesse mit Nx"],"pt":["Automatizar monitoramento de pipeline de CI","Realizar correções de autocura para PRs com falha","Otimizar processos de compilação com Nx"],"ru":["Автоматизировать мониторинг конвейера CI","Выполнять исправления самоисцеления для PR с неудачей","Оптимизировать процессы сборки с помощью Nx"],"ar":["تأتمة مراقبة خط أنابيب CI","إجراء إصلاحات ذاتية للطلبات المرفوضة","تحسين عمليات البناء مع Nx"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Nx Cloud setup","Git repository access needed","Limited to CI pipeline executions"],"zh":["需要Nx Cloud设置","需要Git仓库访问","仅限CI管道执行"],"ja":["Nx Cloudの設定が必要","Gitリポジトリへのアクセスが必要","CIパイプラインの実行のみに限定"],"ko":["Nx Cloud 설정이 필요","Git 저장소 액세스가 필요","CI 파이프라인 실행만 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de Nx Cloud","Se necesita acceso al repositorio de Git","Limitado a las ejecuciones de la canalización de CI"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de Nx Cloud","L''accès au référentiel Git est nécessaire","Limité aux exécutions de la canalisation de CI"],"de":["Benötigt Nx Cloud-Konfiguration","Zugriff auf das Git-Repository erforderlich","Begrenzt auf CI-Pipeline-Ausführungen"],"pt":["Exige configuração do Nx Cloud","Acesso ao repositório Git necessário","Limitado a execuções de pipeline de CI"],"ru":["Требует настройки Nx Cloud","Необходим доступ к репозиторию Git","Ограничен выполнением конвейера CI"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد Nx Cloud","مطلوب الوصول إلى مستودع Git","محدود بتنفيذ خط أنابيب CI"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('angular/angular/reference-core', 'community', 'angular', 'angular', 'angular/angular', 'reference-core', 0, 0, 20, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z', '2026-02-18T14:24:18.726Z', NULL, '{"id":"angular/angular/reference-core","name":"reference-core","description":{"zh":"Angular Core 是 Angular 框架的核心，负责渲染、依赖注入和变化检测等关键功能。","ja":"Angular Core は Angular フレームワークの核心であり、レンダリング、依存性注入、変更検知などの重要な機能を担当します。","ko":"Angular Core는 Angular 프레임워크의 핵심으로 렌더링, 의존성 주입, 변경 감지 등의 주요 기능을 담당합니다.","es":"Angular Core es el núcleo del framework Angular, responsable de la renderización, inyección de dependencias y detección de cambios","fr":"Angular Core est le cœur du framework Angular, responsable de la renderisation, de l''injection de dépendances et de la détection de changements","de":"Angular Core ist das Herzstück des Angular-Frameworks, verantwortlich für die Renderierung, Abhängigkeitsinjektion und Änderungserkennung","pt":"O Angular Core é o coração do framework Angular, responsável por renderização, injeção de dependência e detecção de alterações","ru":"Angular Core является сердцем фреймворка Angular, отвечает за рендеринг, внедрение зависимостей и обнаружение изменений","ar":"نواة أنجULAR هي قلب الإطار أنجULAR، مسؤولة عن العرض وتحقيق الإعتماد والكشف عن التغييرات","en":"Deliver web apps with confidence 🚀"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Angular Core 引擎","ja":"Angular Core エンジン","ko":"Angular Core 엔진","es":"Angular Core: Arquitectura y modelo mental","fr":"Angular Core : Architecture et modèle mental","de":"Angular Core: Architektur und mentales Modell","pt":"Angular Core: Entregue Aplicativos Web com Confiança","ru":"Angular Core: Разработка веб-приложений с уверенностью","ar":"نواة أنجULAR: تسليم تطبيقات الويب بثقة","en":"reference-core"},"description":{"zh":"Angular Core 是 Angular 框架的核心，负责渲染、依赖注入和变化检测等关键功能。","ja":"Angular Core は Angular フレームワークの核心であり、レンダリング、依存性注入、変更検知などの重要な機能を担当します。","ko":"Angular Core는 Angular 프레임워크의 핵심으로 렌더링, 의존성 주입, 변경 감지 등의 주요 기능을 담당합니다.","es":"Angular Core es el núcleo del framework Angular, responsable de la renderización, inyección de dependencias y detección de cambios","fr":"Angular Core est le cœur du framework Angular, responsable de la renderisation, de l''injection de dépendances et de la détection de changements","de":"Angular Core ist das Herzstück des Angular-Frameworks, verantwortlich für die Renderierung, Abhängigkeitsinjektion und Änderungserkennung","pt":"O Angular Core é o coração do framework Angular, responsável por renderização, injeção de dependência e detecção de alterações","ru":"Angular Core является сердцем фреймворка Angular, отвечает за рендеринг, внедрение зависимостей и обнаружение изменений","ar":"نواة أنجULAR هي قلب الإطار أنجULAR، مسؤولة عن العرض وتحقيق الإعتماد والكشف عن التغييرات","en":"Deliver web apps with confidence 🚀"},"definition":{"en":"Deliver web apps with confidence 🚀"},"features":{"zh":["渲染（Ivy/Render3）","依赖注入（DI）","变化检测","高性能的 Web 应用"],"ja":["レンダリング（Ivy/Render3）","依存性注入（DI）","変更検知","高性能の Web アプリケーション"],"ko":["렌더링（Ivy/Render3）","의존성 주입（DI）","변경 감지","고성능의 Web 애플리케이션"],"es":["Renderización (Ivy/Render3)","Inyección de dependencias (DI)","Detección de cambios","Arquitectura de alto nivel","Lógica de ejecución"],"fr":["Renderisation (Ivy/Render3)","Injection de dépendances (DI)","Détection de changements","Architecture de haut niveau","Logique d''exécution"],"de":["Renderierung (Ivy/Render3)","Abhängigkeitsinjektion (DI)","Änderungserkennung","Architektur von höherer Ebene","Laufzeitlogik"],"pt":["Renderização (Ivy/Render3)","Injeção de Dependência (DI)","Detecção de Alterações","Arquitetura de Alto Nível"],"ru":["Рендеринг (Ivy/Render3)","Внедрение Зависимостей (DI)","Обнаружение Изменений","Высокоуровневая Архитектура"],"ar":["العرض (Ivy/Render3)","تحقيق الإعتماد (DI)","كشف التغييرات","هندسة مستوى عال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Angular Core","渲染","依赖注入","变化检测","Web 应用","高性能"],"ja":["Angular Core","レンダリング","依存性注入","変更検知","Web アプリケーション","高性能"],"ko":["Angular Core","렌더링","의존성 주입","변경 감지","Web 애플리케이션","고성능"],"es":["Angular Core","arquitectura Angular","modelo mental Angular","renderización Ivy","inyección de dependencias","detección de cambios"],"fr":["Angular Core","architecture Angular","modèle mental Angular","renderisation Ivy","injection de dépendances","détection de changements"],"de":["Angular Core","Angular-Architektur","mentales Modell Angular","Renderierung Ivy","Abhängigkeitsinjektion","Änderungserkennung"],"pt":["Angular Core","Renderização Ivy","Injeção de Dependência","Detecção de Alterações","Desenvolvimento Web","Frameworks JavaScript"],"ru":["Angular Core","Рендеринг Ivy","Внедрение Зависимостей","Обнаружение Изменений","Разработка Веб-приложений","Фреймворки JavaScript"],"ar":["نواة أنجULAR","عرض Ivy","تحقيق الإعتماد","كشف التغييرات","تطوير الويب","إطارات العمل JavaScript"]}},"owner":"angular","repo":"angular","repoPath":"angular/angular","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.528Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"reference-core","description":"Explains the mental model and architecture of the code under `packages/core`. You MUST use this skill any time you plan to work with code in `packages/core`","bodyPreview":"# Angular Core (`packages/core`) Mental Model\n\nThis document outlines the architecture and mental model for `packages/core`, the heart of the Angular framework.\n\n## 1. High-Level Architecture\n\n`packages/core` contains the runtime logic for Angular. Its primary responsibilities are:\n\n1.  **Rendering (Ivy/Render3)**: Transforming templates into DOM updates.\n2.  **Dependency Injection (DI)**: Managing object creation and lifetime.\n3.  **Change Detection**: Synchronizing the model with the view.\n4.","body":"# Angular Core (`packages/core`) Mental Model\n\nThis document outlines the architecture and mental model for `packages/core`, the heart of the Angular framework.\n\n## 1. High-Level Architecture\n\n`packages/core` contains the runtime logic for Angular. Its primary responsibilities are:\n\n1.  **Rendering (Ivy/Render3)**: Transforming templates into DOM updates.\n2.  **Dependency Injection (DI)**: Managing object creation and lifetime.\n3.  **Change Detection**: Synchronizing the model with the view.\n4.  **Reactivity**: Signals and Zone.js integration.\n\n## 2. Rendering Engine (Ivy / Render3)\n\nThe rendering engine (located in `packages/core/src/render3`) uses an **instruction-based** approach.\n\n### Key Concepts\n\n- **Instructions**: The Angular compiler transforms templates into a sequence of instruction calls (e.g., `ɵɵelementStart`, `ɵɵtext`, `ɵɵproperty`). These instructions are executed at runtime to create and update the view.\n  - _Location_: `packages/core/src/render3/instructions`\n\n- **LView (Logical View)**: An array containing the _state_ of a specific view instance. It holds:\n  - DOM nodes (`RElement`, `RText`).\n  - Binding values (for change detection).\n  - Directive/Component instances.\n  - _Context_: `packages/core/src/render3/interfaces/view.ts`\n\n- **TView (Template View)**: An array containing the _static structure_ of a view. It is shared across all instances (`LView`s) of the same component/template. It holds:\n  - Property names for bindings.\n  - Node relationship information.\n  - Compiled directive definitions.\n  - _Context_: `packages/core/src/render3/interfaces/view.ts`\n\n- **Memory Layout**: `LView` and `TView` are parallel arrays. Index `i` in `LView` corresponds to metadata at index `i` in `TView`.\n  - `HEADER`: Fixed size, contains context (Parent, Host, etc.).\n  - `DECLS`: Static nodes (elements, text, pipes).\n  - `VARS`: Binding values.\n  - `EXPANDO`: Dynamic data (host bindings, injectors).\n\n### The Render Cycle\n\n1.  **Creation Mode**: Instructions create DOM nodes and store them in `LView`.\n2.  **Update Mode**: Instructions check current values against previous values stored in `LView`. If changed, they update the DOM.\n\n## 3. Dependency Injection (DI)\n\nDI in Angular is hierarchical and split into two systems that interact:\n\n### Module Injector (`R3Injector`)\n\n- Configured via `@NgModule.providers` or `providedIn: ''root''`.\n- Stored in a hierarchy of `R3Injector` instances.\n- _Location_: `packages/core/src/di/r3_injector.ts`\n\n### Node Injector\n\n- Configured via `@Component.providers` or `@Directive.providers`.\n- **Not a class**, but a data structure embedded in the `LView` (\"Expando\" section).\n- Uses **Bloom Filters** (`TView.data`) to quickly check if a token is present at a specific node index before traversing up the tree.\n- Resolves tokens starting from the current node, walking up the view tree (Element Injector hierarchy), and falling back to the Module Injector if not found.\n\n## 4. Change Detection\n\n- **Dirty Checking**: Angular checks if values bound in templates have changed.\n- **Strategies**:\n  - `Default`: Checks everything.\n  - `OnPush`: Checks only if inputs change, events fire, or signals update.\n- **Signals**: The new reactivity primitive. Signals notify the scheduler when they change, potentially allowing for fine-grained updates (Zoneless).\n\n## 5. Key Directories to Know\n\n- `src/render3`: The Ivy rendering engine.\n  - `instructions`: The runtime instructions called by compiled code.\n  - `interfaces`: `LView`, `TView`, `TNode` definitions.\n- `src/di`: Dependency injection system.\n- `src/change_detection`: Change detection logic.\n- `src/zone`: Zone.js integration.\n- `src/signal`: Signals implementation (if present in this version, otherwise likely in `primitives`).\n\n## 6. Conventions & Gotchas\n\n- **Prefixes**: Private/Internal exports often start with `ɵ`.\n- **Global State**: Ivy relies heavily on global state (e.g., `getLView()`) during instruction execution to avoid passing context arguments everywhere. This is for performance and code size.\n- **Performance**: The code is highly optimized for performance and memory. You will see arrays used instead of objects, bitmasks, and manual memory management patterns. **Respect these patterns.**\n\n## 7. How to Modify Core\n\n1.  **Understand the Instruction**: If modifying runtime behavior, find the corresponding instruction in `src/render3/instructions`.\n2.  **Check `LView`/`TView` Impact**: If adding state, understand where it fits in the `LView` array.\n3.  **Tests**: Core has extensive tests. Run them using Bazel.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:24:18.726Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents specializing in Angular framework development, seeking to master Ivy/Render3 rendering, Dependency Injection, and Change Detection.","zh":"适合专注于 Angular 框架开发的前端代理，旨在掌握 Ivy/Render3 渲染、依赖注入和变更检测。","ja":"Angular フレームワーク開発に特化したフロントエンド エージェントが Ivy/Render3 レンダリング、依存性注入、変更検知をマスターするのに適しています。","ko":"Angular 프레임워크 개발에 특화된 프론트엔드 에이전트가 Ivy/Render3 렌더링, 의존성 주입, 변경 감지를 마스터하는 데 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de frontend que se especializan en el desarrollo de la framework Angular, que buscan dominar el renderizado Ivy/Render3, la inyección de dependencias y la detección de cambios.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents frontend spécialisés dans le développement de la framework Angular, qui cherchent à maîtriser le rendu Ivy/Render3, l''injection de dépendances et la détection de changements.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agenten, die sich auf die Entwicklung der Angular-Framework spezialisieren und Ivy/Render3-Rendering, Dependency Injection und Change Detection meistern möchten.","pt":"Ideal for Frontend Agents specializing in Angular framework development, seeking to master Ivy/Render3 rendering, Dependency Injection, and Change Detection.","ru":"Ideal for Frontend Agents specializing in Angular framework development, seeking to master Ivy/Render3 rendering, Dependency Injection, and Change Detection.","ar":"Ideal for Frontend Agents specializing in Angular framework development, seeking to master Ivy/Render3 rendering, Dependency Injection, and Change Detection."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to deliver web apps with confidence by understanding the Angular Core mental model, leveraging Dependency Injection for object creation and lifetime management, and utilizing Change Detection for model-view synchronization, all within the Ivy/Render3 rendering framework.","zh":"使代理能够通过了解 Angular Core 心理模型、利用依赖注入进行对象创建和生命周期管理以及利用变更检测进行模型-视图同步，所有这些都在 Ivy/Render3 渲染框架内，以信心交付 Web 应用程序。","ja":"エージェントが Angular Core の心的モデルを理解し、依存性注入を使用してオブジェクトの作成とライフサイクル管理を行い、さらに変更検知を使用してモデルとビューの同期を行うことで、Ivy/Render3 レンダリング フレームワーク内で Web アプリケーションを自信を持って提供できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 Angular Core的心理 모델을 이해하고, 의존성 주입을 사용하여 객체 생성 및 수명 주기 관리를 수행하며, 변경 감지를 사용하여 모델-뷰 동기화를 수행함으로써, Ivy/Render3 렌더링 프레임워크 내에서 웹 애플리케이션을 자신감 있게 제공할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a entregar aplicaciones web con confianza al entender el modelo mental de Angular Core, aprovechar la inyección de dependencias para la creación y gestión del ciclo de vida de los objetos y utilizar la detección de cambios para la sincronización del modelo-vista, todo dentro de la framework de renderizado Ivy/Render3.","fr":"Permet aux agents de livrer des applications web avec confiance en comprenant le modèle mental d''Angular Core, en exploitant l''injection de dépendances pour la création et la gestion du cycle de vie des objets et en utilisant la détection de changements pour la synchronisation du modèle-vue, le tout dans la framework de rendu Ivy/Render3.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Webanwendungen mit Vertrauen zu liefern, indem sie das Angular-Core-Mentalmodell verstehen, die Dependency Injection für die Objekterstellung und Lebenszeitverwaltung nutzen und die Change Detection für die Modell-View-Synchronisierung verwenden, all dies innerhalb der Ivy/Render3-Renderframework.","pt":"Empowers agents to deliver web apps with confidence by understanding the Angular Core mental model, leveraging Dependency Injection for object creation and lifetime management, and utilizing Change Detection for model-view synchronization, all within the Ivy/Render3 rendering framework.","ru":"Empowers agents to deliver web apps with confidence by understanding the Angular Core mental model, leveraging Dependency Injection for object creation and lifetime management, and utilizing Change Detection for model-view synchronization, all within the Ivy/Render3 rendering framework.","ar":"Empowers agents to deliver web apps with confidence by understanding the Angular Core mental model, leveraging Dependency Injection for object creation and lifetime management, and utilizing Change Detection for model-view synchronization, all within the Ivy/Render3 rendering framework."},"useCases":{"en":["Architecting high-performance Angular applications with Ivy/Render3","Implementing efficient Dependency Injection for complex web apps","Optimizing Change Detection for seamless model-view updates"],"zh":["使用 Ivy/Render3 架构高性能 Angular 应用程序","为复杂 Web 应用程序实现高效的依赖注入","优化变更检测以实现无缝的模型-视图更新"],"ja":["Ivy/Render3 アーキテクチャを使用した高パフォーマンス Angular アプリケーション","複雑な Web アプリケーション向けの効率的な依存性注入の実装","モデルとビューの同期のための変更検知の最適化"],"ko":["Ivy/Render3 아키텍처를 사용한 고성능 Angular 애플리케이션 구축","복잡한 웹 애플리케이션을 위한 효율적인 의존성 주입 구현","모델-뷰 동기화를 위한 변경 감지 최적화"],"es":["Diseñar aplicaciones Angular de alto rendimiento con Ivy/Render3","Implementar una inyección de dependencias eficiente para aplicaciones web complejas","Optimizar la detección de cambios para actualizaciones de modelo-vista sin problemas"],"fr":["Concevoir des applications Angular à haute performance avec Ivy/Render3","Mettre en œuvre une injection de dépendances efficace pour des applications web complexes","Optimiser la détection de changements pour des mises à jour de modèle-vue sans problème"],"de":["Entwerfen von Hochleistungs-Angular-Anwendungen mit Ivy/Render3","Implementieren einer effizienten Dependency Injection für komplexe Webanwendungen","Optimieren der Change Detection für nahtlose Modell-View-Updates"],"pt":["Architecting high-performance Angular applications with Ivy/Render3","Implementing efficient Dependency Injection for complex web apps","Optimizing Change Detection for seamless model-view updates"],"ru":["Architecting high-performance Angular applications with Ivy/Render3","Implementing efficient Dependency Injection for complex web apps","Optimizing Change Detection for seamless model-view updates"],"ar":["Architecting high-performance Angular applications with Ivy/Render3","Implementing efficient Dependency Injection for complex web apps","Optimizing Change Detection for seamless model-view updates"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires in-depth knowledge of Angular framework","Specific to Angular Core (packages/core) architecture"],"zh":["需要深入了解 Angular 框架","仅限于 Angular Core（packages/core）架构"],"ja":["Angular フレームワークの深い理解が必要","Angular Core（packages/core）アーキテクチャに限定"],"ko":["Angular 프레임워크에 대한 깊은 이해가 필요함","Angular Core（packages/core）아키텍처에 한정"],"es":["Requiere un conocimiento en profundidad de la framework Angular","Específico de la arquitectura Angular Core (paquetes/core)"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance approfondie de la framework Angular","Spécifique à l''architecture Angular Core (packages/core)"],"de":["Benötigt ein tiefes Verständnis der Angular-Framework","Spezifisch für die Angular-Core-Architektur (packages/core)"],"pt":["Requires in-depth knowledge of Angular framework","Specific to Angular Core (packages/core) architecture"],"ru":["Requires in-depth knowledge of Angular framework","Specific to Angular Core (packages/core) architecture"],"ar":["Requires in-depth knowledge of Angular framework","Specific to Angular Core (packages/core) architecture"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":20}');
