"docs-writer 는 개발자가 정확하고 명확하고 일관된 기술 문서를 작성할 수 있는 오픈소스 AI 에이전트입니다","es":"El agente de IA docs-writer es una herramienta de código abierto que genera documentación técnica precisa y clara","fr":"L''agent IA docs-writer est un outil open-source qui génère une documentation technique précise et claire","de":"Der KI-Agent docs-writer ist ein Open-Source-Tool, das präzise und klare technische Dokumentationen generiert","pt":"O docs-writer é uma ferramenta de documentação AI que ajuda a criar documentação precisa e clara para projetos de código aberto","ru":"docs-writer - это инструмент документации ИИ, помогающий создавать точную и ясную документацию для открытых проектов","ar":"أداة توثيق إيه آي تساعد في إنشاء توثيق دقيق وواضح لمشاريع الكود المفتوح","en":"An open-source AI agent that brings the power of Gemini directly into your terminal."},"definition":{"en":"An open-source AI agent that brings the power of Gemini directly into your terminal."},"features":{"zh":["准确的文档生成","清晰的一致性文档","支持 Gemini CLI 项目","遵循 CONTRIBUTING.md 贡献流程","严格遵循项目标准"],"ja":["正確な文書生成","明確な一貫性のある文書","Gemini CLI プロジェクトをサポート","CONTRIBUTING.md 貢献プロセスに従う","プロジェクト標準を厳格に遵守"],"ko":["정확한 문서 생성","명확한 일관성 있는 문서","Gemini CLI 프로젝트 지원","CONTRIBUTING.md 기여 프로세스 준수","프로젝트 표준 엄격 준수"],"es":["Generación de documentación técnica precisa","Compatibilidad con Gemini CLI","Estándares de documentación estrictos","Proceso de contribución claro","Edición y revisión de documentación"],"fr":["Génération de documentation technique précise","Compatibilité avec Gemini CLI","Normes de documentation strictes","Processus de contribution clair","Édition et révision de documentation"],"de":["Erstellung präziser technischer Dokumentationen","Kompatibilität mit Gemini CLI","Strenge Dokumentationsstandards","Klarer Beitragungsprozess","Bearbeitung und Überprüfung von Dokumentationen"],"pt":["Criação de documentação precisa e clara","Integração com o terminal","Compatibilidade com projetos de código aberto","Suporte à documentação em múltiplos formatos","Fácil de usar e configurar"],"ru":["Создание точной и ясной документации","Интеграция с терминалом","Совместимость с открытыми проектами","Поддержка документации в нескольких форматах","Легко использовать и настраивать"],"ar":["إنشاء توثيق دقيق وواضح","التكامل مع محطة التحكم","التوافق مع مشاريع الكود المفتوح","دعم التوثيق في صيغ متعددة","سهل الاستخدام والتهيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["docs-writer","AI 代理","技术文档","Gemini CLI","CONTRIBUTING.md","项目标准","开发者工具","技术写作"],"ja":["docs-writer","AI エージェント","技術文書","Gemini CLI","CONTRIBUTING.md","プロジェクト標準","開発者ツール","技術ライティング"],"ko":["docs-writer","AI 에이전트","기술 문서","Gemini CLI","CONTRIBUTING.md","프로젝트 표준","개발자 도구","기술 작성"],"es":["documentación técnica","agente de IA","Gemini CLI","estándares de documentación","proceso de contribución","edición de documentación","revisión de documentación"],"fr":["documentation technique","agent IA","Gemini CLI","normes de documentation","processus de contribution","édition de documentation","révision de documentation"],"de":["technische Dokumentation","KI-Agent","Gemini CLI","Dokumentationsstandards","Beitragungsprozess","Dokumentation bearbeiten","Dokumentation überprüfen"],"pt":["documentação AI","ferramenta de documentação","código aberto","terminal","documentação clara","documentação precisa","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["документация ИИ","инструмент документации","открытый проект","терминал","ясная документация","точная документация","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["توثيق إيه آي","أداة توثيق","كود مفتوح","محطة التحكم","توثيق واضح","توثيق دقيق","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"google-gemini","repo":"gemini-cli","repoPath":"google-gemini/gemini-cli","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.529Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"docs-writer","description":"","bodyPreview":"# `docs-writer` skill instructions\n\nAs an expert technical writer and editor for the Gemini CLI project, you produce\naccurate, clear, and consistent documentation. When asked to write, edit, or\nreview documentation, you must ensure the content strictly adheres to the\nprovided documentation standards and accurately reflects the current codebase.\nAdhere to the contribution process in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the following\nproject standards.\n\n## Phase 1: Documentation standards\n\nAdhering to these prin","body":"# `docs-writer` skill instructions\n\nAs an expert technical writer and editor for the Gemini CLI project, you produce\naccurate, clear, and consistent documentation. When asked to write, edit, or\nreview documentation, you must ensure the content strictly adheres to the\nprovided documentation standards and accurately reflects the current codebase.\nAdhere to the contribution process in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the following\nproject standards.\n\n## Phase 1: Documentation standards\n\nAdhering to these principles and standards when writing, editing, and reviewing.\n\n### Voice and tone\nAdopt a tone that balances professionalism with a helpful, conversational\napproach.\n\n- **Perspective and tense:** Address the reader as \"you.\" Use active voice and\n  present tense (e.g., \"The API returns...\").\n- **Tone:** Professional, friendly, and direct. \n- **Clarity:** Use simple vocabulary. Avoid jargon, slang, and marketing hype.\n- **Global Audience:** Write in standard US English. Avoid idioms and cultural\n  references.\n- **Requirements:** Be clear about requirements (\"must\") vs. recommendations\n  (\"we recommend\"). Avoid \"should.\"\n- **Word Choice:** Avoid \"please\" and anthropomorphism (e.g., \"the server\n  thinks\"). Use contractions (don''t, it''s).\n\n### Language and grammar\nWrite precisely to ensure your instructions are unambiguous.\n\n- **Abbreviations:** Avoid Latin abbreviations; use \"for example\" (not \"e.g.\")\n  and \"that is\" (not \"i.e.\").\n- **Punctuation:** Use the serial comma. Place periods and commas inside\n  quotation marks.\n- **Dates:** Use unambiguous formats (e.g., \"January 22, 2026\").\n- **Conciseness:** Use \"lets you\" instead of \"allows you to.\" Use precise,\n  specific verbs.\n- **Examples:** Use meaningful names in examples; avoid placeholders like\n  \"foo\" or \"bar.\"\n\n### Formatting and syntax\nApply consistent formatting to make documentation visually organized and\naccessible.\n\n- **Overview paragraphs:** Every heading must be followed by at least one\n  introductory overview paragraph before any lists or sub-headings.\n- **Text wrap:** Wrap text at 80 characters (except long links or tables).\n- **Casing:** Use sentence case for headings, titles, and bolded text.\n- **Naming:** Always refer to the project as `Gemini CLI` (never\n  `the Gemini CLI`).\n- **Lists:** Use numbered lists for sequential steps and bulleted lists\n  otherwise. Keep list items parallel in structure.\n- **UI and code:** Use **bold** for UI elements and `code font` for filenames,\n  snippets, commands, and API elements. Focus on the task when discussing\n  interaction.\n- **Links:** Use descriptive anchor text; avoid \"click here.\" Ensure the link\n  makes sense out of context.\n- **Accessibility:** Use semantic HTML elements correctly (headings, lists, \n  tables).\n- **Media:** Use lowercase hyphenated filenames. Provide descriptive alt text\n  for all images.\n\n### Structure\n- **BLUF:** Start with an introduction explaining what to expect.\n- **Experimental features:** If a feature is clearly noted as experimental,\nadd the following note immediately after the introductory paragraph:\n  `> **Note:** This is a preview feature currently under active development.`\n- **Headings:** Use hierarchical headings to support the user journey.\n- **Procedures:** \n  - Introduce lists of steps with a complete sentence.\n  - Start each step with an imperative verb.\n  - Number sequential steps; use bullets for non-sequential lists.\n  - Put conditions before instructions (e.g., \"On the Settings page, click...\").\n  - Provide clear context for where the action takes place.\n  - Indicate optional steps clearly (e.g., \"Optional: ...\").\n- **Elements:** Use bullet lists, tables, notes (`> **Note:**`), and warnings \n  (`> **Warning:**`).\n- **Avoid using a table of contents:** If a table of contents is present, remove\n  it.\n- **Next steps:** Conclude with a \"Next steps\" section if applicable.\n\n## Phase 2: Preparation\nBefore modifying any documentation, thoroughly investigate the request and the\nsurrounding context. \n\n1.  **Clarify:** Understand the core request. Differentiate between writing new\n    content and editing existing content. If the request is ambiguous (e.g.,\n    \"fix the docs\"), ask for clarification.\n2.  **Investigate:** Examine relevant code (primarily in `packages/`) for\n    accuracy.\n3.  **Audit:** Read the latest versions of relevant files in `docs/`.\n4.  **Connect:** Identify all referencing pages if changing behavior. Check if\n    `docs/sidebar.json` needs updates.\n5.  **Plan:** Create a step-by-step plan before making changes.\n\n## Phase 3: Execution\nImplement your plan by either updating existing files or creating new ones\nusing the appropriate file system tools. Use `replace` for small edits and\n`write_file` for new files or large rewrites.\n\n### Editing existing documentation\nFollow these additional steps when asked to review or update existing\ndocumentation.\n\n- **Gaps:** Identify areas where the documentation is incomplete or no longer\n  reflects existing code.\n- **Structure:** Apply \"Structure (New Docs)\" rules (BLUF, headings, etc.) when \n  adding new sections to existing pages.\n- **Tone:** Ensure the tone is active and engaging. Use \"you\" and contractions.\n- **Clarity:** Correct awkward wording, spelling, and grammar. Rephrase\n  sentences to make them easier for users to understand.\n- **Consistency:** Check for consistent terminology and style across all edited\n  documents.\n\n\n## Phase 4: Verification and finalization\nPerform a final quality check to ensure that all changes are correctly formatted\nand that all links are functional.\n\n1.  **Accuracy:** Ensure content accurately reflects the implementation and\n  technical behavior.\n2.  **Self-review:** Re-read changes for formatting, correctness, and flow.\n3.  **Link check:** Verify all new and existing links leading to or from modified\n    pages.\n4.  **Format:** Once all changes are complete, ask to execute `npm run format`\n    to ensure consistent formatting across the project. If the user confirms,\n    execute the command.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:26:26.907Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing precise documentation generation and editing capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要生成和编辑精确文档的技术写作代理","ja":"技術文書作成エージェントが正確なドキュメント生成および編集機能を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"정확한 문서 생성 및 편집 기능이 필요한 기술 문서 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de escritura técnica que necesitan una generación y edición de documentación precisa.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de rédaction technique ayant besoin d''une génération et de modification de documentation précise.","de":"Perfekt für technische Schreiber-Agenten, die eine präzise Dokumentenerstellung und -bearbeitung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Escrita Técnica que necessitam de capacidades de geração e edição de documentação precisas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов технической документации, требующих точных возможностей генерации и редактирования документации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الكتابة الفنية الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات دقيقة لإنشاء وتحرير الوثائق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to produce accurate, clear, and consistent documentation adhering to provided standards, such as those outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md, and utilizing project standards for Gemini CLI documentation.","zh":"赋予代理生成准确、清晰、遵守提供的标准（如CONTRIBUTING.md中概述的标准）的文档，并利用Gemini CLI文档的项目标准","ja":"エージェントが、CONTRIBUTING.mdに概説されているような提供された規格に従った、正確で明確で一貫性のあるドキュメントを生成できるようにし、Gemini CLIドキュメントのプロジェクト規格を利用する","ko":"에이전트가 제공된 표준을 준수하여 정확하고 명확하며 일관된 문서를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, CONTRIBUTING.md에 정의된 표준과 Gemini CLI 문서의 프로젝트 표준을 사용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a producir documentación precisa, clara y coherente que se ajusta a los estándares proporcionados, como los que se describen en CONTRIBUTING.md, y que utiliza los estándares del proyecto para la documentación de Gemini CLI.","fr":"Permet aux agents de produire une documentation précise, claire et cohérente qui respecte les normes fournies, comme celles décrites dans CONTRIBUTING.md, et qui utilise les normes du projet pour la documentation de Gemini CLI.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, präzise, klare und konsistente Dokumentation zu erstellen, die den bereitgestellten Standards entspricht, wie in CONTRIBUTING.md beschrieben, und die Projektstandards für die Gemini-CLI-Dokumentation verwendet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a produzir documentação precisa, clara e consistente, que atende aos padrões fornecidos, como os descritos em CONTRIBUTING.md, e que utilizam os padrões do projeto para documentação da Gemini CLI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью производить точную, ясную и последовательную документацию, соответствующую предоставленным стандартам, таким как те, которые описаны в CONTRIBUTING.md, и использующую стандарты проекта для документации Gemini CLI.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية إنتاج توثيق دقيق وواضح ومتناسق يمتثل للمعايير المقدمة، مثل تلك الموصوفة في CONTRIBUTING.md، ويتوافق مع معايير المشروع لوثائق Gemini CLI."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating high-quality technical documentation","Editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency","Reviewing documentation for adherence to project standards"],"zh":["生成高质量的技术文档","编辑现有文档以提高清晰度和一致性","审查文档以确保遵守项目标准"],"ja":["高品質の技術文書を生成する","既存の文書を編集して明確性と一貫性を高める","文書がプロジェクト規格に従っていることを確認する"],"ko":["고품질의 기술 문서를 생성","기존 문서를 편집하여 명확성과 일관성을 높임","문서가 프로젝트 표준을 준수하는지 확인"],"es":["Generación de documentación técnica de alta calidad","Edición de documentación existente para claridad y coherencia","Revisión de la documentación para la adhesión a los estándares del proyecto"],"fr":["Génération de documentation technique de haute qualité","Édition de la documentation existante pour la clarté et la cohérence","Révision de la documentation pour le respect des normes du projet"],"de":["Erstellung von technischer Dokumentation in hoher Qualität","Bearbeitung bestehender Dokumentation für Klarheit und Konsistenz","Überprüfung der Dokumentation auf Einhaltung der Projektstandards"],"pt":["Geração de documentação técnica de alta qualidade","Edição de documentação existente para clareza e consistência","Revisão da documentação para garantir a conformidade com os padrões do projeto"],"ru":["Генерация технической документации высокого качества","Редактирование существующей документации для ясности и последовательности","Проверка документации на соответствие стандартам проекта"],"ar":["إنشاء توثيق فني عالي الجودة","تحرير الوثائق الحالية لضمان الوضوح والاتساق","مراجعة الوثائق للتأكد من امتثالها لمعايير المشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to specific documentation standards","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md","Limited to Gemini CLI project context"],"zh":["需要遵守特定的文档标准","必须遵循CONTRIBUTING.md中概述的贡献流程","仅限于Gemini CLI项目的背景"],"ja":["特定の文書規格に従わなければならない","CONTRIBUTING.mdに概説されている貢献プロセスに従わなければならない","Gemini CLIプロジェクトのコンテキストに限定される"],"ko":["특정 문서 표준을 준수해야 함","CONTRIBUTING.md에 정의된 기여 프로세스를 따라야 함","Gemini CLI 프로젝트의 맥락에서만 제한"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión a estándares de documentación específicos","Debe seguir el proceso de contribución descrito en CONTRIBUTING.md","Limitado al contexto del proyecto Gemini CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite le respect de normes de documentation spécifiques","Doit suivre le processus de contribution décrit dans CONTRIBUTING.md","Limité au contexte du projet Gemini CLI"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung spezifischer Dokumentationsstandards","Muss dem in CONTRIBUTING.md beschriebenen Beitragungsprozess folgen","Begrenzt auf den Kontext des Gemini-CLI-Projekts"],"pt":["Exige a adesão a padrões de documentação específicos","Deve seguir o processo de contribuição descrito em CONTRIBUTING.md","Limitado ao contexto do projeto Gemini CLI"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения определенных стандартов документации","Должен следовать процессу внесения вклада, описанному в CONTRIBUTING.md","Ограничен контекстом проекта Gemini CLI"],"ar":["يتطلب امتثالًا لمعايير توثيق محددة","يجب اتباع عملية المساهمة الموصوفة في CONTRIBUTING.md","محدود سياق مشروع Gemini CLI"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('nrwl/nx/nx-generate', 'community', 'nrwl', 'nx', 'nrwl/nx', 'nx-generate', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.529Z', '2026-02-18T14:26:22.858Z', NULL, '{"id":"nrwl/nx/nx-generate","name":"nx-generate","description":{"zh":"Nx Generate是一个强大的工具，用于自动化代码生成、项目创建和优化，提高开发效率","ja":"Nx Generateは、コード生成、プロジェクト作成、最適化を自動化する強力なツールです","ko":"Nx Generate는 자동 코드 생성, 프로젝트 생성 및 최적화를 자동화하는 강력한 도구입니다","es":"nx-generate es una herramienta de automatización de monorepo que simplifica tareas repetitivas y asegura la consistencia del código","fr":"nx-generate est un outil d''automatisation de monorepo qui simplifie les tâches répétitives et assure la cohérence du code","de":"nx-generate ist ein Monorepo-Automatisierungstool, das repetitive Aufgaben vereinfacht und die Konsistenz des Codes sicherstellt","pt":"O Nx Generate é uma ferramenta poderosa que automatiza tarefas repetitivas e melhora a produtividade no desenvolvimento de software","ru":"Nx Generate - это мощный инструмент, который автоматизирует повторяющиеся задачи и повышает производительность разработки ПО","ar":"نكس جينيريت هو أداة قوية لتحسين الإنتاجية في تطوير البرمجيات من خلال تأتمة المهام المتكررة","en":"The Monorepo Platform that amplifies both developers and AI agents. Nx optimizes your builds, scales your CI, and fixes failed PRs automatically. Ship in half the time."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Nx Generate:自动代码生成和项目优化","ja":"Nx Generate:自動コード生成とプロジェクト最適化","ko":"Nx Generate: 자동 코드 생성 및 프로젝트 최적화","es":"nx-generate: Herramienta de automatización de monorepo","fr":"nx-generate : Outil d''automatisation de monorepo","de":"nx-generate: Monorepo-Automatisierungstool","pt":"Nx Generate: Ferramenta de Geração de Código","ru":"Nx Generate: Инструмент для генерации кода","ar":"نكس جينيريت: أداة توليد الكود","en":"nx-generate"},"description":{"zh":"Nx Generate是一个强大的工具，用于自动化代码生成、项目创建和优化，提高开发效率","ja":"Nx Generateは、コード生成、プロジェクト作成、最適化を自動化する強力なツールです","ko":"Nx Generate는 자동 코드 생성, 프로젝트 생성 및 최적화를 자동화하는 강력한 도구입니다","es":"nx-generate es una herramienta de automatización de monorepo que simplifica tareas repetitivas y asegura la consistencia del código","fr":"nx-generate est un outil d''automatisation de monorepo qui simplifie les tâches répétitives et assure la cohérence du code","de":"nx-generate ist ein Monorepo-Automatisierungstool, das repetitive Aufgaben vereinfacht und die Konsistenz des Codes sicherstellt","pt":"O Nx Generate é uma ferramenta poderosa que automatiza tarefas repetitivas e melhora a produtividade no desenvolvimento de software","ru":"Nx Generate - это мощный инструмент, который автоматизирует повторяющиеся задачи и повышает производительность разработки ПО","ar":"نكس جينيريت هو أداة قوية لتحسين الإنتاجية في تطوير البرمجيات من خلال تأتمة المهام المتكررة","en":"The Monorepo Platform that amplifies both developers and AI agents. Nx optimizes your builds, scales your CI, and fixes failed PRs automatically. Ship in hal..."},"definition":{"en":"The Monorepo Platform that amplifies both developers and AI agents. Nx optimizes your builds, scales your CI, and fixes failed PRs automatically. Ship in half the time."},"features":{"zh":["自动代码生成","项目创建","代码优化","自动化重复任务","确保代码一致性"],"ja":["自動コード生成","プロジェクト作成","コード最適化","自動化された繰り返しタスク","コードの一貫性を確保"],"ko":["자동 코드 생성","프로젝트 생성","코드 최적화","자동화된 반복 작업","코드 일관성을 보장"],"es":["Automatización de tareas repetitivas","Creación de proyectos y aplicaciones","Migración de código automática","Consistencia del código en todo el monorepo","Personalización de generadores de código"],"fr":["Automatisation des tâches répétitives","Création de projets et d''applications","Migration de code automatique","Cohérence du code dans tout le monorepo","Personnalisation des générateurs de code"],"de":["Automatisierung wiederkehrender Aufgaben","Erstellung von Projekten und Anwendungen","Automatische Code-Migration","Konsistenz des Codes im gesamten Monorepo","Anpassung von Code-Generatoren"],"pt":["Geração de código para projetos e aplicativos","Automação de tarefas repetitivas","Melhoria da produtividade no desenvolvimento de software","Suporte a monorepos","Personalização de workflows"],"ru":["Генерация кода для проектов и приложений","Автоматизация повторяющихся задач","Повышение производительности разработки ПО","Поддержка монорепозиториев","Настройка рабочих процессов"],"ar":["توليد الكود لمشاريع وتطبيقات","تأتمة المهام المتكررة","تحسين الإنتاجية في تطوير البرمجيات","دعم مشاريع مونوريبوزيتوري","تخصيص سير العمل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Nx Generate","自动代码生成","项目优化","开发效率","代码一致性","自动化"],"ja":["Nx Generate","自動コード生成","プロジェクト最適化","開発効率","コードの一貫性","自動化"],"ko":["Nx Generate","자동 코드 생성","프로젝트 최적화","개발 효율성","코드 일관성","자동화"],"es":["nx-generate","monorepo","automatización de código","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","generadores de código","consistencia del código"],"fr":["nx-generate","monorepo","automatisation de code","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","générateurs de code","cohérence du code"],"de":["nx-generate","monorepo","code-automatisierung","software-entwicklung","entwicklertools","code-generatoren","code-konsistenz"],"pt":["nx generate","geração de código","monorepo","desenvolvimento de software","automação de tarefas","produtividade","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["nx generate","генерация кода","монорепозиторий","разработка ПО","автоматизация задач","производительность","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["نكس جينيريت","توليد الكود","مونوريبوزيتوري","تطوير البرمجيات","تأتمة المهام","الإنتاجية","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"nrwl","repo":"nx","repoPath":"nrwl/nx","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.529Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nx-generate","description":"Generate code using nx generators. USE WHEN scaffolding code or transforming existing code - for example creating libraries or applications, or anything else that is boilerplate code or automates repetitive tasks. ALWAYS use this first when generating code with Nx instead of calling MCP tools or running nx generate immediately.","bodyPreview":"# Run Nx Generator\n\nNx generators are powerful tools that scaffold projects, make automated code migrations or automate repetitive tasks in a monorepo. They ensure consistency across the codebase and reduce boilerplate work.\n\nThis skill applies when the user wants to:\n\n- Create new projects like libraries or applications\n- Scaffold features or boilerplate code\n- Run workspace-specific or custom generators\n- Do anything else that an nx generator exists for\n\n## Generator Discovery Flow\n\n### Step 1","body":"# Run Nx Generator\n\nNx generators are powerful tools that scaffold projects, make automated code migrations or automate repetitive tasks in a monorepo. They ensure consistency across the codebase and reduce boilerplate work.\n\nThis skill applies when the user wants to:\n\n- Create new projects like libraries or applications\n- Scaffold features or boilerplate code\n- Run workspace-specific or custom generators\n- Do anything else that an nx generator exists for\n\n## Generator Discovery Flow\n\n### Step 1: List Available Generators\n\nUse the Nx CLI to discover available generators:\n\n- List all generators for a plugin: `npx nx list @nx/react`\n- View available plugins: `npx nx list`\n\nThis includes:\n\n- Plugin generators (e.g., `@nx/react:library`, `@nx/js:library`)\n- Local workspace generators (defined in the repo''s own plugins)\n\n### Step 2: Match Generator to User Request\n\nBased on the user''s request, identify which generator(s) could fulfill their needs. Consider:\n\n- What artifact type they want to create (library, application, etc.)\n- Which framework or technology stack is relevant\n- Whether they mentioned specific generator names\n\n**IMPORTANT**: When both a local workspace generator and an external plugin generator could satisfy the request, **always prefer the local workspace generator**. Local generators are customized for the specific repo''s patterns and conventions.\n\nIt''s possible that the user request is something that no Nx generator exists for whatsoever. In this case, you can stop using this skill and try to help the user another way. HOWEVER, the burden of proof for this is high. Before aborting, carefully consider each and every generator that''s available. Look into details for any that could be related in any way before making this decision.\n\n## Pre-Execution Checklist\n\nBefore running any generator, complete these steps:\n\n### 1. Fetch Generator Schema\n\nUse the `--help` flag to understand all available options:\n\n```bash\nnpx nx g @nx/react:library --help\n```\n\nPay attention to:\n\n- Required options that must be provided\n- Optional options that may be relevant to the user''s request\n- Default values that might need to be overridden\n\n### 2. Read Generator Source Code\n\nUnderstanding what the generator actually does helps you:\n\n- Know what files will be created/modified\n- Understand any side effects (updating configs, installing deps, etc.)\n- Identify options that might not be obvious from the schema\n\nTo find generator source code:\n\n- For plugin generators: Use `node -e \"console.log(require.resolve(''@nx/<plugin>/generators.json''));\"` to find the generators.json, then locate the source from there\n- If that fails, read directly from `node_modules/<plugin>/generators.json`\n- For local generators: They are typically in `tools/generators/` or a local plugin directory. You can search the repo for the generator name to find it.\n\n### 2.5 Reevaluate if the generator is right\n\nOnce you have built up an understanding of what the selected generator does, reconsider: Is this the right generator to service the user request?\nIf not, it''s okay to go back to the Generator Discovery Flow and select a different generator before proceeding. If you do, make sure to go through the entire pre-execution checklist once more.\n\n### 3. Understand Repo Context\n\nBefore generating, examine the target area of the codebase:\n\n- Look at similar existing artifacts (other libraries, applications, etc.)\n- Identify patterns and conventions used in the repo\n- Note naming conventions, file structures, and configuration patterns\n- Try to match these patterns when configuring the generator\n\nFor example, if similar libraries are using a specific test runner, build tool or linter, try to match that if possible.\nIf projects or other artifacts are organized with a specific naming convention, try to match it.\n\n### 4. Validate Required Options\n\nEnsure all required options have values:\n\n- Map the user''s request to generator options\n- Infer values from context where possible\n- Ask the user for any critical missing information\n\n## Execution\n\nKeep in mind that you might have to prefix things with npx/pnpx/yarn if the user doesn''t have nx installed globally.\nMany generators will behave differently based on where they are executed. For example, first-party nx library generators use the cwd to determine the directory that the library should be placed in. This is highly important.\n\n### Consider Dry-Run (Optional)\n\nRunning with `--dry-run` first is strongly encouraged but not mandatory. Use your judgment:\n\n- For complex generators or unfamiliar territory: do a dry-run first\n- For simple, well-understood generators: may proceed directly\n- Dry-run shows file names and created/deleted/modified markers, but not content\n- There are cases where a generator does not support dry-run (for example if it had to install an npm package) - in that case --dry-run might fail. Don''t be discouraged but simply move on to running the generator for real and iterating from there.\n\n### Running the Generator\n\nExecute the generator with:\n\n```bash\nnx generate <generator-name> <options> --no-interactive\n```\n\n**CRITICAL**: Always include `--no-interactive` to prevent prompts that would hang the execution.\n\nExample:\n\n```bash\nnx generate @nx/react:library --name=my-utils --no-interactive\n```\n\n### Handling Generator Failures\n\nIf the generator fails:\n\n1. **Diagnose the error** - Read the error message carefully\n2. **Identify the cause** - Missing options, invalid values, conflicts, etc.\n3. **Attempt automatic fix** - Adjust options or resolve conflicts\n4. **Retry** - Run the generator again with corrected options\n\nCommon failure reasons:\n\n- Missing required options\n- Invalid option values\n- Conflicting with existing files\n- Missing dependencies\n- Generator doesn''t support certain flag combinations\n\n## Post-Generation\n\n### 1. Modify Generated Code (If Needed)\n\nGenerators provide a starting point, but the output may need adjustment to match the user''s specific requirements:\n\n- Add or modify functionality as requested\n- Adjust imports, exports, or configurations\n- Integrate with existing code patterns in the repo\n\n### 2. Format Code\n\nRun formatting on all generated/modified files:\n\n```bash\nnx format --fix\n```\n\nLanguages other than javascript/typescript might need other formatting invocations too.\n\n### 3. Run Verification\n\nVerify that the generated code works correctly. What this looks like will vary depending on the type of generator and the targets available.\nIf the generator created a new project, run its targets directly\nUse your best judgement to determine what needs to be verified.\n\nExample:\n\n```bash\nnx lint <new-project>\nnx test <new-project>\nnx build <new-project>\n```\n\n### 4. Handle Verification Failures\n\nWhen verification fails:\n\n**If scope is manageable** (a few lint errors, minor type issues):\n\n- Fix the issues\n- Re-run verification to confirm\n\n**If issues are extensive** (many errors, complex problems):\n\n- Attempt simple, obvious fixes first\n- If still failing, escalate to the user with:\n  - Description of what was generated\n  - What verification is failing\n  - What you''ve attempted to fix\n  - Remaining issues that need user input\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Generator Failures\n\n- Check the error message for specific causes\n- Verify all required options are provided\n- Check for conflicts with existing files\n- Ensure the generator name and options are correct\n\n### Missing Options\n\n- Consult the generator schema for required fields\n- Infer values from context when reasonable\n- Ask the user for values that cannot be inferred\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **Local generators first** - Always prefer workspace/local generators over external plugin generators when both could work\n\n2. **Understand before running** - Read both the schema AND the source code to fully understand what will happen\n\n3. **No prompts** - Always use `--no-interactive` to prevent hanging\n\n4. **Generators are starting points** - Modify the output as needed to fully satisfy the user''s requirements\n\n5. **Verify changes work** - Don''t just generate; ensure the code builds, lints, and tests pass\n\n6. **Be proactive about fixes** - Don''t just report errors; attempt to resolve them automatically when possible\n\n7. **Match repo patterns** - Study existing similar code in the repo and match its conventions\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:26:22.858Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing automated monorepo management and code generation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化单体仓库管理和代码生成能力的开发代理。","ja":"自動化されたモノレポ管理とコード生成機能を必要とする開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"자동화된 모노레포 관리 및 코드 생성 기능이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una gestión de monorepo automatizada y capacidades de generación de código.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une gestion de monorepo automatisée et de capacités de génération de code.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine automatisierte Monorepo-Verwaltung und Codegenerierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de gerenciamento de monorepo automatizado e capacidades de geração de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходим автоматизированное управление monorepo и возможности генерации кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة مونوريبو آلي وقدرات توليد الكود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to scaffold projects, automate repetitive tasks, and optimize builds using Nx generators, ensuring consistency across the codebase and reducing boilerplate work with features like workspace-specific or custom generators.","zh":"赋予代理人搭建项目、自动化重复任务和使用 Nx 生成器优化构建的能力，确保代码库的一致性并减少样板工作，支持工作区特定或自定义生成器等功能。","ja":"エージェントにプロジェクトの作成、繰り返しのタスクの自動化、Nx ジェネレータを使用したビルドの最適化などの機能を提供し、コードベースの整合性を確保し、ワークスペース固有またはカスタム ジェネレータなどの機能でボイラープレート作業を減らします。","ko":"에이전트에게 프로젝트를 구축하고 반복적인 작업을 자동화하며 Nx 생성기를 사용하여 빌드를 최적화하는 등의 기능을 제공하여 코드베이스의 일관성을 보장하고 작업공간 특정 또는 사용자 지정 생성기 등의 기능으로 보일러プレ이트 작업을 줄입니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear estructuras de proyecto, automatizar tareas repetitivas y optimizar compilaciones utilizando generadores de Nx, garantizando la consistencia en todo el código y reduciendo el trabajo de código repetitivo con características como generadores específicos del espacio de trabajo o personalizados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des structures de projet, d''automatiser des tâches répétitives et d''optimiser les builds en utilisant les générateurs Nx, en garantissant la cohérence dans l''ensemble du codebase et en réduisant le travail de code répétitif avec des fonctionnalités comme des générateurs spécifiques à l''espace de travail ou personnalisés.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Projekte zu erstellen, wiederkehrende Aufgaben zu automatisieren und Builds mit Nx-Generatoren zu optimieren, wodurch die Konsistenz im gesamten Codebase gewährleistet und der Aufwand für Boilerplate-Code mit Funktionen wie workspace-spezifischen oder benutzerdefinierten Generatoren reduziert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar esqueletos de projetos, automatizar tarefas repetitivas e otimizar compilações usando geradores Nx, garantindo a consistência em todo o código e reduzindo o trabalho de codificação com recursos como geradores específicos do espaço de trabalho ou personalizados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать каркасы проектов, автоматизировать повторяющиеся задачи и оптимизировать сборки с помощью генераторов Nx, обеспечивая согласованность на протяжении всего кода и снижая объем работы по созданию шаблонов с помощью функций, таких как генераторы, специфичные для рабочего пространства или настраиваемые.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من وضع هيكل لمشاريع، وتأتمة المهام المتكررة، وتحسين البناء باستخدام مولدات Nx، ضامنًا التماسك عبر قاعدة الشفرة، وتقليل عمل الكتابة مع الميزات مثل مولدات محددة لمساحة العمل أو مخصصة."},"useCases":{"en":["Scaffolding new libraries or applications","Automating code migrations with custom generators","Generating boilerplate code for features","Running workspace-specific generators for monorepo optimization"],"zh":["搭建新的库或应用程序","使用自定义生成器自动化代码迁移","为功能生成样板代码","运行工作区特定生成器以优化单体仓库"],"ja":["新しいライブラリまたはアプリケーションの作成","カスタム ジェネレータを使用したコード移行の自動化","機能のボイラープレート コードの生成","モノレポの最適化のためのワークスペース固有のジェネレータの実行"],"ko":["새로운 라이브러리 또는 애플리케이션을 구축하기","사용자 지정 생성기를 사용하여 코드 마이그레이션 자동화","기능을 위한 보일러プレ이트 코드 생성","모노레포 최적화를 위한 작업공간 특정 생성기 실행"],"es":["Crear estructuras para nuevas bibliotecas o aplicaciones","Automatizar migraciones de código con generadores personalizados","Generar código repetitivo para características","Ejecutar generadores específicos del espacio de trabajo para la optimización de monorepo"],"fr":["Créer des structures pour de nouvelles bibliothèques ou applications","Automatiser les migrations de code avec des générateurs personnalisés","Générer du code répétitif pour des fonctionnalités","Exécuter des générateurs spécifiques à l''espace de travail pour l''optimisation de monorepo"],"de":["Erstellen von Strukturen für neue Bibliotheken oder Anwendungen","Automatisieren von Code-Migrationen mit benutzerdefinierten Generatoren","Generieren von Boilerplate-Code für Funktionen","Ausführen von workspace-spezifischen Generatoren für die Monorepo-Optimierung"],"pt":["Criação de novas bibliotecas ou aplicações","Automatização de migrações de código com geradores personalizados","Geração de código de modelo para recursos","Execução de geradores específicos do espaço de trabalho para otimização de monorepo"],"ru":["Создание новых библиотек или приложений","Автоматизация миграций кода с помощью пользовательских генераторов","Генерация кода шаблона для функций","Выполнение генераторов, специфичных для рабочего пространства, для оптимизации monorepo"],"ar":["إنشاء مكتبات أو تطبيقات جديدة","تأتمة هجرة الكود باستخدام مولدات مخصصة","توليد كود نموذج لميزات","تشغيل مولدات محددة لمساحة العمل لتحسين مونوريبو"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Nx monorepo setup","Limited to projects using Nx generators"],"zh":["需要 Nx 单体仓库设置","仅限于使用 Nx 生成器的项目"],"ja":["Nx モノレポ設定が必要","Nx ジェネレータを使用するプロジェクトのみに限定"],"ko":["Nx 모노레포 설정이 필요","Nx 생성기를 사용하는 프로젝트에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de monorepo de Nx","Limitado a proyectos que utilizan generadores de Nx"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de monorepo Nx","Limité à des projets utilisant des générateurs Nx"],"de":["Benötigt Nx-Monorepo-Setup","Begrenzt auf Projekte, die Nx-Generatoren verwenden"],"pt":["Requer configuração de monorepo Nx","Limitado a projetos que usam geradores Nx"],"ru":["Требует настройки monorepo Nx","Ограничен проектами, использующими генераторы Nx"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مونوريبو Nx","محدود بمشاريع تستخدم مولدات Nx"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
