ra la política de evidencia de dev/staging/UAT","Permite la creación de nuevos problemas de Linear","Actualiza el estado de los tickets y adjunta evidencia","Analiza los criterios de aceptación"],"fr":["Méthodologie de développement d''agents multiples validée pour la production","Utilise Claude Code pour assurer la cohérence dans la gestion des tickets","Fournit des modèles de preuve pour la politique de preuve de dev/staging/UAT","Permet la création de nouveaux problèmes de Linear","Met à jour le statut des tickets et attache des preuves","Analyse les critères d''acceptation"],"de":["Für die Produktion validierte Mehragenten-Entwicklungsmethodik","Verwendet Claude Code, um die Konsistenz bei der Ticketverwaltung zu gewährleisten","Bietet Beweismuster für die Beweisrichtlinie von dev/staging/UAT","Ermöglicht die Erstellung neuer Linear-Probleme","Aktualisiert den Status der Tickets und fügt Beweise hinzu","Analysiert die Akzeptanzkriterien"],"pt":["Metodologia de desenvolvimento de agentes SAFe","Guia para gestão de tickets e evidências","11 papéis de agentes especializados","Modelo de trabalho com UUIDs e IDs de issues","Integração com Linear web UI e CLI"],"ru":["Методология разработки агентов SAFe","Руководство по управлению тикетами и доказательствами","11 ролей специализированных агентов","Работа с UUID и ID тикетов","Интеграция с Linear web UI и CLI"],"ar":["منهجية تطوير الوكلاء SAFe","دليل لإدارة التذاكر و الأدلة","11 دورة وكلاء متخصصين","العمل مع UUIDs و IDs التذاكر","التكامل مع Linear واجهة المستخدم و CLI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Linear SOP","代码开发","代码管理","多代理开发","团队协作","Gemini CLI","开发语言"],"ja":["Linear SOP","コード開発","コード管理","マルチエージェント開発","チームコラボレーション","Gemini CLI","開発言語"],"ko":["Linear SOP","코드 개발","코드 관리","멀티 에이전트 개발","팀 협업","Gemini CLI","개발 언어"],"es":["linear-sop","desarrollo de agentes múltiples","metodología de desarrollo de software","Claude Code","gestión de tickets","evidencia de dev/staging/UAT","criterios de aceptación","desarrollo de inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["linear-sop","développement d''agents multiples","méthodologie de développement de logiciels","Claude Code","gestion des tickets","preuve de dev/staging/UAT","critères d''acceptation","développement d''intelligence artificielle"],"de":["linear-sop","Mehragenten-Entwicklung","Software-Entwicklungsmethodik","Claude Code","Ticketverwaltung","Beweis für dev/staging/UAT","Akzeptanzkriterien","künstliche Intelligenz-Entwicklung"],"pt":["linear-sop","desenvolvimento de agentes","SAFe","gestão de tickets","evidências","UUID","IDs de issues","Linear web UI","CLI"],"ru":["linear-sop","разработка агентов","SAFe","управление тикетами","доказательства","UUID","ID тикетов","Linear web UI","CLI"],"ar":["linear-sop","تطوير الوكلاء","SAFe","إدارة التذاكر","الأدلة","UUID","IDs التذاكر","Linear واجهة المستخدم","CLI"]}},"owner":"bybren-llc","repo":"safe-agentic-workflow","repoPath":"bybren-llc/safe-agentic-workflow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.530Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"linear-sop","description":"Linear ticket management best practices. Use when creating issues, updating status, or attaching evidence. Provides evidence templates for dev/staging/done phases.","bodyPreview":"# Linear SOP Skill\n\n## Purpose\n\nGuide consistent Linear ticket management. Provides evidence templates for the mandatory dev/staging/UAT evidence policy.\n\n## When This Skill Applies\n\n- Creating new Linear issues\n- Updating ticket status\n- Attaching evidence to tickets\n- Parsing acceptance criteria\n- Working with UUIDs and issue IDs\n\n## Linear Operations (Manual Process)\n\nSince Gemini CLI doesn''t have native Linear integration, use the Linear web UI or CLI for these operations:\n\n### Reading Issue","body":"# Linear SOP Skill\n\n## Purpose\n\nGuide consistent Linear ticket management. Provides evidence templates for the mandatory dev/staging/UAT evidence policy.\n\n## When This Skill Applies\n\n- Creating new Linear issues\n- Updating ticket status\n- Attaching evidence to tickets\n- Parsing acceptance criteria\n- Working with UUIDs and issue IDs\n\n## Linear Operations (Manual Process)\n\nSince Gemini CLI doesn''t have native Linear integration, use the Linear web UI or CLI for these operations:\n\n### Reading Issues\n\n```bash\n# Via Linear Web UI\n# Navigate to: https://linear.app/team/{PROJECT_TEAM_NAME}/issue/{TICKET_PREFIX}-XXX\n\n# Or use Linear CLI if installed\nlinear issue view {TICKET_PREFIX}-XXX\n```\n\n### Creating Issues\n\n```bash\n# Via Linear Web UI: Click \"New Issue\" or press C\n# Or use Linear CLI:\nlinear issue create --title \"feat(scope): description\" --team {PROJECT_TEAM_NAME}\n```\n\n### Updating Issues\n\n```bash\n# Via Linear Web UI: Open issue and update status\n# Or use Linear CLI:\nlinear issue update {TICKET_PREFIX}-XXX --state \"Done\"\n```\n\n### Adding Comments\n\n```bash\n# Via Linear Web UI: Open issue and add comment\n# Or use Linear CLI:\nlinear issue comment {TICKET_PREFIX}-XXX \"**Dev Evidence**\\n\\n...\"\n```\n\n## Evidence Policy (MUST)\n\nEvery issue requires evidence at each phase:\n\n| Phase       | Required? | Content                 |\n| ----------- | --------- | ----------------------- |\n| **Dev**     | MUST      | Implementation proof    |\n| **Staging** | MUST      | UAT validation (or N/A) |\n| **Done**    | MUST      | Final verification      |\n\n## Evidence Templates\n\n### Dev Evidence Template\n\n```markdown\n**Dev Evidence**\n\n**PR**: https://github.com/{ORG_NAME}/{REPO_NAME}/pull/XXX\n**Commit**: [short-hash]\n**Branch**: {TICKET_PREFIX}-XXX-description\n\n**Implementation:**\n\n- [x] Feature implemented\n- [x] Tests passing\n- [x] Lint passing\n\n**Verification:**\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\nyarn ci:validate\n\n# Output: All checks passed\n\n\\`\\`\\`\n```\n\n### Staging/UAT Evidence Template\n\n```markdown\n**Staging Evidence**\n\n**Environment**: Pop OS dev server\n**URL**: http://pop-os:3000\n\n**Validation Steps:**\n\n1. Deployed to staging: [timestamp]\n2. Smoke test passed: [yes/no]\n3. Feature verified: [description]\n\n**UAT Status:** [Passed/Pending/N/A]\n\nIf N/A, reason: [e.g., \"Dev tooling only - no user-facing changes\"]\n```\n\n### Done Evidence Template\n\n```markdown\n**Done Evidence**\n\n**PR Merged**: https://github.com/{ORG_NAME}/{REPO_NAME}/pull/XXX\n**Merge Commit**: [hash]\n\n**Final Checklist:**\n\n- [x] All acceptance criteria met\n- [x] Documentation updated (if applicable)\n- [x] No regressions detected\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Parsing\n\nWhen reading issue descriptions, extract ACs:\n\n```markdown\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] User can perform action X\n- [ ] System responds with Y\n- [ ] Error handling for Z\n```\n\nConvert to testable checklist:\n\n```typescript\nconst acceptanceCriteria = [\n  { criterion: \"User can perform action X\", verified: false },\n  { criterion: \"System responds with Y\", verified: false },\n  { criterion: \"Error handling for Z\", verified: false },\n];\n```\n\n## Status Workflow\n\n```text\nBacklog -> Ready -> In Progress -> Testing -> Ready for Review -> Done\n```\n\n### Status Update Guidelines\n\n| From             | To               | When                     |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------ |\n| Backlog          | Ready            | Sprint planning          |\n| Ready            | In Progress      | Work starts              |\n| In Progress      | Testing          | PR created               |\n| Testing          | Ready for Review | Tests pass, UAT complete |\n| Ready for Review | Done             | POPM approval            |\n\n## UUID Handling\n\nLinear uses UUIDs internally. When working with APIs:\n\n```typescript\n// Issue identifiers (human-readable)\nconst issueId = \"{TICKET_PREFIX}-459\";\n\n// UUIDs (API operations)\nconst uuid = \"ef6a5fa0-2b46-417f-8266-dea2d187b10a\";\n\n// Get UUID from identifier via Linear web UI or API\n// The issue URL contains the UUID\n```\n\n## Common Operations\n\n### Link PR to Issue\n\nPRs are automatically linked when:\n\n- Branch name contains `{TICKET_PREFIX}-XXX`\n- PR title contains `[{TICKET_PREFIX}-XXX]`\n\n### Create Sub-Issue\n\nUse Linear web UI: Click \"Add sub-issue\" on parent issue\n\n### Query by Label\n\nUse Linear web UI filters:\n1. Open team view\n2. Click \"Filter\"\n3. Select label (e.g., \"sprint-1\")\n\n## Reference\n\n- **Agent Workflow SOP**: `docs/sop/AGENT_WORKFLOW_SOP.md`\n- **Linear Documentation**: https://linear.app/docs\n- **CONTRIBUTING.md**: Workflow documentation\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:32:48.750Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for SAFe-aligned Development Agents orchestrating multi-agent workflows across Linear project management systems.","zh":"适用于SAFe对齐的开发代理，用于编排跨线性项目管理系统的多代理工作流。","ja":"SAFeに準拠した開発エージェントが、リニアプロジェクト管理システムを跨ぐマルチエージェントワークフローをオーケストレーションするために不可欠。","ko":"SAFe와 일치하는 개발 에이전트가 선형 프로젝트 관리 시스템을跨ぐ 멀티 에이전트 워크플로우를 오케스트레이션하는 데 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para agentes de desarrollo alineados con SAFe que orquestan flujos de trabajo de multiagentes a través de sistemas de gestión de proyectos lineales.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de développement alignés sur SAFe qui orchestrent des flux de travail multi-agents à travers des systèmes de gestion de projets linéaires.","de":"Wesentlich für SAFe-alignmentierte Entwicklungsmittel, die Multiagenten-Workflows über lineare Projektmanagement-Systeme orchestrieren.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Desenvolvimento alinhados com SAFe que orquestram fluxos de trabalho de multiagentes em sistemas de gerenciamento de projetos lineares.","ru":"Необходим для агентов разработки, выровненных с SAFe, которые управляют рабочими процессами нескольких агентов в линейных системах управления проектами.","ar":"ضروري لعميل تطوير متوافق مع SAFe الذي يدير سير عمل متعدد الوكلاء عبر أنظمة إدارة المشاريع الخطية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables rigorous ticket management compliance with production-validated SAFe methodology, providing structured evidence templates for dev/staging/UAT workflows and specialized role assignments across 11 agent types including BSA, Architect, and QAS. Directly handles UUID parsing, acceptance criteria analysis, and mandatory evidence attachment protocols.","zh":"能够实现严格的票据管理，符合生产验证的SAFe方法论，提供用于开发/预发/测试工作流的结构化证据模板，并跨11种代理类型（包括BSA、架构师和QAS）提供专业的角色分配。直接处理UUID解析、验收标准分析和强制性证据附件协议。","ja":"生産検証されたSAFe方法論に準拠した徹底したチケット管理を可能にし、開発/ステージング/ユーザー受け入れテストワークフローに構造化された証拠テンプレートを提供し、BSA、建築家、QASを含む11種類のエージェントタイプを跨ぐ専門的なロール割り当てを提供する。UUID解析、受け入れ基準分析、および強制的な証拠添付プロトコルを直接処理する。","ko":"생산 검증된 SAFe 방법론에 따라 철저한 티켓 관리를 가능하게 하며, 개발/스태이징/사용자 수락 테스트 워크플로우에 구조화된 증거 템플릿을 제공하며, BSA, 아키텍트 및 QAS를 포함한 11가지 에이전트 유형을跨ぐ 전문적인 역할 할당을 제공합니다. UUID 파싱, 수락 기준 분석 및 강제 증거 첨부 프로토콜을 직접 처리합니다.","es":"Permite un cumplimiento riguroso de la gestión de tickets con la metodología SAFe validada en producción, proporcionando plantillas de evidencia estructuradas para flujos de trabajo de desarrollo/entorno de ensayos/UAT y asignaciones de roles especializados en 11 tipos de agentes, incluidos BSA, Arquitecto y QAS. Maneja directamente el análisis de parsing de UUID, el análisis de criterios de aceptación y los protocolos de adjuntar evidencia obligatoria.","fr":"Permet un respect rigoureux de la gestion des tickets conformément à la méthodologie SAFe validée en production, en fournissant des modèles de preuve structurés pour les flux de travail de développement/ébauche/UAT et des assignations de rôles spécialisés parmi 11 types d''agents, notamment BSA, Architecte et QAS. Gère directement l''analyse de parsing de UUID, l''analyse des critères d''acceptation et les protocoles d''attachement de preuve obligatoire.","de":"Ermöglicht eine strenge Einhaltung der Ticketverwaltung mit der in der Produktion validierten SAFe-Methodik, indem strukturierte Beweisvorlagen für Entwicklungs-/Staging-/UAT-Workflows und spezialisierte Rollenzuweisungen für 11 Agententypen, einschließlich BSA, Architekt und QAS, bereitgestellt werden. Handhabt direkt die UUID-Parsing-Analyse, die Akzeptanzkriterien-Analyse und die obligatorischen Beweisanhängungsprotokolle.","pt":"Permite o cumprimento rigoroso do gerenciamento de tickets com metodologia SAFe validada na produção, fornecendo modelos de evidência estruturados para fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento/estágio/UAT e atribuições de papéis especializados em 11 tipos de agentes, incluindo BSA, Arquiteto e QAS. Lidar diretamente com análise de parsing de UUID, critérios de aceitação e protocolos de anexação de evidência obrigatória.","ru":"Позволяет обеспечить строгое соблюдение требований управления тикетами в соответствии с методологией SAFe, проверенной в производстве, предоставляя структурированные шаблоны доказательств для рабочих процессов разработки/стадии/UAT и специализированных назначений ролей для 11 типов агентов, включая BSA, Архитектор и QAS. Прямо обрабатывает парсинг UUID, анализ критериев приемки и обязательные протоколы прикрепления доказательств.","ar":"يمكنه تمكين الامتثال الصارم لإدارة التذاكر مع منهجية SAFe المُثبتة في الإنتاج، ويوفر قوالب أدلة محددة لتدفقات العمل التطويرية/المرحلية/الاختبار وعمليات التخصيص الدور المتخصصة عبر 11 نوعًا من الوكلاء بما في ذلك BSA و architekt و QAS. يتعامل بشكل مباشر مع تحليل UUID و معايير القبول و بروتوكولات المرفقات الإلزامية للأدلة."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating SAFe-compliant Linear tickets with standardized templates","Attaching mandatory development/staging/UAT evidence to tickets","Parsing and validating acceptance criteria for agent handoffs","Managing UUID and issue ID tracking across multi-agent workflows"],"zh":["使用标准模板创建SAFe兼容的Linear票据","将强制性开发/预发/测试证据附加到票据","解析和验证代理人转交的验收标准","跨多代理工作流管理UUID和问题ID跟踪"],"ja":["標準テンプレートを使用してSAFeに準拠したLinearチケットを作成する","開発/ステージング/ユーザー受け入れテストの強制的な証拠をチケットに添付する","エージェントハンドオフの受け入れ基準を解析および検証する","マルチエージェントワークフローを跨ぐUUIDおよび問題IDの追跡を管理する"],"ko":["표준 템플릿을 사용하여 SAFe와 호환되는 Linear 티켓을 생성하는 것","개발/스태이징/사용자 수락 테스트에 대한 강제적인 증거를 티켓에 첨부하는 것","에이전트 핸드오버의 수락 기준을 분석 및 검증하는 것","멀티 에이전트 워크플로우를跨ぐ UUID 및 문제 ID 추적 관리"],"es":["Crear tickets de Linear que cumplan con SAFe con plantillas estandarizadas","Adjuntar evidencia de desarrollo/entorno de ensayos/UAT obligatoria a los tickets","Analizar y validar los criterios de aceptación para la transferencia de agentes","Administrar el seguimiento de UUID y ID de problema en flujos de trabajo de multiagentes"],"fr":["Créer des tickets Linear conformes à SAFe avec des modèles standardisés","Attacher des preuves de développement/ébauche/UAT obligatoires aux tickets","Analyser et valider les critères d''acceptation pour le transfert d''agents","Gérer le suivi de UUID et d''ID de problème dans les flux de travail multi-agents"],"de":["Erstellen von SAFe-konformen Linear-Tickets mit standardisierten Vorlagen","Anhängen obligatorischer Entwicklungs-/Staging-/UAT-Beweise an Tickets","Analysieren und Validieren der Akzeptanzkriterien für die Übertragung von Agenten","Verwalten der Nachverfolgung von UUID und Problem-ID in Multiagenten-Workflows"],"pt":["Criando tickets do Linear compatíveis com SAFe com modelos padronizados","Anexando evidências de desenvolvimento/estágio/UAT obrigatórias aos tickets","Analise de critérios de aceitação e validação para transferências de agente","Gerenciamento de rastreamento de UUID e ID de problema em fluxos de trabalho de multiagentes"],"ru":["Создание тикетов Linear, соответствующих SAFe, с использованием стандартизированных шаблонов","Прикрепление обязательных доказательств разработки/стадии/UAT к тикетам","Анализ и проверка критериев приемки для передачи агентов","Управление отслеживанием UUID и идентификаторов проблем в рабочих процессах нескольких агентов"],"ar":["إنشاء تذاكر متوافقة مع SAFe في Linear باستخدام قوالب معيارية","إرفاق أدلة تطوير/مرحلي/اختبار إلزامية بالتذاكر","تحليل معايير القبول والتحقق منها لتحويلات الوكيل","إدارة تتبع UUID وأرقام التعريف للمشكلات في سير العمل المتعددة للوكلاء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires manual Linear UI/CLI operations (no native integration)","Gemini CLI dependency for execution","SAFe methodology-specific implementation"],"zh":["需要手动Linear UI/CLI操作（无原生集成）","依赖Gemini CLI执行","SAFe方法论特定实现"],"ja":["手動のLinear UI/CLI操作が必要（ネイティブ統合なし）","Gemini CLI依存の実行","SAFe方法論特有の実装"],"ko":["수동 Linear UI/CLI 작업이 필요함(네이티브 통합 없음)","Gemini CLI 의존성 실행","SAFe 방법론 특정 구현"],"es":["Requiere operaciones manuales de la interfaz de usuario/CLI de Linear (sin integración nativa)","Dependencia de Gemini CLI para la ejecución","Implementación específica de la metodología SAFe"],"fr":["Nécessite des opérations manuelles de l''interface utilisateur/CLI de Linear (pas d''intégration native)","Dépendance de Gemini CLI pour l''exécution","Implémentation spécifique de la méthodologie SAFe"],"de":["Erfordert manuelle Linear-Benutzeroberflächen-/CLI-Operationen (keine native Integration)","Abhängigkeit von Gemini CLI für die Ausführung","SAFe-Methodik-spezifische Implementierung"],"pt":["Requer operações manuais de UI/CLI do Linear (sem integração nativa)","Dependência do CLI Gemini para execução","Implementação específica da metodologia SAFe"],"ru":["Требует ручных операций UI/CLI Linear (без родной интеграции)","Зависимость от CLI Gemini для выполнения","Реализация, специфичная для методологии SAFe"],"ar":["يتطلب عمليات يدويّة لواجهة المستخدم/سطر الأوامر في Linear (بدون تكامل أصلي)","اعتماد على سطر الأوامر Gemini للتنفيذ","تطبيق محدد لمنهجية SAFe"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/orpc-contract-first', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'orpc-contract-first', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.530Z', '2026-02-18T14:32:34.372Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/orpc-contract-first","name":"orpc-contract-first","description":{"zh":"oRPC Contract-First开发是一种新颖的开发方式，通过定义契约来提高开发效率和代码质量","ja":"oRPCコントラクトファースト開発は、コントラクトを定義することで開発効率とコード品質を向上させる新しい開発手法","ko":"oRPC 계약 우선 개발은 계약을 정의함으로써 개발 효율성과 코드 품질을 향상시키는 새로운 개발 방법","es":"El desarrollo de contratos oRPC es un enfoque para crear contratos de manera eficiente","fr":"Le développement de contrats oRPC est une approche pour créer des contrats de manière efficace","de":"Die oRPC-Vertragsentwicklung ist ein Ansatz, um Verträge effizient zu erstellen","pt":"O desenvolvimento de contrato oRPC é uma abordagem eficiente para criar contratos. A interface do usuário inspirada em Antigravity oferece uma experiência de usuário única.","ru":"Разработка контракта oRPC - это эффективный подход к созданию контрактов. Интерфейс пользователя, вдохновленный Antigravity, предоставляет уникальный опыт пользователя.","ar":"تطوير عقد oRPC هو نهج فعال لإنشاء العقود. واجهة المستخدم الملهمة من Antigravity توفر تجربة مستخدم فريدة.","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"oRPC首先开发契约","ja":"oRPCコントラクトファースト開発","ko":"oRPC 계약 우선 개발","es":"Desarrollo de Contratos oRPC","fr":"Développement de Contrats oRPC","de":"oRPC-Vertragsentwicklung","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Contrato oRPC - Primeiro","ru":"Разработка контракта oRPC - Первый","ar":"تطوير عقد oRPC - أولا","en":"orpc-contract-first"},"description":{"zh":"oRPC Contract-First开发是一种新颖的开发方式，通过定义契约来提高开发效率和代码质量","ja":"oRPCコントラクトファースト開発は、コントラクトを定義することで開発効率とコード品質を向上させる新しい開発手法","ko":"oRPC 계약 우선 개발은 계약을 정의함으로써 개발 효율성과 코드 품질을 향상시키는 새로운 개발 방법","es":"El desarrollo de contratos oRPC es un enfoque para crear contratos de manera eficiente","fr":"Le développement de contrats oRPC est une approche pour créer des contrats de manière efficace","de":"Die oRPC-Vertragsentwicklung ist ein Ansatz, um Verträge effizient zu erstellen","pt":"O desenvolvimento de contrato oRPC é uma abordagem eficiente para criar contratos. A interface do usuário inspirada em Antigravity oferece uma experiência de...","ru":"Разработка контракта oRPC - это эффективный подход к созданию контрактов. Интерфейс пользователя, вдохновленный Antigravity, предоставляет уникальный опыт по...","ar":"تطوير عقد oRPC هو نهج فعال لإنشاء العقود. واجهة المستخدم الملهمة من Antigravity توفر تجربة مستخدم فريدة.","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["提高开发效率","提高代码质量","定义契约","规范开发过程","支持多语言开发","易于维护和扩展"],"ja":["開発効率の向上","コード品質の向上","コントラクトの定義","開発プロセスの規定","多言語開発のサポート","メンテナンスと拡張の容易さ"],"ko":["개발 효율성 향상","코드 품질 향상","계약 정의","개발 프로세스 규정","다언어 개발 지원","유지 보수 및 확장의 용이성"],"es":["Desarrollo de contratos con AesopIDE","Interfaz de usuario inspirada en Antigravity","Estructura de proyecto organizada","Compatibilidad con tipos y composición de enrutadores","Soporte para contratos de consola y marketplace"],"fr":["Développement de contrats avec AesopIDE","Interface utilisateur inspirée par Antigravity","Structure de projet organisée","Compatibilité avec les types et la composition de routeurs","Prise en charge des contrats de console et de marketplace"],"de":["Vertragsentwicklung mit AesopIDE","Benutzeroberfläche inspiriert von Antigravity","Organisierte Projektstruktur","Kompatibilität mit Typen und Router-Zusammensetzung","Unterstützung für Consolen- und Marketplace-Verträge"],"pt":["Criação de contratos eficientes","Interface do usuário inspirada em Antigravity","Estrutura de projeto organizada","Tipos de exportação de composição de roteador","Contratos de console por domínio"],"ru":["Эффективное создание контрактов","Интерфейс пользователя, вдохновленный Antigravity","Организованная структура проекта","Типы экспорта состава роутера","Контракты консоли по домену"],"ar":["إنشاء عقود فعال","واجهة المستخدم الملهمة من Antigravity","هيكل مشروع منظم","أنواع تصدير تركيبة الموجه","عقود وحدة التحكم حسب النطاق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["oRPC","Contract-First开发","开发效率","代码质量","契约开发","开发规范","多语言开发","维护和扩展"],"ja":["oRPC","コントラクトファースト開発","開発効率","コード品質","コントラクト開発","開発規定","多言語開発","メンテナンスと拡張"],"ko":["oRPC","계약 우선 개발","개발 효율성","코드 품질","계약 개발","개발 규정","다언어 개발","유지 보수 및 확장"],"es":["desarrollo de contratos oRPC","AesopIDE","Antigravity","contratos de consola","contratos de marketplace","tipos y composición de enrutadores"],"fr":["développement de contrats oRPC","AesopIDE","Antigravity","contrats de console","contrats de marketplace","types et composition de routeurs"],"de":["oRPC-Vertragsentwicklung","AesopIDE","Antigravity","Consolen-Verträge","Marketplace-Verträge","Typen und Router-Zusammensetzung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de contrato oRPC","contrato oRPC","interface do usuário Antigravity","criação de contratos","estrutura de projeto","roteador","console","domínio"],"ru":["разработка контракта oRPC","контракт oRPC","интерфейс пользователя Antigravity","создание контрактов","структура проекта","роутер","консоль","домен"],"ar":["تطوير عقد oRPC","عقد oRPC","واجهة المستخدم Antigravity","إنشاء عقود","هيكل مشروع","موجه","وحدة التحكم","نطاق"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.530Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"orpc-contract-first","description":"Guide for implementing oRPC contract-first API patterns in Dify frontend. Triggers when creating new API contracts, adding service endpoints, integrating TanStack Query with typed contracts, or migrating legacy service calls to oRPC. Use for all API layer work in web/contract and web/service directories.","bodyPreview":"# oRPC Contract-First Development\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nweb/contract/\n├── base.ts           # Base contract (inputStructure: ''detailed'')\n├── router.ts         # Router composition & type exports\n├── marketplace.ts    # Marketplace contracts\n└── console/          # Console contracts by domain\n    ├── system.ts\n    └── billing.ts\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Create contract** in `web/contract/console/{domain}.ts`\n   - Import `base` from `../base` and `type` from `@orpc/contract`\n   - Define route w","body":"# oRPC Contract-First Development\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nweb/contract/\n├── base.ts           # Base contract (inputStructure: ''detailed'')\n├── router.ts         # Router composition & type exports\n├── marketplace.ts    # Marketplace contracts\n└── console/          # Console contracts by domain\n    ├── system.ts\n    └── billing.ts\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Create contract** in `web/contract/console/{domain}.ts`\n   - Import `base` from `../base` and `type` from `@orpc/contract`\n   - Define route with `path`, `method`, `input`, `output`\n\n2. **Register in router** at `web/contract/router.ts`\n   - Import directly from domain file (no barrel files)\n   - Nest by API prefix: `billing: { invoices, bindPartnerStack }`\n\n3. **Create hooks** in `web/service/use-{domain}.ts`\n   - Use `consoleQuery.{group}.{contract}.queryKey()` for query keys\n   - Use `consoleClient.{group}.{contract}()` for API calls\n\n## Key Rules\n\n- **Input structure**: Always use `{ params, query?, body? }` format\n- **Path params**: Use `{paramName}` in path, match in `params` object\n- **Router nesting**: Group by API prefix (e.g., `/billing/*` → `billing: {}`)\n- **No barrel files**: Import directly from specific files\n- **Types**: Import from `@/types/`, use `type<T>()` helper\n\n## Type Export\n\n```typescript\nexport type ConsoleInputs = InferContractRouterInputs<typeof consoleRouterContract>\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:32:34.372Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for TypeScript-based API development agents specializing in structured, type-safe RPC contract composition.","zh":"非常适合专注于结构化、类型安全的RPC合约组合的基于TypeScript的API开发智能体。","ja":"構造化され型安全なRPCコントラクト構成を専門とするTypeScriptベースのAPI開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"구조화되고 타입 안전한 RPC 계약 구성을 전문으로 하는 TypeScript 기반 API 개발 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo de API basados en TypeScript que se especializan en la composición de contratos RPC estructurados y seguros.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement d''API basés sur TypeScript spécialisés dans la composition de contrats RPC structurés et sécurisés.","de":"Ideal für Agenten für die Entwicklung von API-basierten TypeScript, die sich auf die Zusammensetzung von strukturierten, typesicheren RPC-Verträgen spezialisieren.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de desenvolvimento de API baseados em TypeScript especializados na composição estruturada e type-safe de contratos RPC.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки API на TypeScript, специализирующихся на структурированной, типобезопасной композиции RPC-контрактов.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تطوير واجهات برمجة التطبيقات (API) القائمة على TypeScript والمتخصصين في تكوين عقود RPC منظمة وآمنة للنوع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to implement a contract-first development workflow with detailed input structures and router composition. Directly leverages @orpc/contract types for generating type-safe RPC endpoints organized by domain-specific modules like marketplace and console.","zh":"使智能体能够通过详细的输入结构和路由器组合来实现合约优先的开发工作流。直接利用@orpc/contract类型来生成按特定领域模块（如市场和控制台）组织的类型安全RPC端点。","ja":"詳細な入力構造とルーター構成を用いて、コントラクトファーストの開発ワークフローをエージェントに実装可能にします。@orpc/contractの型を直接活用し、マーケットプレイスやコンソールなどのドメイン固有モジュールで整理された型安全なRPCエンドポイントを生成します。","ko":"에이전트가 상세한 입력 구조와 라우터 구성을 통해 계약 중심 개발 워크플로우를 구현할 수 있도록 합니다. @orpc/contract 타입을 직접 활용하여 마켓플레이스 및 콘솔과 같은 도메인별 모듈로 구성된 타입 안전 RPC 엔드포인트를 생성합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar un flujo de trabajo de desarrollo de contrato-primero con estructuras de entrada detalladas y composición de enrutador. Utiliza directamente los tipos @orpc/contract para generar puntos finales RPC seguros organizados por módulos específicos de dominio como marketplace y consola.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre un flux de travail de développement de contrat-premier avec des structures d''entrée détaillées et une composition de routeur. Utilise directement les types @orpc/contract pour générer des points de terminaison RPC sécurisés organisés par modules spécifiques de domaine tels que marketplace et console.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, einen Vertrags-erst-Entwicklungs-Workflow mit detaillierten Eingabestrukturen und Router-Zusammensetzung zu implementieren. Nutzt direkt die @orpc/contract-Typen für die Erzeugung von typesicheren RPC-Endpunkten, die nach domänenspezifischen Modulen wie Marketplace und Konsole organisiert sind.","pt":"Permite que os agentes implementem um fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento contract-first com estruturas de entrada detalhadas e composição de roteador. Aproveita diretamente os tipos @orpc/contract para gerar endpoints RPC type-safe organizados por módulos específicos de domínio, como marketplace e console.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовать процесс разработки по принципу «сначала контракт» с детальными входными структурами и композицией маршрутизатора. Непосредственно использует типы @orpc/contract для создания типобезопасных RPC-конечных точек, организованных по доменно-специфичным модулям, таким как marketplace и console.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تنفيذ سير عمل تطوير يعتمد على العقد أولاً مع هياكل إدخال مفصلة وتكوين الموجه. يستفيد مباشرة من أنواع @orpc/contract لإنشاء نقاط نهاية RPC آمنة للنظم ومنظمة حسب وحدات مجال محدد مثل marketplace و console."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating type-safe RPC contracts for console domains","Composing router structures from base contracts","Exporting contract types for client-server alignment"],"zh":["为控制台领域生成类型安全的RPC合约","从基础合约组合路由器结构","导出合约类型以实现客户端-服务器对齐"],"ja":["コンソールドメイン向けの型安全なRPCコントラクトの生成","ベースコントラクトからのルーター構造の構成","クライアントとサーバーの整合性のためのコントラクト型のエクスポート"],"ko":["콘솔 도메인을 위한 타입 안전 RPC 계약 생성","기본 계약으로부터 라우터 구조 구성","클라이언트-서버 정렬을 위한 계약 타입 내보내기"],"es":["Generación de contratos RPC seguros para dominios de consola","Composición de estructuras de enrutador a partir de contratos base","Exportación de tipos de contrato para la alineación del cliente y del servidor"],"fr":["Génération de contrats RPC sécurisés pour les domaines de console","Composition de structures de routeur à partir de contrats de base","Exportation de types de contrat pour l''alignement client-serveur"],"de":["Erzeugung von typesicheren RPC-Verträgen für Konsolendomänen","Zusammensetzung von Routerstrukturen aus Basisverträgen","Export von Vertragstypen für die Ausrichtung von Client und Server"],"pt":["Geração de contratos RPC type-safe para domínios de console","Composição de estruturas de roteador a partir de contratos base","Exportação de tipos de contrato para alinhamento cliente-servidor"],"ru":["Генерация типобезопасных RPC-контрактов для доменов консоли","Композиция структур маршрутизатора из базовых контрактов","Экспорт типов контрактов для согласования клиента и сервера"],"ar":["إنشاء عقود RPC آمنة للنوع لمجالات console","تكوين هياكل الموجه من العقود الأساسية","تصدير أنواع العقود لمحاذاة العميل والخادم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires TypeScript environment","Depends on @orpc/contract library","Input structure must be ''detailed''"],"zh":["需要TypeScript环境","依赖@orpc/contract库","输入结构必须为“详细”"],"ja":["TypeScript環境が必要","@orpc/contractライブラリに依存","入力構造は「詳細」でなければならない"],"ko":["TypeScript 환경이 필요함","@orpc/contract 라이브러리에 종속됨","입력 구조는 ''상세''해야 함"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de TypeScript","Depende de la biblioteca @orpc/contract","La estructura de entrada debe ser ''detallada''"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement TypeScript","Dépend de la bibliothèque @orpc/contract","La structure d''entrée doit être ''détaillée''"],"de":["Benötigt eine TypeScript-Umgebung","Hängt von der Bibliothek @orpc/contract ab","Die Eingabestruktur muss ''detailliert'' sein"],"pt":["Requer ambiente TypeScript","Depende da biblioteca @orpc/contract","A estrutura de entrada deve ser ''detalhada''"],"ru":["Требует среду TypeScript","Зависит от библиотеки @orpc/contract","Входная структура должна быть ''детальной''"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة TypeScript","يعتمد على مكتبة @orpc/contract","يجب أن يكون هيكل الإدخال ''مفصلاً''"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/Command Development', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'Command Development', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.530Z', '2026-02-18T14:32:36.152Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/Command Development","name":"Command Development","description":{"zh":"Command Development是使用Markdown文件和YAML前端配置创建Claude斜杠命令的技术。通过动态参数、文件引用和Bash执行功能，开发者可以构建强大的可重用工作流程和交互式会话工具。","ja":"Command Developmentは、MarkdownファイルとYAMLフロントマターを使用してClaudeのスラッシュコマンドを作成する技術です。動的引数、ファイル参照、Bash実行機能により、強力な再利用可能なワークフローを構築できます。","ko":"Command Development는 Markdown 파일과 YAML 프론트매터를 사용하여 Claude 슬래시 명령을 생성하는 기술입니다. 동적 인수, 파일 참조, Bash 실행 기능을 통해 강력한 재사용 가능한 워크플로우를 구축할 수 있습니다.","es":"El desarrollo de comandos para Claude Code implica la creación de flujos de trabajo personalizados y reutilizables","fr":"Le développement de commandes pour Claude Code consiste à créer des flux de travail personnalisés et réutilisables","de":"Die Kommando-Entwicklung für Claude Code beinhaltet die Erstellung benutzerdefinierter und wiederverwendbarer Workflows","pt":"Desenvolvimento de comandos personalizados para Claude Code com AesopIDE e UI inspirada em Antigravity","ru":"Разработка пользовательских команд для Claude Code с помощью AesopIDE и UI, вдохновленной Antigravity","ar":"تطوير أوامر مخصصة ل Claude Code باستخدام AesopIDE وواجهة مستخدم مصممة بتقنية Antigravity","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Claude命令开发指南：掌握Markdown与YAML配置","ja":"Claudeコマンド開発：MarkdownとYAML設定の完全ガイド","ko":"Claude 명령 개발: Markdown 및 YAML 구성 완벽 가이드","es":"Desarrollo de Comandos para Claude Code","fr":"Développement de Commandes pour Claude Code","de":"Kommando-Entwicklung für Claude Code","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Comandos para Claude Code","ru":"Разработка Команд для Claude Code","ar":"تطوير أوامر ل Claude Code","en":"Command Development"},"description":{"zh":"Command Development是使用Markdown文件和YAML前端配置创建Claude斜杠命令的技术。通过动态参数、文件引用和Bash执行功能，开发者可以构建强大的可重用工作流程和交互式会话工具。","ja":"Command Developmentは、MarkdownファイルとYAMLフロントマターを使用してClaudeのスラッシュコマンドを作成する技術です。動的引数、ファイル参照、Bash実行機能により、強力な再利用可能なワークフローを構築できます。","ko":"Command Development는 Markdown 파일과 YAML 프론트매터를 사용하여 Claude 슬래시 명령을 생성하는 기술입니다. 동적 인수, 파일 참조, Bash 실행 기능을 통해 강력한 재사용 가능한 워크플로우를 구축할 수 있습니다.","es":"El desarrollo de comandos para Claude Code implica la creación de flujos de trabajo personalizados y reutilizables","fr":"Le développement de commandes pour Claude Code consiste à créer des flux de travail personnalisés et réutilisables","de":"Die Kommando-Entwicklung für Claude Code beinhaltet die Erstellung benutzerdefinierter und wiederverwendbarer Workflows","pt":"Desenvolvimento de comandos personalizados para Claude Code com AesopIDE e UI inspirada em Antigravity","ru":"Разработка пользовательских команд для Claude Code с помощью AesopIDE и UI, вдохновленной Antigravity","ar":"تطوير أوامر مخصصة ل Claude Code باستخدام AesopIDE وواجهة مستخدم مصممة بتقنية Antigravity","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["基于Markdown文件格式的命令定义","YAML前端配置选项","动态参数支持","文件引用功能","Bash执行上下文","命令组织和命名空间管理"],"ja":["Markdownファイル形式によるコマンド定義","YAMLフロントマター設定オプション","動的引数サポート","ファイル参照機能","Bash実行コンテキスト","コマンド組織とネームスペース管理"],"ko":["Markdown 파일 형식 기반 명령 정의","YAML 프론트매터 설정 옵션","동적 인수 지원","파일 참조 기능","Bash 실행 컨텍스트","명령 조직 및 네임스페이스 관리"],"es":["Estructura de comandos basada en Markdown","Opciones de configuración con YAML frontmatter","Argumentos dinámicos y referencias de archivos","Ejecución de Bash para contexto","Organización y espaciado de comandos"],"fr":["Structure de commande basée sur Markdown","Options de configuration avec YAML frontmatter","Arguments dynamiques et références de fichiers","Exécution de Bash pour contexte","Organisation et espacement de commandes"],"de":["Befehlsstruktur basierend auf Markdown","Konfigurationsoptionen mit YAML-Frontmatter","Dynamische Argumente und Dateireferenzen","Bash-Ausführung für Kontext","Befehlsorganisation und Namensgebung"],"pt":["Formato de arquivo Markdown para comandos","Opções de frontmatter em YAML para configuração","Argumentos dinâmicos e referências de arquivo","Execução de Bash para contexto","Organização e namespace de comandos"],"ru":["Формат файла Markdown для команд","Опции frontmatter в YAML для конфигурации","Динамические аргументы и ссылки на файлы","Выполнение Bash для контекста","Организация и пространство имён команд"],"ar":["تنسيق ملف Markdown للأوامر","خيارات frontmatter في YAML للتهيئة","حجج ديناميكية ومراجع ملفات","تنفيذ Bash للسياق","تنظيم الأوامر وتسميتها"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Claude命令开发","斜杠命令配置","Markdown YAML前端","动态参数Claude","Bash执行上下文","命令命名空间","AesopIDE开发","Antigravity UI","Claude工作流程","交互式会话工具"],"ja":["Claudeコマンド開発","スラッシュコマンド設定","Markdown YAMLフロントマター","動的引数Claude","Bash実行コンテキスト","コマンドネームスペース","AesopIDE開発","Antigravity UI","Claudeワークフロー","対話型セッションツール"],"ko":["Claude 명령 개발","슬래시 명령 설정","Markdown YAML 프론트매터","동적 인수 Claude","Bash 실행 컨텍스트","명령 네임스페이스","AesopIDE 개발","Antigravity UI","Claude 워크플로우","대화형 세션 도구"],"es":["desarrollo de comandos","Claude Code","comandos personalizados","flujos de trabajo","Markdown","YAML frontmatter","argumentos dinámicos","Bash"],"fr":["développement de commandes","Claude Code","commandes personnalisées","flux de travail","Markdown","YAML frontmatter","arguments dynamiques","Bash"],"de":["Kommando-Entwicklung","Claude Code","benutzerdefinierte Befehle","Workflows","Markdown","YAML-Frontmatter","dynamische Argumente","Bash"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de comandos","Claude Code","AesopIDE","Antigravity","comandos personalizados","Markdown","YAML","Bash"],"ru":["разработка команд","Claude Code","AesopIDE","Antigravity","пользовательские команды","Markdown","YAML","Bash"],"ar":["تطوير الأوامر","Claude Code","AesopIDE","Antigravity","أوامر مخصصة","Markdown","YAML","Bash"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.530Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Command Development","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to create a slash command, add a command, write a custom command, define command arguments, use command frontmatter, organize commands, create command with file references, interactive command, use AskUserQuestion in command, or needs guidance on slash command structure, YAML frontmatter fields, dynamic arguments, bash execution in commands, user interaction patterns, or command development best practices for Claude Code.","version":"0.2.0","bodyPreview":"# Command Development for Claude Code\n\n## Overview\n\nSlash commands are frequently-used prompts defined as Markdown files that Claude executes during interactive sessions. Understanding command structure, frontmatter options, and dynamic features enables creating powerful, reusable workflows.\n\n**Key concepts:**\n- Markdown file format for commands\n- YAML frontmatter for configuration\n- Dynamic arguments and file references\n- Bash execution for context\n- Command organization and namespacing\n\n## Com","body":"# Command Development for Claude Code\n\n## Overview\n\nSlash commands are frequently-used prompts defined as Markdown files that Claude executes during interactive sessions. Understanding command structure, frontmatter options, and dynamic features enables creating powerful, reusable workflows.\n\n**Key concepts:**\n- Markdown file format for commands\n- YAML frontmatter for configuration\n- Dynamic arguments and file references\n- Bash execution for context\n- Command organization and namespacing\n\n## Command Basics\n\n### What is a Slash Command?\n\nA slash command is a Markdown file containing a prompt that Claude executes when invoked. Commands provide:\n- **Reusability**: Define once, use repeatedly\n- **Consistency**: Standardize common workflows\n- **Sharing**: Distribute across team or projects\n- **Efficiency**: Quick access to complex prompts\n\n### Critical: Commands are Instructions FOR Claude\n\n**Commands are written for agent consumption, not human consumption.**\n\nWhen a user invokes `/command-name`, the command content becomes Claude''s instructions. Write commands as directives TO Claude about what to do, not as messages TO the user.\n\n**Correct approach (instructions for Claude):**\n```markdown\nReview this code for security vulnerabilities including:\n- SQL injection\n- XSS attacks\n- Authentication issues\n\nProvide specific line numbers and severity ratings.\n```\n\n**Incorrect approach (messages to user):**\n```markdown\nThis command will review your code for security issues.\nYou''ll receive a report with vulnerability details.\n```\n\nThe first example tells Claude what to do. The second tells the user what will happen but doesn''t instruct Claude. Always use the first approach.\n\n### Command Locations\n\n**Project commands** (shared with team):\n- Location: `.claude/commands/`\n- Scope: Available in specific project\n- Label: Shown as \"(project)\" in `/help`\n- Use for: Team workflows, project-specific tasks\n\n**Personal commands** (available everywhere):\n- Location: `~/.claude/commands/`\n- Scope: Available in all projects\n- Label: Shown as \"(user)\" in `/help`\n- Use for: Personal workflows, cross-project utilities\n\n**Plugin commands** (bundled with plugins):\n- Location: `plugin-name/commands/`\n- Scope: Available when plugin installed\n- Label: Shown as \"(plugin-name)\" in `/help`\n- Use for: Plugin-specific functionality\n\n## File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\nCommands are Markdown files with `.md` extension:\n\n```\n.claude/commands/\n├── review.md           # /review command\n├── test.md             # /test command\n└── deploy.md           # /deploy command\n```\n\n**Simple command:**\n```markdown\nReview this code for security vulnerabilities including:\n- SQL injection\n- XSS attacks\n- Authentication bypass\n- Insecure data handling\n```\n\nNo frontmatter needed for basic commands.\n\n### With YAML Frontmatter\n\nAdd configuration using YAML frontmatter:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Review code for security issues\nallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Bash(git:*)\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n\nReview this code for security vulnerabilities...\n```\n\n## YAML Frontmatter Fields\n\n### description\n\n**Purpose:** Brief description shown in `/help`\n**Type:** String\n**Default:** First line of command prompt\n\n```yaml\n---\ndescription: Review pull request for code quality\n---\n```\n\n**Best practice:** Clear, actionable description (under 60 characters)\n\n### allowed-tools\n\n**Purpose:** Specify which tools command can use\n**Type:** String or Array\n**Default:** Inherits from conversation\n\n```yaml\n---\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash(git:*)\n---\n```\n\n**Patterns:**\n- `Read, Write, Edit` - Specific tools\n- `Bash(git:*)` - Bash with git commands only\n- `*` - All tools (rarely needed)\n\n**Use when:** Command requires specific tool access\n\n### model\n\n**Purpose:** Specify model for command execution\n**Type:** String (sonnet, opus, haiku)\n**Default:** Inherits from conversation\n\n```yaml\n---\nmodel: haiku\n---\n```\n\n**Use cases:**\n- `haiku` - Fast, simple commands\n- `sonnet` - Standard workflows\n- `opus` - Complex analysis\n\n### argument-hint\n\n**Purpose:** Document expected arguments for autocomplete\n**Type:** String\n**Default:** None\n\n```yaml\n---\nargument-hint: [pr-number] [priority] [assignee]\n---\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Helps users understand command arguments\n- Improves command discovery\n- Documents command interface\n\n### disable-model-invocation\n\n**Purpose:** Prevent SlashCommand tool from programmatically calling command\n**Type:** Boolean\n**Default:** false\n\n```yaml\n---\ndisable-model-invocation: true\n---\n```\n\n**Use when:** Command should only be manually invoked\n\n## Dynamic Arguments\n\n### Using $ARGUMENTS\n\nCapture all arguments as single string:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Fix issue by number\nargument-hint: [issue-number]\n---\n\nFix issue #$ARGUMENTS following our coding standards and best practices.\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```\n> /fix-issue 123\n> /fix-issue 456\n```\n\n**Expands to:**\n```\nFix issue #123 following our coding standards...\nFix issue #456 following our coding standards...\n```\n\n### Using Positional Arguments\n\nCapture individual arguments with `$1`, `$2`, `$3`, etc.:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Review PR with priority and assignee\nargument-hint: [pr-number] [priority] [assignee]\n---\n\nReview pull request #$1 with priority level $2.\nAfter review, assign to $3 for follow-up.\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```\n> /review-pr 123 high alice\n```\n\n**Expands to:**\n```\nReview pull request #123 with priority level high.\nAfter review, assign to alice for follow-up.\n```\n\n### Combining Arguments\n\nMix positional and remaining arguments:\n\n```markdown\nDeploy $1 to $2 environment with options: $3\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```\n> /deploy api staging --force --skip-tests\n```\n\n**Expands to:**\n```\nDeploy api to staging environment with options: --force --skip-tests\n```\n\n## File References\n\n### Using @ Syntax\n\nInclude file contents in command:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Review specific file\nargument-hint: [file-path]\n---\n\nReview @$1 for:\n- Code quality\n- Best practices\n- Potential bugs\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```\n> /review-file src/api/users.ts\n```\n\n**Effect:** Claude reads `src/api/users.ts` before processing command\n\n### Multiple File References\n\nReference multiple files:\n\n```markdown\nCompare @src/old-version.js with @src/new-version.js\n\nIdentify:\n- Breaking changes\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n```\n\n### Static File References\n\nReference known files without arguments:\n\n```markdown\nReview @package.json and @tsconfig.json for consistency\n\nEnsure:\n- TypeScript version matches\n- Dependencies are aligned\n- Build configuration is correct\n```\n\n## Bash Execution in Commands\n\nCommands can execute bash commands inline to dynamically gather context before Claude processes the command. This is useful for including repository state, environment information, or project-specific context.\n\n**When to use:**\n- Include dynamic context (git status, environment vars, etc.)\n- Gather project/repository state\n- Build context-aware workflows\n\n**Implementation details:**\nFor complete syntax, examples, and best practices, see `references/plugin-features-reference.md` section on bash execution. The reference includes the exact syntax and multiple working examples to avoid execution issues\n\n## Command Organization\n\n### Flat Structure\n\nSimple organization for small command sets:\n\n```\n.claude/commands/\n├── build.md\n├── test.md\n├── deploy.md\n├── review.md\n└── docs.md\n```\n\n**Use when:** 5-15 commands, no clear categories\n\n### Namespaced Structure\n\nOrganize commands in subdirectories:\n\n```\n.claude/commands/\n├── ci/\n│   ├── build.md        # /build (project:ci)\n│   ├── test.md         # /test (project:ci)\n│   └── lint.md         # /lint (project:ci)\n├── git/\n│   ├── commit.md       # /commit (project:git)\n│   └── pr.md           # /pr (project:git)\n└── docs/\n    ├── generate.md     # /generate (project:docs)\n    └── publish.md      # /publish (project:docs)\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Logical grouping by category\n- Namespace shown in `/help`\n- Easier to find related commands\n\n**Use when:** 15+ commands, clear categories\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Command Design\n\n1. **Single responsibility:** One command, one task\n2. **Clear descriptions:** Self-explanatory in `/help`\n3. **Explicit dependencies:** Use `allowed-tools` when needed\n4. **Document arguments:** Always provide `argument-hint`\n5. **Consistent naming:** Use verb-noun pattern (review-pr, fix-issue)\n\n### Argument Handling\n\n1. **Validate arguments:** Check for required arguments in prompt\n2. **Provide defaults:** Suggest defaults when arguments missing\n3. **Document format:** Explain expected argument format\n4. **Handle edge cases:** Consider missing or invalid arguments\n\n```markdown\n---\nargument-hint: [pr-number]\n---\n\n$IF($1,\n  Review PR #$1,\n  Please provide a PR number. Usage: /review-pr [number]\n)\n```\n\n### File References\n\n1. **Explicit paths:** Use clear file paths\n2. **Check existence:** Handle missing files gracefully\n3. **Relative paths:** Use project-relative paths\n4. **Glob support:** Consider using Glob tool for patterns\n\n### Bash Commands\n\n1. **Limit scope:** Use `Bash(git:*)` not `Bash(*)`\n2. **Safe commands:** Avoid destructive operations\n3. **Handle errors:** Consider command failures\n4. **Keep fast:** Long-running commands slow invocation\n\n### Documentation\n\n1. **Add comments:** Explain complex logic\n2. **Provide examples:** Show usage in comments\n3. **List requirements:** Document dependencies\n4. **Version commands:** Note breaking changes\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Deploy application to environment\nargument-hint: [environment] [version]\n---\n\n<!--\nUsage: /deploy [staging|production] [version]\nRequires: AWS credentials configured\nExample: /deploy staging v1.2.3\n-->\n\nDeploy application to $1 environment using version $2...\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Review Pattern\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Review code changes\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash(git:*)\n---\n\nFiles changed: !`git diff --name-only`\n\nReview each file for:\n1. Code quality and style\n2. Potential bugs or issues\n3. Test coverage\n4. Documentation needs\n\nProvide specific feedback for each file.\n```\n\n### Testing Pattern\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Run tests for specific file\nargument-hint: [test-file]\nallowed-tools: Bash(npm:*)\n---\n\nRun tests: !`npm test $1`\n\nAnalyze results and suggest fixes for failures.\n```\n\n### Documentation Pattern\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Generate documentation for file\nargument-hint: [source-file]\n---\n\nGenerate comprehensive documentation for @$1 including:\n- Function/class descriptions\n- Parameter documentation\n- Return value descriptions\n- Usage examples\n- Edge cases and errors\n```\n\n### Workflow Pattern\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Complete PR workflow\nargument-hint: [pr-number]\nallowed-tools: Bash(gh:*), Read\n---\n\nPR #$1 Workflow:\n\n1. Fetch PR: !`gh pr view $1`\n2. Review changes\n3. Run checks\n4. Approve or request changes\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**Command not appearing:**\n- Check file is in correct directory\n- Verify `.md` extension present\n- Ensure valid Markdown format\n- Restart Claude Code\n\n**Arguments not working:**\n- Verify `$1`, `$2` syntax correct\n- Check `argument-hint` matches usage\n- Ensure no extra spaces\n\n**Bash execution failing:**\n- Check `allowed-tools` includes Bash\n- Verify command syntax in backticks\n- Test command in terminal first\n- Check for required permissions\n\n**File references not working:**\n- Verify `@` syntax correct\n- Check file path is valid\n- Ensure Read tool allowed\n- Use absolute or project-relative paths\n\n## Plugin-Specific Features\n\n### CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT Variable\n\nPlugin commands have access to `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`, an environment variable that resolves to the plugin''s absolute path.\n\n**Purpose:**\n- Reference plugin files portably\n- Execute plugin scripts\n- Load plugin configuration\n- Access plugin templates\n\n**Basic usage:**\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Analyze using plugin script\nallowed-tools: Bash(node:*)\n---\n\nRun analysis: !`node ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/analyze.js $1`\n\nReview results and report findings.\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n\n```markdown\n# Execute plugin script\n!`bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/script.sh`\n\n# Load plugin configuration\n@${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/config/settings.json\n\n# Use plugin template\n@${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/templates/report.md\n\n# Access plugin resources\n@${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/reference.md\n```\n\n**Why use it:**\n- Works across all installations\n- Portable between systems\n- No hardcoded paths needed\n- Essential for multi-file plugins\n\n### Plugin Command Organization\n\nPlugin commands discovered automatically from `commands/` directory:\n\n```\nplugin-name/\n├── commands/\n│   ├── foo.md              # /foo (plugin:plugin-name)\n│   ├── bar.md              # /bar (plugin:plugin-name)\n│   └── utils/\n│       └── helper.md       # /helper (plugin:plugin-name:utils)\n└── plugin.json\n```\n\n**Namespace benefits:**\n- Logical command grouping\n- Shown in `/help` output\n- Avoid name conflicts\n- Organize related commands\n\n**Naming conventions:**\n- Use descriptive action names\n- Avoid generic names (test, run)\n- Consider plugin-specific prefix\n- Use hyphens for multi-word names\n\n### Plugin Command Patterns\n\n**Configuration-based pattern:**\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Deploy using plugin configuration\nargument-hint: [environment]\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash(*)\n---\n\nLoad configuration: @${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/config/$1-deploy.json\n\nDeploy to $1 using configuration settings.\nMonitor deployment and report status.\n```\n\n**Template-based pattern:**\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Generate docs from template\nargument-hint: [component]\n---\n\nTemplate: @${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/templates/docs.md\n\nGenerate documentation for $1 following template structure.\n```\n\n**Multi-script pattern:**\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Complete build workflow\nallowed-tools: Bash(*)\n---\n\nBuild: !`bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/build.sh`\nTest: !`bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/test.sh`\nPackage: !`bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/package.sh`\n\nReview outputs and report workflow status.\n```\n\n**See `references/plugin-features-reference.md` for detailed patterns.**\n\n## Integration with Plugin Components\n\nCommands can integrate with other plugin components for powerful workflows.\n\n### Agent Integration\n\nLaunch plugin agents for complex tasks:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Deep code review\nargument-hint: [file-path]\n---\n\nInitiate comprehensive review of @$1 using the code-reviewer agent.\n\nThe agent will analyze:\n- Code structure\n- Security issues\n- Performance\n- Best practices\n\nAgent uses plugin resources:\n- ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/config/rules.json\n- ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/checklists/review.md\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Agent must exist in `plugin/agents/` directory\n- Claude uses Task tool to launch agent\n- Document agent capabilities\n- Reference plugin resources agent uses\n\n### Skill Integration\n\nLeverage plugin skills for specialized knowledge:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Document API with standards\nargument-hint: [api-file]\n---\n\nDocument API in @$1 following plugin standards.\n\nUse the api-docs-standards skill to ensure:\n- Complete endpoint documentation\n- Consistent formatting\n- Example quality\n- Error documentation\n\nGenerate production-ready API docs.\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Skill must exist in `plugin/skills/` directory\n- Mention skill name to trigger invocation\n- Document skill purpose\n- Explain what skill provides\n\n### Hook Coordination\n\nDesign commands that work with plugin hooks:\n- Commands can prepare state for hooks to process\n- Hooks execute automatically on tool events\n- Commands should document expected hook behavior\n- Guide Claude on interpreting hook output\n\nSee `references/plugin-features-reference.md` for examples of commands that coordinate with hooks\n\n### Multi-Component Workflows\n\nCombine agents, skills, and scripts:\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Comprehensive review workflow\nargument-hint: [file]\nallowed-tools: Bash(node:*), Read\n---\n\nTarget: @$1\n\nPhase 1 - Static Analysis:\n!`node ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/lint.js $1`\n\nPhase 2 - Deep Review:\nLaunch code-reviewer agent for detailed analysis.\n\nPhase 3 - Standards Check:\nUse coding-standards skill for validation.\n\nPhase 4 - Report:\nTemplate: @${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/templates/review.md\n\nCompile findings into report following template.\n```\n\n**When to use:**\n- Complex multi-step workflows\n- Leverage multiple plugin capabilities\n- Require specialized analysis\n- Need structured outputs\n\n## Validation Patterns\n\nCommands should validate inputs and resources before processing.\n\n### Argument Validation\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Deploy with validation\nargument-hint: [environment]\n---\n\nValidate environment: !`echo \"$1\" | grep -E \"^(dev|staging|prod)$\" || echo \"INVALID\"`\n\nIf $1 is valid environment:\n  Deploy to $1\nOtherwise:\n  Explain valid environments: dev, staging, prod\n  Show usage: /deploy [environment]\n```\n\n### File Existence Checks\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Process configuration\nargument-hint: [config-file]\n---\n\nCheck file exists: !`test -f $1 && echo \"EXISTS\" || echo \"MISSING\"`\n\nIf file exists:\n  Process configuration: @$1\nOtherwise:\n  Explain where to place config file\n  Show expected format\n  Provide example configuration\n```\n\n### Plugin Resource Validation\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Run plugin analyzer\nallowed-tools: Bash(test:*)\n---\n\nValidate plugin setup:\n- Script: !`test -x ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/analyze && echo \"✓\" || echo \"✗\"`\n- Config: !`test -f ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/config.json && echo \"✓\" || echo \"✗\"`\n\nIf all checks pass, run analysis.\nOtherwise, report missing components.\n```\n\n### Error Handling\n\n```markdown\n---\ndescription: Build with error handling\nallowed-tools: Bash(*)\n---\n\nExecute build: !`bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/build.sh 2>&1 || echo \"BUILD_FAILED\"`\n\nIf build succeeded:\n  Report success and output location\nIf build failed:\n  Analyze error output\n  Suggest likely causes\n  Provide troubleshooting steps\n```\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Validate early in command\n- Provide helpful error messages\n- Suggest corrective actions\n- Handle edge cases gracefully\n\n---\n\nFor detailed frontmatter field specifications, see `references/frontmatter-reference.md`.\nFor plugin-specific features and patterns, see `references/plugin-features-reference.md`.\nFor command pattern examples, see `examples/` directory.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:32:36.152Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing advanced command development and execution capabilities.","zh":"适用于 Claude Code、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 等需要高级命令开发和执行能力的 AI 代理。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChain などの高度なコマンド開発と実行機能が必要な AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클라우드 코드, 오토지피티, 랑체인 등과 같은 고급 명령 개발 및 실행 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan capacidades de desarrollo y ejecución de comandos avanzados.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant des capacités de développement et d''exécution de commandes avancées.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die erweiterte Befehlsentwicklungs- und Ausführungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de desenvolvimento e execução de comandos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих продвинутых возможностей разработки и выполнения команд.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتطوير وتشغيل الأوامر."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create powerful, reusable workflows using Markdown files, YAML frontmatter, and dynamic features like Bash execution and file references, enabling seamless integration with interactive sessions.","zh":"使代理能够使用 Markdown 文件、YAML 前置内容和动态功能（如 Bash 执行和文件引用）创建强大的可重用工作流，从而实现与交互式会话的无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントが Markdown ファイル、YAML フロントマター、および Bash の実行やファイル参照などのダイナミック機能を使用して、強力で再利用可能なワークフローを作成できるようにします。これにより、インタラクティブなセッションとのシームレスな統合が可能になります。","ko":"에이전트가 마크다운 파일, YAML 프론트매터 및 Bash 실행 및 파일 참조와 같은 동적 기능을 사용하여 강력하고 재사용 가능한 워크플로우를 만들 수 있도록 하여 대화형 세션과 무缝하게 통합할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear flujos de trabajo potentes y reutilizables utilizando archivos Markdown, frontmatter YAML y características dinámicas como la ejecución de Bash y referencias de archivos, lo que permite una integración sin problemas con sesiones interactivas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des flux de travail puissants et réutilisables en utilisant des fichiers Markdown, des métadonnées YAML et des fonctionnalités dynamiques comme l''exécution de Bash et les références de fichiers, permettant ainsi une intégration sans problème avec les sessions interactives.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, leistungsstarke und wiederverwendbare Workflows mit Markdown-Dateien, YAML-Frontmatter und dynamischen Funktionen wie Bash-Ausführung und Dateireferenzen zu erstellen, was eine nahtlose Integration mit interaktiven Sitzungen ermöglicht.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem fluxos de trabalho poderosos e reutilizáveis usando arquivos Markdown, frontmatter YAML e recursos dinâmicos como execução Bash e referências de arquivo, permitindo uma integração perfeita com sessões interativas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать мощные, повторно используемые рабочие процессы, используя файлы Markdown, YAML-заголовки и динамические функции, такие как выполнение Bash и ссылки на файлы, обеспечивая бесшовную интеграцию с интерактивными сессиями.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء بإنشاء عمليات عمل قوية ومتجددة باستخدام ملفات Markdown و YAML.frontmatter وميزات ديناميكية مثل تنفيذ Bash ومراجع الملفات، مما يتيح التكامل السلس مع الجلسات التفاعلية."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing custom slash commands for interactive sessions","Creating reusable workflows with dynamic arguments and file references","Organizing and namespacing commands for efficient execution"],"zh":["为交互式会话开发自定义斜杠命令","使用动态参数和文件引用创建可重用工作流","组织和命名空间命令以实现高效执行"],"ja":["インタラクティブなセッション用のカスタムスラッシュコマンドの開発","動的引数とファイル参照を使用した再利用可能なワークフローの作成","コマンドの組織化と名前空間化による効率的な実行"],"ko":["대화형 세션을 위한 사용자 지정 슬래시 명령 개발","동적 인수 및 파일 참조를 사용하여 재사용 가능한 워크플로우 생성","명령의 조직 및 네임스페이싱을 통한 효율적인 실행"],"es":["Desarrollar comandos personalizados de barra para sesiones interactivas","Crear flujos de trabajo reutilizables con argumentos dinámicos y referencias de archivos","Organizar y espaciar comandos para una ejecución eficiente"],"fr":["Développer des commandes de barre personnalisées pour les sessions interactives","Créer des flux de travail réutilisables avec des arguments dynamiques et des références de fichiers","Organiser et espacer les commandes pour une exécution efficace"],"de":["Benutzerdefinierte Schrägstrichbefehle für interaktive Sitzungen entwickeln","Wiederverwendbare Workflows mit dynamischen Argumenten und Dateireferenzen erstellen","Befehle organisieren und namensspezifisch für eine effiziente Ausführung"],"pt":["Desenvolver comandos personalizados de barra para sessões interativas","Criar fluxos de trabalho reutilizáveis com argumentos dinâmicos e referências de arquivo","Organizar e criar namespaces para comandos para execução eficiente"],"ru":["Разработка пользовательских команд с баром для интерактивных сессий","Создание повторно используемых рабочих процессов с динамическими аргументами и ссылками на файлы","Организация и создание пространств имен для команд для эффективного выполнения"],"ar":["تطوير أوامر مخصصة للشريط لجلسات التفاعل","إنشاء عمليات عمل متجددة مع حجة ديناميكية ومراجع الملفات","تنظيم وتسمية مساحات للأوامر من أجل التنفيذ الفعال"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Markdown file format and YAML frontmatter","Dependent on Bash execution for context","Specific to Claude Code and similar AI agents"],"zh":["需要了解 Markdown 文件格式和 YAML 前置内容","依赖于 Bash 执行上下文","特定于 Claude Code 和类似的 AI 代理"],"ja":["Markdown ファイル形式と YAML フロントマターの理解が必要","Bash の実行上下文に依存","Claude Code や同等の AI エージェントに特有"],"ko":["마크다운 파일 형식 및 YAML 프론트매터에 대한 이해가 필요","Bash 실행 컨텍스트에 의존","클라우드 코드 또는 유사한 AI 에이전트에 특정"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del formato de archivo Markdown y del frontmatter YAML","Dependiente de la ejecución de Bash para el contexto","Específico para Claude Code y agentes de IA similares"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du format de fichier Markdown et des métadonnées YAML","Dépendant de l''exécution de Bash pour le contexte","Spécifique à Claude Code et aux agents IA similaires"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für das Markdown-Dateiformat und YAML-Frontmatter","Von der Bash-Ausführung für den Kontext abhängig","Spezifisch für Claude Code und ähnliche KI-Agents"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento do formato de arquivo Markdown e frontmatter YAML","Dependente da execução Bash para contexto","Específico para Claude Code e agentes de IA semelhantes"],"ru":["Требует понимания формата файла Markdown и YAML-заголовков","Зависит от выполнения Bash для контекста","Конкретно для Claude Code и аналогичных агентов ИИ"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم صيغة ملف Markdown و YAML.frontmatter","يعتمد على تنفيذ Bash للسياق","محدد لعميل Claude Code والوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المماثلين"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
