Hell-/Dunkel-Themenwechsel mit benutzerdefinierten CSS-Eigenschaften","Erstellung von Multi-Brand-Themen-Systemen","Architektur von Komponentenbibliotheken mit konsistenten APIs","Einrichtung von Design-to-Code-Workflows mit Figma-Tokens","Erstellung von semantischen Komponenten"],"pt":["Criação de tokens de design para cores, tipografia e espaçamento","Implementação de tema claro/escuro com propriedades personalizadas do CSS","Criação de sistemas de temas multi-marca","Arquitetura de bibliotecas de componentes com APIs consistentes","Estabelecimento de fluxos de trabalho de design para código com tokens do Figma","Criação de componentes semânticos"],"ru":["Создание токенов дизайна для цветов, типографики и расстояния","Реализация светлой/тёмной темы с помощью пользовательских свойств CSS","Создание систем тем для нескольких брендов","Архитектура библиотек компонентов с последовательными API","Установление рабочих процессов дизайна для кода с помощью токенов Figma","Создание семантических компонентов"],"ar":["إنشاء رموز التصميم للألوان والطباعة والنسيج","تنفيذ موضوع 明/غامق باستخدام خصائص مخصصة لل CSS","إنشاء أنظمة موضوعات متعددة العلامات التجارية","هندسة مكتبات المكونات مع واجهات برمجة تطبيقات متسقة","إنشاء سير عمل التصميم إلى الكود باستخدام رموز Figma","إنشاء مكونات دلالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["设计系统模式","UI基础","设计令牌","主题切换","多品牌主题","设计到代码","语义化UI"],"ja":["デザインシステムパターン","UI基盤","デザイントークン","テーマ切り替え","マルチブランドテーマ","デザインからコード","セマンティックなUI"],"ko":["디자인 시스템 패턴","UI 기초","디자인 토큰","테마 전환","멀티브랜드 테마","디자인에서 코드","시맨틱한 UI"],"es":["patrones de sistema de diseño","diseño de UI","desarrollo web","desarrollo móvil","tokens de diseño","temas claros y oscuros","bibliotecas de componentes","flujos de trabajo de diseño a código"],"fr":["modèles de système de conception","conception d''UI","développement web","développement mobile","jetons de conception","thèmes clairs et sombres","bibliothèques de composants","flux de travail de conception à code"],"de":["Design-System-Muster","UI-Design","Webentwicklung","Mobile-Entwicklung","Design-Tokens","Hell-/Dunkel-Themen","Komponentenbibliotheken","Design-to-Code-Workflows"],"pt":["padrões de sistema de design","tokens de design","tema claro/escuro","sistemas de temas multi-marca","bibliotecas de componentes","fluxos de trabalho de design para código","desenvolvimento de interfaces de usuário","arquitetura de UI","desenvolvimento web","desenvolvimento móvel"],"ru":["шаблоны системы дизайна","токены дизайна","светлая/тёмная тема","системы тем для нескольких брендов","библиотеки компонентов","рабочие процессы дизайна для кода","разработка интерфейсов пользователя","архитектура UI","веб-разработка","мобильная разработка"],"ar":["نماذج نظام التصميم","رموز التصميم","موضوع 明/غامق","أنظمة موضوعات متعددة العلامات التجارية","مكتبات المكونات","سير عمل التصميم إلى الكود","تطوير واجهة المستخدم","هندسة واجهة المستخدم","تطوير الويب","تطوير الهاتف المحمول"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.531Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"design-system-patterns","description":"Build scalable design systems with design tokens, theming infrastructure, and component architecture patterns. Use when creating design tokens, implementing theme switching, building component libraries, or establishing design system foundations.","bodyPreview":"# Design System Patterns\n\nMaster design system architecture to create consistent, maintainable, and scalable UI foundations across web and mobile applications.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating design tokens for colors, typography, spacing, and shadows\n- Implementing light/dark theme switching with CSS custom properties\n- Building multi-brand theming systems\n- Architecting component libraries with consistent APIs\n- Establishing design-to-code workflows with Figma tokens\n- Creating semantic","body":"# Design System Patterns\n\nMaster design system architecture to create consistent, maintainable, and scalable UI foundations across web and mobile applications.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating design tokens for colors, typography, spacing, and shadows\n- Implementing light/dark theme switching with CSS custom properties\n- Building multi-brand theming systems\n- Architecting component libraries with consistent APIs\n- Establishing design-to-code workflows with Figma tokens\n- Creating semantic token hierarchies (primitive, semantic, component)\n- Setting up design system documentation and guidelines\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. Design Tokens\n\n- Primitive tokens (raw values: colors, sizes, fonts)\n- Semantic tokens (contextual meaning: text-primary, surface-elevated)\n- Component tokens (specific usage: button-bg, card-border)\n- Token naming conventions and organization\n- Multi-platform token generation (CSS, iOS, Android)\n\n### 2. Theming Infrastructure\n\n- CSS custom properties architecture\n- Theme context providers in React\n- Dynamic theme switching\n- System preference detection (prefers-color-scheme)\n- Persistent theme storage\n- Reduced motion and high contrast modes\n\n### 3. Component Architecture\n\n- Compound component patterns\n- Polymorphic components (as prop)\n- Variant and size systems\n- Slot-based composition\n- Headless UI patterns\n- Style props and responsive variants\n\n### 4. Token Pipeline\n\n- Figma to code synchronization\n- Style Dictionary configuration\n- Token transformation and formatting\n- CI/CD integration for token updates\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\n// Design tokens with CSS custom properties\nconst tokens = {\n  colors: {\n    // Primitive tokens\n    gray: {\n      50: \"#fafafa\",\n      100: \"#f5f5f5\",\n      900: \"#171717\",\n    },\n    blue: {\n      500: \"#3b82f6\",\n      600: \"#2563eb\",\n    },\n  },\n  // Semantic tokens (reference primitives)\n  semantic: {\n    light: {\n      \"text-primary\": \"var(--color-gray-900)\",\n      \"text-secondary\": \"var(--color-gray-600)\",\n      \"surface-default\": \"var(--color-white)\",\n      \"surface-elevated\": \"var(--color-gray-50)\",\n      \"border-default\": \"var(--color-gray-200)\",\n      \"interactive-primary\": \"var(--color-blue-500)\",\n    },\n    dark: {\n      \"text-primary\": \"var(--color-gray-50)\",\n      \"text-secondary\": \"var(--color-gray-400)\",\n      \"surface-default\": \"var(--color-gray-900)\",\n      \"surface-elevated\": \"var(--color-gray-800)\",\n      \"border-default\": \"var(--color-gray-700)\",\n      \"interactive-primary\": \"var(--color-blue-400)\",\n    },\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Token Hierarchy\n\n```css\n/* Layer 1: Primitive tokens (raw values) */\n:root {\n  --color-blue-500: #3b82f6;\n  --color-blue-600: #2563eb;\n  --color-gray-50: #fafafa;\n  --color-gray-900: #171717;\n\n  --space-1: 0.25rem;\n  --space-2: 0.5rem;\n  --space-4: 1rem;\n\n  --font-size-sm: 0.875rem;\n  --font-size-base: 1rem;\n  --font-size-lg: 1.125rem;\n\n  --radius-sm: 0.25rem;\n  --radius-md: 0.5rem;\n  --radius-lg: 1rem;\n}\n\n/* Layer 2: Semantic tokens (meaning) */\n:root {\n  --text-primary: var(--color-gray-900);\n  --text-secondary: var(--color-gray-600);\n  --surface-default: white;\n  --interactive-primary: var(--color-blue-500);\n  --interactive-primary-hover: var(--color-blue-600);\n}\n\n/* Layer 3: Component tokens (specific usage) */\n:root {\n  --button-bg: var(--interactive-primary);\n  --button-bg-hover: var(--interactive-primary-hover);\n  --button-text: white;\n  --button-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  --button-padding-x: var(--space-4);\n  --button-padding-y: var(--space-2);\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Theme Switching with React\n\n```tsx\nimport { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState } from \"react\";\n\ntype Theme = \"light\" | \"dark\" | \"system\";\n\ninterface ThemeContextValue {\n  theme: Theme;\n  resolvedTheme: \"light\" | \"dark\";\n  setTheme: (theme: Theme) => void;\n}\n\nconst ThemeContext = createContext<ThemeContextValue | null>(null);\n\nexport function ThemeProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const [theme, setTheme] = useState<Theme>(() => {\n    if (typeof window !== \"undefined\") {\n      return (localStorage.getItem(\"theme\") as Theme) || \"system\";\n    }\n    return \"system\";\n  });\n\n  const [resolvedTheme, setResolvedTheme] = useState<\"light\" | \"dark\">(\"light\");\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const root = document.documentElement;\n\n    const applyTheme = (isDark: boolean) => {\n      root.classList.remove(\"light\", \"dark\");\n      root.classList.add(isDark ? \"dark\" : \"light\");\n      setResolvedTheme(isDark ? \"dark\" : \"light\");\n    };\n\n    if (theme === \"system\") {\n      const mediaQuery = window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\");\n      applyTheme(mediaQuery.matches);\n\n      const handler = (e: MediaQueryListEvent) => applyTheme(e.matches);\n      mediaQuery.addEventListener(\"change\", handler);\n      return () => mediaQuery.removeEventListener(\"change\", handler);\n    } else {\n      applyTheme(theme === \"dark\");\n    }\n  }, [theme]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    localStorage.setItem(\"theme\", theme);\n  }, [theme]);\n\n  return (\n    <ThemeContext.Provider value={{ theme, resolvedTheme, setTheme }}>\n      {children}\n    </ThemeContext.Provider>\n  );\n}\n\nexport const useTheme = () => {\n  const context = useContext(ThemeContext);\n  if (!context) throw new Error(\"useTheme must be used within ThemeProvider\");\n  return context;\n};\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Variant System with CVA\n\n```tsx\nimport { cva, type VariantProps } from \"class-variance-authority\";\nimport { cn } from \"@/lib/utils\";\n\nconst buttonVariants = cva(\n  // Base styles\n  \"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md font-medium transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50\",\n  {\n    variants: {\n      variant: {\n        default: \"bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90\",\n        destructive:\n          \"bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground hover:bg-destructive/90\",\n        outline:\n          \"border border-input bg-background hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground\",\n        secondary:\n          \"bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80\",\n        ghost: \"hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground\",\n        link: \"text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline\",\n      },\n      size: {\n        sm: \"h-9 px-3 text-sm\",\n        md: \"h-10 px-4 text-sm\",\n        lg: \"h-11 px-8 text-base\",\n        icon: \"h-10 w-10\",\n      },\n    },\n    defaultVariants: {\n      variant: \"default\",\n      size: \"md\",\n    },\n  },\n);\n\ninterface ButtonProps\n  extends\n    React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>,\n    VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> {\n  asChild?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport function Button({ className, variant, size, ...props }: ButtonProps) {\n  return (\n    <button\n      className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size, className }))}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Style Dictionary Configuration\n\n```javascript\n// style-dictionary.config.js\nmodule.exports = {\n  source: [\"tokens/**/*.json\"],\n  platforms: {\n    css: {\n      transformGroup: \"css\",\n      buildPath: \"dist/css/\",\n      files: [\n        {\n          destination: \"variables.css\",\n          format: \"css/variables\",\n          options: {\n            outputReferences: true, // Preserve token references\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n    scss: {\n      transformGroup: \"scss\",\n      buildPath: \"dist/scss/\",\n      files: [\n        {\n          destination: \"_variables.scss\",\n          format: \"scss/variables\",\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n    ios: {\n      transformGroup: \"ios-swift\",\n      buildPath: \"dist/ios/\",\n      files: [\n        {\n          destination: \"DesignTokens.swift\",\n          format: \"ios-swift/class.swift\",\n          className: \"DesignTokens\",\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n    android: {\n      transformGroup: \"android\",\n      buildPath: \"dist/android/\",\n      files: [\n        {\n          destination: \"colors.xml\",\n          format: \"android/colors\",\n          filter: { attributes: { category: \"color\" } },\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Name Tokens by Purpose**: Use semantic names (text-primary) not visual descriptions (dark-gray)\n2. **Maintain Token Hierarchy**: Primitives > Semantic > Component tokens\n3. **Document Token Usage**: Include usage guidelines with token definitions\n4. **Version Tokens**: Treat token changes as API changes with semver\n5. **Test Theme Combinations**: Verify all themes work with all components\n6. **Automate Token Pipeline**: CI/CD for Figma-to-code synchronization\n7. **Provide Migration Paths**: Deprecate tokens gradually with clear alternatives\n\n## Common Issues\n\n- **Token Sprawl**: Too many tokens without clear hierarchy\n- **Inconsistent Naming**: Mixed conventions (camelCase vs kebab-case)\n- **Missing Dark Mode**: Tokens that don''t adapt to theme changes\n- **Hardcoded Values**: Using raw values instead of tokens\n- **Circular References**: Tokens referencing each other in loops\n- **Platform Gaps**: Tokens missing for some platforms (web but not mobile)\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Style Dictionary Documentation](https://amzn.github.io/style-dictionary/)\n- [Tokens Studio for Figma](https://tokens.studio/)\n- [Design Tokens W3C Spec](https://design-tokens.github.io/community-group/format/)\n- [Radix UI Themes](https://www.radix-ui.com/themes)\n- [shadcn/ui Theming](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/theming)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:43:32.610Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents needing to master design system architecture for consistent and scalable UI foundations across web and mobile applications.","zh":"适合需要掌握设计系统架构以实现网页和移动应用中一致且可扩展的UI基础的前端代理。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントがデザインシステムアーキテクチャをマスターして、Webおよびモバイルアプリケーションにわたる一貫性とスケーラビリティのあるUI基盤を実現するために最適です。","ko":"프론트엔드 에이전트가 일관성 있고 확장 가능한 UI 기초를 웹과 모바일 애플리케이션에 걸쳐 실현하기 위해 디자인 시스템 아키텍처를 마스터해야 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes frontend que necesitan dominar la arquitectura del sistema de diseño para fundamentos de IU consistentes y escalables en aplicaciones web y móviles.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents frontend qui doivent maîtriser l''architecture du système de conception pour des fondements d''UI cohérents et évolutifs dans les applications web et mobiles.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agents, die die Architektur des Designsystems beherrschen müssen, um konsistente und skalierbare UI-Grundlagen über Web- und Mobile-Anwendungen hinweg zu schaffen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Frontend que precisam dominar a arquitetura de sistema de design para fundamentos de UI consistentes e escaláveis em aplicativos web e móveis.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым необходимо освоить архитектуру системы дизайна для последовательных и масштабируемых основ интерфейса пользователя в веб- и мобильных приложениях.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأمامي الذين يحتاجون إلى التمكن من بنية نظام التصميم لتأسيس واجهة المستخدم المتماثلة والقابلة للتوسيع عبر تطبيقات الويب والجوال."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create consistent design tokens for colors, typography, spacing, and shadows, and implement light/dark theme switching with CSS custom properties, while architecting component libraries with consistent APIs using Figma tokens and semantic design principles.","zh":"赋予代理创建一致的设计令牌以用于颜色、排版、间距和阴影，并使用CSS自定义属性实现浅色/深色主题切换，同时使用Figma令牌和语义设计原则架构具有一致API的组件库。","ja":"エージェントが色、タイポグラフィ、スペーシング、影などの一貫したデザイントークンを作成し、CSSカスタムプロパティを使用してライト/ダークテーマの切り替えを実装し、Figmaトークンとセマンティックデザイン原則を使用して一貫したAPIを持つコンポーネントライブラリを構築することを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 색상, 타이포그래피, 간격, 그림자 등 일관된 디자인 토큰을 생성하고 CSS 커스텀 속성을 사용하여 라이트/다크 테마 전환을 구현하며 Figma 토큰과 의미론적 디자인 원칙을 사용하여 일관된 API를 갖는 컴포넌트 라이브러리를 아키텍처하는 것을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear tokens de diseño consistentes para colores, tipografía, espaciado y sombras, e implementar la conmutación de temas claros/oscuros con propiedades personalizadas de CSS, mientras arquitectan bibliotecas de componentes con API consistentes utilizando tokens de Figma y principios de diseño semántico.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des jetons de conception cohérents pour les couleurs, la typographie, l''espacement et les ombres, et de mettre en œuvre la commutation de thème clair/sombre avec des propriétés CSS personnalisées, tout en architecturant des bibliothèques de composants avec des API cohérentes en utilisant des jetons Figma et des principes de conception sémantique.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, konsistente Design-Tokens für Farben, Typografie, Abstände und Schatten zu erstellen und das Umschalten zwischen hellen und dunklen Designs mit benutzerdefinierten CSS-Eigenschaften zu implementieren, während sie Komponentenbibliotheken mit konsistenten APIs mithilfe von Figma-Tokens und semantischen Designprinzipien architektonisch gestalten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar tokens de design consistentes para cores, tipografia, espaçamento e sombras, e implementar a troca de tema claro/escuro com propriedades personalizadas do CSS, ao mesmo tempo em que arquitetam bibliotecas de componentes com APIs consistentes usando tokens do Figma e princípios de design semântico.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать последовательные токены дизайна для цветов, типографики,间距 и теней, и реализовывать переключение светлой/темной темы с помощью пользовательских свойств CSS, одновременно проектируя библиотеки компонентов с последовательными API с использованием токенов Figma и семантических принципов дизайна.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء رموز تصميم متسقة للألوان والتنسيق والتباعد والظلال، وتطبيق تبديل التحكم في الإضاءة مع خصائص CSS المخصصة، مع بناء مكتبات المكونات ذات واجهات برمجة التطبيقات المتسقة باستخدام رموز Figma ومبادئ التصميم الدلالي."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating design tokens for multi-brand theming systems","Implementing design-to-code workflows with Figma tokens and CSS custom properties","Architecting component libraries with consistent APIs for scalable UI foundations","Building semantic and accessible UI components"],"zh":["为多品牌主题系统创建设计令牌","使用Figma令牌和CSS自定义属性实现设计到代码工作流","使用一致的API架构组件库以实现可扩展的UI基础","构建语义和可访问的UI组件"],"ja":["マルチブランドテーマシステムのためのデザイントークンの作成","FigmaトークンとCSSカスタムプロパティを使用したデザインからコードへのワークフローの実装","一貫したAPIを持つコンポーネントライブラリの構築によるスケーラブルなUI基盤の実現","セマンティックでアクセス可能なUIコンポーネントの構築"],"ko":["다중 브랜드 테마 시스템을 위한 디자인 토큰 생성","Figma 토큰 및 CSS 커스텀 속성을 사용한 디자인에서 코드로의 워크플로우 구현","일관된 API를 갖는 컴포넌트 라이브러리의 아키텍처를 통한 확장 가능한 UI 기초 구현","의미론적이고 접근 가능한 UI 컴포넌트 구축"],"es":["Creación de tokens de diseño para sistemas de temas multi-marca","Implementación de flujos de trabajo de diseño a código con tokens de Figma y propiedades personalizadas de CSS","Arquitectura de bibliotecas de componentes con API consistentes para fundamentos de IU escalables","Creación de componentes de IU semánticos y accesibles"],"fr":["Création de jetons de conception pour les systèmes de thème multi-marque","Mise en œuvre de flux de travail de conception à code avec des jetons Figma et des propriétés CSS personnalisées","Architecture de bibliothèques de composants avec des API cohérentes pour des fondements d''UI évolutifs","Création de composants d''UI sémantiques et accessibles"],"de":["Erstellung von Design-Tokens für Multi-Brand-Themen-Systeme","Implementierung von Design-to-Code-Workflows mit Figma-Tokens und benutzerdefinierten CSS-Eigenschaften","Architektur von Komponentenbibliotheken mit konsistenten APIs für skalierbare UI-Grundlagen","Erstellung semantischer und zugänglicher UI-Komponenten"],"pt":["Criar tokens de design para sistemas de tema multi-marca","Implementar fluxos de trabalho de design-para-código com tokens do Figma e propriedades personalizadas do CSS","Arquitetar bibliotecas de componentes com APIs consistentes para fundamentos de UI escaláveis","Construir componentes de UI semânticos e acessíveis"],"ru":["Создание токенов дизайна для систем темы multi-бренда","Реализация потоков работы дизайн-в-код с токенами Figma и пользовательскими свойствами CSS","Проектирование библиотек компонентов с последовательными API для масштабируемых основ интерфейса пользователя","Создание семантических и доступных компонентов интерфейса пользователя"],"ar":["إنشاء رموز التصميم لأنظمة التهيئة متعددة العلامات التجارية","تطبيق سير عمل التصميم-إلى-البرمجية مع رموز Figma وخصائص CSS المخصصة","بناء مكتبات المكونات ذات واجهات برمجة التطبيقات المتسقة لتأسيس واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتوسيع","بناء مكونات واجهة المستخدم الدلالية والقابلة للوصول"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of CSS custom properties and Figma tokens","Limited to design system architecture and UI foundations","May require additional tools for full design-to-code workflow implementation"],"zh":["需要CSS自定义属性和Figma令牌的知识","仅限于设计系统架构和UI基础","可能需要额外的工具来实现完整的设计到代码工作流"],"ja":["CSSカスタムプロパティとFigmaトークンの知識が必要","デザインシステムアーキテクチャとUI基盤に限定される","完全なデザインからコードへのワークフローの実装には追加のツールが必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["CSS 커스텀 속성 및 Figma 토큰에 대한 지식이 필요","디자인 시스템 아키텍처 및 UI 기초에만 محدود됨","전체 디자인에서 코드로의 워크플로우 구현에는 추가 도구가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de propiedades personalizadas de CSS y tokens de Figma","Limitado a la arquitectura del sistema de diseño y fundamentos de IU","Puede requerir herramientas adicionales para la implementación completa del flujo de trabajo de diseño a código"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en propriétés CSS personnalisées et en jetons Figma","Limité à l''architecture du système de conception et aux fondements d''UI","Peut nécessiter des outils supplémentaires pour la mise en œuvre complète du flux de travail de conception à code"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von benutzerdefinierten CSS-Eigenschaften und Figma-Tokens","Begrenzt auf die Architektur des Designsystems und die UI-Grundlagen","Kann zusätzliche Tools für die vollständige Implementierung des Design-to-Code-Workflows erfordern"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de propriedades personalizadas do CSS e tokens do Figma","Limitado à arquitetura de sistema de design e fundamentos de UI","Pode requerer ferramentas adicionais para implementação completa do fluxo de trabalho de design-para-código"],"ru":["Требуется знание пользовательских свойств CSS и токенов Figma","Ограничен архитектурой системы дизайна и основами интерфейса пользователя","Может потребовать дополнительных инструментов для полной реализации потока работы дизайн-в-код"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة خصائص CSS المخصصة ورموز Figma","محدود ببنية نظام التصميم وتأسيس واجهة المستخدم","يمكن أن يتطلب أدوات إضافية لتنفيذ كامل لسير عمل التصميم-إلى-البرمجية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/postgresql-table-design', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'postgresql-table-design', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.531Z', '2026-02-18T14:43:23.347Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/postgresql-table-design","name":"postgresql-table-design","description":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计是数据库性能和可维护性的关键。通过定义主键、 normalization 和 denormalization 来优化您的表设计","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計はデータベースのパフォーマンスとメンテナンス性を決定づける重要な要素です。主キー、正規化、非正規化を使用してテーブル設計を最適化します","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인은 데이터베이스 성능과 유지 보수의 핵심입니다. 기본 키, 정규화 및 비정규화를 사용하여 테이블 디자인을 최적화합니다","es":"El diseño de tablas en PostgreSQL es crucial para el rendimiento y la escalabilidad de la base de datos. Aprende a hacerlo de manera efectiva.","fr":"La conception de tables dans PostgreSQL est cruciale pour les performances et la scalabilité de la base de données. Découvrez comment le faire de manière efficace.","de":"Das Tabellendesign in PostgreSQL ist entscheidend für die Leistung und Skalierbarkeit der Datenbank. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es effektiv tun können.","pt":"O desenho de tabelas PostgreSQL é fundamental para o desempenho e a manutenção de bancos de dados. Aqui estão as melhores práticas","ru":"Проектирование таблиц PostgreSQL имеет важное значение для производительности и обслуживания баз данных. Лучшие практики","ar":"تصميم جداول PostgreSQL أساسي للأداء وضمان سلامة قواعد البيانات. هنا أفضل الممارسات","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计最佳实践","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計のベストプラクティス","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인 가이드","es":"Diseño de Tablas PostgreSQL: Mejores Prácticas","fr":"Conception de Tables PostgreSQL: Bonnes Pratiques","de":"PostgreSQL-Tabellendesign: Best Practices","pt":"Desenho de Tabela PostgreSQL: Melhores Práticas","ru":"Проектирование таблиц PostgreSQL: Лучшие практики","ar":"تصميم جدول PostgreSQL: أفضل الممارسات","en":"postgresql-table-design"},"description":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计是数据库性能和可维护性的关键。通过定义主键、 normalization 和 denormalization 来优化您的表设计","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計はデータベースのパフォーマンスとメンテナンス性を決定づける重要な要素です。主キー、正規化、非正規化を使用してテーブル設計を最適化します","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인은 데이터베이스 성능과 유지 보수의 핵심입니다. 기본 키, 정규화 및 비정규화를 사용하여 테이블 디자인을 최적화합니다","es":"El diseño de tablas en PostgreSQL es crucial para el rendimiento y la escalabilidad de la base de datos. Aprende a hacerlo de manera efectiva.","fr":"La conception de tables dans PostgreSQL est cruciale pour les performances et la scalabilité de la base de données. Découvrez comment le faire de manière eff...","de":"Das Tabellendesign in PostgreSQL ist entscheidend für die Leistung und Skalierbarkeit der Datenbank. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es effektiv tun können.","pt":"O desenho de tabelas PostgreSQL é fundamental para o desempenho e a manutenção de bancos de dados. Aqui estão as melhores práticas","ru":"Проектирование таблиц PostgreSQL имеет важное значение для производительности и обслуживания баз данных. Лучшие практики","ar":"تصميم جداول PostgreSQL أساسي للأداء وضمان سلامة قواعد البيانات. هنا أفضل الممارسات","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["定义主键"," normalization 和 denormalization","优化表设计","提高性能","改善可维护性"],"ja":["主キーを定義する","正規化と非正規化","テーブル設計を最適化する","パフォーマンスを向上させる","メンテナンス性を向上させる"],"ko":["기본 키 정의","정규화 및 비정규화","테이블 디자인 최적화","성능 향상","유지 보수 향상"],"es":["Definir claves primarias para tablas de referencia","Normalizar datos para eliminar redundancias","Denormalizar solo cuando sea necesario para mejorar el rendimiento","Utilizar BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY para claves primarias","Utilizar UUID solo cuando se requiera unicidad global"],"fr":["Définir des clés primaires pour les tables de référence","Normaliser les données pour éliminer les redondances","Dénormaliser uniquement lorsque cela est nécessaire pour améliorer les performances","Utiliser BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY pour les clés primaires","Utiliser UUID uniquement lorsque l''unicité globale est requise"],"de":["Definieren von Primärschlüsseln für Referenztabelle","Normalisieren von Daten, um Redundanz zu eliminieren","Denormalisieren nur, wenn dies notwendig ist, um die Leistung zu verbessern","Verwenden von BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY für Primärschlüssel","Verwenden von UUID nur, wenn globale Eindeutigkeit erforderlich ist"],"pt":["Definição de chave primária","Normalização para eliminar redundância de dados","Denormalização para melhorar o desempenho de leitura","Uso de BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","Uso de UUID para garantir unicidade global","Otimização do desempenho de join"],"ru":["Определение первичного ключа","Нормализация для исключения избыточности данных","Денормализация для улучшения производительности чтения","Использование BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","Использование UUID для обеспечения глобальной уникальности","Оптимизация производительности соединений"],"ar":["تحديد المفتاح الأساسي","التطبيع لتقليل التكرار البيانات","الغير تطبيع لتحسين أداء القراءة","استخدام BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","استخدام UUID لضمان الفردية العالمية","تحسين أداء الانضمام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PostgreSQL 表设计","数据库性能","可维护性","主键"," normalization","denormalization"],"ja":["PostgreSQL テーブル設計","データベースのパフォーマンス","メンテナンス性","主キー","正規化","非正規化"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인","데이터베이스 성능","유지 보수","기본 키","정규화","비정규화"],"es":["diseño de tablas postgresql","mejores prácticas postgresql","normalización de datos","denormalización de datos","claves primarias postgresql","uuid en postgresql"],"fr":["conception de tables postgresql","bonnes pratiques postgresql","normalisation de données","dénormalisation de données","clés primaires postgresql","uuid dans postgresql"],"de":["tabellendesign postgresql","best practices postgresql","datennormalisierung","datendenormalisierung","primärschlüssel postgresql","uuid in postgresql"],"pt":["desenho de tabela postgresql","normalização de dados","denormalização de dados","chave primária","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","otimização de desempenho","banco de dados relacional","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["проектирование таблиц postgresql","нормализация данных","денормализация данных","первичный ключ","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","оптимизация производительности","реляционная база данных","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تصميم جدول postgresql","تطبيع البيانات","الغير تطبيع البيانات","المفتاح الأساسي","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","تحسين الأداء","قاعدة بيانات متعلقة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.531Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"postgresql-table-design","description":"Design a PostgreSQL-specific schema. Covers best-practices, data types, indexing, constraints, performance patterns, and advanced features","bodyPreview":"# PostgreSQL Table Design\n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenanc","body":"# PostgreSQL Table Design\n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenance burden.\n- Add **NOT NULL** everywhere it’s semantically required; use **DEFAULT**s for common values.\n- Create **indexes for access paths you actually query**: PK/unique (auto), **FK columns (manual!)**, frequent filters/sorts, and join keys.\n- Prefer **TIMESTAMPTZ** for event time; **NUMERIC** for money; **TEXT** for strings; **BIGINT** for integer values, **DOUBLE PRECISION** for floats (or `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic).\n\n## PostgreSQL “Gotchas”\n\n- **Identifiers**: unquoted → lowercased. Avoid quoted/mixed-case names. Convention: use `snake_case` for table/column names.\n- **Unique + NULLs**: UNIQUE allows multiple NULLs. Use `UNIQUE (...) NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+) to restrict to one NULL.\n- **FK indexes**: PostgreSQL **does not** auto-index FK columns. Add them.\n- **No silent coercions**: length/precision overflows error out (no truncation). Example: inserting 999 into `NUMERIC(2,0)` fails with error, unlike some databases that silently truncate or round.\n- **Sequences/identity have gaps** (normal; don''t \"fix\"). Rollbacks, crashes, and concurrent transactions create gaps in ID sequences (1, 2, 5, 6...). This is expected behavior—don''t try to make IDs consecutive.\n- **Heap storage**: no clustered PK by default (unlike SQL Server/MySQL InnoDB); `CLUSTER` is one-off reorganization, not maintained on subsequent inserts. Row order on disk is insertion order unless explicitly clustered.\n- **MVCC**: updates/deletes leave dead tuples; vacuum handles them—design to avoid hot wide-row churn.\n\n## Data Types\n\n- **IDs**: `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` preferred (`GENERATED BY DEFAULT` also fine); `UUID` when merging/federating/used in a distributed system or for opaque IDs. Generate with `uuidv7()` (preferred if using PG18+) or `gen_random_uuid()` (if using an older PG version).\n- **Integers**: prefer `BIGINT` unless storage space is critical; `INTEGER` for smaller ranges; avoid `SMALLINT` unless constrained.\n- **Floats**: prefer `DOUBLE PRECISION` over `REAL` unless storage space is critical. Use `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic.\n- **Strings**: prefer `TEXT`; if length limits needed, use `CHECK (LENGTH(col) <= n)` instead of `VARCHAR(n)`; avoid `CHAR(n)`. Use `BYTEA` for binary data. Large strings/binary (>2KB default threshold) automatically stored in TOAST with compression. TOAST storage: `PLAIN` (no TOAST), `EXTENDED` (compress + out-of-line), `EXTERNAL` (out-of-line, no compress), `MAIN` (compress, keep in-line if possible). Default `EXTENDED` usually optimal. Control with `ALTER TABLE tbl ALTER COLUMN col SET STORAGE strategy` and `ALTER TABLE tbl SET (toast_tuple_target = 4096)` for threshold. Case-insensitive: for locale/accent handling use non-deterministic collations; for plain ASCII use expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` (preferred unless column needs case-insensitive PK/FK/UNIQUE) or `CITEXT`.\n- **Money**: `NUMERIC(p,s)` (never float).\n- **Time**: `TIMESTAMPTZ` for timestamps; `DATE` for date-only; `INTERVAL` for durations. Avoid `TIMESTAMP` (without timezone). Use `now()` for transaction start time, `clock_timestamp()` for current wall-clock time.\n- **Booleans**: `BOOLEAN` with `NOT NULL` constraint unless tri-state values are required.\n- **Enums**: `CREATE TYPE ... AS ENUM` for small, stable sets (e.g. US states, days of week). For business-logic-driven and evolving values (e.g. order statuses) → use TEXT (or INT) + CHECK or lookup table.\n- **Arrays**: `TEXT[]`, `INTEGER[]`, etc. Use for ordered lists where you query elements. Index with **GIN** for containment (`@>`, `<@`) and overlap (`&&`) queries. Access: `arr[1]` (1-indexed), `arr[1:3]` (slicing). Good for tags, categories; avoid for relations—use junction tables instead. Literal syntax: `''{val1,val2}''` or `ARRAY[val1,val2]`.\n- **Range types**: `daterange`, `numrange`, `tstzrange` for intervals. Support overlap (`&&`), containment (`@>`), operators. Index with **GiST**. Good for scheduling, versioning, numeric ranges. Pick a bounds scheme and use it consistently; prefer `[)` (inclusive/exclusive) by default.\n- **Network types**: `INET` for IP addresses, `CIDR` for network ranges, `MACADDR` for MAC addresses. Support network operators (`<<`, `>>`, `&&`).\n- **Geometric types**: `POINT`, `LINE`, `POLYGON`, `CIRCLE` for 2D spatial data. Index with **GiST**. Consider **PostGIS** for advanced spatial features.\n- **Text search**: `TSVECTOR` for full-text search documents, `TSQUERY` for search queries. Index `tsvector` with **GIN**. Always specify language: `to_tsvector(''english'', col)` and `to_tsquery(''english'', ''query'')`. Never use single-argument versions. This applies to both index expressions and queries.\n- **Domain types**: `CREATE DOMAIN email AS TEXT CHECK (VALUE ~ ''^[^@]+@[^@]+$'')` for reusable custom types with validation. Enforces constraints across tables.\n- **Composite types**: `CREATE TYPE address AS (street TEXT, city TEXT, zip TEXT)` for structured data within columns. Access with `(col).field` syntax.\n- **JSONB**: preferred over JSON; index with **GIN**. Use only for optional/semi-structured attrs. ONLY use JSON if the original ordering of the contents MUST be preserved.\n- **Vector types**: `vector` type by `pgvector` for vector similarity search for embeddings.\n\n### Do not use the following data types\n\n- DO NOT use `timestamp` (without time zone); DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `char(n)` or `varchar(n)`; DO use `text` instead.\n- DO NOT use `money` type; DO use `numeric` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timetz` type; DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timestamptz(0)` or any other precision specification; DO use `timestamptz` instead\n- DO NOT use `serial` type; DO use `generated always as identity` instead.\n\n## Table Types\n\n- **Regular**: default; fully durable, logged.\n- **TEMPORARY**: session-scoped, auto-dropped, not logged. Faster for scratch work.\n- **UNLOGGED**: persistent but not crash-safe. Faster writes; good for caches/staging.\n\n## Row-Level Security\n\nEnable with `ALTER TABLE tbl ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`. Create policies: `CREATE POLICY user_access ON orders FOR SELECT TO app_users USING (user_id = current_user_id())`. Built-in user-based access control at the row level.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **PK**: implicit UNIQUE + NOT NULL; creates a B-tree index.\n- **FK**: specify `ON DELETE/UPDATE` action (`CASCADE`, `RESTRICT`, `SET NULL`, `SET DEFAULT`). Add explicit index on referencing column—speeds up joins and prevents locking issues on parent deletes/updates. Use `DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED` for circular FK dependencies checked at transaction end.\n- **UNIQUE**: creates a B-tree index; allows multiple NULLs unless `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+). Standard behavior: `(1, NULL)` and `(1, NULL)` are allowed. With `NULLS NOT DISTINCT`: only one `(1, NULL)` allowed. Prefer `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` unless you specifically need duplicate NULLs.\n- **CHECK**: row-local constraints; NULL values pass the check (three-valued logic). Example: `CHECK (price > 0)` allows NULL prices. Combine with `NOT NULL` to enforce: `price NUMERIC NOT NULL CHECK (price > 0)`.\n- **EXCLUDE**: prevents overlapping values using operators. `EXCLUDE USING gist (room_id WITH =, booking_period WITH &&)` prevents double-booking rooms. Requires appropriate index type (often GiST).\n\n## Indexing\n\n- **B-tree**: default for equality/range queries (`=`, `<`, `>`, `BETWEEN`, `ORDER BY`)\n- **Composite**: order matters—index used if equality on leftmost prefix (`WHERE a = ? AND b > ?` uses index on `(a,b)`, but `WHERE b = ?` does not). Put most selective/frequently filtered columns first.\n- **Covering**: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (id) INCLUDE (name, email)` - includes non-key columns for index-only scans without visiting table.\n- **Partial**: for hot subsets (`WHERE status = ''active''` → `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (user_id) WHERE status = ''active''`). Any query with `status = ''active''` can use this index.\n- **Expression**: for computed search keys (`CREATE INDEX ON tbl (LOWER(email))`). Expression must match exactly in WHERE clause: `WHERE LOWER(email) = ''user@example.com''`.\n- **GIN**: JSONB containment/existence, arrays (`@>`, `?`), full-text search (`@@`)\n- **GiST**: ranges, geometry, exclusion constraints\n- **BRIN**: very large, naturally ordered data (time-series)—minimal storage overhead. Effective when row order on disk correlates with indexed column (insertion order or after `CLUSTER`).\n\n## Partitioning\n\n- Use for very large tables (>100M rows) where queries consistently filter on partition key (often time/date).\n- Alternate use: use for tables where data maintenance tasks dictates e.g. data pruned or bulk replaced periodically\n- **RANGE**: common for time-series (`PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at)`). Create partitions: `CREATE TABLE logs_2024_01 PARTITION OF logs FOR VALUES FROM (''2024-01-01'') TO (''2024-02-01'')`. **TimescaleDB** automates time-based or ID-based partitioning with retention policies and compression.\n- **LIST**: for discrete values (`PARTITION BY LIST (region)`). Example: `FOR VALUES IN (''us-east'', ''us-west'')`.\n- **HASH**: for even distribution when no natural key (`PARTITION BY HASH (user_id)`). Creates N partitions with modulus.\n- **Constraint exclusion**: requires `CHECK` constraints on partitions for query planner to prune. Auto-created for declarative partitioning (PG10+).\n- Prefer declarative partitioning or hypertables. Do NOT use table inheritance.\n- **Limitations**: no global UNIQUE constraints—include partition key in PK/UNIQUE. FKs from partitioned tables not supported; use triggers.\n\n## Special Considerations\n\n### Update-Heavy Tables\n\n- **Separate hot/cold columns**—put frequently updated columns in separate table to minimize bloat.\n- **Use `fillfactor=90`** to leave space for HOT updates that avoid index maintenance.\n- **Avoid updating indexed columns**—prevents beneficial HOT updates.\n- **Partition by update patterns**—separate frequently updated rows in a different partition from stable data.\n\n### Insert-Heavy Workloads\n\n- **Minimize indexes**—only create what you query; every index slows inserts.\n- **Use `COPY` or multi-row `INSERT`** instead of single-row inserts.\n- **UNLOGGED tables** for rebuildable staging data—much faster writes.\n- **Defer index creation** for bulk loads—>drop index, load data, recreate indexes.\n- **Partition by time/hash** to distribute load. **TimescaleDB** automates partitioning and compression of insert-heavy data.\n- **Use a natural key for primary key** such as a (timestamp, device_id) if enforcing global uniqueness is important many insert-heavy tables don''t need a primary key at all.\n- If you do need a surrogate key, **Prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` over `UUID`**.\n\n### Upsert-Friendly Design\n\n- **Requires UNIQUE index** on conflict target columns—`ON CONFLICT (col1, col2)` needs exact matching unique index (partial indexes don''t work).\n- **Use `EXCLUDED.column`** to reference would-be-inserted values; only update columns that actually changed to reduce write overhead.\n- **`DO NOTHING` faster** than `DO UPDATE` when no actual update needed.\n\n### Safe Schema Evolution\n\n- **Transactional DDL**: most DDL operations can run in transactions and be rolled back—`BEGIN; ALTER TABLE...; ROLLBACK;` for safe testing.\n- **Concurrent index creation**: `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` avoids blocking writes but can''t run in transactions.\n- **Volatile defaults cause rewrites**: adding `NOT NULL` columns with volatile defaults (e.g., `now()`, `gen_random_uuid()`) rewrites entire table. Non-volatile defaults are fast.\n- **Drop constraints before columns**: `ALTER TABLE DROP CONSTRAINT` then `DROP COLUMN` to avoid dependency issues.\n- **Function signature changes**: `CREATE OR REPLACE` with different arguments creates overloads, not replacements. DROP old version if no overload desired.\n\n## Generated Columns\n\n- `... GENERATED ALWAYS AS (<expr>) STORED` for computed, indexable fields. PG18+ adds `VIRTUAL` columns (computed on read, not stored).\n\n## Extensions\n\n- **`pgcrypto`**: `crypt()` for password hashing.\n- **`uuid-ossp`**: alternative UUID functions; prefer `pgcrypto` for new projects.\n- **`pg_trgm`**: fuzzy text search with `%` operator, `similarity()` function. Index with GIN for `LIKE ''%pattern%''` acceleration.\n- **`citext`**: case-insensitive text type. Prefer expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` unless you need case-insensitive constraints.\n- **`btree_gin`/`btree_gist`**: enable mixed-type indexes (e.g., GIN index on both JSONB and text columns).\n- **`hstore`**: key-value pairs; mostly superseded by JSONB but useful for simple string mappings.\n- **`timescaledb`**: essential for time-series—automated partitioning, retention, compression, continuous aggregates.\n- **`postgis`**: comprehensive geospatial support beyond basic geometric types—essential for location-based applications.\n- **`pgvector`**: vector similarity search for embeddings.\n- **`pgaudit`**: audit logging for all database activity.\n\n## JSONB Guidance\n\n- Prefer `JSONB` with **GIN** index.\n- Default: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col);` → accelerates:\n  - **Containment** `jsonb_col @> ''{\"k\":\"v\"}''`\n  - **Key existence** `jsonb_col ? ''k''`, **any/all keys** `?\\|`, `?&`\n  - **Path containment** on nested docs\n  - **Disjunction** `jsonb_col @> ANY(ARRAY[''{\"status\":\"active\"}'', ''{\"status\":\"pending\"}''])`\n- Heavy `@>` workloads: consider opclass `jsonb_path_ops` for smaller/faster containment-only indexes:\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col jsonb_path_ops);`\n  - **Trade-off**: loses support for key existence (`?`, `?|`, `?&`) queries—only supports containment (`@>`)\n- Equality/range on a specific scalar field: extract and index with B-tree (generated column or expression):\n  - `ALTER TABLE tbl ADD COLUMN price INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS ((jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT) STORED;`\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (price);`\n  - Prefer queries like `WHERE price BETWEEN 100 AND 500` (uses B-tree) over `WHERE (jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT BETWEEN 100 AND 500` without index.\n- Arrays inside JSONB: use GIN + `@>` for containment (e.g., tags). Consider `jsonb_path_ops` if only doing containment.\n- Keep core relations in tables; use JSONB for optional/variable attributes.\n- Use constraints to limit allowed JSONB values in a column e.g. `config JSONB NOT NULL CHECK(jsonb_typeof(config) = ''object'')`\n\n## Examples\n\n### Users\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  user_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX ON users (LOWER(email));\nCREATE INDEX ON users (created_at);\n```\n\n### Orders\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  order_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  user_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''PENDING'' CHECK (status IN (''PENDING'',''PAID'',''CANCELED'')),\n  total NUMERIC(10,2) NOT NULL CHECK (total > 0),\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (user_id);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (created_at);\n```\n\n### JSONB\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE profiles (\n  user_id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  attrs JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT ''{}'',\n  theme TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (attrs->>''theme'') STORED\n);\nCREATE INDEX profiles_attrs_gin ON profiles USING GIN (attrs);\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:43:23.347Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Modeling Agents needing advanced PostgreSQL table design capabilities with normalization and denormalization strategies.","zh":"非常适合需要高级PostgreSQL表设计能力的数据建模代理，包括规范化和反规范化策略。","ja":"PostgreSQLのテーブル設計の高度な機能が必要なデータモデリングエージェントに最適。正規化と反正規化の戦略を含む。","ko":"데이터 모델링 에이전트에게 필요한 고급 PostgreSQL 테이블 설계 기능을 제공하며, 정규화 및 비정규화 전략을 포함합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de modelado de datos que necesitan capacidades de diseño de tablas avanzadas de PostgreSQL con estrategias de normalización y denormalización.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de modélisation de données nécessitant des capacités de conception de table PostgreSQL avancées avec des stratégies de normalisation et de dénormalisation.","de":"Perfekt für Data Modeling Agents, die erweiterte PostgreSQL-Tabellendesignfunktionen mit Normalisierungs- und Denormalisierungsstrategien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Modelagem de Dados que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de design de tabelas PostgreSQL com estratégias de normalização e denormalização.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по моделированию данных, которым требуются продвинутые возможности проектирования таблиц PostgreSQL с стратегиями нормализации и денормализации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل النمذجة البيانية الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتصميم جداول PostgreSQL مع استراتيجيات التطبيع والتفريغ"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design efficient PostgreSQL tables using PRIMARY KEY definitions, BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, and UUID for global uniqueness, while applying normalization rules to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies, and denormalization for high-ROI reads.","zh":"赋予代理设计高效PostgreSQL表的能力，使用主键定义、BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY和UUID实现全局唯一性，同时应用正規化规则来消除数据冗余和更新异常，并使用反正規化技术实现高ROI的读取。","ja":"エージェントがPRIMARY KEY定義、BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY、UUIDを使用してPostgreSQLの効率的なテーブルを設計できるようにし、正規化ルールを適用してデータの冗長性と更新の異常を排除し、反正規化技術を使用して高ROIの読み取りを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 PRIMARY KEY 정의, BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, UUID를 사용하여 효율적인 PostgreSQL 테이블을 설계할 수 있도록 하며, 정규화 규칙을 적용하여 데이터의冗余성과 갱신의 비일관성을 제거하고, 비정규화 기술을 사용하여 높은 ROI를 가진 읽기를 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar tablas de PostgreSQL eficientes utilizando definiciones de PRIMARY KEY, BIGINT GENERADO SIEMPRE COMO IDENTIDAD y UUID para la unicidad global, al tiempo que se aplican reglas de normalización para eliminar la redundancia de datos y las anomalías de actualización, y la denormalización para lecturas de alto ROI.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des tables PostgreSQL efficaces en utilisant des définitions de PRIMARY KEY, BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY et UUID pour l''unicité globale, tout en appliquant des règles de normalisation pour éliminer la redondance des données et les anomalies de mise à jour, et la dénormalisation pour des lectures à haut ROI.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, effiziente PostgreSQL-Tabellen zu entwerfen, indem sie PRIMARY KEY-Definitionen, BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY und UUID für die globale Eindeutigkeit verwenden, während sie Normalisierungsregeln anwenden, um Datenredundanz und Update-Anomalien zu beseitigen und Denormalisierung für hochrentable Lesevorgänge.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar tabelas PostgreSQL eficientes usando definições de CHAVE PRIMÁRIA, BIGINT GERADO SEMPRE COMO IDENTIDADE e UUID para unicidade global, aplicando regras de normalização para eliminar a redundância de dados e anomalias de atualização, e denormalização para leituras de alto ROI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать эффективные таблицы PostgreSQL, используя определения ПЕРВИЧНОГО КЛЮЧА, BIGINT СГЕНЕРИРОВАННОГО ВСЕГДА КАК ИДЕНТИФИКАТОР и UUID для глобальной уникальности, применяя правила нормализации для устранения избыточности данных и аномалий обновления, и денормализацию для чтений с высокой отдачей от инвестиций.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية تصميم جداول PostgreSQL فعالة باستخدام تعريفات المفتاح الرئيسي و BIGINT المُنشأة دائمًا كидентيتي و UUID لPointF الفريد عالميًا، بتطبيق قواعد التطبيع لإزالة التكرار البيانات والشذوذات التحديث، والتفريغ لقراءات عالية العائد على الاستثمار"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing normalized tables to 3NF for data consistency","Applying denormalization techniques for measured high-ROI reads","Defining PRIMARY KEY and UUID strategies for reference tables"],"zh":["设计规范化表以确保数据一致性到3NF","应用反规范化技术以实现高ROI的读取","定义主键和UUID策略以引用表"],"ja":["データの整合性を確保するために3NFまで正規化されたテーブルを設計する","測定された高ROIの読み取りを実現するために反正規化技術を適用する","参照テーブル用の主キーとUUID戦略を定義する"],"ko":["데이터 일관성을 유지하기 위해 3NF까지 정규화된 테이블을 설계한다","측정된 높은 ROI의 읽기를 구현하기 위해 비정규화 기술을 적용한다","참조 테이블을 위한 주키 및 UUID 전략을 정의한다"],"es":["Diseñar tablas normalizadas a 3NF para la coherencia de los datos","Aplicar técnicas de denormalización para lecturas de alto ROI medidas","Definir estrategias de PRIMARY KEY y UUID para tablas de referencia"],"fr":["Concevoir des tables normalisées à 3NF pour la cohérence des données"," Appliquer des techniques de dénormalisation pour des lectures à haut ROI mesurées","Définir des stratégies de PRIMARY KEY et UUID pour les tables de référence"],"de":["Entwerfen normalisierter Tabellen bis 3NF für die Datenkonsistenz","Anwenden von Denormalisierungstechniken für gemessene hochrentable Lesevorgänge","Definieren von PRIMARY KEY- und UUID-Strategien für Referenztabelle"],"pt":["Projetar tabelas normalizadas para 3NF para consistência de dados","Aplicar técnicas de denormalização para leituras de alto ROI medidas","Definir estratégias de CHAVE PRIMÁRIA e UUID para tabelas de referência"],"ru":["Проектировать нормализованные таблицы до 3NF для согласованности данных","Применять техники денормализации для измеренных чтений с высокой отдачей от инвестиций","Определять стратегии ПЕРВИЧНОГО КЛЮЧА и UUID для таблиц ссылок"],"ar":["تصميم جداول مُطبّقة للتطبيع إلى 3NF لاتساق البيانات","تطبيق تقنيات التفريغ لقراءات عالية العائد على الاستثمار المقاسة","تحديد استراتيجيات المفتاح الرئيسي و UUID لأجـل الجداول المرجعية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of database normalization and denormalization concepts","PostgreSQL-specific syntax and features"],"zh":["需要理解数据库的正規化和反正規化概念","PostgreSQL特有的语法和功能"],"ja":["データベースの正規化と反正規化の概念を理解する必要がある","PostgreSQL固有の構文と機能"],"ko":["데이터베이스의 정규화 및 비정규화 개념을 이해해야 함","PostgreSQL 고유의 구문 및 기능"],"es":["Requiere una comprensión de los conceptos de normalización y denormalización de bases de datos","Sintaxis y características específicas de PostgreSQL"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des concepts de normalisation et de dénormalisation de bases de données","Syntaxe et fonctionnalités spécifiques à PostgreSQL"],"de":["Erfordert ein Verständnis der Datenbanknormalisierungs- und Denormalisierungskonzepte","PostgreSQL-spezifische Syntax und Funktionen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de conceitos de normalização e denormalização de banco de dados","Sintaxe e recursos específicos do PostgreSQL"],"ru":["Требует понимания концепций нормализации и денормализации базы данных","Специфическая синтаксис и функции PostgreSQL"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لمفاهيم تطبيع وتفريغ قاعدة البيانات","تركيب لغوي وميزات محددة لبي إس كيو إل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
