 Entwicklung","Bing''s DALL-E 3","Generierung von KI-Bildern","Prinzip der Effizienz","Ehrlichkeit in der Entwicklung"],"pt":["verificação antes de conclusão","desenvolvimento de software","serviços de IA","DALL-E 3","integridade em projetos","eficiência em desenvolvimento","princípios de desenvolvimento","melhores práticas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["верификация перед завершением","разработка программного обеспечения","сервисы ИИ","DALL-E 3","целостность в проектах","эффективность в разработке","принципы разработки","лучшие практики разработки"],"ar":["التحقق قبل الإنجاز","تطوير البرمجيات","خدمات الذكاء الاصطناعي","DALL-E 3","السلامة في المشاريع","الفعالية في التطوير","مبادئ التطوير","أفضل الممارسات للتطوير"]}},"owner":"involvex","repo":"image-wizard-cli","repoPath":"involvex/image-wizard-cli","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.533Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"verification-before-completion","description":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always","bodyPreview":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing sati","body":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing satisfaction:\n\n1. IDENTIFY: What command proves this claim?\n2. RUN: Execute the FULL command (fresh, complete)\n3. READ: Full output, check exit code, count failures\n4. VERIFY: Does output confirm the claim?\n   - If NO: State actual status with evidence\n   - If YES: State claim WITH evidence\n5. ONLY THEN: Make the claim\n\nSkip any step = lying, not verifying\n```\n\n## Common Failures\n\n| Claim                 | Requires                        | Not Sufficient                 |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Tests pass            | Test command output: 0 failures | Previous run, \"should pass\"    |\n| Linter clean          | Linter output: 0 errors         | Partial check, extrapolation   |\n| Build succeeds        | Build command: exit 0           | Linter passing, logs look good |\n| Bug fixed             | Test original symptom: passes   | Code changed, assumed fixed    |\n| Regression test works | Red-green cycle verified        | Test passes once               |\n| Agent completed       | VCS diff shows changes          | Agent reports \"success\"        |\n| Requirements met      | Line-by-line checklist          | Tests passing                  |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP\n\n- Using \"should\", \"probably\", \"seems to\"\n- Expressing satisfaction before verification (\"Great!\", \"Perfect!\", \"Done!\", etc.)\n- About to commit/push/PR without verification\n- Trusting agent success reports\n- Relying on partial verification\n- Thinking \"just this once\"\n- Tired and wanting work over\n- **ANY wording implying success without having run verification**\n\n## Rationalization Prevention\n\n| Excuse                                  | Reality                |\n| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| \"Should work now\"                       | RUN the verification   |\n| \"I''m confident\"                         | Confidence ≠ evidence  |\n| \"Just this once\"                        | No exceptions          |\n| \"Linter passed\"                         | Linter ≠ compiler      |\n| \"Agent said success\"                    | Verify independently   |\n| \"I''m tired\"                             | Exhaustion ≠ excuse    |\n| \"Partial check is enough\"               | Partial proves nothing |\n| \"Different words so rule doesn''t apply\" | Spirit over letter     |\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n**Tests:**\n\n```\n✅ [Run test command] [See: 34/34 pass] \"All tests pass\"\n❌ \"Should pass now\" / \"Looks correct\"\n```\n\n**Regression tests (TDD Red-Green):**\n\n```\n✅ Write → Run (pass) → Revert fix → Run (MUST FAIL) → Restore → Run (pass)\n❌ \"I''ve written a regression test\" (without red-green verification)\n```\n\n**Build:**\n\n```\n✅ [Run build] [See: exit 0] \"Build passes\"\n❌ \"Linter passed\" (linter doesn''t check compilation)\n```\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n```\n✅ Re-read plan → Create checklist → Verify each → Report gaps or completion\n❌ \"Tests pass, phase complete\"\n```\n\n**Agent delegation:**\n\n```\n✅ Agent reports success → Check VCS diff → Verify changes → Report actual state\n❌ Trust agent report\n```\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nFrom 24 failure memories:\n\n- your human partner said \"I don''t believe you\" - trust broken\n- Undefined functions shipped - would crash\n- Missing requirements shipped - incomplete features\n- Time wasted on false completion → redirect → rework\n- Violates: \"Honesty is a core value. If you lie, you''ll be replaced.\"\n\n## When To Apply\n\n**ALWAYS before:**\n\n- ANY variation of success/completion claims\n- ANY expression of satisfaction\n- ANY positive statement about work state\n- Committing, PR creation, task completion\n- Moving to next task\n- Delegating to agents\n\n**Rule applies to:**\n\n- Exact phrases\n- Paraphrases and synonyms\n- Implications of success\n- ANY communication suggesting completion/correctness\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**No shortcuts for verification.**\n\nRun the command. Read the output. THEN claim the result.\n\nThis is non-negotiable.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:48:49.164Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Quality Assurance Agents requiring rigorous verification protocols before completion","zh":"非常适合需要在完成前执行严格验证协议的质量保证代理","ja":"完了前に厳格な検証プロトコルを要求する品質保証エージェントに最適","ko":"완료 전에 엄격한 검증 프로토콜을 요구하는 품질 보증 에이전트에게 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Aseguramiento de Calidad que requieren protocolos de verificación rigurosos antes de la finalización","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''assurance qualité nécessitant des protocoles de vérification rigoureux avant l''achèvement","de":"Perfekt für Qualitätsprüfungsagenten, die strenge Überprüfungsprotokolle vor der Fertigstellung erfordern","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Garantia de Qualidade que exigem protocolos de verificação rigorosos antes da conclusão","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по обеспечению качества, требующих строгих протоколов верификации перед завершением","ar":"مثالي لعمال ضمان الجودة الذين يتطلبون بروتوكولات تحقق صارمة قبل الإكمال"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce the iron law of verification, ensuring claims are backed by fresh evidence, utilizing protocols like verification commands and gate functions to prevent premature completion claims, thereby promoting honesty and efficiency in workflow management","zh":"赋予代理人执行验证铁律的能力，确保声明有新鲜的证据支持，利用验证命令和门函数等协议防止过早的完成声明，从而促进工作流管理中的诚实和效率","ja":"検証鉄則を強制するエージェントを可能にし、声明が新しい証拠によって裏付けられていることを保証し、検証コマンドやゲート関数などのプロトコルを使用して、早期の完了声明を防ぎ、ワークフローの管理における誠実さと効率を促進する","ko":"검증 철칙을 강제하는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며,声明이 새로운 증거에 의해裏付けられている 것을 보장하며, 검증 명령어나 게이트 함수 등의 프로토콜을 사용하여, 조기 완료声明을 방지하며, 워크플로우 관리에서의 정직과 효율성을 증진","es":"Habilita a los agentes a hacer cumplir la ley de hierro de la verificación, asegurando que las reclamaciones estén respaldadas por pruebas frescas, utilizando protocolos como comandos de verificación y funciones de puerta para prevenir reclamaciones de finalización prematura, promoviendo así la honestidad y la eficiencia en la gestión del flujo de trabajo","fr":"Permet aux agents de faire respecter la loi de fer de la vérification, en s''assurant que les réclamations sont étayées par des preuves fraîches, en utilisant des protocoles tels que des commandes de vérification et des fonctions de porte pour prévenir les réclamations de finalisation prématurée, promouvant ainsi l''honnêteté et l''efficacité dans la gestion du flux de travail","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, das eiserne Gesetz der Überprüfung durchzusetzen, indem sichergestellt wird, dass Ansprüche durch frische Beweise gestützt werden, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie Überprüfungsbefehlen und Schrankenfunktionen, um vorzeitige Fertigstellungsansprüche zu verhindern und damit Ehrlichkeit und Effizienz in der Prozessverwaltung zu fördern","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor a lei de ferro da verificação, garantindo que as alegações sejam respaldadas por evidências recentes, utilizando protocolos como comandos de verificação e funções de porta para prevenir alegações de conclusão prematura, promovendo assim a honestidade e a eficiência na gestão de fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать железное правило верификации, гарантируя, что претензии подтверждаются свежими доказательствами, используя протоколы, такие как команды верификации и функции шлюза, чтобы предотвратить преждевременные заявления о завершении, тем самым способствуя честности и эффективности в управлении рабочим процессом","ar":"يتمكن العمال من فرض قانون الحديد للتحقق، لضمان دعم المطالبات بالدلائل الحديثة، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل أوامر التحقق ووظائف البوابة لمنع المطالبات المسبقة بالإكمال، مما يعزز الكفاءة والصدق في إدارة تدفق العمل"},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying task completion with fresh evidence","Enforcing the iron law in automated workflows","Debugging claims without proper verification"],"zh":["使用新鲜证据验证任务完成","在自动化工作流中执行验证铁律","调试没有适当验证的声明"],"ja":["新しい証拠を使用してタスクの完了を検証する","自動化されたワークフローで検証鉄則を実施する","適切な検証のない声明をデバッグする"],"ko":["새로운 증거를 사용하여 태스크 완료를 검증","자동화된 워크플로우에서 검증 철칙을 시행","적절한 검증이 없는 声明을 디버깅"],"es":["Verificar la finalización de tareas con pruebas frescas","Hacer cumplir la ley de hierro en flujos de trabajo automatizados","Depurar reclamaciones sin verificación adecuada"],"fr":["Vérifier l''achèvement de tâches avec des preuves fraîches","Faire respecter la loi de fer dans les flux de travail automatisés","Déboguer les réclamations sans vérification appropriée"],"de":["Überprüfen des Aufgabenabschlusses mit frischen Beweisen","Durchsetzen des eisernen Gesetzes in automatisierten Arbeitsflüssen","Fehlerbehebung von Ansprüchen ohne ordnungsgemäße Überprüfung"],"pt":["Verificar a conclusão da tarefa com evidências recentes","Impor a lei de ferro em fluxos de trabalho automatizados","Depurar alegações sem verificação adequada"],"ru":["Проверка завершения задачи с помощью свежих доказательств","Реализация железного правила в автоматизированных рабочих процессах","Отладка претензий без надлежащей верификации"],"ar":["التحقق من إكمال المهمة بدلائل حديثة","تطبيق قانون الحديد في سير العمل الآلي","تصحيح المطالبات بدون تحقق كاف"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires implementation of verification commands","Demands strict adherence to the iron law"],"zh":["需要实现验证命令","要求严格遵守验证铁律"],"ja":["検証コマンドの実装が必要","検証鉄則への厳格な遵守を要求"],"ko":["검증 명령의 구현이 필요","검증 철칙에 대한 엄격한 준수를 요구"],"es":["Requiere la implementación de comandos de verificación","Exige una estricta adhesión a la ley de hierro"],"fr":["Nécessite la mise en œuvre de commandes de vérification","Exige une stricte adhésion à la loi de fer"],"de":["Erfordert die Implementierung von Überprüfungsbefehlen","Fordert eine strikte Einhaltung des eisernen Gesetzes"],"pt":["Exige a implementação de comandos de verificação","Exige adesão estrita à lei de ferro"],"ru":["Требует реализации команд верификации","Требует строгого соблюдения железного правила"],"ar":["يتطلب تنفيذ أوامر التحقق","يتطلب الالتزام الصارم بقانون الحديد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('deadronos/gpu-conway-life/openspec-continue-change', 'community', 'deadronos', 'gpu-conway-life', 'deadronos/gpu-conway-life', 'openspec-continue-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.533Z', '2026-02-18T14:48:54.688Z', NULL, '{"id":"deadronos/gpu-conway-life/openspec-continue-change","name":"openspec-continue-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change技能允许开发者继续进行代码更改，实现开发流程的无缝衔接","ja":"openspec-continue-changeスキルは、開発者がコードの変更を続けることができ、開発プロセスを無停止で実現","ko":"openspec-continue-change 기능은 개발자가 코드 변경을 계속할 수 있도록 해주어 개발 프로세스를 원활하게 진행","es":"Openspec-continue-change permite a los desarrolladores continuar trabajando en cambios y crear el siguiente artefacto","fr":"Openspec-continue-change permet aux développeurs de poursuivre les modifications et de créer le prochain artefact","de":"Openspec-continue-change ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Änderungen fortzuführen und das nächste Artefakt zu erstellen","pt":"O OpenSpec permite continuar trabalhando em uma alteração, criando o próximo artefato de forma eficiente","ru":"OpenSpec позволяет продолжить работу над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт эффективно","ar":"OpenSpec يسمح بالاستمرار في العمل على تغيير، قم بإنشاء الملف التالي بفعالية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"继续更改功能 - openspec-continue-change","ja":"変更の継続 - openspec-continue-change","ko":"변경 계속하기 - openspec-continue-change","es":"Continúa cambios con openspec-continue-change","fr":"Poursuivez les modifications avec openspec-continue-change","de":"Führen Sie Änderungen mit openspec-continue-change fort","pt":"Continue Change com OpenSpec","ru":"Продолжить изменение с OpenSpec","ar":"استمرار التغيير مع OpenSpec","en":"openspec-continue-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change技能允许开发者继续进行代码更改，实现开发流程的无缝衔接","ja":"openspec-continue-changeスキルは、開発者がコードの変更を続けることができ、開発プロセスを無停止で実現","ko":"openspec-continue-change 기능은 개발자가 코드 변경을 계속할 수 있도록 해주어 개발 프로세스를 원활하게 진행","es":"Openspec-continue-change permite a los desarrolladores continuar trabajando en cambios y crear el siguiente artefacto","fr":"Openspec-continue-change permet aux développeurs de poursuivre les modifications et de créer le prochain artefact","de":"Openspec-continue-change ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Änderungen fortzuführen und das nächste Artefakt zu erstellen","pt":"O OpenSpec permite continuar trabalhando em uma alteração, criando o próximo artefato de forma eficiente","ru":"OpenSpec позволяет продолжить работу над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт эффективно","ar":"OpenSpec يسمح بالاستمرار في العمل على تغيير، قم بإنشاء الملف التالي بفعالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持继续代码更改","自动提示可用的更改","使用AskUserQuestion工具选择更改","实现开发流程的无缝衔接","支持多语言环境"],"ja":["コードの変更の継続をサポート","利用可能な変更の自動提示","AskUserQuestionツールを使用して変更を選択","開発プロセスの無停止を実現","多言語環境をサポート"],"ko":["코드 변경을 계속할 수 있는 기능","사용 가능한 변경의 자동提示","AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 변경 선택","개발 프로세스의 원활한 진행","다중 언어 환경 지원"],"es":["Permite continuar trabajando en cambios","Crea el siguiente artefacto","Utiliza la herramienta AskUserQuestion para seleccionar cambios","Ejecuta el comando openspec list --json para obtener cambios disponibles","Presenta los 3 cambios más recientes"],"fr":["Permet de poursuivre les modifications","Crée le prochain artefact","Utilise l''outil AskUserQuestion pour sélectionner les modifications","Exécute la commande openspec list --json pour obtenir les modifications disponibles","Présente les 3 modifications les plus récentes"],"de":["Ermöglicht es, Änderungen fortzuführen","Erstellt das nächste Artefakt","Verwendet das Tool AskUserQuestion, um Änderungen auszuwählen","Führt den Befehl openspec list --json aus, um verfügbare Änderungen zu erhalten","Präsentiert die 3 zuletzt geänderten Änderungen"],"pt":["Continuar trabalhando em uma alteração","Criar o próximo artefato","Selecionar alterações disponíveis","Usar a ferramenta AskUserQuestion","Executar comandos OpenSpec","Trabalhar com artefatos eficientemente"],"ru":["Продолжить работу над изменением","Создать следующий артефакт","Выбрать доступные изменения","Использовать инструмент AskUserQuestion","Выполнить команды OpenSpec","Работать с артефактами эффективно"],"ar":["استمرار العمل على تغيير","إنشاء الملف التالي","اختيار التغييرات المتاحة","استخدام أداة AskUserQuestion","تشغيل أوامر OpenSpec","العمل مع الملفات بفعالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-continue-change","代码更改","开发流程","无缝衔接","AskUserQuestion","自动提示","多语言环境"],"ja":["openspec-continue-change","コードの変更","開発プロセス","無停止","AskUserQuestion","自動提示","多言語環境"],"ko":["openspec-continue-change","코드 변경","개발 프로세스","원활한 진행","AskUserQuestion","자동提示","다중 언어 환경"],"es":["openspec-continue-change","desarrollo de software","gestión de cambios","creación de artefactos","herramientas de desarrollo","AskUserQuestion"],"fr":["openspec-continue-change","développement de logiciels","gestion de modifications","création d''artefacts","outils de développement","AskUserQuestion"],"de":["openspec-continue-change","Software-Entwicklung","Änderungsmanagement","Artefakterstellung","Entwicklungstools","AskUserQuestion"],"pt":["OpenSpec","continuar alteração","criar artefato","AskUserQuestion","comandos OpenSpec","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","eficiência no desenvolvimento"],"ru":["OpenSpec","продолжить изменение","создать артефакт","AskUserQuestion","команды OpenSpec","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","эффективность разработки"],"ar":["OpenSpec","استمرار التغيير","إنشاء الملف","AskUserQuestion","أوامر OpenSpec","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","فعالية التطوير"]}},"owner":"deadronos","repo":"gpu-conway-life","repoPath":"deadronos/gpu-conway-life","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.533Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-continue-change","description":"Continue working on an OpenSpec change by creating the next artifact. Use when the user wants to progress their change, create the next artifact, or continue their workflow.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-","body":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-4 most recently modified changes as options, showing:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema (from `schema` field if present, otherwise \"spec-driven\")\n   - Status (e.g., \"0/5 tasks\", \"complete\", \"no tasks\")\n   - How recently it was modified (from `lastModified` field)\n\n   Mark the most recently modified change as \"(Recommended)\" since it''s likely what the user wants to continue.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check current status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand current state. The response includes:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow schema being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\", \"tdd\")\n   - `artifacts`: Array of artifacts with their status (\"done\", \"ready\", \"blocked\")\n   - `isComplete`: Boolean indicating if all artifacts are complete\n\n3. **Act based on status**:\n\n   ---\n\n   **If all artifacts are complete (`isComplete: true`)**:\n   - Congratulate the user\n   - Show final status including the schema used\n   - Suggest: \"All artifacts created! You can now implement this change or archive it.\"\n   - STOP\n\n   ---\n\n   **If artifacts are ready to create** (status shows artifacts with `status: \"ready\"`):\n   - Pick the FIRST artifact with `status: \"ready\"` from the status output\n   - Get its instructions:\n     ```bash\n     openspec instructions <artifact-id> --change \"<name>\" --json\n     ```\n   - Parse the JSON. The key fields are:\n     - `context`: Project background (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `rules`: Artifact-specific rules (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `template`: The structure to use for your output file\n     - `instruction`: Schema-specific guidance\n     - `outputPath`: Where to write the artifact\n     - `dependencies`: Completed artifacts to read for context\n   - **Create the artifact file**:\n     - Read any completed dependency files for context\n     - Use `template` as the structure - fill in its sections\n     - Apply `context` and `rules` as constraints when writing - but do NOT copy them into the file\n     - Write to the output path specified in instructions\n   - Show what was created and what''s now unlocked\n   - STOP after creating ONE artifact\n\n   ---\n\n   **If no artifacts are ready (all blocked)**:\n   - This shouldn''t happen with a valid schema\n   - Show status and suggest checking for issues\n\n4. **After creating an artifact, show progress**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter each invocation, show:\n- Which artifact was created\n- Schema workflow being used\n- Current progress (N/M complete)\n- What artifacts are now unlocked\n- Prompt: \"Want to continue? Just ask me to continue or tell me what to do next.\"\n\n**Artifact Creation Guidelines**\n\nThe artifact types and their purpose depend on the schema. Use the `instruction` field from the instructions output to understand what to create.\n\nCommon artifact patterns:\n\n**spec-driven schema** (proposal → specs → design → tasks):\n- **proposal.md**: Ask user about the change if not clear. Fill in Why, What Changes, Capabilities, Impact.\n  - The Capabilities section is critical - each capability listed will need a spec file.\n- **specs/*.md**: Create one spec per capability listed in the proposal.\n- **design.md**: Document technical decisions, architecture, and implementation approach.\n- **tasks.md**: Break down implementation into checkboxed tasks.\n\n**tdd schema** (spec → tests → implementation → docs):\n- **spec.md**: Feature specification defining what to build.\n- **tests/*.test.ts**: Write tests BEFORE implementation (TDD red phase).\n- **src/*.ts**: Implement to make tests pass (TDD green phase).\n- **docs/*.md**: Document the implemented feature.\n\nFor other schemas, follow the `instruction` field from the CLI output.\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Create ONE artifact per invocation\n- Always read dependency artifacts before creating a new one\n- Never skip artifacts or create out of order\n- If context is unclear, ask the user before creating\n- Verify the artifact file exists after writing before marking progress\n- Use the schema''s artifact sequence, don''t assume specific artifact names\n- **IMPORTANT**: `context` and `rules` are constraints for YOU, not content for the file\n  - Do NOT copy `<context>`, `<rules>`, `<project_context>` blocks into the artifact\n  - These guide what you write, but should never appear in the output\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:48:54.688Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring efficient change management and artifact creation capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高效变更管理和构件创建能力的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが効率的な変更管理とアーティファクト作成機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"효율적인 변경 관리 및 아티팩트 생성 기능이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una gestión de cambios eficiente y capacidades de creación de artefactos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une gestion de changements efficace et des capacités de création d''artefacts.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine effiziente Änderungsverwaltung und Artefakt-Erstellungsfunktionen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem gerenciamento de alterações eficiente e capacidades de criação de artefatos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих эффективного управления изменениями и возможностей создания артефактов.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير التي تتطلب إدارة تغييرات فعالة وقدرات إنشاء مصنوعات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly continue working on changes by creating the next artifact, utilizing the `openspec list --json` command for retrieving available changes and the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection, all while handling change name specification and inference from conversation context.","zh":"通过创建下一个构件、使用 `openspec list --json` 命令检索可用更改以及使用 AskUserQuestion 工具进行用户选择来使代理无缝地继续处理更改，同时处理更改名称的指定和从对话上下文的推断。","ja":"エージェントが次のアーティファクトを作成することで、変更をシームレスに続行し、利用可能な変更を取得するために `openspec list --json` コマンドを使用し、AskUserQuestion ツールを使用してユーザー選択を行い、変更名の指定と会話のコンテキストからの推論を処理します。","ko":"다음 아티팩트를 생성하여 변경을无중단으로 계속 처리하며, `openspec list --json` 명령을 사용하여 사용 가능한 변경을 검색하고 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자 선택을하고, 변경 이름의 지정 및 대화의 contexto에서 추론을 처리합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes continuar trabajando en los cambios de manera fluida creando el siguiente artefacto, utilizando el comando `openspec list --json` para recuperar los cambios disponibles y la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección del usuario, todo mientras maneja la especificación y la inferencia del nombre del cambio desde el contexto de la conversación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de continuer à travailler sur les changements de manière fluide en créant le prochain artefact, en utilisant la commande `openspec list --json` pour récupérer les changements disponibles et l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur, le tout en gérant la spécification et l''inférence du nom du changement depuis le contexte de la conversation.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, nahtlos an den Änderungen weiterzuarbeiten, indem sie das nächste Artefakt erstellen, wobei sie den Befehl `openspec list --json` zur Abrufung der verfügbaren Änderungen und das Tool AskUserQuestion für die Benutzerauswahl verwenden, während sie die Änderungsname-Spezifikation und -Ableitung aus dem Konversationskontext verarbeiten.","pt":"Permite que os agentes continuem trabalhando em alterações de forma contínua, criando o próximo artefato, utilizando o comando `openspec list --json` para recuperar alterações disponíveis e a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção do usuário, tratando também a especificação e inferência do nome da alteração do contexto da conversa.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью бесперебойно продолжать работать над изменениями, создавая следующий артефакт, используя команду `openspec list --json` для получения доступных изменений и инструмент AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя, а также обрабатывая указание и вывод имени изменения из контекста разговора.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من الاستمرار في العمل على التغييرات بشكل متواصل من خلال إنشاء الملف القادم، باستخدام الأمر `openspec list --json` لاسترجاع التغييرات المتاحة وأداة AskUserQuestion لاختيار المستخدم، مع معالجة تحديد اسم التغيير واستخلاصه من سياق المحادثة."},"useCases":{"en":["Continuing interrupted changes","Creating new artifacts based on recent modifications","Streamlining change management workflows"],"zh":["继续中断的更改","根据最近的修改创建新的构件","简化更改管理工作流"],"ja":["中断された変更の続行","最近の変更に基づいて新しいアーティファクトを作成する","変更管理ワークフローのストリームライン化"],"ko":["중단된 변경의 계속","최근의 수정에 기초하여 새로운 아티팩트를 생성","변경 관리 워크플로우의簡略화"],"es":["Continuar cambios interrumpidos","Crear nuevos artefactos basados en modificaciones recientes","Optimizar flujos de trabajo de gestión de cambios"],"fr":["Continuer les changements interrompus","Créer de nouveaux artefacts basés sur des modifications récentes","Optimiser les flux de travail de gestion de changements"],"de":["Unterbrochene Änderungen fortsetzen","Erstellen neuer Artefakte basierend auf kürzlichen Änderungen","Optimieren von Änderungsmanagement-Workflows"],"pt":["Continuar alterações interrompidas","Criar novos artefatos com base em modificações recentes","Otizar fluxos de trabalho de gerenciamento de alterações"],"ru":["Продолжение прерванных изменений","Создание новых артефактов на основе недавних изменений","Оптимизация потоков управления изменениями"],"ar":["استمرار التغييرات المتوقفة","إنشاء مصنوعات جديدة بناءً على التعديلات الحديثة","تسهيل سير عمل إدارة التغييرات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires openspec installation and configuration","Dependent on conversation context for change name inference","Limited to top 3 changes for user selection"],"zh":["需要 openspec 安装和配置","依赖于对话上下文进行更改名称推断","用户选择仅限于前 3 个更改"],"ja":["openspec のインストールと構成が必要","変更名の推論に会話のコンテキストに依存","ユーザー選択は最初の 3 つの変更に限定"],"ko":["openspec 설치 및 구성이 필요","변경 이름 추론에 대화 contexto에 의존","사용자 선택은 최초 3개의 변경으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de openspec","Depende del contexto de conversación para la inferencia del nombre del cambio","Limitado a los 3 primeros cambios para la selección del usuario"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration d''openspec","Dépend du contexte de conversation pour l''inférence du nom du changement","Limité aux 3 premiers changements pour la sélection de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation und Konfiguration von openspec","Hängt vom Konversationskontext für die Ableitung des Änderungsnamens ab","Begrenzt auf die ersten 3 Änderungen für die Benutzerauswahl"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do openspec","Depende do contexto da conversa para inferência do nome da alteração","Limitado aos 3 principais alterações para seleção do usuário"],"ru":["Требует установки и настройки openspec","Зависит от контекста разговора для вывода имени изменения","Ограничен до 3-х лучших изменений для выбора пользователя"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين openspec","يعتمد على سياق المحادثة لاستخلاص اسم التغيير","محدود بالتغييرات الثلاث الأولى لاختيار المستخدم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('JasonRowe/Wahoo-KICKR-Randomizer/bluetooth-trainer-expert', 'community', 'JasonRowe', 'Wahoo-KICKR-Randomizer', 'JasonRowe/Wahoo-KICKR-Randomizer', 'bluetooth-trainer-expert', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.533Z', '2026-02-18T14:49:30.776Z', NULL, '{"id":"JasonRowe/Wahoo-KICKR-Randomizer/bluetooth-trainer-expert","name":"bluetooth-trainer-expert","description":{"zh":"本技能提供了一个用于开发与智能训练器交互的健身应用程序的工作流程","ja":"本スキルは、スマートトレーナーと交互作用するフィットネスアプリケーションを開発するためのワークフローを提供","ko":"본 스킬은 스마트 트레이너와 상호 작용하는 피트니스 애플리케이션을 개발하기 위한 워크플로우를 제공","es":"Esta habilidad proporciona un flujo de trabajo probado para desarrollar aplicaciones de fitness en bicicleta que interactúan con entrenadores inteligentes.","fr":"Cette compétence fournit un workflow éprouvé pour développer des applications de fitness cycliste qui interagissent avec des entraîneurs intelligents.","de":"Diese Fähigkeit bietet einen bewährten Workflow für die Entwicklung von Fitness-Anwendungen für das Fahrrad, die mit intelligenten Trainern interagieren.","pt":"O Bluetooth Trainer Expert é uma ferramenta para desenvolvedores que cria aplicativos de fitness para bicicletas, controlando a resistência do Wahoo KIKR.","ru":"Эксперт Bluetooth Тренировщика - это инструмент для разработчиков, создающий программы для фитнеса на велосипеде, управляющий сопротивлением Wahoo KIKR.","ar":"خبير مدرب بلوتوث هو أداة لمطوري تطبيقات اللياقة البدنية للدراجات الهوائية، التي تتحكم في مقاومة واهو كيكر.","en":"Windows app to control resistance on my Wahoo KIKR to make workouts more fun"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"蓝牙训练师专家 - 智能训练器控制","ja":"Bluetooth Trainer Expert - スマートトレーナー制御","ko":"블루투스 트레이너 전문가 - 스마트 트레이너 제어","es":"Entrenador Bluetooth Expert: Control de Resistencia","fr":"Expert Entraîneur Bluetooth : Contrôle de Résistance","de":"Bluetooth-Trainer-Experte: Widerstandssteuerung","pt":"Bluetooth Trainer Expert: Desenvolvimento de Aplicativos ...","ru":"Эксперт Bluetooth Тренировщика: Разработка Программ для Ф...","ar":"خبير مدرب بلوتوث: تطوير تطبيقات اللياقة البدنية","en":"bluetooth-trainer-expert"},"description":{"zh":"本技能提供了一个用于开发与智能训练器交互的健身应用程序的工作流程","ja":"本スキルは、スマートトレーナーと交互作用するフィットネスアプリケーションを開発するためのワークフローを提供","ko":"본 스킬은 스마트 트레이너와 상호 작용하는 피트니스 애플리케이션을 개발하기 위한 워크플로우를 제공","es":"Esta habilidad proporciona un flujo de trabajo probado para desarrollar aplicaciones de fitness en bicicleta que interactúan con entrenadores inteligentes.","fr":"Cette compétence fournit un workflow éprouvé pour développer des applications de fitness cycliste qui interagissent avec des entraîneurs intelligents.","de":"Diese Fähigkeit bietet einen bewährten Workflow für die Entwicklung von Fitness-Anwendungen für das Fahrrad, die mit intelligenten Trainern interagieren.","pt":"O Bluetooth Trainer Expert é uma ferramenta para desenvolvedores que cria aplicativos de fitness para bicicletas, controlando a resistência do Wahoo KIKR.","ru":"Эксперт Bluetooth Тренировщика - это инструмент для разработчиков, создающий программы для фитнеса на велосипеде, управляющий сопротивлением Wahoo KIKR.","ar":"خبير مدرب بلوتوث هو أداة لمطوري تطبيقات اللياقة البدنية للدراجات الهوائية، التي تتحكم في مقاومة واهو كيكر.","en":"Windows app to control resistance on my Wahoo KIKR to make workouts more fun"},"definition":{"en":"Windows app to control resistance on my Wahoo KIKR to make workouts more fun"},"features":{"zh":["控制Wahoo KICKR等智能训练器的阻力","采用Console First的方法隔离连接和协议逻辑","支持FTMS设备","提供简单的C#控制台应用程序示例","适用于开发健身应用程序","支持多种设备"],"ja":["Wahoo KICKRなどのスマートトレーナーの抵抗を制御","Console Firstアプローチを使用して接続とプロトコルロジックを分離","FTMSデバイスをサポート","シンプルなC#コンソールアプリケーションの例を提供","フィットネスアプリケーションの開発に適する","複数のデバイスをサポート"],"ko":["Wahoo KICKR 등의 스마트 트레이너의 저항을 제어","Console First 방식을 사용하여 연결 및 프로토콜 로직을 분리","FTMS 디바이스를 지원","단순한 C# 콘솔 애플리케이션 예제를 제공","피트니스 애플리케이션 개발에 적합","여러 디바이스를 지원"],"es":["Enfoque ''Consola primero'' para aislar la lógica de conexión y protocolo","Verificación física para garantizar la precisión","Integración con dispositivos FTMS","Compatibilidad con Wahoo KICKR","Desarrollo de aplicaciones de fitness en bicicleta","Control de resistencia en entrenadores inteligentes"],"fr":["Approche ''Console d''abord'' pour isoler la logique de connexion et de protocole","Vérification physique pour garantir la précision","Intégration avec des appareils FTMS","Compatibilité avec Wahoo KICKR","Développement d''applications de fitness cycliste","Contrôle de la résistance sur des entraîneurs intelligents"],"de":["Ansatz ''Konsole zuerst'' zur Isolierung der Verbindungs- und Protokolllogik","Physische Verifizierung zur Gewährleistung der Genauigkeit","Integration mit FTMS-Geräten","Kompatibilität mit Wahoo KICKR","Entwicklung von Fitness-Anwendungen für das Fahrrad","Widerstandssteuerung in intelligenten Trainern"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de aplicativos de fitness para bicicletas","Controle de resistência do Wahoo KIKR","Abordagem Console First para isolamento de lógica de protocolo","Verificação física para garantir a funcionalidade","Suporte a dispositivos FTMS","Desenvolvimento de aplicativos com C# e WPF/MAUI"],"ru":["Разработка программ для фитнеса на велосипеде","Управление сопротивлением Wahoo KIKR","Подход Console First для изоляции логики протокола","Физическая верификация для обеспечения функциональности","Поддержка устройств FTMS","Разработка программ с помощью C# и WPF/MAUI"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات اللياقة البدنية للدراجات الهوائية","التحكم في مقاومة واهو كيكر","منهجية Console First لتفريد منطق البروتوكول","التحقق المادي لضمان الوظيفة","دعم أجهزة FTMS","تطوير التطبيقات باستخدام C# و WPF/MAUI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["蓝牙训练师专家","智能训练器","Wahoo KICKR","FTMS设备","Console First","C#控制台应用程序","健身应用程序","Windows应用程序"],"ja":["Bluetooth Trainer Expert","スマートトレーナー","Wahoo KICKR","FTMSデバイス","Console First","C#コンソールアプリケーション","フィットネスアプリケーション","Windowsアプリケーション"],"ko":["블루투스 트레이너 전문가","스마트 트레이너","Wahoo KICKR","FTMS 디바이스","Console First","C# 콘솔 애플리케이션","피트니스 애플리케이션","윈도우 애플리케이션"],"es":["entrenador bluetooth","control de resistencia","aplicaciones de fitness en bicicleta","desarrollo de aplicaciones","Wahoo KICKR","dispositivos FTMS","ciclismo interior","entrenamiento en bicicleta","tecnología bluetooth"],"fr":["entraîneur bluetooth","contrôle de résistance","applications de fitness cycliste","développement d''applications","Wahoo KICKR","appareils FTMS","cyclisme en salle","entraînement cycliste","technologie bluetooth"],"de":["Bluetooth-Trainer","Widerstandssteuerung","Fitness-Anwendungen für das Fahrrad","Anwendungsentwicklung","Wahoo KICKR","FTMS-Geräte","Innenradfahren","Fahrradtraining","Bluetooth-Technologie"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de aplicativos de fitness","bluetooth trainer expert","wahoo kikr","c#","wpf/maui","ftms","aplicativos de bicicletas","resistência de bicicletas","protocolo de comunicação"],"ru":["разработка программ для фитнеса","эксперт bluetooth тренировщика","wahoo kikr","c#","wpf/maui","ftms","программы для велосипеда","сопротивление велосипеда","протокол связи"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات اللياقة البدنية","خبير مدرب بلوتوث","واهو كيكر","c#","wpf/maui","ftms","تطبيقات الدراجات الهوائية","مقاومة الدراجات الهوائية","بروتوكول الاتصال"]}},"owner":"JasonRowe","repo":"Wahoo-KICKR-Randomizer","repoPath":"JasonRowe/Wahoo-KICKR-Randomizer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.533Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bluetooth-trainer-expert","description":"Expert guidance on reverse-engineering, testing, and integrating Bluetooth Smart Trainers (Wahoo/FTMS) for fitness applications. Use when building or debugging cycling apps.","bodyPreview":"# Bluetooth Trainer Expert\n\nThis skill provides a proven workflow for developing biking fitness applications that interact with Smart Trainers (e.g., Wahoo KICKR, FTMS devices). It emphasizes a \"Console First\" approach to isolate connection and protocol logic before attempting UI integration.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n1.  **Console First**: Always prove the protocol logic in a simple C# Console Application (`BikeFitnessConsole`) before touching the main UI (WPF/MAUI).\n2.  **Physical Verification**: T","body":"# Bluetooth Trainer Expert\n\nThis skill provides a proven workflow for developing biking fitness applications that interact with Smart Trainers (e.g., Wahoo KICKR, FTMS devices). It emphasizes a \"Console First\" approach to isolate connection and protocol logic before attempting UI integration.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n1.  **Console First**: Always prove the protocol logic in a simple C# Console Application (`BikeFitnessConsole`) before touching the main UI (WPF/MAUI).\n2.  **Physical Verification**: Telemetry (Success/Fail responses) is insufficient for brake logic. You MUST ask the user to \"Pedal and verify resistance change\" to confirm the device actually engaged the magnet/motor.\n3.  **Protocol Agnosticism**: Support both standard FTMS (`0x1826`) and legacy Wahoo (`0xA026...`) protocols.\n\n## Phase 1: Diagnostic Console App\n\nCreate a lightweight console app to handle scanning, connection, and raw command testing.\n\n**Key Features to Implement:**\n-   **Scanner**: Filter for `0x1826` (FTMS), `0xA026` (Wahoo), and `0x1818` (Power).\n-   **Service Explorer**: List all available Services and Characteristics to confirm UUIDs.\n-   **Indication Handler**: **CRITICAL**. You must subscribe to `Indicate` on the Control Point characteristic *before* sending any write commands. Failure to do so often results in silent failures or \"Attribute Not Found\" errors on writes.\n\n## Data Format (Endianness)\n\n**Bluetooth LE GATT characteristics standardly use Little Endian byte order.**\n\n-   **Reading**: When parsing multi-byte values (e.g., Speed, Power, Time), interpret the *least significant byte first*.\n    -   Example: `0xE8 0x03` -> `0x03E8` -> `1000`.\n-   **Writing**: When constructing commands (e.g., Target Watts, Grade), ensure you serialize `UInt16`/`Int16` values to Little Endian.\n-   **Note**: While standard FTMS and common Wahoo OpCodes (`0x40-0x45`) follow Little Endian, always verify proprietary manufacturer-specific characteristics if behavior is unexpected.\n\n## Phase 2: Protocol Identification & Control Points\n\nIdentify the correct Control Point (CP) for the device.\n\n### 1. FTMS (Fitness Machine Service) - Preferred\n*   **Service UUID**: `00001826-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb`\n*   **Control Point**: `00002ad9-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb` (Fitness Machine Control Point)\n*   **Init Sequence**:\n    1.  Subscribe to CP Indications.\n    2.  Send `0x00` (Request Control).\n    3.  Send `0x07` (Start/Resume).\n\n### 2. Wahoo Legacy (KICKR / SNAP)\n*   **Service UUID**: `a026ee01-0a7d-4ab3-97fa-f1500f9feb8b`\n*   **Control Point**: `a026e005-0a7d-4ab3-97fa-f1500f9feb8b` (Often hidden inside the Power Service `0x1818` on some firmware).\n*   **Init Sequence**:\n    1.  Subscribe to CP Indications.\n    2.  Send `0x00` (Init/Unlock).\n\n## Phase 3: OpCode Discovery Strategy\n\nDifferent devices support different modes. Use the Console App to \"Scan\" OpCodes `0x40` through `0x45` by sending `[OpCode, 0x00]` and observing the Indication response.\n\n*   **Response Format**: `01-OpCode-Result` (Where Result `01` = Success, `04` = Not Supported, `40` = Fail).\n*   **Common OpCodes**:\n    *   `0x40` **Level Mode**: 0-9 discrete levels. Basic.\n    *   `0x41` **Resistance Mode**: 0-100% brake force. Most reliable.\n    *   `0x42` **Sim Mode Enable**: Activates physics engine (Grade/Wind/Weight). **Warning**: Many older or lower-end devices (e.g., KICKR SNAP) return \"Success\" for params but FAIL (`0x40`) when trying to Enable this mode.\n    *   `0x43` **Sim Parameters**: Sets Grade, Weight, Crr, Cw.\n\n## Phase 4: \"Fake\" Simulation Mode (Grade Mapping)\n\nIf the device fails to support Native Sim Mode (`0x42`), you must implement **Grade-to-Resistance Mapping** in software to support \"Hilly\" or \"Mountain\" workouts.\n\n**Recommended Mapping (User Calibrated):**\nMap the visual \"Grade %\" to the device''s \"Resistance %\" (OpCode `0x41`).\n\n| Grade Input | Resistance Output | Feel |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **-10%** | **0.0%** | Coasting / Free spin. |\n| **0%** | **1.0%** | Flat road friction (light). |\n| **20%** | **40.0%** | Steep climb. (Cap at 40% to avoid \"brick wall\"). |\n\n**Logic:**\nUse a piecewise linear function:\n1.  **Downhill (-10 to 0)**: Interpolate 0.0 -> 0.01.\n2.  **Uphill (0 to 20)**: Interpolate 0.01 -> 0.40.\n\n## Phase 5: Telemetry\n\n*   **Power**: Standard `0x2A63` (Cycling Power Measurement).\n*   **Speed/Distance**: Often missing from FTMS on older devices. Calculate locally using **Wheel Revolutions** from the Power Measurement characteristic (Data bytes `flags & 0x10`).\n    *   `Distance = WheelRevs * TireCircumference`\n    *   `Speed = DeltaDistance / DeltaTime`\n*   **Cadence**: Check `0x1816` (Speed & Cadence) or Crank Data in Power (`0x1818`).\n\n## Checklist for Implementation\n\n1.  [ ] **Console Test**: Can you connect and receive Indications?\n2.  [ ] **OpCode Scan**: Which modes return `01` (Success)?\n3.  [ ] **Physical Test**: Does sending `0x41 0x32` (50% res) make it hard to pedal?\n4.  [ ] **Mapping**: Does -10% Grade feel like zero resistance?\n5.  [ ] **UI**: Does the UI display Grade (not raw resistance) to the user?"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:49:30.776Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Windows-focused AI Agents needing Bluetooth connectivity and Smart Trainer control for fitness applications","zh":"非常适合需要蓝牙连接和智能训练器控制的Windows专用AI代理，适用于健身应用","ja":"Windows 専用 AI エージェントに適したもので、Bluetooth 接続と Smart Trainer 制御が可能で、フィットネス アプリケーションに適する","ko":"블루투스 연결 및 스마트 트레이너 제어가 필요한 윈도우专用 AI 에이전트에 적합한 제품으로, 피트니스 애플리케이션에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de inteligencia artificial centrados en Windows que necesitan conectividad Bluetooth y control de entrenador inteligente para aplicaciones de fitness","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle axés sur Windows nécessitant une connectivité Bluetooth et un contrôle d''entraîneur intelligent pour les applications de fitness","de":"Perfekt für Windows-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine Bluetooth-Verbindung und eine Smart-Trainer-Steuerung für Fitnessanwendungen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA com foco no Windows que necessitam de conectividade Bluetooth e controle de Smart Trainer para aplicações de condicionamento físico","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на Windows, требующих подключения Bluetooth и управления Smart Trainer для фитнес-приложений","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يركزون على نظام التشغيل Windows والذين يحتاجون إلى اتصال بلوتوث وسيطرة على جهاز Smart Trainer لتطبيقات اللياقة البدنية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to control resistance on Smart Trainers like Wahoo KICKR using Bluetooth protocols, leveraging a Console First approach for reliable connection logic and UI integration with C# and WPF/MAUI","zh":"赋予代理控制智能训练器（如Wahoo KICKR）上的阻力，使用蓝牙协议，采用控制台优先方法来确保可靠的连接逻辑和C#及WPF/MAUI的UI集成","ja":"Wahoo KICKR などの Smart Trainer で阻力を制御するエージェントを可能にし、Bluetooth プロトコルを使用し、コンソールファーストアプローチで信頼性の高い接続ロジックと C# および WPF/MAUI との UI 統合を実現する","ko":"에이전트가 스마트 트레이너(Wahoo KICKR 등)에서 저항을 제어할 수 있게 해주며, 블루투스 프로토콜을 사용하고, 콘솔优先 접근 방식을 통해 안정적인 연결 로직 및 C# 및 WPF/MAUI와의 UI 통합을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a controlar la resistencia en entrenadores inteligentes como Wahoo KICKR utilizando protocolos Bluetooth, aprovechando un enfoque de Consola Primero para una lógica de conexión confiable y una integración de la interfaz de usuario con C# y WPF/MAUI","fr":"Permet aux agents de contrôler la résistance sur les entraîneurs intelligents comme Wahoo KICKR en utilisant des protocoles Bluetooth, en exploitant une approche Console First pour une logique de connexion fiable et une intégration de l''interface utilisateur avec C# et WPF/MAUI","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die Resistenz auf Smart Trainern wie Wahoo KICKR über Bluetooth-Protokolle zu steuern, indem es einen Console-First-Ansatz für eine zuverlässige Verbindunglogik und eine Benutzeroberflächenintegration mit C# und WPF/MAUI nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a controlar a resistência em Smart Trainers como o Wahoo KICKR usando protocolos Bluetooth, aproveitando uma abordagem Console First para lógica de conexão confiável e integração da interface do usuário com C# e WPF/MAUI","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность управлять сопротивлением на Smart Trainers, таких как Wahoo KICKR, используя протоколы Bluetooth, используя подход Console First для надёжной логики подключения и интеграции интерфейса пользователя с C# и WPF/MAUI","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من التحكم في المقاومة في أجهزة Smart Trainers مثل Wahoo KICKR باستخدام بروتوكولات Bluetooth، مستفيداً من نهج Console First من أجل منطق اتصال موثوق به وتكامل واجهة المستخدم مع C# و WPF/MAUI"},"useCases":{"en":["Developing biking fitness applications with Smart Trainer integration","Automating workout resistance control via Bluetooth","Debugging connection issues with FTMS devices"],"zh":["开发集成智能训练器的自行车健身应用","通过蓝牙自动控制锻炼阻力","调试FTMS设备的连接问题"],"ja":["Smart Trainer 統合のサイクリング フィットネス アプリケーションを開発","Bluetooth 経由でワークアウトの阻力を自動制御","FTMS デバイスの接続問題をデバッグ"],"ko":["스마트 트레이너 통합 자전거 피트니스 애플리케이션 개발","블루투스를 통해 운동 저항 자동 제어","FTMS 장치의 연결 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Desarrollar aplicaciones de fitness de ciclismo con integración de entrenador inteligente","Automatizar el control de resistencia de entrenamiento a través de Bluetooth","Depurar problemas de conexión con dispositivos FTMS"],"fr":["Développer des applications de fitness de cyclisme avec intégration d''entraîneur intelligent","Automatiser le contrôle de la résistance d''entraînement via Bluetooth","Déboguer les problèmes de connexion avec les appareils FTMS"],"de":["Entwicklung von Fitnessanwendungen für Radfahren mit Smart-Trainer-Integration","Automatisierung der Trainingswiderstandskontrolle über Bluetooth","Fehlerbehebung bei Verbindungsproblemen mit FTMS-Geräten"],"pt":["Desenvolver aplicações de condicionamento físico para bicicletas com integração de Smart Trainer","Automatizar o controle de resistência de treinamento via Bluetooth","Depurar problemas de conexão com dispositivos FTMS"],"ru":["Разработка фитнес-приложений для велосипедов с интеграцией Smart Trainer","Автоматизация управления сопротивлением тренировки через Bluetooth","Отладка проблем подключения с устройствами FTMS"],"ar":["تنمية تطبيقات اللياقة البدنية لدراجات الهوائية مع دمج جهاز Smart Trainer","توفير التحكم التلقائي في مقاومة التمرين عبر بلوتوث","تصحيح مشاكل الاتصال مع أجهزة FTMS"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Windows environment","Limited to Smart Trainers supporting Bluetooth connectivity","C# Console Application and WPF/MAUI expertise recommended"],"zh":["需要Windows环境","仅限支持蓝牙连接的智能训练器","建议具有C#控制台应用程序和WPF/MAUI专业知识"],"ja":["Windows 環境が必要","Bluetooth 接続をサポートする Smart Trainer 限定","C# コンソール アプリケーションおよび WPF/MAUI の専門知識が推奨"],"ko":["윈도우 환경이 필요","블루투스 연결을 지원하는 스마트 트레이너만 해당","C# 콘솔 애플리케이션 및 WPF/MAUI 전문 지식이 권장"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Windows","Limitado a entrenadores inteligentes que admiten conectividad Bluetooth","Se recomienda experiencia en aplicaciones de consola C# y WPF/MAUI"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Windows","Limité aux entraîneurs intelligents prenant en charge la connectivité Bluetooth","Expérience recommandée dans les applications de console C# et WPF/MAUI"],"de":["Benötigt Windows-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf Smart-Trainer, die eine Bluetooth-Verbindung unterstützen","Erfahrung mit C#-Konsolenanwendungen und WPF/MAUI wird empfohlen"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Windows","Limitado a Smart Trainers que suportam conectividade Bluetooth","Conhecimento recomendado de aplicativos de console C# e WPF/MAUI"],"ru":["Требуется среда Windows","Ограничен до Smart Trainers, поддерживающих подключение Bluetooth","Рекомендуется опыт работы с консольными приложениями C# и WPF/MAUI"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة نظام 