围内使用","ja":"リバースエンジニアリング対策は、ソフトウェアの解析を防ぐためのセキュリティ技術です","ko":"반逆향 기술은 소프트웨어의 역공학을 방지하는 보안 기술로, 권한 있는 사용자만 사용할 수 있습니다","es":"Las técnicas anti-reversing ayudan a proteger el software contra la ingeniería inversa. Aprende a implementar estas técnicas en tus proyectos.","fr":"Les techniques anti-reversing aident à protéger les logiciels contre l''ingénierie inverse. Apprenez à mettre en œuvre ces techniques dans vos projets.","de":"Anti-Reversing-Techniken helfen, Software vor Reverse-Engineering zu schützen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie diese Techniken in Ihren Projekten umsetzen.","pt":"Técnicas anti-reversing são métodos utilizados para proteger o código contra engenharia reversa. Elas são essenciais para garantir a segurança e a integridad...","ru":"Техники анти-реверс-инжиниринга - это методы, используемые для защиты кода от обратной разработки. Они необходимы для обеспечения безопасности и целостности ...","ar":"تقنيات منع العكس هي طرق تستخدم لحماية الكود من الهندسة العكسية. هي أساسية لضمان أمان وتكامل التطبيق.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["防止未经授权的软件逆向分析","确保软件安全和保密","需要在授权范围内使用","用于CTF、授权渗透测试、恶意软件分析和安全研究","需要明确的书面许可","需要记录使用范围"],"ja":["リバースエンジニアリングを防ぐ","ソフトウェアのセキュリティと機密性を確保","認可された範囲内でのみ使用","CTF、認可されたペネトレーションテスト、悪意のあるソフトウェア分析、セキュリティ研究に使用","明確な書面による許可が必要","使用範囲を文書化する必要がある"],"ko":["소프트웨어의 역공학을 방지","소프트웨어의 보안과 기밀성을 보장","권한 있는 사용자만 사용","CTF, 권한 있는 펜트리스트 테스트, 악성 코드 분석, 보안 연구에 사용","明确한 서면 허가 필요","사용 범위를 문서화해야 함"],"es":["Protección contra la ingeniería inversa","Técnicas de ofuscamiento de código","Análisis de vulnerabilidades","Implementación de medidas de seguridad","Verificación de autorización y alcance"],"fr":["Protection contre l''ingénierie inverse","Techniques de brouillage de code","Analyse de vulnérabilités","Mise en œuvre de mesures de sécurité","Vérification d''autorisation et de portée"],"de":["Schutz vor Reverse-Engineering","Code-Obfuskationstechniken","Analyse von Schwachstellen","Umsetzung von Sicherheitsmaßnahmen","Überprüfung von Autorisierung und Umfang"],"pt":["Proteção contra engenharia reversa","Técnicas de ofuscação de código","Prevenção de análise de malware","Garantia de segurança da aplicação","Métodos de autenticação e autorização"],"ru":["Защита от обратной разработки","Техники ऑफусцирования кода","Предотвращение анализа вредоносного ПО","Обеспечение безопасности приложения","Методы аутентификации и авторизации"],"ar":["حماية من الهندسة العكسية","طرق تعقيم الكود","منع تحليل البرامج الضارة","ضمان أمان التطبيق","طرق التحقق والتصريح"]},"keywords":{"zh":["反逆向技术","安全技术","软件逆向分析","授权使用","CTF","恶意软件分析","安全研究"],"ja":["リバースエンジニアリング対策","セキュリティ技術","ソフトウェア解析","認可された使用","CTF","悪意のあるソフトウェア分析","セキュリティ研究"],"ko":["반逆향 기술","보안 기술","소프트웨어 역공학","권한 있는 사용","CTF","악성 코드 분석","보안 연구"],"es":["técnicas anti-reversing","ingeniería inversa","ofuscamiento de código","análisis de vulnerabilidades","seguridad de software","desarrollo de software seguro"],"fr":["techniques anti-reversing","ingénierie inverse","brouillage de code","analyse de vulnérabilités","sécurité de logiciels","développement de logiciels sécurisés"],"de":["Anti-Reversing-Techniken","Reverse-Engineering","Code-Obfuskation","Schwachstellenanalyse","Software-Sicherheit","sichere Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["técnicas anti-reversing","proteção de código","engenharia reversa","ofuscação de código","análise de malware","segurança da aplicação"],"ru":["техники анти-реверс-инжиниринга","защита кода","обратная разработка","офусцирование кода","анализ вредоносного ПО","безопасность приложения"],"ar":["تقنيات منع العكس","حماية الكود","الهندسة العكسية","تعقيم الكود","تحليل البرامج الضارة","أمان التطبيق"]}},"owner":"haxllo","repo":"repolens","repoPath":"haxllo/repolens","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.533Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"anti-reversing-techniques","description":"Understand anti-reversing, obfuscation, and protection techniques encountered during software analysis. Use when analyzing protected binaries, bypassing anti-debugging for authorized analysis, or understanding software protection mechanisms.","bodyPreview":"> **AUTHORIZED USE ONLY**: This skill contains dual-use security techniques. Before proceeding with any bypass or analysis:\n>\n> 1. **Verify authorization**: Confirm you have explicit written permission from the software owner, or are operating within a legitimate security context (CTF, authorized pentest, malware analysis, security research)\n> 2. **Document scope**: Ensure your activities fall within the defined scope of your authorization\n> 3. **Legal compliance**: Understand that unauthorized","body":"> **AUTHORIZED USE ONLY**: This skill contains dual-use security techniques. Before proceeding with any bypass or analysis:\n>\n> 1. **Verify authorization**: Confirm you have explicit written permission from the software owner, or are operating within a legitimate security context (CTF, authorized pentest, malware analysis, security research)\n> 2. **Document scope**: Ensure your activities fall within the defined scope of your authorization\n> 3. **Legal compliance**: Understand that unauthorized bypassing of software protection may violate laws (CFAA, DMCA anti-circumvention, etc.)\n>\n> **Legitimate use cases**: Malware analysis, authorized penetration testing, CTF competitions, academic security research, analyzing software you own/have rights to\n\n# Anti-Reversing Techniques\n\nUnderstanding protection mechanisms encountered during authorized software analysis, security research, and malware analysis. This knowledge helps analysts bypass protections to complete legitimate analysis tasks.\n\n## Anti-Debugging Techniques\n\n### Windows Anti-Debugging\n\n#### API-Based Detection\n\n```c\n// IsDebuggerPresent\nif (IsDebuggerPresent()) {\n    exit(1);\n}\n\n// CheckRemoteDebuggerPresent\nBOOL debugged = FALSE;\nCheckRemoteDebuggerPresent(GetCurrentProcess(), &debugged);\nif (debugged) exit(1);\n\n// NtQueryInformationProcess\ntypedef NTSTATUS (NTAPI *pNtQueryInformationProcess)(\n    HANDLE, PROCESSINFOCLASS, PVOID, ULONG, PULONG);\n\nDWORD debugPort = 0;\nNtQueryInformationProcess(\n    GetCurrentProcess(),\n    ProcessDebugPort,        // 7\n    &debugPort,\n    sizeof(debugPort),\n    NULL\n);\nif (debugPort != 0) exit(1);\n\n// Debug flags\nDWORD debugFlags = 0;\nNtQueryInformationProcess(\n    GetCurrentProcess(),\n    ProcessDebugFlags,       // 0x1F\n    &debugFlags,\n    sizeof(debugFlags),\n    NULL\n);\nif (debugFlags == 0) exit(1);  // 0 means being debugged\n```\n\n**Bypass Approaches:**\n\n```python\n# x64dbg: ScyllaHide plugin\n# Patches common anti-debug checks\n\n# Manual patching in debugger:\n# - Set IsDebuggerPresent return to 0\n# - Patch PEB.BeingDebugged to 0\n# - Hook NtQueryInformationProcess\n\n# IDAPython: Patch checks\nida_bytes.patch_byte(check_addr, 0x90)  # NOP\n```\n\n#### PEB-Based Detection\n\n```c\n// Direct PEB access\n#ifdef _WIN64\n    PPEB peb = (PPEB)__readgsqword(0x60);\n#else\n    PPEB peb = (PPEB)__readfsdword(0x30);\n#endif\n\n// BeingDebugged flag\nif (peb->BeingDebugged) exit(1);\n\n// NtGlobalFlag\n// Debugged: 0x70 (FLG_HEAP_ENABLE_TAIL_CHECK |\n//                 FLG_HEAP_ENABLE_FREE_CHECK |\n//                 FLG_HEAP_VALIDATE_PARAMETERS)\nif (peb->NtGlobalFlag & 0x70) exit(1);\n\n// Heap flags\nPDWORD heapFlags = (PDWORD)((PBYTE)peb->ProcessHeap + 0x70);\nif (*heapFlags & 0x50000062) exit(1);\n```\n\n**Bypass Approaches:**\n\n```assembly\n; In debugger, modify PEB directly\n; x64dbg: dump at gs:[60] (x64) or fs:[30] (x86)\n; Set BeingDebugged (offset 2) to 0\n; Clear NtGlobalFlag (offset 0xBC for x64)\n```\n\n#### Timing-Based Detection\n\n```c\n// RDTSC timing\nuint64_t start = __rdtsc();\n// ... some code ...\nuint64_t end = __rdtsc();\nif ((end - start) > THRESHOLD) exit(1);\n\n// QueryPerformanceCounter\nLARGE_INTEGER start, end, freq;\nQueryPerformanceFrequency(&freq);\nQueryPerformanceCounter(&start);\n// ... code ...\nQueryPerformanceCounter(&end);\ndouble elapsed = (double)(end.QuadPart - start.QuadPart) / freq.QuadPart;\nif (elapsed > 0.1) exit(1);  // Too slow = debugger\n\n// GetTickCount\nDWORD start = GetTickCount();\n// ... code ...\nif (GetTickCount() - start > 1000) exit(1);\n```\n\n**Bypass Approaches:**\n\n```\n- Use hardware breakpoints instead of software\n- Patch timing checks\n- Use VM with controlled time\n- Hook timing APIs to return consistent values\n```\n\n#### Exception-Based Detection\n\n```c\n// SEH-based detection\n__try {\n    __asm { int 3 }  // Software breakpoint\n}\n__except(EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) {\n    // Normal execution: exception caught\n    return;\n}\n// Debugger ate the exception\nexit(1);\n\n// VEH-based detection\nLONG CALLBACK VectoredHandler(PEXCEPTION_POINTERS ep) {\n    if (ep->ExceptionRecord->ExceptionCode == EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT) {\n        ep->ContextRecord->Rip++;  // Skip INT3\n        return EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_EXECUTION;\n    }\n    return EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH;\n}\n```\n\n### Linux Anti-Debugging\n\n```c\n// ptrace self-trace\nif (ptrace(PTRACE_TRACEME, 0, NULL, NULL) == -1) {\n    // Already being traced\n    exit(1);\n}\n\n// /proc/self/status\nFILE *f = fopen(\"/proc/self/status\", \"r\");\nchar line[256];\nwhile (fgets(line, sizeof(line), f)) {\n    if (strncmp(line, \"TracerPid:\", 10) == 0) {\n        int tracer_pid = atoi(line + 10);\n        if (tracer_pid != 0) exit(1);\n    }\n}\n\n// Parent process check\nif (getppid() != 1 && strcmp(get_process_name(getppid()), \"bash\") != 0) {\n    // Unusual parent (might be debugger)\n}\n```\n\n**Bypass Approaches:**\n\n```bash\n# LD_PRELOAD to hook ptrace\n# Compile: gcc -shared -fPIC -o hook.so hook.c\nlong ptrace(int request, ...) {\n    return 0;  // Always succeed\n}\n\n# Usage\nLD_PRELOAD=./hook.so ./target\n```\n\n## Anti-VM Detection\n\n### Hardware Fingerprinting\n\n```c\n// CPUID-based detection\nint cpuid_info[4];\n__cpuid(cpuid_info, 1);\n// Check hypervisor bit (bit 31 of ECX)\nif (cpuid_info[2] & (1 << 31)) {\n    // Running in hypervisor\n}\n\n// CPUID brand string\n__cpuid(cpuid_info, 0x40000000);\nchar vendor[13] = {0};\nmemcpy(vendor, &cpuid_info[1], 12);\n// \"VMwareVMware\", \"Microsoft Hv\", \"KVMKVMKVM\", \"VBoxVBoxVBox\"\n\n// MAC address prefix\n// VMware: 00:0C:29, 00:50:56\n// VirtualBox: 08:00:27\n// Hyper-V: 00:15:5D\n```\n\n### Registry/File Detection\n\n```c\n// Windows registry keys\n// HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\VMware, Inc.\\VMware Tools\n// HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Oracle\\VirtualBox Guest Additions\n// HKLM\\HARDWARE\\ACPI\\DSDT\\VBOX__\n\n// Files\n// C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\vmmouse.sys\n// C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\vmhgfs.sys\n// C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\VBoxMouse.sys\n\n// Processes\n// vmtoolsd.exe, vmwaretray.exe\n// VBoxService.exe, VBoxTray.exe\n```\n\n### Timing-Based VM Detection\n\n```c\n// VM exits cause timing anomalies\nuint64_t start = __rdtsc();\n__cpuid(cpuid_info, 0);  // Causes VM exit\nuint64_t end = __rdtsc();\nif ((end - start) > 500) {\n    // Likely in VM (CPUID takes longer)\n}\n```\n\n**Bypass Approaches:**\n\n```\n- Use bare-metal analysis environment\n- Harden VM (remove guest tools, change MAC)\n- Patch detection code\n- Use specialized analysis VMs (FLARE-VM)\n```\n\n## Code Obfuscation\n\n### Control Flow Obfuscation\n\n#### Control Flow Flattening\n\n```c\n// Original\nif (cond) {\n    func_a();\n} else {\n    func_b();\n}\nfunc_c();\n\n// Flattened\nint state = 0;\nwhile (1) {\n    switch (state) {\n        case 0:\n            state = cond ? 1 : 2;\n            break;\n        case 1:\n            func_a();\n            state = 3;\n            break;\n        case 2:\n            func_b();\n            state = 3;\n            break;\n        case 3:\n            func_c();\n            return;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Analysis Approach:**\n\n- Identify state variable\n- Map state transitions\n- Reconstruct original flow\n- Tools: D-810 (IDA), SATURN\n\n#### Opaque Predicates\n\n```c\n// Always true, but complex to analyze\nint x = rand();\nif ((x * x) >= 0) {  // Always true\n    real_code();\n} else {\n    junk_code();  // Dead code\n}\n\n// Always false\nif ((x * (x + 1)) % 2 == 1) {  // Product of consecutive = even\n    junk_code();\n}\n```\n\n**Analysis Approach:**\n\n- Identify constant expressions\n- Symbolic execution to prove predicates\n- Pattern matching for known opaque predicates\n\n### Data Obfuscation\n\n#### String Encryption\n\n```c\n// XOR encryption\nchar decrypt_string(char *enc, int len, char key) {\n    char *dec = malloc(len + 1);\n    for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n        dec[i] = enc[i] ^ key;\n    }\n    dec[len] = 0;\n    return dec;\n}\n\n// Stack strings\nchar url[20];\nurl[0] = ''h''; url[1] = ''t''; url[2] = ''t''; url[3] = ''p'';\nurl[4] = '':''; url[5] = ''/''; url[6] = ''/'';\n// ...\n```\n\n**Analysis Approach:**\n\n```python\n# FLOSS for automatic string deobfuscation\nfloss malware.exe\n\n# IDAPython string decryption\ndef decrypt_xor(ea, length, key):\n    result = \"\"\n    for i in range(length):\n        byte = ida_bytes.get_byte(ea + i)\n        result += chr(byte ^ key)\n    return result\n```\n\n#### API Obfuscation\n\n```c\n// Dynamic API resolution\ntypedef HANDLE (WINAPI *pCreateFileW)(LPCWSTR, DWORD, DWORD,\n    LPSECURITY_ATTRIBUTES, DWORD, DWORD, HANDLE);\n\nHMODULE kernel32 = LoadLibraryA(\"kernel32.dll\");\npCreateFileW myCreateFile = (pCreateFileW)GetProcAddress(\n    kernel32, \"CreateFileW\");\n\n// API hashing\nDWORD hash_api(char *name) {\n    DWORD hash = 0;\n    while (*name) {\n        hash = ((hash >> 13) | (hash << 19)) + *name++;\n    }\n    return hash;\n}\n// Resolve by hash comparison instead of string\n```\n\n**Analysis Approach:**\n\n- Identify hash algorithm\n- Build hash database of known APIs\n- Use HashDB plugin for IDA\n- Dynamic analysis to resolve at runtime\n\n### Instruction-Level Obfuscation\n\n#### Dead Code Insertion\n\n```asm\n; Original\nmov eax, 1\n\n; With dead code\npush ebx           ; Dead\nmov eax, 1\npop ebx            ; Dead\nxor ecx, ecx       ; Dead\nadd ecx, ecx       ; Dead\n```\n\n#### Instruction Substitution\n\n```asm\n; Original: xor eax, eax (set to 0)\n; Substitutions:\nsub eax, eax\nmov eax, 0\nand eax, 0\nlea eax, [0]\n\n; Original: mov eax, 1\n; Substitutions:\nxor eax, eax\ninc eax\n\npush 1\npop eax\n```\n\n## Packing and Encryption\n\n### Common Packers\n\n```\nUPX          - Open source, easy to unpack\nThemida      - Commercial, VM-based protection\nVMProtect    - Commercial, code virtualization\nASPack       - Compression packer\nPECompact    - Compression packer\nEnigma       - Commercial protector\n```\n\n### Unpacking Methodology\n\n```\n1. Identify packer (DIE, Exeinfo PE, PEiD)\n\n2. Static unpacking (if known packer):\n   - UPX: upx -d packed.exe\n   - Use existing unpackers\n\n3. Dynamic unpacking:\n   a. Find Original Entry Point (OEP)\n   b. Set breakpoint on OEP\n   c. Dump memory when OEP reached\n   d. Fix import table (Scylla, ImpREC)\n\n4. OEP finding techniques:\n   - Hardware breakpoint on stack (ESP trick)\n   - Break on common API calls (GetCommandLineA)\n   - Trace and look for typical entry patterns\n```\n\n### Manual Unpacking Example\n\n```\n1. Load packed binary in x64dbg\n2. Note entry point (packer stub)\n3. Use ESP trick:\n   - Run to entry\n   - Set hardware breakpoint on [ESP]\n   - Run until breakpoint hits (after PUSHAD/POPAD)\n4. Look for JMP to OEP\n5. At OEP, use Scylla to:\n   - Dump process\n   - Find imports (IAT autosearch)\n   - Fix dump\n```\n\n## Virtualization-Based Protection\n\n### Code Virtualization\n\n```\nOriginal x86 code is converted to custom bytecode\ninterpreted by embedded VM at runtime.\n\nOriginal:     VM Protected:\nmov eax, 1    push vm_context\nadd eax, 2    call vm_entry\n              ; VM interprets bytecode\n              ; equivalent to original\n```\n\n### Analysis Approaches\n\n```\n1. Identify VM components:\n   - VM entry (dispatcher)\n   - Handler table\n   - Bytecode location\n   - Virtual registers/stack\n\n2. Trace execution:\n   - Log handler calls\n   - Map bytecode to operations\n   - Understand instruction set\n\n3. Lifting/devirtualization:\n   - Map VM instructions back to native\n   - Tools: VMAttack, SATURN, NoVmp\n\n4. Symbolic execution:\n   - Analyze VM semantically\n   - angr, Triton\n```\n\n## Bypass Strategies Summary\n\n### General Principles\n\n1. **Understand the protection**: Identify what technique is used\n2. **Find the check**: Locate protection code in binary\n3. **Patch or hook**: Modify check to always pass\n4. **Use appropriate tools**: ScyllaHide, x64dbg plugins\n5. **Document findings**: Keep notes on bypassed protections\n\n### Tool Recommendations\n\n```\nAnti-debug bypass:    ScyllaHide, TitanHide\nUnpacking:           x64dbg + Scylla, OllyDumpEx\nDeobfuscation:       D-810, SATURN, miasm\nVM analysis:         VMAttack, NoVmp, manual tracing\nString decryption:   FLOSS, custom scripts\nSymbolic execution:  angr, Triton\n```\n\n### Ethical Considerations\n\nThis knowledge should only be used for:\n\n- Authorized security research\n- Malware analysis (defensive)\n- CTF competitions\n- Understanding protections for legitimate purposes\n- Educational purposes\n\nNever use to bypass protections for:\n\n- Software piracy\n- Unauthorized access\n- Malicious purposes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:49:22.059Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced Security Agents requiring expertise in dual-use security techniques and reverse engineering bypass methods.","zh":"非常适合需要双用途安全技术和反向工程绕过方法专业知识的高级安全代理。","ja":"ダブルユースセキュリティ技術とリバースエンジニアリングバイパス方法の専門知識を必要とする高度なセキュリティエージェントに最適です。","ko":"이중 사용 보안 기술 및 역공학 우회 방법에 대한 전문 지식을 필요로하는 고급 보안 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Seguridad Avanzados que requieren experiencia en técnicas de seguridad de doble uso y métodos de bypass de ingeniería inversa.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Sécurité Avancés nécessitant une expertise dans les techniques de sécurité à double usage et les méthodes de contournement d''ingénierie inverse.","de":"Perfekt für Advanced Security Agents, die Expertenwissen in dual-use Sicherheitstechniken und Reverse-Engineering-Bypass-Methoden erfordern.","pt":"Perfect for Advanced Security Agents requiring expertise in dual-use security techniques and reverse engineering bypass methods.","ru":"Perfect for Advanced Security Agents requiring expertise in dual-use security techniques and reverse engineering bypass methods.","ar":"Perfect for Advanced Security Agents requiring expertise in dual-use security techniques and reverse engineering bypass methods."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to employ anti-reversing techniques, including code obfuscation, anti-debugging, and anti-disassembly methods, ensuring secure software development and protection against unauthorized access, utilizing protocols such as CTF and authorized pentest frameworks.","zh":"赋予代理使用反反编译技术的能力，包括代码混淆、反调试和反反汇编方法，确保安全的软件开发和保护免受未经授权的访问，利用诸如CTF和授权渗透测试框架的协议。","ja":"エージェントがコードの複雑化、アンチデバッグ、アンチディスアセンブリなどのアンチリバースエンジニアリング技術を使用できるようにし、CTFや認可されたペネトレーションテストフレームワークなどのプロトコルを使用して、安全なソフトウェア開発と未認可アクセスからの保護を保証する。","ko":"에이전트가 코드 난화, 디버깅 방지, 디스어셈블리 방지 등의 반전조사 기술을 사용할 수 있도록하여, CTF 및 승인된 침투 테스트 프레임워크와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 안전한 소프트웨어 개발 및 비인가 액세스로부터의 보호를 보장한다.","es":"Permite a los agentes emplear técnicas anti-reversing, incluyendo ofuscamiento de código, anti-depuración y métodos anti-desensamblado, garantizando el desarrollo de software seguro y la protección contra el acceso no autorizado, utilizando protocolos como CTF y marcos de pruebas de penetración autorizados.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''employer des techniques anti-reversing, notamment l''obfuscation de code, le débogage anti et les méthodes anti-désassemblage, garantissant un développement de logiciels sécurisés et une protection contre l''accès non autorisé, en utilisant des protocoles tels que CTF et des cadres de test de pénétration autorisés.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Anti-Reversing-Techniken anzuwenden, einschließlich Code-Obfuskation, Anti-Debugging und Anti-Disassembly-Methoden, um sichere Softwareentwicklung und Schutz vor unbefugtem Zugriff zu gewährleisten, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie CTF und autorisierten Pentest-Frameworks.","pt":"Empowers agents to employ anti-reversing techniques, including code obfuscation, anti-debugging, and anti-disassembly methods, ensuring secure software development and protection against unauthorized access, utilizing protocols such as CTF and authorized pentest frameworks.","ru":"Empowers agents to employ anti-reversing techniques, including code obfuscation, anti-debugging, and anti-disassembly methods, ensuring secure software development and protection against unauthorized access, utilizing protocols such as CTF and authorized pentest frameworks.","ar":"Empowers agents to employ anti-reversing techniques, including code obfuscation, anti-debugging, and anti-disassembly methods, ensuring secure software development and protection against unauthorized access, utilizing protocols such as CTF and authorized pentest frameworks."},"useCases":{"en":["Bypassing reverse engineering attempts","Conducting authorized security research and malware analysis","Implementing secure coding practices to prevent unauthorized access"],"zh":["绕过反向工程尝试","进行授权的安全研究和恶意软件分析","实施安全编码实践以防止未经授权的访问"],"ja":["リバースエンジニアリングの試みをバイパスする","認可されたセキュリティ研究とマルウェア分析を実施する","未認可アクセスを防止するためにセキュアコーディングの実践を実施する"],"ko":["역공학 시도를 우회한다.","승인된 보안 연구 및 악성 코드 분석을 수행한다.","비인가 액세스를 방지하기 위한 보안 코딩 관행을 구현한다."],"es":["Contornar intentos de ingeniería inversa","Realizar investigaciones de seguridad autorizadas y análisis de malware","Implementar prácticas de codificación seguras para prevenir el acceso no autorizado"],"fr":["Contourner les tentatives d''ingénierie inverse","Effectuer des recherches de sécurité autorisées et des analyses de logiciels malveillants","Mettre en œuvre des pratiques de codage sécurisées pour prévenir l''accès non autorisé"],"de":["Umgehung von Reverse-Engineering-Versuchen","Durchführung von autorisierten Sicherheitsforschung und Malware-Analyse","Implementierung sicherer Codierungspraktiken, um unbefugten Zugriff zu verhindern"],"pt":["Bypassing reverse engineering attempts","Conducting authorized security research and malware analysis","Implementing secure coding practices to prevent unauthorized access"],"ru":["Bypassing reverse engineering attempts","Conducting authorized security research and malware analysis","Implementing secure coding practices to prevent unauthorized access"],"ar":["Bypassing reverse engineering attempts","Conducting authorized security research and malware analysis","Implementing secure coding practices to prevent unauthorized access"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires explicit written permission from software owners or operating within a legitimate security context","Must comply with legal regulations regarding dual-use security techniques","Limited to authorized personnel and use cases"],"zh":["需要软件所有者或在合法安全上下文中明确的书面许可","必须遵守有关双用途安全技术的法律法规","仅限于授权人员和使用案例"],"ja":["ソフトウェア所有者または正当なセキュリティコンテキストからの明示的な書面による許可が必要","ダブルユースセキュリティ技術に関する法規制に従う必要がある","認可された人員および使用ケースのみに限定される"],"ko":["소프트웨어 소유자 또는 합법적인 보안 상황에서의 명시적인 서면 허가가 필요하다.","이중 사용 보안 기술과 관련된 법적 규정을 준수해야 한다.","승인된 인원 및 사용 사례에만 제한된다."],"es":["Requiere permiso escrito explícito de los propietarios del software o operar dentro de un contexto de seguridad legítimo","Debe cumplir con las regulaciones legales sobre técnicas de seguridad de doble uso","Limitado a personal autorizado y casos de uso"],"fr":["Nécessite une autorisation écrite explicite des propriétaires de logiciels ou opère dans un contexte de sécurité légitime","Doit se conformer aux réglementations légales concernant les techniques de sécurité à double usage","Limité au personnel autorisé et aux cas d''utilisation"],"de":["Erfordert eine explizite schriftliche Genehmigung der Software-Besitzer oder eine Arbeit in einem legitimen Sicherheitskontext","Muss den gesetzlichen Vorschriften über dual-use Sicherheitstechniken entsprechen","Begrenzt auf autorisiertes Personal und Anwendungsfälle"],"pt":["Requires explicit written permission from software owners or operating within a legitimate security context","Must comply with legal regulations regarding dual-use security techniques","Limited to authorized personnel and use cases"],"ru":["Requires explicit written permission from software owners or operating within a legitimate security context","Must comply with legal regulations regarding dual-use security techniques","Limited to authorized personnel and use cases"],"ar":["Requires explicit written permission from software owners or operating within a legitimate security context","Must comply with legal regulations regarding dual-use security techniques","Limited to authorized personnel and use cases"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
