 problemas","Eliminación de soluciones temporales y parches","Mejora de la calidad y la estabilidad del código"],"fr":["Approche structurée pour la résolution de problèmes","Identification de la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions","Résolution efficace et efficiente des problèmes","Élimination des solutions temporaires et des patchs","Amélioration de la qualité et de la stabilité du code"],"de":["Strukturierter Ansatz zur Lösung von Problemen","Identifizierung der Ursache bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen werden","Effiziente und effektive Lösung von Problemen","Beseitigung von temporären Lösungen und Patches","Verbesserung der Qualität und Stabilität des Codes"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz","Evita soluções improvisadas","Melhora a eficiência na resolução de problemas","Reduz o tempo de depuração","Aumenta a qualidade do código"],"ru":["Выявление коренной причины","Избегает импровизированных решений","Улучшает эффективность в решении проблем","Сокращает время отладки","Повышает качество кода"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري","تجنب الحلول العرضية","تحسين الفعالية في حل المشاكل","تقليل وقت التصحيح","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","技术问题解决","根因分析","随机修复","掩盖潜在问题","测试失败","bug 修复"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグ","テクニカルイシュー解決","根本原因分析","ランダムな修復","潜在的な問題のマスキング","テスト失敗","バグ修復"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술적인 문제 해결","근본 원인 분석","임의의 수정","잠재적인 문제의 은폐","테스트 실패","버그 수정"],"es":["depuración sistemática","resolución de problemas","causa raíz","solución eficiente","calidad del código","estabilidad del código","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["débogage systématique","résolution de problèmes","cause profonde","solution efficace","qualité du code","stabilité du code","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","Lösung von Problemen","Ursache","effiziente Lösung","Code-Qualität","Code-Stabilität","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","causa raiz","resolução de problemas","eficiência","qualidade de código","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["системная отладка","коренная причина","решение проблем","эффективность","качество кода","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التصحيح المنهجي","السبب الجذري","حل المشاكل","الفعالية","جودة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"geodez","repo":"vending-admin-v2","repoPath":"geodez/vending-admin-v2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.534Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:50:50.943Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Agents requiring a structured approach to issue resolution, emphasizing root cause analysis over symptomatic fixes.","zh":"适合需要对问题解决采用结构化方法的技术代理，强调根因分析而非症状性修复。","ja":"技術エージェントが問題解決に対して構造化されたアプローチを必要とする場合に適しています。根本原因の分析を症状の修復よりも重視しています。","ko":"기술 에이전트가 문제 해결을 위해 구조화된 접근 방식을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다. 증상적인 해결보다 근본 원인 분석을 강조합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes técnicos que requieren un enfoque estructurado para la resolución de problemas, enfatizando el análisis de causa raíz sobre soluciones sintomáticas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents techniques nécessitant une approche structurée pour la résolution des problèmes, mettant l''accent sur l''analyse de la cause profonde plutôt que sur les solutions symptomatiques.","de":"Ideal für technische Agenten, die einen strukturierten Ansatz für die Problemlösung benötigen, wobei die Analyse der Ursache betont wird und nicht die symptomatischen Lösungen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Técnicos que requerem uma abordagem estruturada para resolução de problemas, enfatizando a análise da causa raiz em vez de soluções sintomáticas.","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов, требующих структурированного подхода к решению проблем, подчеркивающего анализ коренной причины над симптоматическими исправлениями.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الفنيين الذين يحتاجون إلى نهج منظم ل حل المشكلات، مع التركيز على تحليل السبب الجذري أكثر من الإصلاحات الأعراضية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to conduct thorough investigations of technical issues, adhering to the core principle of identifying root causes before proposing fixes, thereby ensuring that solutions are robust and effective, leveraging the Iron Law of NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST.","zh":"赋予代理进行彻底的技术问题调查的能力，遵循找出根本原因然后再提出解决方案的核心原则，从而确保解决方案是强健有效的，利用没有根本原因分析就不进行修复的铁律。","ja":"技術エージェントが技術的な問題について徹底的な調査を実施できるようにし、根本原因を特定した上で修復を提案するという基本原則に従うことで、ロバストで効果的な解決策を提供します。根本原因を分析せずに修復を実施しないという鉄則を活用します。","ko":"기술 에이전트가 기술적인 문제에 대한 철저한 조사를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 근본 원인을 식별한 후에 해결책을 제안하는 기본 원칙을 따라 강력하고 효과적인 해결책을 제공합니다. 근본 원인 분석 없이 수정을 수행하지 않는다는 철칙을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar investigaciones exhaustivas de problemas técnicos, siguiendo el principio fundamental de identificar las causas raíz antes de proponer soluciones, garantizando así que las soluciones sean robustas y efectivas, aprovechando la Ley de Hierro de NO SOLUCIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO.","fr":"Habilite les agents à mener des enquêtes approfondies sur les problèmes techniques, en suivant le principe fondamental d''identifier les causes profondes avant de proposer des solutions, garantissant ainsi que les solutions soient robustes et efficaces, en tirant parti de la Loi de Fer de PAS DE CORRECTIONS SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, gründliche Untersuchungen von technischen Problemen durchzuführen, indem sie dem grundlegenden Prinzip folgen, die Ursachen zu identifizieren, bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen werden, und somit sicherstellen, dass die Lösungen robust und effektiv sind, indem sie das Eisenrecht von KEINE REPARIATUREN OHNE URSACHENFORSCHUNG ZUERST nutzen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes realizem investigações aprofundadas de problemas técnicos, aderindo ao princípio básico de identificar as causas raiz antes de propor soluções, garantindo assim que as soluções sejam robustas e eficazes, utilizando a Lei de Ferro de NENHUMA SOLUÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные расследования технических проблем, придерживаясь основного принципа выявления коренных причин до предложения исправлений, тем самым гарантируя, что решения являются прочными и эффективными, используя Железный Закон НИКАКИХ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إجراء تحقيقات شاملة لقضايا فنية، مع الالتزام بمبدأ أساسي هو تحديد الأسباب الجذرية قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات، مما يضمن بذلك أن تكون الحلول قوية وفعالة، مستخدمين قانون الحديد لا إصلاح بدون تحقيق السبب الجذري أولا."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex software bugs through systematic analysis","Investigating test failures to identify underlying issues","Conducting root cause analysis for recurring technical problems"],"zh":["通过系统分析来调试复杂的软件错误","为了找出潜在问题而调查测试失败","进行反复出现的技术问题的根本原因分析"],"ja":["システム分析を通じて複雑なソフトウェアのバグをデバッグする","潜在的な問題を特定するためにテストの失敗を調査する","反復して発生する技術的な問題の根本原因分析を実施する"],"ko":["시스템 분석을 통해 복잡한 소프트웨어 버그를 디버깅하는 것","潜在적인 문제를 식별하기 위해 테스트 실패를 조사하는 것","재発生하는 기술적인 문제의 근본 원인 분석을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Depuración de errores de software complejos a través del análisis sistemático","Investigación de fallos de prueba para identificar problemas subyacentes","Realización del análisis de causa raíz para problemas técnicos recurrentes"],"fr":["Débogage de bogues de logiciel complexes par analyse systématique","Enquête sur les échecs de test pour identifier les problèmes sous-jacents","Réalisations de l''analyse de cause profonde pour les problèmes techniques récurrents"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung komplexer Softwarefehler durch systematische Analyse","Untersuchung von Testfehlern, um zugrunde liegende Probleme zu identifizieren","Durchführung der Ursachenanalyse für wiederkehrende technische Probleme"],"pt":["Depuração de bugs de software complexos por meio de análise sistemática","Investigação de falhas de teste para identificar problemas subjacentes","Realização de análise de causa raiz para problemas técnicos recorrentes"],"ru":["Отладка сложных программных ошибок посредством систематического анализа","Расследование неудач тестирования для выявления основных проблем","Проведение анализа коренной причины для повторяющихся технических проблем"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء برنامج معقدة من خلال التحليل المنظم","تحقيق فشل الاختبارات لتحديد المشكلات الكامنة","إجراء تحليل السبب الجذري للمشكلات الفنية المتكررة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the systematic debugging process","Demands thorough investigation before fix proposal","May not be suitable for agents prioritizing quick, symptomatic fixes"],"zh":["需要遵守系统的调试过程","要求在提出修复之前进行彻底的调查","可能不适合优先考虑快速、症状性的修复的代理"],"ja":["システム的なデバッグプロセスに従う必要がある","修復を提案する前に徹底的な調査を実施する必要がある","迅速な症状的な修復を優先するエージェントには不向きである可能性がある"],"ko":["시스템적인 디버깅 프로세스를 따라야 하는 것","수정 제안 전에 철저한 조사를 수행해야 하는 것","迅速한 증상적인 수정을 우선하는 에이전트에게는 부적합할 수 있는 것"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión al proceso de depuración sistemático","Exige una investigación exhaustiva antes de proponer una solución","Puede no ser adecuado para agentes que priorizan soluciones rápidas y sintomáticas"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au processus de débogage systématique","Exige une enquête approfondie avant de proposer une solution","Peut ne pas être adapté pour les agents qui donnent la priorité aux solutions rapides et symptomatiques"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des systematischen Fehlersuchprozesses","Fordert eine gründliche Untersuchung vor der Vorschlag einer Lösung","Kann für Agenten, die schnelle, symptomatische Lösungen priorisieren, nicht geeignet sein"],"pt":["Exige adesão ao processo de depuração sistemático","Exige investigação aprofundada antes da proposta de solução","Pode não ser adequado para agentes que priorizam soluções rápidas e sintomáticas"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения систематического процесса отладки","Требует тщательного расследования до предложения исправления","Может быть не подходящим для агентов, отдающих предпочтение быстрым симптоматическим исправлениям"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بالعملية المنظمة للتصحيح","يتطلب تحقيقا شاملا قبل اقتراح الحل","قد لا يكون مناسبا للوكلاء الذين يفضلون الإصلاحات السريعة والأعراضية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
