:["論文ノートの自動生成","テンプレートに基づいて論文タイトルと詳細を自動生成","Googleウェブ検索ツールを使用して論文の公式タイトルとリンクを探す","多言語対応"],"ko":["논문 노트 자동 생성","템플릿을 기반으로 논문 제목과 세부 사항을 자동 생성","구글 웹 검색 도구를 사용하여 논문의 공식 제목과 링크를 찾기","다중 언어 지원"],"es":["Creación automática de resúmenes de artículos","Búsqueda de detalles de artículos en Internet","Uso de plantillas para resúmenes","Organización de resúmenes en un directorio específico","Compatibilidad con arXiv y otros repositorios de artículos"],"fr":["Création automatisée de résumés d''articles","Recherche de détails d''articles sur Internet","Utilisation de modèles pour les résumés","Organisation des résumés dans un répertoire spécifique","Compatibilité avec arXiv et d''autres dépôts d''articles"],"de":["Automatisierte Erstellung von Artikelsummaries","Suche nach Artikeldetails im Internet","Verwendung von Vorlagen für Zusammenfassungen","Organisation von Zusammenfassungen in einem bestimmten Verzeichnis","Kompatibilität mit arXiv und anderen Artikel-Repositorys"]},"keywords":{"zh":["论文笔记","自动创建","研究效率","论文摘要","谷歌网页搜索","多语言支持"],"ja":["論文ノート","自動生成","研究効率","論文サマリー","Googleウェブ検索","多言語対応"],"ko":["논문 노트","자동 생성","연구 효율","논문 요약","구글 웹 검색","다중 언어 지원"],"es":["nota de investigación","resumen de artículo","automatización de tareas","gestión de artículos","arXiv","búsqueda de artículos","organización de notas","productividad de investigación"],"fr":["note de recherche","résumé d''article","automatisation de tâches","gestion d''articles","arXiv","recherche d''articles","organisation de notes","productivité de recherche"],"de":["Forschungsnotiz","Artikelsummary","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Artikelverwaltung","arXiv","Artikelsuche","Organisation von Notizen","Forschungsproduktivität"]}},"owner":"jeongbeenson19","repo":"research_notes","repoPath":"jeongbeenson19/research_notes","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.534Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"create-paper-note","description":"MNS(Workflow).md에 정의된 템플릿에 따라, 논문 제목을 입력받아 60_Library/Research/MNS/04_Papers 디렉토리에 요약 노트를 생성합니다.","bodyPreview":"# Paper Note Creation Skill\n\nThis skill automates the creation of a new paper summary note in the `60_Library/Research/MNS/04_Papers/` directory, based on the template found in `60_Library/Research/MNS/MNS(Workflow).md`.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1.  **Get Paper Title**: The user will provide a paper title.\n2.  **Find Paper Details**: Use the `google_web_search` tool to find the paper''s official title, venue, year, and a public URL (prefer arXiv).\n    - **Query**: Use a query like `\"[paper_title]\" paper arx","body":"# Paper Note Creation Skill\n\nThis skill automates the creation of a new paper summary note in the `60_Library/Research/MNS/04_Papers/` directory, based on the template found in `60_Library/Research/MNS/MNS(Workflow).md`.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1.  **Get Paper Title**: The user will provide a paper title.\n2.  **Find Paper Details**: Use the `google_web_search` tool to find the paper''s official title, venue, year, and a public URL (prefer arXiv).\n    - **Query**: Use a query like `\"[paper_title]\" paper arxiv`.\n3.  **Construct File Content**: Use the paper details to fill out the template below. The \"Extract\" and \"Takeaway\" sections should be left as placeholders for the user to fill in, as they require in-depth analysis.\n4.  **Determine Filename**: The filename should be the paper''s official title.\n5.  **Create File**: Use the `write_file` tool to create the new markdown file in the `40_Papers/` directory.\n\n## Note Template\n\nUse the following markdown template for the file content.\n\n```markdown\n## Paper\n- Title: {{title}}\n- Venue/Year: {{venue_year}}\n- Link: {{url}}\n- 역할(문제정의/방법/평가/반박):\n\n## Extract\n- Task:\n- Unobserved interval:\n- Memory unit:\n- State:\n- Update rule:\n- Reactivation:\n- Fusion:\n- Assumptions:\n- Evaluation:\n- Failure modes:\n\n## Takeaway\n- 내 설계에 적용(1줄):\n- D1/D2/D3에 미치는 영향:\n```"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:52:01.376Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Research Agents needing automated paper note creation and organization capabilities.","zh":"适合需要自动创建和组织论文笔记的研究代理","ja":"研究エージェントが自動で論文のノートを作成および組織する必要がある場合に適しています","ko":"연구 에이전트가 자동으로 논문 노트를 생성하고 조직화하는 데 필요한 경우에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de investigación que necesitan capacidades de creación y organización de notas de papel automatizadas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de recherche ayant besoin de capacités de création et d''organisation de notes de papier automatisées.","de":"Ideal für Forschungsagenten, die automatisierte Funktionen zur Erstellung und Organisation von Papiernotizen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Pesquisa que precisam de capacidades de criação e organização de notas de papel automatizadas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов-исследователей, которым необходимы автоматические возможности создания и организации бумажных заметок.","ar":"مثالي لعميل البحث الذين بحاجة إلى قدرات إنشاء وت организ المذكرات الورقية أوتوماتيكيا."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate paper summary notes in Markdown format, utilizing google_web_search for paper details and organizing them in a designated directory, leveraging tools like arXiv for public URLs.","zh":"赋予代理生成Markdown格式的论文摘要笔记的能力，利用google_web_search获取论文详情，并将其组织在指定目录中，利用arXiv等工具获取公共URL","ja":"エージェントがMarkdown形式の論文サマリーノートを生成する能力を与え、google_web_searchを使用して論文の詳細を取得し、指定されたディレクトリに組織化し、arXivなどのツールを使用してパブリックURLを取得する","ko":"에이전트가 마크다운 형식의 논문 요약 노트를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하고, google_web_search를 사용하여 논문 세부 정보를 얻고, 지정된 디렉토리에 조직화하고, arXiv와 같은 도구를 사용하여 공개 URL을 얻음","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar notas de resumen de papel en formato Markdown, utilizando google_web_search para obtener detalles de los papers y organizándolos en un directorio designado, aprovechando herramientas como arXiv para URLs públicas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des notes de résumé de papier au format Markdown, en utilisant google_web_search pour obtenir des détails sur les articles et en les organisant dans un répertoire désigné, en exploitant des outils comme arXiv pour les URL publiques.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Papierzusammenfassungsnotizen im Markdown-Format zu erstellen, indem sie google_web_search für Papierdetails nutzen und diese in einem bestimmten Verzeichnis organisieren, unter Nutzung von Tools wie arXiv für öffentliche URLs.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar notas de resumo de papéis em formato Markdown, utilizando google_web_search para detalhes do papel e organizá-los em um diretório designado, aproveitando ferramentas como arXiv para URLs públicas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать краткие заметки о статьях в формате Markdown, используя google_web_search для деталей статьи и организовывая их в назначенном каталоге, используя инструменты như arXiv для публичных URL-адресов.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من إنشاء ملخصات أوراق البحث بصيغة Markdown، مستخدمين google_web_search للحصول على تفاصيل الورقة وتنظيمها في دليل معين، مستفيدين من أدوات مثل arXiv للروابط العامة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating paper note creation for research libraries","Generating paper summaries with venue and year information","Organizing research papers in a structured directory hierarchy"],"zh":["自动创建研究图书馆的论文笔记","生成包含场地和年份信息的论文摘要","在结构化目录层次中组织研究论文"],"ja":["研究ライブラリの論文ノートの自動作成","会場と年情報を含む論文サマリーの生成","構造化されたディレクトリ階層で研究論文を整理する"],"ko":["연구 도서관의 논문 노트 자동 생성","장소와 연도 정보를 포함하는 논문 요약 생성","구조화된 디렉토리 계층에서 연구 논문을 조직화"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de notas de papel para bibliotecas de investigación","Generación de resúmenes de papel con información de lugar y año","Organización de papers de investigación en una jerarquía de directorios estructurada"],"fr":["Automatisation de la création de notes de papier pour les bibliothèques de recherche","Génération de résumés de papier avec des informations de lieu et d''année","Organisation des articles de recherche dans une hiérarchie de répertoires structurée"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von Papiernotizen für Forschungsbibliotheken","Erstellung von Papierzusammenfassungen mit Informationen über den Veranstaltungsort und das Jahr","Organisation von Forschungspapieren in einer strukturierten Verzeichnishierarchie"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de notas de papel para bibliotecas de pesquisa","Gerar resumos de papéis com informações de local e ano","Organizar artigos de pesquisa em uma hierarquia de diretório estruturada"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание бумажных заметок для исследовательских библиотек","Генерировать краткие заметки о статьях с информацией о месте и годе","Организовывать исследовательские статьи в структурированной иерархии каталогов"],"ar":["تأتمتة إنشاء المذكرات الورقية لمكتبات البحث","إنشاء ملخصات الأوراق البحثية مع معلومات عن المكان والسنة","تنظيم الأوراق البحثية في هرمية دليلية منظمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires google_web_search tool access","Dependent on arXiv for paper details","Directory structure must be pre-configured"],"zh":["需要google_web_search工具的访问权限","依赖arXiv获取论文详情","目录结构必须预先配置"],"ja":["google_web_searchツールへのアクセスが必要","arXivに依存して論文の詳細を取得する","ディレクトリ構造は事前に設定する必要がある"],"ko":["google_web_search 도구에 대한 액세스 권한이 필요함","arXiv에 의존하여 논문 세부 정보를 얻음","디렉토리 구조는 미리 구성해야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la herramienta google_web_search","Dependiente de arXiv para obtener detalles de los papers","La estructura del directorio debe estar preconfigurada"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à l''outil google_web_search","Dépend de arXiv pour obtenir des détails sur les articles","La structure du répertoire doit être préconfigurée"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Tool google_web_search","Abhängig von arXiv für die Erlangung von Papierdetails","Die Verzeichnisstruktur muss vorkonfiguriert sein"],"pt":["Requer acesso à ferramenta google_web_search","Dependente de arXiv para detalhes do papel","A estrutura do diretório deve ser pré-configurada"],"ru":["Требует доступа к инструменту google_web_search","Зависит от arXiv для деталей статьи","Структура каталога должна быть предварительно настроена"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى أداة google_web_search","يعتمد على arXiv للحصول على تفاصيل الورقة","يجب تحديد هيكل الدليل مسبقا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('guillaumejay/FileIndexer/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'guillaumejay', 'FileIndexer', 'guillaumejay/FileIndexer', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.534Z', '2026-02-18T14:51:41.085Z', NULL, '{"id":"guillaumejay/FileIndexer/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 是一个代码搜索和索引工具，帮助开发者快速找到所需的代码","ja":"OpenSpec はコード検索とインデックス作成ツールで、開発者が必要なコードを見つけるのを支援します","ko":"OpenSpec는 코드 검색과 색인 생성 도구로 개발자가 필요한 코드를 신속하게 찾을 수 있도록 지원합니다","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta que permite indexar y buscar archivos. Este tutorial te guía a través del primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil qui permet d''indexer et de rechercher des fichiers. Ce tutoriel vous guide à travers le premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Tool, das die Indexierung und Suche von Dateien ermöglicht. Dieses Tutorial führt Sie durch den ersten vollständigen Arbeitszyklus mit OpenSpec","pt":"O Openspec é uma ferramenta para indexar e pesquisar arquivos no seu código. Aprenda a usá-lo com o guia de configuração","ru":"Openspec - это инструмент для индексации и поиска файлов в вашем коде. Узнайте, как его использовать с помощью руководства по настройке","ar":"openspec هو أداة لفهارس و بحث الملفات في رمزك. تعلم كيفية استخدامه مع دليل الإعداد","en":"Index and search your files "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南","ja":"OpenSpec を使ってみる","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"Onboarding con OpenSpec: Indexación y Búsqueda de Archivos","fr":"Onboarding OpenSpec : Indexation et Recherche de Fichiers","de":"Onboarding mit OpenSpec: Datei-Indexierung und -Suche","pt":"Onboard Openspec: Indexe e Pesquise Arquivos","ru":"Openspec Настройка: Индексация и Поиск Файлов","ar":"openspec على متن الطائرة: فهرسة و بحث الملفات","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 是一个代码搜索和索引工具，帮助开发者快速找到所需的代码","ja":"OpenSpec はコード検索とインデックス作成ツールで、開発者が必要なコードを見つけるのを支援します","ko":"OpenSpec는 코드 검색과 색인 생성 도구로 개발자가 필요한 코드를 신속하게 찾을 수 있도록 지원합니다","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta que permite indexar y buscar archivos. Este tutorial te guía a través del primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil qui permet d''indexer et de rechercher des fichiers. Ce tutoriel vous guide à travers le premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Tool, das die Indexierung und Suche von Dateien ermöglicht. Dieses Tutorial führt Sie durch den ersten vollständigen Arbeitszyklus mit OpenSpec","pt":"O Openspec é uma ferramenta para indexar e pesquisar arquivos no seu código. Aprenda a usá-lo com o guia de configuração","ru":"Openspec - это инструмент для индексации и поиска файлов в вашем коде. Узнайте, как его использовать с помощью руководства по настройке","ar":"openspec هو أداة لفهارس و بحث الملفات في رمزك. تعلم كيفية استخدامه مع دليل الإعداد","en":"Index and search your files "},"definition":{"en":"Index and search your files "},"features":{"zh":["代码搜索","代码索引","开发效率提高","实时搜索结果","支持多种编程语言"],"ja":["コード検索","コードインデックス","開発効率の向上","リアルタイム検索結果","複数のプログラミング言語のサポート"],"ko":["코드 검색","코드 색인","개발 효율성 향상","실시간 검색 결과","다양한 프로그래밍 언어 지원"],"es":["Indexación de archivos","Búsqueda de archivos","Tutorial de onboarding","Ciclo de trabajo completo","Compatibilidad con proyectos de código abierto"],"fr":["Indexation de fichiers","Recherche de fichiers","Tutoriel d''onboarding","Cycle de travail complet","Compatibilité avec les projets de code ouvert"],"de":["Datei-Indexierung","Datei-Suche","Onboarding-Tutorial","Vollständiger Arbeitszyklus","Kompatibilität mit Open-Source-Projekten"],"pt":["Indexação de arquivos de código","Pesquisa de arquivos de código","Guia de configuração passo a passo","Integração com o seu código","Fácil de usar e configurar"],"ru":["Индексация файлов кода","Поиск файлов кода","Пошаговое руководство по настройке","Интеграция с вашим кодом","Легко использовать и настраивать"],"ar":["فهارس ملفات الرمز","بحث ملفات الرمز","دليل إعداد خطوة بخطوة","دمج مع رمزك","سهل الاستخدام و الإعداد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","代码搜索","代码索引","开发工具","开发效率","代码管理"],"ja":["OpenSpec","コード検索","コードインデックス","開発ツール","開発効率","コード管理"],"ko":["OpenSpec","코드 검색","코드 색인","개발 도구","개발 효율성","코드 관리"],"es":["OpenSpec","indexación de archivos","búsqueda de archivos","onboarding","ciclo de trabajo","proyectos de código abierto","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["OpenSpec","indexation de fichiers","recherche de fichiers","onboarding","cycle de travail","projets de code ouvert","outils de développement"],"de":["OpenSpec","Datei-Indexierung","Datei-Suche","Onboarding","Arbeitszyklus","Open-Source-Projekte","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["openspec","indexação de arquivos","pesquisa de arquivos","guia de configuração","ferramenta de desenvolvimento","desenvolvimento de software","indexação de código","pesquisa de código"],"ru":["openspec","индексация файлов","поиск файлов","руководство по настройке","инструмент разработки","разработка программного обеспечения","индексация кода","поиск кода"],"ar":["openspec","فهارس الملفات","بحث الملفات","دليل الإعداد","أداة التطوير","تطوير البرمجيات","فهارس الرمز","بحث الرمز"]}},"owner":"guillaumejay","repo":"FileIndexer","repoPath":"guillaumejay/FileIndexer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.534Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:51:41.085Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing advanced project initialization and workflow management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级项目初始化和工作流管理功能的代码分析代理。","ja":"コード分析エージェントが高度なプロジェクト初期化とワークフロー管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 프로젝트 초기화 및 워크플로 관리 기능이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de inicialización de proyectos y gestión de flujos de trabajo.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant des capacités avancées d''initialisation de projet et de gestion de workflow.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agenten, die erweiterte Projektinitialisierungs- und Workflow-Management-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que necessitam de recursos avançados de inicialização e gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих продвинутых возможностей инициализации и управления рабочим процессом.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لمبادرة المشروع وإدارة تدفق العمل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to guide users through complete OpenSpec workflow cycles, utilizing JSON output and bash commands like `openspec status` and `openspec init`, to ensure seamless project setup and management.","zh":"能够让代理引导用户完成整个 OpenSpec 工作流周期，利用 JSON 输出和 bash 命令（如 `openspec status` 和 `openspec init`），以确保无缝的项目设置和管理。","ja":"エージェントがユーザーを OpenSpec のワークフロー全体に沿ってガイドできるようにし、JSON 出力や `openspec status` および `openspec init` などの Bash コマンドを使用して、プロジェクトの設定と管理をスムーズに行えるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자를 전체 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 거치도록 안내할 수 있으며, JSON 출력 및 `openspec status` 및 `openspec init` 등의 Bash 명령어를 사용하여無중단 프로젝트 설정 및 관리를 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para guiar a los usuarios a través de ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec completos, utilizando la salida JSON y comandos bash como `openspec status` y `openspec init`, para garantizar una configuración y administración de proyectos sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de guider les utilisateurs à travers des cycles de workflow OpenSpec complets, en utilisant la sortie JSON et les commandes bash telles que `openspec status` et `openspec init`, pour assurer une configuration et une gestion de projet sans problème.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Benutzer durch vollständige OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen zu führen, indem JSON-Ausgaben und Bash-Befehle wie `openspec status` und `openspec init` verwendet werden, um eine reibungslose Projektkonfiguration und -verwaltung zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Permite que os agentes orientem os usuários por meio de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec completos, utilizando a saída JSON e comandos bash como `openspec status` e `openspec init`, para garantir a configuração e gerenciamento de projeto sem interrupções.","ru":"Позволяет агентам руководить пользователями на протяжении полных циклов рабочего процесса OpenSpec, используя выходные данные JSON и команды bash, такие как `openspec status` и `openspec init`, для обеспечения бесшовной настройки и управления проектом.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء أن يوجهوا المستخدمين خلال دورات عمل.OpenSpec الكاملة ، باستخدام إخراج JSON وأوامر bash مثل `openspec status` و `openspec init` ، لضمان إعداد وتشغيل مشروع دون انقطاع."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through first-time workflow cycles","Verifying OpenSpec initialization status"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化 OpenSpec","引导用户完成首次工作流周期","验证 OpenSpec 初始化状态"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトで OpenSpec を初期化する","ユーザーが最初のワークフロー周期を完了するようにガイドする","OpenSpec 初期化の状態を確認する"],"ko":["새 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자가 첫 번째 워크플로 사이클을 완료하도록 안내","OpenSpec 초기화 상태 확인"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guía a los usuarios a través de los primeros ciclos de flujo de trabajo","Verificar el estado de inicialización de OpenSpec"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs à travers les premiers cycles de workflow","Vérifier le statut d''initialisation d''OpenSpec"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","Benutzer durch erste Workflow-Zyklen führen","OpenSpec-Initialisierungsstatus überprüfen"],"pt":["Inicializando OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientando os usuários durante os primeiros ciclos de fluxo de trabalho","Verificando o status de inicialização do OpenSpec"],"ru":["Инициализация OpenSpec в новых проектах","Руководство пользователями в течение первых циклов рабочего процесса","Проверка статуса инициализации OpenSpec"],"ar":["إعداد OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","توجيه المستخدمين خلال دورات العمل الأولى","تحقق من حالة بدء تشغيل OpenSpec"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec installation","Needs bash command execution privileges","Must be used in a project directory"],"zh":["需要 OpenSpec 安装","需要 Bash 命令执行权限","必须在项目目录中使用"],"ja":["OpenSpec のインストールが必要","Bash コマンドの実行権限が必要","プロジェクトディレクトリ内で使用する必要がある"],"ko":["OpenSpec 설치 필요","Bash 명령어 실행 권한 필요","프로젝트 디렉토리 내에서 사용해야 함"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de OpenSpec","Necesita derechos de ejecución de comandos bash","Debe usarse en un directorio de proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation d''OpenSpec","A besoin de privilèges d''exécution de commandes bash","Doit être utilisé dans un répertoire de projet"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von OpenSpec","Benötigt Bash-Befehlsausführungsrechte","Muss in einem Projektverzeichnis verwendet werden"],"pt":["Requer instalação do OpenSpec","Necessita de privilégios de execução de comandos bash","Deve ser usado em um diretório de projeto"],"ru":["Требует установки OpenSpec","Требует привилегий на выполнение команд bash","Должно использоваться в директории проекта"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت OpenSpec","يحتاج إلى صلاحيات تنفيذ أوامر bash","يجب استخدامه في دليل مشروع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('haxllo/repolens/microservices-patterns', 'community', 'haxllo', 'repolens', 'haxllo/repolens', 'microservices-patterns', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.534Z', '2026-02-18T14:51:52.507Z', NULL, '{"id":"haxllo/repolens/microservices-patterns","name":"microservices-patterns","description":{"zh":"微服务模式是指在构建分布式系统时使用的架构模式，包括服务边界、服务间通信、数据管理和恢复模式等","ja":"マイクロサービスパターンは、分散システムを構築する際に使用されるアーキテクチャパターンであり、サービス境界、サービス間通信、データ管理、回復パターンなどを含む","ko":"마이크로 서비스 패턴은 분산 시스템을 구축할 때 사용되는 아키텍처 패턴으로 서비스 경계, 서비스 간 통신, 데이터 관리, 회복 패턴 등을 포함한다","es":"Los patrones de microservicios permiten diseñar sistemas distribuidos escalables y resilientes. Aprende a descomponer monolitos y a implementar comunicación entre servicios de manera efectiva.","fr":"Les modèles de microservices permettent de concevoir des systèmes distribués évolutifs et résilients. Découvrez comment décomposer les monolithes et mettre en œuvre la communication entre services de manière efficace.","de":"Mikrodienst-Muster ermöglichen die Konzeption von skalierbaren und ausfallsicheren verteilten Systemen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Monolithen zerlegen und die Kommunikation zwischen Diensten effektiv implementieren können.","pt":"Padrões de microserviços para arquitetura de sistemas distribuídos, incluindo limites de serviço e gerenciamento de dados","ru":"Шаблоны микросервисов для архитектуры распределенных систем, включая границы сервисов и управление данными","ar":"أنماط مايكروسيرفيس لهندسة الأنظمة الموزعة، بما في ذلك حدود الخدمة وإدارة البيانات","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"微服务模式","ja":"マイクロサービスパターン","ko":"마이크로 서비스 패턴","es":"Patrones de Microservicios para Arquitecturas Distribuidas","fr":"Modèles de Microservices pour les Systèmes Distribués","de":"Mikrodienst-Muster für verteilte Systeme","pt":"Padrões de Microserviços: Arquitetura de Sistemas Distrib...","ru":"Шаблоны Микросервисов: Архитектура Распределенных Систем","ar":"أنماط مايكروسيرفيس: هندسة الأنظمة الموزعة","en":"microservices-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"微服务模式是指在构建分布式系统时使用的架构模式，包括服务边界、服务间通信、数据管理和恢复模式等","ja":"マイクロサービスパターンは、分散システムを構築する際に使用されるアーキテクチャパターンであり、サービス境界、サービス間通信、データ管理、回復パターンなどを含む","ko":"마이크로 서비스 패턴은 분산 시스템을 구축할 때 사용되는 아키텍처 패턴으로 서비스 경계, 서비스 간 통신, 데이터 관리, 회복 패턴 등을 포함한다","es":"Los patrones de microservicios permiten diseñar sistemas distribuidos escalables y resilientes. Aprende a descomponer monolitos y a implementar comunicación ...","fr":"Les modèles de microservices permettent de concevoir des systèmes distribués évolutifs et résilients. Découvrez comment décomposer les monolithes et mettre e...","de":"Mikrodienst-Muster ermöglichen die Konzeption von skalierbaren und ausfallsicheren verteilten Systemen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Monolithen zerlegen und die Kom...","pt":"Padrões de microserviços para arquitetura de sistemas distribuídos, incluindo limites de serviço e gerenciamento de dados","ru":"Шаблоны микросервисов для архитектуры распределенных систем, включая границы сервисов и управление данными","ar":"أنماط مايكروسيرفيس لهندسة الأنظمة الموزعة، بما في ذلك حدود الخدمة وإدارة البيانات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["服务边界","服务间通信","数据管理","恢复模式","服务发现","负载均衡"],"ja":["サービス境界","サービス間通信","データ管理","回復パターン","サービス発見","負荷分散"],"ko":["서비스 경계","서비스 간 통신","데이터 관리","회복 패턴","서비스 발견","부하 분산"],"es":["Descomposición de monolitos en microservicios","Diseño de límites y contratos de servicio","Implementación de la comunicación entre servicios","Gestión de datos y transacciones distribuidas","Construcción de sistemas distribuidos resilientes","Implementación de servicio de descubrimiento y equilibrio de carga"],"fr":["Décomposition de monolithes en microservices","Conception de limites et de contrats de service","Mise en œuvre de la communication entre services","Gestion de données et de transactions distribuées","Construction de systèmes distribués résilients","Mise en œuvre de service de découverte et d''équilibrage de charge"],"de":["Zerlegung von Monolithen in Mikrodienste","Entwurf von Dienstgrenzen und -verträgen","Implementierung der Kommunikation zwischen Diensten","Verwaltung von Daten und Transaktionen in verteilten Systemen","Aufbau von ausfallsicheren verteilten Systemen","Implementierung von Diensterkennung und Lastenausgleich"],"pt":["Decomposição de monolitos em microserviços","Definição de limites de serviço e contratos","Implementação de comunicação entre serviços","Gerenciamento de dados e transações distribuídas","Criação de sistemas distribuídos resilientes"],"ru":["Разделение монолитов на микросервисы","Определение границ сервисов и контрактов","Реализация обмена данными между сервисами","Управление данными и распределенными транзакциями","Создание распределенных систем с повышенной отказоустойчивостью"],"ar":["تقسيم التطبيقات وحيدة القمة إلى مايكروسيرفيس","تحديد حدود الخدمة والاتفاقات","تنفيذ الاتصال بين الخدمات","إدارة البيانات والتعاملات الموزعة","إنشاء أنظمة موزعة متينة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["微服务","分布式系统","服务边界","服务间通信","数据管理","恢复模式","服务发现","负载均衡"],"ja":["マイクロサービス","分散システム","サービス境界","サービス間通信","データ管理","回復パターン","サービス発見","負荷分散"],"ko":["마이크로 서비스","분산 시스템","서비스 경계","서비스 간 통신","데이터 관리","회복 패턴","서비스 발견","부하 분산"],"es":["patrones de microservicios","arquitectura de microservicios","sistemas distribuidos","descomposición de monolitos","comunicación entre servicios","gestión de datos distribuidos","sistemas resilientes","diseño de software","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["modèles de microservices","architecture de microservices","systèmes distribués","décomposition de monolithes","communication entre services","gestion de données distribuées","systèmes résilients","conception de logiciels","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Mikrodienst-Muster","Mikrodienst-Architektur","verteilte Systeme","Zerlegung von Monolithen","Kommunikation zwischen Diensten","Verwaltung von Daten in verteilten Systemen","ausfallsichere Systeme","Software-Design","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["microserviços","arquitetura de sistemas distribuídos","padrões de microserviços","desenvolvimento de software","sistemas escaláveis","gerenciamento de dados"],"ru":["микросервисы","архитектура распределенных систем","шаблоны микросервисов","разработка программного обеспечения","масштабируемые системы","управление данными"],"ar":["مايكروسيرفيس","هندسة الأنظمة الموزعة","أنماط مايكروسيرفيس","تطوير البرمجيات","أنظمة قابلة للتحجيم","إدارة البيانات"]}},"owner":"haxllo","repo":"repolens","repoPath":"haxllo/repolens","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.534Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"microservices-patterns","description":"Design microservices architectures with service boundaries, event-driven communication, and resilience patterns. Use when building distributed systems, decomposing monoliths, or implementing microservices.","bodyPreview":"# Microservices Patterns\n\nMaster microservices architecture patterns including service boundaries, inter-service communication, data management, and resilience patterns for building distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Decomposing monoliths into microservices\n- Designing service boundaries and contracts\n- Implementing inter-service communication\n- Managing distributed data and transactions\n- Building resilient distributed systems\n- Implementing service discovery and load balancing","body":"# Microservices Patterns\n\nMaster microservices architecture patterns including service boundaries, inter-service communication, data management, and resilience patterns for building distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Decomposing monoliths into microservices\n- Designing service boundaries and contracts\n- Implementing inter-service communication\n- Managing distributed data and transactions\n- Building resilient distributed systems\n- Implementing service discovery and load balancing\n- Designing event-driven architectures\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Service Decomposition Strategies\n\n**By Business Capability**\n\n- Organize services around business functions\n- Each service owns its domain\n- Example: OrderService, PaymentService, InventoryService\n\n**By Subdomain (DDD)**\n\n- Core domain, supporting subdomains\n- Bounded contexts map to services\n- Clear ownership and responsibility\n\n**Strangler Fig Pattern**\n\n- Gradually extract from monolith\n- New functionality as microservices\n- Proxy routes to old/new systems\n\n### 2. Communication Patterns\n\n**Synchronous (Request/Response)**\n\n- REST APIs\n- gRPC\n- GraphQL\n\n**Asynchronous (Events/Messages)**\n\n- Event streaming (Kafka)\n- Message queues (RabbitMQ, SQS)\n- Pub/Sub patterns\n\n### 3. Data Management\n\n**Database Per Service**\n\n- Each service owns its data\n- No shared databases\n- Loose coupling\n\n**Saga Pattern**\n\n- Distributed transactions\n- Compensating actions\n- Eventual consistency\n\n### 4. Resilience Patterns\n\n**Circuit Breaker**\n\n- Fail fast on repeated errors\n- Prevent cascade failures\n\n**Retry with Backoff**\n\n- Transient fault handling\n- Exponential backoff\n\n**Bulkhead**\n\n- Isolate resources\n- Limit impact of failures\n\n## Service Decomposition Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: By Business Capability\n\n```python\n# E-commerce example\n\n# Order Service\nclass OrderService:\n    \"\"\"Handles order lifecycle.\"\"\"\n\n    async def create_order(self, order_data: dict) -> Order:\n        order = Order.create(order_data)\n\n        # Publish event for other services\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\n            OrderCreatedEvent(\n                order_id=order.id,\n                customer_id=order.customer_id,\n                items=order.items,\n                total=order.total\n            )\n        )\n\n        return order\n\n# Payment Service (separate service)\nclass PaymentService:\n    \"\"\"Handles payment processing.\"\"\"\n\n    async def process_payment(self, payment_request: PaymentRequest) -> PaymentResult:\n        # Process payment\n        result = await self.payment_gateway.charge(\n            amount=payment_request.amount,\n            customer=payment_request.customer_id\n        )\n\n        if result.success:\n            await self.event_bus.publish(\n                PaymentCompletedEvent(\n                    order_id=payment_request.order_id,\n                    transaction_id=result.transaction_id\n                )\n            )\n\n        return result\n\n# Inventory Service (separate service)\nclass InventoryService:\n    \"\"\"Handles inventory management.\"\"\"\n\n    async def reserve_items(self, order_id: str, items: List[OrderItem]) -> ReservationResult:\n        # Check availability\n        for item in items:\n            available = await self.inventory_repo.get_available(item.product_id)\n            if available < item.quantity:\n                return ReservationResult(\n                    success=False,\n                    error=f\"Insufficient inventory for {item.product_id}\"\n                )\n\n        # Reserve items\n        reservation = await self.create_reservation(order_id, items)\n\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\n            InventoryReservedEvent(\n                order_id=order_id,\n                reservation_id=reservation.id\n            )\n        )\n\n        return ReservationResult(success=True, reservation=reservation)\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: API Gateway\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends\nimport httpx\nfrom circuitbreaker import circuit\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass APIGateway:\n    \"\"\"Central entry point for all client requests.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.order_service_url = \"http://order-service:8000\"\n        self.payment_service_url = \"http://payment-service:8001\"\n        self.inventory_service_url = \"http://inventory-service:8002\"\n        self.http_client = httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0)\n\n    @circuit(failure_threshold=5, recovery_timeout=30)\n    async def call_order_service(self, path: str, method: str = \"GET\", **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"Call order service with circuit breaker.\"\"\"\n        response = await self.http_client.request(\n            method,\n            f\"{self.order_service_url}{path}\",\n            **kwargs\n        )\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        return response.json()\n\n    async def create_order_aggregate(self, order_id: str) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Aggregate data from multiple services.\"\"\"\n        # Parallel requests\n        order, payment, inventory = await asyncio.gather(\n            self.call_order_service(f\"/orders/{order_id}\"),\n            self.call_payment_service(f\"/payments/order/{order_id}\"),\n            self.call_inventory_service(f\"/reservations/order/{order_id}\"),\n            return_exceptions=True\n        )\n\n        # Handle partial failures\n        result = {\"order\": order}\n        if not isinstance(payment, Exception):\n            result[\"payment\"] = payment\n        if not isinstance(inventory, Exception):\n            result[\"inventory\"] = inventory\n\n        return result\n\n@app.post(\"/api/orders\")\nasync def create_order(\n    order_data: dict,\n    gateway: APIGateway = Depends()\n):\n    \"\"\"API Gateway endpoint.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Route to order service\n        order = await gateway.call_order_service(\n            \"/orders\",\n            method=\"POST\",\n            json=order_data\n        )\n        return {\"order\": order}\n    except httpx.HTTPError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\"Order service unavailable\")\n```\n\n## Communication Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Synchronous REST Communication\n\n```python\n# Service A calls Service B\nimport httpx\nfrom tenacity import retry, stop_after_attempt, wait_exponential\n\nclass ServiceClient:\n    \"\"\"HTTP client with retries and timeout.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base_url: str):\n        self.base_url = base_url\n        self.client = httpx.AsyncClient(\n            timeout=httpx.Timeout(5.0, connect=2.0),\n            limits=httpx.Limits(max_keepalive_connections=20)\n        )\n\n    @retry(\n        stop=stop_after_attempt(3),\n        wait=wait_exponential(multiplier=1, min=2, max=10)\n    )\n    async def get(self, path: str, **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"GET with automatic retries.\"\"\"\n        response = await self.client.get(f\"{self.base_url}{path}\", **kwargs)\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        return response.json()\n\n    async def post(self, path: str, **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"POST request.\"\"\"\n        response = await self.client.post(f\"{self.base_url}{path}\", **kwargs)\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        return response.json()\n\n# Usage\npayment_client = ServiceClient(\"http://payment-service:8001\")\nresult = await payment_client.post(\"/payments\", json=payment_data)\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Asynchronous Event-Driven\n\n```python\n# Event-driven communication with Kafka\nfrom aiokafka import AIOKafkaProducer, AIOKafkaConsumer\nimport json\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, asdict\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n@dataclass\nclass DomainEvent:\n    event_id: str\n    event_type: str\n    aggregate_id: str\n    occurred_at: datetime\n    data: dict\n\nclass EventBus:\n    \"\"\"Event publishing and subscription.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, bootstrap_servers: List[str]):\n        self.bootstrap_servers = bootstrap_servers\n        self.producer = None\n\n    async def start(self):\n        self.producer = AIOKafkaProducer(\n            bootstrap_servers=self.bootstrap_servers,\n            value_serializer=lambda v: json.dumps(v).encode()\n        )\n        await self.producer.start()\n\n    async def publish(self, event: DomainEvent):\n        \"\"\"Publish event to Kafka topic.\"\"\"\n        topic = event.event_type\n        await self.producer.send_and_wait(\n            topic,\n            value=asdict(event),\n            key=event.aggregate_id.encode()\n        )\n\n    async def subscribe(self, topic: str, handler: callable):\n        \"\"\"Subscribe to events.\"\"\"\n        consumer = AIOKafkaConsumer(\n            topic,\n            bootstrap_servers=self.bootstrap_servers,\n            value_deserializer=lambda v: json.loads(v.decode()),\n            group_id=\"my-service\"\n        )\n        await consumer.start()\n\n        try:\n            async for message in consumer:\n                event_data = message.value\n                await handler(event_data)\n        finally:\n            await consumer.stop()\n\n# Order Service publishes event\nasync def create_order(order_data: dict):\n    order = await save_order(order_data)\n\n    event = DomainEvent(\n        event_id=str(uuid.uuid4()),\n        event_type=\"OrderCreated\",\n        aggregate_id=order.id,\n        occurred_at=datetime.now(),\n        data={\n            \"order_id\": order.id,\n            \"customer_id\": order.customer_id,\n            \"total\": order.total\n        }\n    )\n\n    await event_bus.publish(event)\n\n# Inventory Service listens for OrderCreated\nasync def handle_order_created(event_data: dict):\n    \"\"\"React to order creation.\"\"\"\n    order_id = event_data[\"data\"][\"order_id\"]\n    items = event_data[\"data\"][\"items\"]\n\n    # Reserve inventory\n    await reserve_inventory(order_id, items)\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Saga Pattern (Distributed Transactions)\n\n```python\n# Saga orchestration for order fulfillment\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom typing import List, Callable\n\nclass SagaStep:\n    \"\"\"Single step in saga.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        name: str,\n        action: Callable,\n        compensation: Callable\n    ):\n        self.name = name\n        self.action = action\n        self.compensation = compensation\n\nclass SagaStatus(Enum):\n    PENDING = \"pending\"\n    COMPLETED = \"completed\"\n    COMPENSATING = \"compensating\"\n    FAILED = \"failed\"\n\nclass OrderFulfillmentSaga:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrated saga for order fulfillment.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.steps: List[SagaStep] = [\n            SagaStep(\n                \"create_order\",\n                action=self.create_order,\n                compensation=self.cancel_order\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                \"reserve_inventory\",\n                action=self.reserve_inventory,\n                compensation=self.release_inventory\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                \"process_payment\",\n                action=self.process_payment,\n                compensation=self.refund_payment\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                \"confirm_order\",\n                action=self.confirm_order,\n                compensation=self.cancel_order_confirmation\n            )\n        ]\n\n    async def execute(self, order_data: dict) -> SagaResult:\n        \"\"\"Execute saga steps.\"\"\"\n        completed_steps = []\n        context = {\"order_data\": order_data}\n\n        try:\n            for step in self.steps:\n                # Execute step\n                result = await step.action(context)\n                if not result.success:\n                    # Compensate\n                    await self.compensate(completed_steps, context)\n                    return SagaResult(\n                        status=SagaStatus.FAILED,\n                        error=result.error\n                    )\n\n                completed_steps.append(step)\n                context.update(result.data)\n\n            return SagaResult(status=SagaStatus.COMPLETED, data=context)\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Compensate on error\n            await self.compensate(completed_steps, context)\n            return SagaResult(status=SagaStatus.FAILED, error=str(e))\n\n    async def compensate(self, completed_steps: List[SagaStep], context: dict):\n        \"\"\"Execute compensating actions in reverse order.\"\"\"\n        for step in reversed(completed_steps):\n            try:\n                await step.compensation(context)\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Log compensation failure\n                print(f\"Compensation failed for {step.name}: {e}\")\n\n    # Step implementations\n    async def create_order(self, context: dict) -> StepResult:\n        order = await order_service.create(context[\"order_data\"])\n        return StepResult(success=True, data={\"order_id\": order.id})\n\n    async def cancel_order(self, context: dict):\n        await order_service.cancel(context[\"order_id\"])\n\n    async def reserve_inventory(self, context: dict) -> StepResult:\n        result = await inventory_service.reserve(\n            context[\"order_id\"],\n            context[\"order_data\"][\"items\"]\n        )\n        return StepResult(\n            success=result.success,\n            data={\"reservation_id\": result.reservation_id}\n        )\n\n    async def release_inventory(self, context: dict):\n        await inventory_service.release(context[\"reservation_id\"])\n\n    async def process_payment(self, context: dict) -> StepResult:\n        result = await payment_service.charge(\n            context[\"order_id\"],\n            context[\"order_data\"][\"total\"]\n        )\n        return StepResult(\n            success=result.success,\n            data={\"transaction_id\": result.transaction_id},\n            error=result.error\n        )\n\n    async def refund_payment(self, context: dict):\n        await payment_service.refund(context[\"transaction_id\"])\n```\n\n## Resilience Patterns\n\n### Circuit Breaker Pattern\n\n```python\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom typing import Callable, Any\n\nclass CircuitState(Enum):\n    CLOSED = \"closed\"  # Normal operation\n    OPEN = \"open\"      # Failing, reject requests\n    HALF_OPEN = \"half_open\"  # Testing if recovered\n\nclass CircuitBreaker:\n    \"\"\"Circuit breaker for service calls.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        failure_threshold: int = 5,\n        recovery_timeout: int = 30,\n        success_threshold: int = 2\n    ):\n        self.failure_threshold = failure_threshold\n        self.recovery_timeout = recovery_timeout\n        self.success_threshold = success_threshold\n\n        self.failure_count = 0\n        self.success_count = 0\n        self.state = CircuitState.CLOSED\n        self.opened_at = None\n\n    async def call(self, func: Callable, *args, **kwargs) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Execute function with circuit breaker.\"\"\"\n\n        if self.state == CircuitState.OPEN:\n            if self._should_attempt_reset():\n                self.state = CircuitState.HALF_OPEN\n            else:\n                raise CircuitBreakerOpenError(\"Circuit breaker is open\")\n\n        try:\n            result = await func(*args, **kwargs)\n            self._on_success()\n            return result\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            self._on_failure()\n            raise\n\n    def _on_success(self):\n        \"\"\"Handle successful call.\"\"\"\n        self.failure_count = 0\n\n        if self.state == CircuitState.HALF_OPEN:\n            self.success_count += 1\n            if self.success_count >= self.success_threshold:\n                self.state = CircuitState.CLOSED\n                self.success_count = 0\n\n    def _on_failure(self):\n        \"\"\"Handle failed call.\"\"\"\n        self.failure_count += 1\n\n        if self.failure_count >= self.failure_threshold:\n            self.state = CircuitState.OPEN\n            self.opened_at = datetime.now()\n\n        if self.state == CircuitState.HALF_OPEN:\n            self.state = CircuitState.OPEN\n            self.opened_at = datetime.now()\n\n    def _should_attempt_reset(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if enough time passed to try again.\"\"\"\n        return (\n            datetime.now() - self.opened_at\n            > timedelta(seconds=self.recovery_timeout)\n        )\n\n# Usage\nbreaker = CircuitBreaker(failure_threshold=5, recovery_timeout=30)\n\nasync def call_payment_service(payment_data: dict):\n    return await breaker.call(\n        payment_client.process_payment,\n        payment_data\n    )\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/service-decomposition-guide.md**: Breaking down monoliths\n- **references/communication-patterns.md**: Sync vs async patterns\n- **references/saga-implementation.md**: Distributed transactions\n- **assets/circuit-breaker.py**: Production circuit breaker\n- **assets/event-bus-template.py**: Kafka event bus implementation\n- **assets/api-gateway-template.py**: Complete API gateway\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Service Boundaries**: Align with business capabilities\n2. **Database Per Service**: No shared databases\n3. **API Contracts**: Versioned, backward compatible\n4. **Async When Possible**: Events over direct calls\n5. **Circuit Breakers**: Fail fast on service failures\n6. **Distributed Tracing**: Track requests across services\n7. **Service Registry**: Dynamic service discovery\n8. **Health Checks**: Liveness and readiness probes\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Distributed Monolith**: Tightly coupled services\n- **Chatty Services**: Too many inter-service calls\n- **Shared Databases**: Tight coupling through data\n- **No Circuit Breakers**: Cascade failures\n- **Synchronous Everything**: Tight coupling, poor resilience\n- **Premature Microservices**: Starting with microservices\n- **Ignoring Network Failures**: Assuming reliable network\n- **No Compensation Logic**: Can''t undo failed transactions\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T14:51:52.507Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Distributed System Agents requiring expertise in microservices architecture patterns for building resilient and scalable systems.","zh":"适用于需要在微服务架构模式方面有专长的分布式系统代理，用于构建可靠和可扩展的系统。","ja":"マイクロサービスアーキテクチャパターンに関する専門知識を必要とする分散システムエージェントに最適です。堅牢でスケーラブルなシステムを構築するために。","ko":"마이크로 서비스 아키텍처 패턴에 대한 전문 지식을 요구하는 분산 시스템 에이전트에 적합합니다. 탄력적이고 확장 가능한 시스템을 구축하기 위해","es":"Ideal para agentes de sistemas distribuidos que requieren experiencia en patrones de arquitectura de microservicios para construir sistemas resilientes y escalables.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de systèmes distribués nécessitant une expertise dans les modèles d''architecture de microservices pour construire des systèmes résilients et évolutifs.","de":"Ideal für verteilte Systemagenten, die Expertenwissen in Mikroservices-Architekturmuster für den Bau von resilienten und skalierbaren Systemen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuídos que requerem conhecimento em padrões de arquitetura de microsserviços para construir sistemas resilientes e escaláveis.","ru":"Идеально для агентов распределенных систем, требующих знаний в области шаблонов микросервисной архитектуры для создания устойчивых и масштабируемых систем.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء أنظمة موزعة يتطلبون الخبرة في أنماط هندسة ميكروسيرفس لإنشاء أنظمة متينة وقابلة للتوسعة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design and implement service boundaries, inter-service communication protocols, and data management strategies using patterns such as API Composition and Event Sourcing, ensuring robust and fault-tolerant distributed systems.","zh":"赋予代理设计和实施服务边界、服务间通信协议和数据管理策略的能力，使用诸如 API 组合和事件源等模式，确保强健和容错的分布式系统。","ja":"サービス境界、サービス間通信プロトコル、データ管理戦略を設計および実装するエージェントを可能にします。API CompositionやEvent Sourcingなどのパターンを使用して、堅牢で障害耐性のある分散システムを保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 서비스 경계, 서비스 간 통신 프로토콜 및 데이터 관리 전략을 설계하고 구현할 수 있도록 합니다. API 컴포지션 및 이벤트 소싱과 같은 패턴을 사용하여 강력하고 장애 허용 분산 시스템을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar e implementar límites de servicio, protocolos de comunicación entre servicios y estrategias de gestión de datos utilizando patrones como la composición de API y el origen de eventos, lo que garantiza sistemas distribuidos robustos y tolerantes a fallos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir et de mettre en œuvre des limites de service, des protocoles de communication inter-service et des stratégies de gestion de données en utilisant des modèles tels que la composition d''API et l''origine d''événements, garantissant ainsi des systèmes distribués robustes et tolérants aux défaillances.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Dienstgrenzen, Kommunikationsprotokolle zwischen Diensten und Datenmanagementstrategien unter Verwendung von Mustern wie API-Zusammensetzung und Ereignisquellen zu entwerfen und umzusetzen, wodurch robuste und fehlertolerante verteilte Systeme gewährleistet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar e implementar limites de serviço, protocolos de comunicação entre serviços e estratégias de gerenciamento de dados usando padrões como Composição de API e Origem de Eventos, garantindo sistemas distribuídos robustos e tolerantes a falhas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам проектировать и реализовывать границы сервисов, протоколы межсервисного взаимодействия и стратегии управления данными, используя шаблоны, такие как Композиция API и Источник событий, обеспечивая надежные и отказоустойчивые распределенные системы.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تصميم وتنفيذ حدود الخدمة وبروتوكولات الاتصال بين الخدمات واستراتيجيات إدارة البيانات باستخدام أنماط مثل تكوين واجهة برمجة التطبيقات ومصدر الحدث، مما يضمن أنظمة موزعة قوية ومتينة."},"useCases":{"en":["Decomposing monolithic applications into microservices","Implementing inter-service communication using RESTful APIs or message queues","Building resilient distributed systems with circuit breakers and service discovery"],"zh":["将单体应用程序分解为微服务","使用RESTful API或消息队列实现服务间通信","使用电路断路器和服务发现构建强大的分布式系统"],"ja":["モノリシックアプリケーションをマイクロサービスに分解する","RESTful APIまたはメッセージキューを使用したサービス間通信の実装","サーキットブレーカーとサービスディスカバリーを使用した強固な分散システムの構築"],"ko":["단일 어플리케이션을 마이크로 서비스로 분해","RESTful API 또는 메시지 큐를 사용한 서비스 간 통신 구현","회로 차단기 및 서비스 발견을 사용한 강력한 분산 시스템 구축"],"es":["Descomponer aplicaciones monolíticas en microservicios","Implementar la comunicación entre servicios utilizando API RESTful o colas de mensajes","Construir sistemas distribuidos resilientes con interruptores de circuito y servicio de descubrimiento"],"fr":["Décomposer les applications monolithiques en microservices","Mettre en œuvre la communication inter-service en utilisant des API RESTful ou des files de messages","Construire des systèmes distribués résilients avec des interrupteurs de circuit et un service de découverte"],"de":["Monolithische Anwendungen in Mikroservices zerlegen","Implementierung der Kommunikation zwischen Diensten unter Verwendung von RESTful-APIs oder Nachrichtenwarteschlangen","Aufbau resilienter verteilter Systeme mit Schaltkreisunterbrechern und Diensterkennung"],"pt":["Decompor aplicações monolíticas em microsserviços","Implementar comunicação entre serviços usando APIs RESTful ou filas de mensagens","Construir sistemas distribuídos resilientes com circuit breakers e service discovery"],"ru":["Разделение монолитных приложений на микросервисы","Реализация межсервисного взаимодействия с использованием RESTful API или очередей сообщений","Создание устойчивых распределенных систем с помощью circuit breakers и service discovery"],"ar":["تجزئة التطبيقات ال monolithic إلى ميكروسيرفس","تنفيذ الاتصال بين الخدمات باستخدام واجهات برمجة التطبيقات RESTful أو طوابير الرسائل","بناء أنظمة موزعة متينة باستخدام دوائر الكسر واكتشاف الخدمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of software architecture principles","Limited to distributed systems using microservices architecture"],"zh":["需要了解软件架构原则","仅限使用微服务架构的分布式系统"],"ja":["ソフトウェアアーキテクチャの原則を理解する必要がある","マイクロサービスアーキテクチャを使用する分散システムに限定される"],"ko":["소프트웨어 아키텍처 원리를 이해해야 함","마이크로 서비스 아키텍처를 사용하는 분산 시스템에 한정됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de arquitectura de software","Limitado a sistemas distribuidos que utilizan arquitectura de microservicios"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes d''architecture logicielle","Limité aux systèmes distribués utilisant l''architecture de microservices"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Prinzipien der Softwarearchitektur","Begrenzt auf verteilte Systeme, die die Mikroservices-Architektur verwenden"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de princípios de arquitetura de software","Limitado a sistemas distribuídos que usam arquitetura de microsserviços"],"ru":["Требует знаний принципов программной архитектуры","Ограничен распределенными системами, использующими микросервисную архитектуру"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ هندسة البرمجيات","محدود لأنظمة موزعة تستخدم هندسة ميكروسيرفس"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
